<node id="American Diabetes Association">
  <data key="d0">American Diabetes Association</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The American Diabetes Association (ADA) is a prominent organization dedicated to supporting individuals with diabetes through advocacy, education, and the dissemination of clinical guidelines. It publishes comprehensive standards of medical care in diabetes, which are regularly updated and featured in its journal, *Diabetes Care*, including the widely referenced 2014 edition. These standards include specific clinical targets such as maintaining HbA1c levels below 7% to achieve optimal glycemic control.

The ADA provides detailed, evidence-based guidelines for diabetes management, with a strong emphasis on insulin administration practices. This includes recommendations on proper insulin injection techniques and the importance of rotating injection sites to prevent complications such as lipohypertrophy. These guidelines are recognized both nationally and internationally, reflecting the organization’s broad influence in diabetes care protocols.

In addition to clinical guidance, the American Diabetes Association offers extensive support resources for people living with diabetes. It advocates for patient rights and provides practical assistance, particularly in navigating travel-related challenges that may affect diabetes management. The organization maintains the official website diabetes.org, which serves as a central hub for educational materials, research updates, and support services, reinforcing its role as a leading authority in diabetes care and advocacy.&lt;SEP&gt;The American Diabetes Association is a nonprofit organization providing information and support for people living with diabetes, including resources on hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;The American Diabetes Association is a health organization providing information and resources on diabetes management, including hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;The American Diabetes Association is the organization responsible for publishing information on hypoglycemia and diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8af713fd3913ed050d96cdd321bca3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eab57247c382bad8d5f1e5eb84a62e24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
