<node id="Insulin Pen">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Insulin Pen is a medical device designed for the administration of insulin, offering a convenient, portable, and accurate alternative to traditional syringes. It is widely used for multiple daily insulin injections and is available in both disposable and reusable forms, some of which are prefilled. The device allows for precise dose selection, including half-unit (0.5U) increments, making it particularly suitable for patients requiring low or finely adjusted doses, such as children. This precision, combined with ease of use, contributes to improved treatment adherence, better glycemic control, and lower rates of hypoglycemia compared to syringe-based insulin delivery.

Proper handling and technique are essential for effective and safe use of the insulin pen. Users are instructed to prime the device by administering a test dose of 1–2 units before each injection to ensure proper insulin flow and eliminate air bubbles. During administration, the injection button must be pressed only after the needle is fully inserted to prevent insulin loss, and it should remain depressed while the needle is held in place for at least 10 seconds post-injection. This practice helps prevent insulin or blood reflux and ensures accurate dosing. Additionally, the needle must stay in the skin until the injection button is fully released and the needle withdrawn.

Storage and maintenance are critical, especially for reusable insulin pens. These devices should not be stored in the refrigerator, as cold temperatures can damage the internal mechanism. While insulin itself may require refrigeration prior to use, the pen device must be kept at appropriate temperatures; studies have shown that insulin pens remain stable without significant degradation at temperatures up to 37°C. Reusable pens typically have a lifespan of up to three years from first use, provided they are handled correctly. The device uses disposable needles and is compatible with shorter, high-flow needles, enhancing comfort and convenience. Technical issues, such as a jammed pen, may occur and should be addressed promptly to ensure uninterrupted therapy. Overall, the insulin pen is a practical, modern tool that supports effective diabetes management through reliable, user-friendly insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be43b1b23852278983f60d0f150b0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
