<node id="Injection Site Rotation">
  <data key="d0">Injection Site Rotation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection Site Rotation is a recommended practice primarily associated with insulin administration, designed to prevent localized tissue complications and ensure consistent insulin absorption. The technique involves systematically varying the locations where insulin is injected, avoiding repeated use of the same site to minimize the risk of adverse effects. By rotating injection sites, individuals reduce the likelihood of developing lipodystrophy—a condition characterized by changes in subcutaneous fat tissue, including both lipo-hypertrophy (thickening of fat) and lipoatrophy (loss of fat)—which can result from frequent injections in the same area.

The practice also helps prevent cutaneous amyloidosis, a rare skin condition where amyloid proteins accumulate at injection sites, as well as other local reactions such as skin lesions and inflammation. Repeated insulin injections in a single location can lead to tissue damage, altered absorption rates, and glycemic instability, contributing to variability in blood glucose levels. Injection Site Rotation mitigates these risks by distributing injections across different anatomical regions—such as the abdomen, thighs, buttocks, and upper arms—and by rotating within regions to avoid localized trauma.

Healthcare guidelines emphasize that Injection Site Rotation should be performed systematically, with the recommendation to avoid using any single injection site more than once per month. This structured approach supports not only the physical integrity of the skin and subcutaneous tissue but also the therapeutic efficacy of insulin therapy by promoting predictable and consistent absorption. Overall, Injection Site Rotation is a critical self-care practice for individuals with diabetes on insulin therapy, aimed at preventing complications and maintaining optimal glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4ac915c4a6b6d9a29fe84cb65e45af82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-327f5a1b7cdf10c29c28d05c7f85ae56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699882</data>
