  <data key="d7">Insulin Absorption</data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Control">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes control is the management of blood glucose levels, improved by proper insulin administration and site rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Diabetes Control</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Vial">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Vial</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin vial is a small, sealed container, typically made of glass, designed to hold multiple doses of insulin medication, such as Novolin® R, for use in managing diabetes. These vials are intended for use with syringes to administer insulin via injection, requiring careful verification of the insulin type, expiration date, and compatibility with the appropriate syringe. Proper handling and storage are essential to maintain insulin stability and efficacy, with storage conditions needing to follow manufacturer guidelines, including protection from extreme temperatures and light.

Before each use, the rubber stopper of the insulin vial must be cleaned with 70% alcohol or another antiseptic to ensure aseptic technique and prevent contamination during access. When preparing a dose, air should be injected into the vial prior to withdrawing insulin to equalize pressure. For insulin formulations that are suspensions, such as NPH insulin, the vial should be gently rolled between the hands approximately 20 times to ensure proper mixing without creating foam or bubbles; vigorous shaking should be avoided to prevent denaturation of the insulin.

Once opened, an insulin vial should be discarded after 30 to 45 days due to the risk of bacterial contamination and loss of potency, even if refrigerated. Prior to each use, the insulin should be visually inspected for any signs of deterioration, including cloudiness, discoloration, or the presence of particles, which may indicate compromised medication. Adherence to these protocols ensures the safe and effective use of insulin vials in clinical and home care settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Vial</data>
</node>
<node id="Sharps Container">
  <data key="d0">Sharps Container</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A sharps container is a rigid, wide-mouthed container designed for the safe disposal of sharp medical waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Sharps containers are durable collection packages, such as metal cans or plastic containers, used for safe disposal of used needles to prevent injury and contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;A Sharps Container is a durable, puncture-resistant container used to safely dispose of used syringes and needles.&lt;SEP&gt;Sharps containers, such as metal cans or sturdy plastic, are used to safely collect and dispose of used syringes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709563</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Sharps Container</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Types">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Types</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal insulins are one of the main categories of insulin, used to maintain stable blood glucose levels over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus insulins are a category of insulin designed to act quickly and manage glucose spikes after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixed insulins are a category combining different types of insulin for simplified dosing before meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0522904b9c236fceb86e75d6da872d4b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778687578</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Types</data>
</node>
<node id="Needle Reuse">
  <data key="d0">Needle Reuse</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle reuse refers to the practice of using the same insulin injection needle multiple times, a behavior commonly observed among individuals managing diabetes despite widespread medical guidance against it. This practice is strongly discouraged by healthcare professionals due to a range of associated risks, including increased likelihood of infection, tissue damage, lipohypertrophy (also referred to as lipodystrophy), needle bending, and dulling of the needle tip. Lipohypertrophy, characterized by the formation of fatty lumps under the skin at injection sites, not only raises the risk of inconsistent insulin absorption but may also contribute to prolonged needle reuse, as these areas often become less sensitive to pain, reducing the user's awareness of discomfort during injection.

Multiple sources emphasize that reusing needles beyond a few uses—specifically more than three to five applications—significantly heightens the risk of complications. While some descriptions specify thresholds such as not exceeding three uses, others warn against reuse beyond five instances, particularly linking higher reuse frequency to greater incidence of injection-related issues. Regardless of the exact number, consensus exists that repeated use compromises both safety and efficacy. Complications include localized pain, inaccurate insulin dosing due to mechanical issues or blocked needles, and increased risk of skin and systemic infections due to microbial contamination of the needle.

Needle reuse is widely regarded as an unsafe practice, with structured patient education and reliable access to needles shown to reduce its prevalence. Studies indicate that individuals who receive comprehensive diabetes management training and have adequate supplies of injection equipment are less likely to reuse needles. Overall, medical guidance uniformly advises against needle reuse, promoting single-use practices to ensure patient safety, optimal insulin delivery, and prevention of long-term injection site complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699876</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Needle Reuse</data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoglobina Glicada">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobina Glicada</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoglobina Glicada, also known as HbA1c, is a measure of average blood glucose levels over time and is used to assess diabetes control.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobina Glicada (HbA1c) is a clinical marker used to assess long-term glycemic control in patients with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710023</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Hemoglobina Glicada</data>
</node>
<node id="Variabilidade Glicêmica">
  <data key="d0">Variabilidade Glicêmica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Variabilidade Glicêmica measures how much blood glucose levels fluctuate throughout the day, with lower variation indicating better stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710104</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Variabilidade Glicêmica</data>
</node>
<node id="Glicemia">
  <data key="d0">Glicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A glicemia é a medida da concentração de glicose no sangue, exibida em unidades numéricas no display do glicosímetro ou sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicemia refers to the concentration of glucose in the blood and is a key parameter in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicemia refere-se ao nível de glicose no sangue, cujo controle é essencial em pessoas com diabetes, especialmente durante a gravidez.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Glicemia</data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglicemia">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglicemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormally low blood glucose levels, typically defined as falling below 70 mg/dL. It is the most frequently reported adverse reaction associated with insulin therapy, occurring when the administered insulin dose exceeds the body's needs, whether due to incorrect dosing, administration into muscle instead of subcutaneous tissue, use of long needles, or rapid absorption. Hipoglicemia can also result from delayed meals, excessive physical activity, or drug interactions, and is particularly common during treatment with insulin formulations such as Levemir and HUMULIN R.

The condition presents a wide range of symptoms, varying in severity from mild to life-threatening. Early signs include shakiness, sweating (particularly cold and clammy skin), paleness, fatigue, tremors, anxiety, palpitations, dizziness, headache, nausea, vomiting, and confusion. As blood sugar levels continue to drop, more severe neurological symptoms may emerge, such as disorientation, apathy, vision changes, seizures, unconsciousness, and, if left untreated, brain damage or death. In severe cases, patients may require assistance from others for treatment, highlighting the potential danger in situations requiring cognitive and motor coordination, such as driving or operating machinery.

Immediate intervention is critical and typically involves the consumption of fast-acting carbohydrates to raise blood glucose levels. The risk of hipoglicemia is reduced with the use of glucose monitoring technologies, such as continuous glucose sensors, which allow for real-time tracking and early detection. Despite advances in diabetes management, hipoglicemia remains a common and serious complication of insulin therapy, affecting multiple patients and necessitating careful dose adjustment, patient education, and vigilance to prevent adverse outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dff1c37dd504c2e0f6d3e3541019e15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d717433722cc9ac8e746440493df9010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Hipoglicemia</data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglicemia Grave">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglicemia Grave</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglicemia Grave is a severe form of low blood sugar, defined as glucose levels below 54 mg/dL, requiring immediate intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia grave is a severe adverse event defined as a significant drop in blood glucose requiring assistance, monitored during pregnancy in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710101</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Hipoglicemia Grave</data>
</node>
<node id="Cetonas">
  <data key="d0">Cetonas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cetonas are substances produced when the body burns fat for energy due to insufficient glucose, often occurring in uncontrolled diabetes or illness.&lt;SEP&gt;Cetonas são substâncias produzidas pelo corpo quando há metabolismo de gordura, frequentemente monitoradas em pessoas com diabetes, especialmente em situações de descompensação metabólica.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Cetonas</data>
</node>
<node id="Cetoacidose Diabética">
  <data key="d0">Cetoacidose Diabética</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cetoacidose Diabética is a serious complication of diabetes caused by high levels of ketones, requiring urgent medical attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Cetoacidose diabética is a serious complication of prolonged hyperglycemia in type 1 diabetes, characterized by fatigue, flushed face, thirst, fruity breath, and potentially leading to coma or death.&lt;SEP&gt;Cetoacidose diabética is a serious complication of diabetes mellitus type 1 caused by prolonged hyperglycemia, presenting symptoms such as fatigue, fruity breath, dehydration, and potentially leading to coma or death if not treated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Cetoacidose Diabética</data>
</node>
<node id="β-Hidroxibutirato">
  <data key="d0">β-Hidroxibutirato</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">β-Hidroxibutirato (β-OHB) is a ketone body measured in blood to assess ketone production and risk of ketoacidosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710050</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">β-Hidroxibutirato</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin is a hormone produced by the beta cells of the pancreas that plays a central role in regulating glucose metabolism. It enables glucose from the bloodstream to enter cells, where it is converted into energy, and signals the liver to store excess glucose. Insulin acts as a key that binds to cell receptors, facilitating glucose uptake, and is essential for maintaining normal blood sugar levels. In individuals with diabetes—particularly type 1 and sometimes type 2 diabetes—insulin production is deficient or its action is impaired, necessitating external insulin administration to prevent hyperglycemia, diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA), and other complications.

As a medication, insulin is used in the treatment and management of diabetes and is administered via subcutaneous injection, insulin pens, or infusion pumps. It does not cross the placental barrier, making it safe for use during pregnancy, though dosage must be carefully adjusted based on diet, exercise, illness, and physiological changes. Insulin is available in various types, including rapid-acting (e.g., Novolin® R), regular, NPH, and long-acting forms, and comes in different concentrations such as U100, U40, U200, and U500. Dosage is prescribed in international units and must be precisely managed, as insulin is classified as a high-alert medication due to the risks of hypoglycemia, allergic reactions, and injection site complications if used incorrectly.

Proper handling, storage, and administration are critical to maintaining insulin’s efficacy and safety. It must be protected from extreme temperatures, not ingested, and stored appropriately during transport and use. When delivered via infusion pumps, insulin is stored in a reservoir and administered through an infusion set, typically requiring replacement every three days. Bolus and basal delivery methods are used to mimic natural insulin release, with pump systems tracking active insulin to guide dosing. Recombinant DNA technology produces human insulin (insulina humana rDNA), ensuring consistent supply and purity. Discovered in 1921 and first tested in dogs before human use, insulin has a short half-life in the bloodstream—lasting only a few minutes—and its pharmacokinetics vary based on individual factors, injection technique, and storage conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be43b1b23852278983f60d0f150b0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d212ccdded1e4ccf51af243a8d38b4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304