<node id="Interstitial Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Interstitial Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Interstitial Fluid is the body fluid found in the spaces between cells, forming a crucial component of the internal environment that supports cellular function. It surrounds tissue cells and serves as a medium through which substances such as glucose and insulin are transported. Glucose moves from the bloodstream into the interstitial fluid before being taken up by cells for energy production, and insulin travels through this fluid from infusion sites to reach the bloodstream, playing a key role in glucose regulation.

This fluid is of particular importance in medical monitoring, especially in the context of diabetes management. Continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems measure glucose levels directly in the interstitial fluid rather than in blood. Sensors placed in the subcutaneous tissue detect glucose concentrations in this fluid to estimate real-time blood glucose levels. However, glucose levels in the interstitial fluid typically lag slightly behind those in the bloodstream due to the time required for glucose to diffuse from blood vessels into the interstitial space. Despite this delay, interstitial fluid provides a reliable and minimally invasive means of tracking glucose trends over time.

Multiple descriptions consistently emphasize its role as the medium where glucose is monitored by CGM sensors and through which glucose passes between blood vessels and cells. It is also highlighted as the environment where insulin action begins and glucose homeostasis is dynamically maintained. Collectively, these functions underscore the significance of interstitial fluid in both physiological processes and clinical technologies aimed at managing metabolic health.&lt;SEP&gt;Interstitial fluid is the body fluid in which glucose is measured by continuous glucose monitoring sensors, located in the subcutaneous tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f14c91b2fb52c8fcc6d43aa4f53f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6</data>
