  <data key="d7">Glucose Reader</data>
</node>
<node id="Smartphone">
  <data key="d0">Smartphone</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A smartphone can receive glucose data from the sensor and display current levels, trends, and alerts for high or low glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Smartphone is a personal device used to receive, display, and store real-time glucose data from continuous glucose monitoring systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A smartphone can be used with the Dexcom G6 system to receive and display real-time glucose data through a dedicated application.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
