<node id="Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycemia is a condition characterized by abnormally low blood glucose levels, commonly defined as below 70 mg/dL (or &lt;4.4 mmol/L), and represents the most frequently reported adverse reaction associated with insulin therapy, including medications such as Levemir and Novolin® R. It occurs when insulin dosage exceeds the body's metabolic needs, which can result from excessive insulin administration, incorrect dosing, intramuscular injection of insulin, or insulin pump malfunctions such as over-infusion due to device errors, incorrect Bolus Wizard settings, or falsely elevated sensor readings. Hypoglycemia can also be triggered by external factors including skipped meals, delayed eating, unplanned or intense physical activity, alcohol consumption, or changes in insulin injection sites, particularly when switching from lipohypertrophic to unaffected areas.

The condition poses significant health risks, especially for individuals with diabetes on insulin or antidiabetic therapy, and is particularly common during the initiation of treatment, dosage adjustments, or when combining insulin with other agents such as GLP-1 agonists, which may necessitate dose reductions to minimize risk. Symptoms range from mild manifestations like sweating, palpitations, confusion, and shaking to severe outcomes including impaired concentration, seizures, loss of consciousness, brain damage, or even death if untreated. Warning signs may be variable or masked in patients with long-standing diabetes, intensive glycemic control, or those taking certain medications, increasing the danger of undetected episodes.

Hypoglycemia is not detectable through HbA1c testing and requires alternative monitoring methods such as glucometers or continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems, which are particularly valuable for identifying asymptomatic or nocturnal events. Technologies like the SmartGuard™ system and the MiniMed™ 640G System help mitigate risk by providing predictive alerts, automatically suspending insulin delivery, or adjusting bolus doses. Features such as Autoapagado also assist by halting insulin infusion and sounding alarms when hypoglycemia is imminent. Despite these advances, missed alerts—especially when relying solely on mobile applications—can still lead to dangerous outcomes.

Effective management of hypoglycemia involves prompt treatment with fast-acting carbohydrates, glucose tablets, or glucagon, along with careful monitoring to prevent recurrence. Preventive strategies include proper insulin administration techniques, frequent glucose checks, matching insulin to carbohydrate intake and activity levels, and avoiding known risk factors such as heat, massage, or exercise at injection sites that can accelerate insulin absorption. Given its prevalence and potential severity, hypoglycemia remains a critical focus in diabetes care, particularly when striving for tight glycemic control, and requires coordinated efforts between patients and medical teams to ensure safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia refers to low blood glucose levels and is a condition that requires monitoring and treatment, especially for individuals with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia refers to low blood glucose levels, which can cause a range of physical and mental symptoms and requires prompt treatment to restore glucose levels to a safe range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be43b1b23852278983f60d0f150b0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e02