  <data key="d7">Traditional Glucose Monitoring</data>
</node>
<node id="Lag Time">
  <data key="d0">Lag Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lag time is the approximately 10-minute delay between glucose levels in the interstitial fluid (measured by sensor) and blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709177</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Lag Time</data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoglobin A1c">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobin A1c</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) reflects the average blood glucose levels over the past 2 to 3 months and is a key indicator in diabetes monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) measures the average blood glucose levels over the past three months and is used to assess long-term diabetes control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
