</node>
<node id="Capillary Blood Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Blood Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Capillary Blood Glucose Monitoring, also known as AMGC, involves pricking the finger to obtain a blood sample and using a glucometer to measure glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary blood glucose monitoring refers to the frequent self-checks of blood glucose levels using a glucometer, used to inform therapy decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary Blood Glucose Monitoring involves measuring blood glucose using a drop of capillary blood on a test strip inserted into a glucose meter, commonly used for self-monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
