</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy is a skin and subcutaneous tissue condition that can develop at insulin injection sites due to repeated injections in the same area, often exacerbated by improper injection practices such as needle reuse and lack of site rotation. It is characterized by abnormal fat distribution and structural changes in the tissue, primarily manifesting as lipoatrophy—localized loss of fat—or lipohypertrophy—thickening or hardening of the tissue due to fat accumulation. These physical alterations appear as lumps or hardened areas under the skin and are recognized as uncommon adverse reactions associated with chronic insulin administration.

The condition is closely linked to impaired insulin absorption, as injections administered into affected tissue may result in delayed or erratic uptake of insulin. This disruption can lead to poor glycemic control and, in some cases, contribute to hyperglycemia if injections continue in compromised areas. Consequently, lipodystrophy not only affects the physical integrity of the skin but also undermines the effectiveness of diabetes management. For this reason, affected sites should be avoided during insulin administration to ensure optimal therapeutic outcomes.

Lipodystrophy is largely preventable through proper injection techniques, particularly the consistent rotation of injection sites. Rotating locations helps prevent localized tissue trauma and reduces the risk of fat tissue alterations. While the condition is considered an uncommon complication in modern insulin therapy, likely due to improved insulin formulations and patient education, vigilance in injection practices remains essential. Overall, lipodystrophy represents a manageable yet clinically significant skin-related adverse effect of insulin therapy that underscores the importance of patient training and adherence to recommended injection protocols.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e023d3ebcda62fd027</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709978</data>
