  <data key="d7">Lipodystrophy</data>
</node>
<node id="Lipoatrophy">
  <data key="d0">Lipoatrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipoatrophy, or lipohipertrofia, is a condition caused by repeatedly injecting insulin in the same spot, leading to lumps under the skin.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrophy is a rare form of lipodystrophy where repeated insulin injections cause loss of fat, resulting in skin depressions or holes.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrophy is a type of lipodystrophy involving gradual loss of subcutaneous tissue at insulin injection sites, resulting in uneven, well-demarcated depressions in the skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Lipoatrophy</data>
</node>
<node id="Lipohypertrophy">
  <data key="d0">Lipohypertrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipohypertrophy is a skin condition characterized by the abnormal accumulation of fat beneath the skin, typically occurring at insulin injection sites due to repeated injections in the same area. It manifests as lumps, hardened nodules, or thickened tissue and is recognized as the most common form of lipodystrophy associated with insulin therapy. These tissue changes result from improper injection practices, particularly the failure to rotate injection sites adequately, and are considered a preventable complication of insulin administration.

The presence of lipohypertrophy disrupts normal insulin absorption, leading to irregular and unpredictable uptake of insulin into the bloodstream. This erratic absorption can significantly impair glycemic control, contributing to unstable blood glucose levels and complicating diabetes management. As such, the condition is not only a physical manifestation of injection-related trauma but also a clinically relevant factor affecting treatment efficacy.

Evidence indicates that the incidence of lipohypertrophy can be reduced through structured injection training, which emphasizes proper site rotation and injection techniques. Avoiding repeated use of the same injection site is critical in preventing the development of fatty lumps and maintaining consistent insulin pharmacokinetics. Overall, lipohypertrophy remains a common yet avoidable complication, underscoring the importance of patient education in diabetes care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709039</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Lipohypertrophy</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Storage">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Storage refers to the specific conditions and practices required to maintain the stability, efficacy, and safety of insulin, a critical medication for diabetes management. Proper storage is essential to prevent degradation and ensure clinical effectiveness, with protocols differing based on whether the insulin is unopened or in use. Unopened insulin must be stored refrigerated at a temperature between 2 °C and 8 °C, typically on a shelf within the main compartment of the refrigerator, preferably above the vegetable drawer and away from freezer walls to avoid accidental freezing. It is crucial that insulin does not freeze, as this compromises its structural integrity and renders it ineffective.

Once opened or in use, insulin can be kept at room temperature—up to 30 °C—for up to 30 days, provided it is stored away from direct sunlight, heat, and excessive agitation. This allows for greater convenience and comfort during administration, as cold insulin may cause injection site discomfort. Whether refrigerated or at room temperature, insulin should be protected from light and extreme environmental conditions. During travel, insulin should be carried in carry-on luggage and stored in a protective container, avoiding direct contact with ice or freezing elements to prevent temperature excursions.

Insulin Storage applies to various forms of insulin, including vials, pens, and cartridges, all of which require adherence to temperature guidelines to preserve drug integrity. The storage protocols are part of broader handling practices for injectable medications, designed to minimize clinical risks associated with improper storage. Overall, Insulin Storage encompasses both sealed and in-use phases, with temperature control, environmental protection, and proper handling being central to ensuring the medication remains safe and effective for patient use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708719</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Storage</data>
</node>
<node id="Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 1 diabetes is an autoimmune condition in which the body's immune system mistakenly attacks and destroys the insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas, leading to little or no insulin production. This absence or severe deficiency of insulin disrupts normal glucose metabolism, as insulin is essential for allowing glucose to enter cells for energy. Consequently, individuals with Type 1 diabetes are unable to regulate blood glucose levels effectively without external intervention.

As a result of this insulin deficiency, Type 1 diabetes necessitates lifelong exogenous insulin therapy to maintain euglycemia and prevent life-threatening complications. Without adequate insulin dosing or if treatment is discontinued, blood glucose levels can rise rapidly, leading to hyperglycemia and potentially progressing to diabetic ketoacidosis—a serious metabolic condition characterized by high blood acidity and ketone accumulation. Clinical studies have examined insulin absorption and glucose regulation in this population, demonstrating that euglycemia can be maintained through precise interventions such as glucose infusion following insulin administration, highlighting the critical balance required in managing the condition.

Management of Type 1 diabetes involves not only daily insulin administration but also careful and continuous monitoring of blood glucose levels to adjust insulin doses and avoid both hyperglycemic and hypoglycemic episodes. The autoimmune nature of the disease distinguishes it from other forms of diabetes, such as Type 2, and underscores the absolute dependence on insulin therapy for survival. Overall, Type 1 diabetes is a chronic, insulin-deficient state requiring comprehensive, lifelong medical management to prevent acute and long-term complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c23215af0c479dce9c09bed4cc782d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710178</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Type 1 Diabetes</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Variability">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose variability refers to large fluctuations in blood sugar levels throughout the day, often caused by inconsistent insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Blood Glucose Variability</data>
</node>
<node id="Brazilian Diabetes Society">
  <data key="d0">Brazilian Diabetes Society</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Brazilian Diabetes Society is the organization that issued clinical guidelines on insulin administration techniques and patient education.&lt;SEP&gt;The Brazilian Diabetes Society is the organization that issued the guidelines on insulin application techniques and regulates standards for diabetes care in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;The Brazilian Diabetes Society is the organization responsible for issuing clinical guidelines on insulin application techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;The Brazilian Diabetes Society is a medical organization that issues clinical guidelines on diabetes management, including insulin application techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;The Brazilian Diabetes Society issued clinical guidelines on insulin application techniques, including storage, site rotation, and injection practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710087</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Brazilian Diabetes Society</data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Activity">
  <data key="d0">Physical Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical activity significantly influences blood glucose levels and insulin dynamics, playing a critical role in glycemic management, particularly for individuals with diabetes. It enhances insulin sensitivity, accelerates insulin absorption—especially when injected into active muscles—and increases glucose utilization, all of which can lower blood sugar levels. The extent and timing of these effects depend on the type, intensity, and duration of the activity, with both immediate and delayed hypoglycemia posing risks, the latter often occurring during or after glycogen replenishment post-exercise.

Due to these physiological changes, physical activity necessitates careful adjustments in insulin therapy to maintain target glucose levels and prevent adverse events. Variations in activity levels can alter insulin requirements, prompting the need for dose modifications in both basal and bolus insulin regimens, including insulin formulations such as Levemir. Injecting insulin into limbs engaged in physical activity may further accelerate absorption, increasing hypoglycemia risk and requiring strategic planning in administration timing and site selection.

In addition to insulin adjustments, managing glucose levels during and after physical activity may involve modifying carbohydrate intake to offset increased glucose utilization. Activities ranging from structured exercise to routine daily tasks like gardening or cleaning can impact glucose metabolism. Without proper management, physical activity may lead to either hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia, depending on individual preparation, fitness level, and metabolic control. Therefore, consistent monitoring and individualized treatment plans are essential to safely integrate physical activity into diabetes care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Physical Activity</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dosing">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dosing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin dosing is the process of adjusting insulin intake based on blood glucose levels, meals, and activity, often guided by capillary glucose testing or sensor data.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dosing refers to the administration of specific amounts of insulin, including small and odd-numbered doses, particularly for children and adolescents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Dosing</data>
</node>
<node id="NPH Insulin">
  <data key="d0">NPH Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">NPH Insulin is an intermediate-acting, human insulin formulation used primarily as a basal insulin in the management of both type 1 and type 2 diabetes. It is commonly employed in clinical practice and has served as a comparator in clinical trials evaluating newer basal insulin therapies. The insulin is characterized by its cloudy appearance, which results from its suspension form, and it must be gently mixed or homogenized before each use to ensure uniform distribution of the active ingredient and consistent dosing. Proper resuspension is critical, as the pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of NPH insulin depend on uniform mixing prior to subcutaneous injection.

This form of insulin requires careful preparation and handling; it should be stored appropriately after opening to maintain efficacy and safety. Due to its suspension nature, NPH insulin is often used in combination with other insulins to achieve optimal glycemic control, necessitating specific steps during preparation to avoid dosing inaccuracies. While effective as a basal insulin, NPH insulin is associated with higher within-patient variability in glucose control compared to more modern basal insulin analogs such as insulin detemir. Despite this limitation, it remains a widely used and accessible treatment option in diabetes care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fc83e266bdeb54c4139a50adf2b793a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44f60a4106da6d70fe72d17aa2728296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c23215af0c479dce9c09bed4cc782d20</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708671</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">NPH Insulin</data>
</node>
<node id="Adolescents">
  <data key="d0">Adolescents</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adolescents are young individuals with thin skin who should use short needles (4, 5, or 6 mm) for insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents are individuals aged 14 to 17 years, showing higher skin thickness values compared to younger age groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents require a subcutaneous pinch and a 45° needle angle during insulin injection, particularly when using needles 6 mm or longer, to prevent intramuscular delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents are a patient group requiring precise insulin dosing, often using specialized equipment for safe and accurate administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents aged 13 to 17 years were included in a study on Novolin® R, with pharmacokinetic data indicating possible differences in Cmax compared to adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709102</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Adolescents</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Syringe">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Syringe</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Syringe is a medical device specifically designed for the accurate measurement and administration of insulin. It functions as a critical tool in diabetes management, enabling users to deliver precise doses of insulin subcutaneously, and in specific clinical situations, intravenously. The syringe is calibrated in international units (UI), typically aligned with U100 insulin concentration, and must be read using the unit scale rather than milliliters to prevent potentially dangerous dosing errors. This unit-based graduation ensures accuracy, particularly for low-dose requirements, with common sizes including 30U and 50U syringes that offer dosing increments of 0.5U or 1U for fine control.

Insulin Syringe is available in various types, differing in capacity, needle configuration, and design features to suit individual patient needs. These syringes may come with either fixed or removable needles, though fixed-needle models are often preferred due to reduced dead space, which enhances dosing accuracy and minimizes insulin waste. The device is used following a standardized procedure that includes injecting air into the insulin vial and expelling air bubbles from the syringe to ensure correct dosage delivery. It is commonly employed when drawing insulin from vials, such as with Novolin® R, and can be used to aspirate insulin from cartridges in the absence of a vial, including for intravenous administration under medical supervision.

Beyond routine insulin delivery, Insulin Syringe plays an essential role in managing acute diabetic conditions. It is frequently used to administer corrective insulin doses when blood glucose levels are elevated, particularly in the presence of ketones or when insulin pump malfunctions are suspected. Its reliability, precision, and compatibility with standard insulin formulations make it a fundamental component of both daily diabetes care and emergency interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Syringe</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Administration">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin administration refers to the process of delivering insulin via injection, with techniques varying by device, needle length, and injection site.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin administration is the process of delivering insulin into the body, typically via subcutaneous injection using proper techniques and equipment.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin administration refers to the process of delivering insulin via bolus types, including square and dual boluses, to manage blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin administration refers to the delivery of insulin via bolus methods, including standard, square, and dual boluses, to manage blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69f89cc6358f0fe2b490d63a60ae0581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b8d4c3fde5ebf7bc3593f47b765f41</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Administration</data>
</node>
<node id="Systematic Review">
  <data key="d0">Systematic Review</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A systematic review of eight databases was conducted, selecting 17 studies to evaluate the efficacy of insulin pens versus syringes in type 2 diabetes patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709118</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Systematic Review</data>
</node>
<node id="Meta-Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Meta-Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Meta-analyses showed better outcomes with insulin pens in HbA1c reduction, hypoglycemia, and treatment adherence compared to vial and syringe methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709107</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Meta-Analysis</data>
</node>
<node id="Intermediate-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Intermediate-Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediate-Acting Insulin, such as NPH, starts working 1 to 3 hours after injection, peaks in 4 to 10 hours, and lasts 10 to 18 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate-acting insulin has a longer duration of action and can be combined with rapid-acting insulin following the correct mixing order.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate-acting insulin can be mixed with rapid-acting insulin or its analogs in the same syringe under specific storage and usage conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate-acting insulin has a longer duration of action and can be mixed with rapid-acting insulin in the same syringe if prepared in the correct sequence.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate-acting insulin can be combined with rapid-acting insulin or its analogs in the same syringe for immediate use to meet patient-specific treatment needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate-acting insulin is a type of basal insulin that may be replaced by Levemir, requiring dose and timing adjustments during transition.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate-acting insulin is used in injection therapy to provide basal insulin coverage, with absorption lasting 12 to 24 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708920</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Intermediate-Acting Insulin</data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Rapid-Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid-Acting Insulin is a type of insulin designed to quickly control blood glucose levels, particularly in individuals with diabetes. It begins working within 10 to 20 minutes after injection, reaches peak activity in 1 to 2 hours, and typically remains effective for 3 to 5 hours, though some descriptions note glucose-lowering effects lasting up to 5 to 6 hours. Common examples include insulin Lispro and insulin Aspart, which are formulated for rapid absorption into the bloodstream. Due to its pharmacokinetic profile, Rapid-Acting Insulin is the only type of insulin approved for intramuscular and intravenous administration, making it suitable for emergency or hospital settings where fast-acting glucose control is required.

This insulin type is frequently used as bolus insulin in basal-bolus insulin regimens, helping to manage postprandial glucose spikes. It is commonly administered via insulin pens, vials, or insulin pump therapy, including systems such as the MiniMed™. Rapid-Acting Insulin is often prescribed in small and sometimes odd-numbered doses, especially for children and adolescents, requiring precise delivery methods to ensure accurate dosing. It is also recommended to have Rapid-Acting Insulin available as a backup during travel to manage unexpected hyperglycemia or pump malfunctions.

Rapid-Acting Insulin can be mixed with intermediate-acting insulin in the same syringe to reduce the number of injections, provided it is done in the correct order and according to manufacturer guidelines. This mixing requires proper handling to maintain insulin stability and efficacy. When used concomitantly with long-acting insulins such as Levemir, dose or timing adjustments may be necessary to optimize glycemic control and avoid hypoglycemia. Overall, Rapid-Acting Insulin plays a critical role in flexible and responsive diabetes management, supporting both daily routines and acute glucose regulation needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708936</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Rapid-Acting Insulin</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin NPH">
  <data key="d0">Insulin NPH</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin NPH, also known as neutral protamine Hagedorn insulin or Protaphane HM, is an intermediate-acting human insulin formulation used in the management of diabetes mellitus. It is characterized as a cloudy suspension that must be properly homogenized before administration to ensure consistent insulin concentration and a predictable clinical response. To achieve uniformity, it is recommended to gently mix the suspension approximately 20 times prior to use. Due to its physical properties, when Insulin NPH is combined with regular (short-acting) insulin in the same syringe, it should be drawn first to prevent contamination and maintain efficacy.

As an intermediate-acting insulin, Insulin NPH provides glycemic control over an extended duration, typically requiring two daily injections to manage blood glucose levels effectively. It plays a significant role in diabetes treatment regimens, particularly where cost and availability are considerations. Proper mixing and accurate dosing are essential components of its safe and effective use. Studies have shown that its pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics remain unaffected by storage temperature when mixed with regular insulin, supporting its stability under various handling conditions.

Insulin NPH has frequently served as a comparator in clinical studies evaluating newer insulin analogs, particularly insulin detemir, marketed as Levemir®. In trials involving pregnant women with diabetes, Insulin NPH was used as a benchmark against Levemir for glycemic management during pregnancy. These studies revealed that, compared to insulin detemir, Insulin NPH is associated with a higher risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia and greater weight gain. Additionally, it demonstrates higher pharmacokinetic variability and less capacity for intensive dose titration, which may limit its precision in achieving optimal glucose control. Despite these limitations, Insulin NPH remains a widely used insulin globally due to its established efficacy, affordability, and long-standing clinical use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975d0ad130a42cf2fe8a0f91e4da2b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708812</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin NPH</data>
</node>
<node id="Flow Test">
  <data key="d0">Flow Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The flow test for insulin pens involves expelling 1–2 units to confirm unobstructed flow and absence of air in the needle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637673</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Flow Test</data>
</node>
<node id="Glycemic Variability">
  <data key="d0">Glycemic Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycemic variability measures how much blood glucose levels fluctuate throughout the day, with greater stability being a desired outcome in diabetes treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic variability refers to fluctuations in blood glucose levels, which can be influenced by improper insulin absorption due to inadequate injection practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic variability was observed in 49.1% of patients with lipohipertrophy versus 6.5% in those without, reflecting unstable blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic Variability refers to fluctuations in blood glucose levels, including episodes of hyperglycemia and hypoglycemia, which are not captured by Hba1c.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic variability refers to fluctuations in blood glucose levels, associated with increased risk of complications, measured by metrics like coefficient of variation and standard deviation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710135</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Glycemic Variability</data>
</node>
<node id="Brazil">
  <data key="d0">Brazil</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Brazil is a country where the disposal of medical waste, including sharps, is regulated by specific technical and legal guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Brazil is the country where U100 insulin is the most common type and where syringe usage remains the primary method of insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Brazil is the country where Novolin® R is distributed and regulated by Anvisa, with local operations managed by Novo Nordisk Farmacêutica do Brasil Ltda.&lt;SEP&gt;Brazil is a country where the Accu-Chek Solo system is registered and supported, with local regulatory approval and customer service.&lt;SEP&gt;Brazil is the country where the product is registered and distributed, under ANVISA regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Brazil is the country where the FreeStyle Libre system is currently available, while the FreeStyle Libre 2 is not yet available, and where insulin pumps have been in use for approximately 20 years.</data>
