<node id="Lipohipertrofia">
  <data key="d0">Lipohipertrofia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipohipertrofia is a condition associated with insulin injection sites, studied in relation to reuse of needles and patient risk factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipohipertrofia is a condition caused by repeated insulin injections in the same area, leading to fat deposits that impair insulin absorption and may cause hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipohipertrofia is a rare adverse effect of subcutaneous insulin injection, characterized by thickening or enlargement of tissue at the injection site.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fc83e266bdeb54c4139a50adf2b793a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311</data>
