</node>
<node id="Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 2 diabetes is a condition where the body develops insulin resistance and gradually loses the ability to produce sufficient insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes is a metabolic disorder characterized by insulin resistance, studied in trials involving combination therapies including insulin detemir, liraglutide, and metformin.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by insulin resistance and hyperglycemia, often managed with insulin and oral agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes is a condition in which Levemir was studied in combination with liraglutide at steady state.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes is a metabolic disorder characterized by insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44f60a4106da6d70fe72d17aa2728296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c23215af0c479dce9c09bed4cc782d20</data>
