</node>
<node id="Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes is a chronic metabolic disease characterized by persistently high blood glucose levels due to the body's inability to properly produce or effectively use insulin, a hormone essential for regulating glucose metabolism. This condition arises when the pancreas fails to generate sufficient basal and bolus insulin or when the body's cells become resistant to insulin's effects, leading to impaired glucose uptake and cellular energy deficiency. As a result, individuals with diabetes must engage in ongoing management to maintain optimal blood glucose control and prevent long-term complications affecting vital organs such as the eyes, kidneys, heart, and nervous system.

Effective management of diabetes typically requires insulin therapy, especially in cases where endogenous insulin production is inadequate. Insulin administration may be delivered through injections or insulin pumps, with specific formulations such as Novolin® R used to meet therapeutic needs. Treatment adherence includes proper storage of insulin and strict compliance with safety guidelines to minimize risks. Careful monitoring of blood glucose levels is essential, particularly during activities such as travel, to avoid acute complications like hyperglycemia and hypoglycemia, which can occur due to improper dosing or inconsistent management.

Beyond insulin therapy, diabetes management often involves dietary control, lifestyle modifications, and continuous glucose monitoring to achieve stable metabolic regulation. The condition is frequently referred to colloquially as "my diabetes" or "my sugar" by patients, reflecting its personal and chronic nature. Without optimized glucose control, the risk of progressive organ damage increases significantly. Therefore, diabetes demands a comprehensive, lifelong approach to treatment that integrates medical therapy, patient education, and vigilant self-care to delay complications and maintain quality of life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be43b1b23852278983f60d0f150b0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84d2aca165fc0184360972207bae8c6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6900fc7e5ef921c29efe412333f2e7ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
