<node id="Patient">
  <data key="d0">Patient</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patient is an individual receiving diabetes treatment who engages in various aspects of insulin therapy and disease management under the guidance of healthcare professionals. This includes learning and practicing proper insulin application techniques, particularly for those new to insulin therapy who require step-by-step instructions on safe usage, storage, dosage adjustment, and injection site rotation. The patient must understand how to correctly administer insulin using specific devices such as the Levemir Penfill, Novolin® R Penfill, and NovoFine needles, following prescribed protocols for dose calculation and device handling.

Responsibility for proper administration extends to the safe disposal of needles after each use and adherence to storage guidelines. In emergency situations—such as hospitalization or device malfunction—the patient may require insulin extraction from a cartridge using an insulin syringe, a procedure that must be performed with care. The patient’s insulin regimen may be influenced by factors including age, emotional state, life stage, diet, physical activity, and illness, necessitating individualized education and ongoing support to ensure effective self-management.

Additionally, the patient may utilize advanced diabetes management technologies, including continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion via a pump device and glucose monitoring systems, to maintain glycemic control. These tools enable real-time tracking and more precise insulin delivery, reflecting a comprehensive, technology-assisted approach to diabetes care. Across all contexts, the patient plays an active role in their treatment, relying on both medical guidance and personal adherence to achieve optimal health outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f765b5ffd5740652b2b5a3ee5760e8cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
