</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose refers to the concentration of glucose in the bloodstream, commonly measured in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL) using a blood glucose meter. It is a critical physiological parameter in the management of diabetes, serving as a direct indicator of blood sugar levels at any given time. These measurements are essential for monitoring glycemic control, guiding insulin therapy, and informing treatment decisions. Blood glucose levels are typically obtained from capillary blood through fingerstick testing and are considered the standard for accuracy, especially when compared to sensor glucose (SG) readings from continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems.

Regular monitoring of blood glucose is necessary for effective diabetes management, particularly during situations that introduce variability, such as travel, changes in time zones, stress, or dietary shifts. Measurements are used to calibrate CGM sensors, verify their accuracy when symptoms do not align with sensor readings, and support bolus insulin calculations via tools like the Bolus Wizard. Blood glucose values—such as 103 mg/dL or 131 mg/dL—are manually entered into insulin pump systems to determine appropriate insulin dosage, and they play a crucial role when sensor data is unavailable or unreliable. 

Blood glucose (often abbreviated as BG or GS) is distinct from sensor glucose readings, particularly during periods of rapid glucose fluctuations, when discrepancies between actual blood levels and sensor estimates may occur. For this reason, blood glucose measurements are preferred for critical decisions like insulin dosing and are required when confirming hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia. They are also recommended one to three hours after changing an infusion set or insulin reservoir to ensure proper system function and accurate dosing. Overall, blood glucose remains a foundational metric in diabetes care, integral to both self-monitoring and advanced treatment technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69f89cc6358f0fe2b490d63a60ae0581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f14c91b2fb52c8fcc6d43aa4f53f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03aab2b6261ddc73d474d0c866e7b37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b8d4c3fde5ebf7bc3593f47b765f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0deeba398b22b91d8da1b31653eede4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654d7a203c4eab9f3a89f577edc2a5ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710069</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Blood Glucose</data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperglycemia is a condition characterized by abnormally high blood glucose levels, commonly referred to by patients as "the sugar went up," and is detectable through glucometer testing, continuous glucose monitoring (CGM), or real-time glucose data analysis. It occurs when there is insufficient insulin delivery or action relative to the body's needs, which may result from inadequate insulin dosing, treatment discontinuation, incorrect bolus calculations, or insulin under-delivery due to pump-related issues such as blocked infusion sets, low reservoir levels, leaks, or system errors. Insulin effectiveness can also be compromised by exposure to extreme temperatures, improper pump settings like inaccurate Bolus Wizard inputs, or failure to resume basal insulin delivery.

The condition frequently arises when insulin action does not align with food intake, particularly after meals with delayed glucose absorption such as those high in fat and protein, or due to miscalculated carbohydrate intake. It may also occur during or after physical activity if insulin and carbohydrate levels are not properly adjusted. Additional causes include repeated insulin injections in areas affected by lipodystrophy or localized cutaneous amyloidosis, leading to impaired absorption. Hyperglycemia is a hallmark of diabetes and poses a particular risk in type 1 diabetes, where untreated elevations can rapidly progress to diabetic ketoacidosis, especially during insulin interruption or missed alerts in pump-dependent individuals.

Hyperglycemia is not only a marker of acute metabolic imbalance but also a key factor in long-term diabetes complications and poor glycemic control. It necessitates corrective actions such as administration of bolus insulin and identification of underlying causes. Persistent or recurrent episodes indicate a potential need for therapy adjustment, including insulin regimen, device settings, or infusion site management. During pregnancy, uncontrolled hyperglycemia significantly increases the risk of fetal malformations and intrauterine death, underscoring its clinical urgency. Regular monitoring through glucose trend analysis, sensor-augmented technologies like SMCG, and pattern recognition is essential for timely intervention and effective diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be43b1b23852278983f60d0f150b0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e023d3ebcda62fd027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96a4da2f877f1b93eb7d982c91358ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca77ae5b015fee5d1a21879c1a2b444&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23235296c6ccfffc5ec397dd6b0dc7b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44b69a8e50a0a4230b6963fe643d8cd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-425759c12d133ef4832928e8f5d50896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f2cf8a591a83e4436ab6a76c2d30e2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc77598dbeb5980c719d1d54a6c3ab77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f5ebaa0341f051ad33cfb9895a3851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc61f77b003d0086bd985ddb94fc2a98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
