<node id="Diabetes Management">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ongoing process of monitoring and controlling blood glucose levels, supported by regular glucometer use.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes management involves monitoring blood glucose levels, carbohydrate intake, and insulin administration to maintain optimal health.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb7ffc723b939ad50f1b00ca6ec8b9a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710135</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Diabetes Management</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Transport">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Transport</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin transport refers to the proper handling and carrying of insulin, requiring it to be kept in carry-on baggage and protected from direct sunlight and extreme temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin should be transported in hand luggage with precautions to avoid freezing by limiting direct contact with ice.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin transport requires adherence to manufacturer guidelines to maintain drug integrity, especially during travel, and must always be carried in hand luggage.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin transport involves maintaining proper temperature and handling conditions when moving insulin between locations.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin transport requires adherence to manufacturer recommendations, including avoiding direct contact with ice and carrying insulin in hand luggage during travel.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin transport refers to the safe handling and carrying of insulin, requiring it to be kept in carry-on baggage and protected from direct sunlight and extreme temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696408</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Transport</data>
</node>
<node id="Lancet">
  <data key="d0">Lancet</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A small needle device used to perform a finger prick to collect a blood sample for glucose testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710133</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Lancet</data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Sensor is a medical device designed to continuously monitor glucose levels, primarily in the interstitial fluid, as part of continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) or flash monitoring systems. It serves as a modern alternative to traditional finger-prick blood sampling, enabling real-time tracking of glucose trends and variability throughout the day without the need for frequent blood draws. The device is typically inserted subcutaneously and remains in place for several days, during which it measures sensor glucose (SG) levels and transmits data wirelessly to a receiver, smartphone, insulin pump, or dedicated display device.

Glucose Sensor is a key component in advanced diabetes management systems, including the MiniMed™ 640G and other integrated insulin pump systems. It supports automated insulin delivery by providing continuous glucose readings that inform insulin dosing decisions and can trigger alerts or suspend insulin delivery when glucose levels approach predefined thresholds, such as those indicating hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia. The sensor operates through an electrochemical reaction involving glucose oxidase, which detects glucose in the interstitial fluid and converts it into measurable electrical signals.

While Glucose Sensor provides real-time data and trend information crucial for managing insulin therapy, its readings are not intended to be used in isolation for treatment decisions. The device may require periodic calibration and must be reinserted if dislodged, with proper skin disinfection recommended before insertion. Although highly effective, users are advised to confirm readings with blood glucose tests when making critical treatment choices. Overall, Glucose Sensor enhances glycemic control by offering continuous, actionable insights into glucose dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1faf2db5ce0667a0d479a8832c2bc8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44b69a8e50a0a4230b6963fe643d8cd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03aab2b6261ddc73d474d0c866e7b37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc5c57277d034fb00908385613bf5a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f2cf8a591a83e4436ab6a76c2d30e2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6</data>
