<node id="Basal-Bolus Regimen">
  <data key="d0">Basal-Bolus Regimen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal-Bolus Regimen is a treatment plan combining long-acting (basal) and rapid-acting (bolus) insulin to mimic natural insulin release.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708704</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Basal-Bolus Regimen</data>
</node>
<node id="Healthcare Professional">
  <data key="d0">Healthcare Professional</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Healthcare Professional is a qualified medical expert responsible for the comprehensive management and guidance of insulin therapy for individuals with diabetes. This role encompasses a wide range of duties, including educating patients on proper insulin administration techniques, ensuring safe injection practices, and teaching the correct use of devices such as insulin syringes, pens (including Novolin® R FlexPen® and Penfill), and insulin pumps. Healthcare professionals, such as doctors, nurses, and diabetes educators, provide up-to-date, accurate training to patients and caregivers, emphasizing the importance of injection site rotation, skin assessment during consultations, and avoiding common errors through demonstration and verification.

These professionals play a critical role in personalizing diabetes treatment plans by calculating and prescribing appropriate basal rates, determining bolus settings, and configuring advanced pump features such as the Bolus Wizard—setting parameters like carbohydrate ratio, insulin sensitivity, blood glucose target, and active insulin time based on individual patient data. They are authorized to administer insulin intravenously or intramuscularly, including specific formulations like Novolin® R, and are responsible for managing insulin delivery during emergencies or device malfunctions. Healthcare professionals also guide patients on responding to pump and continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) alerts, adjusting therapy accordingly, and safely using features like Suspend on Low and SmartGuard.

Furthermore, a Healthcare Professional collaborates with patients to interpret blood glucose readings, manage abnormal glucose levels, and adjust insulin dosing and basal patterns. They provide medical guidance on disconnecting and reconnecting insulin pumps, recommend alternate insulin delivery methods when pumps are not in use, and advise on rapid insulin replacement strategies. Patients are instructed to consult their healthcare professional before making significant changes to pump settings such as Basal Max or Bolus Max, when using the MiniMed 780G system under special medical conditions, or when taking medications that may interfere with glucose monitoring. Additionally, these experts advise on emergency preparedness, including kit contents, device use training, and appropriate waiting periods after manual insulin injections before resuming automated features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc3409d91fe33592f741a0002d70749c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc77598dbeb5980c719d1d54a6c3ab77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88cdb970e2c2f1aaaab96fdc11b589f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7534f3bc09ac6e2eece38e12eb89cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b04d1a6d29b90441d249d701d54d862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d536bf636b4a29c1f9f46de648b2b306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f608f07eae4ddd5409aed9d4ecef75ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200c1e93d7f4cbc3027cec4d0898dc00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Healthcare Professional</data>
</node>
<node id="Caregiver">
  <data key="d0">Caregiver</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A caregiver assists in the management of a patient's diabetes and may be involved in learning and performing insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;A caregiver supports a person with diabetes and must be educated on safe insulin administration practices.&lt;SEP&gt;A caregiver handles used needles and the Novolin® R FlexPen® with caution to prevent needlestick injuries and cross-infection.&lt;SEP&gt;A caregiver is an individual who can enable Block mode to restrict access to critical pump features for safety and control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc3409d91fe33592f741a0002d70749c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709090</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Caregiver</data>
</node>
<node id="Hospital">
  <data key="d0">Hospital</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes diagnosed in the first 6 months of life, typically identified during or after a hospital stay, is classified as neonatal diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A hospital is a healthcare facility where defined protocols, electronic prescriptions, staff training, and double-checking procedures are essential for safe insulin use.&lt;SEP&gt;Hospital é o local onde devem existir protocolos definidos, prescrição eletrônica, treinamento contínuo e dupla checagem no uso de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0de4d525c273cda4939a501eaecc6d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Hospital</data>
</node>
<node id="Refrigerator">
  <data key="d0">Refrigerator</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A refrigerator is used to store unopened insulin at 2 °C to 8 °C, preferably on middle or lower shelves or in the vegetable drawer, away from freezer walls.&lt;SEP&gt;A Refrigerator is used to store unopened insulin vials or pens at the proper temperature to maintain potency.&lt;SEP&gt;A refrigerator is used for storing unopened insulin between 2°C and 8°C, with specific placement recommended to avoid freezing and maintain stability.&lt;SEP&gt;A refrigerator is used to store Novolin® R at temperatures between 2°C and 8°C, protecting it from freezing and light.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Refrigerator</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dose">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Insulin Dose varies per individual and depends on body weight, carbohydrate intake, physical activity, age, life stage, and special conditions like illness.&lt;SEP&gt;The amount of insulin to be administered, set according to medical prescription.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin dose refers to the measured amount of insulin administered, prescribed in international units (UI), and must be accurately prepared to avoid dosing errors.&lt;SEP&gt;The measured amount of insulin to be administered, determined by medical prescription.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dose refers to the prescribed amount of insulin, often in small and odd numbers, especially for children and adolescents using rapid-acting or analog insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dose is the amount of insulin, in units, recommended or administered to manage blood glucose levels for meals or corrections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eb891fdc2320360f3af78eb373161d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-425759c12d133ef4832928e8f5d50896</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Dose</data>
</node>
<node id="Clothing">
  <data key="d0">Clothing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Applying insulin through clothing is unsafe and increases the risk of contamination and infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Clothing must not be used as a barrier during insulin injection, as it prevents proper skin inspection and formation of the subcutaneous fold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Clothing</data>
</node>
<node id="Gestational Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Gestational Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gestational Diabetes is a form of diabetes that occurs during pregnancy, where insulin is considered safe and effective for treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709966</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Gestational Diabetes</data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra-Rapid-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Ultra-Rapid-Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra-Rapid-Acting Insulin, such as Fiasp and inhaled forms, begins acting in 2 to 5 minutes, peaks in 30 minutes to 1 hour, and lasts up to 3 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Ultra-Rapid-Acting Insulin</data>
</node>
<node id="Long-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Long-Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Long-Acting Insulin, such as Glargine and Detemir, begins acting in 1 to 2 hours, has no peak, and lasts 20 to 24 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-acting insulin refers to basal insulins like Levemir, used for sustained glucose control, with specific protocols for switching from other long-acting formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-acting insulin is used in injection therapy to provide a steady level of basal insulin over an extended period.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-acting insulin provides baseline insulin coverage and should be available as backup during travel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Long-Acting Insulin</data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra-Long-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Ultra-Long-Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra-Long-Acting Insulin, such as Degludec, starts working in up to 6 hours, has no peak, and lasts up to 42 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708924</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Ultra-Long-Acting Insulin</data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Basal Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal insulin refers to the continuous, low-level delivery of insulin that maintains stable blood glucose levels between meals and during sleep. It mimics the steady secretion of insulin naturally produced by the pancreas in individuals without diabetes, providing a background level of insulin to meet the body's metabolic needs throughout the day and night. This form of insulin is essential for regulating glucose production by the liver and ensuring consistent glucose control during fasting states.

Basal insulin can be administered through long-acting or intermediate-acting insulin injections, or via continuous subcutaneous infusion using insulin pumps. In pump therapy, basal insulin is delivered as a small, steady stream of insulin, and it must not be interrupted during illness unless specifically advised by a healthcare provider. Modern insulin pump systems, such as the MiniMed 780G, are designed to provide precise basal insulin delivery, often with automated adjustments to maintain target glucose levels.

Whether delivered by injection or pump, the primary function of basal insulin is to cover the body's insulin requirements when not eating, ensuring metabolic stability over extended periods. It works in conjunction with bolus insulin, which addresses glucose spikes from meals, but operates independently to sustain baseline glycemic control. Effective basal insulin management is crucial for preventing both hyperglycemia and hypoglycemia in individuals with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca86c4a53b7e0983cbdb18336b916858&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23235296c6ccfffc5ec397dd6b0dc7b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Basal Insulin</data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Insulin is a type of insulin dose specifically administered to manage sharp increases in blood glucose levels, primarily those occurring after meals or due to carbohydrate intake. It is designed to act rapidly or ultra-rapidly, allowing it to effectively control postprandial glucose spikes by mimicking the natural insulin response of a healthy pancreas. This form of insulin is distinct from basal insulin, which provides a steady background level of insulin throughout the day; instead, bolus insulin is delivered in larger, single doses timed with food consumption or to correct hyperglycemia.

Bolus insulin serves two primary functions: covering the anticipated rise in blood glucose from ingested carbohydrates and correcting elevated blood glucose levels back into the target range. The dosage is often adjustable and personalized, taking into account factors such as the amount of carbohydrates consumed, current blood glucose levels, and anticipated physical activity. It can be administered via multiple methods, including insulin pens, injections, or insulin pumps, with pump therapy offering additional flexibility through different bolus types—such as standard boluses for immediate insulin delivery or extended boluses for slower absorption, particularly useful with high-fat meals.

This insulin regimen is a critical component of intensive insulin therapy for individuals with type 1 and some cases of type 2 diabetes, enabling tighter glycemic control. Whether delivered manually or through automated systems, bolus insulin plays an essential role in maintaining glucose homeostasis around meals and in response to acute hyperglycemic events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac7fb8feaa2febe2b5f8525b93f3080f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Bolus Insulin</data>
</node>
