<node id="Carbohydrate Intake">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Intake</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate Intake refers to the consumption of foods or substances containing carbohydrates, which plays a central role in blood glucose management, particularly for individuals with diabetes. It is a critical factor in determining mealtime insulin bolus doses, as the amount of carbohydrates consumed directly influences postprandial blood glucose levels. Carbohydrate intake is typically measured in grams—such as 35 g or 41 g—or in carbohydrate servings, and this quantitative value serves as a key input in insulin dose calculations, often facilitated by tools like the Bolus Wizard on insulin pumps.

Accurate assessment of Carbohydrate Intake is essential to prevent both hyperglycemia and hypoglycemia. On one hand, insufficient insulin relative to carbohydrate consumption can lead to elevated blood glucose levels; on the other, excessive insulin without adequate carbohydrate availability increases hypoglycemia risk. To mitigate this, patients are advised to consume a meal or snack containing carbohydrates within 30 minutes after injecting rapid-acting insulins such as Novolin® R, ensuring that insulin action coincides with glucose absorption. This timing helps maintain glycemic stability and prevents low blood sugar episodes.

In addition to its role in insulin dosing and meal planning, Carbohydrate Intake also encompasses the therapeutic consumption of carbohydrates—such as glucose tablets or other fast-acting sources—to treat hypoglycemia when it occurs. Thus, the term applies both to proactive carbohydrate consumption in alignment with insulin therapy and to reactive intake during hypoglycemic events. Overall, Carbohydrate Intake is a multifaceted concept integral to effective diabetes management, requiring careful calculation, timing, and monitoring to support optimal blood glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97d9a9de5f40419555bf7bf36cc9f84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-425759c12d133ef4832928e8f5d50896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-402361ced0649a06619dcaf93b0eb651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b8d4c3fde5ebf7bc3593f47b765f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0deeba398b22b91d8da1b31653eede4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450</data>
