  <data key="d7">Reusable Insulin Pen</data>
</node>
<node id="Alcohol">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol is commonly used as an antiseptic in diabetes care, particularly for cleaning the skin prior to insulin injection or infusion set insertion. It is typically applied with a cotton swab to the injection site to ensure hygiene and prevent infection, and must be allowed to dry completely to avoid skin irritation. Additionally, alcohol is recommended for cleaning the exterior of insulin delivery devices such as the Levemir® FlexPen®, though the device should never be soaked or submerged in alcohol to prevent damage.

Beyond its topical use, alcohol has significant physiological effects that impact blood glucose management. It inhibits the liver's ability to release glucose into the bloodstream, which can lead to reduced blood glucose levels; this effect may persist for several hours after consumption. Alcohol's interaction with insulin is complex and context-dependent—it can either intensify or reduce insulin's hypoglycemic effect, resulting in unpredictable blood sugar levels. This variability poses notable risks for individuals managing diabetes, as alcohol consumption may compromise blood sugar control and increase the likelihood of hypoglycemia, especially when combined with insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d212ccdded1e4ccf51af243a8d38b4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709083</data>
