<node id="Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Mellitus is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by high blood glucose levels due to the body's inability to properly produce or effectively use insulin, a hormone essential for glucose regulation. It encompasses various forms, including type 1 diabetes, often resulting from immune-mediated destruction of insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas, and type 2 diabetes, which arises from a combination of insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency. This condition leads to both acute and chronic hyperglycemia, necessitating lifelong management to prevent complications and maintain glucose homeostasis.

The management of Diabetes Mellitus involves comprehensive treatment strategies centered on insulin therapy, particularly for individuals with type 1 diabetes and some with advanced type 2 diabetes. Multiple insulin formulations are indicated for treatment across different age groups, including Levemir, Novolin® R (available in Penfill and FlexPen® formats), and Humulin R. These therapies are used in adults, adolescents, and children over one year of age, supporting glycemic control in diverse patient populations. Treatment is complemented by regular monitoring of blood glucose levels through methods such as self-monitoring, HbA1c testing, and continuous glucose monitoring systems.

Diabetes Mellitus requires ongoing clinical supervision and patient education, supported by public health policies in various countries, including Brazil, to ensure access to treatment and promote disease management. As a long-term condition, it demands a multidisciplinary approach involving medication, lifestyle modifications, and consistent monitoring to reduce the risk of complications such as cardiovascular disease, neuropathy, retinopathy, and kidney disease. The integration of medical, technological, and policy-based interventions underscores the complexity and global significance of Diabetes Mellitus as a major public health challenge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d9cf8845dcb3d8d9a2db7f8843f0fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975d0ad130a42cf2fe8a0f91e4da2b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7d99aa72407a6721b69e4da3cbbcba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710016</data>
