  <data key="d5">1778710017</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Dysglycemia</data>
</node>
<node id="Inflammation">
  <data key="d0">Inflammation</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Inflammation is a localized immune response indicated by redness, swelling, or heat, and should prevent insulin application.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflammation, characterized by redness or swelling, is a skin condition that contraindicates insulin injection at the affected site.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflammation is an internal bodily response triggered by dysglycemia, contributing to tissue damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709907</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Inflammation</data>
</node>
<node id="Vascular Damage">
  <data key="d0">Vascular Damage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vascular damage refers to injury to blood vessels caused by prolonged and fluctuating high blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Vascular Damage</data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Memory">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Memory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic memory is the phenomenon where the body retains the negative effects of past high blood sugar levels, even after glucose control improves.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic memory is a theory suggesting that prior periods of poor glycemic control can have long-lasting effects on cellular metabolism and organ damage in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Metabolic Memory</data>
</node>
<node id="Fasting Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Fasting Blood Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Fasting blood glucose is a measurement of blood sugar levels before eating, used to assess diabetes control.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting blood glucose was significantly lower in the Levemir group compared to the insulin NPH group at weeks 24 and 36 of gestation.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting blood glucose is a metric used to assess glycemic control, reflecting baseline glucose levels before meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
