<node id="Blood Glucose Level">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Level</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose Level refers to the concentration of glucose in the bloodstream, a critical physiological measurement commonly discussed by patients in terms of "sugar" levels, such as "the sugar went up" or "the sugar went down." It is a key metric in diabetes care, used to assess metabolic status, monitor therapy effectiveness, and detect conditions such as hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia. Typically measured in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL), blood glucose levels below 70 mg/dL are clinically recognized as indicative of hypoglycemia, necessitating prompt intervention.

This measurement plays a central role in the management of diabetes, guiding both immediate and long-term treatment decisions. Blood Glucose Level is used to determine the appropriate dosage of insulin, including bolus insulin administered around meals, and to make corrections to basal insulin patterns. As a quantifiable value—such as 124 mg/dL—it serves as direct input for insulin dosage calculations and bolus advisor systems, supporting precise metabolic control. The term is sometimes abbreviated as GS in clinical or technological contexts, particularly in systems involving automated insulin delivery or diabetes management software.

Regular monitoring of Blood Glucose Level enables individuals and healthcare providers to evaluate the effectiveness of diabetes therapy, adjust treatment plans, and maintain glucose concentrations within a target range. By integrating real-time data, this measurement supports proactive management of insulin therapy and helps prevent acute and chronic complications associated with unstable glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4ac915c4a6b6d9a29fe84cb65e45af82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be43b1b23852278983f60d0f150b0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97d9a9de5f40419555bf7bf36cc9f84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bfad6c7b0e936c6a9c113798a2d963e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0f18d3b5098557dfd71a1955adc3a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5cace75be2ca46efd8033523e47b6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb7ffc723b939ad50f1b00ca6ec8b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b299154da4c58d8322b7ac4e3af2f5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-402361ced0649a06619dcaf93b0eb651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708653</data>
