</node>
<node id="Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Monitoring is the process of measuring and tracking blood glucose levels over time, a critical practice for managing diabetes and guiding appropriate treatment decisions. It involves the frequent assessment of blood sugar levels using various methods, including capillary blood samples obtained through fingerstick tests with a glucose meter and test strips, as well as continuous monitoring via interstitial glucose sensors. These sensor systems provide real-time data and trends, enabling more precise management of insulin therapy and facilitating timely adjustments in treatment.

The practice of Glucose Monitoring is essential for individuals using insulin, particularly those on insulin pump therapy, as it informs dosage decisions and helps prevent both hyperglycemia and hypoglycemia. It is especially important when changing insulin injection sites or after disruptions in insulin delivery, such as a pump disconnection, during which users are advised to monitor glucose levels for at least four hours to detect potential delivery issues. Integration with advanced diabetes technologies, such as the MiniMed 670G system, allows Glucose Monitoring to support automated insulin adjustments through features like SmartGuard, which relies on continuous sensor glucose data to modulate insulin delivery.

Overall, Glucose Monitoring serves as a foundational component of modern diabetes care, combining traditional capillary testing with sensor-based tracking to provide comprehensive insights into glucose patterns. This enables personalized and responsive management of insulin therapy, improving both safety and efficacy in diabetes treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69f89cc6358f0fe2b490d63a60ae0581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f14c91b2fb52c8fcc6d43aa4f53f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4aefb790519642667af4aaebc974bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a8417d6099b09e6129d10f9827b5a35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Glucose Monitoring</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Analog">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Analog</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin analog can be mixed with intermediate-acting insulin in the same syringe for immediate use, but improper handling may lead to loss of stability and altered therapeutic effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin analog is a modified form of insulin designed to act quickly, used in diabetes management for faster glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin analog is a modified form of insulin, often rapid-acting, used in clinical practice to meet individual patient needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin analog is a modified form of insulin with altered pharmacokinetic properties, differing from human insulin in species classification for therapeutic use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Analog</data>
</node>
<node id="Patient Education">
  <data key="d0">Patient Education</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Patient education involves teaching patients and caregivers about proper insulin use, storage, and injection techniques to ensure safety and efficacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Patient education involves teaching patients, families, or caregivers to repeat insulin preparation and administration techniques to assess learning and ensure safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Patient Education</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Reservoir">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Reservoir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Insulin Reservoir is a critical component of insulin pump systems, serving as a container that stores the insulin supply prior to delivery into the body. It is commonly integrated into devices such as the MiniMed™ insulin pump and functions as a holding chamber from which insulin is dispensed in controlled amounts. Typically filled using an insulin pen or vial, the reservoir ensures a continuous and adjustable supply of insulin, supporting automated or on-demand delivery as part of diabetes management therapy.

This reservoir must be routinely monitored and maintained to ensure effective insulin delivery. It is designed to be replaced during regular maintenance, therapy adjustments, or when the insulin supply runs low. In addition to scheduled replacements, the reservoir should be changed when troubleshooting issues such as persistent high blood glucose levels, elevated ketones, or suspected problems with insulin delivery. These proactive changes help mitigate risks associated with ineffective dosing, such as hyperglycemia or insulin degradation.

The insulin reservoir plays a vital role in the reliability and functionality of insulin pumps. Its proper operation is essential for consistent therapy, and replacement is recommended not only when empty but also when delivery problems are suspected. By enabling repeated and precise dosing, the insulin reservoir supports the overall efficacy of insulin pump treatment regimens for individuals managing diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The insulin reservoir is a part of the infusion pump that stores the insulin before delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0270c70980e605771c5d1e6b4de949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc46b3924459ec23a123df1dad4bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Reservoir</data>
</node>
