<node id="Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus is a specific form of diabetes requiring insulin therapy, for which clinical protocols and specific insulins are provided by the Unified Health System.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 is an autoimmune condition requiring insulin therapy, for which Levemir has established efficacy and safety data.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes mellitus tipo 1 is a chronic condition where prolonged hyperglycemia can lead to diabetic ketoacidosis due to insufficient insulin production.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes mellitus tipo 1 is a chronic condition where the body produces little or no insulin, increasing the risk of hyperglycemia and diabetic ketoacidosis.</data>
