<node id="Ministério Da Saúde">
  <data key="d0">Ministério Da Saúde</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Ministério da Saúde is the Brazilian federal ministry responsible for overseeing public health policies and serving as the national health authority with regulatory oversight over drug information and labeling. It plays a central role in the approval, regulation, and dissemination of professional health bulletins and drug-related materials, ensuring that accurate and standardized information is available to healthcare professionals and the public. As the governing body for public health in Brazil, Ministério da Saúde is tasked with formulating and implementing health policies that address the needs of the population, including the regulation of pharmaceutical products.

The ministry is specifically responsible for the approval and regulation of professional drug information, including the bula (package insert or leaflet) for medications such as Novolin® R and its delivery device, the Novolin® R FlexPen®. This includes overseeing the content of professional labeling to ensure it meets national health standards and provides essential clinical and safety information. All professional health bulletins and drug information materials related to Novolin® R distributed in Brazil must be authorized by Ministério da Saúde, reflecting its authority in maintaining the integrity and reliability of medical product information. Through these functions, Ministério da Saúde ensures that healthcare providers have access to up-to-date, accurate, and officially sanctioned drug information, supporting safe and effective medical practice across the country.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b93b5769e8df2e4aa6c2c1dc9e65fd85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ae5fe50adf25db0be3b8cdde6282e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Ministério Da Saúde</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Pump Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pump Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Pump Therapy is a method of diabetes management that delivers insulin continuously through a portable pump device, designed to regulate blood glucose levels in individuals with type 1 and type 2 diabetes. The therapy mimics the natural function of the pancreas by providing a steady infusion of rapid-acting insulin, known as basal insulin, while also allowing for adjustable bolus doses to account for meals, carbohydrate intake, and physical activity. This approach enables precise control over insulin delivery, offering improved glycemic control compared to traditional injection methods.

The insulin pump is typically a small, wearable device, such as the MiniMed™ 640G, which administers insulin subcutaneously through a catheter. Users can customize basal rates and deliver bolus doses based on real-time glucose monitoring, often in conjunction with continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems for enhanced accuracy and responsiveness. This integration supports proactive management of glucose fluctuations and reduces the risk of severe hypoglycemia, although careful calibration, ongoing monitoring, and attention to carbohydrate intake are essential to prevent complications.

Insulin Pump Therapy is valued not only for its clinical benefits but also for the lifestyle flexibility it provides. It allows individuals greater freedom in meal timing and physical activity while maintaining tight glucose control. The therapy requires user engagement and education to manage settings effectively, but it remains a preferred option for many due to its comfort, precision, and adaptability in daily diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ca77ae5b015fee5d1a21879c1a2b444&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d34031cb8a1d125e7f615c71a7c56df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f14c91b2fb52c8fcc6d43aa4f53f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03aab2b6261ddc73d474d0c866e7b37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b7bb277d16feead8d082fc004d51d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5cace75be2ca46efd8033523e47b6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eab57247c382bad8d5f1e5eb84a62e24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b</data>
