<node id="Thiazolidinediones">
  <data key="d0">Thiazolidinediones</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Thiazolidinediones are a class of antidiabetic drugs that, when combined with insulin, have been associated with cases of congestive heart failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones are a class of antidiabetic drugs that may cause congestive heart failure when used in combination with insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones are medications that, when combined with insulin, have been associated with reported cases of congestive heart failure, especially in patients with risk factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones are oral antidiabetic drugs that, when combined with insulin, may increase the risk of congestive heart failure and can either increase or decrease insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones are medications that, when combined with insulin, have been associated with cases of congestive heart failure, especially in at-risk patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones are a class of antidiabetic drugs that, when combined with insulin, may increase the risk of congestive heart failure.</data>
