<node id="Insulin Sensitivity">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Sensitivity is a parameter used in diabetes management, particularly within insulin dosing systems such as the Bolus Wizard, to quantify the body's response to insulin. It is defined as the amount by which blood glucose levels decrease per unit of insulin administered. This measure plays a critical role in calculating the appropriate insulin dosage, especially for mealtime or correction boluses, ensuring that blood glucose levels are managed effectively.

The value of Insulin Sensitivity is typically user-defined, based on individual physiological response and clinical guidance, and reflects how responsive a person's body is to insulin. It is commonly expressed in milligrams per deciliter per unit (mg/dL per unit) of insulin and is used in automated bolus calculations to determine the precise insulin dose needed to correct elevated blood glucose levels. As a key input in systems like the Bolus Wizard, Insulin Sensitivity helps personalize diabetes therapy by tailoring insulin delivery to individual metabolic needs.

Across various descriptions, Insulin Sensivity is consistently described as a setting that indicates the drop in blood glucose per unit of insulin, underscoring its functional importance in both manual and device-assisted insulin dosing. While minor variations in phrasing exist, all sources agree on its core definition and application in bolus calculations for diabetes care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-560db599319a34f19671d0bafeda5775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97d9a9de5f40419555bf7bf36cc9f84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b299154da4c58d8322b7ac4e3af2f5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc77598dbeb5980c719d1d54a6c3ab77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0deeba398b22b91d8da1b31653eede4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f608f07eae4ddd5409aed9d4ecef75ad</data>
