<node id="Insulin Infusion Pump">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Infusion Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The insulin infusion pump is a medical device designed for continuous subcutaneous insulin delivery, functioning as an external insulin delivery system to help manage blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes. Typically about the size of a pager and weighing between 80 to 100 grams, the device is a mechanical system with electronic controls that allows for precise insulin administration. It operates by delivering basal insulin at a steady rate throughout the day to mimic the natural, low-level insulin secretion seen in non-diabetic individuals, while also enabling users to administer bolus doses at mealtimes to manage postprandial glucose spikes.

The insulin infusion pump is classified as a Class 4 medical device and is part of advanced systems such as the Accu-Chek Solo Micropump System. Its primary function is to provide a more physiologic insulin delivery pattern compared to multiple daily injections, improving glycemic control for certain patients. However, not all insulin formulations are compatible with this device. Specifically, Novolin® R—whether in FlexPen® or Penfill® form—must not be used with insulin infusion pumps due to the risk of precipitation within the pump’s catheters, which can obstruct insulin flow and compromise therapy. Similarly, Levemir (insulin detemir) is not recommended for administration via insulin infusion pumps. These incompatibilities highlight the importance of using only pump-approved insulin formulations to ensure safety and efficacy in continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e74309cb16c52bec3be6426cd46e8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636a6ab7d0bef06e011ae7bf2140d2e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c</data>
