  <data key="d5">1778708570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">SmartGuard Technology</data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion is a method of insulin delivery via pump, used in the management of type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eab57247c382bad8d5f1e5eb84a62e24</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710142</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion</data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Set">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Set</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">The Infusion Set is a medical device component used to deliver insulin from an insulin pump, specifically models such as the MiniMed™ and MiniMed 780G system, to the body. It serves as a critical link between the pump’s reservoir and the patient, consisting of tubing, a cannula or needle, connectors, and an adhesive patch that secures the device to the skin. Some infusion sets, such as Quick-Set®, Silhouette®, and Mio®, are designed to remain in place during MRI procedures, distinguishing them from traditional needle-based systems. The device enables subcutaneous insulin delivery and is not intended for intravenous use or infusion of blood products.

The Infusion Set must be regularly monitored and maintained to ensure effective insulin delivery. Users are advised to check for dislodgement, leaks, blockages, cracks, or other damage, as these issues can disrupt insulin flow and lead to elevated blood glucose levels. Alarms on the pump may indicate delivery problems, and persistent alarms or failure of a correction bolus to produce expected results are signals for inspection or replacement. The set must also be replaced if ketone bodies are present, if there is suspected insulin delivery failure, or if liquid blocks the tubing connector.

As a single-use device, the Infusion Set requires periodic replacement, typically every up to three days, in accordance with labeled usage duration guidelines. It should be changed routinely, when beginning a new reservoir setup, or when adjusting therapy. Replacement is also necessary during software updates, as the set must be disconnected and then reconnected following specific instructions, or if the pump itself fails. Proper cannula filling after insertion is essential for effective operation. Risks associated with use include occlusions, infection, and skin irritation, underscoring the importance of proper handling and timely replacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc61f77b003d0086bd985ddb94fc2a98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
