<node id="Severe Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Severe Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Severe hypoglycemia is a serious and potentially life-threatening condition characterized by dangerously low blood glucose levels that impair an individual's ability to self-treat, necessitating assistance from another person for recovery. It is a critical complication commonly associated with insulin therapy, including treatments such as Levemir, and affects approximately 6% of patients using this medication. The condition constitutes a medical emergency, requiring immediate intervention to prevent severe outcomes.

Symptoms of severe hypoglycemia include disorientation, confusion, seizures, loss of consciousness, and, in extreme cases, death if not promptly addressed. Cognitive and physical functions are significantly impaired, rendering the affected person unable to recognize or manage their low blood glucose independently. This incapacitation underscores the necessity for external help, often involving the administration of glucagon or intravenous glucose to restore normal blood sugar levels.

Due to its acute nature, severe hypoglycemia demands urgent medical attention and consultation with a healthcare professional when suspected. Without timely treatment, the condition can lead to irreversible neurological damage or fatality. Emergency interventions are critical to reversing the effects and stabilizing the patient, highlighting the importance of awareness, preparedness, and rapid response in both clinical and home settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5cace75be2ca46efd8033523e47b6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
