<node id="Medtronic">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Medtronic is a global medical technology company that specializes in the development, manufacturing, and distribution of advanced medical devices, with a significant focus on diabetes management solutions. The company is best known for its MiniMed line of insulin pump systems, including the MiniMed 670G, MiniMed 770G, and MiniMed 780G, which are designed to automate insulin delivery and improve glycemic control for individuals with diabetes. Medtronic manufactures not only the insulin pumps but also compatible components such as infusion sets and insulin reservoirs, including a 3.0 mL reservoir, ensuring seamless integration within its ecosystem of diabetes care products.

In addition to hardware, Medtronic provides comprehensive support systems and digital tools for diabetes therapy. The company develops and maintains the CareLink® Personal program and CareLink systems, which enable users and healthcare providers to analyze therapy data and optimize treatment plans. Medtronic also offers the Bolus Wizard® feature—a trademarked technology that calculates insulin dosage based on real-time inputs such as blood glucose levels and carbohydrate intake. These technologies are supported by software and mobile applications, with compatibility information and technical specifications made available through official Medtronic websites and local representatives.

Medtronic is the parent company of Medtronic MiniMed, Inc., and holds multiple trademarks related to its products, including MiniMed™, Bolus Wizard®, and CareLink®. The company actively publishes educational materials, such as the "Pumping Protocol" guide, which provides structured approaches to initiating insulin pump therapy, and explicitly states that while it compiles and disseminates information on insulin pump therapy, it does not assume liability for damages arising from its use. To support patients globally, Medtronic offers technical support, training resources, and a travel loan program that provides temporary insulin pump access for users traveling abroad.

Furthermore, Medtronic manufactures continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems that integrate with its insulin pumps to enable advanced hybrid closed-loop functionalities. The company emphasizes authorized device compatibility, specifying which sensors and software can be used with its systems to ensure safety and performance. Medtronic also manages customer support, incident reporting, and recycling programs for its devices, reinforcing its role as a full-service provider in the diabetes care landscape. Through innovation, education, and patient support, Medtronic remains a leading force in medical technology, particularly in the field of insulin delivery and diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic is a medical technology company that developed the Guardian Real-Time continuous glucose monitoring system.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic is a medical technology company that developed the Medtronic MiniMed continuous glucose monitoring system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-641adeabab10205d29d07a0c3e82f2e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97d9a9de5f40419555bf7bf36cc9f84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7468847533eb17ed84cb659bebb72483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fac8b3f8df4c710a4e2c9640b886b16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191c82775d35bbc705205ed493c43c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec9910e322fb247c0bf85c8b8cb3e948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84d2aca165fc0184360972207bae8c6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d34031cb8a1d125e7f615c71a7c56df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b7bb277d16feead8d082fc004d51d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb7ffc723b939ad50f1b00ca6ec8b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8af713fd3913ed050d96cdd321bca3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eab57247c382bad8d5f1e5eb84a62e24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a8417d6099b09e6129d10f9827b5a35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709307</data>
