  <data key="d7">Medtronic</data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a metabolic disorder where the body resists insulin or doesn't produce enough, managed with medications including Levemir in combination therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a metabolic disorder characterized by insulin resistance, treated with oral agents and insulin, including Levemir in adolescents and adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710107</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2</data>
</node>
<node id="CareLink">
  <data key="d0">CareLink</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CareLink is a trademarked data management system designed for the transfer, synchronization, and analysis of medical data from insulin pumps and glucose monitoring devices, particularly within Medtronic’s MiniMed product line. It functions as a connectivity feature that enables seamless data exchange between insulin delivery devices—such as the MiniMed 670G system—and external software platforms or mobile applications, including the MiniMed Mobile App. This integration supports comprehensive diabetes management by allowing users and healthcare providers to monitor trends, review therapy patterns, and make informed treatment decisions.

The system serves both personal and clinical purposes, offering tools for individuals to manage their diabetes data at home and for healthcare professionals to access detailed reports prior to medical consultations. CareLink supports the uploading and secure storage of pump settings, ensuring that critical configuration data is preserved in case of device malfunctions or power failures. It is commonly used in conjunction with training programs to ensure proper utilization and data interpretation.

CareLink operates as a software program accessible through dedicated platforms, facilitating the review of insulin delivery, glucose levels, and device performance over time. It can be paired with a patient’s device ecosystem to provide continuous data management and connectivity, enhancing treatment accuracy and patient safety. By centralizing data from multiple diabetes management devices, CareLink streamlines record-keeping and supports proactive, data-driven healthcare interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-63644bff2af5cc96a50e636bff8e339b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec9910e322fb247c0bf85c8b8cb3e948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4aefb790519642667af4aaebc974bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708643</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">CareLink</data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Calculation">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Calculation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus calculation is the process of determining the correct insulin dose needed to cover carbohydrate intake or correct high blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus calculation is the process of determining the correct insulin dose based on glucose levels, carbohydrate intake, and trend information.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus calculation is a function of the Diabetes Manager Accu-Chek Solo that provides recommendations for correction or mealtime insulin doses.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Calculation is the process of determining the required insulin dose using inputs like blood glucose and carbohydrate values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5fdff66ffcd1f4d4e10a8825e7905c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/IFU Accu-Chek Guide Solo Diabetes Manager.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Bolus Calculation</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin bolus refers to rapid-acting insulin administered to control blood glucose levels after meals, used in combination with basal insulin like Levemir in a basal-bolus regimen.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin bolus is a dose of insulin administered to manage blood glucose levels, either for meals, corrections, or both.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin bolus is a dose of insulin delivered to manage blood glucose, particularly around meals, and must be timed correctly with food intake.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin bolus refers to a dose of insulin delivered to manage blood glucose levels, particularly around meals or for correction.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin bolus is a dose of insulin delivered to manage blood glucose levels, particularly around meals or to correct high glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin bolus is a dose of insulin administered to cover carbohydrate intake or correct high glucose levels, delivered via the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Bolus refers to a manual or preset dose of insulin delivered to manage blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0f18d3b5098557dfd71a1955adc3a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b7bb277d16feead8d082fc004d51d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88cdb970e2c2f1aaaab96fdc11b589f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708581</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Bolus</data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Site">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Site</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion site is the location on the body where the insulin infusion set is inserted and through which insulin is delivered.&lt;SEP&gt;The infusion site is the location on the body where the insulin pump delivers insulin and should be checked for irritation, redness, or swelling.&lt;SEP&gt;The infusion site is the location on the body where the pump delivers insulin; placing the pump more than 14 inches above it may cause over-delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The location on the body where the infusion set is inserted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708582</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Infusion Site</data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus refers to a dose of insulin administered to manage blood glucose levels, particularly in response to meals or elevated glucose readings. It is commonly used to cover carbohydrate intake during eating or to correct high blood sugar levels, and can be delivered via an insulin pump, syringe, or other injection methods. In the context of insulin pump therapy, bolus is a menu option accessible through the device interface, allowing users to manually input and deliver a calculated dose based on their carbohydrate consumption or current glucose levels.

Bolus doses can be delivered in various forms, including standard, extended, dual, or correction types, depending on the individual’s needs and the features of their insulin delivery system. Some advanced systems, such as those with SmartGuard technology, can automatically deliver correction boluses based on real-time glucose monitoring. The duration of a bolus’s insulin action is clinically significant and must be considered when making therapy adjustments to avoid hypoglycemia or overlapping doses.

Bolus delivery via an insulin pump can be interrupted by events such as battery removal or system errors; however, many systems allow the bolus to be resumed within a short timeframe, typically up to ten minutes. The calculation of a bolus dose is often based on personal insulin-to-carbohydrate ratios, insulin sensitivity factors, and current glucose readings, with displayed values on devices serving as illustrative guides. Bolus administration can be either manual or programmed, and users are typically trained to understand the different types and proper usage for effective diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus refers to the insulin dose delivered before meals to manage postprandial glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-63644bff2af5cc96a50e636bff8e339b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edf22db77193377cf626b08881757226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191c82775d35bbc705205ed493c43c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1064c42775365801d8ca4df533dcda0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b56844dd3520b94bbf5737a044bec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b83b1b837df0b960758dfd02d42d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d74e338f7a37de66d4b2268a49021c4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4aefb790519642667af4aaebc974bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Bolus</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Basal">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin basal refers to long-acting insulin used to maintain baseline insulin levels in diabetic patients, including Levemir.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin basal refers to the small, continuous production of insulin by the pancreas that maintains stable glucose levels between meals and during sleep.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Basal</data>
</node>
<node id="Table 4">
  <data key="d0">Table 4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 4 presents the intraindividual variability of the time-action profiles of insulin detemir, NPH insulin, and insulin glargine, showing lower variance for insulin detemir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
