<node id="Insulin Detemir">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Detemir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin detemir is a long-acting basal insulin analog used for the management of diabetes mellitus, including both type 1 and type 2 diabetes, in patients such as adults, adolescents, and children aged 1 year and older. It is produced using recombinant DNA technology and functions as a modified form of human insulin designed to provide prolonged glycemic control. Marketed under the brand name Levemir, insulin detemir serves as the active pharmaceutical ingredient in this formulation and is valued for its stable, extended pharmacokinetic profile, which supports once- or twice-daily dosing to maintain basal insulin levels.

Compared to other basal insulins such as NPH insulin and insulin glargine, insulin detemir exhibits a more prolonged and less variable action, contributing to improved predictability in blood glucose control and potentially reducing the risk of hypoglycemia. Its mechanism involves structural modifications that reduce its affinity for both insulin and insulin-like growth factor-1 (IGF-1) receptors relative to human insulin, which may influence its metabolic and mitogenic activity. These properties make it a suitable option for diverse patient populations, including pediatric, pregnant, and elderly individuals, although careful dose individualization and monitoring are recommended, particularly in those with renal or hepatic impairment.

Insulin detemir must not be mixed with solutions containing thiols or sulfides, as these substances can lead to its degradation and compromise therapeutic efficacy. Clinical studies have evaluated its pharmacodynamic and pharmacokinetic characteristics, confirming its safety and effectiveness across various age groups and clinical settings. Overall, insulin detemir represents a key therapeutic option in modern diabetes care, offering reliable basal insulin coverage with a favorable safety and consistency profile.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44f60a4106da6d70fe72d17aa2728296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975d0ad130a42cf2fe8a0f91e4da2b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c23215af0c479dce9c09bed4cc782d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5561a191d3b525d406e49933648e27bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709086</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Detemir</data>
</node>
