<node id="Meal Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Meal Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Meal bolus refers to an insulin dose administered to cover carbohydrates consumed during a meal, calculated using features like Bolus Wizard.&lt;SEP&gt;A meal bolus is an insulin dose calculated based on the amount of carbohydrates to be consumed and the individual's insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;A meal bolus is an insulin dose administered to cover the rise in blood glucose from consuming carbohydrates in food or drinks.&lt;SEP&gt;A Meal Bolus is an insulin dose given to cover carbohydrates consumed during a meal, calculated using blood glucose values when interfering medications are used.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec9910e322fb247c0bf85c8b8cb3e948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0f18d3b5098557dfd71a1955adc3a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb7ffc723b939ad50f1b00ca6ec8b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
