<node id="Hipoglicemia Noturna">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglicemia Noturna</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglicemia noturna é uma condição de baixa glicose durante o sono, detectável por meio de monitoramento contínuo.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia noturna refers to low blood glucose levels during the night, with Levemir showing a significantly reduced risk compared to NPH insulin, especially in type 1 diabetes patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia Noturna refers to low blood glucose levels during the night, a risk reduced with Levemir compared to NPH insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia Noturna refers to episodes of low blood sugar during the night, which were less frequent with Levemir compared to NPH insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
