<node id="Injection Site Reactions">
  <data key="d0">Injection Site Reactions</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection site reactions include pain, redness, urticaria, inflammation, bruising, edema, and itching, which may occur during insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection site reactions such as pain, redness, itching, inflammation, bruising, edema, and urticaria may occur and can be mitigated by rotating injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection site reactions include pain, redness, itching, inflammation, bruising, edema, and urticaria, which may resolve over time or require treatment discontinuation.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection site reactions such as pain, redness, itching, inflammation, bruising, edema, and urticaria are uncommon and usually transient.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection site reactions include pain, redness, itching, inflammation, bruising, swelling, and hives, and are usually temporary.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection site reactions are potential adverse effects of Novolin® R, including pain, redness, itching, inflammation, bruising, edema, and urticaria, which can be minimized by rotating injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection site reactions include pain, redness, itching, inflammation, bruising, swelling, and urticaria, which are generally transient and occur during insulin therapy.</data>
