<node id="Insulin Infusion">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Infusion</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Infusion is the process of delivering insulin into the body via a pump, which can be manually suspended or adjusted according to user needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin infusion is the continuous delivery of insulin via a pump, which can be suspended by the Autoapagado function in case of inactivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin infusion is the continuous delivery of insulin via a pump system, which can be manually or automatically suspended based on glucose trends.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Infusion is the delivery of insulin into the body via a pump, which can be miscalculated if incorrect Bolus Wizard settings are used.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Infusion is the process of delivering insulin into the body using a pump, which can be suspended or adjusted based on medical needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Infusion refers to the continuous delivery of insulin via a pump, which can be suspended by the Autoapagado function if no user input is detected.&gt;</data>
