<node id="Glucose Trend Arrows">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Trend Arrows</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose trend arrows (up, flat, down) show whether glucose levels are rising, stable, or falling, helping in proactive diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose trend arrows indicate the direction and speed of glucose level changes, such as increasing or decreasing, on the insulin pump display.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose Trend Arrows are on-screen indicators showing the direction and rate of change of glucose levels, used to adjust bolus doses accordingly.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose trend arrows are visual indicators on a glucose monitoring system that show the direction and speed of glucose level changes.</data>
