<node id="Diabetes Tipo 1">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Tipo 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes tipo 1 é uma condição autoimune caracterizada pela falta de produção de insulina, exigindo controle rigoroso, especialmente em crianças, adolescentes e mulheres grávidas.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Tipo 1 is a chronic metabolic condition in which the pancreas produces little or no insulin, requiring external insulin administration, especially during pregnancy.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes tipo 1 is a chronic condition where the pancreas produces little or no insulin, requiring exogenous insulin therapy such as Levemir®.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Tipo 1 is a chronic condition characterized by the body's inability to produce insulin, requiring insulin therapy such as basal-bolus regimens.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba8a91b916675f6f4ef560f6976957e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133</data>
