  <data key="d5">1778710049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Diabetes Tipo 1</data>
</node>
<node id="Dexcom G6">
  <data key="d0">Dexcom G6</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d2">Dexcom G6 is a glucose sensor system approved for use in insulin dosing decisions without requiring finger-prick confirmation, particularly in the US.&lt;SEP&gt;The Dexcom G6 is a real-time continuous glucose monitoring system that does not require capillary glucose calibration, transmits data wirelessly every 5 minutes, and allows data sharing with up to five people via a smartphone app.</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Dexcom G6</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Meter">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Meter</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">A Blood Glucose Meter is a medical device designed to measure actual blood glucose levels by analyzing a small blood sample, typically obtained through a fingerstick. It serves as a critical tool for individuals managing diabetes, particularly those using insulin therapy or continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems. The device provides direct, manual measurement of blood glucose, which is essential for calibration, verification, and treatment decision-making.

The Blood Glucose Meter is frequently used to confirm glucose readings when CGM sensor values are inconsistent with physical symptoms, especially during the first 12 hours after a new sensor is inserted. It is also employed when sensor accuracy may be compromised, such as in the presence of interfering medications like acetaminophen or paracetamol, which can skew sensor data. In such cases, the blood glucose meter offers more reliable and accurate measurements, particularly at lower glucose thresholds where precision is vital.

This device plays a key role in integrated insulin delivery systems, such as the MiniMed 780G pump, where it is used to manually enter blood glucose readings when pump integration is unavailable or after changes to the infusion set or insulin reservoir. As an ISO 15197:2013 compliant device, it ensures standardized accuracy and reliability in glucose measurement. The Blood Glucose Meter is required for entering verified glucose values into insulin pumps, supporting proper calibration and safe, data-driven insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f2cf8a591a83e4436ab6a76c2d30e2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d536bf636b4a29c1f9f46de648b2b306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709135</data>
