<node id="Carbohydrates">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrates</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrates, measured in grams, are used in insulin calculations, with examples including 41 grams and 63 grams.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrates are the main dietary source of glucose, found in sugars and starches, and are metabolized during digestion to provide energy.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrates are a macronutrient that directly affects blood glucose levels and determines bolus insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrates are a key nutrient that affects blood glucose levels and require insulin for proper management, especially when consumed alone or with fats and proteins.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrates, specifically 20 to 30 grams, are used to treat low glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrates are nutrients that cause a rise in glucose levels after consumption, requiring insulin coverage via a food bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrates are nutrients used to raise blood glucose levels during hypoglycemia, especially fast-acting types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-69f89cc6358f0fe2b490d63a60ae0581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
