  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ambulatory Glucose Profile (AGP) is a standardized software system used for statistical analysis and reporting of continuous glucose monitoring data, providing metrics such as time in range, average glucose, hyperglycemia and hypoglycemia periods, sensor usage time, and estimated HbA1c.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ambulatory Glucose Profile is a clinical report derived from continuous glucose monitoring, showing glucose trends over time.</data>
