<node id="Temporary Basal Rate">
  <data key="d0">Temporary Basal Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Temporary Basal Rate is a feature in insulin pump therapy that enables users to adjust basal insulin delivery for a defined period, typically to accommodate changing physiological needs. This function allows for temporary modifications either as a percentage of the current basal rate or as a specific insulin delivery value, providing flexibility in diabetes management. The adjustment is programmed by the user and remains active for a specified duration before automatically reverting to the original basal rate.

This feature is commonly used during situations that affect glucose metabolism, such as physical activity, illness, or other transient conditions. By reducing basal insulin delivery, particularly during exercise, the temporary basal rate helps prevent hypoglycemia—low blood glucose levels—making it a critical tool for maintaining glucose stability. It is supported by various insulin pump models, including the MiniMed 670G, and is designed to offer precise, short-term control over insulin infusion rates.

Overall, the temporary basal rate serves as a configurable and user-programmable setting that enhances the adaptability of insulin pump therapy. It allows individuals with diabetes to tailor insulin delivery to their immediate needs, improving glycemic control and safety in dynamic daily scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feedb8da72881894bf4c6529f7baca60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8190aff898356450e3514b751c9193c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a8417d6099b09e6129d10f9827b5a35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709101</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Temporary Basal Rate</data>
</node>
<node id="Extended Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Extended Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An extended bolus is a bolus type that delivers insulin over a period of time, useful for meals high in fats and proteins that digest slowly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709042</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Extended Bolus</data>
</node>
<node id="Square Wave Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Square Wave Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Square Wave Bolus is an insulin delivery method designed to manage glucose levels by spreading a bolus dose evenly over a predetermined period, typically ranging from 30 minutes to 8 hours. This delivery pattern is particularly useful for meals with slow digestion or delayed glucose absorption, such as high-fat or high-fiber foods, as well as for situations involving extended snacking. By administering insulin gradually, the Square Wave Bolus better matches the body's insulin needs during prolonged food absorption, helping to prevent postprandial hyperglycemia or hypoglycemia.

The duration of the Square Wave Bolus can be customized using a Duration setting, allowing users to select the time period over which the insulin is delivered. It is available through either the Bolus Wizard or Manual bolus feature on compatible insulin pumps, though it is only accessible in Manual mode. The function requires the Square Wave bolus feature to be enabled on the device. As an extended bolus type, it is also referred to as an extended insulin dose delivery pattern, distinguishing it from standard immediate boluses.

In certain pump systems, the Square Wave Bolus can be interrupted and resumed, but only if the interruption occurs within a specific window—typically ten minutes—allowing for flexibility in dosing. Overall, this insulin delivery mode provides a tailored approach to bolus insulin therapy, supporting improved glycemic control in individuals with variable meal digestion patterns or prolonged eating periods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d536bf636b4a29c1f9f46de648b2b306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654d7a203c4eab9f3a89f577edc2a5ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b0e9023a7c03c6a284d69e0930b8a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709108</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Square Wave Bolus</data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Wave Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Dual Wave Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual Wave Bolus is a type of insulin delivery method that combines an immediate bolus with an extended, square wave bolus to address both rapid and prolonged insulin needs. This combination bolus delivers a portion of the insulin dose immediately, similar to a normal bolus, while the remaining portion is administered gradually over a user-defined period as a square wave bolus. The Dual Wave Bolus is specifically designed to manage blood glucose levels effectively after consuming meals high in carbohydrates and fat, or meals with mixed nutrients that cause delayed glucose absorption.

The functionality requires the Dual Wave bolus feature to be enabled on the insulin pump and can be programmed using either the Bolus Wizard or the Manual bolus feature. It is available only in Manual mode and allows for flexibility in dosing strategies, such as combining mealtime insulin with correction doses for elevated blood glucose levels prior to eating. The extended component of the bolus can be interrupted and resumed under certain conditions, offering additional control in dynamic situations. Overall, the Dual Wave Bolus provides a tailored insulin delivery approach for complex meal scenarios and variable glucose patterns, enhancing glycemic management for individuals using insulin pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d536bf636b4a29c1f9f46de648b2b306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654d7a203c4eab9f3a89f577edc2a5ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Dual Wave Bolus</data>
</node>
