<node id="Acetaminophen">
  <data key="d0">Acetaminophen</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetaminophen, also known as paracetamol, can falsely elevate sensor glucose readings when used with glucose monitoring systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is a medication ingredient that can interfere with glucose sensor readings, causing falsely elevated values and potentially leading to insulin over-delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is a medication that can falsely elevate sensor glucose readings, leading to potential insulin over-delivery and hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is a medication that interferes with sensor glucose readings, requiring the use of blood glucose values for bolus calculations for up to eight hours after intake.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is an active ingredient in some medications, such as cold and fever remedies, that can falsely elevate sensor glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Acetaminophen</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydroxyurea">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyurea</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyurea, also known as hydroxycarbamide, causes higher sensor glucose readings compared to blood glucose, increasing hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyurea, also known as hydroxycarbamide, is a medication that causes inaccuracies in sensor glucose readings and should not be used during continuous glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyurea is a medication used to treat diseases such as cancer and sickle cell anemia, and its use affects glucose monitoring by increasing sensor glucose readings compared to blood glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709107</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Hydroxyurea</data>
</node>
