<node id="Insulin Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Delivery refers to the process of administering insulin into the body, primarily through the use of an insulin pump, which serves as the core mechanism for controlled and adjustable insulin administration. The pump enables precise delivery by allowing users to set and modify basal insulin rates, including fixed basal rates when sensor glucose (SG) data is unavailable, or automated basal rates when SG readings are accessible. These basal settings, along with temporary rate adjustments, allow for personalized insulin management tailored to individual metabolic needs and daily activities.

The system supports various bolus types to accommodate different meal and glucose management scenarios, including standard (normal), square wave, and dual wave boluses, offering flexibility in how insulin is delivered over time. Insulin delivery is closely integrated with glucose monitoring technologies, particularly in systems involving integrated continuous glucose monitoring (iCGM), such as iCGM 25, where delivery decisions can be informed by real-time glucose readings. Based on these readings, the pump can automatically suspend or resume insulin delivery, particularly in response to hypoglycemic trends or low glucose alerts, enhancing safety and glycemic control.

User-initiated actions and system alerts also play a critical role in managing insulin delivery, allowing for manual suspension or resumption of insulin flow. The pump tracks active insulin and daily insulin doses, contributing to informed dosing decisions and overall therapy management. However, insulin delivery can be interrupted by technical issues such as power loss, system errors, or component damage, which may result in over-delivery or under-delivery of insulin, posing clinical risks. Additionally, during self-tests, insulin delivery is temporarily suspended for up to two minutes, ensuring system integrity without prolonged interruption of therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8190aff898356450e3514b751c9193c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654d7a203c4eab9f3a89f577edc2a5ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709092</data>
