<node id="Continuous Glucose Monitoring System">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Glucose Monitoring System</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Continuous Glucose Monitoring System is a medical device used to monitor glucose levels in real time, particularly in pediatric type 1 diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;A continuous glucose monitoring system includes a sensor and transmitter to track glucose levels in real time.&lt;SEP&gt;The Continuous Glucose Monitoring System (SMCG) is a technological device that measures and records glucose levels in the interstitial fluid continuously, providing real-time data and trends.&lt;SEP&gt;The Continuous Glucose Monitoring System is a technology that provides real-time glucose data, enabling detailed assessment of glycemic patterns and variability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eab57247c382bad8d5f1e5eb84a62e24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
