<node id="Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicose is used to treat hypoglycemia, administered orally for mild episodes or intravenously by medical professionals for severe cases unresponsive to glucagon.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose is used to treat hypoglycemia, administered orally for mild episodes or intravenously by a healthcare professional for severe cases, especially if the patient does not respond to glucagon within 10 to 15 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose is used orally or intravenously to treat hypoglycemia; intravenous administration is required if the patient does not respond to glucagon within 10 to 15 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose is a simple sugar used to treat hypoglycemia, administered orally for mild cases or intravenously for severe cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose é um açúcar cujo transporte intracelular é estimulado pela insulina em tecidos como músculo e fígado, e cujos níveis no sangue são regulados por esse hormônio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709177</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Glicose</data>
</node>
