  <data key="d7">Storage</data>
</node>
<node id="Paracetamol">
  <data key="d0">Paracetamol</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Paracetamol, also known as acetaminophen, can falsely elevate sensor glucose readings and affect insulin dosing accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Paracetamol is a medication ingredient, equivalent to acetaminophen, that can falsely elevate sensor glucose readings and affect the accuracy of the SmartGuard system.&lt;SEP&gt;Paracetamol is a medication noted in the document, potentially affecting glucose readings, referenced on pages 158 and 197.&lt;SEP&gt;Paracetamol is an alternative name for acetaminophen and has the same effect of falsely raising sensor glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Paracetamol is an alternative name for acetaminophen and has the same effect on sensor glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Paracetamol is an alternative name for acetaminophen and can cause inaccuracies in sensor glucose readings when used during continuous glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Paracetamol</data>
</node>
<node id="Collection Point">
  <data key="d0">Collection Point</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A Collection Point is a designated facility such as a pharmacy, clinic, or hospital where patients can safely dispose of used medical waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Collection points located in pharmacies, drugstores, health centers, or hospitals accept used or expired medications and sharps containers for proper disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;Collection points, such as pharmacies, drugstores, health centers, or hospitals, have proper containers for disposing of used medications and sharps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709563</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Collection Point</data>
</node>
<node id="Storage Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Storage Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage conditions for Levemir require refrigeration between 2°C and 8°C before opening and room temperature below 30°C during use for up to 42 days.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage conditions for Novolin® R Penfill® include refrigeration between 2°C and 8°C before opening, protection from light and heat, and room temperature storage (15°C to 30°C) for up to 6 weeks after opening.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage conditions for Novolin® R FlexPen® require refrigeration between 2°C and 8°C to maintain medication stability and effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Humulin R must be stored refrigerated between 2°C and 8°C before opening; after opening, it can be kept at room temperature (15°C to 30°C) for up to 28 days, protected from heat and direct sunlight.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage conditions for the product and its packaging are specified on the outer packaging and in the user manual.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage conditions are the recommended environmental conditions for storing the Accu-Chek Solo system and its components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8430c8897032c30391e131ac6fd24f47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5fdff66ffcd1f4d4e10a8825e7905c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/IFU Accu-Chek Guide Solo Diabetes Manager.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709556</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Storage Conditions</data>
</node>
<node id="Profissionais De Saúde">
  <data key="d0">Profissionais De Saúde</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Profissionais de saúde devem promover o descarte correto de agulhas em caixas rígidas para segurança e sustentabilidade.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Profissionais De Saúde</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Testing">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Testing</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f2616cb245736f951a3dcbf261b3b9b</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental conditions such as temperature and altitude can affect the accuracy of blood glucose tests.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776645505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Altitudes">
  <data key="d0">High Altitudes</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f2616cb245736f951a3dcbf261b3b9b</data>
  <data key="d2">High altitudes (&gt;2000 m) may influence glucose readings, particularly in certain device types.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776645506</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
