  <data key="d2">Pharmacokinetic profile of Novolin® R in children (6–12 years) and adolescents (13–17 years) appears similar to adults, though differences in Cmax highlight the need for individual dose titration.&lt;SEP&gt;Children and adolescents with diabetes aged 6 to 17 years show pharmacokinetic profiles of Novolin® R similar to adults, though differences in Cmax exist.&lt;SEP&gt;Children and adolescents aged 6 to 17 years were studied in limited numbers to assess the pharmacokinetic profile of Novolin® R, which appears similar to adults but with noted differences in Cmax, requiring individualized dose titration.</data>
