  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Liraglutide is a GLP-1 receptor agonist used in combination with metformin and insulin detemir in the treatment of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Liraglutide is a GLP-1 receptor agonist used in combination with basal insulin to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Liraglutide is a GLP-1 receptor agonist used in type 2 diabetes treatment, often combined with basal insulin and metformin.&lt;SEP&gt;Liraglutide is a medication that, when co-administered with Levemir, shows no clinically relevant pharmacokinetic or pharmacodynamic interaction.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Liraglutide is a glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) receptor agonist used in the treatment of type 2 diabetes.</data>
