</node>
<node id="Fever">
  <data key="d0">Fever</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fever is a symptom that can trigger ketone production in people with diabetes and is a condition under which ketone testing is recommended.&lt;SEP&gt;Fever is a symptom that may trigger the need to test for ketones in individuals with diabetes, especially when accompanied by other signs of infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Fever increases insulin absorption due to elevated metabolic and circulatory activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Fever is a condition that increases insulin needs in diabetic patients and may complicate glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Fever</data>
</node>
<node id="Abdominal Pain">
  <data key="d0">Abdominal Pain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Abdominal pain is a symptom associated with potential diabetic ketoacidosis and is a recommended indicator for performing ketone tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696474</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Abdominal Pain</data>
</node>
<node id="Refil">
  <data key="d0">Refil</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Refil é um cartucho com 3 mL de insulina usado em canetas recarregáveis, devendo ser do mesmo fabricante da caneta para garantir aplicação correta da dose.&lt;SEP&gt;A 3 mL insulin cartridge used in a reusable insulin pen, which is replaced when empty.&lt;SEP&gt;The refil is a 3 mL cartridge containing Humulin R insulin, designed for use with reusable Lilly insulin pens.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699580</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Refil</data>
</node>
<node id="Heat">
  <data key="d0">Heat</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Heat from sources like hot baths, fever, or warm compresses increases insulin absorption and the risk of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat from sources like hot baths, fever, or warm compresses accelerates insulin absorption and increases hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Excessive heat is a condition that Novolin® R must be protected from to maintain its stability and effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Heat</data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacist">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacist</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A pharmacist provides guidance on the correct use of insulin pens, storage, and disposal, and assists in case of device malfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Pharmacist</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Cartridge">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Cartridge</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin cartridge, also known as a refill, contains 3 mL of insulin and is used in reusable insulin pens.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin cartridge is a 3ml container of insulin used in insulin pens, which must not be reused or mixed with other types of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696481</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Cartridge</data>
</node>
<node id="Exercise">
  <data key="d0">Exercise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exercise is a factor that increases insulin absorption and can lead to hypoglycemia if not managed properly.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise increases insulin absorption rate, potentially leading to hypoglycemia if not managed properly.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise is a physical activity that can influence blood glucose levels and requires careful monitoring when using insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise is a physical activity that can lower blood glucose levels and may require temporary reduction of basal insulin rate to prevent hypoglycemia in insulin pump users.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise can affect glucose levels and must be managed carefully during a rising glucose trend, depending on current glucose and ketone levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44b69a8e50a0a4230b6963fe643d8cd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702522</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Exercise</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dose Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The process of modifying insulin dosage based on blood glucose readings obtained from the glucometer.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dose adjustment refers to the process of modifying insulin dosage based on changes in weight, routine, diet, or health, under medical supervision.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dose adjustment is performed regularly by patients or family members in collaboration with the healthcare team based on glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dose adjustment may be required when switching insulin types, brands, or concentrations, or during physiological changes such as pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dose adjustment may be necessary during lactation, illness, or changes in medication that affect glucose metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dose adjustment is required during illness, exercise, travel across time zones, or changes in diet and activity levels, based on individual metabolic needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eb891fdc2320360f3af78eb373161d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulin Dose Adjustment</data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Administration">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous administration is a method of delivering medication, particularly insulin, into the fat layer located just beneath the skin, enabling gradual absorption into the bloodstream. This route is commonly used for insulin therapies, including insulin detemir, which is marketed under the brand name Levemir® FlexPen®. As a delivery mechanism, subcutaneous administration allows for controlled release of the drug, influencing its absorption rate, pharmacokinetics, and overall therapeutic effect. The plasma concentration of insulin delivered via this method typically peaks within 1.5 to 2.5 hours, with the terminal half-life largely determined by the rate at which the drug is absorbed from the subcutaneous tissue.

For Levemir, subcutaneous administration is the only approved and required route of delivery. Recommended injection sites include the abdominal wall, thigh, upper arm, deltoid, and gluteal region. To minimize complications such as lipodystrophy and cutaneous amyloidosis—conditions associated with repeated injections in the same area—it is essential to rotate injection sites regularly. The choice of subcutaneous administration for insulin and similar medications ensures predictable absorption patterns and sustained pharmacological activity, making it a critical component of effective diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous administration is the primary route for injecting Humulin R, with injection sites including arms, thighs, buttocks, and abdomen.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous administration of Humulin R is performed in the upper arms, thighs, buttocks, or abdomen, with site rotation recommended to prevent lipodystrophy and localized cutaneous amyloidosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975d0ad130a42cf2fe8a0f91e4da2b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699581</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Subcutaneous Administration</data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Administration">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous administration involves injecting insulin directly into a vein, used in emergency medical situations for immediate effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravenous administration of Levemir is contraindicated as it may cause severe hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R can be administered intravenously by healthcare professionals using infusion systems with specific insulin concentrations in sodium chloride 0.9% or dextrose solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravenous Administration refers to delivering Novolin® R directly into the bloodstream, which must be performed by healthcare professionals.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravenous administration of Novolin® R Penfill is a method restricted to healthcare professionals and used in clinical settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravenous administration of Novolin® R FlexPen® is permitted only for healthcare professionals using infusion systems with specific insulin concentrations and infusion fluids, and is stable for 24 hours at room temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R FlexPen® can also be administered intravenously under medical supervision.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698972</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Intravenous Administration</data>
</node>
<node id="Refeição">
  <data key="d0">Refeição</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A refeição é um fator contextual anotado com a medição de glicemia para avaliar seu impacto nos níveis de açúcar no sangue.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealtime is a critical factor in insulin administration timing, especially for rapid-acting analogs like insulin lispro.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Refeição</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Glargina">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Glargina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Glargina is a long-acting insulin that must not be mixed with any other insulin in the same syringe.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina glargina is a long-acting insulin analog used in diabetes treatment, with a distinct pharmacokinetic profile compared to Levemir® and NPH insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina glargina is a long-acting insulin analog used in the treatment of diabetes, with glycemic control comparable to Levemir but associated with greater weight gain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba8a91b916675f6f4ef560f6976957e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Insulina Glargina</data>
</node>
<node id="Pregnant Women">
  <data key="d0">Pregnant Women</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pregnant women are advised to use the subcutaneous fold technique for insulin injection as a safety measure.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnant women can use insulin in the abdomen during the first two trimesters with a 4 mm needle, prega, and 45° angle, but should avoid abdominal injections in the third trimester.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnant women require special considerations for insulin injection, particularly avoiding abdominal injections in the third trimester.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnant women who inject insulin in the abdomen should consult a doctor to adjust injection site and technique, avoiding abdominal injections in the third trimester.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnant women are advised to use the subcutaneous skin fold technique during insulin injection as a safety measure, even when using short needles.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnant women require special considerations during insulin injection, including the use of a subcutaneous pinch and a 45° needle angle, with avoidance of abdominal injections in the third trimester.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Pregnant Women</data>
</node>
<node id="Lantus">
  <data key="d0">Lantus</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">A brand of ultra-slow-acting insulin, stable for 30 days after opening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778697169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Lantus</data>
</node>
<node id="Farmacêutico">
  <data key="d0">Farmacêutico</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">O farmacêutico é o profissional responsável por orientar o uso correto dos medicamentos e registrar as entregas no e-SUS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Farmacêutico</data>
</node>
<node id="Paciente">
  <data key="d0">Paciente</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Paciente is an individual managing diabetes who seeks guidance on monitoring and managing blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Paciente é o indivíduo que recebe ensinamentos sobre a aplicação de insulina e deve repetir o procedimento para confirmar o entendimento.&lt;SEP&gt;O paciente é a pessoa com diabetes que recebe orientações, utiliza a caneta reutilizável e deve seguir as recomendações para descarte e reposição.&lt;SEP&gt;The patient experienced hypoglycemia after receiving insulin due to medication errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Paciente refers to individuals with diabetes who require insulin therapy and must monitor blood glucose levels to recognize and manage hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Paciente is the individual managing diabetes and following medical advice for insulin therapy and illness management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2dff1c37dd504c2e0f6d3e3541019e15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0de4d525c273cda4939a501eaecc6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84d2aca165fc0184360972207bae8c6b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Paciente</data>
</node>
<node id="Crianças">
  <data key="d0">Crianças</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Crianças are young individuals who, along with very thin adults and pregnant women, have specific insulin administration considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;Crianças são um grupo populacional para o qual o uso de HUMULIN R requer supervisão médica, especialmente aquelas menores de 3 anos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Crianças</data>
</node>
<node id="Atividade Física">
  <data key="d0">Atividade Física</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Atividade física accelerates insulin absorption, increasing the risk of hypoglycemia if injections are given in active body parts like legs before exercise.&lt;SEP&gt;Atividade física influencia a necessidade de insulina e a resposta glicêmica, podendo aumentar o risco de hipoglicemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A atividade física altera a sensibilidade à insulina e pode afetar a necessidade de dose e o risco de hipoglicemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709847</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Atividade Física</data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Injection">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous injection is the standard and recommended route for administering insulin, including various formulations such as Levemir® Penfill®, Novolin® R, and Novolin® R FlexPen®. This method involves delivering medication into the fatty tissue layer beneath the skin, ensuring controlled absorption and optimal pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic profiles. Proper technique is critical to effective delivery and includes considerations such as needle angle, use of a skin fold to avoid intramuscular injection, and adherence to product-specific instructions.

Common anatomical sites for subcutaneous injection include the abdominal wall, thigh, gluteal region, and deltoid area. The abdomen is frequently preferred due to its consistent and relatively faster absorption rates. To prevent complications such as lipohypertrophy or localized tissue damage, healthcare guidelines recommend regular rotation of injection sites among these approved areas. This practice is specifically advised for products like Novolin® R, whether administered via vial and syringe or pre-filled devices such as the FlexPen®.

Different insulin products share the same subcutaneous administration route but may have nuanced recommendations based on formulation and delivery device. For example, Novolin® R FlexPen® is optimally administered in the abdominal wall using a skin fold to ensure accurate placement in subcutaneous tissue and to minimize the risk of intramuscular delivery. Overall, subcutaneous injection remains a safe, effective, and widely used method for insulin therapy, with consistent emphasis on correct technique, site selection, and rotation across all described insulin types and delivery systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5561a191d3b525d406e49933648e27bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91</data>
