<node id="Levemir">
  <data key="d0">Levemir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir is the brand name for insulin detemir, a long-acting, soluble basal insulin analog used in the treatment of diabetes mellitus, including both type 1 and type 2 diabetes. It functions as a basal insulin in regimens designed to manage blood glucose levels, often administered once or twice daily via subcutaneous injection, commonly using the FlexPen delivery system. Levemir’s prolonged and reproducible time-action profile is due to a fatty acid side chain that enables binding to albumin in the bloodstream, resulting in slow release and extended duration of action. The medication is stable for up to 45 days after opening and is available as an injectable aqueous solution requiring medical supervision during use.

Levemir is indicated for use in adults, adolescents, and children over one year of age, offering glycemic control comparable to other basal insulins such as NPH insulin, insulin glargine, and insulin degludec. Clinical studies have demonstrated its non-inferiority to NPH insulin, particularly in pregnant women with type 1 diabetes, where it has been studied extensively for effects on maternal and fetal outcomes. It is considered a safe and effective option during pregnancy, often used in basal-bolus regimens, and may require dose adjustments when transitioning from other insulin therapies. Levemir has also been evaluated for its efficacy and safety in combination with other antidiabetic medications.

A key advantage of Levemir over some other insulins is its association with a lower risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia and reduced weight gain, making it a favorable option for long-term diabetes management. However, like all insulin therapies, it carries risks of adverse reactions, including hypoglycemia, injection site reactions, and allergic responses. Careful handling and administration are required to prevent medication errors. Dose individualization is essential, based on patient-specific factors such as age, metabolic needs, and concomitant therapies. Overall, Levemir plays a significant role in modern diabetes care due to its predictable pharmacokinetic profile—encompassing absorption, distribution, metabolism, and elimination—and its established safety and efficacy across diverse patient populations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c04e4797bbd8720e9c40ccd6a195cf12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c339ce22a1216d3b019fe67db4ddc37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
