<node id="Needle Disposal">
  <data key="d0">Needle Disposal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle disposal must be done in a rigid sharps container to prevent injury and contamination, never in regular household waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The safe disposal of used syringes and needles in a rigid plastic container, such as a fabric softener or disinfectant bottle.&lt;SEP&gt;The safe disposal of used needles in a designated container to prevent injury and contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle disposal involves placing used needles in puncture-resistant containers and discarding them at designated collection points to prevent injury and contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Used needles must be disposed of in puncture-resistant containers to prevent injury and contamination.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
