  <data key="d0">Thigh</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The thigh is a site for insulin injection where absorption is slower compared to the abdomen and arms.&lt;SEP&gt;The thigh is an insulin injection site where insulin is absorbed more slowly, making it suitable for more controlled insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The thigh is a possible site for subcutaneous injection of Novolin® R.</data>
