<node id="Needle">
  <data key="d0">Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle is a disposable medical device primarily used for subcutaneous insulin injection, typically attached to an insulin pen or syringe. It serves as a critical component in diabetes management, enabling the precise delivery of insulin into the fatty tissue beneath the skin. Needles are designed for single use and must be discarded after each injection to ensure hygiene, prevent infection, and maintain effectiveness. Proper handling is essential to avoid bending or damage, and safe disposal is required to prevent injury and comply with medical waste guidelines.

These devices come in various lengths, including 4mm, 5mm, 6mm, 8mm, and 12.7mm, with the choice of length influencing the injection angle and technique. Shorter needles generally allow for injection at a 90-degree angle without the need for skin pinching, improving comfort and ease of use. The Needle must be applied in one smooth motion and inserted correctly to avoid hitting blood vessels or causing tissue trauma. Specific models, such as those used with the Levemir® FlexPen®, are engineered for compatibility with particular insulin delivery systems and must be removed immediately after use to prevent leakage, dosing inaccuracies, or contamination.

Overall, the Needle plays a vital role in the safe and effective administration of insulin, requiring careful adherence to usage protocols, including gentle insertion, avoidance of reuse, and compliance with distribution and disposal regulations. Its design and application are optimized to enhance patient safety, comfort, and treatment consistency in insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Needles are used for administering Novolin® R Penfill and must be disposed of in puncture-resistant containers to prevent injury and contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;The needle used with Novolin® R FlexPen® must remain under the skin for at least 6 seconds to ensure complete dose delivery and should be discarded after each use; needles up to 8 mm in length are compatible.&lt;SEP&gt;The needle is a disposable component attached to the Novolin® R FlexPen® for subcutaneous insulin injection, which must be replaced if clogged or damaged.&lt;SEP&gt;The needle is a component used with the Novolin® R FlexPen® for insulin injection and must be discarded after use to prevent infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5561a191d3b525d406e49933648e27bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc3409d91fe33592f741a0002d70749c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ae5fe50adf25db0be3b8cdde6282e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91</data>
