<node id="Insulin Mixing">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Mixing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin mixing refers to combining two types of insulin in one syringe, such as intermediate-acting with rapid-acting or rapid-acting analogs, requiring proper handling and immediate use.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin mixing is the process of combining two types of insulin in one syringe, requiring care and proper sequence to avoid contamination and ensure efficacy.</data>
