<node id="Agulha">
  <data key="d0">Agulha</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A needle used with insulin pens, available in short lengths (4, 5, or 6 mm), with 4 mm high-flow needles being recommended for ease of use and reduced discomfort.&lt;SEP&gt;Agulha is a medical device used to inject insulin into the subcutaneous tissue at the correct angle.&lt;SEP&gt;Agulha é usada na inserção da cânula do conjunto de infusão e deve ser descartada após o uso.&lt;SEP&gt;Agulha is the disposable needle attached to the Levemir® FlexPen® for insulin injection, to be replaced after each use.&lt;SEP&gt;Agulha refers to the disposable needles used with the Novolin® R FlexPen®, which must be replaced for each injection to prevent contamination, infection, or inaccurate dosing.</data>
