</node>
<node id="Lipohipertrophy">
  <data key="d0">Lipohipertrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipohipertrophy is a form of lipodystrophy characterized by fatty tissue overgrowth at insulin injection sites, linked to poor site rotation and needle reuse.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7da978df74ee7f686dcc3c260d75577</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778697019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Lipohipertrophy</data>
</node>
<node id="Controle Glicêmico">
  <data key="d0">Controle Glicêmico</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">O controle glicêmico refere-se à gestão da glicemia ao longo do tempo, monitorada por meio de anotações e dispositivos.&lt;SEP&gt;Controle Glicêmico refers to the management of blood glucose levels, measured by HbA1c, and is comparable between Levemir and other insulins.&lt;SEP&gt;Controle glicêmico refers to the regulation of blood glucose levels during pregnancy, assessed via HbA1c and fasting glucose measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Controle Glicêmico refers to the management of blood glucose levels in diabetic patients, a key outcome measured in clinical trials involving Levemir® and liraglutida.&lt;SEP&gt;Controle glicêmico refere-se à regulação dos níveis de glicose no sangue, cuja melhora repentina pode estar associada a efeitos adversos como neuropatia ou piora da retinopatia.&lt;SEP&gt;Controle glicêmico refers to the regulation of blood glucose levels, measured by HbA1c, which is comparable between Levemir and NPH insulin but achieved with less weight gain and lower hypoglycemia risk with Levemir.&lt;SEP&gt;Controle glicêmico refers to the management of blood sugar levels, and significant improvement in glycemic control may lead to reduced awareness of hypoglycemia symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e2fd1844a95ab6fd4f7d89cdbddbc58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Controle Glicêmico</data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Route">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Route</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The subcutaneous route is the standard method for insulin administration, allowing gradual absorption through capillary networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778697021</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Subcutaneous Route</data>
</node>
<node id="Abdomen">
  <data key="d0">Abdomen</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The abdomen is a commonly recommended site for subcutaneous insulin injection, widely preferred due to its fast and consistent absorption rates compared to other injection sites. This rapid and predictable insulin uptake makes the abdomen particularly advantageous for effective glucose management. Injections are typically administered on the lateral sides of the abdomen, at a distance of three to four finger widths away from the navel, to avoid scar tissue and ensure proper absorption.

Multiple descriptions emphasize the importance of site rotation within the abdominal region to prevent lipohypertrophy and maintain efficacy, often suggesting a quadrant-based approach. The consistency of absorption in the abdominal area further supports its use in routine insulin therapy. However, special considerations apply during pregnancy. While the abdomen is considered safe for insulin injections during the first and second trimesters when proper spacing from the navel is maintained, caution is advised in the third trimester. Pregnant women are encouraged to consult a healthcare provider before using the abdominal site during later stages of pregnancy due to changes in fat distribution and skin thickness.

Overall, the abdomen remains a primary choice for insulin administration for most individuals, balancing efficiency, accessibility, and reliability, provided appropriate injection techniques and anatomical guidelines are followed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778697191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Abdomen</data>
</node>
<node id="Tecido Subcutâneo">
  <data key="d0">Tecido Subcutâneo</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Tecido subcutâneo é a camada logo abaixo da pele onde a insulina deve ser aplicada para garantir absorção adequada e eficaz.&lt;SEP&gt;The layer of tissue beneath the skin where insulin is intended to be delivered for proper absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
