  <data key="d7">Lucidi P</data>
</node>
<node id="Seringa de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Seringa de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringa de Insulina is a medical device used to draw and administer precise doses of insulin, requiring proper handling and sterilization.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin syringe is a device specifically designed for measuring and administering insulin doses accurately.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778697241</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Seringa de Insulina</data>
</node>
<node id="Water">
  <data key="d0">Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Used with soap to clean hands before insulin application.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is recommended for hydration during hyperglycemia and ketosis, especially when consuming non-carbohydrate fluids.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Water</data>
</node>
<node id="Alcohol 70%">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol 70%</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol 70% is an antiseptic solution commonly used in medical settings for skin and surface disinfection, particularly in the context of insulin administration. It is applied to the skin at the injection site to perform antisepsis, reducing the risk of infection during insulin injection. The solution must be allowed to dry completely before the injection is administered, ensuring both efficacy and patient comfort. This practice is standard in various healthcare environments, including clinics and nursing homes, where maintaining sterile conditions is critical.

In addition to skin preparation, Alcohol 70% is used to disinfect the rubber stopper of insulin vials prior to needle insertion. This step prevents microbial contamination of the insulin solution, preserving its sterility and safety. The antiseptic is routinely applied to both the injection site on the skin and the vial’s rubber stopper, serving as a dual safeguard against infection. As a liquid antiseptic, Alcohol 70% plays a key role in maintaining aseptic technique during insulin administration, contributing to overall patient safety and infection control.&lt;SEP&gt;Used to clean the injection site and the area where the needle is attached to the pen.&lt;SEP&gt;An antiseptic solution used to clean the insulin vial and application site to prevent infection.&lt;SEP&gt;An antiseptic solution used for skin and equipment disinfection before insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin">
  <data key="d0">Skin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin is the body's outer layer where insulin is administered; it must be inspected for health and free from abnormalities before injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin is the body's outer layer that should be visually and tactilely examined before insulin injection to detect abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin is the body's outer layer where insulin injections are administered, requiring cleaning before injection to prevent infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694919</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Redness">
  <data key="d0">Redness</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Redness is a sign of inflammation or irritation on the skin and is a contraindication for insulin injection at that site.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Swelling">
  <data key="d0">Swelling</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Swelling is a skin condition that should be checked before insulin injection, as injecting into swollen areas can lead to complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Swelling, or edema, is an abnormal accumulation of fluid in tissues and is a reason to avoid insulin injection in the affected area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wounds">
  <data key="d0">Wounds</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Wounds, injuries, or scars are damaged areas of skin where insulin should not be injected due to impaired healing and absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infections">
  <data key="d0">Infections</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infections, including those with discharge, are sites to avoid during insulin administration to prevent complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Infections are concurrent illnesses that increase insulin requirements in diabetic patients due to heightened metabolic stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fistulas">
  <data key="d0">Fistulas</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Fistulas are abnormal passages between organs or between an organ and the skin, and represent unsafe sites for insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Fold">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Fold</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The subcutaneous fold is a technique involving pinching the skin to lift the subcutaneous fat layer, preventing intramuscular insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;The subcutaneous fold is a technique where the skin is lifted to create a fold before insulin injection, helping to ensure the needle reaches subcutaneous tissue and not muscle.&lt;SEP&gt;A subcutaneous fold is a technique used during insulin injection to ensure proper delivery into subcutaneous tissue, based on needle length and patient anatomy.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique involving pinching the skin to create a fold before injecting insulin subcutaneously.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique where the skin is pinched to create a fold for proper subcutaneous needle insertion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intramuscular Injection">
  <data key="d0">Intramuscular Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intramuscular injection refers to the delivery of a substance, such as insulin, directly into muscle tissue. In the context of insulin administration, this route is typically unintended and occurs when the needle penetrates beyond the subcutaneous tissue into the underlying muscle. This can happen due to factors such as using needles longer than 12 mm, incorrect injection angles, failure to use a proper skin fold technique, or in young children who have less subcutaneous fat. When insulin is administered intramuscularly, it is absorbed more rapidly than when delivered subcutaneously, which significantly increases the risk of hypoglycemia, particularly with long-acting insulin formulations.

The rapid absorption associated with intramuscular injection can lead to unpredictable blood glucose levels and potentially severe hypoglycemic episodes, making this route undesirable for routine insulin therapy. It is generally considered an avoidable complication of improper injection technique and is not recommended for standard insulin delivery. However, certain insulin products, such as Novolin® R and its formulation in the Novolin® R FlexPen®, may be administered via intramuscular injection under strict medical supervision when clinically necessary. In such cases, the procedure is performed deliberately and with caution, acknowledging the altered pharmacokinetics and increased risks involved.

Overall, while intramuscular injection is not the standard or intended route for insulin administration, it can occur unintentionally due to technical errors or anatomical factors, especially in pediatric patients. Healthcare providers emphasize proper injection techniques—such as using appropriate needle lengths, correct angles, and skin pinch methods—to ensure insulin is delivered into the subcutaneous tissue and to minimize the risk of intramuscular deposition. When used intentionally, as with specific formulations under medical guidance, intramuscular injection remains a controlled and monitored intervention rather than a routine practice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Injection Technique">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Injection Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin injection technique includes proper skin preparation, use of subcutaneous fold, correct needle angle, and post-injection needle retention.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin injection technique refers to the proper method of administering insulin subcutaneously, including needle selection, angle of insertion, and use of skin fold to prevent intramuscular injection.&lt;SEP&gt;A change in insulin injection technique, including rotation of injection sites, may help alleviate complications such as lipodystrophy and fluctuations in blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e023d3ebcda62fd027</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle Angle">
  <data key="d0">Needle Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle angle refers to the correct insertion angle (45° or 90°) during insulin injection, depending on needle length and patient age.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle angle refers to the recommended 90° or 45° angle for insulin injection depending on needle length and patient anatomy.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle angle refers to the degree at which the insulin needle enters the skin, typically 90° for short needles and 45° for longer needles or in children, to ensure proper delivery into subcutaneous fat.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle angle refers to the angle at which the needle is inserted during injection, varying by needle length and patient age to ensure proper subcutaneous delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The needle angle refers to the degree at which the needle is inserted into the skin during insulin injection, determined by needle length, patient age, and subcutaneous tissue thickness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695957</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Leakage">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Leakage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin leakage may occur if the needle is removed too quickly; holding it in place after injection helps prevent this.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin leakage refers to the unintended escape of insulin from the injection site after administration, which can be minimized by keeping the needle in place for several seconds post-injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin leakage refers to the unintended loss of insulin from the injection site or needle after administration, which can compromise dosing effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin leakage refers to the unintended loss of insulin from the Levemir® FlexPen® due to damage or improper handling, leading to inaccurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d212ccdded1e4ccf51af243a8d38b4c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arm">
  <data key="d0">Arm</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The arm is a possible insulin injection site, often used in morning routines as part of site rotation.&lt;SEP&gt;The arm is a common site for insulin injection, with moderate absorption speed.&lt;SEP&gt;The arm is an insulin injection site with moderate absorption speed, slower than the abdomen but faster than thighs and buttocks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leg">
  <data key="d0">Leg</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The leg is a possible insulin injection site, often used in evening routines as part of site rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children Under 6 Years">
  <data key="d0">Children Under 6 Years</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Children under 6 years old should always use the subcutaneous fold technique during insulin injection, regardless of needle size.&lt;SEP&gt;Children under 6 years are a patient group for whom subcutaneous skin fold technique is recommended during insulin injection, regardless of needle size, due to low body fat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adolescents With Low Body Fat">
  <data key="d0">Adolescents With Low Body Fat</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adolescents with low body fat at injection sites should use the subcutaneous fold to prevent intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adults With Low Body Fat">
  <data key="d0">Adults With Low Body Fat</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adults with low body fat should use the subcutaneous fold technique to ensure proper subcutaneous insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adults With High Body Fat">
  <data key="d0">Adults With High Body Fat</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adults with high body fat at injection sites may not require a subcutaneous fold, especially when using short needles (4–5 mm).&lt;SEP&gt;Adults with high body fat at the injection site may not require the subcutaneous skin fold technique, especially when using 4 mm or 5 mm needles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Prega">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Prega</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous prega is a technique involving a light pinch of the skin during insulin injection to ensure proper needle placement and avoid intramuscular delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694381</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="4 Mm Needle">
  <data key="d0">4 Mm Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A 4 mm needle is a short insulin injection needle recommended for children, adults with low body fat, and pregnant women to ensure safe and effective insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The 4 mm needle is a short insulin injection needle recommended for all individuals, safe and well-tolerated, often used without a skin fold except in young children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695968</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="8 Mm Needle">
  <data key="d0">8 Mm Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An 8 mm needle is a longer insulin injection needle that may require use of a skin fold and is not recommended for children or thin individuals due to higher risk of muscle penetration.&lt;SEP&gt;The 8 mm needle is not recommended for children and adolescents due to the risk of intramuscular injection and requires a skin fold and proper angle adjustment based on tissue availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695968</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adults">
  <data key="d0">Adults</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adults typically have skin thickness under 3 mm and can safely use short needles (4–8 mm), with technique adjustments based on body fat and motor ability.&lt;SEP&gt;Adults may not require a subcutaneous pinch when using short needles (4–5 mm), but the technique is recommended when subcutaneous tissue is limited or longer needles are used.&lt;SEP&gt;Adults with type 1 diabetes were used as a reference group in pharmacokinetic studies of Levemir.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698078</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Sites">
  <data key="d0">Injection Sites</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Recommended insulin injection sites include the abdomen, thighs, arms, and buttocks, selected based on accessibility and absence of bones, joints, or major vessels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Buttocks">
  <data key="d0">Buttocks</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The buttocks, specifically the upper outer quadrant, are a recommended site for insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;The buttocks are a site for insulin injection with the slowest absorption rate among common injection areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Buttocks are a recommended injection site, specifically the upper outer lateral quadrant.&lt;SEP&gt;Buttocks are a less commonly used insulin injection site with the slowest absorption rate among recommended areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The buttocks, particularly the upper outer lateral quadrant, are recommended insulin injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695949</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Condition">
  <data key="d0">Skin Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proper skin condition is essential for insulin injection; the site must be healthy, clean, dry, and free from redness, inflammation, or swelling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694385</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alcohol Cleaning">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol Cleaning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol cleaning with 70% alcohol is recommended in public settings like clinics or schools before insulin injection, but not always necessary at home.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle Bending">
  <data key="d0">Needle Bending</data>
  <data key="d1">risk</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle bending during use can affect insulin delivery and cause pain, so care must be taken to avoid bending, especially when removing protective caps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Technique">
  <data key="d0">Injection Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection technique includes steps such as attaching the needle, setting the dose, using a skin fold, and injecting at the correct angle to ensure safe and effective insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;To ensure proper delivery, the needle must remain under the skin for at least 6 seconds after injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="90° Angle Injection">
  <data key="d0">90° Angle Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A 90° angle injection is used when administering insulin with shorter needles if sufficient subcutaneous tissue is present, ensuring proper delivery into fat tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="45° Angle Injection">
  <data key="d0">45° Angle Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A 45° angle injection is recommended during pregnancy and for thin individuals to reduce the risk of intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hand Luggage">
  <data key="d0">Hand Luggage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hand luggage is the recommended place to carry insulin during travel, as opposed to checked baggage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Sunlight">
  <data key="d0">Direct Sunlight</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct sunlight should be avoided when storing insulin to prevent degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct sunlight is a risk factor for insulin degradation and must be avoided during transport.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696408</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glove Compartment">
  <data key="d0">Glove Compartment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The glove compartment in a vehicle is an inappropriate place to store insulin due to temperature fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Car Dashboard">
  <data key="d0">Car Dashboard</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The car dashboard is an unsuitable location for insulin storage because of exposure to heat and sunlight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bus Luggage Compartment">
  <data key="d0">Bus Luggage Compartment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The bus luggage compartment is not recommended for insulin storage due to uncontrolled temperature conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694394</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sealed Insulin Vials">
  <data key="d0">Sealed Insulin Vials</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sealed insulin vials must be kept between 2°C and 8°C, typically in a cooler with gel packs, without direct contact with ice.&lt;SEP&gt;Sealed insulin vials must be stored at temperatures between 2 to 8°C during transport, typically using thermal bags with gel packs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696408</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Bag">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Bag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A thermal bag is used to transport insulin safely, maintaining stable temperature without allowing direct contact with ice or frozen elements.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermal bag is used to transport insulin at safe temperatures, often with gel packs or ice.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermal bag is used to maintain proper temperature for insulin during transport, often with gel packs to keep it cool without freezing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696408</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gelox">
  <data key="d0">Gelox</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gelox or ice packs are used in thermal bags to maintain proper insulin storage temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;Gelox refers to cooling packs used in thermal bags to maintain proper insulin storage temperature during transport.&lt;SEP&gt;Gelox é um elemento refrigerante usado em bolsas térmicas para manter a insulina na temperatura recomendada durante o transporte.&lt;SEP&gt;Gelox refers to cooling gel packs used in thermal bags to maintain insulin at recommended temperatures during transport.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696408</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Supplies">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Supplies</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes supplies include used syringes, needles, lancets, insulin pens, and insulin pump materials that require proper disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes supplies include necessary medical tools and materials carried by individuals to manage diabetes, such as test strips, insulin, and delivery devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sharps Waste">
  <data key="d0">Sharps Waste</data>
  <data key="d1">waste</data>
  <data key="d2">Sharps waste includes any blood-contaminated, sharp medical items such as needles, lancets, and syringes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacy">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacy</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharmacies are locations where sharps containers can be purchased.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surgical Supply Store">
  <data key="d0">Surgical Supply Store</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Surgical supply stores sell sharps containers and related medical equipment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Softener Bottle">
  <data key="d0">Softener Bottle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A rigid softener bottle with a wide mouth can be repurposed as a sharps container for safe disposal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resistant Transport Bag">
  <data key="d0">Resistant Transport Bag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A resistant transport bag is used to carry a sealed sharps container to a health unit for disposal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pets">
  <data key="d0">Pets</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Pets must be kept away from sharps containers to prevent accidental injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694398</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipo-hypertrophy">
  <data key="d0">Lipo-hypertrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipo-hypertrophy is the most common type of lipodystrophy, characterized by hard lumps or nodules under the skin due to fat buildup from repeated insulin injections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694398</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enzyme">
  <data key="d0">Enzyme</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Enzyme is a substance in the test strip that reacts with blood sugar to produce an electrical current used by the glucose meter to determine glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance on the test strip that reacts with blood sugar to initiate the glucose measurement process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694399</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electrical Signal">
  <data key="d0">Electrical Signal</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A small current generated by the chemical reaction between the enzyme and blood sugar, which the glucometer converts into a glucose reading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694399</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ideal Glucose Range">
  <data key="d0">Ideal Glucose Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The target range for blood glucose levels, used to assess whether a person's diabetes is well-controlled.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694400</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Finger Prick">
  <data key="d0">Finger Prick</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A technique involving puncturing the fingertip to obtain a blood sample for glucose testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694400</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lancet Device">
  <data key="d0">Lancet Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A tool that holds and controls the lancet, often with adjustable settings for less painful pricking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Result Recording">
  <data key="d0">Result Recording</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The practice of documenting glucose readings in a notebook, app, or device to track patterns over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile Application">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Application</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A smartphone app used to record and analyze blood glucose results for better diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Computer-Connected Device">
  <data key="d0">Computer-Connected Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A glucometer that stores results and can transfer data to a computer for medical review.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hand Washing">
  <data key="d0">Hand Washing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A recommended step before glucose testing to remove sugar residues that could affect test accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Finger Selection">
  <data key="d0">Finger Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The practice of rotating fingers and using the side of the fingertip for pricking to reduce pain and skin damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Strip Expiration">
  <data key="d0">Test Strip Expiration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The validity period of a test strip, which must be checked before use to ensure accurate blood glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Strip Coding">
  <data key="d0">Test Strip Coding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A process where the glucometer is calibrated to match the batch code of the test strips to ensure measurement accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caneta De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Caneta De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Caneta de insulina é um dispositivo utilizado para aplicação de insulina, disponível em versões descartáveis ou recarregáveis, permitindo doses precisas e prática de uso.&lt;SEP&gt;Caneta de insulina é um dispositivo usado para aplicação do medicamento, especialmente as recarregáveis, que não devem ser guardadas na geladeira.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caneta Recarregável">
  <data key="d0">Caneta Recarregável</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Caneta recarregável é um tipo de caneta de insulina que utiliza refis (cartuchos) de 3 mL de insulina, sendo possível trocar o refil após o esgotamento.&lt;SEP&gt;A reusable insulin pen that uses replaceable 3 mL insulin cartridges (refills), designed for continued use by replacing the cartridge when empty.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulha De 4 Mm">
  <data key="d0">Agulha De 4 Mm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agulha de 4 mm é a mais curta disponível para canetas de insulina, recomendada por ser menos dolorosa e segura, especialmente para crianças e pessoas magras.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulha De 5 Mm">
  <data key="d0">Agulha De 5 Mm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agulha de 5 mm é uma opção curta para aplicação de insulina, adequada para adultos e crianças, com menor risco de dor e complicações.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulha De 6 Mm">
  <data key="d0">Agulha De 6 Mm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agulha de 6 mm pode ser usada em adultos e crianças, exigindo prega de pele para aplicação em ângulo de 90° ou 45°, dependendo do grupo etário.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulha De 8 Mm">
  <data key="d0">Agulha De 8 Mm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agulha de 8 mm é mais longa e não recomendada para crianças e pessoas magras, exigindo prega de pele para evitar aplicação intramuscular.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prega Subcutânea">
  <data key="d0">Prega Subcutânea</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Prega subcutânea é uma técnica que consiste em levantar uma dobra de pele no local da aplicação para garantir que a insulina seja administrada no tecido subcutâneo.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique involving a skin pinch during insulin injection to ensure proper delivery into the subcutaneous tissue, especially recommended for children and individuals with low body fat.&lt;SEP&gt;Prega subcutânea is a technique involving a light pinch of the skin to lift the subcutaneous tissue, ensuring insulin is injected correctly and not into muscle.&lt;SEP&gt;Prega subcutânea is a technique involving pinching the skin to ensure proper subcutaneous insulin injection and prevent intramuscular delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695743</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depósito Rígido">
  <data key="d0">Depósito Rígido</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Depósito rígido é um recipiente plástico, como garrafas de amaciante ou desinfetante, usado para descartar agulhas e lancetas de forma segura.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unidade De Saúde">
  <data key="d0">Unidade De Saúde</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Unidade de Saúde é o local onde o depósito contendo agulhas usadas deve ser entregue para descarte adequado.&lt;SEP&gt;A Unidade de Saúde é o local onde pacientes com diabetes devem procurar para orientações, reposição de canetas e relato de eventos adversos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seringa De 30 Unidades">
  <data key="d0">Seringa De 30 Unidades</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringa de 30 unidades é indicada para doses pequenas ou precisas de insulina, com marcações de 0,5 ou 1 unidade, comumente usada em crianças.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seringa De 50 Unidades">
  <data key="d0">Seringa De 50 Unidades</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringa de 50 unidades é utilizada para doses mais precisas de insulina, com marcações de 0,5 ou 1 unidade, adequada para pacientes que necessitam de controle rigoroso.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Application">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Application</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Application is the process of administering insulin, primarily through subcutaneous injection, to manage blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes. This procedure involves the use of medical devices such as syringes with vials or insulin pens, each requiring specific safety protocols, preparation steps, and proper handling techniques to ensure accurate dosing and patient safety. Central to effective insulin application is the selection of appropriate injection sites on the body—commonly the abdomen, thighs, buttocks, or upper arms—where subcutaneous tissue allows for consistent insulin absorption.

Proper technique during insulin application includes skin preparation, hygiene practices, and site inspection to prevent infection and tissue damage. Rotating injection sites is a recommended practice to avoid lipohypertrophy and ensure optimal insulin absorption, thereby maintaining the treatment’s efficacy. The process also emphasizes minimizing discomfort during injection, particularly in pediatric patients, through methods such as skin pinching, rapid needle insertion, and distraction techniques. Additionally, individuals are advised to consider factors such as physical activity, as exercise can influence insulin absorption rates and increase the risk of hypoglycemia if injection sites are not carefully chosen in relation to active muscles.

Post-injection care and adherence to structured routines further support the safety and effectiveness of insulin application. Overall, successful insulin administration relies on a combination of correct device use, anatomical knowledge, hygiene, and patient education to achieve consistent therapeutic outcomes and reduce the risk of complications associated with diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f4c3fffcb1c054dd2b100c36c64717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Double Checking">
  <data key="d0">Double Checking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Double checking is a safety procedure in hospitals where two professionals verify insulin preparation and administration to prevent medication errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694407</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electronic Prescription">
  <data key="d0">Electronic Prescription</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An electronic prescription is a digital system for ordering medications that helps avoid handwriting-related errors in insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694408</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Abbreviation">
  <data key="d0">Medical Abbreviation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical abbreviations in prescriptions can lead to misunderstandings and medication errors if not clearly written, so they should be avoided in insulin prescriptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694408</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Transportation">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Transportation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin transportation requires adherence to temperature guidelines and protection from extreme conditions, especially during travel, with insulin carried in hand luggage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694408</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vegetable Drawer">
  <data key="d0">Vegetable Drawer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The vegetable drawer in a refrigerator is a recommended place to store insulin as it maintains a stable temperature and is away from freezer walls.&lt;SEP&gt;The vegetable drawer in a refrigerator is a recommended storage location for insulin, as it maintains stable temperature and avoids direct contact with cold walls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696360</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Preparation">
  <data key="d0">Skin Preparation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin preparation involves cleaning the injection site with alcohol and waiting for it to dry before applying insulin to prevent infection and irritation.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin preparation involves cleaning the injection site with 70% alcohol in institutional settings, ensuring the skin is dry before injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695956</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Division">
  <data key="d0">Dose Division</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose division is the practice of splitting a high insulin dose into two separate injections, which should be discussed with a doctor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distraction Technique">
  <data key="d0">Distraction Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Distraction techniques are used during insulin application in young children to reduce anxiety and discomfort.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Reaction to Freezing">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Reaction to Freezing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">If insulin freezes accidentally, it must be discarded and not used, as freezing destroys its effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-Filled Insulin Pen">
  <data key="d0">Pre-Filled Insulin Pen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A pre-filled insulin pen is a disposable device containing insulin that should not be refrigerated once in use to avoid mechanism damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heart Attack And Stroke">
  <data key="d0">Heart Attack And Stroke</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Heart attack and stroke are serious cardiovascular complications associated with poorly managed diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tira">
  <data key="d0">Tira</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A tira é um componente descartável de glicosímetro que reage com uma gota de sangue para medir a glicemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prazo De Validade">
  <data key="d0">Prazo De Validade</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">O prazo de validade é o período durante o qual a tira de glicosímetro mantém sua eficácia e precisão.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Código Da Tira">
  <data key="d0">Código Da Tira</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">O código da tira é um identificador que deve corresponder ao código do glicosímetro em certos modelos para garantir medições corretas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horário Da Medição">
  <data key="d0">Horário Da Medição</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">O horário da medição é a informação temporal registrada junto com o valor da glicemia para fins de controle clínico.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sintomas">
  <data key="d0">Sintomas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sintomas como tontura, fome e dor de cabeça são observações clínicas registradas junto com a glicemia para avaliação médica.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Líquido Intersticial">
  <data key="d0">Líquido Intersticial</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">O líquido intersticial é o fluido entre as células onde o sensor de glicose mede a concentração de açúcar, em vez de no sangue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subida De Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Subida De Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Subida de glicose refere-se a aumentos repentinos nos níveis de açúcar no sangue, que podem passar despercebidos sem monitoramento contínuo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Erro No Horário Da Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Erro No Horário Da Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Erro no horário da insulina é um fator que pode impactar o controle glicêmico e ser identificado por meio de análise de dados do sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vantagens Dos Sensores">
  <data key="d0">Vantagens Dos Sensores</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">As vantagens dos sensores incluem menos furos no dedo, visualização de tendências, prevenção de hipoglicemia e controle mais preciso da glicemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibração">
  <data key="d0">Calibração</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A calibração é um processo necessário em alguns sensores de glicose que envolve a confirmação com medição de sangue capilar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sangue Na Fita">
  <data key="d0">Sangue Na Fita</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sangue na fita refers to the instruction for applying a blood sample to the test strip for glucose measurement using a glucometer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Fat">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Fat</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous fat is the layer of fat beneath the skin where insulin should be injected to avoid muscle delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Lesion">
  <data key="d0">Skin Lesion</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin lesion is a potential complication of improper insulin injection practices, such as failing to rotate sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Used Syringe Disposal">
  <data key="d0">Used Syringe Disposal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Used syringe disposal involves placing used needles and syringes into a proper sharps container to ensure safety and prevent injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seringa U100">
  <data key="d0">Seringa U100</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringa U100 é um dispositivo projetado especificamente para aplicar insulina U100, com graduações em unidades e disponível em modelos de 100, 50 e 30 unidades.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seringa com Agulha Fixa">
  <data key="d0">Seringa com Agulha Fixa</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringa com agulha fixa é o tipo mais seguro e recomendado, com baixo espaço morto, ideal para doses precisas e mistura de tipos de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694424</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seringa com Agulha Removível">
  <data key="d0">Seringa com Agulha Removível</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringa com agulha removível não é recomendada para uso doméstico devido a riscos como erro de dose, maior espaço morto e agulha longa que pode atingir o músculo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulha de 6 mm">
  <data key="d0">Agulha de 6 mm</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Agulha de 6 mm é a mais segura e menos dolorosa para aplicação de insulina, sendo a mais indicada para pacientes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina U100">
  <data key="d0">Insulina U100</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina U100 é o tipo mais comum de insulina no Brasil, com concentração de 100 unidades por mililitro, exigindo o uso de seringas U100.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Armazenamento de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Armazenamento de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">O armazenamento correto da insulina envolve mantê-la fechada entre 2 °C e 8 °C na geladeira e, após aberta, em local fresco e longe do sol por até 30 dias.&lt;SEP&gt;Proper insulin storage includes labeling with opening date and separating from other injectables like heparin and vaccines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695965</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aplicação de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Aplicação de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A aplicação de insulina envolve etapas como preparar o material, limpar o frasco, aspirar a dose correta, fazer prega na pele e aplicar em ângulo de 45° ou 90°.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of administering insulin using a pen device, involving steps such as handwashing, site preparation, dose setting, and correct injection angle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ajuste de Dose de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Ajuste de Dose de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A dose de insulina pode mudar com o tempo devido a fatores como peso, alimentação, rotina ou saúde, exigindo revisão médica regular.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Profissional de Saúde">
  <data key="d0">Profissional de Saúde</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Profissional de saúde é responsável por orientar o uso correto da insulina, revisar doses e receber notificações sobre problemas com o medicamento.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Espaço Morto">
  <data key="d0">Espaço Morto</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Espaço morto é a quantidade de insulina que fica presa na seringa após a aplicação, resultando em desperdício e erro de dose, comum em seringas com agulha removível.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Descarte de Seringas">
  <data key="d0">Descarte de Seringas</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">O descarte de seringas deve ser feito em recipientes rígidos, como garrafas de amaciante, para evitar acidentes e contaminação.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Application Devices">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Application Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin application devices include syringes and other tools used to administer insulin, with specific types recommended for safety and accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin application devices are tools used for administering insulin, including syringes, pens, and other injection systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Storage Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Storage Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin storage guidelines specify proper conditions for storing insulin, including temperature ranges and duration outside refrigeration.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Storage Guidelines specify that insulin must not be frozen and should be stored at 2°C to 8°C when unopened, and at room temperature up to 30°C when in use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695742</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Safe Insulin Injection Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Safe Insulin Injection Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Safe insulin injection procedure includes steps such as preparing materials, cleaning the vial, aspirating the correct dose, and injecting at the correct angle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intramuscular Administration">
  <data key="d0">Intramuscular Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intramuscular administration is the injection of insulin directly into muscle tissue, resulting in rapid absorption and used only under medical supervision.&lt;SEP&gt;Intramuscular administration of Levemir should be avoided due to unpredictable absorption and risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698087</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intradermal Administration">
  <data key="d0">Intradermal Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intradermal administration refers to injecting insulin into the superficial layer of the skin, which delays absorption and may reduce effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694430</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Absorption Rate">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Absorption Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin absorption rate varies by injection site, with the abdomen being the fastest, followed by arms, thighs, and buttocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin absorption rate varies depending on the injection site, with the abdomen being the fastest, followed by arms, thighs, and buttocks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Used Needle">
  <data key="d0">Used Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A used needle is a disposable medical item that must be discarded in a proper container after insulin injection to prevent contamination and injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Suspension">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Suspension</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin suspension contains particles that must be gently mixed by rolling the vial to ensure proper dosing and effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin suspension contains particles that must be properly mixed before use to ensure correct dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin suspension refers to insulin formulations containing particles that must be homogenized before use to ensure proper dosing and effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin suspension refers to cloudy insulin formulations, such as NPH, that require homogenization before use.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin suspension is a function that stops all insulin infusion, typically used during activities like swimming or showering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700935</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transport Of Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Transport Of Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Transport of insulin should be done in carry-on luggage with protection from direct ice contact to maintain stability and prevent damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elliott P. Joslin">
  <data key="d0">Elliott P. Joslin</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Elliott P. Joslin was a physician in 1918 who emphasized patient education and helped train nurses to teach diabetes management at home.&lt;SEP&gt;Elliott P. Joslin was a physician in 1918 who emphasized the importance of patient education in diabetes management and helped train nurses to teach patients at home on proper insulin use, diet, and physical activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Elliott P. Joslin was a physician who emphasized patient education in diabetes management and expanded the role of nurses in community-based diabetes care in 1923.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695945</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Education">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Education</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes education involves training patients, families, and caregivers on proper insulin use, diet, exercise, and emotional support to manage diabetes effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes education involves teaching patients, families, and caregivers how to manage diabetes, including proper insulin use, diet, and physical activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes education involves teaching patients, caregivers, and families about insulin therapy, self-care, diet, exercise, and safe injection practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695945</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Healthcare Professionals">
  <data key="d0">Healthcare Professionals</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Healthcare professionals including doctors, nurses, and diabetes educators are responsible for providing up-to-date, personalized training on safe insulin use.&lt;SEP&gt;Healthcare professionals are responsible for being trained and equipped to provide quality care and guidance on safe insulin use to patients and caregivers.&lt;SEP&gt;Healthcare professionals are responsible for prescribing, preparing, and administering insulin, and require ongoing training to prevent medication errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Healthcare professionals are individuals who analyze retrospective SMCG data to adjust diabetes treatment based on glucose profiles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pain Reduction In Insulin Injection">
  <data key="d0">Pain Reduction In Insulin Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pain reduction in insulin injection involves using short needles, allowing insulin to reach room temperature, waiting for alcohol to dry, and applying the needle smoothly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="i-Port">
  <data key="d0">i-Port</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The i-Port is a device that allows multiple insulin injections without repeated skin punctures, improving comfort and convenience.&lt;SEP&gt;The i-Port is a device that allows multiple insulin injections without repeated skin punctures, improving convenience and comfort.&lt;SEP&gt;The i-Port is an injection port device that allows multiple insulin injections through a single insertion site, improving convenience and reducing discomfort.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695944</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cold Compress">
  <data key="d0">Cold Compress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A cold compress can slow insulin absorption and potentially increase blood sugar levels.&lt;SEP&gt;A cold compress can slow down insulin absorption and increase blood sugar levels when applied after injection.&lt;SEP&gt;A cold compress decreases insulin absorption rate by reducing local blood flow, potentially leading to hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoramento de Cetonas">
  <data key="d0">Monitoramento de Cetonas</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitoramento de Cetonas involves testing for ketone levels in urine or blood to prevent diabetic ketoacidosis during high glucose or illness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fita de Urina para Cetonas">
  <data key="d0">Fita de Urina para Cetonas</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fita de Urina para Cetonas is a test strip used to detect ketone levels in urine, similar to a pregnancy test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medidor de Cetonas no Sangue">
  <data key="d0">Medidor de Cetonas no Sangue</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Medidor de Cetonas no Sangue is a device that measures β-hidroxibutirato (β-OHB) in the blood, providing faster and more reliable results than urine tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carboidrato de Ação Rápida">
  <data key="d0">Carboidrato de Ação Rápida</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Carboidrato de Ação Rápida includes fast-acting sugars like juice, glucose tablets, or honey used to treat hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tempo no Alvo">
  <data key="d0">Tempo no Alvo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tempo no Alvo refers to the percentage of time a person's glucose levels remain within the target range of 70–180 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicemia em Jejum">
  <data key="d0">Glicemia em Jejum</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicemia em Jejum is the blood glucose level measured after fasting, typically used to evaluate baseline glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicemia após as Refeições">
  <data key="d0">Glicemia após as Refeições</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicemia após as Refeições refers to blood glucose levels measured two hours after meals, with a target of less than 180 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adultos em Geral">
  <data key="d0">Adultos em Geral</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adultos em Geral refers to adult patients with type 1 or type 2 diabetes, with specific glucose and HbA1c targets for management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crianças e Adolescentes">
  <data key="d0">Crianças e Adolescentes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Crianças e Adolescentes are pediatric patients with type 1 diabetes, requiring individualized targets to balance control and hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Idosos com Doenças ou Limitações">
  <data key="d0">Idosos com Doenças ou Limitações</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Idosos com Doenças ou Limitações are elderly patients with comorbidities, requiring flexible glucose goals focused on safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vomiting">
  <data key="d0">Vomiting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vomiting is a symptom associated with illness that can contribute to ketone buildup and necessitates ketone testing in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Vomiting is a condition that can indicate metabolic imbalance in people with diabetes, prompting the need for ketone testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urine Test">
  <data key="d0">Urine Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Urine test is a method introduced in 1925 for detecting sugar in urine at home, allowing early self-monitoring of glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694444</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Monitor">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Monitor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The blood glucose monitor is a device introduced in 1964 that measures blood sugar from a finger-prick drop of blood, marking the beginning of home glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709847</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Blood Glucose Monitor</data>
</node>
<node id="Flash Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Flash Glucose Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Flash Glucose Sensor is a glucose monitoring device similar to CGM, but requires a reader to scan the sensor to retrieve glucose data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Invasive Glucose Monitor">
  <data key="d0">Non-Invasive Glucose Monitor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-invasive glucose monitors are emerging devices that use light or heat to measure glucose without requiring a finger prick.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wearable Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Wearable Glucose Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Wearable glucose sensors include devices shaped like watches or contact lenses, or tattoo-like sensors that display glucose levels through the skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Measurement Every 5 Minutes">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Measurement Every 5 Minutes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM measures glucose levels every 5 minutes, providing continuous data without the need for frequent finger pricks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Glucose Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Low Glucose Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The low glucose alarm is a feature of CGM that alerts users when glucose levels are too low, helping prevent severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Glucose Alarm">
  <data key="d0">High Glucose Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The high glucose alarm notifies users when glucose levels are too high, enabling timely intervention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nighttime Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Nighttime Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM helps monitor glucose levels during sleep, a time when traditional monitoring is typically not performed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbA1c Reduction">
  <data key="d0">HbA1c Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Studies show that CGM use can help lower HbA1c levels, indicating improved long-term glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trend Interpretation">
  <data key="d0">Trend Interpretation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Interpreting glucose trend arrows is crucial for anticipating glucose changes, more so than relying solely on numerical values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic MiniMed">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic MiniMed</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Medtronic MiniMed is an insulin pump system that can integrate with CGM sensors for automated diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic MiniMed is a division of Medtronic focused on developing insulin delivery systems, including the MiniMed 770G pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic MiniMed es una organización que fabrica dispositivos médicos, incluyendo la bomba de insulina MiniMed® 670G.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic MiniMed is a division of Medtronic that develops and produces insulin delivery systems and diabetes care technologies.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-641adeabab10205d29d07a0c3e82f2e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e199c63f77bb267d92abb101f110ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Calibration">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Calibration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Some glucose sensors require calibration using finger-prick blood glucose tests, typically done fasting or before meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor calibration is the process of adjusting the glucose sensor readings to ensure accuracy, required at specific intervals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700935</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="No Calibration">
  <data key="d0">No Calibration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The FreeStyle Libre system does not require calibration, making it more convenient for users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pediatric Use">
  <data key="d0">Pediatric Use</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM is safe and effective for children, though adherence to daily use can be a challenge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Management in Children">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Management in Children</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Using CGM regularly in children helps control diabetes and reduce HbA1c levels over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694453</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Treatment Goals">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Treatment Goals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes treatment goals involve maintaining blood glucose within target ranges to prevent long-term complications in organs such as eyes, kidneys, heart, and nerves.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Má Formação Do Bebê">
  <data key="d0">Má Formação Do Bebê</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Má formação do bebê é um risco aumentado quando a glicemia materna está alta no início da gestação, especialmente em mulheres com diabetes tipo 1 ou 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bebê Grande">
  <data key="d0">Bebê Grande</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bebê grande, ou macrossomia fetal, é uma complicação associada ao diabetes mal controlado durante a gravidez, aumentando o risco de parto cesáreo e internação em UTI neonatal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fitas Para Cetonas">
  <data key="d0">Fitas Para Cetonas</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fitas para cetonas são dispositivos usados para medir níveis de cetonas no sangue, cuja disponibilidade é limitada na rede pública de saúde no Brasil.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rede Pública">
  <data key="d0">Rede Pública</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Rede pública refere-se ao sistema de saúde pública no Brasil, onde há dificuldades no acesso a fitas para cetonas no sangue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Controle Rigoroso De Glicemia">
  <data key="d0">Controle Rigoroso De Glicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Controle rigoroso de glicemia envolve medições frequentes da glicose sanguínea e ajustes terapêuticos para manter os níveis dentro das metas recomendadas durante a gravidez.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medição Da Glicemia 7 Vezes Ao Dia">
  <data key="d0">Medição Da Glicemia 7 Vezes Ao Dia</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Medição da glicemia 7 vezes ao dia é uma prática recomendada para mulheres com diabetes tipo 1 ou 2 durante a gravidez, incluindo medições antes e depois das refeições.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medição Da Glicemia 4 Vezes Ao Dia">
  <data key="d0">Medição Da Glicemia 4 Vezes Ao Dia</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Medição da glicemia 4 vezes ao dia é recomendada para mulheres com diabetes gestacional, incluindo em jejum e 1 hora após cada refeição principal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Montes Claros">
  <data key="d0">Montes Claros</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Montes Claros is a city in Brazil where Novo Nordisk Farmacêutica do Brasil Ltda is located.&lt;SEP&gt;Montes Claros is a city in Minas Gerais, Brazil, where Novo Nordisk Produção Farmacêutica do Brasil Ltda. manufactures Levemir® FlexPen®.&lt;SEP&gt;Montes Claros is a city in Brazil where Novo Nordisk Produção Farmacêutica do Brasil Ltda. manufactures pharmaceutical products.&lt;SEP&gt;Montes Claros is a city in Minas Gerais, Brazil, where Novo Nordisk's pharmaceutical production facility is located.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68f15567df531c98c7bb5ae57a2836b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad7b7e8e5212b6d7ea0f4b0505f82c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
