<node id="Metas De Glicemia">
  <data key="d0">Metas De Glicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metas de glicemia são valores-alvo de concentração de glicose no sangue que devem ser mantidos durante a gravidez para reduzir riscos maternos e fetais.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycemia Above 250 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d0">Glycemia Above 250 Mg/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycemia above 250 mg/dL for several hours is a key indicator for testing ketones, particularly in individuals with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System Failure">
  <data key="d0">System Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">System failure refers to malfunctions in insulin pump devices, which can lead to metabolic instability and require immediate ketone testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children and Adolescents with Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Children and Adolescents with Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">This group includes young individuals with type 1 diabetes who require individualized glycemic targets, such as HbA1c &lt; 7% or up to &lt; 7.5% if at risk of severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adults with Type 1 or Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Adults with Type 1 or Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adults with diabetes are typically managed with standard targets including HbA1c &lt; 7%, fasting glucose of 80–130 mg/dL, and post-meal glucose below 180 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elderly with Chronic Illness">
  <data key="d0">Elderly with Chronic Illness</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Elderly patients with chronic diseases or limitations may have relaxed targets, such as HbA1c up to 8% and fasting glucose of 90–150 mg/dL, to prioritize safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Target Range">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Target Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The glucose target range is defined as blood glucose levels between 70 and 180 mg/dL, which is the ideal zone for minimizing complications and hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
