</node>
<node id="Ketones">
  <data key="d0">Ketones</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals with type 1 diabetes, especially children and adolescents, are at higher risk of ketone production and should test regularly under specific conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketones are substances measured in blood or urine to assess metabolic status, particularly during insulin delivery interruptions.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketones are substances produced when the body burns fat for energy, and testing for them is recommended when insulin delivery is blocked.</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicemias Capilares">
  <data key="d0">Glicemias Capilares</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicemias capilares refer to blood glucose measurements taken through a finger prick, used to monitor sugar levels in individuals with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2dff1c37dd504c2e0f6d3e3541019e15</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
