<node id="Insulin Storage And Transport">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Storage And Transport</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Storage And Transport involves proper handling of insulin, including refrigeration of unopened vials and room temperature storage for in-use insulin, to maintain its effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694917</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Syringe">
  <data key="d0">Syringe</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A syringe is a medical device primarily used to draw insulin from a vial and administer it through subcutaneous injection. It serves as a traditional tool for insulin delivery, commonly employed in diabetes management to ensure accurate dosing. Syringes are available in various capacities, including 100UI, 50UI, and 30UI, with specific types such as U100 syringes designed to measure insulin in standardized units, thereby supporting precise administration.

Proper handling of the syringe is critical to ensure effective insulin delivery and prevent dosing errors. Users must carefully prepare the device, ensuring it is graduated in insulin units rather than milliliters, as using a syringe marked in milliliters can lead to significant dosing inaccuracies. During administration, best practices include maintaining pressure on the plunger after injection and holding the needle in place for approximately 5 seconds to minimize insulin reflux and ensure complete delivery.

While syringes remain a reliable method for insulin administration, they are generally considered less convenient than modern alternatives such as insulin pens. They typically involve longer needles and require more steps during preparation and injection, which may affect user compliance and comfort. Despite these drawbacks, syringes continue to play an essential role in insulin therapy, particularly in settings where cost or availability limits access to more advanced delivery systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A syringe is a medical device used for administering insulin, available with fixed or removable needles and in various capacities for accurate dose measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;Syringes used for administering Novolin® R must be disposed of in puncture-resistant containers to prevent injury and contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;A Syringe is a medical device required to administer insulin from a vial, used specifically with Novolin® R and other insulin preparations.&lt;SEP&gt;A syringe is a medical device used to administer insulin correction doses when the insulin pump or infusion set may be malfunctioning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regular Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Regular Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Regular Insulin is a short-acting, clear insulin that does not require mixing but must be checked for clarity before use.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular insulin is a short-acting insulin type used in diabetes management and often mixed with NPH insulin in the same syringe.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular insulin is a short-acting insulin that was mixed with NPH insulin in a clinical evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular insulin is a short-acting insulin that should be aspirated before NPH insulin when preparing a mixed dose.&lt;SEP&gt;A clear, fast-acting form of human insulin that should be aspirated before NPH insulin when mixing.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular insulin is a short-acting insulin that is clear and typically drawn into the syringe before NPH when mixing.&lt;SEP&gt;A short-acting insulin used in combination with other insulins for blood glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695962</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Site">
  <data key="d0">Application Site</data>
  <data key="d1">bodypart</data>
  <data key="d2">An Application Site is a body location, such as the abdomen or thigh, where insulin is injected subcutaneously.&lt;SEP&gt;Application site is the location on the body where insulin is injected, which can experience pain or irritation if cold insulin is used directly from the refrigerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cotton">
  <data key="d0">Cotton</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Cotton or gauze is used to press the injection site if bleeding occurs, without rubbing, to avoid irritation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cotton is used to compress the injection site for 5 seconds after insulin administration to prevent bleeding or leakage.&lt;SEP&gt;Material used in the insulin application process, likely for wiping.&lt;SEP&gt;A material used to compress the injection site after insulin administration and for cleaning purposes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778695666</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FLUXO 1">
  <data key="d0">FLUXO 1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">FLUXO 1 is a document or guide focused on insulin therapy, containing instructions and dialogue about insulin application and storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778694919</data>
