  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isopor">
  <data key="d0">Isopor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Isopor é um material utilizado no transporte de insulina para manter a temperatura, mas deve-se evitar o contato direto entre o gelo e os frascos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frasco Lacrado">
  <data key="d0">Frasco Lacrado</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Frasco lacrado é o recipiente que contém insulina ainda não aberta, que deve ser armazenado entre 2 °C e 8 °C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperatura Da Geladeira">
  <data key="d0">Temperatura Da Geladeira</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperatura da geladeira deve ser mantida entre 2 °C e 8 °C para garantir a estabilidade da insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Therapy Care">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Therapy Care</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Therapy Care refers to the guidelines and practices for managing insulin treatment in patients, including education, monitoring, and storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Care Education">
  <data key="d0">Self-Care Education</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Self-care education involves teaching patients and caregivers about insulin use, application techniques, and glucose monitoring to support treatment adherence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In-Use Insulin Vial">
  <data key="d0">In-Use Insulin Vial</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An in-use insulin vial can be stored under refrigeration or at room temperature up to 30°C and remains usable for 4 to 8 weeks after opening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In-Use Disposable Insulin Pen">
  <data key="d0">In-Use Disposable Insulin Pen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An in-use disposable insulin pen can be stored under refrigeration or at room temperature up to 30°C and remains usable for 4 to 8 weeks after opening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In-Use Reusable Insulin Pen">
  <data key="d0">In-Use Reusable Insulin Pen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An in-use reusable insulin pen should be stored at room temperature up to 30°C and remains usable for 4 to 8 weeks after opening, following manufacturer instructions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multidisciplinary Team">
  <data key="d0">Multidisciplinary Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The multidisciplinary team collaborates with patients and families to adjust insulin doses and support diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696139</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Household Refrigerator">
  <data key="d0">Household Refrigerator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A household refrigerator should maintain insulin between 2 and 8°C; insulin should be stored on middle or lower shelves or in the vegetable drawer, away from walls.&lt;SEP&gt;A household refrigerator is used for storing unopened insulin, with specific placement advised to avoid freezing and maintain stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778696360</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Portal">
  <data key="d0">Portal</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Portal is an online platform providing access to health care guidelines and information on Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 and insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
