<node id="Insulin Asparte">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Asparte</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin asparte is a rapid-acting prandial insulin used in combination with basal insulins like Levemir or NPH in the basal-bolus regimen for pregnant women with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin asparte is a rapid-acting insulin used in combination with insulin detemir in basal-bolus therapy to achieve better glycemic control with reduced risk of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin asparte is a rapid-acting insulin used in combination with other insulins like Levemir or NPH in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975d0ad130a42cf2fe8a0f91e4da2b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698051</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lactation">
  <data key="d0">Lactation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Lactation is a postpartum condition where the safety of Levemir use has not been fully established, requiring medical guidance.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactation is a postpartum condition during which it is unknown whether insulin detemir is excreted in breast milk, though no metabolic effects are expected in nursing infants.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactation is a postpartum condition during which treatment with Novolin® R is considered safe and compatible with breastfeeding.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactation is compatible with Novolin® R Penfill® use, posing no risk to the infant, though dosage adjustments may be necessary.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactation is a period during which Novolin® R FlexPen® use is permitted, poses no risk to the infant, and may require insulin dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698946</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cutaneous Amyloidosis">
  <data key="d0">Cutaneous Amyloidosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cutaneous amyloidosis is a rare skin condition associated with repeated insulin injections at the same site, often developing as a localized tissue reaction in individuals undergoing long-term insulin therapy. It is considered a rare or unknown adverse reaction, with its exact frequency not well established due to limited data from post-marketing surveillance and clinical studies. The condition typically manifests at insulin injection sites and is preventable or reducible through the practice of rotating injection locations, which helps minimize localized skin damage and tissue changes.

The primary clinical significance of cutaneous amyloidosis lies in its potential to impair insulin absorption, leading to delayed insulin action and poor glycemic control. Multiple descriptions highlight that the accumulation of amyloid deposits at repeated injection sites can interfere with the normal pharmacokinetics of insulin, resulting in suboptimal glucose management. This complication underscores the importance of proper injection techniques in diabetes care, as consistent use of the same skin area for insulin administration increases the risk of developing this condition. While cutaneous amyloidosis is specifically linked to insulin therapy, it remains a relatively uncommon complication, often underreported or unrecognized in clinical practice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congestive Heart Failure">
  <data key="d0">Congestive Heart Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Congestive heart failure is a condition where the heart cannot pump sufficient blood, reported in patients using thiazolidinediones with insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Congestive heart failure is a serious condition reported when thiazolidinediones are used in combination with insulin, particularly in at-risk patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Congestive heart failure is a condition reported in patients using thiazolidinediones in combination with insulin, especially those with pre-existing risk factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Congestive heart failure has been reported in patients using thiazolidinediones in combination with insulin, requiring monitoring for symptoms and weight gain.&lt;SEP&gt;Congestive heart failure is a serious condition that may be exacerbated by the combination of thiazolidinediones and insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Congestive heart failure is a condition reported when thiazolidinediones are used in combination with insulin, especially in patients with predisposing risk factors, requiring monitoring for symptoms and weight gain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698945</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-Eclampsia">
  <data key="d0">Pre-Eclampsia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-eclampsia incidence was higher in the Levemir group (10.5%) compared to the insulin NPH group (7.0%).&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-eclampsia is a pregnancy complication observed in a clinical study, with differing incidence rates between Levemir and insulin NPH groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congenital Malformations">
  <data key="d0">Congenital Malformations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Congenital malformations occurred in 5% of infants in the Levemir group and 7% in the insulin NPH group, with severe malformations in 4% and 2%, respectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Congenital malformations are birth defects monitored in clinical studies of insulin use during pregnancy, with comparable rates between Levemir and insulin NPH.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698054</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication Error Prevention">
  <data key="d0">Medication Error Prevention</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Medication error prevention includes checking insulin labels before injection to avoid accidental mix-ups between Levemir and other insulins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698055</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Levemir®">
  <data key="d0">Levemir®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir® is the brand name for insulin detemir, a soluble, long-acting basal insulin analog developed and manufactured by Novo Nordisk for the treatment of diabetes. It is indicated for glycemic control in patients with both type 1 and type 2 diabetes, helping to manage blood glucose levels through subcutaneous administration. Levemir® is not to be mixed or diluted with other insulin preparations, ensuring its stability and predictable pharmacokinetic profile.

The medication is characterized by a prolonged duration of action and a more reproducible absorption profile compared to neutral protamine Hagedorn (NPH) insulin, making it a preferred basal insulin option in various clinical settings. Clinical trials have evaluated Levemir® for both its efficacy and safety, particularly in populations requiring careful glucose management, including pregnant women with type 1 or type 2 diabetes and patients with type 2 diabetes. These studies often compare Levemir® to NPH insulin to assess improvements in glycemic control and hypoglycemic risk.

As an injectable solution, Levemir® provides consistent basal insulin coverage and is registered as a medication product specifically formulated with insulin detemir. Its use supports long-term diabetes management strategies by offering a reliable and sustained insulin effect, contributing to improved outcomes in diabetic care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44f60a4106da6d70fe72d17aa2728296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e2fd1844a95ab6fd4f7d89cdbddbc58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c23215af0c479dce9c09bed4cc782d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba8a91b916675f6f4ef560f6976957e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad7b7e8e5212b6d7ea0f4b0505f82c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Injection Site Reactions">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Injection Site Reactions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin injection site reactions include pain, redness, itching, swelling, bruising, and edema, which can be minimized by rotating injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FlexPen">
  <data key="d0">FlexPen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FlexPen is a pen device for administering Levemir, referenced in the professional prescribing information.&lt;SEP&gt;FlexPen is a pre-filled insulin delivery device used for administering Levemir.&lt;SEP&gt;FlexPen is a pre-filled pen device used for the administration of Levemir, allowing for convenient and accurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Supervision">
  <data key="d0">Medical Supervision</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical supervision is required when changing insulin types, brands, or during special conditions such as pregnancy or illness.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical supervision is required when administering Humulin R to specific populations such as children under 3 years or patients with organ failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Study">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical studies have been conducted to evaluate the efficacy, safety, and metabolic predictability of insulin detemir compared to NPH and glargine insulins.&lt;SEP&gt;A clinical study was conducted on pregnant women with type 1 diabetes comparing Levemir and insulin NPH for safety and efficacy.&lt;SEP&gt;A 26-week, randomized, double-blind clinical study evaluated the efficacy and safety of adding liraglutide to basal insulin in type 2 diabetes patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975d0ad130a42cf2fe8a0f91e4da2b29</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Post-Marketing Data">
  <data key="d0">Post-Marketing Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Post-marketing data from over 4,500 pregnancies indicate no fetal or neonatal malformations or toxicity associated with Levemir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Levemir FlexPen">
  <data key="d0">Levemir FlexPen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir FlexPen is a pre-filled pen device for administering Levemir insulin, requiring specific storage conditions and disposal after 42 days of use.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir FlexPen is a pre-filled insulin delivery device containing Levemir, designed for convenient and accurate administration of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir FlexPen is a pre-filled pen device for the administration of Levemir insulin, designed for convenient and accurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698057</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Zone Change">
  <data key="d0">Time Zone Change</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time zone change refers to the adjustment required when traveling across time zones, which affects insulin administration and meal timing for diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Time zone change is a factor affecting insulin management during travel, requiring medical consultation to adjust insulin timing and meal schedules accordingly.&lt;SEP&gt;Traveling across time zones may require changes in insulin administration and meal timing, necessitating medical consultation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renal Disease">
  <data key="d0">Renal Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Renal disease affects kidney function and may require adjustment of insulin dosage in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698057</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatic Disease">
  <data key="d0">Hepatic Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatic disease affects liver function and may alter insulin metabolism, necessitating dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698057</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adrenal Gland Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Adrenal Gland Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adrenal gland disorders can impact insulin requirements and glucose regulation in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Disorders of the adrenal glands may impact insulin needs and require dose adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Disorders of the adrenal glands can significantly affect insulin requirements in patients using insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pituitary Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Pituitary Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pituitary disorders may affect hormonal balance and influence insulin needs in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Pituitary disorders can influence insulin requirements and may necessitate dose changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thyroid Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Thyroid Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thyroid disorders can alter metabolic rate and insulin sensitivity, requiring changes in insulin dosage.&lt;SEP&gt;Thyroid disorders may affect insulin sensitivity and require dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antidiabetics">
  <data key="d0">Antidiabetics</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Antidiabetics are oral medications used to manage blood glucose levels in patients with type 2 diabetes, often used in combination with Levemir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GLP-1 Receptor Agonist">
  <data key="d0">GLP-1 Receptor Agonist</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GLP-1 receptor agonists are injectable medications that enhance insulin secretion and are used in combination with Levemir for improved glycemic control in type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;GLP-1 receptor agonists are medications used in combination with Levemir for treating type 2 diabetes, requiring dose adjustment to minimize hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal-Bolus Insulin Regimen">
  <data key="d0">Basal-Bolus Insulin Regimen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The basal-bolus insulin regimen combines basal insulin like Levemir with bolus insulin to mimic natural insulin release, requiring one or two daily Levemir doses and individualized adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;A basal-bolus insulin regimen combines long-acting (basal) insulin like Levemir with rapid-acting (bolus) insulin to mimic natural insulin secretion for optimal glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renal Dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">Renal Dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Renal dysfunction affects insulin metabolism, necessitating intensified glucose monitoring and individualized dosing of insulin detemir in affected patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698059</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatic Dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">Hepatic Dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatic dysfunction impacts glucose regulation and insulin clearance, requiring careful monitoring and personalized Levemir dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698059</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diet Change">
  <data key="d0">Diet Change</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Changes in habitual diet can influence blood glucose levels, requiring individualized adjustments in Levemir or concomitant antidiabetic therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Changes in habitual diet can affect insulin requirements and may necessitate dose modification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Concomitant Illness">
  <data key="d0">Concomitant Illness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Concomitant illnesses can alter insulin requirements and glucose metabolism, warranting dose adjustments and close monitoring during treatment with Levemir.&lt;SEP&gt;Concomitant illnesses such as infections or febrile conditions increase insulin requirements, and diseases affecting adrenal, pituitary, or thyroid glands may necessitate insulin dose adjustments.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Conditions such as infections or fever increase insulin needs, requiring dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Titration Guide">
  <data key="d0">Titration Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The titration guide provides structured dose adjustment recommendations for Levemir based on fasting plasma glucose levels to achieve glycemic targets in adults with type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698060</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congenital Malformation">
  <data key="d0">Congenital Malformation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Congenital malformation refers to structural abnormalities present at birth, monitored as a key adverse outcome in pregnancy studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698061</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neonatal Death">
  <data key="d0">Neonatal Death</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neonatal death refers to the death of a live-born infant within the first 28 days of life, monitored in maternal diabetes studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698061</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-eclampsia">
  <data key="d0">Pre-eclampsia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-eclampsia is a pregnancy complication characterized by high blood pressure and organ damage, monitored as an adverse outcome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fetal Macrosomia">
  <data key="d0">Fetal Macrosomia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fetal macrosomia is a condition where a fetus grows larger than average, often associated with maternal diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Large For Gestational Age">
  <data key="d0">Large For Gestational Age</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Large for gestational age refers to a newborn whose birth weight is above the 90th percentile for gestational age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preterm Birth">
  <data key="d0">Preterm Birth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preterm birth is delivery before 37 weeks of gestation, a potential complication in diabetic pregnancies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes In Offspring">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes In Offspring</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes in offspring refers to the development of diabetes in children born to diabetic mothers, monitored up to one year of age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Post-Authorization Safety Study">
  <data key="d0">Post-Authorization Safety Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A prospective, non-interventional post-authorization safety study monitored pregnancy outcomes in women with diabetes using Levemir versus other basal insulins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Levemir Penfill">
  <data key="d0">Levemir Penfill</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir Penfill is a pre-filled pen device for the administration of Levemir insulin, referenced in the professional label.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir Penfill is a cartridge system designed for use with Novo Nordisk insulin delivery systems and NovoFine disposable needles.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir Penfill is a cartridge form of Levemir insulin designed for use with Novo Nordisk injection devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CCDS">
  <data key="d0">CCDS</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">CCDS refers to the Clinical and Consumer Data Sheet, a versioned document containing prescribing information for Levemir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Version 20.0">
  <data key="d0">Version 20.0</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Version 20.0 is a specific release version of the CCDS document for Levemir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Version 2.0">
  <data key="d0">Version 2.0</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Version 2.0 is a specific release version of the Levemir Penfill professional label.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Levemir® FlexPen®">
  <data key="d0">Levemir® FlexPen®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir® FlexPen® is a pre-filled injection system containing insulin detemir solution at 100 U/mL, used for subcutaneous administration in the treatment of diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir® FlexPen® is an injectable insulin delivery device used for subcutaneous administration, containing a clear and colorless aqueous solution, with specific storage, handling, and disposal requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir® FlexPen® is an insulin delivery system designed to administer doses from 1 to 60 units in 1-unit increments, compatible with NovoFine® needles up to 8 mm in length.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir® FlexPen® is a device used for insulin delivery, requiring proper handling and dose selection to ensure accurate administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir® FlexPen® is a disposable insulin delivery device designed for subcutaneous injection, requiring proper handling and priming before use to ensure accurate dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir® FlexPen® is a medical device used for administering insulin, referenced in usage instructions and packaging details.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e28113203725f3be159eca88531cfc4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975d0ad130a42cf2fe8a0f91e4da2b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5561a191d3b525d406e49933648e27bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d212ccdded1e4ccf51af243a8d38b4c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698064</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Levemir® Penfill®">
  <data key="d0">Levemir® Penfill®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir® Penfill® is an injectable insulin solution containing insulin detemir at 100 U/mL, supplied in 3 mL cartridges for use with insulin delivery devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir® Penfill® is a pre-filled cartridge form of insulin detemir designed for use with Novo Nordisk injection devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir® Penfill® is a cartridge used in insulin pens, designed for use with Levemir insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir® Penfill® is a cartridge system for insulin delivery, compatible with injection devices.&lt;SEP&gt;A cartridge-based insulin product designed for use with pen injectors in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e28113203725f3be159eca88531cfc4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c04e4797bbd8720e9c40ccd6a195cf12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c339ce22a1216d3b019fe67db4ddc37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5561a191d3b525d406e49933648e27bf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698064</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RDC 60/12">
  <data key="d0">RDC 60/12</data>
  <data key="d1">regulation</data>
  <data key="d2">RDC 60/12 is a regulatory framework issued by Anvisa governing the submission and modification of medication leaflets in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;RDC 60/12 is a regulatory standard governing the notification and alteration of drug package inserts in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;RDC 60/12 is a regulatory guideline issued by ANVISA that governs the submission and modification of drug package inserts in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;RDC 60/12 is a regulatory guideline related to the notification of changes in drug labeling or package insert texts in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;RDC 60/12 is a regulatory guideline governing changes to drug labeling in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;RDC 60/12 is a regulatory framework governing the publication and modification of drug leaflets in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;RDC 60/12 is a regulatory framework governing the submission and alteration of drug labeling texts in Brazil.</data>
