  <data key="d0">Study Nn 304-1687</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN 304-1687 is a randomized, parallel-group, open-label, multinational trial comparing insulin detemir (Levemir®) and NPH insulin in pregnant women with type 1 diabetes, using insulin aspart as bolus insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study Nn 1250-3561">
  <data key="d0">Study Nn 1250-3561</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN 1250-3561 is a randomized, multinational, multicenter, two-arm, parallel-group, treat-to-target trial comparing insulin degludec (IDeg) and insulin detemir (IDet) as basal insulin with insulin aspart (IAsp) as bolus insulin in children and adolescents with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study Nn 2211-3917">
  <data key="d0">Study Nn 2211-3917</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN 2211-3917 is a 26-week, double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized, multicenter, multinational trial evaluating liraglutide versus placebo added to basal insulin analogs with or without metformin in type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacodynamic Properties">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacodynamic Properties</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharmacodynamic properties describe the biological effects of a drug, including insulin detemir's prolonged action, reduced variability, and dose-proportional response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacokinetic Properties">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacokinetic Properties</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharmacokinetic properties refer to the absorption, distribution, metabolism, and elimination behavior of Levemir in the body.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Pharmacokinetic properties refer to the absorption, distribution, and serum concentration profile of insulin detemir, including peak concentration at 6–8 hours and lower intra-patient variability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Albumin Binding">
  <data key="d0">Albumin Binding</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Albumin binding is a mechanism by which insulin detemir achieves prolonged action through fatty acid side chain attachment to serum albumin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto-Association">
  <data key="d0">Auto-Association</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto-association is a process where insulin detemir molecules strongly associate at the injection site, contributing to delayed absorption and prolonged effect.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time-Action Profile">
  <data key="d0">Time-Action Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The time-action profile of insulin detemir is more reproducible and less variable than NPH insulin and insulin glargine, as shown in clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intra-Patient Variability">
  <data key="d0">Intra-Patient Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intra-patient variability refers to fluctuations in insulin effect within an individual over time, which is lower with insulin detemir than with NPH insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IDet">
  <data key="d0">IDet</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">IDet is the abbreviated form of insulin detemir, used as a basal insulin in clinical trials comparing its efficacy and safety with insulin degludec.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AUCGIR, 0-24h">
  <data key="d0">AUCGIR, 0-24h</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">AUCGIR, 0-24h refers to the area under the curve for glucose infusion rate over a 24-hour period, used as a pharmacodynamic outcome measure in insulin studies.&lt;SEP&gt;AUCGIR, 0-24h refers to the area under the curve for glucose infusion rate over 24 hours, a pharmacodynamic endpoint used to measure insulin effect.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c23215af0c479dce9c09bed4cc782d20</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GIRmax">
  <data key="d0">GIRmax</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">GIRmax refers to the maximum glucose infusion rate, a pharmacodynamic parameter used to assess insulin action.&lt;SEP&gt;GIRmax refers to the maximum glucose infusion rate, a pharmacodynamic parameter used to assess insulin activity.&lt;SEP&gt;GIRmax refers to the maximum glucose infusion rate, a pharmacodynamic parameter used to assess the peak effect of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c23215af0c479dce9c09bed4cc782d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba8a91b916675f6f4ef560f6976957e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 1">
  <data key="d0">Figure 1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 1 illustrates the activity profile of Levemir in patients with type 1 diabetes, depicting its time-action characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 1 is a visual representation of the Medtronic continuous glucose monitoring device, illustrating one of the first glucose monitoring apparatuses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Randomized Controlled Clinical Study">
  <data key="d0">Randomized Controlled Clinical Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A randomized controlled clinical study was conducted to compare the efficacy and safety of Levemir and insulin NPH in pregnant women with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemia Episodes">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia Episodes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycemia episodes were monitored during pregnancy, with no statistically significant difference observed between Levemir and insulin NPH treatment groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adverse Maternal Events">
  <data key="d0">Adverse Maternal Events</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adverse maternal events during pregnancy were reported at a numerically higher frequency in the Levemir group compared to the insulin NPH group.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adverse Fetal Events">
  <data key="d0">Adverse Fetal Events</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adverse fetal events during pregnancy and after birth were slightly more frequent in the Levemir group than in the insulin NPH group.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Live Birth">
  <data key="d0">Live Birth</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Live birth refers to the outcome of pregnancy where infants were born alive, with rates of 83% in the Levemir group and 89% in the insulin NPH group.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cord Blood">
  <data key="d0">Cord Blood</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir was detected in cord blood in approximately one-quarter of newborns, above the lower limit of quantification (&lt;25 pmol/L).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Propensity Score Matching">
  <data key="d0">Propensity Score Matching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Propensity score matching was used to adjust for differences between treatment groups in the analysis of clinical outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gestational Week 36">
  <data key="d0">Gestational Week 36</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Gestational week 36 is a key timepoint for assessing HbA1c levels and evaluating glycemic control during pregnancy in the clinical study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mulheres Grávidas">
  <data key="d0">Mulheres Grávidas</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Mulheres Grávidas refers to pregnant women with diabetes who are treated with insulin therapies such as Levemir or NPH, requiring intensified glucose monitoring.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698074</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Malformações Congênitas">
  <data key="d0">Malformações Congênitas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Malformações Congênitas are birth defects observed in newborns, monitored in clinical studies involving Levemir and NPH insulin use during pregnancy.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698075</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Controle da Glicose Sanguínea">
  <data key="d0">Controle da Glicose Sanguínea</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Controle da Glicose Sanguínea refers to the monitoring and regulation of blood sugar levels, especially intensified during pregnancy in diabetic women.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698075</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Armazenamento do Medicamento">
  <data key="d0">Armazenamento do Medicamento</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Armazenamento do Medicamento involves storing Levemir under refrigeration before use and at room temperature or refrigerated for up to 6 weeks after opening.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;O armazenamento correto do medicamento envolve manter HUMULIN R entre 2°C e 8°C quando lacrado e em temperatura ambiente (15°C a 30°C) por até 28 dias após abertura, protegido da luz e do calor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interações Medicamentosas">
  <data key="d0">Interações Medicamentosas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Interações Medicamentosas refer to the effects of other drugs on insulin requirements, either increasing or decreasing the need for insulin therapy.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Interações Medicamentosas referem-se aos efeitos que outros medicamentos podem ter sobre as necessidades de insulina, podendo aumentá-las ou reduzi-las.&lt;SEP&gt;Interações com outras drogas, como hipoglicemiantes orais, salicilatos, sulfas e antidepressivos, podem potencializar o efeito hipoglicemiante da insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medicamento">
  <data key="d0">Medicamento</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Medicamento refers to Levemir and other pharmaceutical substances that require proper storage, usage instructions, and carry warnings about doping and medication errors.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698075</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lactação">
  <data key="d0">Lactação</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Lactação refers to the period during which a woman breastfeeds her child, and it is noted that insulin detemir's presence in breast milk is unknown but not expected to affect the infant metabolically.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Lactação é um período em que o uso de Novolin® R é compatível com a amamentação, sem riscos para o bebê, embora possa exigir ajuste de dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698982</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direção de Veículos">
  <data key="d0">Direção de Veículos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Direção de Veículos refers to the activity of driving, which may be impaired in patients using Levemir due to the risk of hypoglycemia affecting concentration and reaction time.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698076</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operação de Máquinas">
  <data key="d0">Operação de Máquinas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operação de Máquinas refers to the use of machinery, which can be hazardous for patients on insulin therapy if hypoglycemia impairs their cognitive or motor functions.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698076</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liraglutida">
  <data key="d0">Liraglutida</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Liraglutida is a GLP-1 receptor agonist used in type 2 diabetes treatment, often combined with metformina and studied with Levemir.&lt;SEP&gt;Liraglutida is a GLP-1 receptor agonist used in combination with metformin and studied for its effectiveness in improving glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Liraglutida is a GLP-1 receptor agonist used in diabetes treatment, with no clinically relevant pharmacokinetic or pharmacodynamic interaction observed when co-administered with Levemir®.&lt;SEP&gt;Liraglutida is a GLP-1 receptor agonist used in type 2 diabetes treatment, often combined with metformina and evaluated with Levemir in clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e2fd1844a95ab6fd4f7d89cdbddbc58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba8a91b916675f6f4ef560f6976957e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698076</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gravidez">
  <data key="d0">Gravidez</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Gravidez refers to the condition of pregnancy, specifically studied in women with pre-existing type 1 or type 2 diabetes exposed to Levemir® or other basal insulins to assess adverse outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Gravidez é um estado fisiológico no qual o uso de insulina é seguro e recomendado, com ajustes nas necessidades de insulina ao longo dos trimestres.&lt;SEP&gt;Gravidez é um estado fisiológico durante o qual as necessidades de insulina podem variar, exigindo controle adequado em pacientes com diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Gravidez is a condition during which insulin requirements typically decrease in the first trimester and increase in the second and third trimesters, requiring careful medical supervision.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e2fd1844a95ab6fd4f7d89cdbddbc58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estudo Clínico De 26 Semanas">
  <data key="d0">Estudo Clínico De 26 Semanas</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Estudo Clínico De 26 Semanas is a double-blind, randomized clinical trial investigating the efficacy and safety of adding liraglutida versus placebo in patients with inadequately controlled type 2 diabetes on basal insulin with or without metformin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e2fd1844a95ab6fd4f7d89cdbddbc58</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698077</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peso Corpóreo">
  <data key="d0">Peso Corpóreo</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Peso Corpóreo refers to body weight, monitored as a parameter to assess changes during treatment with Levemir®, liraglutida, and metformin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e2fd1844a95ab6fd4f7d89cdbddbc58</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698077</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FlexPen®">
  <data key="d0">FlexPen®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FlexPen® is a pen device used for the administration of Levemir®, designed for convenient and accurate insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;FlexPen® is a delivery device for Levemir®, designed for subcutaneous administration of insulin detemir.&lt;SEP&gt;FlexPen® is a reusable insulin pen device designed for the administration of insulin, developed and trademarked by Novo Nordisk A/S.&lt;SEP&gt;FlexPen® is a registered pre-filled pen device used for administering Levemir®.&lt;SEP&gt;FlexPen® is a registered trademark for a type of insulin pen delivery device owned by Novo Nordisk A/S and used in the Novolin® R FlexPen® product.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e2fd1844a95ab6fd4f7d89cdbddbc58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba8a91b916675f6f4ef560f6976957e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad7b7e8e5212b6d7ea0f4b0505f82c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b93b5769e8df2e4aa6c2c1dc9e65fd85</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698966</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estudo Prospectivo De Segurança Pós-Autorização">
  <data key="d0">Estudo Prospectivo De Segurança Pós-Autorização</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Estudo Prospectivo De Segurança Pós-Autorização is a non-interventional study monitoring pregnant women with type 1 or type 2 diabetes exposed to Levemir® or other basal insulins to assess adverse pregnancy outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e2fd1844a95ab6fd4f7d89cdbddbc58</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698078</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serum Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Serum Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Serum concentration refers to the level of Levemir in the blood, reaching maximum levels 6–8 hours after administration and achieving steady state after 2–3 doses.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698078</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Half-Life">
  <data key="d0">Half-Life</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The half-life of Levemir ranges from 5 to 7 hours post-subcutaneous injection, depending on the dose administered.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698078</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Steady State">
  <data key="d0">Steady State</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Steady state concentrations of Levemir are achieved after 2–3 twice-daily administrations.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698078</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elderly">
  <data key="d0">Elderly</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Elderly individuals show no clinically relevant differences in Levemir pharmacokinetics compared to healthy individuals.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698078</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients With Renal Impairment">
  <data key="d0">Patients With Renal Impairment</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with renal insufficiency exhibit no clinically relevant differences in Levemir pharmacokinetics.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698079</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients With Hepatic Impairment">
  <data key="d0">Patients With Hepatic Impairment</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with liver insufficiency show no clinically relevant differences in Levemir pharmacokinetics.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698079</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Of Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Change Of Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Changing to another type or brand of insulin must be done under strict medical supervision due to potential differences in concentration, origin, or manufacturing method requiring dose adjustments.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698079</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Penfill">
  <data key="d0">Penfill</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Penfill is a delivery device for Levemir insulin, indicated by the product name Levemir® Penfill® in the text.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Penfill is a delivery device for Levemir insulin, used in the administration of insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Penfill is a cartridge system designed for use with insulin pens, containing 3 mL of insulin solution at a concentration of 100 UI/mL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10</data>
