</node>
<node id="Dose Titration">
  <data key="d0">Dose Titration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose titration refers to the process of adjusting Levemir dosage based on fasting plasma glucose levels to achieve glycemic targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication Disposal">
  <data key="d0">Medication Disposal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Medication disposal includes proper handling of expired or unused medications, which should be discarded at collection points in pharmacies, clinics, or hospitals.&lt;SEP&gt;Medication Disposal refers to the proper handling and disposal of used or expired medications and sharps through designated collection points.&lt;SEP&gt;Used or expired medications, application systems, and needle containers must be discarded at designated collection points such as pharmacies or hospitals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698972</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recyclable Waste">
  <data key="d0">Recyclable Waste</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Recyclable waste includes materials like the Levemir cartilage and package insert that do not contact the medication and can be disposed of in recycling bins.&lt;SEP&gt;The cartridge and package insert of Novolin® R, which do not contact the medication, can be disposed of in recyclable waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Recyclable Waste includes non-contaminated packaging materials like cartons and instruction leaflets that can be disposed of in recycling bins.&lt;SEP&gt;The cartridge and patient information leaflet, which do not contact the medication, can be disposed of in recyclable waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The cartridge and package insert of Novolin® R FlexPen®, which do not contact the medication, can be disposed of in recyclable waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
