  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water For Injections">
  <data key="d0">Water For Injections</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Water for injections is the solvent used in the formulation of the insulin detemir solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Water for injections is the solvent used in Levemir® Penfill® solution to dissolve the active and inactive ingredients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-975d0ad130a42cf2fe8a0f91e4da2b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5561a191d3b525d406e49933648e27bf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698086</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication Error">
  <data key="d0">Medication Error</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medication error refers to accidental misuse, such as confusing Levemir with other insulins, which can be prevented by checking labels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698086</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transport Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Transport Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transport conditions for Levemir require thermal protection, avoidance of direct light, vibration, and freezing, especially during air travel.&lt;SEP&gt;Transport of Novolin® R FlexPen® requires thermal protection, avoidance of direct light, and prevention of vibration and temperature fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peptide">
  <data key="d0">Peptide</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A peptide is a compound like insulin that is broken down into amino acids in the human gastrointestinal tract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698087</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amino Acids">
  <data key="d0">Amino Acids</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Amino acids are the breakdown products of peptides such as insulin in the gastrointestinal tract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698087</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drug Interactions">
  <data key="d0">Drug Interactions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Drug interactions with insulin include medications that either increase or decrease insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Drug interactions refer to the effects of various medications on insulin requirements, either increasing or decreasing the needed dosage.&lt;SEP&gt;Drug interactions with Humulin R may alter insulin needs, including increases due to hyperglycemic agents or decreases due to oral antidiabetics, salicylates, sulfonamide antibiotics, MAO inhibitors, ACE inhibitors, and angiotensin II receptor blockers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Antidiabetics">
  <data key="d0">Oral Antidiabetics</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral antidiabetics are medications that reduce insulin requirements by enhancing glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698088</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MAO Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">MAO Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MAO inhibitors are psychiatric medications that can reduce insulin requirements by affecting glucose metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698088</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta-Blockers">
  <data key="d0">Beta-Blockers</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta-blockers are cardiovascular drugs that can mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia and alter insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta-blockers are drugs that can mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia and delay recovery from low blood sugar, posing risks for diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta-blockers are medications that can mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia and delay recovery from low blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698949</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ACE Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">ACE Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ACE inhibitors are antihypertensive drugs that may reduce insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;ACE inhibitors are medications that may reduce insulin requirements in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;ACE inhibitors are medications that can reduce insulin requirements and are known to interact with glucose metabolism in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698949</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Salicylates">
  <data key="d0">Salicylates</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Salicylates are anti-inflammatory drugs that can decrease insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Salicylates are drugs known to decrease insulin needs by affecting glucose metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Salicylates are compounds that may decrease insulin needs and influence glucose metabolism in patients with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Salicylates are a class of drugs that can enhance the hypoglycemic effect of insulin when used concomitantly.&lt;SEP&gt;Salicylates can reduce insulin requirements in patients using insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anabolic Steroids">
  <data key="d0">Anabolic Steroids</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Anabolic steroids are performance-enhancing drugs that can reduce insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Anabolic steroids are substances that can reduce insulin requirements in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfonamides">
  <data key="d0">Sulfonamides</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfonamides are antibiotics that may lower insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonamides are antibiotics that may lower insulin needs due to their hypoglycemic effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonamides are antibiotics that may lower insulin needs by affecting glucose metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonamides are antibiotics that may interact with insulin, contributing to increased hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Contraceptives">
  <data key="d0">Oral Contraceptives</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral contraceptives are hormonal medications that can increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral contraceptives are medications that may increase insulin requirements in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral contraceptives are hormonal medications that can increase insulin requirements in diabetic patients.</data>
