<node id="Anaphylactic Reactions">
  <data key="d0">Anaphylactic Reactions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anaphylactic reactions are very rare but potentially life-threatening systemic hypersensitivity events associated with Levemir, involving symptoms like generalized rash, angioedema, and respiratory distress.&lt;SEP&gt;Anaphylactic reactions are very rare but potentially life-threatening systemic hypersensitivity reactions to insulin, requiring immediate medical attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Anaphylactic reactions are very rare but serious systemic allergic responses that can occur during insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Anaphylactic reactions are very rare but possible adverse effects of Novolin® R, requiring immediate medical attention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edema">
  <data key="d0">Edema</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Edema is a condition characterized by abnormal fluid retention and swelling in tissues, commonly manifesting as an uncommon adverse reaction associated with insulin therapy. It frequently occurs at the initiation of insulin treatment or following intensified glycemic control, particularly in patients who previously experienced poor metabolic control and subsequently show improvement with therapy. This fluid retention may present either locally at the site of insulin injection or systemically throughout the body.

The occurrence of edema is also linked to the concomitant use of thiazolidinediones (TZDs) and insulin, with reports indicating an increased risk when these agents are used in combination. This association is especially notable in patients with underlying heart disease, who may be more susceptible to fluid accumulation. While edema remains an uncommon side effect overall, its incidence appears to rise in the context of enhanced insulin sensitivity and improved glucose regulation, whether through insulin monotherapy or combined regimens involving insulin and TZDs. The condition is generally manageable but requires clinical monitoring, particularly in vulnerable populations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e023d3ebcda62fd027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
