  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study NN2211-3917">
  <data key="d0">Study NN2211-3917</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN2211-3917 is a 26-week, double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized, multicentre, multinational parallel-group trial evaluating the effect of liraglutide versus placebo when added to basal insulin analogues with or without metformin in subjects with type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c23215af0c479dce9c09bed4cc782d20</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698095</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agonists Of The Receptor Of GLP-1">
  <data key="d0">Agonists Of The Receptor Of GLP-1</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agonists of the receptor of GLP-1 are antidiabetic medications used in combination with Levemir® for the treatment of type 2 diabetes in adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698095</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antidiabetics Orals">
  <data key="d0">Antidiabetics Orals</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Antidiabetics orals are oral hypoglycemic agents used in combination with Levemir® for managing type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NovoFine®">
  <data key="d0">NovoFine®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NovoFine® is a brand of disposable needles compatible with the Levemir® FlexPen® system for safe and effective insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;NovoFine® is a brand of disposable needles designed for use with the Levemir® FlexPen® insulin delivery system.&lt;SEP&gt;NovoFine® is a registered brand of insulin injection needles manufactured by Novo Nordisk A/S.&lt;SEP&gt;NovoFine® is a registered trademark of Novo Nordisk A/S, referring to a line of insulin delivery devices or accessories.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad7b7e8e5212b6d7ea0f4b0505f82c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698980</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="8 °C">
  <data key="d0">8 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">8 °C is the upper limit for refrigerated storage of Levemir® FlexPen®, which must be kept between 2 °C and 8 °C before use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2 °C">
  <data key="d0">2 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">2 °C is the lower limit for refrigerated storage of Levemir® FlexPen®, which must not be frozen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30 °C">
  <data key="d0">30 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">30 °C is the maximum ambient temperature for storing Levemir® FlexPen® during use or as backup for up to 42 days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="42 Days">
  <data key="d0">42 Days</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">42 days is the maximum duration Levemir® FlexPen® can remain in use after initial activation, after which it must be discarded regardless of remaining insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30 Months">
  <data key="d0">30 Months</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">30 months is the shelf life of unopened Levemir® FlexPen® from the date of manufacture, as indicated on the packaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Protection Packaging">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Protection Packaging</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal protection packaging is required for transporting Levemir® to prevent temperature fluctuations, direct light exposure, and excessive vibration.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal protection packaging is required during transport to shield Novolin® R from temperature fluctuations, direct light, and excessive vibration.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal protection packaging is required during transport to prevent temperature fluctuations, direct light, and excessive vibration that could damage the medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Collection Points">
  <data key="d0">Collection Points</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Collection points are designated facilities such as pharmacies, drugstores, health centers, or hospitals equipped with proper medical waste disposal units for used insulin devices and expired medications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Dose Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose adjustment involves modifying the amount of insulin administered based on self-monitored plasma glucose levels, lifestyle changes, or clinical conditions to maintain glycemic targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Dose Adjustment involves modifying insulin dosage based on factors such as illness, physical activity, diet, or changes in insulin preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698972</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plasma Glucose Self-Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Plasma Glucose Self-Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Plasma glucose self-monitoring is the process by which patients measure their own blood glucose levels using a glucometer to guide insulin dosing and detect hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Site Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Injection Site Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection site reactions are adverse effects more commonly observed with Levemir than human insulin, including pain, redness, urticaria, inflammation, bruising, edema, and itching, typically mild and transient.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection site reactions include pain, redness, itching, inflammation, bruising, swelling, and hives, which may resolve within days or weeks and can be minimized by rotating injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Allergic Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Allergic Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Allergic reactions to Levemir are uncommon and include urticaria, erythema, and skin rashes, with anaphylactic reactions being very rare.&lt;SEP&gt;Allergic reaction to insulin includes local reactions like redness and itching, and rare systemic reactions involving rash, breathing difficulties, hypotension, and tachycardia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anaphylactic Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Anaphylactic Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anaphylactic reaction is a very rare but serious immune system response to Levemir, potentially life-threatening and requiring immediate medical attention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refractive Disorder">
  <data key="d0">Refractive Disorder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refractive disorder is an uncommon transient condition that may occur at the start of insulin therapy due to fluid shifts, affecting vision temporarily.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients With Renal Dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">Patients With Renal Dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with renal dysfunction have reduced insulin clearance and are more susceptible to hypoglycemia, necessitating careful dose titration and monitoring when using Levemir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients With Hepatic Dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">Patients With Hepatic Dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with hepatic dysfunction have impaired gluconeogenesis and glycogen storage, increasing hypoglycemia risk and requiring individualized Levemir dosing and close monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Concomitant Medications">
  <data key="d0">Concomitant Medications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Concomitant medications, such as oral antidiabetics or rapid-acting insulins, may require dose or timing adjustments when used with Levemir, especially during treatment transition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulinas De Ação Intermediária">
  <data key="d0">Insulinas De Ação Intermediária</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulinas de ação intermediária são tipos de insulina que têm duração de efeito prolongada e podem requerer ajuste de dose e horário de administração.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulinas De Ação Prolongada">
  <data key="d0">Insulinas De Ação Prolongada</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulinas de ação prolongada são utilizadas para controle glicêmico contínuo e podem necessitar de ajustes na dose e no tempo de administração.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reações No Local Da Injeção">
  <data key="d0">Reações No Local Da Injeção</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reações no local da injeção incluem dor, rubor, urticária, inflamação, equimose, edema e prurido, sendo mais comuns com Levemir do que com insulina humana.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neuropatia Dolorosa">
  <data key="d0">Neuropatia Dolorosa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neuropatia dolorosa aguda pode ocorrer com melhora rápida do controle glicêmico e é geralmente reversível.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodistrofia">
  <data key="d0">Lipodistrofia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodistrofia is a condition characterized by changes in subcutaneous adipose tissue at insulin injection sites, commonly arising as an uncommon adverse reaction to repeated insulin injections in the same area. It encompasses two primary manifestations: lipoatrophy, which involves the loss of fat tissue, and lipohipertrophy, which refers to the abnormal accumulation of fat at the injection site. These alterations in fat tissue can occur due to localized irritation or immune responses triggered by insulin, particularly with older insulin formulations, though they remain possible even with modern analogs.

The condition may impair insulin absorption, leading to delayed or inconsistent uptake of insulin into the bloodstream. This disruption in absorption can result in poor glycemic control and may contribute to episodes of hyperglycemia. The risk of developing lipodistrofia is heightened when injection sites are not adequately rotated, as repetitive injections in a specific region increase tissue trauma and the likelihood of fat distribution abnormalities.

To mitigate the occurrence of lipodistrofia, healthcare guidelines recommend consistent rotation of injection sites within a given anatomical region, such as the abdomen, thighs, or arms. This practice helps prevent localized tissue damage and promotes more predictable insulin absorption. Despite its reduced prevalence with advances in insulin purity and injection techniques, lipodistrofia remains a clinically relevant concern for individuals with diabetes on long-term insulin therapy, warranting patient education and regular clinical assessment of injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amiloidose Cutânea">
  <data key="d0">Amiloidose Cutânea</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Amiloidose cutânea é uma reação adversa de frequência desconhecida associada ao uso de insulina, podendo ocorrer em locais de injeção repetidos.&lt;SEP&gt;Amiloidose cutânea is a skin condition that can develop at the insulin injection site and may impair local insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Amiloidose Cutânea is a rare adverse reaction where amyloid deposits form in the skin, potentially affecting insulin absorption at injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Amiloidose cutânea is an adverse reaction with unknown frequency that may occur at the injection site and can impair local insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Amiloidose cutânea is an unknown-frequency adverse reaction that may occur at the injection site and can interfere with insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698980</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reações Alérgicas">
  <data key="d0">Reações Alérgicas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reações alérgicas ao Levemir são incomuns em regime basal-bolus, mas ocorrem com frequência comum quando combinado com antidiabéticos orais.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reações Anafiláticas">
  <data key="d0">Reações Anafiláticas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reações anafiláticas são muito raras, mas potencialmente fatais, podendo incluir eritema generalizado, dificuldade respiratória e queda pressórica.&lt;SEP&gt;Reações Anafiláticas are severe, potentially life-threatening allergic reactions that may include generalized rash, difficulty breathing, and loss of consciousness.&lt;SEP&gt;Reações anafiláticas are rare but potentially life-threatening generalized hypersensitivity reactions that may include widespread rash, itching, sweating, gastrointestinal disturbances, angioedema, breathing difficulties, palpitations, hypotension, and fainting or loss of consciousness.&lt;SEP&gt;Reações anafiláticas are very rare but potentially fatal systemic hypersensitivity reactions that may include generalized rash, itching, sweating, gastrointestinal disturbances, angioedema, breathing difficulties, palpitations, reduced blood pressure, and fainting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antidiabéticos Orais">
  <data key="d0">Antidiabéticos Orais</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Antidiabéticos orais são medicamentos usados no tratamento do diabetes que podem requerer ajuste de dose ou horário quando usados concomitantemente com insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Antidiabéticos Orais são medicamentos que reduzem as necessidades de insulina ao interagir com o metabolismo da glicose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698982</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoramento Da Glicose Sanguínea">
  <data key="d0">Monitoramento Da Glicose Sanguínea</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitoramento rigoroso da glicose sanguínea é recomendado durante a transição para Levemir e nas primeiras semanas de tratamento.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Malformação Congênita Grave">
  <data key="d0">Malformação Congênita Grave</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Malformação congênita grave refers to serious congenital abnormalities observed in fetuses or newborns, used as an adverse outcome measure in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Malformação Congênita Leve">
  <data key="d0">Malformação Congênita Leve</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Malformação congênita leve refers to minor congenital abnormalities in newborns, analyzed as a safety outcome in the clinical comparison.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Morte Perinatal">
  <data key="d0">Morte Perinatal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Morte perinatal refers to fetal or early neonatal death around the time of birth, used as a critical endpoint in pregnancy outcome assessments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Morte Neonatal">
  <data key="d0">Morte Neonatal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Morte neonatal refers to death of a newborn within the first 28 days of life, monitored as a safety outcome in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aborto Espontâneo">
  <data key="d0">Aborto Espontâneo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Aborto espontâneo refers to the natural loss of pregnancy before viability, analyzed as an adverse pregnancy outcome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Macrossomia Fetal">
  <data key="d0">Macrossomia Fetal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Macrossomia fetal is a condition where the fetus grows larger than average for gestational age, associated with maternal diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grande Para A Idade Gestacional">
  <data key="d0">Grande Para A Idade Gestacional</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Grande para a idade gestacional refers to a newborn whose size exceeds the 90th percentile for gestational age, indicating abnormal fetal growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parto Prematuro">
  <data key="d0">Parto Prematuro</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Parto prematuro refers to delivery before 37 weeks of gestation, monitored as a potential complication in diabetic pregnancies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crescimento Do Bebê">
  <data key="d0">Crescimento Do Bebê</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Crescimento do bebê refers to the physical development of the infant during and after pregnancy, assessed up to one year of age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Do Bebê">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Do Bebê</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes do bebê refers to the presence of diabetes in infants at one year of age, evaluated as a long-term outcome in offspring of diabetic mothers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sangue Do Cordão-Umbilical">
  <data key="d0">Sangue Do Cordão-Umbilical</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sangue do cordão-umbilical was tested for the presence of Levemir, with detectable levels found in approximately a quarter of newborns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estudo Clínico Controlado Randomizado">
  <data key="d0">Estudo Clínico Controlado Randomizado</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Estudo clínico controlado randomizado involved 310 pregnant women with type 1 diabetes comparing Levemir and NPH insulin for safety and efficacy during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698101</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eventos Adversos Maternos">
  <data key="d0">Eventos Adversos Maternos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Eventos adversos maternos include all negative health outcomes in pregnant women, with similar overall frequency between Levemir and NPH insulin groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698101</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eventos Adversos Sérios Durante A Gravidez">
  <data key="d0">Eventos Adversos Sérios Durante A Gravidez</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Eventos adversos sérios durante a gravidez refer to severe complications in mothers or babies, numerically more frequent in the Levemir group.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698101</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nascimento De Crianças">
  <data key="d0">Nascimento De Crianças</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Nascimento de crianças refers to live births from women who became pregnant post-randomization, with 83% for Levemir and 89% for NPH insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698101</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bodenz M">
  <data key="d0">Bodenz M</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Bodenz M is a co-author of a clinical study on insulin detemir, contributing to research on its pharmacological properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
