</node>
<node id="Novolin® R Penfill">
  <data key="d0">Novolin® R Penfill</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® R Penfill is a clear, colorless aqueous solution of fast-acting insulin used in the treatment of diabetes, administered via subcutaneous or intravenous injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R Penfill is a medical product containing human insulin, used for the treatment of diabetes mellitus, available as an injectable solution in a cartridge format.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R Penfill is an insulin product designed for use with Novo Nordisk insulin delivery systems and disposable needles up to 8 mm in length, intended for subcutaneous or intravenous administration under medical supervision.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698966</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Humana">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Humana</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Humana is a biosynthetic human insulin used as a medication to manage blood glucose levels in patients with diabetes mellitus. It is structurally identical to the insulin produced naturally by the human pancreas and is manufactured using recombinant DNA technology, primarily in genetically modified microorganisms such as Saccharomyces cerevisiae and, in some descriptions, Escherichia coli. This synthetic production differentiates it from animal-derived insulins and ensures a consistent, human-identical molecular structure.

Insulina Humana serves as the active pharmaceutical ingredient in several insulin formulations, including Novolin® R Penfill, Novolin® R FlexPen®, and Humulin R (HUMULIN R). These products are indicated for the treatment of diabetes mellitus, particularly in managing hyperglycemia through the regulation of glucose metabolism. The standard concentration of Insulina Humana is 100 UI per mL, with an equivalence of approximately 0,035 mg per UI in its anhydrous form, and it is characterized by a short duration of action, making it suitable for immediate blood glucose control.

The medication is especially utilized in complex clinical scenarios, including during pregnancy and in patients with renal or hepatic impairment, due to its predictable efficacy and safety profile. Its primary therapeutic effect is the lowering of blood glucose levels, contributing to glucose homeostasis in diabetic individuals. While most sources agree on its production via recombinant yeast systems, one description attributes its synthesis to genetically modified Escherichia coli, which may reflect variations in manufacturing processes across different brands or regional formulations. Despite this discrepancy, the consensus confirms Insulina Humana as a recombinant, short-acting insulin critical in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a402290353e4c1eaad827dec818b0f68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NovoRapid®">
  <data key="d0">NovoRapid®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NovoRapid® is a brand name for insulin asparte, a fast-acting insulin analog used in clinical studies comparing its efficacy to Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;NovoRapid® é um medicamento contendo insulina asparte, utilizado como alternativa à insulina humana de ação rápida no tratamento do diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;NovoRapid® is a brand name for insulin asparte, a fast-acting insulin analog used in clinical studies comparing glycemic control with human insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;NovoRapid® is a brand name for insulin asparte, a fast-acting insulin analog used in clinical comparisons with Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zinco Cloreto">
  <data key="d0">Zinco Cloreto</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Zinco Cloreto is an excipient in Novolin® R Penfill, used in the formulation of the insulin solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
