</node>
<node id="Glicerol">
  <data key="d0">Glicerol</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicerol é um excipiente presente na formulação do Novolin® R, contribuindo para sua estabilidade.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicerol is an excipient in Novolin® R Penfill, contributing to the stability of the insulin formulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicerol is an excipient in Novolin® R FlexPen®, functioning as a stabilizer and isotonic agent.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicerol is an excipient in Humulin R that acts as a stabilizer in the injectable solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicerol is an excipient in insulin solutions that helps stabilize the formulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicerol is an excipient in HUMULIN R used to stabilize the insulin solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a402290353e4c1eaad827dec818b0f68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699577</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidróxido De Sódio">
  <data key="d0">Hidróxido De Sódio</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hidróxido de sódio é um excipiente presente na formulação do Novolin® R, utilizado para ajuste de pH.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidróxido de sódio is an excipient used to adjust the pH of the insulin solution in Novolin® R Penfill.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidróxido de sódio is an excipient used to adjust the pH of the Novolin® R FlexPen® solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698968</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Água Para Injetáveis">
  <data key="d0">Água Para Injetáveis</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Água para injetáveis é um excipiente presente na formulação do Novolin® R, servindo como veículo.&lt;SEP&gt;Água para injetáveis is a solvent used in the formulation of the Novolin® R Penfill insulin solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Água para injetáveis is a solvent used in the formulation of the injectable insulin solution in Novolin® R FlexPen®.&lt;SEP&gt;Água Para Injetáveis is a sterile water used as a solvent in injectable pharmaceutical preparations.&lt;SEP&gt;Água para injetáveis is a solvent used in the formulation of HUMULIN R to prepare the injectable solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a402290353e4c1eaad827dec818b0f68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699577</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Farmacologia De Segurança">
  <data key="d0">Farmacologia De Segurança</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Farmacologia de segurança refers to conventional preclinical safety studies assessing the pharmacological and toxicological profile of Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Farmacologia de segurança refers to non-clinical studies assessing the safety profile of Novolin® R Penfill, including toxicity and genotoxicity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Toxicidade De Dose Repetida">
  <data key="d0">Toxicidade De Dose Repetida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Toxicidade de dose repetida refers to the assessment of adverse effects from repeated administration of Novolin® R in non-clinical studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Toxicidade de dose repetida refers to preclinical safety studies evaluating the effects of repeated administration of Novolin® R Penfill.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genotoxicidade">
  <data key="d0">Genotoxicidade</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Genotoxicidade refers to the potential of Novolin® R to cause damage to genetic material, evaluated in non-clinical safety studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Genotoxicidade refers to the potential of Novolin® R Penfill to cause genetic damage, assessed in non-clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potencial Carcinogênico">
  <data key="d0">Potencial Carcinogênico</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Potencial carcinogênico refers to the assessment of cancer risk associated with long-term use of Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Potencial carcinogênico refers to the assessment of cancer risk associated with long-term use of Novolin® R Penfill, evaluated in preclinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Toxicidade Para Reprodução">
  <data key="d0">Toxicidade Para Reprodução</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Toxicidade para reprodução refers to the evaluation of Novolin® R's effects on fertility and reproductive function in preclinical studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Toxicidade para reprodução refers to studies evaluating the impact of Novolin® R Penfill on reproductive health and fertility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Farmacodinâmica">
  <data key="d0">Farmacodinâmica</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Farmacodinâmica describes the biochemical and physiological effects of Novolin® R, including glucose-lowering action through insulin receptor binding.&lt;SEP&gt;A farmacodinâmica da insulina envolve a facilitação da absorção de glicose em células musculares e adiposas e a inibição da produção hepática de glicose.&lt;SEP&gt;Farmacodinâmica describes the glucose-lowering effect of insulin through glucose uptake in muscle and fat cells and inhibition of hepatic glucose production.&lt;SEP&gt;Farmacodinâmica da insulina envolve a regulação do metabolismo da glicose e ações anabólicas em diversos tecidos, como músculo e fígado.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Farmacocinética">
  <data key="d0">Farmacocinética</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Farmacocinética refers to the absorption, distribution, metabolism, and elimination of insulin in the bloodstream, influencing its duration of action.&lt;SEP&gt;A farmacocinética da insulina é influenciada por fatores como dose, via de administração, local de injeção e características individuais, com meia-vida terminal de 2 a 5 horas.&lt;SEP&gt;Farmacocinética refers to the absorption, distribution, and metabolism of insulin in the bloodstream, with peak plasma concentration occurring 1.5–2.5 hours after subcutaneous administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Farmacocinética refers to the study of insulin absorption, distribution, metabolism, and excretion, which is highly variable in Novolin® R due to individual and administration factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Farmacocinética refere-se ao estudo da absorção, distribuição, metabolismo e excreção da insulina, embora não reflita diretamente sua ação metabólica.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Absorção">
  <data key="d0">Absorção</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A absorção da insulina ocorre após administração subcutânea, com concentração plasmática máxima atingida entre 1,5 e 2,5 horas.&lt;SEP&gt;Absorção refers to the process by which insulin enters the bloodstream after subcutaneous injection, influenced by factors such as dose, injection site, and patient-specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distribuição">
  <data key="d0">Distribuição</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A distribuição da insulina no plasma não envolve forte ligação a proteínas, exceto em presença de anticorpos anti-insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Distribuição refers to the spread of insulin in the body, with minimal plasma protein binding except for circulating insulin antibodies when present.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolismo">
  <data key="d0">Metabolismo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">O metabolismo da insulina humana ocorre por meio da degradação enzimática por protease de insulina, enzimas de degradação ou proteína dissulfeto isomerase, gerando metabólitos inativos.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolismo refers to the breakdown of insulin in the body, primarily in the liver and kidneys.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meia-Vida">
  <data key="d0">Meia-Vida</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Meia-vida refers to the short duration insulin remains active in the bloodstream, lasting only a few minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Início Da Ação">
  <data key="d0">Início Da Ação</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Início da ação of Novolin® R occurs within half an hour after administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Efeito Máximo">
  <data key="d0">Efeito Máximo</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Efeito máximo of Novolin® R is reached within 1.5 to 3.5 hours after administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Duração Da Ação">
  <data key="d0">Duração Da Ação</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Duração da ação of Novolin® R lasts approximately 7 to 8 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Via De Administração">
  <data key="d0">Via De Administração</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Via de administração refers to the routes through which Novolin® R is delivered, including subcutaneous, intravenous, and intramuscular.&lt;SEP&gt;Via de administração for Novolin® R includes subcutaneous, intravenous, or intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698971</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normoglicemia">
  <data key="d0">Normoglicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Normoglicemia refers to normal blood glucose levels between 4.4 and 6.1 mmol/L, which Novolin® R helps achieve in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Normoglicemia, com glicemia entre 4,4 e 6,1 mmol/L, foi alcançada com injeção intravenosa de Novolin® R, associada à redução de 42% na mortalidade.&lt;SEP&gt;Normoglicemia refers to normal blood glucose levels (4.4 to 6.1 mmol/L), achieved through intravenous administration of Novolin® R, associated with reduced mortality in surgical patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Normoglicemia refers to the target blood glucose range of 4.4 to 6.1 mmol/L, which when achieved with Novolin® R, was associated with reduced mortality in ICU patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698971</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mortalidade">
  <data key="d0">Mortalidade</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Mortalidade refers to death rate; Novolin® R reduced mortality by 42% in critically ill surgical patients when normoglycemia was maintained.&lt;SEP&gt;Mortalidade was reduced by 42% in critically ill patients when normoglycemia was maintained using intravenous Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Mortalidade was reduced by 42% in critically ill patients when normoglycemia was achieved using intravenous Novolin® R in intensive care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698971</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unidade Internacional">
  <data key="d0">Unidade Internacional</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Unidade Internacional (UI) is a standardized unit of measurement for biological activity, where 1 UI of human insulin corresponds to 0.035 mg of anhydrous insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Unidade Internacional (UI) is a unit of measurement for insulin activity, where 1 UI equals 0.035 mg of anhydrous human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e53353cd9fcafe8d9581b3d0e7980b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698971</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novolin® N">
  <data key="d0">Novolin® N</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® N is an insulin preparation that must be used with a syringe, requiring separate purchase of injection equipment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Bag">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Bag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An Infusion Bag made of polypropylene is used for intravenous delivery of Novolin® R and is stable at room temperature for 24 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698974</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sodium Chloride 0.9%">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Chloride 0.9%</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium chloride 0.9% is an infusion fluid used in combination with Novolin® R, forming a stable solution for intravenous administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride 0.9% is a compatible infusion fluid for intravenous administration of Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium Chloride 0.9% is an infusion fluid compatible with Novolin® R for intravenous use.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride 0.9% is an infusion fluid used in combination with Novolin® R for intravenous administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698974</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dextrose 5%">
  <data key="d0">Dextrose 5%</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dextrose 5% is an infusion fluid compatible with Novolin® R and used in intravenous solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Dextrose 5% is a compatible infusion fluid for intravenous administration of Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Dextrose 5% is a glucose solution used as an infusion fluid compatible with Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Dextrose 5% is an infusion fluid compatible with Novolin® R for intravenous use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698974</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dextrose 10%">
  <data key="d0">Dextrose 10%</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dextrose 10% is an infusion fluid used with Novolin® R in intravenous infusions and maintains stability under specified conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Dextrose 10% is a compatible infusion fluid for intravenous administration of Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Dextrose 10% is a concentrated glucose solution used as an infusion fluid compatible with Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Dextrose 10% is an infusion fluid used with Novolin® R in intravenous infusions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698974</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potassium Chloride 40 mmol/L">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Chloride 40 mmol/L</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium chloride 40 mmol/L is an additive in infusion fluids that is compatible with Novolin® R in polipropylene bags.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium Chloride 40 mmol/L is an electrolyte additive compatible with Novolin® R in infusion solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium chloride 40 mmol/L is an additive in infusion fluids used with Novolin® R, compatible within specified conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698974</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thiol-Containing Medications">
  <data key="d0">Thiol-Containing Medications</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Thiol-Containing Medications are incompatible with insulin solutions and may cause degradation when mixed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698974</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfide-Containing Medications">
  <data key="d0">Sulfide-Containing Medications</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfide-Containing Medications are incompatible with insulin solutions and may lead to insulin degradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698974</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frozen Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Frozen Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Frozen Insulin refers to insulin preparations that have been exposed to freezing temperatures, rendering them ineffective and unsafe for use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novolin® R Frasco_Bula do profissional_Ministério da Saúde (CCDS V.17_V6.0)">
  <data key="d0">Novolin® R Frasco_Bula do profissional_Ministério da Saúde (CCDS V.17_V6.0)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">This is the full title of the professional package insert for Novolin® R, issued by the Ministry of Health, containing detailed usage instructions and safety information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ministry of Health">
  <data key="d0">Ministry of Health</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ministry of Health is the governmental body responsible for issuing and regulating medical documentation and guidelines for pharmaceutical products in the country.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polypropylene Infusion Bag">
  <data key="d0">Polypropylene Infusion Bag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Polypropylene infusion bags are used to hold Novolin® R solutions for intravenous infusion and maintain stability at room temperature for 24 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NovoFine® Needle">
  <data key="d0">NovoFine® Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NovoFine® needles are disposable needles, up to 8 mm in length, designed for use with Novolin® R Penfill and Novo Nordisk delivery systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refraction Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Refraction Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Refraction disorders are uncommon side effects of insulin therapy, typically transient, occurring at the start of treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Adsorption">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Adsorption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin adsorption refers to the initial binding of insulin to the material of the infusion bag, reducing available dosage.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin adsorption refers to the initial loss of insulin due to binding with the material of the infusion bag, affecting dosage accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication Incompatibility">
  <data key="d0">Medication Incompatibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medication incompatibility occurs when drugs containing thiols or sulfides are mixed with insulin, potentially causing degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Products containing thiols or sulfides are incompatible with insulin and may cause its degradation when mixed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cartridge">
  <data key="d0">Cartridge</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The cartridge is a container for Novolin® R Penfill that must not be refilled and should only be used with compatible devices; insulin can be aspirated from it in emergencies using an insulin syringe.&lt;SEP&gt;The cartridge is the insulin reservoir within the Novolin® R FlexPen® that holds a limited amount of insulin for administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc3409d91fe33592f741a0002d70749c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novolin R® FlexPen®">
  <data key="d0">Novolin R® FlexPen®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin R® FlexPen® is a pre-filled insulin delivery device containing 3 mL of suspension, designed for application via an insulin delivery system.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin R® FlexPen® is a pre-filled insulin delivery system used for administering medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89c8be7635129e99145e2508cbd7f95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f59efd4d9af0314b057127c7fefd45c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frasco-Ampola">
  <data key="d0">Frasco-Ampola</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Frasco-ampola is a 10 mL vial containing insulin solution for medical use.&lt;SEP&gt;Frasco-Ampola is a type of pharmaceutical container used for storing medication, such as insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89c8be7635129e99145e2508cbd7f95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f59efd4d9af0314b057127c7fefd45c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carpules (Penfill®)">
  <data key="d0">Carpules (Penfill®)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Carpules (Penfill®) are insulin cartridges designed for use with reusable insulin pens.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89c8be7635129e99145e2508cbd7f95a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sistema de Aplicação Preenchido (FlexPen®)">
  <data key="d0">Sistema de Aplicação Preenchido (FlexPen®)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sistema de Aplicação Preenchido (FlexPen®) is a pre-filled insulin pen device for patient use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89c8be7635129e99145e2508cbd7f95a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
