  <data key="d0">Lanreotida</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lanreotida é um medicamento que pode tanto reduzir quanto aumentar as necessidades de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698984</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Álcool">
  <data key="d0">Álcool</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Álcool pode intensificar ou reduzir o efeito hipoglicemiante da insulina, representando um risco durante o tratamento.&lt;SEP&gt;O consumo de álcool pode causar hipoglicemia em pacientes que utilizam insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699600</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novolin® R Frasco_Bula Do Profissional">
  <data key="d0">Novolin® R Frasco_Bula Do Profissional</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® R Frasco_Bula Do Profissional is the professional package insert for Novolin® R, containing detailed medical and safety information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698984</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Freezer">
  <data key="d0">Freezer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The freezer is a part of the refrigeration system that must be avoided for storing Novolin® R, as freezing the medication is prohibited.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="External Packaging">
  <data key="d0">External Packaging</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The external packaging of Novolin® R protects the medication from light and must be used to store the vial during refrigeration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Light">
  <data key="d0">Light</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct light, especially sunlight, can degrade Novolin® R, so the medication must be protected from light exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;Light exposure can degrade Novolin® R Penfill, necessitating protection by keeping it in its original packaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="6-Week Validity">
  <data key="d0">6-Week Validity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">After opening, Novolin® R remains valid for use for up to 6 weeks when stored at room temperature or in the refrigerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Batch Number">
  <data key="d0">Batch Number</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The batch number of Novolin® R is printed on the packaging and is used to identify the production lot.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manufacturing Date">
  <data key="d0">Manufacturing Date</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The manufacturing date of Novolin® R is indicated on the packaging and is part of the product's traceability information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expiration Date">
  <data key="d0">Expiration Date</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The expiration date of Novolin® R is 30 months from manufacturing, and the medication must not be used beyond this date.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30-Month Shelf Life">
  <data key="d0">30-Month Shelf Life</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® R has a shelf life of 30 months when unopened and stored properly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Travel">
  <data key="d0">Air Travel</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Air travel poses a risk to Novolin® R due to low temperatures in aircraft baggage compartments, which may cause freezing; the medication should not be checked in luggage.&lt;SEP&gt;During air travel, Novolin® R Penfill must not be checked in luggage due to the risk of freezing in the cargo compartment.&lt;SEP&gt;During air travel, Novolin® R FlexPen® should not be checked in luggage due to risk of freezing in the baggage compartment.&lt;SEP&gt;Air travel involves changes in air pressure during takeoff and landing that can cause over- or under-delivery of insulin from the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Endogenous Insulin Production">
  <data key="d0">Endogenous Insulin Production</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with residual endogenous insulin production may require lower daily doses of exogenous insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Residual endogenous insulin production can reduce the daily insulin dosage required by patients with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liver Disease">
  <data key="d0">Liver Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Liver disease can alter insulin requirements and may require dose modification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Regimen Change">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Regimen Change</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Switching from one insulin preparation to another may require dose adjustments and careful monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abdominal Wall">
  <data key="d0">Abdominal Wall</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The abdominal wall is a recommended site for subcutaneous injection of Novolin® R, offering faster absorption compared to other sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gluteal Region">
  <data key="d0">Gluteal Region</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The gluteal region is a possible site for subcutaneous injection of Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deltoid Region">
  <data key="d0">Deltoid Region</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The deltoid region is a possible site for subcutaneous injection of Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potassium Chloride">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Chloride</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium chloride may be included in infusion fluids containing Novolin® R for intravenous use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Notificação Alteração De Texto De Bula">
  <data key="d0">Notificação Alteração De Texto De Bula</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Notificação Alteração de Texto de Bula refers to the formal notification of changes made to the drug's package insert or labeling in compliance with RDC 60/12.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f59efd4d9af0314b057127c7fefd45c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carpules">
  <data key="d0">Carpules</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Carpules are 3 mL insulin cartridges designed to be used with an insulin application system, compatible with Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Carpules are 3 mL insulin cartridges designed to be used with an insulin application system, such as a Penfill® device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f59efd4d9af0314b057127c7fefd45c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ae5fe50adf25db0be3b8cdde6282e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VP">
  <data key="d0">VP</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">VP refers to "Versão para Profissionais de Saúde" (Healthcare Professionals Version), a section of the drug’s package insert intended for medical practitioners.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f59efd4d9af0314b057127c7fefd45c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698990</data>
