  <data key="d0">N/A (Renotificação)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">N/A (renotificação) indicates a re-notification event where no new changes are submitted, often used in regulatory filings to reaffirm previous submissions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f59efd4d9af0314b057127c7fefd45c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novo Nordisk Pharm. Industries LP">
  <data key="d0">Novo Nordisk Pharm. Industries LP</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Novo Nordisk Pharm. Industries LP is a manufacturing site in Clayton, United States, responsible for producing Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VigiMed">
  <data key="d0">VigiMed</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">VigiMed is the adverse event reporting system managed by Anvisa for monitoring and notifying drug-related safety issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous glucose is a medical intervention used to treat severe hypoglycemia when glucagon is ineffective, administered by healthcare professionals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Overdose">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Overdose</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin overdose refers to the administration of insulin in amounts higher than required, leading to progressive hypoglycemia and potentially life-threatening complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin overdose can lead to hypoglycemia with symptoms including apathy, confusion, palpitations, sweating, vomiting, and headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e023d3ebcda62fd027</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sweating">
  <data key="d0">Sweating</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sweating is a symptom of hypoglycemia, often presenting as cold sweat and signaling the onset of low blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Palpitations">
  <data key="d0">Palpitations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Palpitations are a symptom of hypoglycemia, characterized by rapid or irregular heartbeat, commonly occurring during low blood sugar episodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nausea">
  <data key="d0">Nausea</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nausea is a gastrointestinal symptom associated with hypoglycemia and may occur suddenly during low blood sugar events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Headache">
  <data key="d0">Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Headache is a neurological symptom frequently reported during hypoglycemic episodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blurred Vision">
  <data key="d0">Blurred Vision</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blurred vision is a sensory symptom of hypoglycemia, affecting visual clarity during low blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fatigue">
  <data key="d0">Fatigue</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fatigue is a common symptom of hypoglycemia, manifesting as unusual tiredness or weakness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anxiety">
  <data key="d0">Anxiety</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anxiety is a psychological symptom of hypoglycemia, often accompanied by nervousness or tremors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confusion">
  <data key="d0">Confusion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Confusion is a cognitive symptom of hypoglycemia, impairing concentration and mental clarity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seizures">
  <data key="d0">Seizures</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Seizures are a severe neurological consequence of untreated hypoglycemia, potentially leading to brain damage or death.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loss of Consciousness">
  <data key="d0">Loss of Consciousness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Loss of consciousness is a critical outcome of severe hypoglycemia, requiring immediate medical intervention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Rotation">
  <data key="d0">Skin Rotation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin rotation refers to the practice of rotating insulin injection sites within a body region to prevent lipodystrophy and ensure consistent insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="France">
  <data key="d0">France</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">France is the location of Novo Nordisk Production SAS in Chartres, one of the manufacturing sites for Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;France is a country where Roche Diabetes Care France SAS distributes Accu-Chek products.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4f0d15ae81e49555dae7c149b2250be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/IFU Accu-Chek Guide Solo Diabetes Manager.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="United States of America">
  <data key="d0">United States of America</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The United States of America is the location of Novo Nordisk Pharm. Industries LP in Clayton, a production facility for Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698995</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zinc Chloride">
  <data key="d0">Zinc Chloride</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Zinc chloride is an excipient in Novolin® R that helps stabilize the insulin formulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698995</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water For Injection">
  <data key="d0">Water For Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Water for injection is the solvent used in Novolin® R to prepare the injectable insulin solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698995</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Humana Rdna">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Humana Rdna</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina humana rDNA is the active substance in Novolin® R, produced using recombinant DNA technology in Saccharomyces cerevisiae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698995</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frasco-Ampola 10 Ml">
  <data key="d0">Frasco-Ampola 10 Ml</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Frasco-ampola 10 mL is the container for Novolin® R, containing 10 mL of 100 UI/mL insulin solution with a protective plastic seal.&lt;SEP&gt;Frasco-ampola 10 mL is a pharmaceutical packaging format containing 10 mL of a medicinal product.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-468d65c900c2223d037944f792640027</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solução Injetável 100 Ui/Ml">
  <data key="d0">Solução Injetável 100 Ui/Ml</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Solução injetável 100 UI/mL refers to the formulation of Novolin® R, a 100 International Units per milliliter injectable insulin solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698996</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novorapid®">
  <data key="d0">Novorapid®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NovoRapid® is a brand name for insulin asparte, used as a comparator in clinical studies against Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698996</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbA1C">
  <data key="d0">HbA1C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">HbA1c, or glycated hemoglobin, is a clinical marker used to evaluate long-term blood glucose control in patients with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698996</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Absorção De Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Absorção De Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Absorção de glicose refers to the facilitated uptake of glucose into muscle and fat cells mediated by insulin binding to its receptors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698996</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Produção De Glicose Pelo Fígado">
  <data key="d0">Produção De Glicose Pelo Fígado</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Produção de glicose pelo fígado refers to hepatic glucose production, which is inhibited by insulin action as part of glucose regulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82a0f540a03b366d4d206f9c895849de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698996</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novolin® R FlexPen® Bula">
  <data key="d0">Novolin® R FlexPen® Bula</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® R FlexPen® Bula is the official product insert or package leaflet intended for healthcare professionals, containing safety, usage, and storage information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloreto De Zinco">
  <data key="d0">Cloreto De Zinco</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Cloreto de zinco é um excipiente presente na formulação do Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Cloreto de zinco is an excipient in Novolin® R FlexPen®, used to stabilize the insulin formulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eliminação">
  <data key="d0">Eliminação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A eliminação da insulina é determinada pela taxa de absorção no tecido subcutâneo, com meia-vida terminal de 2 a 5 horas, refletindo a cinética de absorção e não a depuração plasmática.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estudo Clínico">
  <data key="d0">Estudo Clínico</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Estudos clínicos controlados com cerca de dois mil pacientes compararam a insulina asparte e a insulina humana de ação rápida quanto ao controle glicêmico.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terapia Intensiva">
  <data key="d0">Terapia Intensiva</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Em uma unidade de terapia intensiva, um estudo com 204 pacientes diabéticos e 1.344 não diabéticos submetidos a cirurgia mostrou redução de mortalidade com o uso de Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="100 UI">
  <data key="d0">100 UI</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">100 UI refers to the concentration of human insulin in 1 mL of solution, where one International Unit (IU) corresponds to 0.035 mg of anhydrous human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1000 UI">
  <data key="d0">1000 UI</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">1000 UI refers to the total insulin content in a 10 mL vial of Novolin® R, equivalent to 10 mL × 100 UI/mL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Página 1 de 6">
  <data key="d0">Página 1 de 6</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Página 1 de 6 is the page indicator in the professional information leaflet for Novolin® R, showing the document's structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frasco">
  <data key="d0">Frasco</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Frasco refers to the container holding 10 mL of Novolin® R solution, equivalent to 1000 UI of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1d9cc89371adea01fc1a946ca6d1690</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion Pump">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® R should not be used in continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion pumps due to the risk of precipitation in the catheters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Injection Site Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Injection Site Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reactions at the injection site may include pain, redness, itching, inflammation, bruising, edema, and urticaria, which can be mitigated by site rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cmax">
  <data key="d0">Cmax</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Cmax refers to the maximum concentration of a drug in the bloodstream, with differences observed between age groups in the pharmacokinetic profile of Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb-Filled Meal">
  <data key="d0">Carb-Filled Meal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A meal or snack containing carbohydrates should be consumed within 30 minutes after insulin injection to prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amyloidosis Cutis">
  <data key="d0">Amyloidosis Cutis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Amyloidosis cutis is a rare skin complication associated with repeated insulin injections, which can be minimized by alternating injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778698999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dosage Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Dosage Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dosage adjustment refers to modifying insulin intake based on factors such as illness, physical activity, diet, or changes in insulin resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Dosage of insulin may need adjustment due to concomitant illnesses, changes in physical activity, diet, or transitions between insulin types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expired Medication">
  <data key="d0">Expired Medication</data>
  <data key="d1">waste</data>
  <data key="d2">Expired medication must not be used and should be disposed of at designated collection points such as pharmacies or hospitals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Puncture-Resistant Container">
  <data key="d0">Puncture-Resistant Container</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A puncture-resistant container, such as a metal can or hard plastic, is used for the safe disposal of used needles to prevent injury and contamination.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Original Packaging">
  <data key="d0">Original Packaging</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The original packaging of Novolin® R Penfill® provides protection from light and should be retained during storage to maintain medication integrity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Light Exposure">
  <data key="d0">Light Exposure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® R FlexPen® must be protected from direct light and excessive heat to maintain stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Flow">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin flow refers to the proper movement of insulin from the cartridge through the needle, which must be verified before injection to ensure correct dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc3409d91fe33592f741a0002d70749c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Infusion">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Infusion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous infusion is a method of administering Novolin® R, which must be performed by healthcare professionals using compatible infusion systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polipropylene Infusion Bag">
  <data key="d0">Polipropylene Infusion Bag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Polipropylene infusion bags are used to hold Novolin® R solutions and maintain stability for 24 hours at room temperature during intravenous infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication Insert">
  <data key="d0">Medication Insert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The medication insert accompanies Novolin® R and contains detailed instructions for proper use and handling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Degradation">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Degradation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin degradation may occur when incompatible substances, such as drugs containing thiols or sulfides, are added to insulin solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refractive Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Refractive Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refractive disorders are uncommon side effects of insulin therapy, typically transient and occurring at the start of treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Painful Neuropathy">
  <data key="d0">Acute Painful Neuropathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute painful neuropathy is an uncommon neurological adverse effect associated with rapid improvement in glycemic control during insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute painful neuropathy is a neurological condition associated with rapid improvement in glycemic control and is generally reversible.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thiols">
  <data key="d0">Thiols</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Thiols are chemical compounds that can cause degradation of insulin when mixed in solution, making them incompatible with insulin preparations.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiols are chemical compounds that can cause degradation of insulin when mixed, leading to incompatibility issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfides">
  <data key="d0">Sulfides</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfides are chemical substances that may degrade insulin when added to its solution, leading to incompatibility.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfides are chemical substances that may degrade insulin when combined, resulting in incompatibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novolin® R Continuous Subcutaneous Infusion Pump">
  <data key="d0">Novolin® R Continuous Subcutaneous Infusion Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® R must not be used in continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion pumps, as specified in special handling precautions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sistemas De Aplicação Preenchidos">
  <data key="d0">Sistemas De Aplicação Preenchidos</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sistemas De Aplicação Preenchidos refer to pre-filled application systems, specifically Novolin® R FlexPen®, each containing 3 mL of injectable insulin solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="3 mL">
  <data key="d0">3 mL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">3 mL is the volume of injectable solution contained in each Novolin® R FlexPen® pre-filled application system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="100 UI/mL">
  <data key="d0">100 UI/mL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">100 UI/mL is the concentration of human insulin in the Novolin R Penfill solution, indicating 100 international units per milliliter.&lt;SEP&gt;100 UI/mL is the concentration of human insulin in the Novolin® R FlexPen® solution.&lt;SEP&gt;100 UI/mL is the concentration of human insulin in the Novolin® R formulation, indicating 100 international units per milliliter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ae5fe50adf25db0be3b8cdde6282e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Protease Enzyme">
  <data key="d0">Protease Enzyme</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Protease enzyme refers to insulin protease or insulin-degrading enzymes responsible for the metabolism of insulin human, cleaving the molecule at specific sites to form inactive metabolites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novolin® R Frasco_Bula do profissional_Privado (CCDS V.17_V6.0)">
  <data key="d0">Novolin® R Frasco_Bula do profissional_Privado (CCDS V.17_V6.0)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® R Frasco_Bula do profissional_Privado (CCDS V.17_V6.0) is the professional package insert document for Novolin® R, containing detailed prescribing and safety information.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R Frasco_Bula do profissional_Privado (CCDS V.17_V6.0) is a professional package insert or prescribing information document for the insulin product Novolin® R, containing detailed pharmacological and clinical use data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frozen Insulin Preparations">
  <data key="d0">Frozen Insulin Preparations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Frozen insulin preparations are insulin solutions that have been exposed to freezing temperatures and must not be used due to potential loss of efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clear And Colorless Insulin Solution">
  <data key="d0">Clear And Colorless Insulin Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A clear and colorless insulin solution is the required physical appearance for safe use; any deviation indicates potential contamination or degradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion Pumps">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion Pumps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous insulin infusion pumps are medical devices used for continuous insulin delivery, but Novolin® R should not be used with them.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refractive Abnormalities">
  <data key="d0">Refractive Abnormalities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refractive abnormalities are temporary visual disturbances that may occur at the beginning of insulin therapy due to rapid changes in blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urticaria">
  <data key="d0">Urticaria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Urticaria is a skin reaction listed as an uncommon adverse effect of insulin therapy, manifesting as hives or welts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Rash">
  <data key="d0">Skin Rash</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin rash is an uncommon adverse reaction associated with insulin use, categorized under skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic And Nutritional Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic And Nutritional Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic and nutritional disorders are a category of adverse reactions associated with insulin therapy, including hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nervous System Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Nervous System Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nervous system disorders are a class of adverse reactions linked to insulin treatment, such as peripheral neuropathy and acute painful neuropathy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vision Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Vision Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vision disorders are adverse reactions related to insulin therapy, including refractive abnormalities and diabetic retinopathy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin And Subcutaneous Tissue Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Skin And Subcutaneous Tissue Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders are a category of adverse reactions from insulin use, including urticaria, skin rash, and lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="General Disorders And Administration Site Conditions">
  <data key="d0">General Disorders And Administration Site Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">General disorders and administration site conditions are adverse reactions associated with insulin therapy, such as edema and injection site reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distúrbios Do Sistema Imune">
  <data key="d0">Distúrbios Do Sistema Imune</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distúrbios do sistema imune include hypersensitivity reactions such as anaphylactic reactions, which are classified as very rare adverse events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distúrbios Do Metabolismo E Nutrição">
  <data key="d0">Distúrbios Do Metabolismo E Nutrição</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distúrbios do metabolismo e nutrição include metabolic conditions such as hipoglicemia, which is very commonly associated with insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distúrbios Do Sistema Nervoso">
  <data key="d0">Distúrbios Do Sistema Nervoso</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distúrbios do sistema nervoso include uncommon neurological conditions such as peripheral neuropathy (painful neuropathy) associated with insulin treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distúrbios Da Visão">
  <data key="d0">Distúrbios Da Visão</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distúrbios da visão include uncommon visual disturbances such as refractive disorders and very rare cases of diabetic retinopathy linked to insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distúrbios Da Pele E Do Tecido Subcutâneo">
  <data key="d0">Distúrbios Da Pele E Do Tecido Subcutâneo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distúrbios da pele e do tecido subcutâneo include skin-related adverse reactions such as urticaria, rashes, lipodistrofia, and cutaneous amyloidosis occurring at the injection site.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distúrbios Gerais E Condições Do Local De Aplicação">
  <data key="d0">Distúrbios Gerais E Condições Do Local De Aplicação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distúrbios gerais e condições do local de aplicação include uncommon local reactions such as edema and injection site reactions associated with insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urticária">
  <data key="d0">Urticária</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Urticária is an uncommon skin reaction that may occur as an adverse effect of insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Erupções Cutâneas">
  <data key="d0">Erupções Cutâneas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Erupções cutâneas are uncommon dermatological adverse reactions associated with insulin use, including generalized rash as part of hypersensitivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reações No Local De Aplicação">
  <data key="d0">Reações No Local De Aplicação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reações no local de aplicação are uncommon local responses to insulin injection, including redness, swelling, or discomfort.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Injection Site">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Injection Site</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin injection site is the anatomical location where insulin is administered, commonly subject to local adverse reactions like lipodystrophy, amyloidosis, and other tissue disturbances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novo Nordisk Production Sas Chartres">
  <data key="d0">Novo Nordisk Production Sas Chartres</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Novo Nordisk Production Sas Chartres is a manufacturing facility located in Chartres, France, responsible for producing Novolin R insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novo Nordisk Pharm Industries Lp Clayton">
  <data key="d0">Novo Nordisk Pharm Industries Lp Clayton</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Novo Nordisk Pharm Industries Lp Clayton is a manufacturing facility located in Clayton, United States, involved in the production of Novolin R insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Registro 1.1766.0003">
  <data key="d0">Registro 1.1766.0003</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Registro 1.1766.0003 is the official product registration number assigned by Anvisa for Novolin R in Brazil.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699006</data>
