  <data key="d0">Frasco-Ampola 10 mL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Frasco-Ampola 10 mL is a pharmaceutical container format holding 10 mL of a medicinal product, used for storage and administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-468d65c900c2223d037944f792640027</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tiazolidinediona">
  <data key="d0">Tiazolidinediona</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tiazolidinediona is a class of medication used in combination with insulin, associated with increased risk of edema and heart failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiazolidinediona (TZD) é uma classe de medicamentos usada em combinação com insulina, associada ao aumento do risco de edema e insuficiência cardíaca.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiazolidinediona is a class of medication used in combination with insulin, associated with increased risk of edema and heart failure, especially in patients with underlying heart disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicose Intravenosa">
  <data key="d0">Glicose Intravenosa</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicose intravenosa is a medical treatment used in severe hypoglycemia for patients who are unconscious or unable to ingest sugar orally.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose intravenosa is a medical treatment used in severe hypoglycemia cases, administered in appropriate medical settings when patients are unconscious or unable to consume sugar orally.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Balas/Drops Açucarados">
  <data key="d0">Balas/Drops Açucarados</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Balas/drops açucarados are fast-acting sugar sources recommended for treating mild to moderate hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tabletes De Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Tabletes De Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tabletes de glicose are fast-acting carbohydrate products used to treat mild to moderate hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cirurgião-Dentista">
  <data key="d0">Cirurgião-Dentista</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cirurgião-dentista is a medical professional involved in the evaluation and guidance for medication use during pregnancy or lactation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amamentação">
  <data key="d0">Amamentação</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Amamentação é um período em que pacientes com diabetes podem necessitar de ajustes na dose de insulina ou na dieta.&lt;SEP&gt;Amamentação is a postpartum condition where diabetic patients may require adjustments in insulin dosage or diet under medical supervision.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Doença">
  <data key="d0">Doença</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Doença refers to medical conditions that can increase the body's need for insulin, such as infections or fever.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alteração Emocional">
  <data key="d0">Alteração Emocional</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Alteração emocional refers to psychological or emotional stress that can increase insulin requirements in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neuropatia Diabética">
  <data key="d0">Neuropatia Diabética</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neuropatia diabética is a type of nerve damage caused by diabetes, which can reduce or eliminate the early warning symptoms of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta-Bloqueadores">
  <data key="d0">Beta-Bloqueadores</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta-bloqueadores are medications that may mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia and affect glucose awareness.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta-bloqueadores are medications that, when used concomitantly, may mask or alter the early warning signs of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoramento Da Glicose No Sangue">
  <data key="d0">Monitoramento Da Glicose No Sangue</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitoramento da glicose no sangue is a recommended practice for patients to recognize hypoglycemia symptoms, especially before activities like driving.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Testes De Sangue E Urina">
  <data key="d0">Testes De Sangue E Urina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Testes de sangue e urina are diagnostic methods used to detect high levels of glucose and ketone bodies in cases of diabetic ketoacidosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Concomitant Diseases">
  <data key="d0">Concomitant Diseases</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Concomitant diseases such as adrenal, pituitary, or thyroid gland disorders, renal failure, or hepatic failure can significantly alter insulin needs in patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dietary Habits">
  <data key="d0">Dietary Habits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Changes in dietary habits can affect the usual dose of Humulin R and require insulin dosage adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pituitary Gland Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Pituitary Gland Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disorders of the pituitary gland can significantly affect insulin requirements in patients using insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thyroid Gland Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Thyroid Gland Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disorders of the thyroid gland can significantly affect insulin requirements, especially when undergoing thyroid hormone replacement therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renal Failure">
  <data key="d0">Renal Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Renal failure may reduce the amount of insulin required by patients, necessitating careful monitoring and dose adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatic Failure">
  <data key="d0">Hepatic Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatic failure requires careful monitoring of glucose levels and insulin dose adjustments due to altered insulin metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children Under 3 Years">
  <data key="d0">Children Under 3 Years</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The use of Humulin R in children under 3 years has not been studied and should only occur under medical supervision.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperglycemic Agents">
  <data key="d0">Hyperglycemic Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperglycemic agents such as oral contraceptives, corticosteroids, and thyroid hormone replacement therapy can increase insulin requirements in patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Antidiabetic Agents">
  <data key="d0">Oral Antidiabetic Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral antidiabetic agents can decrease insulin requirements in patients using insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfonamide Antibiotics">
  <data key="d0">Sulfonamide Antibiotics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfonamide antibiotics can reduce insulin requirements in patients using insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Angiotensin Converting Enzyme Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Angiotensin Converting Enzyme Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ACE inhibitors can reduce insulin requirements in patients using insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Angiotensin II Receptor Blockers">
  <data key="d0">Angiotensin II Receptor Blockers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Angiotensin II receptor blockers can reduce insulin requirements in patients using insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medicinal Plants">
  <data key="d0">Medicinal Plants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The interaction between Humulin R and medicinal plants has not been studied.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nicotine">
  <data key="d0">Nicotine</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The interaction between Humulin R and nicotine has not been studied.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Laboratory Tests">
  <data key="d0">Laboratory Tests</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The interaction between Humulin R and laboratory or non-laboratory tests has not been studied.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unopened Vial">
  <data key="d0">Unopened Vial</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An unopened vial of Humulin R should be stored refrigerated between 2°C and 8°C, protected from light and heat, and not frozen; it has a shelf life of 36 months under these conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Used Vial">
  <data key="d0">Used Vial</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A used vial of Humulin R can be stored refrigerated or at room temperature (15°C to 30°C), protected from heat and direct sunlight, and must be discarded after 28 days regardless of remaining insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Pumps">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Pumps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion pumps are devices used for continuous subcutaneous infusion of Humulin R to manage insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Vessels">
  <data key="d0">Blood Vessels</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Care must be taken during Humulin R injection to avoid puncturing blood vessels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children Over 3 Years">
  <data key="d0">Children Over 3 Years</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Humulin R can be used in children over 3 years without special precautions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insuficiência Cardíaca">
  <data key="d0">Insuficiência Cardíaca</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insuficiência cardíaca is a condition that may be exacerbated by the use of thiazolidinediones in combination with insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Insuficiência Cardíaca é um risco aumentado com o uso combinado de tiazolidinedionas (TZD) e insulina, particularmente em pacientes com doença cardíaca preexistente.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Corticosteroides">
  <data key="d0">Corticosteroides</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Corticosteroides são medicamentos que podem aumentar as necessidades de insulina devido ao seu efeito hiperglicemiante.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hormônio Tireoidiano">
  <data key="d0">Hormônio Tireoidiano</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hormônio Tireoidiano é usado em terapia de reposição e pode aumentar as necessidades de insulina em pacientes diabéticos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agentes Antidiabéticos Orais">
  <data key="d0">Agentes Antidiabéticos Orais</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agentes Antidiabéticos Orais são medicamentos que podem reduzir as necessidades de insulina em pacientes diabéticos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antibióticos Sulfas">
  <data key="d0">Antibióticos Sulfas</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibióticos Sulfas são medicamentos que podem reduzir as necessidades de insulina em pacientes diabéticos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inibidores da Monoaminoxidase">
  <data key="d0">Inibidores da Monoaminoxidase</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Inibidores da Monoaminoxidase são antidepressivos que podem diminuir as necessidades de insulina em pacientes diabéticos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
