  <data key="d0">CNPJ 43.940.618/0001-44</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">CNPJ 43.940.618/0001-44 is the corporate tax identification number for Eli Lilly do Brasil Ltda in Brazil.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d717433722cc9ac8e746440493df9010</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glândulas Suprarrenais">
  <data key="d0">Glândulas Suprarrenais</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">As glândulas suprarrenais, quando afetadas, podem influenciar a resposta ao tratamento com insulina devido ao seu papel na regulação do metabolismo.&lt;SEP&gt;Glândulas suprarrenais are endocrine glands whose diseases can alter insulin requirements in the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipófise">
  <data key="d0">Hipófise</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A hipófise regula hormônios que afetam o metabolismo, e sua disfunção pode alterar a necessidade de insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipófise is a gland that regulates various hormonal functions, and its diseases can affect insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tireoide">
  <data key="d0">Tireoide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A tireoide influencia o metabolismo basal, e alterações em sua função podem impactar a resposta à insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Tireoide is a gland involved in metabolism regulation, and its disorders can influence insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Doença Renal">
  <data key="d0">Doença Renal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A evolução de doença renal pode alterar a depuração da insulina e a necessidade de ajuste de dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Doença renal refers to impaired kidney function, which can alter insulin metabolism and requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Doença Hepática">
  <data key="d0">Doença Hepática</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A evolução de doença hepática afeta o metabolismo da glicose e a capacidade de armazenamento de glicogênio, influenciando a necessidade de insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Doença hepática refers to impaired liver function, affecting glucose regulation and insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglicemiantes Orais">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglicemiantes Orais</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglicemiantes orais are oral medications that lower blood glucose and can interact with insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfas">
  <data key="d0">Sulfas</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfas are medications that can decrease glycemia and potentially interact with insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antidepressivos">
  <data key="d0">Antidepressivos</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Antidepressivos are drugs that, in some cases, can lower blood sugar and interact with insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bebidas Alcoólicas">
  <data key="d0">Bebidas Alcoólicas</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bebidas alcoólicas are alcoholic beverages whose excessive consumption can increase the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pacientes">
  <data key="d0">Pacientes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pacientes are individuals with diabetes who require insulin therapy and must monitor for symptoms of hypoglycemia and hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agua Para Injecao">
  <data key="d0">Agua Para Injecao</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agua para Injeção is the solvent used in the formulation of Humulin R, ensuring sterility and proper dilution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidroxido De Sodio">
  <data key="d0">Hidroxido De Sodio</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hidróxido de Sódio may be added to adjust the pH of the Humulin R solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acido Cloridrico">
  <data key="d0">Acido Cloridrico</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ácido Clorídrico may be added to adjust the pH of the Humulin R solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uso Pediatrico Acima De 3 Anos">
  <data key="d0">Uso Pediatrico Acima De 3 Anos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Uso Pediatrico Acima de 3 Anos indicates that Humulin R is approved for pediatric use in children over three years of age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estudo Cruzado Duplo-Cego">
  <data key="d0">Estudo Cruzado Duplo-Cego</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Estudo Cruzado Duplo-Cego was a six-week clinical trial comparing biosynthetic human insulin with porcine and bovine insulin in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Estudo Cruzado Duplo-Cego was a clinical trial involving diabetic patients comparing biosynthetic human insulin with animal-derived insulins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Suina">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Suina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Suína is porcine insulin previously used in diabetes treatment, compared with biosynthetic human insulin in clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Bovina">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Bovina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Bovina is bovine insulin used in diabetes treatment, compared with biosynthetic human insulin in clinical studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina Bovina is a type of animal-derived insulin used in diabetes treatment, extracted from cows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Humana Biossintetica">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Humana Biossintetica</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Humana Biossintética is biosynthetic human insulin used in clinical trials and as a therapeutic alternative to animal-derived insulins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicemia Media">
  <data key="d0">Glicemia Media</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicemia Média refers to the average blood glucose level measured from seven capillary blood samples in a single day during clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indice M Modificado">
  <data key="d0">Indice M Modificado</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Índice M Modificado is a metric used to assess glycemic control in diabetic patients during clinical evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Necessidade De Insulina Diaria Total">
  <data key="d0">Necessidade De Insulina Diaria Total</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Necessidade de Insulina Diária Total refers to the total daily insulin requirement observed in patients during treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Episodios Hipoglicemicos">
  <data key="d0">Episodios Hipoglicemicos</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Episódios Hipoglicêmicos are low blood sugar events that were infrequent in patients using biosynthetic human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Efeitos Imunologicos">
  <data key="d0">Efeitos Imunologicos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Efeitos Imunológicos refer to immunological responses observed when transitioning patients from animal insulins to biosynthetic human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anticorpos Anti-Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Anticorpos Anti-Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Anticorpos anti-insulina são proteínas produzidas pelo sistema imunológico em resposta à insulina não homóloga, cujos níveis podem diminuir com a troca para insulina humana.&lt;SEP&gt;Anticorpos Anti-Insulina are antibodies measured in patients to evaluate immune response to different insulin types.&lt;SEP&gt;Anticorpos Anti-Insulina are immune system proteins that bind to insulin, potentially affecting its efficacy, with levels decreasing upon switching to human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Farmacocinetica Da Insulina Humana Biossintetica">
  <data key="d0">Farmacocinetica Da Insulina Humana Biossintetica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Farmacocinética da Insulina Humana Biossintética refers to the absorption, distribution, and effects of biosynthetic human insulin influencing blood glucose response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VV-REG-426622 v2.0">
  <data key="d0">VV-REG-426622 v2.0</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">VV-REG-426622 v2.0 is a document version identifier associated with the Humulin R product information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CDS01JUN20">
  <data key="d0">CDS01JUN20</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">CDS01JUN20 is a code or identifier appearing on the document, likely related to batch or document control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67bb351395e7176e28675caef7c9b6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Escherichia Coli">
  <data key="d0">Escherichia Coli</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Escherichia coli é uma bactéria não patogênica geneticamente alterada para produzir insulina humana.&lt;SEP&gt;Escherichia Coli is a non-pathogenic bacterial strain genetically modified to produce human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Não Homóloga">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Não Homóloga</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina não homóloga refere-se a formas de insulina de origem animal (como bovina ou suína) que diferem estruturalmente da insulina humana.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fígado">
  <data key="d0">Fígado</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fígado é um órgão onde a insulina promove a captação e armazenamento de glicose como glicogênio, inibe a gliconeogênese e favorece a conversão de glicose em gordura.&lt;SEP&gt;Fígado é um órgão onde a insulina promove a captação e o armazenamento de glicose como glicogênio, inibe a gliconeogênese e favorece a conversão de glicose em gordura.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amiloidose Cutânea Localizada">
  <data key="d0">Amiloidose Cutânea Localizada</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Amiloidose cutânea localizada é uma condição rara onde depósitos de amiloide na pele podem interferir na absorção de insulina, levando à hiperglicemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Amiloidose cutânea localizada é uma complicação rara do uso crônico de insulina, associada a má absorção do hormônio e hiperglicemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Dose De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A dose de insulina influencia o tempo de início, duração e intensidade da ação, variando conforme necessidade individual e condições fisiológicas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local De Injeção">
  <data key="d0">Local De Injeção</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">O local de injeção afeta a absorção da insulina, com variações na farmacocinética dependendo da região corporal utilizada.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperatura">
  <data key="d0">Temperatura</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A temperatura corporal ou ambiental pode afetar a disponibilidade sanguínea e a absorção da insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alterações Na Necessidade De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Alterações Na Necessidade De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fatores fisiológicos e patológicos, como doenças endócrinas ou hepáticas, podem alterar a necessidade de insulina em pacientes diabéticos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sintomas De Alerta De Hipoglicemia">
  <data key="d0">Sintomas De Alerta De Hipoglicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alguns pacientes relatam que os sintomas de alerta de hipoglicemia são menos pronunciados ao mudar da insulina animal para a insulina humana.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Hypoglycemic Agents">
  <data key="d0">Oral Hypoglycemic Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral hypoglycemic agents are medications that lower blood glucose and can interact with insulin, increasing the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antidepressants">
  <data key="d0">Antidepressants</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Certain antidepressants are reported to interact with insulin, potentially lowering blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Humana Biossintética">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Humana Biossintética</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Humana Biossintética is a synthetic form of human insulin produced using genetically modified Escherichia coli, used in the treatment of diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Suína">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Suína</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Suína is a type of animal-derived insulin used in diabetes treatment, extracted from pigs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Via Subcutânea">
  <data key="d0">Via Subcutânea</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Via Subcutânea is the preferred route of administration for Humulin R, involving injection under the skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tratamento Com Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Tratamento Com Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Tratamento Com Insulina refers to the therapeutic use of insulin to regulate blood glucose levels in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Farmacocinética Da IHB">
  <data key="d0">Farmacocinética Da IHB</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Farmacocinética Da IHB refers to the absorption, distribution, metabolism, and excretion characteristics of biosynthetic human insulin influencing blood glucose response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Concentração De Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Concentração De Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Concentração De Glicose refers to the level of glucose in the blood, a key parameter monitored in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Índice M Modificado">
  <data key="d0">Índice M Modificado</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Índice M Modificado is a metric used to assess glycemic control in diabetic patients during treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mistura De Insulina Bovina-Suína">
  <data key="d0">Mistura De Insulina Bovina-Suína</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Mistura De Insulina Bovina-Suína is a combination of bovine and porcine insulin used in diabetes treatment before switching to human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91d6c1005cdb303d60e909b05fe5abb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cérebro">
  <data key="d0">Cérebro</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cérebro é um órgão que não depende da insulina para o transporte de glicose, diferentemente de outros tecidos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aminoácidos">
  <data key="d0">Aminoácidos</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aminoácidos são moléculas cujo transporte intracelular é facilitado pela insulina, contribuindo para o anabolismo proteico.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicogênio">
  <data key="d0">Glicogênio</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicogênio é a forma de armazenamento da glicose no fígado, cuja formação é estimulada pela insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gordura">
  <data key="d0">Gordura</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gordura é um tipo de lipídio cuja produção a partir do excesso de glicose é promovida pela insulina no fígado.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Farmacocinética da Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Farmacocinética da Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A farmacocinética da insulina não reflete diretamente sua ação metabólica, sendo mais apropriado avaliar a atividade hormonal por meio de curvas de utilização de glicose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perfil de Resposta Glicêmica">
  <data key="d0">Perfil de Resposta Glicêmica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">O perfil de resposta glicêmica varia entre indivíduos e depende de fatores como dose, local de injeção e atividade física.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tempo de Início de Ação">
  <data key="d0">Tempo de Início de Ação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">O tempo de início de ação da insulina é definido como o momento da primeira alteração na taxa de infusão de glicose em estudos euglicêmicos após a administração da dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Dose de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A dose de insulina influencia a duração e intensidade de sua ação, sendo um fator determinante no controle glicêmico.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699613</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local de Injeção">
  <data key="d0">Local de Injeção</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">O local de injeção afeta a absorção e a ação da insulina, podendo influenciar o perfil de resposta glicêmica.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699613</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Animal">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Animal</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina animal é derivada de fontes bovinas ou suínas e difere estruturalmente da insulina humana, podendo causar diferentes respostas glicêmicas e sintomas de alerta de hipoglicemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699613</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alteração de Regime de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Alteração de Regime de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Qualquer alteração no regime de insulina, incluindo concentração, tipo, espécie ou método de fabricação, deve ser feita com cautela e sob supervisão médica.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699613</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoramento da Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Monitoramento da Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">O monitoramento frequente da glicose é necessário durante mudanças no regime de insulina para prevenir hipoglicemia ou hiperglicemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699613</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interação Medicamentosa">
  <data key="d0">Interação Medicamentosa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Certos medicamentos como hipoglicemiantes orais, salicilatos, sulfas e antidepressivos podem potencializar o efeito da insulina, aumentando o risco de hipoglicemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699613</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemia Symptoms">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia Symptoms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycemia symptoms range from mild to severe and include sudden onset of sweating, dizziness, palpitations, tremor, hunger, restlessness, drowsiness, sleep disturbances, anxiety, blurred vision, difficulty speaking, depressed mood, tingling in extremities, lightheadedness, inability to concentrate, headache, irritability, abnormal behavior, unsteady movement, and personality changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778699613</data>
