</node>
<node id="Basal 1">
  <data key="d0">Basal 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal 1 is a named basal insulin infusion pattern used in insulin pump therapy for managing diabetes, specifically designed to deliver a continuous, adjustable rate of insulin over defined time segments throughout the day. It functions as a configurable and programmable profile within the insulin pump system, allowing healthcare providers or users to set, edit, and save specific insulin delivery rates based on individual patient needs. The pattern consists of multiple time-based segments, each with designated start and end times and corresponding insulin unit-per-hour (U/h) rates, enabling precise glycemic control tailored to daily physiological demands.

Initially, Basal 1 was programmed with a rate of 0.750 U/h, which was later adjusted to 0.900 U/h, reflecting the dynamic nature of insulin therapy and the need for personalized dose optimization. This adjustment capability underscores its role as an editable and adaptable basal rate profile, integral to ongoing diabetes management. The total daily insulin delivery associated with Basal 1 is 19.25 units, indicating a quantifiable and monitored regimen designed to maintain baseline insulin levels in the absence of food intake or other insulin demands.

As a pre-programmed and selectable basal pattern, Basal 1 can be reviewed, activated, modified, or replaced within the insulin pump interface, making it a core component of advanced insulin delivery systems. It is stored in the pump’s memory as one of potentially several basal profiles, allowing users to switch between different patterns based on lifestyle, activity, or metabolic changes. Overall, Basal 1 represents a structured, customizable, and clinically relevant insulin delivery strategy essential for effective long-term diabetes care.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal 1 is a default basal insulin delivery pattern that can be edited, copied, or deleted in the pump settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cae8b84f90a8e9c929a19f036d8f1e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1134674d4e1ab07998567f3fa77e251d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feedb8da72881894bf4c6529f7baca60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6366eda06d68d222b47729f7ca841b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7534f3bc09ac6e2eece38e12eb89cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707420</data>
