</node>
<node id="Total 24 Hr">
  <data key="d0">Total 24 Hr</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Total 24 Hr refers to the cumulative daily insulin dosage, measured in units (U), delivered over a full day according to the basal pattern.&lt;SEP&gt;Total 24 Hr represents the cumulative amount of basal insulin delivered over a 24-hour period, calculated from the basal rate settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Total 24 Hr refers to the total insulin units administered over a 24-hour period, initially recorded as 18 U and later adjusted to 21.6 U.&lt;SEP&gt;Total 24 Hr represents the total daily insulin dose delivered over a 24-hour period, such as 19.7 U or 21.6 U, based on basal settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cae8b84f90a8e9c929a19f036d8f1e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b28f926a642d5f692433ed41fafafa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6366eda06d68d222b47729f7ca841b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704140</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Radiation">
  <data key="d0">Radiation</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Radiation is a concern that may disable an insulin pump or damage its insulin delivery mechanism, potentially causing excessive insulin infusion and hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation from x-ray, CT scan, or other sources can damage the pump components and lead to insulin over-delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
