  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="International Security Commissioner">
  <data key="d0">International Security Commissioner</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The international security commissioner is the equivalent of the TSA commissioner abroad and can be contacted if difficulties arise during international travel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700890</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate ratio is a setting that defines how many grams of carbohydrates are covered by one unit of insulin, used in bolus calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate Ratio is the numerical value representing grams of carbohydrates covered by one unit of insulin, equivalent to Ratio HC.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate Ratio refers to the amount of carbohydrates covered by one unit of insulin, used as a parameter in the Bolus Wizard function.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate ratio is a user-configured setting that defines how much insulin is needed per gram of carbohydrate, used by the Bolus Wizard for dose calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate Ratio refers to the amount of carbohydrates covered by one unit of insulin, used as a parameter in the Bolus Wizard function.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbohydrate ratio is a setting that defines how many grams of carbohydrates are covered by one unit of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate Ratio is a setting in the Bolus Wizard indicating the amount of carbohydrates covered by one unit of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-560db599319a34f19671d0bafeda5775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1250027f75a49e3288b12fc80a630d33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b299154da4c58d8322b7ac4e3af2f5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc77598dbeb5980c719d1d54a6c3ab77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-402361ced0649a06619dcaf93b0eb651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704104</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Target">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Target</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose target is a user-defined blood glucose level that the system aims to maintain, used in SmartGuard and Bolus Wizard calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose Target is the desired blood glucose level range set by the user, used by the Bolus Wizard to determine appropriate insulin dosage.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose target is the desired blood glucose level set for an individual, used as a reference point in correction bolus calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose Target is the desired blood glucose level set by a healthcare professional, used as a reference point in the Bolus Wizard calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose target is a user-defined blood glucose level that the pump uses as a reference for automated insulin delivery in SmartGuard mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-560db599319a34f19671d0bafeda5775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0f18d3b5098557dfd71a1955adc3a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc77598dbeb5980c719d1d54a6c3ab77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Duration Of Insulin Activity">
  <data key="d0">Duration Of Insulin Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Duration Of Insulin Activity is the length of time insulin remains active in the body, set in the Bolus Wizard to improve dose accuracy.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Duration of insulin activity is a configurable setting that defines how long a bolus of insulin remains active in the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-560db599319a34f19671d0bafeda5775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704118</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Wizard™">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Wizard™</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Wizard™ is a proprietary feature developed by Medtronic MiniMed, Inc., integrated into certain models of insulin pumps, particularly within the MiniMed™ line, including the MiniMed™ 640G system. It functions as an automated calculation tool designed to assist individuals with diabetes in determining accurate insulin bolus doses for both mealtime and correction of high blood glucose levels. The system computes the required insulin dose by analyzing multiple user-specific inputs, including current blood glucose levels, carbohydrate intake, insulin-to-carbohydrate ratios, insulin sensitivity factors, and target glucose levels.

A key aspect of Bolus Wizard™ is its ability to account for active insulin—insulin that remains effective in the body from previous bolus doses—thereby helping to prevent insulin stacking and reduce the risk of hypoglycemia. This functionality is especially prominent in the MiniMed™ 640G insulin pump, where the feature not only calculates recommended bolus doses but also displays the amount of insulin still active in the body. By combining meal bolus and correction bolus calculations into a single, integrated recommendation, Bolus Wizard™ streamlines decision-making and supports more precise glucose management.

In addition to dose calculation, the feature tracks insulin administration history, maintains records of carbohydrate intake, and logs glucose readings, contributing to improved treatment monitoring and long-term diabetes management. Bolus Wizard™ operates based on pre-programmed user settings and real-time data inputs, making it a comprehensive tool for personalized insulin therapy. As a registered trademark of Medtronic MiniMed, Inc., Bolus Wizard™ is specifically associated with Medtronic’s insulin pump technologies and is not a generic function available across all diabetes devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-560db599319a34f19671d0bafeda5775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b6ed50dde321317a11d8dcc6ef2a579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191c82775d35bbc705205ed493c43c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4f908910b79b1f9ccf095fd5fb4035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bfad6c7b0e936c6a9c113798a2d963e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0f18d3b5098557dfd71a1955adc3a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d266340be3ade6b2a58718fd568af4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb7ffc723b939ad50f1b00ca6ec8b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8af713fd3913ed050d96cdd321bca3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-425759c12d133ef4832928e8f5d50896</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Dual">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Dual</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus dual is an insulin delivery function that administers a portion of insulin immediately and the remainder over time, useful for managing glucose levels after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus dual is a combined insulin delivery method that administers part of the dose immediately and part over time to manage meals with high fat and carbohydrate content.&lt;SEP&gt;A bolus dual is an insulin delivery method that administers a portion of insulin immediately and the remainder over a set period of time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39f2ee843ae28cc44b37c7f51f7722a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b8d4c3fde5ebf7bc3593f47b765f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e15921d1b7d6415709a3d0c795cefc3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Cuadrado">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Cuadrado</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus cuadrado is an insulin delivery function that administers a bolus over a prolonged period, used for meals with delayed digestion or high fat content.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus cuadrado is an insulin delivery method that administers a dose over a prolonged period, typically between 30 minutes to 8 hours, to match delayed glucose absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;A bolus cuadrado is an insulin delivery method that administers insulin gradually over a specified duration to manage delayed glucose elevation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39f2ee843ae28cc44b37c7f51f7722a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b8d4c3fde5ebf7bc3593f47b765f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e15921d1b7d6415709a3d0c795cefc3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Normal">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Normal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus normal is an insulin delivery method that administers a single immediate dose of insulin, typically used to cover mealtime glucose or correct high blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;A bolus normal is a standard insulin bolus administered immediately to manage blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39f2ee843ae28cc44b37c7f51f7722a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e15921d1b7d6415709a3d0c795cefc3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704181</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equipo Médico">
  <data key="d0">Equipo Médico</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">El equipo médico es el grupo de profesionales de la salud que calcula y recomienda los índices basales adecuados para el paciente al comenzar a usar la bomba de insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;El equipo médico proporciona los ajustes personales necesarios para configurar la función Bolus Wizard.&lt;SEP&gt;The equipo médico is responsible for guiding patients on insulin therapy, adjusting pump settings, and managing glucose-related health issues.&lt;SEP&gt;El equipo médico es un grupo de profesionales de la salud que supervisa y asesora a los pacientes en el uso de terapias de insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;El equipo médico es el grupo de profesionales sanitarios que supervisan y asesoran a los pacientes sobre su terapia con bomba de insulina y ajustes personalizados.&lt;SEP&gt;The Equipo Médico is responsible for providing medical guidance and therapy-related recommendations for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39f2ee843ae28cc44b37c7f51f7722a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1cf60a28692e32a5ea7181943e41938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1064c42775365801d8ca4df533dcda0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Función Bolus Wizard">
  <data key="d0">Función Bolus Wizard</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">La función Bolus Wizard calcula la cantidad de insulina del bolus basándose en la lectura de glucosa en sangre y los hidratos de carbono consumidos, utilizando ajustes médicos personalizados.&lt;SEP&gt;The función bolus wizard is a feature that calculates insulin bolus doses based on glucose levels but cannot administer square boluses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39f2ee843ae28cc44b37c7f51f7722a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1064c42775365801d8ca4df533dcda0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700893</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gastroparesia">
  <data key="d0">Gastroparesia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gastroparesia is a condition causing delayed digestion, which may require the use of square bolus for better glucose management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39f2ee843ae28cc44b37c7f51f7722a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700893</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucosa En Sangre">
  <data key="d0">Glucosa En Sangre</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucosa en sangre refers to blood glucose levels, which must be monitored frequently during insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;La glucosa en sangre es un indicador critico en el manejo de la diabetes, cuyos niveles deben monitorearse regularmente, especialmente cuando se interrumpe la administracion de insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucosa En Sangre refers to blood glucose levels, which must be monitored regularly to ensure proper insulin dosing and diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucosa en sangre es un valor fisiológico que se monitorea continuamente en personas con diabetes para mantenerlo dentro de un rango deseado.&lt;SEP&gt;La glucosa en sangre aumenta cuando no hay suficiente insulina disponible, lo que es un signo clave de advertencia de cetoacidosis diabetica.&lt;SEP&gt;La glucosa en sangre es una sustancia química cuyos niveles deben monitorearse y calibrarse en terapias de diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucosa En Sangre refers to blood glucose levels, which decrease gradually after alcohol consumption and may result in hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39f2ee843ae28cc44b37c7f51f7722a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357e07e3b068c4c6d31ac6913e35178f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17d4cfa9183f9c1eb5a0c2212479127a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guía De Consulta Rápida">
  <data key="d0">Guía De Consulta Rápida</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The guía de consulta rápida provides safety rules and instructions for responding to high or low blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39f2ee843ae28cc44b37c7f51f7722a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700893</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglucemia">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglucemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglucemia is a condition characterized by abnormally low levels of glucose in the blood, typically defined as below 70 mg/dL. It commonly occurs as a result of excessive insulin administration, particularly in the context of diabetes therapy management, and is frequently discussed as a significant risk in insulin treatment regimens. The condition may also arise due to variability in insulin absorption, physical activity, alcohol consumption, or insufficient counterregulatory responses, such as the lack of glucagon to enable the liver to restore glucose levels.

Episodes of hipoglucemia require immediate intervention to prevent complications. Treatment typically involves the consumption of carbohydrates through food or drink, followed by re-measurement of blood glucose to ensure recovery. Severe or frequent occurrences necessitate medical attention and may prompt adjustments in therapy. Importantly, hipoglucemia is not directly reflected in hemoglobin A1C measurements, which means it can go undetected in standard long-term glucose monitoring, highlighting the need for additional tracking methods.

Technological systems such as the MiniMed™ 640G aim to mitigate the risk of hipoglucemia by providing alerts and continuous trend monitoring to detect downward glucose trends before critical levels are reached. Given its potential severity and impact on patient safety, hipoglucemia remains a central concern in the management of diabetes, requiring vigilant monitoring, prompt treatment, and individualized therapeutic strategies to maintain blood glucose within a safe range.&lt;SEP&gt;La hipoglucemia es una condición que puede ocurrir si se administra una cantidad excesiva de insulina, lo que reduce peligrosamente los niveles de glucosa en sangre.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglucemia refers to low blood glucose levels, a condition that Thomas is prone to, especially at night after running.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39f2ee843ae28cc44b37c7f51f7722a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edf22db77193377cf626b08881757226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1cf60a28692e32a5ea7181943e41938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd7b4fa0ccd15d540a9299e77dbf1dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59696e5e7f94ff9d51e39d90ec169e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac418ceabab52352571a8024e5602ec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
