<node id="Hiperglucemia">
  <data key="d0">Hiperglucemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hiperglucemia is a condition characterized by elevated levels of glucose in the blood, commonly referred to as high blood sugar. It occurs when there is insufficient insulin available in the body to effectively regulate glucose, whether due to inadequate insulin administration, interruption of basal insulin supply, degraded insulin, or issues with insulin delivery systems such as pumps. Blood glucose levels exceeding 250 mg/dL, especially when persistent or accompanied by symptoms like nausea or the presence of ketones, are typically indicative of hiperglucemia.

This condition may arise from poor regulation of insulin therapy, malfunction in insulin delivery mechanisms, or other underlying factors that impair glucose metabolism. While insulin plays a critical role in preventing hiperglucemia, the condition itself is not directly reflected in hemoglobin A1C levels, which measure average glucose over time rather than acute spikes. As such, monitoring is essential to detect episodes and initiate timely corrective actions, including the administration of correction boluses or adjustments in therapy.

If left uncontrolled, hiperglucemia can lead to serious complications associated with diabetes, including long-term damage to organs and tissues. Management strategies include regular blood glucose checks, investigation into the root causes—such as infusion problems or insulin quality—and therapeutic interventions to bring glucose levels back into a safe range. Advanced systems may assist in prevention by issuing alerts and providing guidance for therapy adjustments, emphasizing the importance of proactive and continuous care in individuals with insulin-dependent diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;La hiperglucemia es una condición que puede ocurrir si se administra una cantidad insuficiente de insulina, lo que eleva los niveles de glucosa en sangre.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39f2ee843ae28cc44b37c7f51f7722a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191c82775d35bbc705205ed493c43c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1cf60a28692e32a5ea7181943e41938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd7b4fa0ccd15d540a9299e77dbf1dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59696e5e7f94ff9d51e39d90ec169e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
