  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indice Basal">
  <data key="d0">Indice Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Indice Basal is the insulin delivery rate setting, measured in units per hour (U/h), used in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Indice Basal refers to the programmed rate of insulin delivery over time in the MiniMed™ system, which may require adjustment based on glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Indice Basal refers to the background insulin delivery rate in insulin pump therapy, crucial for maintaining glucose levels within the target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Indice Basal refers to the basal insulin rate used in insulin pump therapy, which should be adjusted to maintain glucose levels within the target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Indice basal refers to the continuous background insulin delivery rate used to manage glucose levels between meals and during fasting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5b6ed50dde321317a11d8dcc6ef2a579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e15921d1b7d6415709a3d0c795cefc3c</data>
