</node>
<node id="Reservoir">
  <data key="d0">Reservoir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The reservoir is a critical component of the insulin pump system, specifically designed to store and hold the insulin supply used for continuous subcutaneous infusion. It functions as a small, disposable container—commonly with a 3.0 mL (300-unit) capacity—used in insulin delivery systems such as the MiniMed 780G and other Medtronic devices. The reservoir is inserted into the pump's reservoir compartment and connects directly to the infusion set tubing, enabling the controlled delivery of insulin into the body. It must be compatible with the specific pump model to ensure proper operation, secure connections, and waterproof integrity upon insertion.

Integral to diabetes management, the reservoir not only stores insulin but also supports monitoring of insulin availability. Many systems display the reservoir’s fill level via status icons or percentage ranges on the pump screen, with some providing estimates in units to enhance precision. This real-time feedback allows users to track remaining insulin, which is particularly important during alarm conditions such as blocked insulin flow or low volume. Checking the reservoir helps determine whether an issue arises from insulin depletion or a mechanical obstruction. Alarms are often associated with low insulin levels, improper insertion, or delivery disruptions.

The reservoir must be filled with insulin before insertion and replaced regularly—either independently or in conjunction with the infusion set—when empty or during routine maintenance to ensure uninterrupted therapy and hygiene. It is contraindicated for the infusion of blood or blood products, emphasizing its dedicated use for insulin. Proper filling and insertion are essential, as liquid in the tubing connector can block vents and disrupt insulin delivery. As a key element of the insulin delivery system, the reservoir works in tandem with the infusion set to store, monitor, and deliver insulin reliably, supporting effective and informed self-management of insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-682b7d7aa57e01aca00a1d4393db7bd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca77ae5b015fee5d1a21879c1a2b444&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc61f77b003d0086bd985ddb94fc2a98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
