<node id="Home Screen">
  <data key="d0">Home Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Home Screen is the primary and main interface of insulin pump devices, particularly models such as the MiniMed 770G and MiniMed 780G, serving as the central hub from which users navigate to various functions, settings, and status information. It appears after startup, battery insertion, waking from Sleep mode, or after periods of inactivity, and is essential for resuming basal insulin delivery, especially after exiting screens like Fill Cannula or following a battery change. The screen provides immediate access to critical device functions, including bolus delivery, temporary basal rate adjustments, blood glucose entry, Sensor Glucose (SG) review, history logs, alert configurations, and device pairing or reconnection.

The Home Screen displays real-time and status-related information crucial for diabetes management, such as current glucose values, trend arrows, active insulin (including bolus insulin), insulin delivery status, and CGM sensor data when the Sensor Feature is active. It also shows system status indicators and banners, including "Basal Temporal," SmartGuard shield, suspend-by-sensor status, and alerts for conditions like low sensor life, sensor warm-up, or pairing success. Messages prompting user action—such as "Enter BG" or "Exit in X:XX hr"—are presented here, and some alerts only appear upon returning to this screen. Key icons and shortcuts provide quick access to functions like Delivery Settings, Alert Settings, High Alert configuration, Bolus Wizard Setup, Easy Bolus, and reminders.

Overall, the Home Screen integrates operational control with comprehensive monitoring, enabling users to manage insulin delivery, respond to system alerts, and access detailed device data efficiently. It functions as the foundational interface for both routine interaction and urgent interventions within the insulin pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-682b7d7aa57e01aca00a1d4393db7bd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0270c70980e605771c5d1e6b4de949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d536bf636b4a29c1f9f46de648b2b306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b0e9023a7c03c6a