<node id="Transmitter">
  <data key="d0">Transmitter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Transmitter is a critical component of a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) system, specifically designed to wirelessly transmit glucose data collected by the sensor to an insulin pump, receiver, display device, or mobile application. It serves as a communication bridge between the sensor placed on the body and external devices used for monitoring and managing glucose levels, such as the MiniMed 780G system. The device connects directly to the sensor and securely relays real-time glucose readings, enabling timely decision-making for diabetes management.

Functionally, the Transmitter pairs with the insulin pump or monitoring system, with its pairing status often indicated by a green LED light. Once paired, it ensures continuous data transmission, which is essential for effective glucose tracking and automated insulin delivery. The pairing and unpairing processes are documented in user manuals, underscoring the importance of proper setup and device synchronization. The Transmitter's battery status is monitored through the pump’s status screens, and when depleted, the device requires recharging to maintain operation.

Safety considerations include the need to avoid exposure to MRI machines or strong magnetic fields, as such environments may interfere with or damage the Transmitter. It is integral to the overall CGM system, requiring a secure connection to the sensor for reliable performance. By enabling wireless communication between the sensor and pump or display device, the Transmitter supports seamless, real-time glucose monitoring and enhances the functionality of integrated diabetes management systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The transmitter is a component of the Eversense system that pairs with the implanted sensor and delivers glucose alerts and predictive notifications via vibrations and through the smartphone app.&lt;SEP&gt;A transmitter is a component in continuous glucose monitoring systems that sends glucose data from the sensor to a display device such as a monitor or smartphone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1faf2db5ce0667a0d479a8832c2bc8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636a6ab7d0bef06e011ae7bf2140d2e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MRI">
  <data key="d0">MRI</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MRI, or magnetic resonance imaging, is a medical imaging technique that uses strong magnetic fields and radio waves, posing risks to insulin pumps and sensors if exposed.&lt;SEP&gt;The acronym for magnetic resonance imaging, a medical imaging technique.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1faf2db5ce0667a0d479a8832c2bc8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CT Scan">
  <data key="d0">CT Scan</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CT scan, or computed tomography, is a type of radiological imaging that involves X-rays and requires caution when used by individuals with insulin pumps or sensors.&lt;SEP&gt;CT scan equipment emits radiation and generates magnetic fields that can damage the pump or CGM device.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical imaging procedure that uses X-rays to create detailed cross-sectional images of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The acronym for computed tomography scan, a medical imaging technique.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1faf2db5ce0667a0d479a8832c2bc8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="X-Ray">
  <data key="d0">X-Ray</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">X-ray is a form of ionizing radiation used in medical imaging that can damage insulin pumps and should be avoided during airport security screening.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray machines emit radiation that can damage pump components and result in insulin over-delivery and hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1faf2db5ce0667a0d479a8832c2bc8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airport Security Screening">
  <data key="d0">Airport Security Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Airport security screening involves procedures such as metal detectors and full-body scanners that may require special handling for individuals carrying insulin pumps and glucose monitoring devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1faf2db5ce0667a0d479a8832c2bc8d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700907</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diathermy Devices">
  <data key="d0">Diathermy Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Diathermy devices are medical equipment that generate heat through electromagnetic currents and can interfere with insulin pumps and sensors due to strong magnetic fields.&lt;SEP&gt;Diathermy devices are medical equipment that generate intense magnetic fields and can interfere with the operation of insulin pumps, sensors, and transmitters.&lt;SEP&gt;Diathermy devices produce electromagnetic fields and can pose risks to medical devices such as insulin pumps and glucose sensors.&lt;SEP&gt;Diathermy devices produce strong magnetic fields that may interfere with the pump and CGM, posing a risk of malfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1faf2db5ce0667a0d479a8832c2bc8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airport Body Scanner">
  <data key="d0">Airport Body Scanner</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An airport body scanner is a full-body imaging device used in security screening that emits X-rays and requires users to remove their insulin pump and glucose monitoring devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1faf2db5ce0667a0d479a8832c2bc8d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700907</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Pump User">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pump User</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin pump user is an individual with diabetes who relies on an insulin pump for continuous insulin delivery and must take precautions during travel and medical procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1faf2db5ce0667a0d479a8832c2bc8d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700907</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Index">
  <data key="d0">Basal Index</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A basal index represents the insulin delivery rate (in units per hour) during a specific time segment within a basal pattern.&lt;SEP&gt;A basal index refers to the specific insulin delivery value at a given time segment within a basal pattern, expressed in units per hour.&lt;SEP&gt;The Basal Index refers to the programmed insulin delivery rate used in diabetes management, which can be adjusted temporarily or permanently.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feedb8da72881894bf4c6529f7baca60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Infusion Settings">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Infusion Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin infusion settings include configurations such as basal patterns, bolus delivery, and temporary basal rates on an insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin infusion settings are configurations within the pump that allow users to program basal rates, bolus doses, and temporary adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;A menu or system function used to adjust how insulin is delivered, including basal rate patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin infusion settings include configurations for basal rates, bolus doses, and temporary adjustments on an insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Infusion Settings encompass configurations such as basal patterns, bolus types, and temporary rates on the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feedb8da72881894bf4c6529f7baca60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b299154da4c58d8322b7ac4e3af2f5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704107</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quick Reference Guide">
  <data key="d0">Quick Reference Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Quick Reference Guide contains step-by-step instructions for pairing the insulin pump and glucose meter, available on page 82 of the documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;A quick reference guide provides step-by-step instructions for configuring basal indices and temporary basal rates on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quick Reference Guide is a document included in the MiniMed 670G user manual providing summarized instructions for key functions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quick Reference Guide is a document included in the training materials that provides safety rules and instructions for responding to high or low blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quick Reference Guide is a section in the manual designed to provide users with concise instructions for managing basal indices and insulin delivery settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feedb8da72881894bf4c6529f7baca60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0760c4e75f4ab51e1f860c2ae998ef46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f5ebaa0341f051ad33cfb9895a3851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a8417d6099b09e6129d10f9827b5a35</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Pump User Interface">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pump User Interface</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The insulin pump user interface includes on-screen menus and navigation options such as ©), W, and text prompts for configuring basal patterns and settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feedb8da72881894bf4c6529f7baca60</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700908</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Config. Patrón Basal">
  <data key="d0">Config. Patrón Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Config. Patrón Basal is a menu option used to configure basal patterns on the insulin pump, allowing users to add or edit time segments and insulin rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feedb8da72881894bf4c6529f7baca60</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
