</node>
<node id="Opciones de Audio">
  <data key="d0">Opciones de Audio</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Opciones de Audio refers to audio settings on the insulin pump that allow users to adjust sound alerts and notifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feedb8da72881894bf4c6529f7baca60</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700908</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspender Infusión">
  <data key="d0">Suspender Infusión</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspender Infusión is a function that allows the user to temporarily stop insulin delivery from the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feedb8da72881894bf4c6529f7baca60</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700908</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Square Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Square Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A square bolus is an insulin delivery mode where the full dose is delivered evenly over a user-specified time.&lt;SEP&gt;A square bolus is an insulin delivery method that administers a set amount of insulin evenly over a specified period, such as 45 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Square bolus is a type of insulin delivery that administers a portion of the bolus evenly over a defined duration.&lt;SEP&gt;A square bolus is an insulin delivery method where the dose is spread evenly over a set period, useful for meals with delayed glucose impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Square bolus is an insulin delivery function that administers insulin gradually over a set period, useful for managing glucose from certain meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-69f89cc6358f0fe2b490d63a60ae0581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96a4da2f877f1b93eb7d982c91358ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f5ebaa0341f051ad33cfb9895a3851</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Dual Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A dual bolus is an insulin delivery mode that combines an immediate bolus with an extended bolus over time.&lt;SEP&gt;A dual bolus combines a standard bolus with a square bolus, delivering part of the insulin immediately and the rest over time to match delayed glucose absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual bolus is an insulin delivery method that splits the bolus into an immediate dose and a square wave component administered over time.&lt;SEP&gt;A dual bolus combines an immediate and extended insulin delivery, suitable for meals with mixed carbohydrate, fat, and protein content.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual bolus is an insulin delivery function that administers a portion of insulin immediately and the remainder over time to better manage glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-69f89cc6358f0fe2b490d63a60ae0581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96a4da2f877f1b93eb7d982c91358ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f5ebaa0341f051ad33cfb9895a3851</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Insulin refers to the amount of insulin that remains physiologically effective in the body following a previous bolus dose, also known as insulin on board. This residual insulin continues to lower blood glucose levels for a duration determined by the insulin's pharmacokinetic profile, typically lasting several hours after administration. The concept is particularly critical in diabetes management for individuals using insulin pumps, as it directly influences subsequent dosing decisions and helps prevent hypoglycemia.

Active Insulin is dynamically calculated and displayed on insulin pump screens, often shown as a real-time value such as 0.0 U during bolus review or on the home screen. The value is derived from the timing, dosage, and expected duration of action of recent bolus deliveries. It is used by various pump features, including the Bolus Wizard™ and SmartGuard, to inform automated dosing algorithms. These systems incorporate the remaining insulin effect when calculating recommended correction doses, subtracting the active amount from the total insulin required to avoid insulin stacking and ensure safe, accurate dosing.

The tracking of Active Insulin is essential for preventing both over- and under-dosing, as its continued effect can cause sensor glucose levels to decline even after the bolus has been delivered. Some systems allow the Active Insulin value to be reset or cleared in response to alerts or specific user actions, particularly before initiating new therapy or recalibrating the system. Across all descriptions, Active Insulin consistently represents the ongoing glucose-lowering effect of prior insulin doses and plays a central role in the safety and precision of modern insulin delivery systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97d9a9de5f40419555bf7bf36cc9f84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0270c70980e605771c5d1e6b4de949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-425759c12d133ef4832928e8f5d50896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0deeba398b22b91d8da1b31653eede4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707290</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual/Square Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Dual/Square Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual/square bolus is an insulin delivery mode that combines immediate and extended insulin release, used for specific meal types or digestion patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual/Square Bolus is an insulin delivery mode that combines an immediate bolus with a prolonged square-wave bolus over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97d9a9de5f40419555bf7bf36cc9f84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b299154da4c58d8322b7ac4e3af2f5bf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704106</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predefined Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Predefined Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Predefined bolus is a saved insulin dose configuration that allows users to administer a previously set bolus amount quickly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97d9a9de5f40419555bf7bf36cc9f84c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700910</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Settings">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion settings are configurable parameters on an insulin pump that control how and when insulin is delivered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97d9a9de5f40419555bf7bf36cc9f84c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700910</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic Logo">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic Logo</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Medtronic logo is a visual trademark representing the identity of Medtronic, used in branding and product documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97d9a9de5f40419555bf7bf36cc9f84c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700910</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jessica">
  <data key="d0">Jessica</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Jessica is a person who uses an insulin pump to manage her glucose levels, previously experiencing high morning readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Jessica is a person who uses an insulin pump to manage her blood glucose levels, previously experiencing high readings in the morning when using injections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Level">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Level</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose level refers to the concentration of sugar in the blood, monitored to assess diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose level refers to the concentration of glucose in the blood, which users monitor to determine the need for insulin bolus or correction doses.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose level is a measurement of blood sugar that can be affected by physical activity and insulin dosage, requiring monitoring and management.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose level refers to the concentration of glucose in the blood, measured in mg/dL, and monitored by Dennis.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose level is a measurement of blood sugar, entered manually into the pump and used for bolus calculation and system monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose level is a measurement of blood sugar that can be affected by physical activity and insulin dosage, requiring adjustments like temporary basal rates to maintain stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose level refers to the concentration of glucose in the blood, measured in mg/dL, and is critical in managing diabetes and treatment decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8190aff898356450e3514b751c9193c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Rate Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Basal Rate Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal rate adjustment is the process of changing the amount of insulin delivered per hour based on glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700910</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.750 U/h">
  <data key="d0">0.750 U/h</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">0.750 U/h is the initial basal insulin delivery rate for Basal 1, resulting in 18 units over 24 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;0.750 U/h is the initial basal insulin infusion rate set for Basal 1 before being modified.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.900 U/h">
  <data key="d0">0.900 U/h</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">0.900 U/h is the modified basal insulin delivery rate for Basal 1, resulting in 21.6 units over 24 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;0.900 U/h is the updated basal insulin infusion rate for Basal 1 after adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="8:00 A To 6:00 P">
  <data key="d0">8:00 A To 6:00 P</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">This time period indicates a segment of the day when the basal rate is reduced to 0.650 U/h.&lt;SEP&gt;8:00 A To 6:00 P is a time segment during which the basal insulin rate is reduced to 0.650 U/h to better manage blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.650 U/h">
  <data key="d0">0.650 U/h</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">0.650 U/h is the reduced basal insulin rate prescribed for the period between 8:00 A and 6:00 P.&lt;SEP&gt;0.650 U/h is the reduced basal insulin infusion rate determined necessary for the time period between 8:00 A and 6:00 P.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edit Basal 1">
  <data key="d0">Edit Basal 1</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Edit Basal 1 is a menu function used to modify the basal insulin rate settings on an insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700912</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Save">
  <data key="d0">Save</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Save is a command used to confirm and store changes made to the basal pattern settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Save is a command used to store newly configured basal patterns or settings into the insulin pump's memory.&lt;SEP&gt;Save is a command used to confirm and store changes made to any reminder configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;Save is a function used to confirm and store settings changes within the pump system, such as enabling or modifying the Set Change reminder.&lt;SEP&gt;Save is the action used to confirm and store a configured preset bolus setting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Segment">
  <data key="d0">Time Segment</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A time segment is a defined period within a basal pattern during which a specific insulin rate is applied.&lt;SEP&gt;A Time Segment represents a portion of the 24-hour period with a defined start and end time, each可having a unique high glucose limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Max">
  <data key="d0">Basal Max</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal Max is the maximum amount of basal insulin that can be delivered per hour by the insulin pump, set for safety and medical oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal Max is the maximum basal insulin infusion rate setting on the pump, which can be adjusted based on recommendations from a healthcare professional.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Basal max is the maximum amount of basal insulin that can be delivered per hour by the pump, often set at 2.0 U/h but adjustable based on medical guidance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b28f926a642d5f692433ed41fafafa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7534f3bc09ac6e2eece38e12eb89cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b04d1a6d29b90441d249d701d54d862</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704185</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Max">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Max</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Max is the maximum amount of insulin that can be delivered in a single bolus dose, configurable on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Max is the maximum amount of insulin that can be delivered in a single bolus, serving as a safety limit to prevent overdosing.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus max is the maximum bolus insulin dose the pump allows to be delivered at once, set to 10.0 U in the displayed configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b28f926a642d5f692433ed41fafafa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7534f3bc09ac6e2eece38e12eb89cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b04d1a6d29b90441d249d701d54d862</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704185</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoapagado">
  <data key="d0">Autoapagado</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoapagado is a safety feature on the insulin pump that stops insulin infusion and triggers an alarm if no button is pressed within a defined time period.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoapagado is a safety function that emits an alarm and stops insulin infusion if no button is pressed within a defined number of hours, designed for situations where the user does not respond to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoapagado is a safety feature that triggers an alarm and stops insulin infusion if no buttons are pressed within a defined time period, designed for situations where the user may not respond to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoapagado is a feature that stops insulin delivery after a set duration and triggers an alarm if the user does not respond, providing safety during sleep.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b28f926a642d5f692433ed41fafafa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc17381a558f271a9da13b99091c2ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac418ceabab52352571a8024e5602ec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b04d1a6d29b90441d249d701d54d862</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuracion Temp Predefinido">
  <data key="d0">Configuracion Temp Predefinido</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Configuracion Temp Predefinido refers to the predefined temporary basal rate settings that can be programmed into the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b28f926a642d5f692433ed41fafafa4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700913</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equipo Medico">
  <data key="d0">Equipo Medico</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Equipo Medico refers to the healthcare team responsible for managing a patient’s insulin therapy and guiding adjustments to pump settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Equipo Medico refers to the healthcare professionals who assist patients in determining their appropriate insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio when starting insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Equipo Medico refers to the medical team responsible for overseeing a patient's diabetes care and treatment plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Equipo Medico is the healthcare team responsible for guiding patients in setting basal rates, adjusting insulin ratios, and interpreting glucose data.&lt;SEP&gt;Equipo Medico is the healthcare team responsible for advising patients on insulin therapy adjustments related to physical activity and alcohol consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;A healthcare team responsible for advising patients on insulin therapy adjustments, medication effects, and personalized glucose management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b28f926a642d5f692433ed41fafafa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84d2aca165fc0184360972207bae8c6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd60281301900b9df0acbe6be09fa2f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Actual">
  <data key="d0">Actual</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Actual refers to the current or real-time basal insulin delivery rate being used, as opposed to a predefined or scheduled rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b28f926a642d5f692433ed41fafafa4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700913</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indice">
  <data key="d0">Indice</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Indice refers to the insulin delivery rate in units per hour (U/h) for a given time interval in a basal pattern.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b28f926a642d5f692433ed41fafafa4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
