<node id="Medtronic MiniMed, Inc.">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic MiniMed, Inc.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Medtronic MiniMed, Inc. is a subsidiary of Medtronic that holds trademarks for diabetes care products such as Bolus Wizard, Quick-set, and SmartGuard.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic MiniMed, Inc. is a company that develops medical devices for diabetes management and owns the Bolus Wizard trademark.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic MiniMed, Inc. is the manufacturer and trademark owner of the MiniMed and MiniMed logo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec9910e322fb247c0bf85c8b8cb3e948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc46b3924459ec23a123df1dad4bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707471</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quick-set">
  <data key="d0">Quick-set</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Quick-set is a trademarked infusion set used with insulin pumps like the MiniMed 770G for subcutaneous insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Quick-set is an infusion set used with the insulin pump for delivering insulin, designed for quick and easy application.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Quick-set is an infusion set used with the insulin pump for delivering insulin, which can be changed as part of routine maintenance or therapy management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec9910e322fb247c0bf85c8b8cb3e948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc17381a558f271a9da13b99091c2ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac418ceabab52352571a8024e5602ec4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704142</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard is an advanced automated insulin delivery feature developed by Medtronic for use in its MiniMed insulin pump systems, particularly the MiniMed 770G and MiniMed 780G models. It functions as a control algorithm that leverages continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) data to automatically adjust basal insulin delivery in real time, aiming to maintain glucose levels within a target range and reduce the risk of both hypoglycemia and hyperglycemia. The system continuously analyzes sensor glucose values and glucose trends, dynamically modifying insulin delivery without requiring manual intervention, and operates without relying on user-defined maximum basal rate settings, instead determining delivery limits autonomously.

In the MiniMed 780G system, SmartGuard extends its functionality by delivering automatic correction boluses every five minutes based on current glucose levels, using the Active Insulin Time setting to calculate insulin on board and prevent overcorrection. It integrates carb entries, user-defined target glucose values, and real-time sensor data to optimize insulin dosing and maximize time in range. The feature supports both Auto Basal delivery and Auto Correction boluses, and requires proper system configuration, sensor calibration, and readiness checks before activation. In certain situations—such as sensor signal loss or system alerts—SmartGuard may require manual blood glucose (BG) meter input to resume insulin delivery.

SmartGuard also incorporates a comprehensive alert system that remains active even when general sensor alerts are silenced, ensuring critical notifications like the Low SG alarm, High SG alert, and system exit alert are not missed. It influences the display of trend arrows on the pump interface, reflecting its active role in glucose trend analysis. The feature is closely tied to graph displays of sensor glucose data and supports meal bolus management, offering users visual and operational tools for effective diabetes management. As a system mode, SmartGuard affects insulin delivery behavior and requires careful setup of BG targets, delivery limits, and alert preferences to function safely and effectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec9910e322fb247c0bf85c8b8cb3e948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b7bb277d16feead8d082fc004d51d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61911be532419242af177a0b5feeb72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b0e9023a7c03c6a284d69e0930b8a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Wave">
  <data key="d0">Dual Wave</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual Wave is a trademarked bolus delivery mode by Medtronic MiniMed, Inc. that combines immediate and extended insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual Wave is a delivery mode in the MiniMed insulin pump that allows splitting an insulin bolus into immediate and extended components.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Dual Wave is a bolus delivery type that combines immediate and extended insulin delivery, configurable via the Bolus Wizard and manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual Wave is an insulin delivery mode that splits a bolus dose into an immediate and extended component.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual Wave is a bolus type that delivers part of the insulin immediately and the remainder as a square wave over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec9910e322fb247c0bf85c8b8cb3e948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61911be532419242af177a0b5feeb72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Square Wave">
  <data key="d0">Square Wave</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Square Wave is a trademarked bolus delivery mode by Medtronic MiniMed, Inc. that delivers insulin evenly over a set period.&lt;SEP&gt;Square Wave is an insulin delivery mode that administers a bolus over a selected period, useful for managing prolonged glucose elevation.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A Square Wave is an insulin delivery method that administers a bolus over a specified duration, used for food absorbed slowly.&lt;SEP&gt;Square Wave is a bolus type that delivers insulin over an extended period, used for managing post-meal glucose spikes.&lt;SEP&gt;Square Wave is a bolus type that spreads insulin delivery evenly over a user-defined period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec9910e322fb247c0bf85c8b8cb3e948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61911be532419242af177a0b5feeb72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
