</node>
<node id="Basal Rate">
  <data key="d0">Basal Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal Rate refers to the continuous, background delivery of insulin administered by an insulin pump to maintain stable blood glucose levels during fasting periods, particularly between meals and overnight. It is designed to mimic the low, steady release of insulin that a healthy pancreas would normally produce, ensuring glycemic control in the absence of food intake. This rate is typically measured in units per hour (U/h) and serves as a foundational component of insulin therapy for individuals with diabetes, especially those using insulin pump systems.

The Basal Rate is a programmable setting that determines the amount of basal insulin delivered per hour and must be configured to enable certain pump functions, such as Manual mode and the SmartGuard feature. It can be structured into one or more 24-hour basal patterns, allowing for customization based on individual metabolic needs and daily physiological rhythms. These patterns enable segmented adjustments throughout the day, reflecting variations in insulin sensitivity—such as lower rates to prevent hypoglycemia at night or higher rates during early morning hours to counteract the dawn phenomenon. Adjustments can be made either as permanent patterns or temporary rates, offering flexibility and precision in glucose management.

The Basal Rate can be delivered as a fixed, user-programmed rate or adjusted automatically by advanced features like SmartGuard when sufficient data is available; otherwise, the pump defaults to a fixed rate based on historical insulin delivery. This setting is accessible and modifiable through the pump’s interface, such as the Basal screen, and is essential for both manual and automated insulin delivery modes. Effectiveness is evaluated through fasting blood glucose measurements, and if levels are consistently outside the target range, the Basal Rate may require recalibration. Overall, the Basal Rate is a critical, customizable function in insulin pump therapy, enabling personalized, dynamic insulin delivery to support optimal long-term glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e96a4da2f877f1b93eb7d982c91358ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac418ceabab52352571a8024e5602ec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4aefb790519642667af4aaebc974bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a8417d6099b09e6129d10f9827b5a35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f608f07eae4ddd5409aed9d4ecef75ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707374</data>
