<node id="Ba">
  <data key="d0">Ba</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ba represents the low blood glucose target value (in mg/dL) used in setting glucose control goals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89156e5c9ff284920f8f122774e1ee34</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700927</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Al">
  <data key="d0">Al</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Al represents the high blood glucose target value (in mg/dL) used in setting glucose control goals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89156e5c9ff284920f8f122774e1ee34</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700927</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Duracion Insulina Activa">
  <data key="d0">Duracion Insulina Activa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Duracion Insulina Activa refers to the duration of active insulin in the body, a parameter used in the Bolus Wizard to avoid insulin stacking.&lt;SEP&gt;Duracion Insulina Activa is the duration (e.g., 4:00 hours) during which an insulin bolus continues to lower blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89156e5c9ff284920f8f122774e1ee34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1250027f75a49e3288b12fc80a630d33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700927</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Correctora">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Correctora</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Correctora is the corrective insulin dose calculated to bring blood glucose levels back to the target range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89156e5c9ff284920f8f122774e1ee34</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700927</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ratio Hc">
  <data key="d0">Ratio Hc</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ratio Hc is the carbohydrate-to-insulin ratio used by the Bolus Wizard to determine insulin dosage based on carbohydrate intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89156e5c9ff284920f8f122774e1ee34</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700927</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medidor De Gs">
  <data key="d0">Medidor De Gs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Medidor de Gs is a device that measures current blood glucose levels and provides input for insulin dosing decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89156e5c9ff284920f8f122774e1ee34</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700928</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ajuste Ins Activa">
  <data key="d0">Ajuste Ins Activa</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ajuste ins. activa is the adjustment made by subtracting the remaining active insulin from the corrective insulin dose to prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89156e5c9ff284920f8f122774e1ee34</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700928</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thomas">
  <data key="d0">Thomas</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Thomas is a runner who uses the Autoapagado function to feel safer at night, especially on days when he runs and is more prone to nighttime hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Thomas is a runner who experiences increased risk of nighttime hypoglycemia on days he runs and uses temporary basal rates and the Auto-shutdown feature for safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4dc17381a558f271a9da13b99091c2ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac418ceabab52352571a8024e5602ec4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The alarm is a sound signal emitted by the Autoapagado function when no button has been pressed within the set time, alerting the user to potential danger.&lt;SEP&gt;An alarm is a notification triggered by the insulin pump to indicate a problem such as blocked infusion or empty reservoir.&lt;SEP&gt;Alarms are notifications generated by the pump to alert the user to events, displayed in the Notifications section with timestamps.&lt;SEP&gt;An alarm indicates a condition preventing insulin delivery, shown with a red icon and requiring immediate user action on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;An alarm is a warning signal generated by the pump indicating an error or interruption in insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;An alarm is a warning signal generated by the pump to indicate critical issues such as low battery, delivery interruption, or system errors.&lt;SEP&gt;An Alarm is an audible beep or vibration accompanied by a message that requires immediate user response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4dc17381a558f271a9da13b99091c2ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc46b3924459ec23a123df1dad4bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patrón Basal">
  <data key="d0">Patrón Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Un patrón basal es un programa configurado en la bomba de insulina que define uno o más índices basales durante el ciclo de 24 horas para ajustar la insulina a las necesidades del organismo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1cf60a28692e32a5ea7181943e41938</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700928</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Índice Basal">
  <data key="d0">Índice Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">El índice basal es la cantidad de insulina administrada por hora, expresada en unidades por hora (U/h), que se programa en la bomba de insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;El índice basal es la cantidad de insulina que se administra continuamente para mantener niveles estables de glucosa en sangre entre comidas y durante el sueño.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1cf60a28692e32a5ea7181943e41938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lynn">
  <data key="d0">Lynn</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lynn es una persona con diabetes que antes debía inyectarse insulina de acción prolongada cada noche, pero ahora usa una bomba de insulina que le administra insulina basal automáticamente.&lt;SEP&gt;Lynn is a person who previously relied on long-acting insulin injections before using an insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Lynn is a person with diabetes who previously had difficulty maintaining a consistent schedule for long-acting insulin injections due to her university lifestyle, and now uses an insulin pump for automated basal insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1cf60a28692e32a5ea7181943e41938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9a22fae9e4c986d3a8e2a8dcdad44fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="12:00 A-12:00 A">
  <data key="d0">12:00 A-12:00 A</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">12:00 A-12:00 A represents a 24-hour time period used for configuring a basal pattern on the insulin pump, from noon to noon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1cf60a28692e32a5ea7181943e41938</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700929</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Blood Sugar">
  <data key="d0">Low Blood Sugar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low blood sugar refers to glucose levels below 70 mg/dL, requiring immediate treatment with fast-acting carbohydrates or glucagon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2bfad6c7b0e936c6a9c113798a2d963e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700929</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Blood Sugar">
  <data key="d0">High Blood Sugar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High blood sugar refers to glucose levels above the target range, particularly above 250 mg/dL, which may require corrective insulin dosing and ketone testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2bfad6c7b0e936c6a9c113798a2d963e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700929</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucagon Emergency Kit">
  <data key="d0">Glucagon Emergency Kit</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The glucagon emergency kit contains injectable glucagon to treat severe hypoglycemia when a person cannot eat or drink.&lt;SEP&gt;The glucagon emergency kit is used for treating severe hypoglycemia in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;The Glucagon Emergency Kit is a medical device used to administer glucagon via injection to raise blood glucose levels during severe hypoglycemia when oral intake is not possible.&lt;SEP&gt;The Glucagon Emergency Kit is a medical device used to administer glucagon in cases of severe hypoglycemia when the person cannot eat or drink or is unconscious.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon Emergency Kit is a registered trademark of Eli Lilly and Company.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon Emergency Kit is a registered trademark of Eli Lilly and Company, used for treating severe hypoglycemia in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Glucagon Emergency Kit contains glucagon for injection and is used to treat severe hypoglycemia when a person cannot eat or drink or is unconscious.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2bfad6c7b0e936c6a9c113798a2d963e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b7bb277d16feead8d082fc004d51d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5cace75be2ca46efd8033523e47b6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8af713fd3913ed050d96cdd321bca3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fac4937227d8065e4742d7cebf8db204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac418ceabab52352571a8024e5602ec4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ketone Testing">
  <data key="d0">Ketone Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketone testing is a procedure to detect the presence of ketones in the body when blood glucose levels exceed 250 mg/dL, indicating potential insulin deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketone testing is a procedure to check for ketones in the blood or urine, recommended before physical activity when blood glucose exceeds 240 mg/dL and rising.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketone testing is used to detect the presence of ketones in blood or urine, especially when glucose levels exceed 250 mg/dL or during illness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2bfad6c7b0e936c6a9c113798a2d963e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="15-15 Rule">
  <data key="d0">15-15 Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The 15-15 rule is a guideline for treating mild to moderate hypoglycemia by consuming 15 grams of fast-acting carbohydrates and rechecking blood glucose after 15 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;The 15-15 Rule is a treatment protocol for mild hypoglycemia involving consuming 15 grams of fast-acting carbohydrates and rechecking blood glucose after 15 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;The 15-15 Rule is a treatment guideline involving consuming 15 grams of fast-acting carbs and rechecking blood glucose after 15 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2bfad6c7b0e936c6a9c113798a2d963e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710326</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Rate Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Basal Rate Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A basal rate pattern is a programmed insulin delivery schedule used to maintain blood glucose levels between meals and overnight.&lt;SEP&gt;A basal rate pattern is a programmed insulin delivery schedule designed for different days or activity levels, which can be customized or copied and modified as needed.&lt;SEP&gt;A basal rate pattern is a programmed setting on an insulin pump that defines one or more basal insulin delivery rates over a 24-hour cycle.&lt;SEP&gt;The basal rate pattern is a configurable schedule that defines how the insulin delivery rate changes throughout the day.&lt;SEP&gt;A basal rate pattern is a programmed insulin delivery schedule that can be customized or copied to suit different daily routines, such as weekends or periods of reduced activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8190aff898356450e3514b751c9193c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Off Feature">
  <data key="d0">Auto Off Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Auto Off Feature is a safety setting on the MiniMed 770G that turns the pump off after a period of inactivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700930</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetic Ketoacidosis Prevention">
  <data key="d0">Diabetic Ketoacidosis Prevention</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetic ketoacidosis prevention includes monitoring ketones and adjusting insulin during illness to avoid a dangerous metabolic state.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic ketoacidosis prevention involves monitoring ketone levels, administering correction insulin, changing infusion equipment, and seeking medical help when necessary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile Device Application">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Device Application</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The mobile device application connects to the MiniMed 770G pump to allow remote monitoring and management via a smartphone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700930</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CareLink Personal Program">
  <data key="d0">CareLink Personal Program</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The CareLink Personal Program is software used to download and review insulin pump and glucose data for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700930</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airport Security Devices">
  <data key="d0">Airport Security Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Airport security devices are checkpoints where travelers pass through screening, requiring special considerations when carrying medical devices like insulin pumps.&lt;SEP&gt;Airport security devices include metal detectors and full-body scanners that may require special handling when passengers use medical devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704132</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic MiniMed 770G">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic MiniMed 770G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Medtronic MiniMed 770G is an insulin pump system that integrates continuous glucose monitoring and automated insulin delivery for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700931</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Mode">
  <data key="d0">Manual Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual Mode is an operational setting available on Medtronic's MiniMed 770G and MiniMed 780G insulin pump systems, designed to allow users to manually control insulin delivery without automated adjustments from the SmartGuard feature. In this mode, automated insulin dosing is disabled, and users are responsible for making all treatment decisions, including bolus delivery and glucose corrections, based on blood glucose (BG) meter readings rather than sensor glucose (SG) values. The SmartGuard feature, which enables automated glucose-based insulin adjustments in other modes, is inactive during Manual Mode, rendering SG values unsuitable for treatment decisions.

Users operating in Manual Mode retain access to key pump functions such as the Bolus Wizard, which assists in calculating insulin boluses based on user input, though proper configuration requires guidance from a healthcare professional. This mode supports various bolus types, including Square Wave, Dual Wave, Easy, Manual, and Preset boluses, all of which require manual initiation and often rely on BG meter input for setup. Basal insulin delivery continues according to a user-defined pattern and is subject to preconfigured limits such as the Max basal setting, but it does not adapt automatically in response to sensor data.

Manual Mode can be used with or without continuous glucose monitoring (CGM), but when active, the sensor functionality may be turned off, affecting the display and operation of the pump’s Home screen. Despite the absence of automated features, the pump continues to deliver insulin at a fixed basal rate based on historical delivery settings. Overall, Manual Mode represents a state of direct user control over insulin therapy, where system automation is suspended, and all dosing decisions depend on user intervention and external glucose measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audio Options">
  <data key="d0">Audio Options</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Audio options let the user configure alert types including sound, vibration, or both, and adjust volume settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Audio Options are user-configurable sound settings on the MiniMed 770G for alerts and notifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Audio options are settings on the insulin pump that control sound feedback or voice guidance during operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Audio Options are settings within the insulin pump that control sound alerts and feedback for user interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Audio Options are settings that control sound alerts and notifications on the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Screen Options">
  <data key="d0">Screen Options</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Screen Options are display settings on the MiniMed 770G that allow users to customize brightness, timeout, and visual elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700931</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend Infusion">
  <data key="d0">Suspend Infusion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend Infusion is a function on the MiniMed 770G that temporarily stops insulin delivery, either manually or automatically.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend infusion is a function that stops all insulin delivery temporarily, used during activities like swimming or showering.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend Infusion is a function that temporarily stops insulin delivery, accessible through the pump’s menu system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704115</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resume Basal Insulin Infusion">
  <data key="d0">Resume Basal Insulin Infusion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resume Basal Insulin Infusion is the action of restarting background insulin delivery after a suspension period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700931</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interrupt Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Interrupt Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Interrupt Bolus is a feature that allows users to stop an ongoing bolus insulin delivery before completion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Review Last Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Review Last Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Review Last Bolus is a function on the MiniMed 770G that displays details of the most recent insulin bolus administered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Review Bolus History">
  <data key="d0">Review Bolus History</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Review Bolus History is a feature that allows users to view a log of past bolus deliveries for tracking and analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile Device">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A mobile device is a smartphone or tablet used with the MiniMed 770G application for remote monitoring and control.&lt;SEP&gt;A mobile device is required to interact with the Instinct Sensor and must support NFC functionality for the sensor to operate.&lt;SEP&gt;The mobile device is used to run the MiniMed Mobile app and must support NFC to start the Instinct sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;A Mobile Device is a compatible smartphone or tablet used to interact with the pump via a dedicated app.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Radiographic Examinations">
  <data key="d0">Radiographic Examinations</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Radiographic Examinations include CT and MRI scans, during which users are advised on whether to remove the MiniMed 770G pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Travel With Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d0">Travel With Insulin Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Travel With Insulin Pump refers to guidelines and considerations for carrying and using the MiniMed 770G while traveling, including air travel and security checks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Be Prepared">
  <data key="d0">Be Prepared</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Be Prepared is a safety recommendation advising users to always carry backup supplies and emergency information for insulin pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Call Technical Support">
  <data key="d0">Call Technical Support</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Call Technical Support refers to contacting Medtronic’s 24-hour technical support line for assistance with device issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Call Medical Team">
  <data key="d0">Call Medical Team</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Call Medical Team is a guideline advising users to contact their healthcare providers for medical concerns related to insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe4cbdd5aa97cd45d28222067ba8cff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parar Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Parar Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Parar bolus es una función que permite interrumpir la administración de un bolus en curso.&lt;SEP&gt;Parar Bolus is the function used to interrupt an ongoing bolus infusion on the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1064c42775365801d8ca4df533dcda0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d74e338f7a37de66d4b2268a49021c4e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704180</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Detenido">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Detenido</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus detenido es una pantalla que muestra la cantidad de insulina que se ha administrado antes de la interrupción del bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Detenido is the screen displayed when a bolus has been interrupted, showing the amount of insulin already delivered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1064c42775365801d8ca4df533dcda0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d74e338f7a37de66d4b2268a49021c4e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704180</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ratio HC">
  <data key="d0">Ratio HC</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ratio HC es un valor de ajuste personal que indica cuántas unidades de insulina se necesitan por gramo de hidratos de carbono.&lt;SEP&gt;Ratio HC refers to the amount of carbohydrates covered by one unit of insulin, used in configuring the Bolus Wizard.&lt;SEP&gt;Ratio HC is the carbohydrate-to-insulin ratio, such as 15 g/U, used to determine insulin dosage based on grams of carbohydrates consumed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1064c42775365801d8ca4df533dcda0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1250027f75a49e3288b12fc80a630d33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed9acad938fa761961897e399e22d5c3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensibilidad Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Sensibilidad Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensibilidad insulina es un ajuste personal que indica cuánto disminuye la glucosa en sangre por cada unidad de insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensibilidad Insulina refers to the amount of blood glucose drop per unit of insulin, for example, 50 mg/dL per U.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1064c42775365801d8ca4df533dcda0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed9acad938fa761961897e399e22d5c3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Duración Insulina Activa">
  <data key="d0">Duración Insulina Activa</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Duración insulina activa es un ajuste que define cuánto tiempo la insulina sigue teniendo efecto en el cuerpo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1064c42775365801d8ca4df533dcda0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucosa en Sangre">
  <data key="d0">Glucosa en Sangre</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucosa en sangre is the measured blood sugar level used as input for the Bolus Wizard function to calculate insulin dosage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1064c42775365801d8ca4df533dcda0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700934</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidratos de Carbono">
  <data key="d0">Hidratos de Carbono</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hidratos de carbono refers to the carbohydrates consumed, which must be entered into the Bolus Wizard to determine the correct insulin bolus amount.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidratos de Carbono are nutrients that directly impact blood glucose levels and must be counted accurately to calculate correct bolus doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1064c42775365801d8ca4df533dcda0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patricia">
  <data key="d0">Patricia</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patricia is a person who enjoys gardening but experiences low glucose levels during the activity and uses a temporary basal rate to manage her insulin intake.&lt;SEP&gt;Patricia is a person who enjoys gardening but experiences low glucose levels during physical activity, so she uses a temporary basal rate to reduce insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8190aff898356450e3514b751c9193c1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Suspension">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Suspension</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion suspension is a function that temporarily stops insulin delivery, accessible through the device's menu options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700934</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Settings">
  <data key="d0">Pump Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump settings include configurations such as basal patterns, temporary rates, and audio options, adjustable through the device menu.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700934</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Interface">
  <data key="d0">Pump Interface</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The pump interface is the device screen and control system used to navigate menus, adjust settings, and monitor insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2f934e06027507283d7abfd94d072e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700934</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lisa">
  <data key="d0">Lisa</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lisa is a person who started using an insulin pump and learned its functions gradually, beginning with basic features.&lt;SEP&gt;Lisa is a user who started using an insulin pump and gradually learned its basic and additional functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704108</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temporary Basal">
  <data key="d0">Temporary Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Temporary basal is a function that allows the user to set a temporary insulin basal rate for a specified duration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700934</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predefined Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Predefined Basal Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A predefined basal pattern is a stored insulin delivery schedule that can be selected for automatic basal insulin infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700934</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Mode">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic mode is an operating mode enabled by SmartGuard that adjusts insulin delivery automatically based on sensor glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic mode is a system state that manages insulin delivery based on sensor data and user settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic Mode is a function within the SmartGuard system that adjusts insulin delivery based on glucose levels and can be turned on or off.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic Mode is an operational state of the pump system that requires readiness checks before activation, indicated in the Preparation screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Silence">
  <data key="d0">Alert Silence</data>
  <data key="d1">feature</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert silence is a function that allows the user to temporarily mute pump alerts and notifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Silence is a feature that disables sound and vibration for certain alerts, indicated by a status icon when active.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Silence is a feature that temporarily disables sound and vibration for certain sensor alerts, except for critical ones like high SG, low SG, and SmartGuard exit alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Silence is a feature that allows users to temporarily disable specific sensor alerts for a set duration, with options to silence High Alerts Only, High &amp; Low Alerts, or All Sensor Alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707399</data>
