<node id="Rise Alert">
  <data key="d0">Rise Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rise alert is a notification that triggers when glucose levels are increasing rapidly, helping prevent hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise Alert is a notification feature that triggers when glucose levels are rising rapidly, allowing the user to set a limit for activation.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise Alert is a type of high SG alert triggered when glucose levels are increasing rapidly, based on predefined rise rate thresholds.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise Alert is a feature that triggers when the sensor glucose (SG) level is rising quickly, based on a defined rate threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;The Rise Alert is triggered when sensor glucose levels are rising rapidly, at or faster than a preset limit, indicating a need for user attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise Alert is a notification indicating a rapid increase in sensor glucose levels, signaling the need for user awareness or intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise Alert is a notification indicating a rapid increase in glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707375</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resume Basal Alert">
  <data key="d0">Resume Basal Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resume Basal Alert is a notification system integrated into insulin pump technology designed to inform users when basal insulin infusion resumes after a suspension event. This alert is typically triggered following an automatic suspension of insulin delivery, often initiated by safety features such as Suspend Before Low or Suspend On Low, which activate in response to predicted or actual low glucose levels. The primary function of the Resume Basal Alert is to notify the user that insulin delivery has been automatically restarted, either because continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) readings indicate that glucose levels are stabilizing or rising, or because the maximum allowable suspension period—commonly two hours—has elapsed.

The alert serves as a critical component of high and low glucose management systems, ensuring users remain aware of changes in insulin delivery to prevent potential complications. It is part of a broader category of High &amp; Low Alerts, emphasizing its role in maintaining glycemic control. By signaling the resumption of basal insulin, the Resume Basal Alert helps users monitor their treatment regimen and respond appropriately, particularly in automated insulin delivery systems where interventions occur without manual input. Multiple descriptions confirm that the alert consistently appears after suspension events, reinforcing its role in enhancing safety and awareness in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
