<node id="Easy Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Easy Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Easy Bolus is a simplified bolus delivery feature designed to enable quick and efficient insulin dosing for users of insulin pump systems. It streamlines the bolus administration process by minimizing the number of steps required, allowing users to deliver insulin without navigating through multiple menus or complex interface layers. This functionality is particularly useful in situations where rapid dosing is preferred or necessary, enhancing convenience and usability.

The feature operates exclusively in Manual mode, meaning it is available only when the user is not relying on automated or calculated insulin delivery systems. Easy Bolus allows the delivery of a normal bolus dose in preset increments, which can be customized during setup according to individual needs. Users can confirm both the setup and delivery of the bolus through sound alerts or vibration, providing immediate feedback without requiring visual confirmation.

Notably, Easy Bolus functions independently of the Bolus Wizard or other advanced calculation tools, making it a straightforward option for those who prefer manual control over their insulin dosing. Instead of inputting carbohydrate counts or blood glucose levels for algorithmic dose calculation, users can directly administer a preconfigured amount of insulin. The setup and delivery options for Easy Bolus are accessible directly through the pump’s interface, ensuring ease of access and consistent user experience. Overall, Easy Bolus serves as a practical, user-friendly tool for simplified insulin management in routine or time-sensitive scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707345</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Duration">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Duration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active insulin duration is a setting that defines how long insulin remains active in the body, used to prevent insulin stacking.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Insulin Duration is the length of time insulin remains active in the body, a parameter required for configuring the Bolus Wizard.&lt;SEP&gt;Active insulin duration is the time period over which a bolus of insulin continues to lower blood glucose levels, set during configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc77598dbeb5980c719d1d54a6c3ab77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-402361ced0649a06619dcaf93b0eb651</data>
