<node id="Pair Device">
  <data key="d0">Pair Device</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pair device is a function that establishes a secure wireless connection between the insulin pump and a new external device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700938</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Blocked">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Blocked</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion blocked is a specific alarm condition indicating that insulin cannot be delivered through the tubing or cannula.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700938</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Red Light Notification">
  <data key="d0">Red Light Notification</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The red light notification is a visual indicator on the insulin pump that blinks in a specific pattern to signal an alarm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700938</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audio Alert">
  <data key="d0">Audio Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The audio alert is a sound emitted by the insulin pump to notify the user of an alarm, based on audio settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vibration Alert">
  <data key="d0">Vibration Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The vibration alert is a tactile notification from the insulin pump that occurs in a pattern of three pulses if enabled.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Tubing">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Tubing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion tubing is a part of the insulin delivery system that can become kinked, knotted, or obstructed, leading to infusion issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Measurement">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Measurement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose measurement is a procedure to check current glucose levels, recommended when resolving an alarm.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose measurement is a method of checking glucose levels in the blood, typically through capillary testing, used to confirm sensor readings before making therapy decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Measurement is a function integrated into the Accu-Chek Solo Diabetes Manager for self-monitoring of blood sugar levels at home.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4f0d15ae81e49555dae7c149b2250be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/IFU Accu-Chek Guide Solo Diabetes Manager.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resume Basal">
  <data key="d0">Resume Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resume basal is an option on the insulin pump to restart basal insulin delivery after resolving an issue.&lt;SEP&gt;Resume Basal restarts basal insulin delivery after it has been suspended.&lt;SEP&gt;Resume Basal is a function used to restart basal insulin delivery after it has been suspended on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Resume Basal is a function used to restart basal insulin delivery after an Auto Suspend alarm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rewind">
  <data key="d0">Rewind</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rewind is a function on the insulin pump used to change the reservoir and infusion set when an alarm persists.&lt;SEP&gt;Rewind is a function used to retract the infusion set tubing, often required after a pump error or reservoir change.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature that returns the piston to its start position to allow placement of a new reservoir into the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707387</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Pattern Configuration">
  <data key="d0">Basal Pattern Configuration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal pattern configuration allows users to modify the timing and rate of basal insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ulina">
  <data key="d0">Ulina</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ulina is a person who is not receiving insulin and requires immediate attention due to an active alarm on the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91eefcd3f117b070db0c6aae336adcf9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspensión Manual de Infusión">
  <data key="d0">Suspensión Manual de Infusión</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">La suspensión manual de infusión es un procedimiento que detiene temporalmente la administración de insulina basal mediante la bomba, accesible a través del menú del dispositivo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reanudación de Infusión">
  <data key="d0">Reanudación de Infusión</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">La reanudación de infusión es el proceso que restablece la administración de insulina basal después de una suspensión manual, requiriendo confirmación en la pantalla de la bomba.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Administración de Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Administración de Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">La administración de bolus es una función de la bomba de insulina que permite al usuario introducir una dosis adicional de insulina para cubrir carbohidratos o corregir niveles altos de glucosa en sangre.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Manual">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Manual</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Manual is a function in the insulin pump that allows the user to manually deliver a bolus dose of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;El bolus manual es un tipo de dosis de insulina que el usuario programa directamente en la bomba según sus necesidades inmediatas de carbohidratos o glucosa.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Manual is a method of manually administering a specific insulin dose using an insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus manual is a function on the insulin pump that allows the user to manually input and deliver a dose of insulin for carbohydrates or high glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88cdb970e2c2f1aaaab96fdc11b589f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d74e338f7a37de66d4b2268a49021c4e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Menú de la Bomba">
  <data key="d0">Menú de la Bomba</data>
  <data key="d1">interface</data>
  <data key="d2">El menú de la bomba es la interfaz de usuario que permite acceder a funciones como suspender infusión, reanudar infusión y administrar bolus mediante la selección de opciones en pantalla.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advertencia de Infusión Suspendida">
  <data key="d0">Advertencia de Infusión Suspendida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Esta advertencia indica que al reanudar la infusión, la bomba no compensará la insulina basal no administrada durante la suspensión.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advertencia de Bolus Interrumpido">
  <data key="d0">Advertencia de Bolus Interrumpido</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Esta advertencia señala que si se suspende la infusión durante la administración de un bolus, el resto del bolus no se administrará al reanudar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Susi">
  <data key="d0">Susi</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Susi es una usuaria de la bomba de insulina que encuentra más fácil administrarse bolus con la bomba que con inyecciones tradicionales.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pantalla de Confirmación">
  <data key="d0">Pantalla de Confirmación</data>
  <data key="d1">interface</data>
  <data key="d2">La pantalla de confirmación aparece al realizar acciones críticas como suspender o reanudar la infusión, solicitando al usuario verificar su decisión.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Insulin Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Basal Insulin Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal insulin pattern refers to the programmed schedule of background insulin delivery by the pump, which continues unless manually suspended.&lt;SEP&gt;A basal insulin pattern defines the rate at which insulin is delivered over specific time segments throughout the day and night.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus for Carbohydrates">
  <data key="d0">Bolus for Carbohydrates</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus for carbohydrates is a type of insulin dose calculated to cover the intake of carbohydrate-containing foods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f095f73e1ec982aa57fd66798ffaec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensibilidad">
  <data key="d0">Sensibilidad</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensibilidad, or insulin sensitivity factor, is the amount of blood glucose reduction per unit of insulin, used in the Bolus Wizard calculation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1250027f75a49e3288b12fc80a630d33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuracion de Infusion">
  <data key="d0">Configuracion de Infusion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Configuracion de Infusion refers to the process of setting up infusion parameters on an insulin pump, including basal rates and bolus settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1250027f75a49e3288b12fc80a630d33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Target">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Target</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose Target is the desired blood glucose level, equivalent to Objetivo GS, used in therapy management.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose target is the desired glucose level set by a physician and programmed into the Bolus Wizard™ to guide correction bolus calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1250027f75a49e3288b12fc80a630d33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-425759c12d133ef4832928e8f5d50896</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702627</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Rate Configuration">
  <data key="d0">Basal Rate Configuration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal Rate Configuration is the process of setting predefined temporary or pattern-based basal insulin infusion rates on an insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1250027f75a49e3288b12fc80a630d33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed MMT-332A">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed MMT-332A</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed MMT-332A is a 3.0 mL insulin reservoir used in an insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audio Icon">
  <data key="d0">Audio Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The audio icon displays the current audio option in use, such as audio only, vibration only, or both audio and vibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700942</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump">
  <data key="d0">Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pump is a medical device designed for continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion, primarily used in diabetes management to deliver insulin in both basal (continuous) and bolus (on-demand) amounts. It functions as the central component in advanced insulin delivery systems such as the MiniMed™ and the MiniMed 780G system, where it operates based on programmed settings and integrates with continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) devices, sensors, transmitters, and mobile applications for coordinated treatment. The device features a screen that displays critical information including time, insulin activity, status icons, alerts, messages, and sensor data, and it supports user interaction through buttons and various operational modes such as Sleep mode, which requires unlocking to resume full functionality.

The Pump delivers insulin from a reservoir through an infusion set using a piston mechanism, requiring a battery for operation and periodic maintenance such as rewinding before inserting a new reservoir. It supports advanced features like SmartGuard technology, basal rate control, bolus delivery (including various bolus types), and automatic suspension in response to glucose trends or system alerts. The device includes safety mechanisms such as alarms, alerts, reminders, tones, and vibrations to notify users of malfunctions, low power, connectivity issues, or disconnections from sensors and transmitters. It performs self-tests, manages settings, and may require restarts and re-entry of configurations when encountering operational errors.

Connectivity is a core function of the Pump, enabling it to pair with CGM systems, receive real-time sensor readings, detect sensor status, and respond to glucose monitoring alerts. It communicates with transmitters and mobile devices, though it may fail to receive sensor data if signal connectivity is disrupted. The Pump is susceptible to operational issues caused by physical impact, magnetic fields, radiation, battery problems, or sensor disconnection, and it actively detects flow issues and system faults, displaying appropriate warnings. As a comprehensive insulin delivery system, the Pump integrates screen-based navigation, including a Home screen, with robust user interface functions, ensuring effective and safe diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc61f77b003d0086bd985ddb94fc2a98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707229</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sleep Mode">
  <data key="d0">Sleep Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sleep Mode is a power-saving state designed for insulin pumps, particularly models such as the MiniMed 780G, that allows the device to conserve energy while maintaining full functionality, including uninterrupted insulin delivery. This low-power state is typically activated automatically after approximately two minutes of inactivity, though it can also be manually triggered by the user. Upon activation, the pump's screen turns off or dims and the backlight is deactivated, reducing visual disturbances—especially beneficial during nighttime use.

During Sleep Mode, the insulin pump remains fully operational, ensuring that therapeutic functions such as basal insulin delivery continue without interruption. Certain features, like Easy Bolus, remain enabled, allowing for convenient dosing adjustments while minimizing screen illumination. The device can quickly wake from this state, returning to the Home screen upon user interaction, ensuring timely access to critical functions. Additionally, Sleep Mode often includes adjustments to alert settings, reducing or suppressing non-urgent notifications to prevent sleep disruption, thereby optimizing the user experience during rest periods.

A key security feature associated with Sleep Mode is the automatic locking of the device, particularly when Block mode is active, which helps prevent unintended button presses or unauthorized access. This locking mechanism enhances safety during periods of inactivity. Overall, Sleep Mode serves as an essential operational state that balances energy efficiency, patient safety, uninterrupted therapy, and user convenience, especially tailored for nighttime or restful periods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707345</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Margaret">
  <data key="d0">Margaret</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Margaret is a user of the insulin pump who observed the screen dimming and learned to reactivate it by pressing a button.&lt;SEP&gt;Margaret is a user who observed the screen dimming and learned to reactivate it by pressing a button.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Predefined">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Predefined</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Predefined is a feature that enables the user to deliver a preset bolus dose from previously configured settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700942</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scroll Bar">
  <data key="d0">Scroll Bar</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The scroll bar appears on the right side of the screen when a menu or display has more than six lines, allowing navigation through additional items.&lt;SEP&gt;The scroll bar appears when a screen or menu contains more than six lines, allowing navigation through additional items.&lt;SEP&gt;A scroll bar is a user interface element that appears when not all basal rates are visible, allowing the user to navigate through the full list of programmed rates.&lt;SEP&gt;A scroll bar is a user interface element that allows navigation through a list of basal indices when not all entries are visible on the screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7534f3bc09ac6e2eece38e12eb89cf1f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed Mobile">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed Mobile</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">MiniMed Mobile is a mobile application used to configure and manage the MiniMed insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0760c4e75f4ab51e1f860c2ae998ef46</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700943</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blue Adapter">
  <data key="d0">Blue Adapter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Blue Adapter is a device used to transfer data from the insulin pump to the CareLink software when the mobile app is not usable.&lt;SEP&gt;The Blue Adapter is a hardware component used to connect the insulin pump to a computer and should be disconnected when not in use for security.&lt;SEP&gt;The Blue Adapter is a device that uploads system data from the MiniMed 780G system to CareLink software via a USB port on a computer.&lt;SEP&gt;The Blue Adapter is a hardware device used to upload system data from the insulin pump to CareLink Software.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0760c4e75f4ab51e1f860c2ae998ef46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707360</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Julia">
  <data key="d0">Julia</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Julia is a patient who transfers pump data to the CareLink Personal software before medical visits and grants caregivers access to her reports.&lt;SEP&gt;Julia is a user who transfers data from her insulin pump and glucose meter to CareLink Personal before doctor visits and shares reports with her physician.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0760c4e75f4ab51e1f860c2ae998ef46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704150</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Reading">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose reading is a measurement of blood sugar levels transmitted from the Accu-Chek Guide Link meter to the MiniMed 770G insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose Reading displays the most recent glucose level measured within the last 12 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose readings are values displayed by the CGM system every 5 minutes, representing the amount of glucose in interstitial fluid.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0760c4e75f4ab51e1f860c2ae998ef46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Manual">
  <data key="d0">User Manual</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The user manual is a document included with the Accu-Chek Guide Link meter that provides detailed instructions on its use.&lt;SEP&gt;The user manual provides instructions and educational content for patients using the MiniMed insulin pump system.&lt;SEP&gt;The User Manual contains instructions, warnings, and information necessary for the safe and proper use of the Accu-Chek Solo micro pump system, including details on cleaning, maintenance, and symbol meanings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0760c4e75f4ab51e1f860c2ae998ef46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b7bb277d16feead8d082fc004d51d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd22ca03a61055434dc1e128fb57ee3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/IFU Accu-Chek Guide Solo Diabetes Manager.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extreme Temperatures">
  <data key="d0">Extreme Temperatures</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d2">Exposure to extreme heat or cold, such as in checked luggage, can reduce insulin effectiveness and lead to hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Extreme temperatures are environmental conditions that can affect the performance and safety of the MiniMed 780G system.&lt;SEP&gt;Exposure to extreme temperatures, either too high or too low, can damage the insulin pump or degrade insulin, affecting device performance and safety.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traveler">
  <data key="d0">Traveler</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4</data>
  <data key="d2">The American Diabetes Association advises travelers with diabetes to contact them at 1.703.549.1500 ext. 1768 if they encounter problems during security screening.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700968</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
