  <data key="d0">Total 24 hr</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1134674d4e1ab07998567f3fa77e251d</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal 1 covers a full 24-hour period with a total insulin delivery of 19.1 units.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778700985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal 1 Total 24 Hr: 21.6 U">
  <data key="d0">Basal 1 Total 24 Hr: 21.6 U</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a</data>
  <data key="d2">Setting Basal 1 to 0.900 U/h results in a total daily insulin delivery of 21.6 units.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778701012</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal 1 Total 24 Hr: 18 U">
  <data key="d0">Basal 1 Total 24 Hr: 18 U</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a</data>
  <data key="d2">A basal rate of 0.750 U/h delivers a total of 18 units of insulin over 24 hours.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778701012</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Higado">
  <data key="d0">Higado</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">El hígado almacena glucosa cuando hay insulina presente y la libera cuando hay glucagón, ayudando a mantener el equilibrio glucémico.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfd7b4fa0ccd15d540a9299e77dbf1dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liquido Intersticial">
  <data key="d0">Liquido Intersticial</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Liquido Intersticial is the fluid surrounding cells where glucose accumulates when insufficient insulin is available, leading to high glucose levels in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;El líquido intersticial es el medio a través del cual la glucosa se traslada desde la sangre hacia las células bajo la acción de la insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfd7b4fa0ccd15d540a9299e77dbf1dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6900fc7e5ef921c29efe412333f2e7ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina De Acción Intermedia">
  <data key="d0">Insulina De Acción Intermedia</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina de acción intermedia es un tipo de insulina utilizada para cubrir los requisitos de insulina basal, con una absorción que tarda entre 12 y 24 horas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59696e5e7f94ff9d51e39d90ec169e17</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina De Acción Prolongada">
  <data key="d0">Insulina De Acción Prolongada</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina de acción prolongada es un tipo de insulina que se inyecta una o dos veces al día y proporciona insulina basal, aunque con variabilidad en su absorción.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59696e5e7f94ff9d51e39d90ec169e17</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina De Acción Rápida">
  <data key="d0">Insulina De Acción Rápida</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina de acción rápida es absorbida aproximadamente 15 minutos después de la administración y es utilizada por las bombas de insulina para cubrir las necesidades basales de manera constante y fiable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59696e5e7f94ff9d51e39d90ec169e17</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Absorción De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Absorción De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">La absorción de insulina se refiere al proceso mediante el cual la insulina inyectada bajo la piel entra en el torrente sanguíneo, con variabilidad significativa en los tipos de acción intermedia y prolongada.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59696e5e7f94ff9d51e39d90ec169e17</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control De Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Control De Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">El control de glucosa implica mantener los niveles de azúcar en sangre dentro de un rango razonable, lo cual es más difícil con insulina de acción intermedia o prolongada debido a la variabilidad en la absorción.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59696e5e7f94ff9d51e39d90ec169e17</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Índice Basal Temporal">
  <data key="d0">Índice Basal Temporal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">El índice basal temporal es una función de la bomba de insulina que permite ajustar temporalmente la tasa de suministro de insulina basal durante situaciones como ejercicio o enfermedad.&lt;SEP&gt;El índice basal temporal es una ajuste temporal en la tasa de infusión basal de insulina, utilizado para manejar aumentos temporales en las necesidades de insulina, como durante una enfermedad.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59696e5e7f94ff9d51e39d90ec169e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Piel Grasa">
  <data key="d0">Piel Grasa</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Piel grasa es un tipo de tejido cutáneo que puede afectar la absorción de insulina cuando se inyecta bajo la piel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59696e5e7f94ff9d51e39d90ec169e17</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sara">
  <data key="d0">Sara</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Sara is a person using an insulin pump to manage her blood glucose levels, with specific carbohydrate ratio, FSI, and glucose target settings programmed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d0f18d3b5098557dfd71a1955adc3a2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Current Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Current glucose is the measured blood glucose level at a given time, used as input for correction bolus calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d0f18d3b5098557dfd71a1955adc3a2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSI">
  <data key="d0">FSI</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">FSI, or correction factor, is the amount by which blood glucose decreases per unit of insulin, expressed in mg/dL per unit.&lt;SEP&gt;FSI stands for Factor de Sensibilidad a la Insulina (Insulin Sensitivity Factor), measured in mg/dL, indicating how much blood glucose drops per unit of insulin, such as 40 or 50 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;FSI (Factor de Sensibilidad a la Insulina) es un valor que indica cuánto disminuye la glucosa en sangre por cada unidad de insulina administrada.&lt;SEP&gt;FSI refers to the correction factor (insulin sensitivity factor) used to calculate insulin doses for high blood glucose correction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d0f18d3b5098557dfd71a1955adc3a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec2fea6c095d8e93483ff43ef875fb9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702453</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Servings">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Servings</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate servings are standardized units used in carbohydrate counting to quantify carbohydrate intake for insulin dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate servings represent the amount of carbohydrates in a meal, measured in portions or exchanges, used to calculate meal bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d0f18d3b5098557dfd71a1955adc3a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb7ffc723b939ad50f1b00ca6ec8b9a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG">
  <data key="d0">SG</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SG refers to glucose in the sensor, representing glucose levels in interstitial fluid as measured by a continuous glucose monitoring system.&lt;SEP&gt;SG se refiere al nivel de glucosa en sangre medido por el sensor del sistema MiniMed™ 640G.&lt;SEP&gt;SG refers to sensor glucose values obtained from a continuous glucose monitoring system used to track glucose trends.&lt;SEP&gt;SG refers to sensor glucose readings obtained from the continuous glucose monitoring system.&lt;SEP&gt;SG refers to sensor glucose, a reading from a CGM device that estimates blood glucose levels and triggers alerts when values are high or low.&lt;SEP&gt;The acronym for sensor glucose; refers to glucose readings obtained from a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) system.&lt;SEP&gt;The acronym for sensor glucose, referring to glucose levels measured by a CGM sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f2cf8a591a83e4436ab6a76c2d30e2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707289</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Actividad">
  <data key="d0">Actividad</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Actividad refers to physical activity, which can influence blood glucose levels and must be considered when evaluating insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cenar Tarde">
  <data key="d0">Cenar Tarde</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cenar Tarde refers to eating dinner late, a factor that may affect glucose levels and interfere with basal insulin effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tentempié Antes de Acostarse">
  <data key="d0">Tentempié Antes de Acostarse</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tentempié Antes de Acostarse refers to a snack consumed before bedtime, which can impact overnight glucose levels if not matched with appropriate insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Adicional">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Adicional</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Adicional refers to an extra insulin dose that may be needed when consuming snacks or meals outside regular times.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tendencia">
  <data key="d0">Tendencia</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Tendencia refers to the direction and rate of change in glucose levels as displayed by continuous glucose monitoring systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alertas Alta">
  <data key="d0">Alertas Alta</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alertas Alta are notifications from the insulin pump or glucose monitoring system indicating that glucose levels are rising or are above a set threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grafico del Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Grafico del Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Grafico del Sensor is a visual representation of sensor glucose data over time, used to analyze patterns and detect high glucose values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prueba del Indice Basal">
  <data key="d0">Prueba del Indice Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Prueba del Indice Basal is a method used to evaluate the accuracy of the basal insulin rate by monitoring glucose levels under fasting conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equipo para la Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Equipo para la Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Equipo para la Diabetes is the medical team responsible for supporting patients in managing insulin therapy and adjusting basal and bolus doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hoja de Documentacion">
  <data key="d0">Hoja de Documentacion</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hoja de Documentacion is a form used to record glucose values, trends, and basal rates for discussion with the diabetes care team.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fundamentos de la Terapia con Bomba de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Fundamentos de la Terapia con Bomba de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fundamentos de la Terapia con Bomba de Insulina is an educational resource providing guidance on managing insulin pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Omitidos (Comidas)">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Omitidos (Comidas)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Omitidos (Comidas) is a function in the insulin pump that sends alerts if a mealtime bolus is missed during a programmed time window.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ratio Insulina/Racion">
  <data key="d0">Ratio Insulina/Racion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ratio Insulina/Racion determines the amount of insulin needed per carbohydrate serving and is evaluated by comparing glucose levels before and after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Ratio Insulina/Racion refers to the number of units of insulin needed to cover one carbohydrate serving, used in calculating mealtime insulin doses.&lt;SEP&gt;Ratio Insulina/Racion (I/C ratio) determines the amount of insulin needed per gram of carbohydrate consumed and is evaluated if post-meal glucose levels are too low.&lt;SEP&gt;Ratio Insulina/Racion is the insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio used to determine the correct bolus dose based on carbohydrate intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd60281301900b9df0acbe6be09fa2f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Factor de Sensibilidad a la Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Factor de Sensibilidad a la Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Factor de Sensibilidad a la Insulina (FSI) indicates how much blood glucose drops per unit of insulin and is reviewed if correction boluses lead to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Factor de Sensibilidad a la Insulina is a parameter that indicates how much one unit of insulin lowers blood glucose, used in dose calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Comida con Grasas y Proteinas">
  <data key="d0">Comida con Grasas y Proteinas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Comida con Grasas y Proteinas refers to meals high in fat and protein, which digest more slowly and can cause delayed increases in blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus de Comida">
  <data key="d0">Bolus de Comida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus de Comida is the insulin dose calculated to cover carbohydrates consumed, based on carbohydrate servings and an insulin-to-carb ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus de Comida refers to the insulin dose administered before meals to manage postprandial glucose levels, which may be forgotten or miscalculated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec2fea6c095d8e93483ff43ef875fb9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Historial de Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Historial de Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Historial de Bolus is a log within the MiniMed™ 640G system that records the timing and amount of previous bolus doses, used to confirm if a mealtime bolus was delivered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerta Antes Limite Bajo">
  <data key="d0">Alerta Antes Limite Bajo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A warning feature in the MiniMed™ 640G system that alerts the user before glucose levels reach a predefined low threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerta En Limite Alto">
  <data key="d0">Alerta En Limite Alto</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert function in the MiniMed™ 640G system that activates when glucose levels reach a predefined high threshold, helping prevent hyperglycemia and potential ketosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta En Limite Alto is triggered when the sensor glucose value reaches the predefined high glucose limit in the MiniMed™ 640G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerta Ascenso">
  <data key="d0">Alerta Ascenso</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert in the MiniMed™ 640G system that notifies the user of a rising glucose trend, enabling early intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta Ascenso is an alert activated when glucose levels rise faster than a preset rate, indicating a rapid increase in blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sistema MiniMed ™ 640G">
  <data key="d0">Sistema MiniMed ™ 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin pump system designed to deliver insulin therapy with features like glucose trend monitoring, bolus calculation, and customizable alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guia De Usuario Del Sistema MiniMed ™ 640G">
  <data key="d0">Guia De Usuario Del Sistema MiniMed ™ 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A user manual providing instructions on operating the MiniMed™ 640G insulin pump, including alert management and therapy adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tendencia Ascendente">
  <data key="d0">Tendencia Ascendente</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An upward glucose trend indicated by directional arrows on the MiniMed™ 640G display, signaling potential hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autocontrol De Glucemia Capilar">
  <data key="d0">Autocontrol De Glucemia Capilar</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">El autocontrol de glucemia capilar es una técnica para medir los niveles de glucosa en sangre mediante una muestra de sangre capilar, utilizada para confirmar lecturas antes de tomar decisiones terapéuticas.&lt;SEP&gt;El autocontrol de glucemia capilar es una prueba manual para medir los niveles de glucosa en sangre mediante una gota de sangre, utilizada para confirmar lecturas del sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;A self-testing procedure where the user checks blood glucose levels using a glucometer to verify sensor readings and inform therapy decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Duracion Hasta Limite Alto">
  <data key="d0">Duracion Hasta Limite Alto</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A user-defined time interval, such as 20 minutes, before the expected high glucose threshold is reached, triggering the "Alerta antes de limite alto".</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medicamentos Sin Receta">
  <data key="d0">Medicamentos Sin Receta</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Over-the-counter medications that may affect glucose levels and require consultation with a pharmacist or medical team before use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cetosis">
  <data key="d0">Cetosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A metabolic state caused by high glucose and insulin deficiency, which the system aims to prevent through high glucose alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cetoacidosis">
  <data key="d0">Cetoacidosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A severe form of ketosis that can result from untreated hyperglycemia, prevented by timely response to system alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="40 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d0">40 Mg/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A critical low glucose threshold value, indicating a potential hypoglycemic event.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="240 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d0">240 Mg/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A high glucose threshold value, above which corrective insulin bolus may be required.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed ™ 640G">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed ™ 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin pump system that provides automated insulin delivery and glucose monitoring with advanced alert features for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAP En La Rutina Diaria">
  <data key="d0">SAP En La Rutina Diaria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A chapter in the user guide describing how to integrate the Sensor-Augmented Pump (SAP) therapy into daily life.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP En La Rutina Diaria is a chapter in the user guide that discusses the use of the MiniMed™ 640G system in daily life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ecb158d437bb3657976e38d9b2e33dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bloodstream">
  <data key="d0">Bloodstream</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The bloodstream acts as a continuous transport system that carries glucose and other nutrients throughout the body after absorption from the digestive tract.&lt;SEP&gt;The bloodstream is where insulin enters after administration and through which it is distributed to regulate glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702468</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liver">
  <data key="d0">Liver</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The liver stores excess glucose after meals and releases it back into the bloodstream when energy is needed, such as during fasting or exercise.&lt;SEP&gt;The liver stores glucose after meals and releases it back into the bloodstream between meals, contributing to energy balance.&lt;SEP&gt;The liver stores and releases glucose in response to hormonal signals from the pancreas, particularly insulin and glucagon, to maintain glucose balance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Liver stores and releases glucose to help maintain stable blood glucose levels between meals and during sleep.&lt;SEP&gt;The liver stores and releases glucose and is regulated by insulin to maintain blood glucose balance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intestine">
  <data key="d0">Intestine</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The small intestine is part of the digestive tract where nutrients, including glucose, are absorbed into the bloodstream after food is metabolized.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stomach">
  <data key="d0">Stomach</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The stomach is part of the digestive system where food begins to be broken down before moving to the small intestine for nutrient absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;The stomach is a digestive organ mentioned in the context of glucose processing, though its role is not elaborated in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;The Stomach processes food, contributing to glucose release into the bloodstream after digestion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fat">
  <data key="d0">Fat</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fat is a form of long-term energy storage in the body; excess glucose beyond liver storage capacity is converted into fat.&lt;SEP&gt;Fat is used as an alternative energy source when cells cannot access glucose due to insulin deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Fat is a nutrient that slows the digestion of carbohydrates, delaying the rise in blood glucose during hypoglycemia treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digestive Tract">
  <data key="d0">Digestive Tract</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The digestive tract, including the stomach and small intestine, is where food is broken down and nutrients like glucose are absorbed into the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Levels">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose levels refer to the concentration of glucose in the blood, which must be monitored regularly to ensure they remain within the target range for effective diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose levels refer to the concentration of glucose in the blood, which can rise rapidly if insulin delivery is interrupted.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose levels are affected by the composition of meals, including carbohydrates, fats, and proteins, and can be influenced by insulin administration timing and physical activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose levels refer to the concentration of glucose in the blood, which the insulin infusion system aims to normalize between meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23235296c6ccfffc5ec397dd6b0dc7b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44b69a8e50a0a4230b6963fe643d8cd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ketone Bodies">
  <data key="d0">Ketone Bodies</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketone bodies are acidic waste products formed when the body uses fat for energy in the absence of sufficient insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketone bodies are produced when the body uses fat for energy due to insufficient insulin and are a key indicator of metabolic imbalance in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketone bodies are substances produced when the body burns fat for energy, and their presence indicates potential insulin deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketone bodies are acidic byproducts produced when the body breaks down fat for energy due to lack of insulin, and their presence is a warning sign of diabetic ketoacidosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23235296c6ccfffc5ec397dd6b0dc7b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702474</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Illness Management Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">Illness Management Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Illness management guidelines provide instructions for people using insulin pumps on how to handle sickness, including frequent glucose and ketone checks and maintaining basal insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23235296c6ccfffc5ec397dd6b0dc7b7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702480</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medico">
  <data key="d0">Medico</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Medico is a healthcare professional who provides medical guidance and instructions for managing diabetes during illness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84d2aca165fc0184360972207bae8c6b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
