</node>
<node id="MiniMed™ 640G">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed™ 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed™ 640G is an insulin pump system designed for diabetes therapy, integrating continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) technology to support comprehensive glucose management. It functions as a sensor-augmented pump (SAP) system, combining insulin delivery with real-time glucose data from the Guardian™ 2 Sensor to provide continuous monitoring, trend visualization, and automated alerts. The system enables users to track glucose levels in real time, view trends, and receive predictive notifications, including customizable alerts for high glucose levels and rapid glucose rises, enhancing proactive diabetes care.

A key feature of the MiniMed™ 640G is its SmartGuard™ technology, which provides predictive low glucose management by automatically suspending insulin delivery when sensor readings indicate an anticipated hypoglycemic event. This automated suspension function helps reduce the risk of low blood sugar episodes. The system also supports flexible insulin delivery through features such as temporary basal rate adjustments, multiple bolus delivery options, and the Bolus Wizard™, which calculates appropriate insulin doses by factoring in active insulin, current glucose levels, carbohydrate intake, and user-specific insulin settings. Additional tools include bolus history tracking and alerts for missed meals, supporting consistent therapy adherence.

The MiniMed™ 640G requires periodic calibration using blood glucose readings to maintain sensor accuracy and includes wireless communication capabilities via the Guardian™ 2 Link for seamless data transmission. It also offers practical functions such as airplane mode for use during air travel. Designed to automate and simplify insulin therapy, the MiniMed™ 640G integrates sensor data with customizable alerts and delivery features to assist users in maintaining stable glucose levels, representing an advanced solution in insulin infusion technology for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d265f691032645cfa3e43210043f3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f14c91b2fb52c8fcc6d43aa4f53f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03aab2b6261ddc73d474d0c866e7b37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc5c57277d034fb00908385613bf5a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
