<node id="Fat And Protein Meal">
  <data key="d0">Fat And Protein Meal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A meal high in fats and proteins digests slowly, affecting glucose absorption and insulin needs differently than carbohydrate-rich meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Blood Glucose Alert">
  <data key="d0">High Blood Glucose Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert is triggered by the insulin pump system if a bolus is missed, such as at 8:01 h after the scheduled breakfast bolus time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meal Composition">
  <data key="d0">Meal Composition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Meal composition refers to the nutritional content of food, including carbohydrates, fats, and proteins, which affects blood glucose response and insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702511</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAP">
  <data key="d0">SAP</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SAP refers to Sensor-Augmented Pump therapy, a treatment approach designed to improve diabetes management by combining insulin pump therapy with continuous glucose monitoring. This integrated system enables real-time tracking of blood glucose levels, providing users with ongoing data on glucose trends, including the direction and rate of change in glucose levels. By merging insulin delivery through a pump with continuous glucose monitoring, SAP offers a more dynamic and responsive method for maintaining optimal glucose control.

The therapy is used primarily in the management of diabetes, particularly type 1 diabetes, where precise insulin dosing is critical. SAP systems allow for timely adjustments in insulin administration based on continuous feedback from glucose sensors, thereby reducing the risk of both hyperglycemia and hypoglycemia. Multiple descriptions consistently define SAP as an advanced approach that enhances glycemic control through the synergistic use of two key technologies: insulin pumps and continuous glucose monitors.

Although one description refers to SAP as "Sistema Avanzado de Bomba," a direct translation of "Advanced Pump System," the overwhelming majority of sources align on "Sensor-Augmented Pump" as the correct expansion of the acronym. This consistency across definitions confirms that SAP, in the context of diabetes care, denotes Sensor-Augmented Pump therapy—a comprehensive, technology-driven strategy aimed at improving long-term outcomes for individuals with diabetes through integrated monitoring and insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23235296c6ccfffc5ec397dd6b0dc7b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702511</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Insulin Index">
  <data key="d0">Basal Insulin Index</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The basal insulin index refers to the rate of background insulin delivery in pump therapy, which can be adjusted based on glucose patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8</data>
