</node>
<node id="Muscle Glycogen Replenishment">
  <data key="d0">Muscle Glycogen Replenishment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Muscle glycogen replenishment is a physiological process that can cause delayed hypoglycemia after physical activity due to increased glucose uptake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alcohol Intake">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol Intake</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol intake can affect blood glucose levels and may contribute to hypoglycemia, especially if not accounted for in therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
