</node>
<node id="High Glucose Trend">
  <data key="d0">High Glucose Trend</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A high glucose trend indicates a sustained increase in sensor glucose values, which may result from various factors including dietary, technical, or physiological causes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702523</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid Glucose Rise">
  <data key="d0">Rapid Glucose Rise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A rapid glucose rise occurs when glucose increases faster than a user-defined threshold, triggering an alert to allow early corrective action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
