  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trend Arrows">
  <data key="d0">Trend Arrows</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Trend Arrows are graphical and directional indicators displayed on continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems and insulin pumps, such as the MiniMed™ 640G, to represent the direction and rate of change in glucose levels. These visual cues appear on the device screen, often on the home display, and provide real-time updates on whether glucose levels are rising, falling, or remaining stable, along with the speed of these changes. By illustrating the current trend, Trend Arrows help users anticipate rapid fluctuations in glucose, enabling timely interventions.

The primary function of Trend Arrows is to support informed decision-making in diabetes management, particularly in adjusting insulin therapy and dosing. Users rely on these indicators to respond proactively to potential hypoglycemic or hyperglycemic events. The arrows are typically displayed continuously, though in some cases, they may only appear when glucose levels fall below 50 mg/dL unless interrupted by an alarm condition. Overall, Trend Arrows serve as a critical tool in dynamic glucose monitoring, enhancing user awareness and therapeutic precision by translating complex glucose data into intuitive visual signals.&lt;SEP&gt;Trend arrows are visual indicators in glucose monitoring systems that show the direction and rate of glucose change, helping users anticipate hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03aab2b6261ddc73d474d0c866e7b37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
