<node id="Bombas De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Bombas De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Las bombas de insulina son dispositivos médicos que administran insulina de forma continua y controlada, utilizados en la terapia para el manejo de la diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor De Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Sensor De Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El sensor de glucosa es un componente del sistema SAP que mide continuamente los niveles de glucosa en el líquido intersticial y transmite los datos al dispositivo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Umbral De Alerta De Glucosa Alta">
  <data key="d0">Umbral De Alerta De Glucosa Alta</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">El umbral de alerta de glucosa alta es un valor configurado en el sistema SAP que activa una alerta cuando los niveles de glucosa superan un límite predefinido.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus De Corrección">
  <data key="d0">Bolus De Corrección</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">El bolus de corrección es una dosis adicional de insulina administrada para reducir niveles elevados de glucosa en sangre.&lt;SEP&gt;The bolus de corrección is an insulin dose administered to correct high blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian™ 2 Link Transmitter">
  <data key="d0">Guardian™ 2 Link Transmitter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guardian™ 2 Link Transmitter is a device that connects to the Enlite™ glucose sensor and enables glucose monitoring, allowing for activities like swimming with proper adhesion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enlite™ Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Enlite™ Glucose Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enlite™ Glucose Sensor is a medical device used for continuous glucose monitoring and must be properly adhered to the skin for accurate readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Alert">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor alerts are notifications from the MiniMed™ 640G System that can be silenced for discretion, including high, low, or all alerts, with visual indication on the pump screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor alerts are notifications from the CGM device indicating glucose trends, thresholds, or system events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Glucose Alert">
  <data key="d0">High Glucose Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High glucose alert is a type of sensor alert triggered when glucose levels exceed a set threshold, which users can choose to silence.&lt;SEP&gt;High glucose alert is a notification from a continuous glucose monitoring system indicating blood glucose levels are above a set threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Glucose Alert">
  <data key="d0">Low Glucose Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low glucose alert is a type of sensor alert triggered when glucose levels fall below a set threshold, which users can choose to silence.&lt;SEP&gt;Low Glucose Alert is an automatic notification activated when sensor glucose reaches the low limit during suspended insulin infusion, warning the user of critical glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="All Sensor Alerts">
  <data key="d0">All Sensor Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">All sensor alerts include high, low, and calibration alerts; silencing all means no audible or vibration alerts, though alerts appear on screen and in history.&lt;SEP&gt;All Sensor Alerts encompass all alerts related to the CGM device, including calibration or BG check alerts, reminders, error messages, sensor change notifications, sensor updating, and connection issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Silencing">
  <data key="d0">Alert Silencing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert silencing is a feature allowing users to mute sensor alerts temporarily in increments from 30 minutes to 24 hours for discretion during daily activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airplane Mode">
  <data key="d0">Airplane Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Airplane Mode is a setting on the MiniMed™ 640G that disables wireless communication during flights and can be activated before takeoff and deactivated after landing.&lt;SEP&gt;Airplane mode is a setting on the MiniMed™ 640G pump that must be activated before takeoff when traveling by air to comply with regulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc5c57277d034fb00908385613bf5a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Trend Information">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Trend Information</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose trend information provides real-time data on glucose direction and rate of change, helping users make decisions about insulin, food, and activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alternative Basal Profile">
  <data key="d0">Alternative Basal Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An alternative basal profile is a programmable insulin delivery setting used during specific conditions such as illness or increased physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Trend">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Trend</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose trend refers to the direction and rate of change in blood glucose levels as displayed by continuous glucose monitoring systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Counting Error">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Counting Error</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate counting error occurs when the amount of carbohydrates consumed is miscalculated, leading to incorrect insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Counterregulation After Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Counterregulation After Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Counterregulation after hypoglycemia is a physiological response where the body releases hormones to raise blood glucose, potentially leading to rebound hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication Interaction">
  <data key="d0">Medication Interaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medication interaction refers to the effect certain drugs, including over-the-counter medications, may have on blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customizable Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Customizable Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Customizable alerts are user-configurable notifications on the MiniMed™ 640G system for high, low, or rapidly changing glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sick Day Plan">
  <data key="d0">Sick Day Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A sick day plan is a physician-provided protocol for managing insulin therapy during illness to prevent complications like hyperglycemia or DKA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Plan for DKA">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Plan for DKA</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The emergency plan for DKA (diabetic ketoacidosis) outlines steps to take when ketones are present and blood glucose is high, especially before physical activity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Emergency Plan for DKA is a medical protocol provided by a healthcare team to manage diabetic ketoacidosis when ketone test results are positive.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cell">
  <data key="d0">Cell</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A cell requires glucose for energy, which can only enter with the assistance of insulin binding to its receptors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Receptor">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Receptor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin receptor is a specific site on the cell wall where insulin binds to trigger the chemical reaction allowing glucose entry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ketoacidosis Diabética">
  <data key="d0">Ketoacidosis Diabética</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketoacidosis Diabética is a serious condition caused by high glucose and high ketone levels in the blood due to lack of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Correction Dose">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Correction Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin correction dose is administered to manage high blood glucose levels, either via syringe or insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin correction dose is a measured amount of insulin administered to lower high blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Ketone Test">
  <data key="d0">Blood Ketone Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A blood ketone test measures ketone levels using a small blood sample and is one method to assess insulin deficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urine Ketone Test">
  <data key="d0">Urine Ketone Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A urine ketone test uses reactive strips to detect ketone bodies in urine and is an accessible, low-cost method for monitoring ketosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reactive Test Strip">
  <data key="d0">Reactive Test Strip</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Reactive test strips are used to detect ketone bodies in urine by changing color based on ketone concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed™ Pump">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed™ Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed™ pump is a specific insulin pump that can be programmed with up to 48 different basal rate segments in 24 hours and includes the Bolus Wizard™ feature.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed™ pump is a medical device used for insulin delivery in diabetes management, part of the insulin pump therapy system.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed™ pump is an insulin delivery device that includes features like Bolus Wizard™ to calculate correction doses.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed™ pump is an insulin delivery device that includes the Bolus Wizard™ function and maintains a bolus history for user review.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed™ Pump is an insulin delivery device manufactured by Medtronic that connects with a glucose meter for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb7ffc723b939ad50f1b00ca6ec8b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704123</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Service">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Service</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Emergency services are to be contacted or visited if blood glucose continues to rise or if symptoms like vomiting or difficulty breathing occur.&lt;SEP&gt;The emergency service is the nearest facility to visit when experiencing severe symptoms such as high ketone levels, vomiting, or breathing difficulties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Carbohydrate Fluids">
  <data key="d0">Non-Carbohydrate Fluids</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-carbohydrate fluids, such as water, are recommended to maintain hydration without increasing blood glucose during ketosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-carbohydrate fluids are recommended for consumption during high glucose episodes to stay hydrated without raising blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insertion Site">
  <data key="d0">Insertion Site</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The insertion site is the location on the body where the infusion set is placed and should be changed if ketone bodies are present.&lt;SEP&gt;The insertion site is a location on the body where the infusion set is placed, chosen from recommended shaded areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The insertion site is the area on the body where an infusion set is placed and must be cleaned and rotated regularly to prevent complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ec727091282384bd8f9c91eb1d29b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Red Symbol">
  <data key="d0">Red Symbol</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Red Symbol appears on the screen when sensor glucose is below the low limit, indicating an active hypoglycemic state requiring immediate action.&lt;SEP&gt;The Red Symbol is a visual indicator displayed on the MiniMed™ 640G screen to signify that sensor glucose levels are still below the low limit after suspension of insulin infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Yellow Symbol">
  <data key="d0">Yellow Symbol</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Yellow Symbol appears when sensor glucose is above the low limit, indicating recovery or absence of severe hypoglycemia but still requiring monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard™">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard™</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard™ is an advanced feature of the MiniMed™ 640G system that predicts low glucose levels 30 minutes in advance and automatically suspends insulin infusion to prevent hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard™ is an automated insulin suspension system that helps prevent hypoglycemia by interrupting insulin infusion when glucose levels approach a preset low threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard™ is a feature of the MiniMed™ 640G system that automatically suspends insulin infusion when a drop in glucose levels is predicted.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard™ is an automated insulin suspension and resumption system designed to prevent low glucose levels and hypoglycemia in insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard™ is a system feature that predicts approaching low glucose levels 30 minutes in advance and automatically suspends insulin infusion when the low threshold is reached or exceeded, resuming when glucose levels recover.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard™ is an automated insulin suspension feature that predicts approaching low glucose levels up to 30 minutes in advance and stops insulin infusion to prevent hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard™ es una función del sistema MiniMed™ 640G que ayuda a prevenir la hipoglucemia suspendiendo automáticamente la infusión de insulina cuando los niveles de glucosa se acercan o alcanzan el límite bajo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03aab2b6261ddc73d474d0c866e7b37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Glucose Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Low Glucose Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Glucose Threshold is a personalized glucose level limit, typically set at or above 70 mg/dL, used to detect and prevent hypoglycemia through alerts or automated insulin suspension.&lt;SEP&gt;The Low Glucose Threshold is a user-adjustable setting between 50-90 mg/dL that determines when SmartGuard™ initiates suspension or alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Low Glucose Threshold is a user-configurable setting that defines the glucose level at which hypoglycemia alerts are triggered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Alert Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Alert Reminder is a configurable function that repeats low glucose alerts at intervals (e.g., every 20 minutes) until glucose levels rise above the low limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Adjustment is the process of modifying insulin bolus doses based on current glucose levels and trend arrows to prevent hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina De Accion Intermedia">
  <data key="d0">Insulina De Accion Intermedia</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina de accion intermedia tiene una absorcion y accion mas irregular, utilizada principalmente para cubrir las necesidades de insulina basal en tratamientos por inyecciones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-357e07e3b068c4c6d31ac6913e35178f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina De Accion Prolongada">
  <data key="d0">Insulina De Accion Prolongada</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina de accion prolongada presenta una accion menos predecible en cuanto a absorcion y duracion, empleada para satisfacer las necesidades de insulina basal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-357e07e3b068c4c6d31ac6913e35178f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreas Sano">
  <data key="d0">Pancreas Sano</data>
  <data key="d1">organ</data>
  <data key="d2">El pancreas sano regula naturalmente los niveles de glucosa en sangre mediante la liberacion de insulina basal y en bolus segun las necesidades metabolicas del organismo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-357e07e3b068c4c6d31ac6913e35178f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tratamiento Mediante Inyecciones">
  <data key="d0">Tratamiento Mediante Inyecciones</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">El tratamiento mediante inyecciones utiliza insulina de accion intermedia o prolongada para satisfacer las necesidades de insulina basal, con menor capacidad de ajuste y control en comparacion con la terapia con bomba.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-357e07e3b068c4c6d31ac6913e35178f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Administracion De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Administracion De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">La administracion de insulina se realiza mediante bomba o inyecciones, siendo fundamental mantenerla continua para evitar aumentos rapidos de glucosa en sangre.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-357e07e3b068c4c6d31ac6913e35178f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Bolus De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus de insulina es una dosis adicional de insulina administrada para cubrir alimentos con hidratos de carbono o corregir niveles altos de glucosa en sangre.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-357e07e3b068c4c6d31ac6913e35178f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Total">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Total</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus total is the sum of the food bolus and correction bolus used in insulin therapy to manage blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b0f14c91b2fb52c8fcc6d43aa4f53f64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Food Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Food Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Food bolus is the amount of insulin calculated to cover the carbohydrates consumed in a meal.&lt;SEP&gt;A food bolus is an insulin dose delivered to cover carbohydrate intake, calculated using the Carb Ratio setting in the Bolus Wizard.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A food bolus is an insulin dose calculated based on the carbohydrate content of a meal.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A dose of insulin given to cover an expected rise in glucose levels from carbohydrates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b0f14c91b2fb52c8fcc6d43aa4f53f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Glucose (SG) refers to the real-time glucose level measured in the interstitial fluid by a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) system. These readings are obtained through a subcutaneous sensor that detects glucose concentrations in the interstitial fluid, which may lag slightly behind blood glucose levels, especially during periods of rapid glucose fluctuation. As a result, Sensor Glucose values can differ from direct blood glucose measurements, though they provide a continuous and dynamic picture of glucose trends over time.

The Sensor Glucose readings are integral to diabetes management systems, particularly those involving automated insulin delivery. They are used by devices such as the MiniMed 780G and integrated with systems like SmartGuard to guide real-time insulin dosing decisions, trigger hypoglycemic or hyperglycemic alerts, and automate insulin delivery adjustments or suspensions. When Sensor Glucose data is unavailable, these automated features may deactivate, underscoring the dependency of such systems on continuous sensor input.

Sensor Glucose is displayed on sensor graphs and used for both immediate treatment decisions and long-term monitoring. It supports insulin delivery calculations and enables predictive algorithms to anticipate glucose trends, allowing for proactive intervention. In summary, Sensor Glucose is a critical parameter derived from CGM technology, enabling advanced diabetes management through continuous, real-time glucose estimation in the interstitial fluid.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b0f14c91b2fb52c8fcc6d43aa4f53f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03aab2b6261ddc73d474d0c866e7b37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707226</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor-Augmented Pump (SAP)">
  <data key="d0">Sensor-Augmented Pump (SAP)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor-Augmented Pump (SAP) therapy combines insulin pump use with continuous glucose monitoring to provide real-time glucose data and trends.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor-augmented pump (SAP) therapy combines insulin pump delivery with continuous glucose monitoring to improve glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor-Augmented Pump (SAP) therapy combines continuous glucose monitoring with insulin pump delivery to help prevent hyperglycemia through real-time data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b0f14c91b2fb52c8fcc6d43aa4f53f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capillary Blood Glucose Testing">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Blood Glucose Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Capillary blood glucose testing is a method of measuring blood sugar levels through finger-prick samples, required for calibration and verification in sensor-based systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Root Cause Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Root Cause Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Root cause analysis is a systematic process used to identify the underlying reasons for episodes of hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Root Cause Analysis is a systematic approach used to identify the underlying reasons for glucose fluctuations, such as hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic Technical Support">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic Technical Support</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Medtronic Technical Support is the service department responsible for assisting users with technical issues related to the MiniMed™ 640G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daily Routine">
  <data key="d0">Daily Routine</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The daily routine includes considerations for discretion, such as silencing alerts during meetings or other situations where notifications are undesirable.&lt;SEP&gt;The daily routine refers to the structured schedule of diabetes management activities, including monitoring, insulin delivery, and response to glucose fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc5c57277d034fb00908385613bf5a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapy Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Therapy Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Therapy optimization involves making adjustments to insulin pump settings and treatment plans to improve glucose control based on data analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Therapy Optimization involves adjusting insulin delivery settings based on glucose data to improve glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Calibration">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Calibration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic calibration is a feature that allows the glucose sensor to adjust its readings without manual input, though it may be turned off in some configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoglobina A1C">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobina A1C</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoglobina A1C es una prueba médica que mide el control glucémico promedio de los últimos 2-3 meses y se expresa como un porcentaje.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucosa Media Estimada">
  <data key="d0">Glucosa Media Estimada</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucosa Media Estimada es un valor derivado del porcentaje de hemoglobina A1C que representa el nivel promedio de glucosa en sangre en mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terapia con Bomba de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Terapia con Bomba de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">La terapia con bomba de insulina es un método de administración de insulina que busca mejorar el control glucémico y reducir la variabilidad glucémica.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variabilidad Glucémica">
  <data key="d0">Variabilidad Glucémica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">La variabilidad glucémica se refiere a las fluctuaciones frecuentes entre niveles altos y bajos de glucosa en sangre, que no son mostradas por la hemoglobina A1C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Servicio de Asistencia Técnica 24 Horas">
  <data key="d0">Servicio de Asistencia Técnica 24 Horas</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">El Servicio de Asistencia Técnica 24 horas es un soporte disponible para resolver problemas relacionados con la bomba de insulina, accesible al número 900 120 330.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Los Indices Basales">
  <data key="d0">Los Indices Basales</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Los Indices Basales se refieren a los niveles de insulina basal necesarios para mantener el control glucémico entre comidas y durante el sueño.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Desnaturalizada">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Desnaturalizada</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">La insulina desnaturalizada es insulina que ha perdido su eficacia debido a exposición a altas temperaturas o luz solar directa.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina desnaturalizada refers to insulin that has lost effectiveness due to exposure to heat or sunlight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control Glucémico">
  <data key="d0">Control Glucémico</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">El control glucémico es la regulación de los niveles de glucosa en sangre en personas con diabetes, evaluado mediante mediciones frecuentes y pruebas como la hemoglobina A1C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapy With Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d0">Therapy With Insulin Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Therapy with insulin pump is a method for managing diabetes by delivering insulin continuously through a pump device, requiring regular glucose monitoring and parameter adjustments based on medical guidance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44b69a8e50a0a4230b6963fe643d8cd0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702540</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Needs">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Needs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin needs represent the amount of insulin required by a person with diabetes, which may change over time and require adjustments in insulin pump settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44b69a8e50a0a4230b6963fe643d8cd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702540</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Pump Parameters">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pump Parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin pump parameters are the settings on an insulin pump that determine insulin delivery rates and dosages, which may need adjustment based on glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44b69a8e50a0a4230b6963fe643d8cd0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702540</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sleep">
  <data key="d0">Sleep</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Sleep is a physiological state during which glucose levels may fluctuate, necessitating monitoring to avoid hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia episodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44b69a8e50a0a4230b6963fe643d8cd0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702540</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capillary Glucose Testing">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Glucose Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Capillary glucose testing is the traditional method of measuring blood glucose levels using a fingerstick and glucometer, often used for self-monitoring in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44b69a8e50a0a4230b6963fe643d8cd0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702540</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina En Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Insulina En Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina En Bolus refers to the larger amounts of insulin produced by the pancreas in response to increased glucose levels after eating.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6900fc7e5ef921c29efe412333f2e7ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702540</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Suspension">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Suspension</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic Suspension is a function of the MiniMed™ 640G that suspends insulin delivery when sensor glucose is at or below 70 mg/dL and a further drop is predicted within 30 minutes, provided the pump is not in a refractory period.&lt;SEP&gt;Dynamic Suspension is a SmartGuard™ function that automatically stops insulin infusion when sensor glucose reaches or falls below the low threshold and predictive criteria are met.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702540</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Resume">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Resume</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic Resume is a function that restarts insulin delivery when sensor glucose rises above 20 mg/dL above the low threshold and is predicted to reach 40 mg/dL above it within 30 minutes, after at least 20 minutes of suspension.&lt;SEP&gt;Dynamic Resume is a SmartGuard™ function that automatically restarts insulin infusion when glucose levels rise above specified thresholds and the suspension has lasted at least 30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Basal Resume">
  <data key="d0">Manual Basal Resume</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual Basal Resume allows the user to manually restart insulin infusion at any time through the pump interface.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Before Low Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Alert Before Low Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Alert Before Low Threshold is a warning issued 30 minutes before the glucose level is predicted to reach the low threshold, allowing proactive intervention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User">
  <data key="d0">User</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The User is the individual operating the MiniMed™ 640G insulin pump and utilizing SmartGuard™ features for glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;The user is the individual operating the MiniMed™ 640G system, responsible for confirming alerts, performing blood glucose tests, and making therapy decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The user is the individual performing the device setup steps, including language selection, connection, and configuration of features like AutoLog.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704123</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspension Before Low Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Suspension Before Low Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspension Before Low Threshold is a SmartGuard™ feature that automatically suspends insulin infusion when glucose levels are predicted to reach the low threshold within 30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Glucose Limit">
  <data key="d0">High Glucose Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The High Glucose Limit is a user-defined threshold that triggers alerts when glucose levels exceed the set upper limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Before High Limit">
  <data key="d0">Alert Before High Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert Before High Limit is a warning system that notifies the user when glucose levels are predicted to exceed the high threshold soon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rising Glucose Alert">
  <data key="d0">Rising Glucose Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rising Glucose Alert is a notification that activates when glucose levels are increasing rapidly, prompting user awareness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="400 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">400 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">400 mg/dL is the upper threshold value where high glucose alerts are triggered in the MiniMed™ 640G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="40 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">40 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">40 mg/dL is a reference value associated with glucose change thresholds, possibly indicating a rate-based alert or system parameter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Glucose Threshold">
  <data key="d0">High Glucose Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Glucose Threshold is a personalized glucose level limit set by the user in consultation with their medical team, used to trigger alerts or system responses.&lt;SEP&gt;High Glucose Threshold is a user-defined limit above which the system triggers high glucose alerts; setting it too low may cause excessive alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Glucose Alert Reminder">
  <data key="d0">High Glucose Alert Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Glucose Alert Reminder is a configurable setting that repeats high glucose alerts at intervals (e.g., every 30 or 60 minutes) until glucose drops below the threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed™ 640G System User Guide">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed™ 640G System User Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed™ 640G System User Guide is a document providing instructions and educational information on the use of the MiniMed™ 640G insulin pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Review Questions">
  <data key="d0">Review Questions</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Review Questions are educational prompts included in the user guide to reinforce understanding of insulin pump therapy concepts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chapter 4">
  <data key="d0">Chapter 4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Chapter 4 is referenced as the section where further information about the frequency and timing of system calibration will be provided.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c03aab2b6261ddc73d474d0c866e7b37</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">MiniMed is a brand under Medtronic that specializes in insulin delivery systems, including insulin pumps.&lt;SEP&gt;MiniMed is the manufacturer of the insulin pump device and provides the Bolus Wizard feature as part of its therapy system.&lt;SEP&gt;MiniMed is a brand associated with medical devices, specifically insulin pumps and reservoirs.&lt;SEP&gt;MiniMed is a brand that produces insulin pumps, reservoirs, and infusion sets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6b7bb277d16feead8d082fc004d51d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd60281301900b9df0acbe6be09fa2f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed Insulin Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed Insulin Pump is a medical device manufactured by Medtronic that delivers insulin in a manner similar to the pancreas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6b7bb277d16feead8d082fc004d51d2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small Intestine">
  <data key="d0">Small Intestine</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Small Intestine absorbs glucose from digested food into the bloodstream for energy use.&lt;SEP&gt;The small intestine absorbs carbohydrates from food, which affects blood glucose levels and determines the need for bolus insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Injection Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Injection Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin injection treatment is a diabetes management method using multiple daily injections of both rapid-acting and intermediate or long-acting insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mild Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Mild Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mild hypoglycemia is a condition where blood glucose levels drop below 70 mg/dL, but the individual can recognize and treat it themselves by consuming fast-acting carbohydrates.&lt;SEP&gt;Mild hypoglycemia is a condition where blood glucose levels drop below normal but can be self-recognized and treated by consuming fast-acting carbohydrates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5cace75be2ca46efd8033523e47b6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="15/15 Rule">
  <data key="d0">15/15 Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The 15/15 rule is a method for treating mild hypoglycemia by consuming 5-15 grams of fast-acting carbohydrates and rechecking blood glucose after 15 minutes, repeating if necessary until levels rise above 70 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5cace75be2ca46efd8033523e47b6de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Family Member">
  <data key="d0">Family Member</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A family member is someone close to the patient who should be trained to administer glucagon in case of severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5cace75be2ca46efd8033523e47b6de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Friend">
  <data key="d0">Friend</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A friend is a close acquaintance who may need to assist in administering glucagon during a hypoglycemic emergency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5cace75be2ca46efd8033523e47b6de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Companion">
  <data key="d0">Companion</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A companion is an individual who spends time with the patient and should be educated on how to properly administer glucagon if needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5cace75be2ca46efd8033523e47b6de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin-to-Carb Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Insulin-to-Carb Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The insulin-to-carb ratio (I/R) defines the number of insulin units needed to cover one serving of carbohydrates and is used in bolus calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfb7ffc723b939ad50f1b00ca6ec8b9a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus History">
  <data key="d0">Bolus History</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus history is a record of insulin bolus doses, carbohydrate intake, and glucose readings stored in the insulin pump for review and analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus History is a record of previous bolus deliveries stored in the pump, used to review insulin administration patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfb7ffc723b939ad50f1b00ca6ec8b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Actividad Fisica">
  <data key="d0">Actividad Fisica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Actividad Fisica is a factor that can influence blood glucose levels and diabetes therapy outcomes, requiring consideration during treatment adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Actividad Fisica refers to physical activity and its impact on glucose levels, particularly in individuals using insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cena Tardia">
  <data key="d0">Cena Tardia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cena Tardia refers to late-night eating, a behavioral factor that may affect glucose levels and insulin requirements during the night.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor de Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Sensor de Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor de Glucosa is a device used in SAP therapy to monitor glucose levels continuously and provide trend data for therapy adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proteinas">
  <data key="d0">Proteinas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proteinas are macronutrients that, when consumed with carbohydrates, can influence the timing and magnitude of glucose response after meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grasas">
  <data key="d0">Grasas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Grasas are macronutrients that delay glucose absorption and may require extended bolus delivery to match the prolonged glucose effect.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b47e3679b82b031ef2f4cb55f5d1ca61</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidratos De Carbono Adicionales">
  <data key="d0">Hidratos De Carbono Adicionales</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hidratos De Carbono Adicionales are extra carbohydrates consumed to prevent hypoglycemia during or after physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reduccion De La Insulina Basal">
  <data key="d0">Reduccion De La Insulina Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Reduccion De La Insulina Basal refers to the temporary decrease in basal insulin infusion to manage blood glucose levels during physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tiempo">
  <data key="d0">Tiempo</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Tiempo refers to the duration in hours used to monitor the effects of physical activity, insulin, and alcohol on blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ultimo Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Ultimo Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultimo Bolus refers to the most recent insulin bolus administered, which affects blood glucose levels for several hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nivel De Actividad Fisica">
  <data key="d0">Nivel De Actividad Fisica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nivel De Actividad Fisica describes the intensity or extent of physical exertion, which influences insulin and carbohydrate requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Valor De GS">
  <data key="d0">Valor De GS</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Valor De GS refers to the blood glucose level measured before physical activity to assess risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Efecto De La Actividad">
  <data key="d0">Efecto De La Actividad</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Efecto De La Actividad refers to the prolonged impact of physical activity on glucose metabolism, lasting beyond the activity period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ajuste De La Terapia">
  <data key="d0">Ajuste De La Terapia</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ajuste De La Terapia involves modifying insulin delivery, such as bolus or basal rates, in response to alcohol intake or physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Efecto Reductor De La Glucosa En Sangre">
  <data key="d0">Efecto Reductor De La Glucosa En Sangre</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Efecto Reductor De La Glucosa En Sangre describes the prolonged lowering effect of alcohol on blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bebidas Alcoholicas Dulces">
  <data key="d0">Bebidas Alcoholicas Dulces</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bebidas Alcoholicas Dulces are alcoholic drinks with high sugar content, such as cocktails and liqueurs, which are discouraged due to their impact on glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Niveles De Glucosa Bajos A Primeras Horas De La Manana">
  <data key="d0">Niveles De Glucosa Bajos A Primeras Horas De La Manana</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Niveles De Glucosa Bajos A Primeras Horas De La Manana refer to low blood glucose levels occurring in the early morning after nighttime alcohol consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglucemia Inadvertida">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglucemia Inadvertida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglucemia Inadvertida occurs when hypoglycemia is masked by the effects of alcohol, making it difficult to recognize symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspension De Infusion De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Suspension De Infusion De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspension De Infusion De Insulina is a strategy to temporarily stop insulin delivery to prevent hypoglycemia, either manually or automatically.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Limite Bajo De Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Limite Bajo De Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Limite Bajo De Glucosa is the predefined threshold for blood glucose at which automatic insulin suspension is triggered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tendencia Descendente De Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Tendencia Descendente De Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tendencia Descendente De Glucosa indicates a continuous drop in blood glucose levels, increasing the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CAPITULO 4">
  <data key="d0">CAPITULO 4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">CAPITULO 4 is a section in the guide focused on daily routine management for insulin pump users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7fe03750967000c5e6da4698616f3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contour Next Link 2.4">
  <data key="d0">Contour Next Link 2.4</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Contour Next Link 2.4 is a blood glucose meter designed to work with the MiniMed™ 640G system, providing calibration values.&lt;SEP&gt;The Contour Next Link 2.4 is a glucose meter used in conjunction with the MiniMed 670G insulin pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4aefb790519642667af4aaebc974bcb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704182</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initial Calibration">
  <data key="d0">Initial Calibration</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Initial Calibration refers to the required calibration steps after inserting a new sensor: first within 2 hours, then again within the following 6 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daily Calibration">
  <data key="d0">Daily Calibration</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Daily Calibration involves entering a blood glucose reading into the system at least once every 12 hours to maintain sensor accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Sensor Calibration">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Sensor Calibration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Sensor Calibration is the process of aligning sensor glucose readings with blood glucose measurements to ensure accuracy in the MiniMed™ 640G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid Glucose Change">
  <data key="d0">Rapid Glucose Change</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid Glucose Change refers to periods when blood glucose levels are rising or falling quickly, during which calibration should be avoided for accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibration Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Calibration Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Calibration Reminder is a system-generated alert from the MiniMed™ 640G prompting the user to perform calibration, though it may occur at inopportune times.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terapia De Bomba Con Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Terapia De Bomba Con Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Terapia De Bomba Con Sensor (SAP) is an insulin delivery method that uses a pump combined with a sensor to manage diabetes, though it does not replace capillary glucose measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Terapia de bomba con sensor es un método de administración de insulina que utiliza tecnología avanzada para monitorear y entregar insulina de forma continua.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibración">
  <data key="d0">Calibración</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">La calibración es el proceso de introducir valores de glucosa en sangre en el sistema MiniMed™ 640G para asegurar la precisión del sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nivel De Glucosa Estable">
  <data key="d0">Nivel De Glucosa Estable</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Un nivel de glucosa estable se refiere a una condición en la que los niveles de glucosa no están en rápido ascenso o descenso, ideal para la calibración.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flechas De Tendencia">
  <data key="d0">Flechas De Tendencia</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Las flechas de tendencia son indicadores visuales en la pantalla del sistema MiniMed™ 640G que muestran la dirección y velocidad del cambio en los niveles de glucosa.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transmisor Guardian™ 2 Link">
  <data key="d0">Transmisor Guardian™ 2 Link</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El Transmisor Guardian™ 2 Link es un dispositivo que se conecta al sensor de glucosa y transmite datos al sistema MiniMed™ 640G.&lt;SEP&gt;The Transmisor Guardian™ 2 Link sends glucose data from the sensor to the insulin pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guía De Usuario De MiniMed™ 640G">
  <data key="d0">Guía De Usuario De MiniMed™ 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">La Guía de Usuario de MiniMed™ 640G es un documento que proporciona instrucciones detalladas sobre el uso y mantenimiento del sistema.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guía De Inicio Rápido">
  <data key="d0">Guía De Inicio Rápido</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">La Guía de Inicio Rápido es un manual que contiene instrucciones básicas para la inserción del sensor y el uso inicial del sistema.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Irritación Del Sitio">
  <data key="d0">Irritación Del Sitio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">La irritación del sitio se refiere a la inflamación o reacción cutánea en el lugar de inserción del sensor o transmisor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adhesivos">
  <data key="d0">Adhesivos</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Los adhesivos son materiales utilizados para mantener el sensor y el transmisor fijos en la piel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Valores De Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Valores De Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Los valores de glucosa son mediciones numéricas del nivel de glucosa en sangre o en el líquido intersticial, mostradas por el sistema.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Profundidad De 3.6 Metros">
  <data key="d0">Profundidad De 3.6 Metros</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">La profundidad de 3.6 metros es el límite de sumersión especificado para el sistema MiniMed™ 640G bajo condiciones normales.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Duración De 24 Horas">
  <data key="d0">Duración De 24 Horas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">La duración de 24 horas es el tiempo máximo durante el cual el sistema MiniMed™ 640G puede permanecer sumergido sin dañarse.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distancia De 1.2 Metros">
  <data key="d0">Distancia De 1.2 Metros</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">La distancia de 1.2 metros es el rango dentro del cual el sistema MiniMed™ 640G debe estar del Transmisor Guardian™ 2 Link para recibir datos de glucosa.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Almacenamiento De 10 Horas">
  <data key="d0">Almacenamiento De 10 Horas</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">El almacenamiento de 10 horas es la capacidad del Transmisor Guardian™ 2 Link para retener datos de glucosa cuando no está en contacto con la bomba.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CAPITULO 4 | SAP EN LA RUTINA DIARIA">
  <data key="d0">CAPITULO 4 | SAP EN LA RUTINA DIARIA</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">CAPITULO 4 | SAP EN LA RUTINA DIARIA es una sección de un manual que aborda el uso del sistema SAP en actividades diarias.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SECCION 2: SAP EN SITUACIONES COTIDIANAS">
  <data key="d0">SECCION 2: SAP EN SITUACIONES COTIDIANAS</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">SECCION 2: SAP EN SITUACIONES COTIDIANAS es una parte del material educativo que describe cómo manejar el sistema SAP en escenarios comunes como duchas, baños y natación.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7c10f0a011d51190fa761b5c0aff4ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bano, Ducha Y Natacion">
  <data key="d0">Bano, Ducha Y Natacion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
