  <data key="d2">Fax refers to the fax numbers provided for Medtronic Ibérica S.A. in Madrid and Medtronic International Trading Sarl. in Tolochenaz.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8af713fd3913ed050d96cdd321bca3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lifestyle Flexibility">
  <data key="d0">Lifestyle Flexibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lifestyle flexibility involves adapting diabetes management to accommodate personal routines, including dietary habits and exercise.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exercise and Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Exercise and Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exercise and glucose refers to the impact of physical activity on blood sugar levels, requiring careful monitoring to prevent extreme fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Worry About Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Worry About Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Worry about diabetes refers to the psychological burden and stress associated with managing the condition on a daily basis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAP Therapy">
  <data key="d0">SAP Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SAP Therapy (Sensor-Augmented Pump Therapy) combines insulin pump functionality with continuous glucose monitoring for enhanced diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose-Insulin Balance">
  <data key="d0">Glucose-Insulin Balance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose-insulin balance refers to the equilibrium between blood glucose levels and insulin delivery, essential for effective diabetes control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daily Routine with SAP">
  <data key="d0">Daily Routine with SAP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Daily routine with SAP refers to integrating sensor-augmented pump therapy into everyday life, including meals, activities, and sleep patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basic Programming">
  <data key="d0">Basic Programming</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basic programming involves setting up initial parameters on an insulin pump, such as basal rates and insulin-to-carbohydrate ratios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Menu Map">
  <data key="d0">Menu Map</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Menu map refers to the navigational structure of an insulin pump’s user interface, guiding users through settings and functions.&lt;SEP&gt;The menu map provides a navigational overview of the MiniMed 780G system interface for accessing features and settings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Menu Map is a visual guide showing the navigation structure of the pump’s interface.&lt;SEP&gt;The Menu map on page 339 provides a visual diagram of the pump's menu structure for navigation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Menu Map is a visual guide showing the available screens and features accessible from the Menu screen of the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Troubleshooting">
  <data key="d0">Troubleshooting</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Troubleshooting involves identifying and resolving common issues that may arise during insulin pump use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Training Notebooks">
  <data key="d0">Training Notebooks</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Training notebooks are educational materials provided to users to support learning and retention during insulin pump training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initial Training Form">
  <data key="d0">Initial Training Form</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The initial training form contains physician-prescribed pump settings such as basal rate, insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio, sensitivity factor, active insulin time, and target range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Online Training">
  <data key="d0">Online Training</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Online training provides digital educational resources for learning about insulin pump therapy at the user’s own pace.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Classroom Training">
  <data key="d0">Classroom Training</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Classroom training refers to in-person or group instructional sessions for learning insulin pump use and diabetes management strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702563</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Product User Guide">
  <data key="d0">Product User Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The product user guide is a manual providing detailed instructions for operating and maintaining the MiniMed™ insulin pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702563</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Log">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Log</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The glucose log is a record of blood glucose readings, including at least one week of data, used to assess diabetes control and adjust therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702563</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus De Comida">
  <data key="d0">Bolus De Comida</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus De Comida is the insulin dose administered to cover carbohydrates consumed during a meal or snack, calculated using the insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus De Comida is an insulin dose given in response to carbohydrate consumption during a meal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd60281301900b9df0acbe6be09fa2f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed9acad938fa761961897e399e22d5c3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calculo Del Bolus De Comida">
  <data key="d0">Calculo Del Bolus De Comida</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Calculo Del Bolus De Comida is the process of determining the required insulin dose by multiplying the number of carbohydrate servings by the insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd60281301900b9df0acbe6be09fa2f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unidades De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Unidades De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Unidades De Insulina represent the quantity of insulin needed to cover a given amount of carbohydrates, derived from the bolus calculation formula.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd60281301900b9df0acbe6be09fa2f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raciones De Hidratos De Carbono">
  <data key="d0">Raciones De Hidratos De Carbono</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Raciones De Hidratos De Carbono refer to standardized portions of carbohydrates consumed in a meal or snack, used as input in bolus insulin calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd60281301900b9df0acbe6be09fa2f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bomba MiniMed">
  <data key="d0">Bomba MiniMed</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bomba MiniMed is an insulin pump device that delivers precise insulin doses, including bolus amounts less than one unit, and supports advanced features like Bolus Wizard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd60281301900b9df0acbe6be09fa2f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Funcion Bolus Wizard">
  <data key="d0">Funcion Bolus Wizard</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Funcion Bolus Wizard is a feature of the MiniMed insulin pump that automatically calculates the precise insulin dose based on the user's insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd60281301900b9df0acbe6be09fa2f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dora">
  <data key="d0">Dora</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dora is a person who consumes 2.5 carbohydrate servings and uses an insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio of 0.5 to calculate her mealtime insulin dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd60281301900b9df0acbe6be09fa2f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerta Baja">
  <data key="d0">Alerta Baja</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerta Baja es una notificación emitida por el sistema MiniMed™ 640G cuando los niveles de glucosa alcanzan o se acercan al límite bajo establecido.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702566</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Límite Bajo">
  <data key="d0">Límite Bajo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Límite Bajo es el umbral de glucosa en sangre configurado en el sistema MiniMed™ 640G, por debajo del cual se considera hipoglucemia y se activan alertas o funciones de seguridad.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702566</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sistema MiniMed™ 640G">
  <data key="d0">Sistema MiniMed™ 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El Sistema MiniMed™ 640G es un dispositivo de terapia con bomba de insulina que incluye funciones como SmartGuard™ para el manejo automatizado de la glucosa.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702566</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regla 15-15">
  <data key="d0">Regla 15-15</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">La regla 15-15 es una recomendación para tratar la hipoglucemia: consumir 15 gramos de hidratos de carbono y esperar 15 minutos antes de reevaluar los niveles de glucosa.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702566</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recordar Baja En">
  <data key="d0">Recordar Baja En</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recordar Baja En es una configuración que determina la frecuencia con la que se repite la Alerta Baja hasta que los niveles de glucosa superen el umbral bajo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702566</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ratio I/R">
  <data key="d0">Ratio I/R</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">El Ratio I/R (Insulina/Carbohidratos) es la relación que indica cuántas unidades de insulina se necesitan para cubrir una cantidad determinada de hidratos de carbono.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Actividad Física">
  <data key="d0">Actividad Física</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">La actividad física puede afectar los niveles de glucosa en sangre, aumentando el riesgo de hipoglucemia, especialmente durante o después del ejercicio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusión De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Infusión De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">La infusión de insulina es la administración continua de insulina a través de la bomba, que puede ser suspendida automáticamente por funciones como SmartGuard™.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dennis">
  <data key="d0">Dennis</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dennis is a person managing his glucose levels while socializing with friends at a bar on a Saturday night.&lt;SEP&gt;Dennis es un usuario del sistema MiniMed™ 640G que realiza actividad física y consume alcohol, lo que requiere ajustes en su terapia con insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guía De Usuario Del Sistema MiniMed™ 640G">
  <data key="d0">Guía De Usuario Del Sistema MiniMed™ 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guía de Usuario del Sistema MiniMed™ 640G is a user manual providing instructions and information on the proper use of the insulin pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preguntas De Repaso">
  <data key="d0">Preguntas De Repaso</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Preguntas De Repaso are review questions included in the user guide to reinforce understanding of the insulin pump therapy and device functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capítulo 4">
  <data key="d0">Capítulo 4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Capítulo 4 is a section in the user guide titled "SAP EN LA RUTINA DIARIA" that covers the daily use of the MiniMed™ 640G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1161d90ae3c3dfe3fc54cc15351e9452</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Páncreas">
  <data key="d0">Páncreas</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">El páncreas es un órgano que produce insulina de forma natural en el cuerpo humano.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitorización Continua De Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Monitorización Continua De Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">La monitorización continua de glucosa es una técnica que permite medir los niveles de glucosa en tiempo real.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoglobina A1c">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobina A1c</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">La hemoglobina A1c es un indicador de control glucémico a largo plazo en personas con diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calculo De Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Calculo De Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">El cálculo de bolus es un proceso para determinar la cantidad de insulina necesaria para cubrir carbohidratos o corregir niveles altos de glucosa.</data>
