  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Monitoring Device">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Monitoring Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The glucose monitoring device is used to check sensor glucose values and display trend arrows for real-time glycemic management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid Glucose Increase">
  <data key="d0">Rapid Glucose Increase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid glucose increase refers to a sudden rise in blood glucose levels, which can impact diabetes management and is detectable via continuous glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capillary Glucose Test">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Glucose Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Capillary glucose test is a method of measuring blood glucose levels using a small blood sample from the fingertip, used to confirm sensor readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Spike">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Spike</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A glucose spike refers to a sudden and sharp increase in blood glucose levels, which can occur due to various factors and is detectable through continuous monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interstitial Fluid Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Interstitial Fluid Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Interstitial fluid glucose is the glucose present in the fluid between cells, measured by glucose sensors as a proxy for blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Insulin Level">
  <data key="d0">High Insulin Level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A high insulin level occurs when excess insulin is present in the body, leading to increased glucose uptake by cells and potential hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alcoholic Beverages">
  <data key="d0">Alcoholic Beverages</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcoholic beverages can increase the risk of hypoglycemia, especially when consumed without carbohydrate-containing foods, particularly in individuals using insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High-Fat Foods">
  <data key="d0">High-Fat Foods</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">High-fat foods delay gastric emptying and glucose absorption, requiring extended insulin coverage and careful monitoring to avoid late-onset hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daily Summary">
  <data key="d0">Daily Summary</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Daily Summary is a report providing an overview of glucose readings, insulin delivery, and events such as hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia for a given day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daily Overlap Report">
  <data key="d0">Daily Overlap Report</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Daily Overlap Report is a visualization tool that superimposes glucose sensor data across multiple days to identify recurring patterns in glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus/Basal Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Bolus/Basal Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus/Basal Ratio is a metric comparing the amount of mealtime (bolus) insulin to background (basal) insulin delivered by an insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capillary Glucose Measurement">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Glucose Measurement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Capillary Glucose Measurement is a method of checking blood sugar levels using a fingerstick and glucometer, often compared with sensor data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AUC &gt;180 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">AUC &gt;180 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">AUC &gt;180 mg/dL represents the area under the curve where glucose levels exceed 180 mg/dL, indicating duration and severity of hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AUC &lt;70 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">AUC &lt;70 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">AUC &lt;70 mg/dL represents the area under the curve where glucose levels fall below 70 mg/dL, indicating duration and severity of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
