  <data key="d0">MM670G System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MM670G System is a medical device used for insulin delivery and glucose monitoring, requiring specific reports for configuration and performance evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapy Follow-Up">
  <data key="d0">Therapy Follow-Up</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Therapy Follow-Up involves tracking glucose levels, food intake, and insulin consumption to assess and adjust diabetes management over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702604</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Frequency">
  <data key="d0">Event Frequency</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Event Frequency refers to the number of occurrences of specific glucose events, such as hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia, within a given time period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Distribution measures the spread between the highest and lowest glucose values recorded, indicating variability in blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sistema Integrado Minimed™">
  <data key="d0">Sistema Integrado Minimed™</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sistema Integrado Minimed™ is a medical device system used for insulin pump therapy with sensor integration, requiring parameter personalization such as basal rate, insulin-to-carb ratio, and sensitivity factor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Factor De Sensibilidad">
  <data key="d0">Factor De Sensibilidad</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Factor De Sensibilidad indicates how much one unit of insulin lowers blood glucose and is used to adjust insulin dosing within the MiniMed™ system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rangos Objetivo">
  <data key="d0">Rangos Objetivo</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Rangos Objetivo are target glucose level ranges set in the MiniMed™ system to guide therapy effectiveness and parameter adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tiempo De Insulina Activa">
  <data key="d0">Tiempo De Insulina Activa</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Tiempo De Insulina Activa is a parameter in the MiniMed™ system that defines how long insulin remains effective in the body, influencing dosing decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autocontroles De Glucemia Capilar">
  <data key="d0">Autocontroles De Glucemia Capilar</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autocontroles De Glucemia Capilar are routine fingerstick glucose tests performed multiple times daily to inform therapy adjustments, even during sensor-augmented pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horario De Autocontrol De La Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Horario De Autocontrol De La Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Horario De Autocontrol De La Glucosa is a structured schedule for checking blood glucose levels at specific times, such as before and after meals, at bedtime, during sleep, and upon waking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc23f53afc0fcecdd9527e9dab84cb8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
