  <data key="d5">1778702619</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alternative Insulin Administration Method">
  <data key="d0">Alternative Insulin Administration Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An alternative method for insulin delivery may be required if the insulin pump is disconnected for an extended period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dc5c57277d034fb00908385613bf5a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702619</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intimacy">
  <data key="d0">Intimacy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">During intimacy, the insulin pump can be disconnected for up to two hours, but must be reconnected afterward to maintain therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dc5c57277d034fb00908385613bf5a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sports and Physical Activity">
  <data key="d0">Sports and Physical Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">During sports, glucose values and alerts are useful, and users must consider placement of the sensor/transmitter and pump, with a maximum operational distance of 1.2 meters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dc5c57277d034fb00908385613bf5a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flying">
  <data key="d0">Flying</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">During flights, users must activate Airplane Mode on the MiniMed™ 640G due to restrictions on wireless communication, with specific steps to reconnect after landing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dc5c57277d034fb00908385613bf5a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed™ System">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed™ System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed™ system is a medical device used for insulin therapy management, including an insulin pump and related components.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed™ system is an insulin pump therapy device requiring parameter adjustments for effective glucose management.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed™ system is an insulin pump therapy device that includes the Bolus Wizard™ function and tracks active insulin for bolus calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-425759c12d133ef4832928e8f5d50896</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Levels">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose levels refer to the concentration of glucose in the bloodstream, normally maintained between 70 mg/dL and 120 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Levels refer to the concentration of glucose in the blood, typically measured in mg/dL, with a normal range of 70–120 mg/dL in non-diabetic individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose levels are measurements used to assess metabolic control and determine necessary insulin dosage adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose levels are measurable concentrations of glucose in the blood, typically measured in mg/dL, used to monitor and manage diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Correction Factor">
  <data key="d0">Correction Factor</data>
  <data key="d1">parameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The correction factor, or insulin sensitivity factor, indicates how much one unit of insulin lowers blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Time">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Insulin Time is a parameter used in insulin pump systems, particularly within features such as the Bolus Wizard and SmartGuard, to define the duration for which bolus insulin remains active in the body in terms of lowering blood glucose levels. This setting plays a critical role in diabetes management by influencing the calculation of correction boluses and mealtime insulin doses. By estimating how long insulin continues to exert its glucose-lowering effect, Active Insulin Time helps prevent insulin stacking—a condition where overlapping doses of insulin lead to an increased risk of hypoglycemia.

The setting is typically configured during the initial setup of the insulin pump, such as through the Startup Wizard, and is used by the system to track residual insulin activity when determining subsequent insulin doses. Active Insulin Time is generally set between 2 to 3 hours in systems like the MiniMed 780G, although individual settings may vary based on personal metabolic response. It serves as a crucial input for the Bolus Wizard, ensuring that new insulin doses are adjusted according to any active insulin still in effect from prior boluses. Overall, Active Insulin Time enhances dosing accuracy and safety by incorporating pharmacokinetic considerations into automated insulin delivery algorithms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b0e9023a7c03c6a284d69e0930b8a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physician">
  <data key="d0">Physician</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A physician provides medical guidance on adjusting MiniMed™ system parameters and interpreting glucose data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Dose">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">dose</data>
  <data key="d2">A bolus dose is a manual or programmed insulin dose delivered to cover meals or correct high blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Testing Routine">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Testing Routine</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The glucose testing routine involves checking blood glucose levels at specific times such as upon waking, before meals, after meals, and during sleep.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="8 to 10 Times Daily Testing">
  <data key="d0">8 to 10 Times Daily Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">When starting insulin pump therapy, patients are required to check blood glucose levels 8 to 10 times daily to ensure accurate parameter adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="4 to 6 Times Daily Testing">
  <data key="d0">4 to 6 Times Daily Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Once pump parameters are well-adjusted and glucose levels are stable, patients may reduce glucose testing to 4 to 6 times daily as directed by medical team.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Step-By-Step Guide">
  <data key="d0">Step-By-Step Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Step-By-Step Guide is a manual that offers detailed, sequential instructions for setting up and using the MiniMed™ system before attending the therapy training class.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Online Training Completion Certificate">
  <data key="d0">Online Training Completion Certificate</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Online Training Completion Certificate is documentation verifying that the user has completed required online training for the MiniMed™ system, if necessary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniLink™ Transmitter">
  <data key="d0">MiniLink™ Transmitter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniLink™ Transmitter is a device that sends glucose data from the Enlite™ sensor to the MiniMed™ system for continuous monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702625</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enlite™ Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Enlite™ Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enlite™ Sensor is a glucose sensor used with the MiniMed™ system to measure glucose levels in real time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702625</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ketone Test Strips">
  <data key="d0">Ketone Test Strips</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketone Test Strips are reactive strips used to measure ketone levels in the blood, an important monitoring tool for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IV Prep™ Wipes">
  <data key="d0">IV Prep™ Wipes</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">IV Prep™ Wipes are alcohol-impregnated wipes used for cleaning the skin before inserting the infusion set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IV3000™ Transparent Dressing">
  <data key="d0">IV3000™ Transparent Dressing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">IV3000™ Transparent Dressing is a covering used to secure the infusion set in place, if included with the MiniMed™ pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapy Initiation Class">
  <data key="d0">Therapy Initiation Class</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Therapy Initiation Class is an educational session where users learn to operate the MiniMed™ system, requiring prior completion of manuals and bringing necessary supplies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Starting Therapy With MiniMed™ System">
  <data key="d0">Starting Therapy With MiniMed™ System</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Starting Therapy With MiniMed™ System refers to the process of beginning insulin pump treatment, including preparation, training, and device setup.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Human Body">
  <data key="d0">Human Body</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Human Body relies on glucose for energy and uses insulin to regulate glucose levels; in diabetes, this balance is disrupted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heart">
  <data key="d0">Heart</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Heart requires glucose for energy to maintain continuous beating and proper function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702627</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lungs">
  <data key="d0">Lungs</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Lungs require glucose for energy to support respiration and oxygen exchange.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702627</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brain">
  <data key="d0">Brain</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Brain depends on a constant supply of glucose to function, including thinking and regulating bodily processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702627</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Current Blood Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Current blood glucose is the measured level of glucose in the blood at a given time, required for calculating a correction bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-425759c12d133ef4832928e8f5d50896</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702627</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fats">
  <data key="d0">Fats</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fats, especially when consumed with proteins, delay digestion and glucose absorption, potentially requiring adjusted insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proteins">
  <data key="d0">Proteins</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proteins, like fats, can independently affect glucose levels and contribute to delayed glucose rise, particularly in high-fat, high-protein meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Standard Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A standard bolus delivers the full insulin dose immediately, which may not align with delayed glucose absorption from high-fat, high-protein meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Absorption">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Absorption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose absorption is delayed in meals high in fats and proteins, leading to a mismatch with standard bolus insulin timing and increasing hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Action">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Action</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin action refers to the timing and effect of insulin after subcutaneous administration, which may not align with carbohydrate absorption from certain meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycogen">
  <data key="d0">Glycogen</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycogen is the stored form of glucose in the liver and muscles, which is converted back to glucose during physical activity to provide energy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Free Fatty Acids">
  <data key="d0">Free Fatty Acids</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Free fatty acids become a primary energy source after 30 minutes of physical activity, contributing to the body's shift away from glucose utilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucosa Actual">
  <data key="d0">Glucosa Actual</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucosa Actual refers to the current blood glucose level measured in mg/dL, such as 220 mg/dL or 75 mg/dL, used in insulin dosage calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec2fea6c095d8e93483ff43ef875fb9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucosa Objetivo">
  <data key="d0">Glucosa Objetivo</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucosa Objetivo refers to the target blood glucose level, typically set at 100 mg/dL, used as a reference point in insulin correction calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec2fea6c095d8e93483ff43ef875fb9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unidades de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Unidades de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Unidades de Insulina refers to the calculated insulin dose in units, derived from formulas involving blood glucose levels and carbohydrate intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec2fea6c095d8e93483ff43ef875fb9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus de Correccion">
  <data key="d0">Bolus de Correccion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus de Correccion is the insulin correction dose calculated to adjust blood glucose levels toward the target, using the formula (Glucosa Actual - Glucosa Objetivo) / FSI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec2fea6c095d8e93483ff43ef875fb9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cantidad de Bolus Total">
  <data key="d0">Cantidad de Bolus Total</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Cantidad de Bolus Total is the total insulin bolus dose, calculated as the sum of the bolus for food and the correction bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec2fea6c095d8e93483ff43ef875fb9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ratio refers to the insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio, indicating how many grams of carbohydrates are covered by one unit of insulin, such as 1 or 1.5.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec2fea6c095d8e93483ff43ef875fb9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raciones">
  <data key="d0">Raciones</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Raciones represent the amount of carbohydrate servings consumed, used in calculating the meal bolus, such as 3, 8, or 8 raciones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec2fea6c095d8e93483ff43ef875fb9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Sensor Value">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Sensor Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Sensor Value (SG) refers to the glucose level readings obtained from the continuous glucose monitoring (MCG) system, used to track current glucose levels and trends.&lt;SEP&gt;The glucose sensor value (SG) is a real-time measurement of blood glucose levels provided by a continuous glucose monitoring system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Training">
  <data key="d0">User Training</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">User Training refers to the educational process where users learn how to configure and operate the MiniMed™ 640G system, including interpreting alerts and using therapy features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Optimization is the third step in SAP therapy, involving systematic review of pump and MCG data to fine-tune settings and maintain stable glucose levels over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Servicio De Asistencia Técnica De Medtronic">
  <data key="d0">Servicio De Asistencia Técnica De Medtronic</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Servicio de Asistencia Técnica de Medtronic provides technical support for Medtronic devices but cannot offer medical advice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sistema Minimed™ 640G">
  <data key="d0">Sistema Minimed™ 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sistema MiniMed™ 640G is an insulin pump system used for diabetes therapy, including sensor integration and insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702631</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Software Carelink™ Personal">
  <data key="d0">Software Carelink™ Personal</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Software CareLink™ Personal is used to manage and analyze data from the MiniMed™ 640G system, including report generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702631</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Índices Basales">
  <data key="d0">Índices Basales</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Índices basales are programmed insulin delivery rates that maintain glucose control between meals and overnight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702631</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ajuste De Alarmas">
  <data key="d0">Ajuste De Alarmas</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ajuste de alarmas refers to the process of modifying alert thresholds on the insulin pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702631</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Programación De La Bomba De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Programación De La Bomba De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Programación de la bomba de insulina involves setting insulin delivery parameters such as basal rates and bolus settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702631</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Descarga De Datos">
  <data key="d0">Descarga De Datos</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Descarga de datos refers to the process of transferring data from the MiniMed™ 640G system to the CareLink™ Personal software.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702631</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Creación De Informes">
  <data key="d0">Creación De Informes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Creación de informes involves generating therapy reports using the CareLink™ Personal software for clinical review.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702631</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Problemas De Conexión">
  <data key="d0">Problemas De Conexión</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Problemas de conexión refer to issues between the reservoir and infusion set, such as leaks or loose fittings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702631</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fugas">
  <data key="d0">Fugas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fugas refer to insulin leaks in the infusion system that can disrupt proper insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702632</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Burbujas En El Tubo">
  <data key="d0">Burbujas En El Tubo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Burbujas en el tubo are air bubbles in the infusion tubing that may block insulin flow and require purging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702632</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sangre En El Tubo">
  <data key="d0">Sangre En El Tubo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sangre en el tubo indicates backflow of blood into the infusion tubing, which may require system replacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702632</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enrojecimiento/Irritación De La Piel">
  <data key="d0">Enrojecimiento/Irritación De La Piel</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Enrojecimiento/irritación de la piel refers to skin reactions at the infusion site that may necessitate site change.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702632</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caducidad De La Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Caducidad De La Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Caducidad de la insulina refers to expired insulin that should no longer be used for therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702632</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
