<node id="Cuerpos Cetonico">
  <data key="d0">Cuerpos Cetonico</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Los cuerpos cetonicos son productos de desecho generados cuando el cuerpo quema grasa como fuente de energia, y su acumulacion indica riesgo de cetoacidosis diabetica.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17d4cfa9183f9c1eb5a0c2212479127a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Niveles Altos De Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Niveles Altos De Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Los niveles altos de glucosa en sangre son un signo de advertencia principal de la posible aparicion de cetoacidosis diabetica.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17d4cfa9183f9c1eb5a0c2212479127a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Signos De Advertencia De La Cad">
  <data key="d0">Signos De Advertencia De La Cad</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Los signos de advertencia de la cetoacidosis diabetica incluyen niveles altos de glucosa, presencia de cuerpos cetonicos, nauseas, vomitos, dolor abdominal, confusión, letargo y dificultad para respirar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17d4cfa9183f9c1eb5a0c2212479127a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin In Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Insulin In Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin in bolus refers to the increased production of insulin after eating to manage the rise in blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose In Blood">
  <data key="d0">Glucose In Blood</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose in blood is the primary energy source obtained from food and measured by glucose meters during blood glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f2cf8a591a83e4436ab6a76c2d30e2d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose In Interstitial Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Glucose In Interstitial Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose in interstitial fluid refers to the glucose level measured by sensors, reflecting delayed changes compared to blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f2cf8a591a83e4436ab6a76c2d30e2d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Guide For MiniMed™ 640G System">
  <data key="d0">User Guide For MiniMed™ 640G System</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The user guide for the MiniMed™ 640G System provides instructions on operating the insulin pump and interpreting glucose data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f2cf8a591a83e4436ab6a76c2d30e2d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Guide For CareLink™ Personal">
  <data key="d0">User Guide For CareLink™ Personal</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The user guide for CareLink™ Personal explains how to use the software to view glucose trends and patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f2cf8a591a83e4436ab6a76c2d30e2d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Self-Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Self-Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose self-monitoring involves fingerstick testing to confirm sensor glucose values and inform therapy decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapy Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Therapy Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Therapy adjustment refers to modifying insulin delivery settings based on glucose trends, sensor data, and medical consultation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="3-Hour Trend Curve">
  <data key="d0">3-Hour Trend Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The 3-hour trend curve displays the speed and magnitude of glucose level changes after a meal, helping to assess bolus effectiveness and insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="6-Hour Trend Curve">
  <data key="d0">6-Hour Trend Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The 6-hour trend curve shows glucose fluctuations between meals and during physical activity, aiding in the evaluation of basal insulin and activity-related adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="12-Hour Trend Curve">
  <data key="d0">12-Hour Trend Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The 12-hour trend curve provides an extended view of glucose trends, highlighting deviations from target range and insulin administration patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="24-Hour Trend Curve">
  <data key="d0">24-Hour Trend Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The 24-hour trend curve offers a full-day overview of glucose levels, supporting long-term therapy optimization and pattern recognition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Timing">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Timing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus timing refers to the interval between insulin delivery and food intake, which must be properly selected to match meal absorption and prevent glucose spikes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspension Before Low Limit">
  <data key="d0">Suspension Before Low Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspension Before Low Limit is a feature that automatically stops insulin infusion when sensor glucose levels approach a predefined low threshold to prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Before Low Limit">
  <data key="d0">Alert Before Low Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert Before Low Limit is a function that notifies the user when insulin infusion is interrupted due to approaching low glucose levels, triggering periodic alerts until acknowledged.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid-Absorption Carbohydrates">
  <data key="d0">Rapid-Absorption Carbohydrates</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid-absorption carbohydrates are fast-acting sugars, such as glucose tablets, consumed to prevent or treat low blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Training Team">
  <data key="d0">Medical Training Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The medical training team is a group of healthcare professionals who provide guidance and education to the user on insulin pump therapy and diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equilibrio Glucosa Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Equilibrio Glucosa Insulina</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfd7b4fa0ccd15d540a9299e77dbf1dd</data>
  <data key="d2">El páncreas mantiene el equilibrio entre glucosa e insulina mediante la liberación alternante de insulina y glucagón.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702645</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cells">
  <data key="d0">Cells</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626</data>
  <data key="d2">Cells absorb glucose from the interstitial fluid to produce energy.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778702661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enfermedad O Infección">
  <data key="d0">Enfermedad O Infección</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9</data>
  <data key="d2">Durante una enfermedad o infección, se puede usar un índice basal temporal para cubrir el aumento en las necesidades de insulina basal.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
