  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Status">
  <data key="d0">Pump Status</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump status includes information such as reservoir level, start time, remaining time, and serial number.&lt;SEP&gt;Pump status refers to the operational and functional state of the insulin pump, including reservoir level, sensor calibration, and transmitter battery status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704114</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Status">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Status</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor status includes details such as the last calibration and the next pending calibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704114</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuration Review">
  <data key="d0">Configuration Review</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Configuration review allows users to check and manage the current pump settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Configuration Review displays the current programmed settings on the insulin pump for user verification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704114</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="History">
  <data key="d0">History</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">History includes records such as daily summaries, alarm logs, and sensor data.&lt;SEP&gt;History is a menu option on the insulin pump that provides access to various historical data screens including Daily History, Alarm History, and Paired Sensors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Remote Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Remote Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Remote bolus is a feature that allows insulin delivery to be initiated from a remote device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704115</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time And Date">
  <data key="d0">Time And Date</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time and date refers to the current clock settings on the insulin pump, which can be configured by the user.&lt;SEP&gt;Time And Date is a setting used to synchronize the pump’s internal clock.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alarms And Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Alarms And Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Alarms and alerts are notifications for conditions such as low reservoir, missed bolus, or glucose level thresholds.&lt;SEP&gt;Alarms and alerts are notifications generated by the MiniMed 780G system to inform the user of events such as low or high glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Target Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Target Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Target glucose is a user-set goal for optimal blood glucose level, used by the pump to adjust insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704117</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal/Bolus Maximum">
  <data key="d0">Basal/Bolus Maximum</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal/bolus maximum is a safety limit that sets the upper threshold for basal and bolus insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704118</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Increment">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Increment</data>
  <data key="d1">setting</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus increment is a configurable step size for adjusting bolus doses, allowing precise insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Increment defines the smallest adjustable unit for bolus dosing, allowing precise insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus increment determines the number of insulin units increased or decreased per button press during bolus delivery, with options of 0.1, 0.05, or 0.025 units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707345</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Speed">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Speed</data>
  <data key="d1">setting</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus speed is a setting that controls the rate at which insulin is delivered during a bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Speed controls the rate at which insulin is delivered during a bolus, affecting absorption dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus speed sets the rate at which the pump delivers bolus insulin, with standard (1.5 units per minute) or quick (15 units per minute) options.&lt;SEP&gt;The delivery speed for bolus insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707344</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Screen Brightness">
  <data key="d0">Screen Brightness</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Screen brightness is a display setting that adjusts the visibility of the pump screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704120</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Management">
  <data key="d0">Device Management</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Device management allows the user to connect and manage external devices paired with the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704121</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meter">
  <data key="d0">Meter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The meter is a medical device used to measure blood glucose levels and connect with the MiniMed™ pump.&lt;SEP&gt;A glucose meter is used alongside the insulin pump system to measure blood glucose levels and requires proper handling per its user guide.&lt;SEP&gt;The meter is a device used to measure blood glucose levels from a fingertip sample.&lt;SEP&gt;A term for any blood glucose meter used to measure blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Connection">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Connection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic Connection is a feature that allows the meter and pump to pair wirelessly when selected on both devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Connection">
  <data key="d0">Manual Connection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual Connection is an alternative method to link the meter and pump, requiring user intervention to initiate pairing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Pairing">
  <data key="d0">Device Pairing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Device Pairing refers to the process of connecting the meter and pump so they can communicate and share data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AutoLog">
  <data key="d0">AutoLog</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">AutoLog is a function that allows users to label blood glucose readings as Before Meal, After Meal, or Fasting for tracking purposes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Language Selection">
  <data key="d0">Language Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Language Selection allows the user to choose their preferred language, such as Español, during the initial setup.&lt;SEP&gt;Language Selection is a setup step where the user chooses their preferred language on the meter interface.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serial Number Verification">
  <data key="d0">Serial Number Verification</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Serial Number Verification ensures the correct pump and meter are paired by confirming matching serial numbers on both devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704123</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bomba Minimed">
  <data key="d0">Bomba Minimed</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bomba MiniMed is an insulin pump device used in diabetes management and can connect with a glucose meter for automated data transfer.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f61911be532419242af177a0b5feeb72</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
