</node>
<node id="Autolog">
  <data key="d0">Autolog</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autolog is a feature that automatically logs glucose readings or device events, though it can be deactivated by the user.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f61911be532419242af177a0b5feeb72</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704124</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Objetivo Rango Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Objetivo Rango Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Objetivo Rango Glucosa refers to the target blood glucose range, such as 70-130 mg/dL, set for diabetes management.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f61911be532419242af177a0b5feeb72</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704125</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian">
  <data key="d0">Guardian</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Guardian is a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) system produced by Medtronic MiniMed for real-time glucose tracking.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Guardian is the manufacturer or brand associated with the CGM transmitter used in conjunction with the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f61911be532419242af177a0b5feeb72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Pump">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion pump is a medical device used to deliver insulin continuously, allowing for programmable basal rates and temporary adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8190aff898356450e3514b751c9193c1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Additional Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Additional Basal Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An additional basal pattern is a configurable insulin delivery schedule that can be created or copied for days requiring different basal insulin needs, such as weekends or periods of varying activity.&lt;SEP&gt;An extra basal insulin delivery schedule that can be added beyond the default pattern, such as Workday, Day Off, or Sick Day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8190aff898356450e3514b751c9193c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Copy Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Copy Basal Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The copy basal pattern function allows users to duplicate an existing basal pattern and modify it to suit new requirements, simplifying the creation of additional basal schedules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8190aff898356450e3514b751c9193c1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guia De Inicio">
  <data key="d0">Guia De Inicio</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Guia De Inicio is a user manual section that provides instructions for setting up and navigating the device's main menu and functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9a22fae9e4c986d3a8e2a8dcdad44fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Utilidades">
  <data key="d0">Utilidades</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Utilidades is a menu option within the device interface that contains various settings, including screen options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9a22fae9e4c986d3a8e2a8dcdad44fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entrada De Gs">
  <data key="d0">Entrada De Gs</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Entrada De Gs refers to the input of blood glucose values into the device for monitoring and insulin delivery adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9a22fae9e4c986d3a8e2a8dcdad44fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704130</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Objetivo Temp">
  <data key="d0">Objetivo Temp</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Objetivo Temp is a temporary target setting used to adjust insulin delivery for short-term glucose management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9a22fae9e4c986d3a8e2a8dcdad44fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704130</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quick-Set®">
  <data key="d0">Quick-Set®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Quick-Set® is an infusion set with a cannula that can remain in place during MRI procedures, unlike needle-based systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Quick-Set® is a type of infusion set with a cannula that can remain inserted during medical procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704130</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silhouette®">
  <data key="d0">Silhouette®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Silhouette® is a cannula-based infusion set designed for use with insulin pumps and approved for remaining in place during MRI scans.&lt;SEP&gt;Silhouette® is a type of infusion set with a cannula that can remain inserted during medical procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704130</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mio®">
  <data key="d0">Mio®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Mio® is an infusion set that uses a cannula for insulin delivery and can be left in place during MRI or other medical imaging procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Mio® is a type of infusion set with a cannula that can remain inserted during medical procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704131</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sure-T®">
  <data key="d0">Sure-T®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sure-T® is a needle-based infusion set that must be removed before undergoing MRI or other procedures involving strong magnetic fields or radiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Sure-T® is an insulin infusion device that uses a needle instead of a cannula and must be removed before medical procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704131</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magnetic Resonance Equipment">
  <data key="d0">Magnetic Resonance Equipment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnetic resonance equipment generates intense magnetic fields and can interfere with the function of medical devices like sensors and transmitters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704132</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="24-Hour Support Line">
  <data key="d0">24-Hour Support Line</data>
  <data key="d1">service</data>
  <data key="d2">The 24-hour support line is a helpline for users of the MiniMed 670G to report issues or seek assistance at any time.&lt;SEP&gt;The 24-hour support line is a service provided by Medtronic Diabetes for users needing assistance, especially after exposure of the pump to magnetic fields.&lt;SEP&gt;The 24-hour support line provides assistance for users who experience issues with their medical devices, such as accidental exposure to magnetic fields.&lt;SEP&gt;The 24-hour support line is a technical assistance service provided by Medtronic Diabetes for troubleshooting insulin pump issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f5ebaa0341f051ad33cfb9895a3851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a8417d6099b09e6129d10f9827b5a35</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704132</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="X-Ray Machine">
  <data key="d0">X-Ray Machine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">X-ray machines at airports can damage insulin pumps or cause malfunctions due to radiation exposure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704132</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Travel Card">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Travel Card</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An emergency travel card contains important medical information for airport security and should be carried when traveling with an insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704132</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transportation Security Administration">
  <data key="d0">Transportation Security Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Transportation Security Administration (TSA) regulates airport security procedures in the United States and provides guidelines for traveling with medical devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704132</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nutrition Bars">
  <data key="d0">Nutrition Bars</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Nutrition bars are portable food items recommended for travel to manage blood sugar during flight delays or cancellations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704133</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Bolus Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Bolus Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Bolus Therapy involves administering precise doses of insulin to manage blood glucose levels, often supported by tools like the Bolus Wizard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc77598dbeb5980c719d1d54a6c3ab77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704135</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Practice Settings">
  <data key="d0">Practice Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Practice Settings are example values provided for learning how to configure the Bolus Wizard, not intended for actual therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc77598dbeb5980c719d1d54a6c3ab77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ratio Hc Actual">
  <data key="d0">Ratio Hc Actual</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ratio Hc Actual refers to the current carbohydrate-to-insulin ratio set at 15 g/U.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2b56844dd3520b94bbf5737a044bec7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensibilidad Actual">
  <data key="d0">Sensibilidad Actual</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensibilidad Actual refers to the current insulin sensitivity set at 50 mg/dL per U.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2b56844dd3520b94bbf5737a044bec7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Objetivo Gs Actual">
  <data key="d0">Objetivo Gs Actual</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Objetivo Gs Actual refers to the current blood glucose target level, though the specific value is not provided.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2b56844dd3520b94bbf5737a044bec7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohidratos">
  <data key="d0">Carbohidratos</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohidratos represent the amount of carbohydrates to be consumed, which is input into the Bolus Wizard for insulin dose calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohidratos represent the amount of carbohydrates in grams consumed, used in bolus calculation for insulin dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohidratos refer to carbohydrates consumed, measured in grams, and used in insulin dosage calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohidratos are nutrients that affect blood glucose levels and are used in insulin dosage calculations via the Bolus Wizard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed9acad938fa761961897e399e22d5c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b83b1b837df0b960758dfd02d42d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d74e338f7a37de66d4b2268a49021c4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e15921d1b7d6415709a3d0c795cefc3c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Corrector">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Corrector</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Corrector is an insulin dose administered to correct high blood glucose levels without food intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed9acad938fa761961897e399e22d5c3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuracion Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Configuracion Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Configuracion Insulina involves setting parameters such as carbohydrate ratio, insulin sensitivity, and target glucose for the Bolus Wizard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed9acad938fa761961897e399e22d5c3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Wizard®">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Wizard®</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Wizard® is a trademarked feature used to calculate insulin dosage based on glucose levels and carbohydrate intake, with warnings about its use after manual insulin injections.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Wizard® is a function that calculates insulin dosage based on carbohydrate intake, blood glucose levels, insulin sensitivity, and active insulin, featuring a registered trademark symbol.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Wizard® is a trademarked feature used to calculate insulin dosage based on glucose levels, carbohydrate intake, and active insulin adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed9acad938fa761961897e399e22d5c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b83b1b837df0b960758dfd02d42d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0deeba398b22b91d8da1b31653eede4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704139</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Danielle">
  <data key="d0">Danielle</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Danielle is a person who uses an insulin pump and chooses to disconnect it during swimming, suspending insulin infusion manually.&lt;SEP&gt;Danielle is a person who disconnects her insulin pump when swimming and manually suspends insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be6366eda06d68d222b47729f7ca841b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88cdb970e2c2f1aaaab96fdc11b589f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704140</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuracion De Patrones Basales">
  <data key="d0">Configuracion De Patrones Basales</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Configuracion de Patrones Basales refers to the process of setting up or modifying basal insulin infusion patterns on the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be6366eda06d68d222b47729f7ca841b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704140</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Segmento De Tiempo">
  <data key="d0">Segmento De Tiempo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Segmento de Tiempo is a defined period in the basal insulin schedule, such as 12:00A to 8:00A, with a specified insulin rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be6366eda06d68d222b47729f7ca841b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704140</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gulia De INICIO">
  <data key="d0">Gulia De INICIO</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Gulia de INICIO is a guide or manual providing instructions for setting up basal insulin patterns on an insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be6366eda06d68d222b47729f7ca841b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704140</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoreo Continuo de Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Monitoreo Continuo de Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitoreo Continuo de Glucosa is a glucose monitoring system that provides real-time glucose readings but should not be solely relied upon for treatment decisions during hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac418ceabab52352571a8024e5602ec4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704142</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alarmas">
  <data key="d0">Alarmas</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alarmas are alerts generated by the insulin pump to notify the user of events such as the Auto-shutdown activation or system warnings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac418ceabab52352571a8024e5602ec4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704142</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guia de Consulta Rapida">
  <data key="d0">Guia de Consulta Rapida</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Guia de Consulta Rapida refers to a series of quick reference guides provided for safety rules, basal rates, bolus calculations, and infusion set changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac418ceabab52352571a8024e5602ec4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
