<node id="Pattern Editing">
  <data key="d0">Pattern Editing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pattern editing is the process of modifying insulin delivery rates and timing within a basal pattern after it has been copied or selected.&lt;SEP&gt;Pattern editing is the process of modifying a basal insulin delivery pattern through a series of user interface steps on an insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7534f3bc09ac6e2eece38e12eb89cf1f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predefined Bolus Configuration">
  <data key="d0">Predefined Bolus Configuration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Predefined bolus configuration allows users to set and save specific bolus types, such as dual or square wave boluses, for consistent use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Page 87">
  <data key="d0">Page 87</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 87 refers to a specific page in a user manual or guide containing instructions for configuring basal insulin patterns on a medical device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Page 88">
  <data key="d0">Page 88</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 88 is a continuation of the manual, providing additional guidance on basal index configuration and temporary basal rate settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="International Airline Regulations">
  <data key="d0">International Airline Regulations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">International airline regulations refer to the rules passengers must follow when traveling with medical devices like insulin pumps across borders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26f5ebaa0341f051ad33cfb9895a3851</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traveling With Diabetes Supplies">
  <data key="d0">Traveling With Diabetes Supplies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Traveling with diabetes supplies includes carrying insulin pumps, lancets, syringes, and other medical equipment in compliance with TSA and airline regulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26f5ebaa0341f051ad33cfb9895a3851</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704145</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic Diabetes 670G System">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic Diabetes 670G System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Medtronic Diabetes 670G System is an insulin pump system with advanced features, including dual and square bolus functions, and is accompanied by a user guide for operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26f5ebaa0341f051ad33cfb9895a3851</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704145</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Training Materials">
  <data key="d0">Training Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Training materials are informational resources provided to users of the insulin pump, including the Quick Reference Guide and user manuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26f5ebaa0341f051ad33cfb9895a3851</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704146</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.650 Units Per Hour">
  <data key="d0">0.650 Units Per Hour</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific insulin delivery rate of 0.650 units per hour, required between 8:00 A.M. and 6:00 P.M.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704146</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.900 Units Per Hour">
  <data key="d0">0.900 Units Per Hour</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific insulin delivery rate of 0.900 units per hour, used during parts of the day outside the 8:00 A.M. to 6:00 P.M. period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704146</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="8:00 A.M.">
  <data key="d0">8:00 A.M.</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A time point marking the start of a new basal rate segment, when the insulin rate must be reduced to 0.650 units per hour.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704147</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="6:00 P.M.">
  <data key="d0">6:00 P.M.</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A time point marking the end of the reduced basal rate segment at 0.650 units per hour.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704147</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="12:00 A.M.">
  <data key="d0">12:00 A.M.</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A time point used as a reference to complete the 24-hour basal rate cycle, starting and ending the daily pattern.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704147</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multiple Basal Rate Settings">
  <data key="d0">Multiple Basal Rate Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A configuration method allowing the use of different insulin basal rates at different times of the day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="5:30 P.M.">
  <data key="d0">5:30 P.M.</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A revised time point marking the end of the reduced basal rate segment, changing from 6:00 P.M. to 5:30 P.M. for a new setting of 0.700 units per hour.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.700 Units Per Hour">
  <data key="d0">0.700 Units Per Hour</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A new insulin delivery rate of 0.700 units per hour, set to replace the 0.650 rate between 8:00 A.M. and 5:30 P.M.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-113df8f96ec77242ec482c5116a12b1e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edit Basal 1 Screen">
  <data key="d0">Edit Basal 1 Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Edit Basal 1 screen is an interface on the insulin pump used to modify the time segments and insulin delivery rates for Basal 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704150</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GS Reading">
  <data key="d0">GS Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">GS reading refers to the glucose level input manually entered into the device for monitoring and insulin calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;GS Reading refers to the measurement of blood glucose levels, used by patients and healthcare professionals to assess and adjust insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704150</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pattern Basal">
  <data key="d0">Pattern Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pattern basal refers to a predefined schedule for insulin delivery that can be selected and changed in the basal settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Pattern Basal is a configurable insulin delivery schedule that allows different basal rates to be set for various times of the day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9947b75a4183c17b6384b798fcda161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704150</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Personal Computer">
  <data key="d0">Personal Computer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A personal computer is used in conjunction with the glucose meter to receive and process data transferred from the insulin pump via the CareLink program.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704150</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Website">
  <data key="d0">Website</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The website www.medtronicdiabetes.com provides information about accessories, product support, and user resources for insulin pump users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704150</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magnetic Resonance Imaging">
  <data key="d0">Magnetic Resonance Imaging</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) is a medical procedure involving strong magnetic fields that can interfere with the proper functioning of insulin pumps and sensors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Radiation Equipment">
  <data key="d0">Radiation Equipment</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Radiation equipment such as X-ray, CT, and other imaging devices generate intense magnetic fields or radiation that may damage insulin pumps and require precautionary measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Product Certified Instructor">
  <data key="d0">Product Certified Instructor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A product certified instructor is a professional who provides training on insulin pump use and answers user questions during the learning process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfb1fdb931a758d328534e48eca5ad7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audio Mode">
  <data key="d0">Audio Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Audio mode is a setting that controls how the device provides alerts and notifications through sound.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vibration Mode">
  <data key="d0">Vibration Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Vibration mode is a setting that uses vibration to notify the user of alerts and system events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audio And Vibration Mode">
  <data key="d0">Audio And Vibration Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Audio and vibration mode combines sound and vibration to deliver alerts and notifications from the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Lock Mode">
  <data key="d0">Pump Lock Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump lock mode is an inactive state the device enters after a period of inactivity, requiring unlocking before use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704152</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Main Menu">
  <data key="d0">Main Menu</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The main menu contains seven sections, each offering specific features and functions related to insulin delivery and device settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704152</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Status Screens">
  <data key="d0">Status Screens</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Status screens display detailed information including reservoir level, battery status, recent bolus, last glucose reading, basal rate, and sensor calibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704152</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Life">
  <data key="d0">Battery Life</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery life refers to the remaining operational time of the device, which is preserved by turning off the backlight when idle.&lt;SEP&gt;Battery life refers to the operational duration of the insulin pump's batteries, which can be reduced by physical impacts like dropping the device.&lt;SEP&gt;Battery life refers to the operational duration of the pump's batteries, which may be shortened after physical impact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerts are notifications provided by the device to inform the user of system status, warnings, or required actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerts are non-critical notifications indicating a condition that may require attention, such as low battery, displayed with yellow icons and periodic audio tones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Notification Silence Screen">
  <data key="d0">Notification Silence Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The notification silence screen allows the user to temporarily disable or manage alert sounds and vibrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Menu Button">
  <data key="d0">Menu Button</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The menu button is used to access the main menu from the home screen of the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucagon Design">
  <data key="d0">Glucagon Design</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucagon design is a trademark of Eli Lilly and Company related to glucagon products.&lt;SEP&gt;The glucagon design is a trademarked product of Eli Lilly and Company used in diabetes emergency treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3bc46b3924459ec23a123df1dad4bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704154</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert">
  <data key="d0">Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert is a notification indicating a situation that may require user attention, displayed with a yellow icon and specific audio/vibration patterns on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert is a notification from the pump that requires resolution, accompanied by beeping every 5 or 15 minutes and potentially escalating to a loud emergency siren after 10 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert is a non-critical notification from the pump indicating conditions like low reservoir or low battery that require user attention.&lt;SEP&gt;An Alert is a notification that informs the user of a condition that may require attention but is not immediately critical.&lt;SEP&gt;An audible beep or vibration with a message to inform of a situation that may require attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert refers to a general notification or warning issued by the device for various conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3bc46b3924459ec23a123df1dad4bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weak Insulin Vial">
  <data key="d0">Weak Insulin Vial</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A weak insulin vial refers to a compromised or degraded insulin supply that may reduce effectiveness and lead to elevated glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3bc46b3924459ec23a123df1dad4bdcb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704154</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audio/Vibration Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Audio/Vibration Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Audio and vibration patterns are signaling methods used by the insulin pump to indicate alerts or alarms, repeating at set intervals until acknowledged.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3bc46b3924459ec23a123df1dad4bdcb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Rate Setting">
  <data key="d0">Basal Rate Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal rate setting is a configurable insulin delivery rate used in diabetes management, adjustable through the pump's settings menu.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3bc46b3924459ec23a123df1dad4bdcb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Susie">
  <data key="d0">Susie</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Susie finds it easier to administer bolus insulin with a pump than with injections and no longer forgets her insulin when going out to eat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88cdb970e2c2f1aaaab96fdc11b589f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Suspension">
  <data key="d0">Manual Suspension</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual suspension is a procedure to temporarily stop insulin delivery from the pump, triggering alerts every 15 minutes to remind the user.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88cdb970e2c2f1aaaab96fdc11b589f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Insulin Infusion">
  <data key="d0">Basal Insulin Infusion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal insulin infusion is the continuous delivery of insulin by the pump to maintain glucose levels, which stops during suspension and resumes afterward.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88cdb970e2c2f1aaaab96fdc11b589f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Level Measurement">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Level Measurement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose level measurement, or GS, involves checking blood sugar levels, often recommended when disconnecting or reconnecting the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88cdb970e2c2f1aaaab96fdc11b589f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Reconnection">
  <data key="d0">Pump Reconnection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump reconnection is the process of resuming insulin infusion after suspension, requiring user confirmation to restart basal insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88cdb970e2c2f1aaaab96fdc11b589f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tubo">
  <data key="d0">Tubo</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El tubo es una parte del sistema de infusión que transporta la insulina desde la bomba hasta el cuerpo del paciente.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conector del Reservorio">
  <data key="d0">Conector del Reservorio</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El conector del reservorio es la pieza que une el tubo al reservorio dentro del sistema de infusión de la bomba de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sección del Lugar de Inserción">
  <data key="d0">Sección del Lugar de Inserción</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">La sección del lugar de inserción es la parte del equipo de infusión que se conecta al cuerpo del paciente y contiene la canula.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704157</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canula">
  <data key="d0">Canula</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">La canula es un pequeño tubo flexible insertado en el cuerpo que permite la administración continua de insulina desde la bomba.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704157</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adhesivo">
  <data key="d0">Adhesivo</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El adhesivo es una pieza que mantiene fijo en su lugar el equipo de infusión en la piel del paciente.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704157</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compartimento del Reservorio">
  <data key="d0">Compartimento del Reservorio</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El compartimento del reservorio es la cavidad dentro de la bomba donde se coloca el reservorio que contiene insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pistón">
  <data key="d0">Pistón</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El pistón es un mecanismo interno en la bomba que actúa como émbolo para empujar la insulina desde el reservorio hacia el tubo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Miniordenador">
  <data key="d0">Miniordenador</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El miniordenador es un componente interno de la bomba que controla la administración precisa de insulina en dosis pequeñas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equipo de Infusión">
  <data key="d0">Equipo de Infusión</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El equipo de infusión es el conjunto de componentes, incluyendo el tubo, la canula y el adhesivo, que se encargan de entregar insulina al cuerpo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guía del Usuario del Sistema MiniMed® 670G">
  <data key="d0">Guía del Usuario del Sistema MiniMed® 670G</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">La Guía del Usuario del Sistema MiniMed® 670G proporciona información técnica y operativa detallada sobre el uso de la bomba de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capacitación en Persona">
  <data key="d0">Capacitación en Persona</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">La capacitación en persona es una sesión guiada por un instructor certificado para enseñar al usuario cómo usar correctamente la bomba de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Instructor">
  <data key="d0">Instructor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">El instructor es un profesional capacitado que guía a los usuarios durante la capacitación formal sobre el uso de la bomba de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Profesional de Salud">
  <data key="d0">Profesional de Salud</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">El profesional de salud es un experto médico que autoriza el uso de la bomba de insulina y proporciona indicaciones sobre su manejo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quick-set®">
  <data key="d0">Quick-set®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Quick-set® es un modelo específico de equipo de infusión utilizado con la bomba de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pantalla de la Bomba">
  <data key="d0">Pantalla de la Bomba</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">La pantalla de la bomba muestra información operativa y requiere interacción del usuario; se oscurece tras 15 segundos de inactividad.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b69a34f389efb36d99ba8a4506a2a2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="50 Mg/Dl Threshold">
  <data key="d0">50 Mg/Dl Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A glucose level below 50 mg/dL indicates hypoglycemia, requiring immediate treatment with carbohydrates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="250 Mg/Dl Threshold">
  <data key="d0">250 Mg/Dl Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A glucose level above 250 mg/dL indicates hyperglycemia and requires ketone testing and possible corrective actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic Minimed, Inc">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic Minimed, Inc</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Medtronic Minimed, Inc is the company that owns the Bolus Wizard trademark and manufactures insulin pump systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Target Range">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Target Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The blood glucose target range is a personalized setting indicating the desired blood glucose levels, defined by high and low values in mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-402361ced0649a06619dcaf93b0eb651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Wizard Function">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Wizard Function</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus Wizard function is a feature that calculates insulin dosage based on blood glucose levels, carbohydrate intake, and other personalized settings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Wizard function calculates insulin bolus doses based on current blood glucose levels and carbohydrate intake, supporting diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-402361ced0649a06619dcaf93b0eb651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b8d4c3fde5ebf7bc3593f47b765f41</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Corrective Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Corrective Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Corrective insulin is the amount of insulin needed to bring high blood glucose levels back to the target range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-402361ced0649a06619dcaf93b0eb651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Bolus Administration">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Bolus Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin bolus administration is the process of delivering a measured dose of insulin, typically before meals or to correct high glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-402361ced0649a06619dcaf93b0eb651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Wizard Setup">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Wizard Setup</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Wizard Setup is the configuration process where parameters like insulin sensitivity, target range, and active insulin duration are entered.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Wizard Setup is the procedure required to configure the Bolus Wizard feature in Manual mode, involving the input of four settings: Carb Ratio, Insulin Sensitivity Factor, BG Target, and Active Insulin Time.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-402361ced0649a06619dcaf93b0eb651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b0e9023a7c03c6a284d69e0930b8a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medidor Contour Next Link 2.4">
  <data key="d0">Medidor Contour Next Link 2.4</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Medidor Contour Next Link 2.4 is a blood glucose meter that wirelessly communicates with the MiniMed® 670G insulin pump to automatically send glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704163</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed® 670G">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed® 670G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">El MiniMed® 670G es un modelo específico de bomba de insulina producido por Medtronic MiniMed.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed® 670G is an insulin pump that wirelessly connects with the Contour Next Link 2.4 meter for automated glucose data transmission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e199c63f77bb267d92abb101f110ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704163</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Marcador Eventos">
  <data key="d0">Marcador Eventos</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Marcador Eventos is a feature used to log events such as meals or exercise that affect glucose levels in relation to insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704163</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tiras Para Medición De Glucosa Contour® Next">
  <data key="d0">Tiras Para Medición De Glucosa Contour® Next</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">These are test strips required for the Contour Next Link 2.4 meter to measure blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704163</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Programa Carelink® Personal">
  <data key="d0">Programa Carelink® Personal</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Programa CareLink® Personal is a web-based application provided by Medtronic to upload and analyze data from the insulin pump and glucose meter in readable reports and charts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704164</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sitio Web Seguro">
  <data key="d0">Sitio Web Seguro</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sitio Web Seguro is the secure online platform where glucose and insulin data are uploaded and analyzed via the CareLink® Personal program.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704164</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Informes Y Gráficas">
  <data key="d0">Informes Y Gráficas</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Informes y Gráficas are generated by the CareLink® Personal program to visualize trends in glucose levels and the impact of insulin, food intake, and exercise.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Profesional De Salud">
  <data key="d0">Profesional De Salud</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Profesional De Salud is a medical professional who provides personalized settings for insulin therapy, including Bolus Wizard parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;The Profesional de Salud is a medical provider who reviews patient glucose data and helps adjust insulin pump settings accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d74e338f7a37de66d4b2268a49021c4e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cuenta De Carelink® Personal">
  <data key="d0">Cuenta De Carelink® Personal</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A Cuenta de CareLink® Personal is required to transfer and access pump and meter data online, created through the Medtronic website.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="USB Connector">
  <data key="d0">USB Connector</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The USB connector is a port on the Contour Next Link 2.4 meter used for charging the device via a wall charger or computer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Protective USB Cover">
  <data key="d0">Protective USB Cover</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The protective USB cover shields the USB connector of the meter when not in use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reactive Strip Port">
  <data key="d0">Reactive Strip Port</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The reactive strip port is where glucose test strips are inserted into the Contour Next Link 2.4 meter for blood glucose testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reactive Strip Port Light">
  <data key="d0">Reactive Strip Port Light</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The reactive strip port light blinks during charging and indicates the charging status of the meter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Display Screen">
  <data key="d0">Display Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The display screen shows glucose readings, messages, and menu options on the Contour Next Link 2.4 meter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Menu And Power Button">
  <data key="d0">Menu And Power Button</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The menu and power button is used to turn on the meter and navigate through its menu system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Selection/Scrolling Buttons">
  <data key="d0">Selection/Scrolling Buttons</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The selection/scrolling buttons allow navigation through the meter's interface and selection of options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f9cff4e37113031ee37a1e3ffad55d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuration Assistant">
  <data key="d0">Configuration Assistant</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Configuration Assistant is a guided setup process that helps users configure the pump by setting language, date, and time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Start Screen">
  <data key="d0">Start Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Start Screen is the main interface of the pump, displaying current time, glucose reading, active insulin, and status icons.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Status Icons">
  <data key="d0">Status Icons</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Status Icons provide a quick overview of the pump's condition, including battery level and reservoir amount.&lt;SEP&gt;Status icons are graphical indicators on the Home Screen that convey system status, alerts, and connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Status Icons are visual indicators on the Home screen that provide a quick overview of the pump system's current status, including battery, connection, and alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Status icons provide visual indicators on the Home screen for various system states, including alert status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Icon">
  <data key="d0">Battery Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Battery Icon indicates the charge level of the pump's battery, changing color and fill level from green to red to black as the charge depletes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservoir Icon">
  <data key="d0">Reservoir Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reservoir Icon shows the approximate amount of insulin remaining in the pump, displayed in percentage ranges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time">
  <data key="d0">Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time is displayed on the Start Screen and can be set in 12-hour (AM/PM) or 24-hour format during configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;Time refers to the configurable duration setting for the Set Change reminder, allowing users to select the number of days between infusion set changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Date">
  <data key="d0">Date</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Date includes year, month, and day, and is set during the Configuration Assistant setup process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Housing">
  <data key="d0">Pump Housing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The pump housing is the outer casing of the pump, used as a reference point for aligning components during setup or maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gastroparesis">
  <data key="d0">Gastroparesis</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Gastroparesis is a medical condition causing delayed digestion, which can be managed using a square bolus to align insulin action with delayed carbohydrate absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Gastroparesis is a medical condition characterized by delayed stomach emptying, which can affect insulin timing and make Square Wave boluses useful.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4b8d4c3fde5ebf7bc3593f47b765f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b0e9023a7c03c6a284d69e0930b8a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707471</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Square Bolus Duration">
  <data key="d0">Square Bolus Duration</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Square bolus duration is a configurable time period ranging from 30 minutes to 8 hours in 15-minute increments, during which the insulin is delivered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4b8d4c3fde5ebf7bc3593f47b765f41</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704172</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="24-Hour Cycle">
  <data key="d0">24-Hour Cycle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The 24-hour cycle refers to the full day period over which basal insulin delivery is programmed and monitored in an insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704173</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Practice Basal Rate">
  <data key="d0">Practice Basal Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Practice basal rates are example values provided for training purposes to help users learn how to program their insulin pump; they are not for actual therapy and using them could lead to incorrect insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704173</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Start Time">
  <data key="d0">Start Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Start Time refers to the beginning of a specific basal rate segment in the insulin pump programming.&lt;SEP&gt;Start Time is a configurable setting for the Missed Meal Bolus Reminder that defines when the reminder period begins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="End Time">
  <data key="d0">End Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">End Time refers to the conclusion of a specific basal rate segment, used when setting or editing basal patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;End Time is a configurable setting for the Missed Meal Bolus Reminder that defines when the reminder period ends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hourly Rate">
  <data key="d0">Hourly Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Hourly Rate is the amount of insulin delivered per hour (measured in U/h) within a basal segment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704174</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Percentage Basal">
  <data key="d0">Percentage Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Percentage Basal is a setting that adjusts the current basal rate by a percentage of the original programmed rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704174</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Duration">
  <data key="d0">Duration</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Duration refers to the length of time a temporary basal rate will remain active before reverting to the normal basal pattern.&lt;SEP&gt;Duration refers to the length of time a temp basal rate is active, which can be set between 30 minutes and 24 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Duration refers to the time period for which Alert Silence is set, configurable in 15-minute increments from 30 minutes to 24 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Duration refers to the time period over which the square portion of a Dual Wave bolus is delivered, adjustable by the user.&lt;SEP&gt;Duration is a setting used to define the time period over which a Square Wave bolus is delivered.&lt;SEP&gt;Duration is the time period over which the Square portion of a Square Wave or Dual Wave bolus is delivered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edit Basal">
  <data key="d0">Edit Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Edit Basal is a function allowing users to modify existing basal rate segments, including start time, end time, and insulin rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704174</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Add New">
  <data key="d0">Add New</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Add New is a menu option used to create additional basal patterns or time segments within the insulin pump programming.&lt;SEP&gt;Add New is an option used to create a new reminder entry, such as a Personal or Missed Meal Bolus Reminder.&lt;SEP&gt;Add New is an option within Preset Bolus Setup that initiates the creation of a new preset bolus configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cancel Basal Temporal">
  <data key="d0">Cancel Basal Temporal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cancel Basal Temporal is a function that stops the temporary basal rate and reverts to the normal programmed basal pattern immediately.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704174</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Review">
  <data key="d0">Review</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Review is a function that allows users to view current basal settings, including active temporary rates and scheduled patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Review is a step in the configuration process that allows users to confirm and save the high SG settings before finalizing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ferrer">
  <data key="d0">Ferrer</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Ferrer is a pharmaceutical company referenced in the context of insulin pump usage or device branding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704175</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal 2">
  <data key="d0">Basal 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal 2 is an additional basal insulin pattern that can be configured and selected for use in the insulin pump system.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal 2 is an additional basal insulin delivery pattern with a 24-hour total of 1.2 U and configurable rate intervals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Laborable">
  <data key="d0">Laborable</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Laborable is a label for a basal pattern associated with a workday or regular weekday routine in the insulin pump settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704175</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Festivo">
  <data key="d0">Festivo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Festivo is a named basal pattern with a total 24-hour insulin delivery of 17.4 U, indicating it is designed for special occasions or holidays.&lt;SEP&gt;Festivo is a label for a basal pattern associated with holidays or weekends, indicating a different insulin delivery schedule.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7534f3bc09ac6e2eece38e12eb89cf1f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704175</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Administración De Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Administración De Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Administración De Bolus is the process of delivering an insulin bolus through the pump, initiated manually or via Bolus Wizard.&lt;SEP&gt;Administración De Bolus is the process of delivering an insulin bolus using a device, guided by specific steps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-69b83b1b837df0b960758dfd02d42d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d74e338f7a37de66d4b2268a49021c4e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704175</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parte Frontal De La Bomba">
  <data key="d0">Parte Frontal De La Bomba</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">La parte frontal de la bomba contiene controles como botones de dirección, selección y acceso al menú o gráfico de glucosa.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17e199c63f77bb267d92abb101f110ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704176</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parte Inferior De La Bomba">
  <data key="d0">Parte Inferior De La Bomba</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">La parte inferior de la bomba incluye el compartimento de la pila y otros elementos estructurales.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17e199c63f77bb267d92abb101f110ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704176</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parte Posterior De La Bomba">
  <data key="d0">Parte Posterior De La Bomba</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">La parte posterior de la bomba es donde se pueden adherir carátulas protectoras y personalizadas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17e199c63f77bb267d92abb101f110ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778704176</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Botones De La Bomba">
  <data key="d0">Botones De La Bomba</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Los botones incluyen arriba, abajo, izquierda, derecha, atrás y seleccionar, utilizados para navegar menús y confirmar opciones.</data>
