<node id="Low SG Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Low SG Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Low SG Alarm is an alert triggered when sensor glucose is below the preset low value and cannot be silenced during All Sensor Alerts silencing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Low SG Alarm is triggered when sensor glucose levels fall below a predefined threshold, alerting the user to a potential hypoglycemic event.&lt;SEP&gt;The low SG alarm notifies the user when sensor glucose falls below a specified threshold, such as 55 mg/dL, and may be updated when a new sensor type is paired.&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG Alarm is a system alert for low sensor glucose levels, referenced on page 323 and related to user-configurable settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707206</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend on Low">
  <data key="d0">Suspend on Low</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend on Low is a safety feature that stops insulin delivery when sensor glucose reaches a low limit, but it is not available when the SmartGuard feature is active.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707206</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm Up">
  <data key="d0">Warm Up</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Warm up is the initialization phase of a new CGM sensor that requires interstitial fluid detection to begin; failure to start triggers an alert.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707207</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Instinct">
  <data key="d0">Instinct</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Instinct is a device or system component that displays alerts and messages related to sensor, calibration, and connectivity issues in the CGM system.&lt;SEP&gt;Instinct is a type of sensor used in the CGM system, factory-set to trigger alarms at specific glucose thresholds.&lt;SEP&gt;Instinct is a device or system model associated with the CGM device that generates alerts such as "Sensor ending soon."&lt;SEP&gt;A CGM system or pump model that interacts with sensors and displays alerts related to pairing, temperature, and glucose monitoring.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Instinct is a CGM device model that supports glucose monitoring and alerts within the SmartGuard system.&lt;SEP&gt;Instinct is a sensor system used for glucose monitoring, which can be started, removed, or unpaired from the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707207</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low SG Alert">
  <data key="d0">Low SG Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Low SG alert is a notification system in the MiniMed 780G system that warns users when sensor glucose levels are low or predicted to drop.&lt;SEP&gt;The Low SG Alert is activated when sensor glucose falls below 55 mg/dL or 64 mg/dL, depending on the alarm type, and cannot be turned off.&lt;SEP&gt;The Low SG Alert is a notification that occurs when sensor glucose falls below a specified threshold and is distinct from the Low SG Alarm in its severity and response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707212</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Very High Basal Setting">
  <data key="d0">Very High Basal Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Very High Basal Setting message warns that a selected basal pattern delivers significantly more insulin than typically needed, requiring healthcare professional consultation.&lt;SEP&gt;Very High Basal Setting is a warning that the programmed basal insulin rate is unusually high.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707213</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Feature">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The SmartGuard feature is an automated insulin delivery system integrated into the MiniMed 780G insulin pump, designed to help individuals with diabetes maintain glucose levels within a target range of 70 mg/dL to 180 mg/dL. It functions by continuously analyzing sensor glucose (SG) readings to automatically adjust basal insulin delivery and administer correction boluses as needed, using advanced algorithms that consider current glucose levels and carbohydrate intake. The system supports both basal rate adjustments and bolus dose calculations, aiming to maximize time in range and reduce the burden of manual insulin management.

To activate the SmartGuard feature, specific setup conditions must be met, including configuration of target glucose levels, auto-correction settings, and a warm-up period. Notably, the system requires a 5-hour warm-up after a software update or pump reset before it becomes operational, during which insulin delivery adjustments are unavailable to ensure accurate active insulin calculations. Additionally, the feature is not available during the first 12 hours of initial sensor use and may suspend automatically under certain conditions, such as sensor glucose unavailability, unsafe basal insulin patterns, or prolonged periods of maximum insulin delivery, requiring user intervention to resume.

The SmartGuard feature alters the pump’s Home screen interface when active, reflecting its advanced functionality and providing system-specific alerts and messages to guide user interaction. It operates only when not in Manual mode and relies on accurate sensor data, though its performance with alternative sample sites like the palm is not established. Calibration and performance verification are based on blood glucose values, and the system may require temporary adjustments when medications such as acetaminophen are used, as they can interfere with sensor accuracy. Overall, SmartGuard represents a comprehensive, sensor-driven insulin delivery system that combines automated basal adjustments, bolus assistance, and safety mechanisms to support effective glucose management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200c1e93d7f4cbc3027cec4d0898dc00</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm Up Not Started">
  <data key="d0">Warm Up Not Started</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Warm Up Not Started alert appears when the CGM sensor fails to begin warm-up after pairing, indicating possible insertion issues or sensor malfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Warm Up Not Started indicates that the glucose sensor has not initiated its warm-up phase after activation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enter BG Now">
  <data key="d0">Enter BG Now</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enter BG Now alert prompts the user to input a blood glucose reading after the SmartGuard feature has operated at maximum delivery rate for 7 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Enter BG Now is a prompt for the user to manually input a blood glucose value.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM Device">
  <data key="d0">CGM Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The CGM Device, or Continuous Glucose Monitoring device, is a critical component of insulin pump systems such as the MiniMed 780G, designed to continuously track sensor glucose (SG) levels in real time. It functions as part of an integrated system, working in conjunction with an insulin pump to support automated insulin delivery by transmitting glucose readings via a transmitter. Compatible models include the Instinct, Simplera Sync, and Guardian 4 sensors, all of which must be securely paired with the pump for proper operation. This pairing is essential not only during initial setup but also after a pump restart, ensuring uninterrupted communication between the CGM device and the pump.

The CGM Device consists of a sensor and transmitter that are worn externally and inserted subcutaneously to monitor glucose levels continuously. After a warm-up period, the system begins providing real-time glucose data, which informs insulin delivery decisions and enables dynamic adjustments in automated insulin dosing. The device generates alerts and alarms based on predefined glucose thresholds, notifying users of high or low sensor glucose values, connection issues, or system updates. In some cases, such as when using the Simplera Sync or Guardian 4, the CGM may require calibration to maintain accuracy, and it can trigger alerts if sensor readings become unavailable.

As a sensor-based system, the CGM Device is sensitive to environmental factors and must be removed before exposure to magnetic fields or radiation to prevent interference or damage. While the device operates independently in monitoring glucose, it remains unaffected when pump settings are cleared, maintaining its paired status and data continuity. Regular maintenance is required, including periodic sensor changes and troubleshooting for connectivity alerts. Overall, the CGM Device plays a central role in modern diabetes management by delivering continuous, real-time glucose monitoring and enhancing the safety and efficacy of insulin therapy through seamless integration with insulin pump technology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707216</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Error Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Power Error Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Power Error Alarm indicates that the pump's internal power source cannot charge and it is operating solely on the AA battery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707217</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Loss Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Power Loss Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Power loss alarm occurs if the pump is without power for an extended period, requiring re-entry of time and date settings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Power Loss Alarm triggers when the AA battery has been removed for more than 10 minutes or power was lost, requiring time and date to be re-entered.&lt;SEP&gt;Power Loss Alarm is a notification triggered when the insulin pump experiences unexpected power interruption, referenced on page 311.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707217</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Error Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Pump Error Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A pump error alarm is triggered when an issue occurs with the insulin pump, such as a software reset, requiring user intervention to clear.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump error alarm alerts the user to malfunctions such as software reset due to electrostatic discharge.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pump Error Alarm indicates a malfunction that stops insulin delivery, clears current settings, and requires a restart of the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Pump Error Alarm is a general system alert indicating a malfunction in the insulin pump operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="24 Hour Technical Support">
  <data key="d0">24 Hour Technical Support</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">24 Hour Technical Support provides assistance for pump-related issues, especially if alarms recur frequently.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707222</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian 4">
  <data key="d0">Guardian 4</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Guardian 4 is a specific model of continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) system designed for the management of diabetes by continuously tracking glucose levels and integrating with insulin delivery devices, particularly insulin pumps. It functions as a comprehensive device system that includes a sensor, transmitter, and associated software to enable real-time glucose monitoring and data transmission. The transmitter component of the Guardian 4 connects directly to the CGM sensor and wirelessly relays glucose data to a compatible insulin pump, allowing for coordinated diabetes management.

The Guardian 4 system is engineered for seamless operation with insulin pumps, enabling users to start the CGM directly from the pump interface. It requires secure physical and wireless connections between the sensor and transmitter to ensure reliable signal transmission and accurate readings. As part of its functionality, the system provides various alerts and on-screen messages to inform users of potential issues, such as sensor malfunctions, transmitter connectivity problems, or the need for calibration. These alerts serve to maintain system integrity and support effective user intervention when necessary.

In addition to monitoring glucose levels, the Guardian 4 supports sensor calibration and offers user guidance through its interface, enhancing usability and accuracy. It is specifically designed to work within an integrated diabetes management ecosystem, where glucose data informs insulin delivery decisions. Overall, Guardian 4 serves as a critical tool for individuals requiring close glycemic control, combining continuous monitoring, alert systems, and pump integration into a unified platform.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alarm History">
  <data key="d0">Alarm History</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Alarm History is a feature that stores error codes from past alarms, which can be used for troubleshooting with technical support.&lt;SEP&gt;Alarm History is a log within the pump that records past alarms and their corresponding error codes for review.&lt;SEP&gt;Alarm History stores records of past alarms and alerts that required user attention.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature that stores information about recent alarms and alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Alarm history logs past alerts and warnings generated by the pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time And Date Screen">
  <data key="d0">Time And Date Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Time And Date Screen is an interface where the user must re-enter current time and date after a power loss or restart.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Restore Settings">
  <data key="d0">Restore Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Restore Settings replaces current pump settings with the last saved settings, provided settings have been previously saved.&lt;SEP&gt;Restore Settings is an option to reapply the last saved pump settings after a restart or power loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Restore Settings is a function that allows users to recover previously saved pump settings after an error.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Appendix A">
  <data key="d0">Appendix A</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Appendix A is a section of the document listing alarms, alerts, and messages related to the pump system.&lt;SEP&gt;Appendix A is a section of the document that contains a list of alarms, alerts, and messages with their explanations and next steps.&lt;SEP&gt;Appendix A is a section of the document that lists alarms, alerts, and messages related to the pump and CGM device.&lt;SEP&gt;Appendix A contains supplementary information related to device operations, including data download procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AA Battery">
  <data key="d0">AA Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The AA battery is the designated power source for the MiniMed 780G insulin pump, serving as a replaceable and essential component for the device's operation. It functions both as the primary external power supply and as a temporary backup when the pump's internal power source is unable to charge or maintain function. Proper connection of the AA battery is critical; if the pump buttons become unresponsive or the device malfunctions, users are advised to check, reconnect, or replace the battery to restore functionality.

As a replaceable power source, the AA battery must be inserted anew whenever it is removed or becomes depleted, ensuring uninterrupted insulin delivery. If the battery is removed for more than 10 minutes, the pump triggers a power loss alarm, indicating a significant disruption in power supply. Battery replacement is necessary not only when the charge is low but also in cases of incompatibility, which may prevent proper operation. Maintaining a functional AA battery is therefore crucial to sustaining the therapeutic function of the insulin pump, with timely replacement required to resume or continue insulin delivery effectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d536bf636b4a29c1f9f46de648b2b306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compatible CGM Device">
  <data key="d0">Compatible CGM Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A compatible CGM device measures glucose levels and communicates with the insulin pump via wireless connection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian 4 Transmitter">
  <data key="d0">Guardian 4 Transmitter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guardian 4 transmitter is used with the Guardian 4 sensor to transmit glucose data to the MiniMed 780G insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guardian 4 transmitter is a device that wirelessly sends glucose data from the Guardian 4 sensor to the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guardian 4 transmitter is a Bluetooth-enabled device that sends glucose data from the Guardian 4 sensor to the MiniMed 780G pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guardian 4 transmitter communicates glucose data from the sensor to the pump via wireless connection.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guardian 4 transmitter (MMT-7841) pairs with the MiniMed 780G insulin pump, collects glucose data from the Guardian 4 sensor, and wirelessly sends it to monitoring devices; it is required for CGM.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guardian 4 Transmitter is a specific model of transmitter used with the CGM system, referenced in user instructions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guardian 4 Transmitter is the wireless component designed to work with the Guardian 4 Sensor and pair with the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707232</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compatible Mobile Device">
  <data key="d0">Compatible Mobile Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A compatible mobile device is required to control the MiniMed Mobile app and interact with the MiniMed 780G system.&lt;SEP&gt;A compatible mobile device is required to start the Instinct sensor and must meet specifications provided by Medtronic, including supported operating systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A compatible mobile device can be paired with the pump to enable communication and must confirm successful pairing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707233</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump is a medical device designed for the subcutaneous delivery of insulin to aid in the management of diabetes, particularly Type 1 diabetes, in individuals aged 7 years and older. It functions as part of an integrated diabetes management system, delivering insulin continuously and automatically adjusting delivery based on real-time glucose data from compatible continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensors. The device operates using SmartGuard™ technology, which leverages predictive algorithms to anticipate glucose trends and proactively adjust insulin levels, including the use of Predictive Low Glucose features to help prevent hypoglycemia. Insulin delivery occurs through an infusion set, with settings customized by a healthcare professional, and the device supports both automated and manual delivery modes, including basal rate patterns, temporary adjustments, and bolus dosing.

The MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump features advanced functionalities such as the Bolus Wizard, which calculates insulin doses based on current glucose levels, carbohydrate intake, and insulin on board, as well as a bolus calculator and history tracking for improved treatment oversight. It pairs wirelessly with compatible CGM devices to receive glucose readings, though it does not support wireless connection with blood glucose (BG) meters. The device requires the user to be on the Home screen during sensor scanning to ensure proper data transmission. It includes a user interface with buttons and screens, adjustable display settings, and a Block mode for access control, enhancing usability and security. Additional alert features, such as the Low Reservoir Reminder, help maintain consistent operation.

For safe and effective use, the MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump requires proper setup, including correct reservoir and infusion set installation, as well as routine maintenance such as cleaning, battery management, and appropriate storage. It is contraindicated for individuals under the age of 7 or those unable to operate the device safely. By combining automated insulin delivery with interoperable technology and smart device connectivity, the MiniMed 780G supports comprehensive, personalized diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d536bf636b4a29c1f9f46de648b2b306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200c1e93d7f4cbc3027cec4d0898dc00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707234</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Mode">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard mode automatically adjusts and delivers basal insulin and provides automatic correction boluses to regulate glucose levels to a target value.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707235</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Simplera Sync Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Simplera Sync Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Simplera Sync Sensor (MMT-5120) is a disposable, single-use continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) device developed by Medtronic for integration with the MiniMed 780G insulin pump system. It measures glucose levels in the interstitial fluid beneath the skin and communicates wirelessly with the insulin pump to enable real-time glucose monitoring and system functionality. The sensor must be paired with the MiniMed 780G pump within 20 minutes of activation, using a security code from the inserter label, to ensure secure operation and to activate features such as SmartGuard, which relies on the sensor-pump connection for automated insulin delivery.

The Simplera Sync Sensor is designed specifically for compatibility with the MiniMed 780G system and can be both paired and unpaired with the pump as needed. It operates without requiring user calibration, using built-in algorithms for glucose measurement, and includes a preset low sensor glucose (SG) value of 64 mg/dL to support glucose detection and alert generation. However, the device has limitations regarding low glucose alert reliability, and its performance may be affected by certain medications, including acetaminophen and hydroxyurea, which can interfere with glucose readings.

Notably, the Simplera Sync Sensor is not approved for treatment decisions in Manual mode for users under 18 years of age when used with the MiniMed 780G system. While the MiniMed Mobile App can serve as an optional accessory for glucose monitoring, the primary interface remains the insulin pump. As an integral component of Medtronic’s diabetes management platform, the Simplera Sync Sensor supports seamless CGM integration, enabling data-driven insulin delivery and enhancing glycemic control for individuals with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200c1e93d7f4cbc3027cec4d0898dc00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707238</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian 4 Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Guardian 4 Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guardian 4 Sensor is a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) device developed by Medtronic, specifically designed for use with the MiniMed 780G insulin pump system. It is a disposable, single-use glucose sensor (model MMT-7040) that measures glucose levels in the interstitial fluid beneath the skin and is the only sensor compatible with the Guardian 4 transmitter. The sensor integrates with the MiniMed 780G system to enable automated insulin delivery through the SmartGuard technology, providing real-time glucose readings, tracking trends, and issuing alerts based on glucose values, including a preset low sensor glucose (SG) threshold of 64 mg/dL.

The Guardian 4 Sensor pairs wirelessly with the insulin pump, and successful pairing is indicated by a green LED on the transmitter that stops blinking once the connection is established. It requires a warm-up period after insertion before it begins transmitting data. Notably, the system is designed to automatically calibrate using blood glucose readings, eliminating the need for manual user calibration, which distinguishes it from some earlier CGM models. The transmitter also displays battery status information, allowing users to monitor its operational readiness.

In addition to pump integration, the Guardian 4 Sensor can be used with the optional MiniMed Mobile App, which provides supplementary monitoring capabilities. However, the sensor’s performance may be affected by certain medications, particularly hydroxyurea, which can interfere with glucose readings and lead to inaccuracies. As a key component of Medtronic’s advanced diabetes management ecosystem, the Guardian 4 Sensor supports seamless, continuous glucose monitoring to enhance glycemic control for individuals using compatible MiniMed systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707243</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed Mobile App">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed Mobile App</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed Mobile App is a software application designed to support users of the MiniMed 780G insulin pump system, particularly when using the Instinct continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor. Available as MMT-6101 for Android and MMT-6102 for iOS, the app is compatible with select mobile devices and requires a stable internet connection for full functionality. It serves as a critical interface between the user and their diabetes management devices, enabling remote monitoring, data synchronization, and system control.

The app provides a secondary display of insulin pump data, including real-time sensor glucose readings, alarms, alerts, and messages, which can be viewed on a paired mobile device. Users can customize notification preferences to receive timely updates about pump status and glucose trends. It supports wireless software updates for the pump, facilitates the uploading of device data to CareLink™ software, and allows sharing of information with the CareLink Connect app for enhanced care coordination. Additionally, the MiniMed Mobile App plays an essential role in sensor management by guiding users through the setup process, starting and restarting the Instinct sensor, managing sensor pairing with the pump, and troubleshooting errors that may occur during sensor activation.

The MiniMed Mobile App is required for initiating the Instinct sensor and managing its pairing with the pump, though its use is optional when employing other sensor types. It enables users to pair their mobile device with the insulin pump, manage device functions remotely, and access user guidance, including cybersecurity precautions necessary for safe operation. As a system component, the app links to user accounts for access control and ensures secure interaction with Medtronic diabetes devices, emphasizing both usability and data protection in its design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Instinct Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Instinct Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Instinct Sensor (also known as the Simplera Sync sensor and model number MMT-5420) is a disposable, single-use continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) device designed for use with the MiniMed 780G insulin pump system. Manufactured by Abbott, it is inserted subcutaneously to measure glucose levels in interstitial fluid and supports real-time glucose monitoring, enabling integration with Medtronic insulin pump technologies such as SmartGuard and Predictive Low Glucose Suspend. The sensor is interoperable with the MiniMed system and requires pairing via the MiniMed Mobile app, as direct activation through the pump is not supported. NFC capability is essential for operation, and users must rely on NFC-compatible mobile devices to start a new sensor session or to unpair and restart the sensor as needed.

The Instinct Sensor functions as part of a comprehensive CGM system, where blood glucose readings are used to verify system accuracy rather than for calibration. It features a fixed preset low sensor glucose (SG) threshold of 55 mg/dL, which supports automated insulin delivery and alert generation to help prevent hypoglycemia. Users are required to consult the MiniMed Mobile App user guide for proper setup procedures and security precautions. While the device enhances diabetes management through seamless integration with the MiniMed 780G system, it is susceptible to interference from high doses of Vitamin C, which may lead to falsely elevated glucose readings. The sensor can be removed or replaced as part of routine use, with instructions for these actions referenced in user documentation. Overall, the Instinct Sensor serves as a critical component in advanced insulin delivery systems, combining app-based control with real-time glucose tracking for improved glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Bolus Feature">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Bolus Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The SmartGuard bolus feature delivers bolus insulin based on sensor glucose values and carbohydrate entries in SmartGuard mode.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature that assists in calculating a recommended bolus amount based on optional carbohydrate intake and optional blood glucose or sensor glucose measurement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tubing">
  <data key="d0">Tubing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tubing connects the reservoir to the infusion site; correct assembly ensures the pump remains waterproof.&lt;SEP&gt;Tubing is a component of the infusion set that carries insulin from the reservoir to the cannula inserted in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The tubing is a component of the infusion set that carries insulin from the reservoir into the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Tubing is part of the infusion set that carries insulin from the reservoir to the cannula.&lt;SEP&gt;Tubing is part of the infusion set used for insulin delivery and must be checked for cracks.&lt;SEP&gt;Tubing is a component used in the insulin delivery system that connects the reservoir to the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc61f77b003d0086bd985ddb94fc2a98</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Battery Alert">
  <data key="d0">Low Battery Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The low battery alert indicates that the pump's battery is running low and needs replacement soon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loading Incomplete Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Loading Incomplete Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The loading incomplete alarm occurs when the reservoir and set procedure is interrupted, possibly due to premature button press.&lt;SEP&gt;Loading Incomplete Alarm is a system alert indicating that insulin reservoir filling was not completed properly.&lt;SEP&gt;Loading Incomplete Alarm is an alert indicating that the insulin loading process was not completed successfully.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manage Settings Error">
  <data key="d0">Manage Settings Error</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The manage settings error stops insulin delivery and clears backup settings, though current settings remain functional.&lt;SEP&gt;Manage Settings Error indicates a problem occurred while attempting to modify device settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Fill Reached Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Max Fill Reached Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The max fill reached alarm indicates that more insulin units than expected have been used to fill the tubing, suggesting possible air or blockage.&lt;SEP&gt;Max fill reached alarm indicates the reservoir or system has reached its maximum fill capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;Max Fill Reached Alarm indicates that the insulin reservoir has reached its maximum capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;Max Fill Reached Alarm indicates that the reservoir has reached its maximum capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;Max Fill Reached Alarm is an alert triggered when the insulin reservoir reaches its maximum capacity during filling.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="No Reservoir Detected Alarm">
  <data key="d0">No Reservoir Detected Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The no reservoir detected alarm appears when the pump does not detect a properly installed reservoir.&lt;SEP&gt;No Reservoir Detected Alarm is a system error indicating the insulin reservoir is not properly installed, referenced on page 311.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Error Detected">
  <data key="d0">Power Error Detected</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The power error detected alarm indicates a failure in the pump's internal power source to charge, halting insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Power Error Detected indicates an issue with the device's power supply or electrical system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CareLink Software">
  <data key="d0">CareLink Software</data>
  <data key="d1">software</data>
  <data key="d2">CareLink Software is a digital health platform designed to receive, manage, and analyze data from medical devices, particularly insulin delivery systems such as the MiniMed 780G insulin pump. It enables users and healthcare providers to monitor device performance and patient glucose trends by facilitating the upload of system data through multiple pathways, including the MiniMed Mobile app or the Blue Adapter. The software supports pairing with insulin pumps to streamline data transfer and device management, allowing for efficient communication between the medical device and the digital interface.

The platform is capable of downloading and analyzing both pump and glucose data, offering comprehensive insights into patient therapy patterns and device functionality. CareLink Software not only stores uploaded device data but also generates alerts and messages related to device operation, helping users and clinicians identify potential issues or trends in real time. These features support proactive management of diabetes care by enhancing visibility into treatment efficacy and device behavior.

CareLink Software serves as a centralized tool for managing data from various Medtronic diabetes devices, supporting remote monitoring and clinical decision-making. By integrating data from the MiniMed 780G system and associated applications, it provides a cohesive environment for reviewing therapy history, generating reports, and ensuring continuity of care. Its functionality spans data upload, analysis, alert generation, and device pairing, making it a critical component in the ecosystem of connected diabetes management technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend Before Low">
  <data key="d0">Suspend Before Low</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend Before Low is a safety feature designed to prevent hypoglycemia by automatically pausing insulin delivery when sensor glucose (SG) levels are predicted to drop below a user-defined threshold. This predictive function is part of advanced diabetes management systems, particularly integrated within the MiniMed 780G insulin pump system, and operates as a component of Predictive Low Glucose technology. The feature anticipates low glucose events approximately 30 minutes in advance, temporarily stopping insulin infusion to reduce the time spent in hypoglycemic ranges.

The Suspend Before Low feature functions in Manual mode when continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) is active, relying on real-time sensor data and predictive algorithms to determine when glucose levels are approaching the set low limit. It triggers an alert to notify the user of the impending low glucose event, and if enabled, this alert cannot be silenced, ensuring the user remains aware and responsive. Users are required to check their blood glucose levels when the alert is activated, promoting active engagement in glucose management.

While Suspend Before Low enhances safety by proactively mitigating hypoglycemia risk, its use is not recommended for individuals without prior insulin pump experience, as the safety profile has not been established in such populations. Additionally, the feature is disabled when SmartGuard mode is active, indicating a mode-specific functionality within the broader insulin delivery system. Overall, Suspend Before Low serves as a predictive, automated safety mechanism that integrates sensor data, user settings, and timely alerts to improve glycemic control and reduce the incidence of low glucose events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Check Connection Alert">
  <data key="d0">Check Connection Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The check connection alert appears when the pump fails to locate the transmitter signal after 15 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Check Connection Alert notifies the user when the pump fails to detect the transmitter and cannot receive sensor signals.&lt;SEP&gt;Check connection alert indicates a communication issue between the pump and sensor or transmitter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707253</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend On Low">
  <data key="d0">Suspend On Low</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend On Low is a safety feature designed to automatically suspend or stop insulin delivery when sensor glucose (SG) levels reach or fall below a predefined low threshold. This function is integrated into insulin pump systems, including the MiniMed 780G, and operates primarily in Manual mode when continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) is active. The threshold for activation is user-defined, ensuring personalized glucose management based on individual patient settings. Once triggered, the feature halts basal insulin delivery to prevent further decline in glucose levels, serving as a protective mechanism against hypoglycemia.

The Suspend On Low feature includes additional safety protocols: it prevents the silencing of the Alert On Low function while active, ensuring that users remain aware of low glucose events. It is intended for use only after established pump settings have been confirmed, emphasizing the importance of proper system configuration. Notably, Suspend On Low cannot operate simultaneously with the Suspend Before Low feature, and it is automatically disabled when the SmartGuard feature is active, indicating interdependencies with other advanced control algorithms within the insulin delivery system. As an automated response, it provides a critical layer of safety by intervening when low glucose levels are confirmed by the sensor, thereby reducing the risk of severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707254</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Failed To Start Alert">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Failed To Start Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This alert occurs when the sensor is unable to detect interstitial fluid and begin the warm-up process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Glucose Not Available Alert">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Glucose Not Available Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This alert indicates that sensor glucose values are not available, requiring user action such as BG checks or sensor replacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Failed BG Check Alert">
  <data key="d0">Failed BG Check Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Failed BG Check Alert appears when the system cannot use the entered blood glucose meter readings to verify performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Failed BG check alert notifies the user when a blood glucose measurement could not be completed.&lt;SEP&gt;Failed BG Check Alert signals an unsuccessful blood glucose verification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707256</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Sensor Alert">
  <data key="d0">Change Sensor Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The change sensor alert appears when the sensor is not functioning properly or is not securely connected, prompting replacement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Change Sensor Alert prompts the user to replace the sensor, typically after failed calibration attempts or persistent signal issues.&lt;SEP&gt;The Change Sensor Alert prompts the user to discard the current sensor and insert a new one, typically due to calibration issues or sensor failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Change sensor alert prompts the user to replace the glucose sensor after its lifespan ends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707258</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enter BG Now Alert">
  <data key="d0">Enter BG Now Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enter BG Now Alert appears when SG readings may be inaccurate or when no SG data has been received for more than 5 minutes, prompting immediate user action.&lt;SEP&gt;The Enter BG Now Alert requires the user to input a blood glucose value to calibrate or restore sensor glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Enter BG now alert prompts the user to input a blood glucose value for calibration or bolus calculation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High SG Alert">
  <data key="d0">High SG Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A High SG alert notifies the user when sensor glucose reaches or approaches a high limit, rises rapidly, or is predicted to exceed the limit.&lt;SEP&gt;High SG Alert is a non-silenceable notification triggered when sensor glucose exceeds 250 mg/dL for more than three hours.&lt;SEP&gt;High SG Alert is a critical alert for high sensor glucose levels that remains active even when All Sensor Alerts are silenced.&lt;SEP&gt;The High SG Alert is triggered when sensor glucose levels are abnormally high, indicating a potential medical concern.&lt;SEP&gt;The High SG Alert is triggered when sensor glucose reaches 250 mg/dL or higher for more than three hours, prompting user action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Software Update">
  <data key="d0">Pump Software Update</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pump Software Update is a process that updates the firmware of the insulin pump using the MiniMed Mobile App, requiring a stable internet connection and specific preparation steps including suspending insulin delivery and disconnecting the infusion set.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump software update is a procedure performed via the MiniMed Mobile App to upgrade the MiniMed 780G insulin pump's software.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707260</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Warm Up">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Warm Up</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Warm Up is a 1-hour period during which the Instinct sensor prepares to send glucose readings to the pump, indicated by a message on the pump screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor warm up is a process that takes time before the pump begins receiving SG readings from the sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sensor Warm Up is a two-hour initialization period during which the glucose sensor prepares for accurate readings, with a message displayed until completion.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor warm up is a two-hour initialization period after starting a new sensor, during which the pump prepares to receive glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707260</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Software Update Installation">
  <data key="d0">Software Update Installation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Software Update Installation is a 10-minute process during which the pump updates its software, suspends insulin delivery, and does not display sensor glucose values for up to 20 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707260</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Kit">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Kit</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An emergency kit for diabetes management should include rapid-acting glucose, BG testing supplies, ketone monitoring supplies, extra infusion sets, reservoirs, batteries, insulin syringes, short- and long-acting insulin, adhesive dressings, and glucagon, kept available and unexpired.&lt;SEP&gt;The Emergency Kit contains necessary supplies for backup insulin delivery and is referenced as a resource in case of pump malfunction during software updates.&lt;SEP&gt;The emergency kit is a collection that should include spare batteries and other essential supplies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200c1e93d7f4cbc3027cec4d0898dc00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707260</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wi-Fi">
  <data key="d0">Wi-Fi</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Wi-Fi is a wireless networking technology used to connect the MiniMed Mobile App to the internet during the pump software update process, with a caution against using unsecure or public networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707261</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Stopped Screen">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Stopped Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus Stopped screen displays the amount of insulin delivered and the originally programmed bolus amount after stopping a bolus.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d536bf636b4a29c1f9f46de648b2b306</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707262</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="24-Hour Technical Support">
  <data key="d0">24-Hour Technical Support</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">24-Hour Technical Support is a service provided by Medtronic to offer round-the-clock assistance for technical issues related to the MiniMed insulin pump system, including the insulin pump and integrated continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) devices. This support service is designed to help users resolve a wide range of device-related concerns, such as error messages, unexpected pump behavior, recurring alarms, unlisted alerts, and malfunctions that occur during system testing or data downloads. It is specifically recommended when issues persist despite troubleshooting, including RF interference affecting the MiniMed 780G system or other connectivity problems between device components.

The service provides comprehensive technical assistance for both hardware and software issues, including those caused by external factors such as exposure to magnetic fields or water damage. Users can contact 24-Hour Technical Support for help with device troubleshooting, resolving critical pump errors, and addressing problems related to sensor functionality, sensor connectivity, and proper disposal of sensor components. Additionally, the support team assists with issues involving CGM device alerts, data transmission failures, and unresolved technical difficulties that impact the overall performance of the pump and sensor systems.

24-Hour Technical Support ensures immediate access to expert guidance for urgent or complex technical challenges, emphasizing timely resolution of pump-related issues, error correction, and system optimization. As a dedicated resource available at all times, it plays a critical role in maintaining the safety, reliability, and effectiveness of Medtronic’s diabetes management technologies for users who depend on consistent device performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d536bf636b4a29c1f9f46de648b2b306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Reset To Zero Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Reset To Zero Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">This alarm resets active insulin tracking to zero and affects Bolus Wizard calculations, requiring user caution.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;This alarm occurs when active insulin is reset to zero due to pump shutdown, error, or manual clearance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d536bf636b4a29c1f9f46de648b2b306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Failed To Pair">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Failed To Pair</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Failed To Pair is an alert indicating that the sensor could not be successfully paired with the pump, requiring user action to resolve.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert indicating that the CGM sensor failed to establish a connection with the pump during pairing, requiring user intervention to restart the process.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Grace Period Starting Soon">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Grace Period Starting Soon</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert notifying the user that the sensor's grace period is about to begin, with less than a specified number of hours remaining before it starts, prompting preparation for sensor replacement.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Simplera Sync">
  <data key="d0">Simplera Sync</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Simplera Sync is a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) system or device designed to integrate with insulin pump technology, particularly referenced in conjunction with the MiniMed 780G system. It functions as a sensor component that enables real-time glucose monitoring by transmitting sensor data wirelessly to a compatible insulin pump, supporting automated insulin delivery. The system is involved in sensor data transmission, alerts, and synchronization processes, facilitating seamless communication between the CGM sensor and the pump.

There is some variation in the described technical requirements for calibration. Some sources indicate that Simplera Sync does not require manual calibration, operating as a factory-calibrated system when used with the MiniMed 780G. In contrast, other descriptions state that it requires blood glucose meter readings for calibration, suggesting either differing configurations, potential inconsistencies in documentation, or confusion with other systems. This discrepancy may reflect different operational modes or updates to the technology over time.

Simplera Sync is also described as a feature or process related to synchronizing data between the CGM device and associated systems, particularly during sensor pairing and ongoing monitoring. It supports wireless communication between the sensor and the insulin pump, enabling alerts for calibration needs, pairing status, and signal interruptions. As part of a broader CGM ecosystem, Simplera Sync plays a key role in ensuring reliable glucose data transmission, user alerts, and system interoperability, contributing to effective diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707269</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Signal Not Found">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Signal Not Found</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert triggered when the pump is unable to detect the sensor signal after multiple attempts, instructing the user to check the connection and contact technical support if unresolved.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Signal Not Found indicates that the pump is unable to receive data from the glucose sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707269</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Still Calibrating">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Still Calibrating</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert indicating that the sensor is still in the calibration phase after multiple blood glucose entries, requiring the user to wait at least 30 minutes for calibration to complete.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Still Calibrating indicates that the glucose sensor is in the process of calibration and not yet fully operational.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707270</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Too Hot">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Too Hot</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert generated when the CGM device temperature exceeds the safe operating threshold, making glucose readings unavailable until the device is moved to a cooler environment.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Too Hot is an alert indicating that the glucose sensor is operating above its functional temperature range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707270</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Too Cold">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Too Cold</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert generated when the CGM device temperature falls below the minimum operating threshold, making glucose readings unavailable until the device is moved to a warmer environment.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Too Cold is an alert indicating that the glucose sensor is operating below its functional temperature range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707271</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Updating">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Updating</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert indicating that the sensor is undergoing quality checks, temporarily pausing glucose readings, with instructions to wait for at least 30 minutes before normal operation resumes.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Updating indicates that the glucose sensor is undergoing a software or firmware update.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707272</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb Amount">
  <data key="d0">Carb Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carb amount refers to the quantity of carbohydrates in food, entered to calculate an appropriate insulin bolus.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed 780G System">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed 780G System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed 780G System is an advanced insulin pump system designed for diabetes management, integrating automated insulin delivery with continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) to support effective blood glucose control. It functions as a medical device that delivers insulin through a pump, utilizes a CGM device for real-time glucose tracking, and includes a reservoir for insulin storage. The system operates using specific rapid-acting U-100 insulins and requires compatible components to ensure safe and accurate performance.

A key feature of the MiniMed 780G System is SmartGuard technology, which enables automatic basal insulin delivery and administers correction boluses when glucose levels exceed preset thresholds. This automated dosing system adjusts insulin delivery every five minutes based on CGM readings, aiming to keep glucose levels within a target range. The system also supports advanced bolus features such as Bolus Wizard, which calculates insulin doses based on current glucose levels, carbohydrate intake, and active insulin, as well as Square Wave Bolus for extended insulin delivery. These functions operate under defined settings, including Active Insulin Time, to ensure precise dosing.

The MiniMed 780G System integrates with the MiniMed Mobile App, allowing users to monitor glucose data, receive alerts, and perform pump software updates. It generates various alarms and alerts to notify users of potential issues, such as high or low glucose levels, pump malfunctions, or sensor inaccuracies. The CGM component uses blood glucose readings for calibration and performance verification, ensuring reliable data for insulin adjustments. Additionally, the device generates and uses radio frequency energy, necessitating proper handling to avoid interference.

Designed for long-term insulin pump therapy, the MiniMed 780G System requires regular care and maintenance to ensure optimal functionality and safety. It is intended for use under medical supervision and as part of a comprehensive diabetes management plan. By combining automated insulin delivery, real-time glucose monitoring, and digital connectivity, the MiniMed 780G System offers a cohesive solution for individuals seeking improved glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b0e9023a7c03c6a284d69e0930b8a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adjustment Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Adjustment Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An adjustment bolus is a modified insulin dose, adjusted up or down by the SmartGuard feature based on predicted glucose trends.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deliver Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Deliver Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deliver Bolus is the function that initiates the insulin dose delivery after bolus calculations are complete.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Deliver Bolus is the action that initiates insulin delivery after a bolus amount and duration have been set.&lt;SEP&gt;Deliver Bolus is the command that initiates the delivery of a selected preset bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707283</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stop Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Stop Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stop Bolus is an option available during bolus delivery that allows the user to halt the active bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Stop Bolus is a feature used to halt bolus insulin delivery, accessed through the Insulin menu.&lt;SEP&gt;Stop Bolus is a function that allows the user to halt an ongoing bolus delivery.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707283</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Correction Feature">
  <data key="d0">Auto Correction Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Auto Correction feature automatically adjusts insulin delivery based on glucose levels, but is inactive during a temp target.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707283</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="150 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">150 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">150 mg/dL is the temporary glucose target level set during a temp target, such as for exercise, to reduce insulin delivery.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30g Carbs">
  <data key="d0">30g Carbs</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">30g carbs is a saved carbohydrate amount used in future bolus adjustment calculations by the SmartGuard feature.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="15g Carbs">
  <data key="d0">15g Carbs</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">15g carbs is a saved carbohydrate amount used in future bolus adjustment calculations after a reduced bolus.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="18g Carbs">
  <data key="d0">18g Carbs</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">18g carbs is a saved carbohydrate amount used in future bolus adjustment calculations after an increased bolus.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2.5 U">
  <data key="d0">2.5 U</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">2.5 U is the insulin amount of a bolus that was started, as displayed on the device screen.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707286</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.5 U">
  <data key="d0">0.5 U</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">0.5 U is the adjustment amount added to a bolus when a correction is calculated based on high glucose and low active insulin.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2.3 U">
  <data key="d0">2.3 U</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">2.3 U is the insulin amount of a bolus that was started, as displayed on the device screen.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707288</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lost Sensor Signal Alert">
  <data key="d0">Lost Sensor Signal Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Lost Sensor Signal Alert appears when the pump loses communication with the sensor, indicating a need for user intervention to restore SG data flow.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sensor Signal Alert appears after 30 minutes without a sensor signal and prompts troubleshooting steps.&lt;SEP&gt;The lost sensor signal alert appears on the pump screen after 30 minutes without a signal from the sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sensor Signal Alert occurs when the CGM device fails to send a signal to the pump for up to 30 minutes, requiring repositioning of the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Lost Sensor Signal Alert is a notification that the pump has lost connection with the glucose sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707289</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Battery Transmitter Alert">
  <data key="d0">Low Battery Transmitter Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Low Battery Transmitter Alert indicates the transmitter battery needs recharging within 24 hours to maintain CGM functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Low Battery Transmitter Alert indicates low power in the glucose monitoring transmitter, referenced on page 322.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707289</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Basal Rate">
  <data key="d0">Max Basal Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Max Basal Rate is the highest allowable basal insulin delivery rate programmed in the pump for safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Max basal rate is the user-defined maximum number of basal insulin units per hour that can be set, with warnings issued for values above 6 U/hr and special procedures for values above 10 U/hr.&lt;SEP&gt;Max Basal Rate is the upper limit for both basal and temp basal insulin delivery rates, constraining the maximum amount of insulin that can be delivered per hour.&lt;SEP&gt;Max Basal Rate defines the upper limit of insulin delivery per hour in Manual mode, adjustable through the Manage Settings menu.&lt;SEP&gt;Max Basal Rate is a pump setting that defines the maximum basal insulin delivery rate, which cannot be set lower than existing basal rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Max basal rate is a user-configurable setting that defines the maximum amount of background insulin delivered by the pump per hour.&lt;SEP&gt;The maximum amount of basal insulin that can be programmed by the user per hour in Manual mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707291</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Basal Message">
  <data key="d0">Max Basal Message</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Max Basal Message is a notification indicating that the Max basal rate setting is being changed, prompting user confirmation or cancellation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Max Basal Message appears when the maximum basal rate setting is being changed, requiring user confirmation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Basal Error Alert">
  <data key="d0">Max Basal Error Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Max Basal Error Alert is triggered when a user attempts to set the Max basal rate lower than an existing basal rate, requiring resolution before proceeding.&lt;SEP&gt;The Max Basal Error Alert occurs when an invalid or incorrect attempt is made to change the maximum basal rate setting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed 780G">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed 780G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed 780G is an insulin pump system designed for diabetes management, featuring SmartGuard and Predictive Low Glucose technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed 780G is an insulin pump system that provides detailed therapy history, including insulin delivery, glucose readings, and alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;MiniMed 780G is an insulin pump model designed for users aged 7-13 and integrates with CGM systems for automated insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temp Target">
  <data key="d0">Temp Target</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temp Target is a temporary glucose target feature within insulin pump systems, particularly those equipped with SmartGuard technology, designed to allow users to adjust insulin delivery in response to specific physiological or situational needs. It enables individuals with diabetes to set a temporary glucose goal—commonly 150 mg/dL for a defined duration, such as two to eight hours—during events like exercise, illness, or when taking medications such as acetaminophen (also known as paracetamol). By modifying the target glucose level, the system adapts its insulin delivery algorithm to reduce the amount of insulin administered, which is beneficial when less insulin is required or when sensor accuracy may be compromised.

The Temp Target function is particularly recommended during acetaminophen use, as this medication can interfere with continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor readings, potentially leading to inaccurate insulin dosing. Setting a Temp Target during such periods enhances safety by preventing overcorrection with insulin due to falsely elevated glucose readings. Additionally, during physical activity or illness, metabolic demands shift, and the Temp Target allows for proactive management by pausing auto-correction boluses and adjusting basal insulin delivery accordingly. This temporary setting is visually represented in some systems as green runners on the glucose trend graph, providing clear user feedback.

Overall, the Temp Target serves as a customizable, time-limited adjustment tool that influences the behavior of automated insulin delivery systems, improving both safety and efficacy in dynamic health situations. It reflects a user-initiated, context-sensitive control mechanism that supports more personalized diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plunger">
  <data key="d0">Plunger</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The plunger is a component of the reservoir that can be twisted to loosen or remove it.&lt;SEP&gt;The Plunger is a mechanical component inside the insulin reservoir used to push insulin during delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Menu Screen">
  <data key="d0">Menu Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Menu Screen provides navigation options for accessing various pump settings and features.&lt;SEP&gt;The Menu Screen allows navigation to various system functions such as insulin delivery, history, SmartGuard setup, and settings.&lt;SEP&gt;The menu screen is an interface on the pump that allows users to navigate system functions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Menu Screen is the pump's interface where users can select options such as Reservoir &amp; Set to begin a new reservoir setup.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG">
  <data key="d0">BG</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">BG refers to blood glucose, a critical metabolic parameter representing the concentration of glucose present in the bloodstream. It is commonly measured using a blood glucose meter, often referred to as a BG meter, and is typically displayed in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL). Accurate measurement of BG is essential for individuals managing diabetes, as it provides real-time insight into their current metabolic and diabetic state.

BG levels play a central role in the operation of insulin pump systems, where they are used both for calibration of continuous glucose monitoring sensors and for ongoing monitoring of glycemic control. Users are frequently instructed to check their BG when specific alarms are triggered by the device, ensuring that any deviations in glucose levels are promptly assessed and addressed. These checks are vital for evaluating the immediate diabetic condition and determining appropriate clinical responses.

Furthermore, BG readings directly inform critical treatment decisions, particularly regarding insulin delivery. Before administering a bolus of insulin, users review current BG levels to ensure accurate dosing and avoid adverse events such as hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia. The integration of BG data into insulin pump systems enables more precise and personalized diabetes management, supporting both calibration processes and therapeutic decision-making. Overall, BG serves as a foundational metric in the safe and effective use of diabetes technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Checkmark">
  <data key="d0">Checkmark</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The checkmark is a visual indicator on the pump screen that signals completion of a step.</data>
