  <data key="d5">1778707295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Set User Guide">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Set User Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion set user guide provides instructions for inserting and using the infusion set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serter User Guide">
  <data key="d0">Serter User Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The serter user guide provides instructions for using a device that assists in inserting the infusion set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CareLink Uploader">
  <data key="d0">CareLink Uploader</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The CareLink uploader is a device or software that provides instructions related to the pump’s operation or status.&lt;SEP&gt;The CareLink uploader is a device used to transfer data from the insulin pump to the CareLink software.&lt;SEP&gt;The CareLink Uploader is a tool that provides instructions for uploading device data to CareLink software.&lt;SEP&gt;CareLink Uploader is a device or software used to transfer pump data, with a message indicating it was not found, referenced on page 325.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Data">
  <data key="d0">Pump Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump data refers to the information collected from an insulin pump that can be downloaded for review and analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Download Slow Alert">
  <data key="d0">Download Slow Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Download Slow Alert indicates that data transfer from the pump to CareLink may take longer than usual, though insulin delivery is unaffected.&lt;SEP&gt;The Download Slow Alert indicates that the transfer of pump data is taking longer than expected, though data integrity is not compromised.&lt;SEP&gt;Download slow alert appears during data transfer via CareLink when the connection speed is below expected levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temp Basal">
  <data key="d0">Temp Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temp Basal is a feature that allows the user to set a temporary basal insulin rate for a specified duration, either as a percentage or a fixed rate, to manage short-term changes in blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Temp Basal is a temporary adjustment to the basal insulin delivery rate for a specified period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend All Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Suspend All Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend All Delivery stops all insulin delivery; this option is available on the Status screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend all delivery is a function that stops both basal and bolus insulin delivery, with reminders every 15 minutes until insulin delivery resumes.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend All Delivery is a feature that stops both basal and bolus insulin delivery, distinct from stopping only bolus delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend All Delivery is a feature that stops all insulin delivery, accessed via the Home Screen, distinct from stopping only a bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend All Delivery is a function that stops all insulin delivery from the pump, with the option to resume later.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="History &amp; Graph">
  <data key="d0">History &amp; Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">History &amp; Graph is a feature that displays historical data and graphical trends of insulin delivery, glucose levels, and other metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Glucose Review">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Glucose Review</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Glucose Review is a feature that displays sensor glucose data with high and low limits for analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Glucose Review allows users to view and analyze continuous glucose monitoring data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sound &amp; Vibration">
  <data key="d0">Sound &amp; Vibration</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sound &amp; Vibration are alert mechanisms used by the device to notify the user of events or conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Settings">
  <data key="d0">Alert Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert settings determine how the pump notifies the user, including sound and vibration options.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Settings is a menu where users configure various glucose-related alerts, including High Alert and Snooze High &amp; Low.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Settings is a menu option accessible from the Home screen that allows users to configure High Snooze and Low SG alert parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Settings is a menu where users configure reminders and notification preferences on the device.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Settings is a menu option where users configure various types of reminders and notifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Settings is a menu within the pump system where users configure reminders and notifications, including the Set Change reminder.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Settings allow users to configure notifications for various device conditions such as high or low glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Settings">
  <data key="d0">Device Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Device settings refer to the configuration options for the insulin pump, including sound, vibration, and alert settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Device Settings is a menu option that allows users to access and manage various pump configurations including self test and settings management.&lt;SEP&gt;Device Settings is a menu accessible from the Home Screen where users can configure features like Easy Bolus and set parameters such as Step Size.&lt;SEP&gt;Device Settings include configurations for pump operation, including time, date, language, and system preferences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired Devices">
  <data key="d0">Paired Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Paired Devices is a screen listing all currently connected devices, allowing users to manage connections.&lt;SEP&gt;Paired Devices refers to the list of compatible external devices connected to the pump, limited by device type.&lt;SEP&gt;Paired Devices are external devices such as meters or CGMs that are connected and synchronized with the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservoir &amp; Set">
  <data key="d0">Reservoir &amp; Set</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Reservoir &amp; Set is a menu option used to initiate the process of installing a new reservoir and infusion set after a rewind or error.&lt;SEP&gt;Reservoir &amp; Set refers to the component of the insulin pump that holds and delivers insulin, requiring periodic replacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glossary">
  <data key="d0">Glossary</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The glossary contains definitions of terms and acronyms used in the MiniMed 780G user guide.&lt;SEP&gt;The Glossary provides definitions for technical terms and acronyms used in the device documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ACE">
  <data key="d0">ACE</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ACE is an acronym for Alternate Controller Enabled, indicating compatibility with external control devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Activity Guard">
  <data key="d0">Activity Guard</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The activity guard is an optional accessory that helps prevent the reservoir from being rotated or removed from the MiniMed 780G insulin pump during physical activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Activity Guard is an attachment designed to secure the insulin reservoir during physical activity or when used by children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OK">
  <data key="d0">OK</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">OK is a button or selection option used to confirm actions such as clearing messages or alerts on the device interface.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Appendix B">
  <data key="d0">Appendix B</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Appendix B provides a menu map detailing the navigation structure and available features of the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG History">
  <data key="d0">SG History</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">SG History refers to the historical data of sensor glucose readings used for review and analysis on the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG Review Screen">
  <data key="d0">SG Review Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">interface</data>
  <data key="d2">The SG Review Screen allows users to view historical sensor glucose data and trends.&lt;SEP&gt;The SG Review Screen displays sensor glucose data and allows users to set high and low limits for review.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Limit">
  <data key="d0">High Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">High Limit is a user-configurable threshold for sensor glucose, set between 100 and 400 mg/dL, used to trigger high SG alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;High Limit is a user-defined glucose threshold ranging from 100 to 400 mg/dL in 5 mg/dL increments, used to trigger high glucose alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;High Limit is a user-defined threshold value in mg/dL used to define the upper boundary for sensor glucose data review.&lt;SEP&gt;High Limit is a user-defined threshold for maximum acceptable sensor glucose levels, beyond which alerts or alarms are triggered.&lt;SEP&gt;The setting the insulin pump uses to determine when to alert for a high sensor glucose condition.&lt;SEP&gt;High limit is a user-defined threshold for maximum allowable glucose levels, associated with high SG alerts and settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Limit">
  <data key="d0">Low Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Low Limit is a user-defined threshold between 50 mg/dL and 90 mg/dL used as the basis for low SG alerts and Suspend by sensor features, configurable for up to eight time segments.&lt;SEP&gt;The low limit is the predefined threshold for sensor glucose below which an alert or suspension of insulin delivery is triggered.&lt;SEP&gt;Low Limit is a user-defined threshold value in mg/dL used to define the lower boundary for sensor glucose data review, with a default of 70 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;Low Limit is the predefined threshold for sensor glucose levels that triggers alerts or suspensions in insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Low Limit is a user-defined threshold for minimum acceptable sensor glucose levels, below which alerts or alarms are activated.&lt;SEP&gt;The setting the insulin pump uses to determine when to alert for a low sensor glucose condition and suspend insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Default High Limit">
  <data key="d0">Default High Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The default high limit for SG review is set at 180 mg/dL when no custom value is entered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Default Low Limit">
  <data key="d0">Default Low Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The default low limit for SG review is set at 70 mg/dL when no custom value is entered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Days to Average">
  <data key="d0">Days to Average</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Days to Average is a user-entered value that determines the number of days of SG history to include in the average analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph Screen">
  <data key="d0">Graph Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">interface</data>
  <data key="d2">The Graph Screen displays glucose trends over time using data from the CGM system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Graph Screen displays trends in sensor glucose readings, BG entries, bolus deliveries, and may show backfilled SG values as dotted lines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time in Range Screen">
  <data key="d0">Time in Range Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">interface</data>
  <data key="d2">The Time in Range Screen shows the percentage of time sensor glucose levels were within, above, or below the standard range over the last 24 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Before Low">
  <data key="d0">Alert Before Low</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert Before Low is a feature designed to notify users when sensor glucose levels are approaching a predefined low threshold, serving as an early warning system for potential hypoglycemia. This optional alert operates independently of other safety mechanisms such as Suspend Before Low, allowing users to enable it based on individual monitoring preferences. It functions by analyzing real-time glucose data and predicting when levels are likely to fall below the set limit, triggering a notification before the actual threshold is reached.

The primary purpose of Alert Before Low is to increase user awareness and facilitate timely intervention to prevent hypoglycemic events. It provides advance warning by detecting downward glucose trends, enabling individuals to take corrective actions such as consuming carbohydrates or adjusting insulin delivery. The alert is predictive in nature, relying on sensor glucose (SG) readings to anticipate future drops in blood glucose levels before they occur.

Alert Before Low enhances diabetes management by promoting proactive monitoring and reducing the risk of severe low glucose episodes. It is particularly useful during periods of increased insulin sensitivity, physical activity, or delayed meals, when hypoglycemia risk is elevated. By signaling that glucose levels are nearing the specified low limit, the feature supports continuous vigilance and informed decision-making in daily glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Alarms, Alerts, and Messages">
  <data key="d0">Pump Alarms, Alerts, and Messages</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">These are notifications generated by the MiniMed 780G pump to inform users of system status, errors, or required actions.&lt;SEP&gt;This refers to a section in the user guide that describes the meaning, consequences, reasons, and resolutions for common or serious device notifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Personal Reminders">
  <data key="d0">Personal Reminders</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Personal Reminders are customizable alerts that users can set for any purpose, with up to five allowed.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal Reminders are user-defined alerts for routine diabetes management tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Meter Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Meter Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific reminder prompting the user to perform a blood glucose meter reading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707311</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Medication Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific reminder prompting the user to take medication.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific reminder type for medication, part of the system's alert functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707311</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservoir Set Up">
  <data key="d0">Reservoir Set Up</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Reservoir Set Up is a process during which alerts do not appear on the MiniMed Mobile App, requiring reliance on the pump itself.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707311</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backfilled SG Values">
  <data key="d0">Backfilled SG Values</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Backfilled SG values are estimated glucose readings represented by a dotted line on the sensor graph, recorded when the sensor is out of wireless range from the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Backfilled SG Values are historical glucose readings added to the sensor graph when data was previously missing due to connection issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Backfilled SG Values are sensor glucose readings recorded as dotted lines on the graph when the sensor is out of wireless range from the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707311</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tubing Connector">
  <data key="d0">Tubing Connector</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The tubing connector is a component of an insulin pump system that may be blocked by liquid, affecting pump function.&lt;SEP&gt;The tubing connector attaches the tubing to the reservoir in the infusion set.&lt;SEP&gt;The tubing connector attaches the infusion set tubing to the reservoir and must be locked in place by turning clockwise.&lt;SEP&gt;The tubing connector is part of the infusion set that should be inspected for damage.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tubing Connector is a component that links the insulin reservoir to the infusion set tubing in the pump system.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc61f77b003d0086bd985ddb94fc2a98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insertion Piece">
  <data key="d0">Insertion Piece</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The insertion piece is part of the infusion set that attaches to the body and includes the cannula or needle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Cap">
  <data key="d0">Battery Cap</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The battery cap secures the battery in the pump and must be properly tightened to ensure correct battery detection.&lt;SEP&gt;The battery cap covers and secures the AA battery in the pump and must be removed and reinstalled during troubleshooting.&lt;SEP&gt;The Battery Cap is a component of the MiniMed 780G insulin pump that requires periodic cleaning to remove battery residue using a dry, clean cotton swab.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707313</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AA Lithium Battery">
  <data key="d0">AA Lithium Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An AA lithium (FR6) battery is recommended for best performance in the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;AA lithium batteries are a type of power source recommended for use in the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707313</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AA Alkaline Battery">
  <data key="d0">AA Alkaline Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An AA alkaline (LR6) battery is compatible with the pump and can be used as a power source.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707313</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AA NiMH Battery">
  <data key="d0">AA NiMH Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An AA NiMH (HR6) nickel-metal hydride rechargeable battery is acceptable for use in the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707313</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbon Zinc Battery">
  <data key="d0">Carbon Zinc Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbon zinc batteries are not compatible with the pump and can cause inaccurate battery level reports.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Startup Wizard">
  <data key="d0">Startup Wizard</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Startup Wizard is a step-by-step setup process consisting of three stages: selecting time format, entering time, and entering date.&lt;SEP&gt;The Startup Wizard is a setup process that appears the first time a battery is inserted, guiding the user to set language, time format, time, date, and rewind the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The Startup Wizard is a guided setup process that appears after clearing all settings, allowing users to re-enter necessary pump configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Startup Wizard is a setup process used to re-enter personalized pump settings after a reset.&lt;SEP&gt;The Startup Wizard is a setup process that guides users through initial pump configuration and settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Startup Wizard is a setup guide used during initial pump configuration to input settings like date and delivery parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Startup Wizard is a guided setup process for initializing the insulin pump and configuring initial settings.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insert Battery Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Insert Battery Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Insert Battery alarm appears when a new battery needs to be inserted and must be cleared within 10 minutes to avoid a Power loss alarm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Occlusion Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Occlusion Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The occlusion alarm is triggered when there is a blockage in the infusion set, indicating a potential delivery issue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Reading">
  <data key="d0">BG Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">BG reading refers to blood glucose measurement obtained via a blood glucose meter to confirm insulin dosing accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;BG Reading displays the current blood glucose level from a meter on the Home screen.&lt;SEP&gt;A BG reading is a blood glucose measurement entered manually or requested by the system for calibration or verification.&lt;SEP&gt;A BG (blood glucose) reading is a measurement of current blood sugar levels that must be entered into the system for SmartGuard to function correctly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soft Cannula">
  <data key="d0">Soft Cannula</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">The soft cannula is part of the infusion set that may become dislodged, crimped, or partially clogged, requiring replacement.&lt;SEP&gt;The soft cannula is a flexible tube component of the infusion set that requires filling with insulin after insertion into the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG Value">
  <data key="d0">SG Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SG value refers to the sensor glucose reading obtained from a continuous glucose monitoring system, which may differ from blood glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;SG value refers to sensor glucose readings used by the pump to calculate insulin delivery when the SmartGuard feature is active.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vitamin C">
  <data key="d0">Vitamin C</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Vitamin C, when taken in excess of 1000 mg, can falsely raise glucose sensor readings and lead to incorrect insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707315</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydroxycarbamide">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxycarbamide</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxycarbamide is an alternative name for hydroxyurea, a medication that causes higher sensor glucose readings compared to blood glucose readings when using continuous glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxycarbamide is an alternative name for hydroxyurea, a medication that interferes with continuous glucose monitoring by causing falsely high sensor glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxycarbamide is an alternative name for hydroxyurea and is an active ingredient in certain medications that can impact glucose sensor accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707315</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stuck Button Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Stuck Button Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Stuck Button Alarm is triggered when a button on the pump has been pressed for more than 3 minutes, requiring user action to clear the alarm.&lt;SEP&gt;Stuck Button Alarm indicates that a physical button on the pump is being pressed continuously.&lt;SEP&gt;Stuck Button Alarm is a system alert indicating that a physical button on the pump is being pressed continuously, possibly due to mechanical failure or obstruction.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707315</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Very High Basal Alert">
  <data key="d0">Very High Basal Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Very High Basal Alert warns that the current basal insulin setting delivers significantly more insulin than typically needed, posing potential safety risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Very High Basal Alert is triggered when a basal pattern delivers significantly more insulin than typically required, indicating a potential safety risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707316</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Mode Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Manual Mode Basal Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual Mode Basal Pattern refers to a user-defined insulin delivery schedule that may trigger alerts if deemed unsafe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707316</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Before High">
  <data key="d0">Alert Before High</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert Before High provides a warning when sensor glucose is predicted to reach the high limit within a specified time.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Before High allows users to receive a warning before the glucose level reaches the set high limit, with a configurable time interval.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Before High is a predictive alert that warns of an impending high glucose level before it reaches the preset threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;The Alert Before High notifies the user that sensor glucose levels are approaching the specified high limit, prompting blood glucose checks.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Before High is a predictive warning that blood glucose levels are expected to rise above the target range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707316</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert On High">
  <data key="d0">Alert On High</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert On High is triggered when sensor glucose reaches or exceeds the user-defined high limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert On High is a notification triggered when glucose levels reach a preset high threshold, part of the High &amp; Low Alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Alert On High is triggered when sensor glucose reaches or exceeds the defined high limit, signaling the need for immediate monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert On High is a notification triggered when blood glucose levels exceed a predefined threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert On Low">
  <data key="d0">Alert On Low</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert On Low is a feature that triggers a pump alert when sensor glucose (SG) reaches or falls below the low limit, supporting Suspend Before Low and Suspend On Low.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert On Low is an alert that activates when sensor glucose falls below the preset low value; it is automatically enabled if Suspend Before Low is turned on.&lt;SEP&gt;An Alert on low occurs when sensor glucose reaches the low limit, indicating a current low glucose condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert On Low is a notification activated when glucose levels drop to a preset low value, and cannot be silenced if Suspend Before Low or Suspend On Low is enabled.&lt;SEP&gt;The Alert On Low occurs when sensor glucose drops to or below the defined low limit, prompting the user to check blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert that occurs when the SG reading reaches or falls below the low limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert On Low is a notification triggered when blood glucose levels fall below a predefined threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Delivery Resumed">
  <data key="d0">Basal Delivery Resumed</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal Delivery Resumed indicates that the pump has restarted basal insulin delivery after a suspension event caused by low glucose detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal Delivery Resumed is an alert indicating that the delivery of basal insulin has restarted after a pause.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Delivery Suspended">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Delivery Suspended</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Delivery Suspended is an alarm state where the pump halts insulin delivery due to a detected low glucose level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Check">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Check</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose Check is a recommended action following glucose-related alerts to verify sensor readings using a traditional blood test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Page 284">
  <data key="d0">Page 284</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 284 contains information about pump issues and is referenced as a resource for resolving alarms that cannot be cleared.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clear Active Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Clear Active Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Clear Active Insulin resets the active insulin value to zero and clears SmartGuard therapy history, necessary when using the pump with insulin for the first time.&lt;SEP&gt;Clear Active Insulin is a one-time function that resets the active insulin amount in the pump system.&lt;SEP&gt;Clear Active Insulin is a feature on the Manage Settings screen that resets the active insulin count to zero.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Graph">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Graph is a visual representation of glucose trends over time derived from continuous glucose monitoring data.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sensor Graph visually represents glucose trends over time, showing current and historical SG readings, correction bolus events, carb entries, BG entries, and the desired glucose range as a green band.&lt;SEP&gt;The sensor graph is a visual display showing historical and current sensor glucose readings, trend arrows, carb entries, boluses, suspend events, and high/low limits.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Graph is a visual display showing glucose levels over time, used to review recent bolus effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor graph visually displays glucose trends over time from CGM data on the pump screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Graph is a visual representation of glucose trends over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Suspend">
  <data key="d0">Auto Suspend</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Suspend is a safety feature that stops insulin delivery and triggers an alarm if no user input is received within a set time.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Suspend is a pump feature that automatically stops insulin delivery when no buttons are pressed for a set period.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature that suspends insulin delivery and triggers an alarm if no buttons are pressed for the specified period of time; insulin delivery resumes when the alarm is cleared.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Suspend is a feature that automatically pauses insulin delivery under certain conditions, such as low glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Screen">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus Screen allows the user to deliver insulin doses and varies depending on the active bolus feature; accessible via a shortcut from the Home screen.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Screen is a pump interface used to enter and deliver insulin boluses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manage Settings Screen">
  <data key="d0">Manage Settings Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Manage Settings Screen is a menu on the pump where users can access the Clear Active Insulin option.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Feature">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sensor Feature is a system function integral to continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) in diabetes management systems, particularly those integrated with insulin pumps. When activated, this feature enables the device to monitor glucose levels in real time by receiving data from a paired sensor transmitter. The activation of the Sensor Feature is contingent upon successful communication between the sensor transmitter and the insulin pump, establishing a functional CGM system.

Once enabled, the Sensor Feature significantly influences the device's interface and operational capabilities. It modifies the Home screen display to include glucose data and alerts, and it unlocks access to a range of configurable sensor-based settings. These include thresholds for high and low sensor glucose (SG) levels, customizable alerts, and advanced functions such as automated insulin suspension in response to hypoglycemic trends. Without the Sensor Feature activated, these configurations remain inaccessible, limiting the system’s ability to respond dynamically to glucose fluctuations.

The Sensor Feature is essential for the effective operation of CGM-dependent functionalities, ensuring timely glucose readings and therapeutic responses. However, its use requires careful consideration in specific medical contexts. For instance, the feature must be deactivated when patients are undergoing treatment with certain medications, such as hydroxyurea, which are known to interfere with sensor accuracy and potentially lead to unreliable glucose readings. Proper management of the Sensor Feature is therefore critical to maintaining both the safety and efficacy of the integrated diabetes care system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Reminder Message">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Reminder Message</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">This message appears when the Bolus Wizard or Manual Bolus screen is accessed before the time indicated in the reminder.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Failed Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Battery Failed Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Battery Failed Alarm indicates the pump's battery is low and needs replacement.&lt;SEP&gt;Battery failed alarm signals a critical power issue requiring immediate battery replacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Not Compatible Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Battery Not Compatible Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">This alarm occurs when a non-compatible battery is inserted into the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Battery not compatible alarm warns that the installed battery does not meet pump specifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Not Delivered Alert">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Not Delivered Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">This alert appears when a bolus entry times out and no insulin is delivered within 30 seconds.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus not delivered alert notifies the user when an intended bolus was not administered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Stopped Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Stopped Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus Stopped Alarm indicates that a bolus delivery was interrupted and cannot be resumed.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus stopped alarm indicates that a bolus delivery was interrupted before completion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KJ">
  <data key="d0">KJ</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">KJ is a status indicator displayed on the Home Screen and Bolus Screens after the Active Insulin reset to zero alarm, visible until the time specified in the alarm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Silence Feature">
  <data key="d0">Alert Silence Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Alert Silence Feature allows users to temporarily mute sensor alerts without disabling them permanently.&lt;SEP&gt;The Alert Silence Feature allows certain sensor alerts to be silenced for a set period of time, reducing interruptions while maintaining system functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;The Alert silence feature temporarily silences specific sensor alerts on the insulin pump for a defined duration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Basal Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Auto Basal Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto basal deliveries are continuous insulin doses adjusted by the SmartGuard feature based on sensor glucose trends.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Basal delivery is an automated insulin delivery function that adjusts basal insulin rates based on sensor glucose values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Correction Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Auto Correction Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An Auto Correction bolus is an automatically delivered insulin dose by the pump to correct high glucose levels, aiming to maximize time in the target glucose range.&lt;SEP&gt;An auto correction bolus is an insulin dose automatically delivered by the SmartGuard feature to bring glucose levels into the desired range.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto correction bolus is a feature that automatically delivers corrective insulin doses when blood glucose levels are outside the target range, if enabled.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Display Options">
  <data key="d0">Display Options</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Display Options allow users to customize the appearance and visibility of information on the pump screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Display options are settings on the insulin pump that allow users to adjust screen timeout and other visual preferences.&lt;SEP&gt;Display options allow users to adjust screen brightness and backlight timeout duration on the MiniMed 780G insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Display options allow users to adjust the display timeout duration on the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brightness">
  <data key="d0">Brightness</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Brightness refers to the screen luminance level of the insulin pump, adjustable from 1 to 5 or set to Auto for environmental adaptation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backlight Timeout">
  <data key="d0">Backlight Timeout</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Backlight timeout determines how long the pump screen remains lit after user inactivity, with options of 15 seconds, 30 seconds, 1 minute, or 3 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Glucose Value">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Glucose Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Glucose Value refers to glucose readings from a sensor, which should not be used in place of blood glucose meter readings in the Bolus Wizard.&lt;SEP&gt;A Sensor Glucose Value is a glucose reading from a continuous glucose monitoring system, which should not be used in place of a blood glucose meter reading for Bolus Wizard calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor glucose (SG) values are real-time glucose readings received by the MiniMed 780G insulin pump from a connected glucose sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor glucose (SG) value is derived from continuous glucose monitoring but should not be used for bolus delivery in Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;A glucose reading from a continuous glucose monitoring system, which should not be used for bolus delivery in Manual mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Meter Reading">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Meter Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose Meter Reading is a value obtained from a blood glucose meter used to calibrate the sensor or verify system performance, distinct from sensor glucose values.&lt;SEP&gt;A Blood Glucose Meter Reading is a measured value of blood glucose (in mg/dL) obtained from a glucose meter, used by the Bolus Wizard for calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;A blood glucose (BG) meter reading is a manually entered value from a glucometer used to calibrate the sensor or verify system accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose (BG) meter readings are manual glucose measurements that can be entered and accepted by the MiniMed 780G insulin pump for calibration or verification.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose (BG) meter reading is the measured value of blood glucose used for bolus calculations in Manual mode, required instead of sensor glucose values.&lt;SEP&gt;A measured value of blood glucose that must be entered when delivering a bolus in Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;A blood glucose meter reading is a measurement between 50 mg/dL and 400 mg/dL used to calibrate certain CGM sensors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Lock">
  <data key="d0">Pump Lock</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump lock is the state activated when Block mode is enabled and the pump enters sleep mode, restricting access to critical functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Manual Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual Bolus is a user-initiated insulin delivery feature available on insulin pumps, specifically designed to allow individuals to manually set and administer a bolus dose without relying on the Bolus Wizard or other automated dose calculation tools. This function provides full user control over insulin administration, enabling the delivery of a specified amount of insulin directly through the pump interface. It is accessible only in Manual mode, emphasizing user-defined dosing rather than algorithm-assisted recommendations.

The Manual Bolus feature supports multiple types of bolus delivery to accommodate varying insulin needs. These include the standard normal bolus, which delivers the full dose immediately, as well as extended options such as the Square Wave bolus, which administers the dose evenly over a set period, and the Dual Wave bolus, which combines an immediate bolus with a delayed, extended component. The availability of Dual Wave and Square Wave boluses within the Manual Bolus function depends on whether these advanced features are enabled on the device.

By allowing direct input and delivery of insulin doses, Manual Bolus serves as a flexible tool for individuals who prefer to calculate their insulin requirements independently, using external methods or personal judgment. It is referenced in user documentation, specifically on pages 94 and 104, highlighting its role in the broader operation of the insulin pump. Overall, Manual Bolus enhances user autonomy in diabetes management by providing immediate, customizable insulin delivery options without computational assistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Setting History">
  <data key="d0">Pump Setting History</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Setting History is a record of previous configurations and changes made to the insulin pump settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daily History Screen">
  <data key="d0">Daily History Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Daily History Screen displays a summary of daily insulin delivery, glucose readings, and related events.&lt;SEP&gt;The Daily History Screen is a feature of the insulin pump system that displays historical delivery data, including bolus amounts delivered and intended, used for review and recalibration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Daily History Screen displays historical insulin delivery data, including details of stopped boluses.&lt;SEP&gt;The Daily History Screen provides additional information related to insulin delivery and usage, referenced on page 227.&lt;SEP&gt;The Daily History Screen displays a chronological list of pump actions and events for a selected day, with the most recent first.&lt;SEP&gt;The Daily History screen displays past insulin delivery data, including the amount of bolus already delivered before an alarm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alarm History Screen">
  <data key="d0">Alarm History Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Alarm History Screen shows a log of past alarms generated by the insulin pump system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Alarm History Screen stores and displays past alerts, including those that were silenced.&lt;SEP&gt;The Alarm History Screen shows a list of alarms and alerts that occurred on a selected day, ordered by recency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired Sensors Screen">
  <data key="d0">Paired Sensors Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Paired Sensors Screen lists all sensors that have been paired with the insulin pump for glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;The Paired Sensors Screen displays current and past sensor pairing details, including serial number, code, date, and time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Basal">
  <data key="d0">Auto Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Basal is an automated insulin delivery feature that adjusts basal insulin rates based on sensor glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Basal is a function within the SmartGuard feature that automatically delivers basal insulin based on sensor glucose readings and recent insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Basal is a mode that SmartGuard returns to after a BG meter reading is entered, allowing automated basal insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The automatically adjusted basal insulin delivered by the SmartGuard feature based on the current SG readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Correction">
  <data key="d0">Auto Correction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Correction is a function that automatically administers correction boluses when glucose levels are outside the target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Correction is a function that allows the system to deliver automatic boluses every 5 minutes if a correction is needed to maintain glucose levels within the target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Correction is a setting within the SmartGuard feature that enables automatic delivery of correction boluses when blood glucose levels are high.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Correction is the amount of insulin automatically delivered by the SmartGuard feature to correct glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;A correction bolus automatically delivered by the MiniMed 780G system to maximize time in range; only occurs when using the SmartGuard feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus BG Check Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Bolus BG Check Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">feature</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus BG Check Reminder is a notification that prompts the user to check blood glucose before delivering a bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;A reminder for a BG check after programming a bolus; the reminder appears when the specified time period has passed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Missed Meal Bolus Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Missed Meal Bolus Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Missed Meal Bolus Reminder alerts the user if a meal bolus has not been delivered within a expected timeframe after a meal.&lt;SEP&gt;A reminder that can be set around typical meal times to prompt a missed meal bolus, with up to eight such reminders configurable.&lt;SEP&gt;A reminder when a bolus is not delivered during a specified time period, often around meal times.&lt;SEP&gt;Missed Meal Bolus Reminder is an alert that notifies the user if a meal bolus was not delivered at the expected time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Reservoir Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Low Reservoir Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">feature</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Reservoir Reminder notifies the user when insulin levels in the pump are running low.&lt;SEP&gt;The Low Reservoir Reminder alerts when insulin levels in the reservoir reach a specified threshold and again when half of that amount remains, with values set between 5 and 50 units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Block Mode">
  <data key="d0">Block Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Block Mode is a feature or setting on insulin pumps, particularly models such as the MiniMed 780G, designed to restrict access to critical functions for safety or user control purposes. It functions as a locked state of the device, often indicated by a status icon, which prevents unauthorized use and limits the ability to modify key settings. This mode is commonly utilized by caregivers to ensure that certain users, such as children or individuals requiring supervision, cannot inadvertently or intentionally alter essential pump operations.

While Block Mode restricts access to most settings and functions, it allows specific operations to continue, depending on the configuration. For instance, Auto Basal insulin delivery and Auto correction boluses may still be permitted if these features are enabled. Additionally, users may retain the ability to suspend insulin delivery, resume flow, or clear alarms and alerts, ensuring that urgent actions can still be taken when necessary. This balance between restriction and functionality supports both safety and effective diabetes management.

There is some variation in how Block Mode is described across sources, particularly regarding insulin delivery. While some descriptions indicate that Block Mode restricts settings but allows insulin delivery to continue under automated features, others suggest that Block Mode may stop insulin delivery entirely, with options to resume or suspend flow. This discrepancy may reflect different interpretations, pump models, or user scenarios. However, the predominant understanding is that Block Mode serves as a protective lockout feature rather than a full suspension of therapy, preserving critical automated functions while limiting manual control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9155c2d6ee74c467d00906235fe430b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Set Change Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Set Change Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Set Change Reminder alerts the user when it is time to replace the insulin infusion set.&lt;SEP&gt;The Set Change Reminder tracks the time elapsed between infusion set changes, helping ensure timely replacements.&lt;SEP&gt;The Set Change reminder tracks the time between infusion set changes and provides a notification to change the infusion set, with configurable duration settings.&lt;SEP&gt;A reminder notification prompting the user to change the infusion set on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Set Change Reminder is an alert prompting the user to replace the insulin infusion set.&lt;SEP&gt;Set Change Reminder is a notification prompting the user to replace the infusion set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Language">
  <data key="d0">Language</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Language is a configurable system setting that determines the display language of the insulin pump interface.&lt;SEP&gt;Language refers to the display language setting of the insulin pump, which can be changed by the user in Device Settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Language is a user setting that determines the display language on the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time and Date">
  <data key="d0">Time and Date</data>
  <data key="d1">setting</data>
  <data key="d2">Time and Date is a system setting that must be correctly configured for accurate logging and dosing calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preset Temp Basal Rates">
  <data key="d0">Preset Temp Basal Rates</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Preset Temp Basal Rates are predefined temporary basal profiles that can be activated quickly for anticipated changes in insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Preset Temp Basal Rates are predefined temporary basal settings configured for recurring short-term situations, allowing quick activation without re-entering parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Additional Basal Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Additional Basal Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Additional Basal Patterns allow users to create and switch between multiple basal insulin delivery schedules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707344</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Target">
  <data key="d0">BG Target</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BG Target is a user-defined glucose level that the system uses as a goal for insulin delivery adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;BG Target is a blood glucose target range used by the Bolus Wizard to calculate correction doses. It includes high and low values; if the same value is used for both, it functions as a single target.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;BG Target is the desired blood glucose level range (Lo-Hi in mg/dL) that the insulin system will work to achieve.&lt;SEP&gt;The BG Target is a user-defined blood glucose range between 60 and 250 mg/dL used in insulin dose calculations when the Bolus Wizard is enabled.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b0e9023a7c03c6a284d69e0930b8a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707346</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Possible Signal Interference Alert">
  <data key="d0">Possible Signal Interference Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The possible signal interference alert appears when the pump cannot find the sensor or transmitter signal, possibly due to electronic interference.&lt;SEP&gt;Possible Signal Interference Alert is a warning indicating that wireless communication between devices may be disrupted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707346</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibration Not Accepted Alert">
  <data key="d0">Calibration Not Accepted Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The calibration not accepted alert occurs when a blood glucose reading cannot be used for sensor calibration due to range, accuracy, or signal issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Calibration not accepted alert occurs when a glucose sensor calibration attempt fails.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend By Sensor Icon">
  <data key="d0">Suspend By Sensor Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Suspend By Sensor Icon appears when Suspend before low or Suspend on low features are active and can flash or display a red X based on system status.&lt;SEP&gt;The suspend by sensor icon on the Home screen indicates the status of sensor-driven insulin suspension, appearing with a red X when features are unavailable.&lt;SEP&gt;The suspend by sensor icon on the pump's home screen indicates the status of automated suspension features; a red X appears when the features are unavailable.&lt;SEP&gt;The suspend by sensor icon appears with a red X when the Suspend before low or Suspend on low feature is unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Near Field Communication">
  <data key="d0">Near Field Communication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Near Field Communication (NFC) is a wireless technology used to enable communication between the mobile device and the Instinct Sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Near Field Communication (NFC) is a wireless technology required to start the Instinct sensor using the MiniMed Mobile app.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG Graph">
  <data key="d0">SG Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The SG graph is a visual display on the pump screen that shows sensor glucose readings and may display alerts such as "Sensor signal not found - See User Guide".</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic Website">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic Website</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Medtronic website provides a list of compatible mobile devices and operating systems for use with the Instinct sensor and MiniMed Mobile app.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pair New Device">
  <data key="d0">Pair New Device</data>
  <data key="d1">function</data>
  <data key="d2">Pair New Device is an option on the device interface that initiates the process of connecting a new CGM device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Searching Screen">
  <data key="d0">Searching Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">interface</data>
  <data key="d2">The Searching Screen appears during the device discovery process and indicates the system is looking for available devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Select Device Screen">
  <data key="d0">Select Device Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">interface</data>
  <data key="d2">The Select Device Screen displays a list of available CGM devices for pairing, based on detected serial numbers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serial Number">
  <data key="d0">Serial Number</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The serial number uniquely identifies an individual MiniMed 780G system unit.&lt;SEP&gt;The Serial Number is a unique identifier on the transmitter used to match and verify the correct CGM device during pairing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Serial Number is a unique identifier for the CGM device used during pairing and troubleshooting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pairing Successful Message">
  <data key="d0">Pairing Successful Message</data>
  <data key="d1">message</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pairing Successful Message confirms that the transmitter has been successfully connected to the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unpair">
  <data key="d0">Unpair</data>
  <data key="d1">function</data>
  <data key="d2">Unpair is a function that disconnects the transmitter from the pump, used during device replacement or maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unpair Device Screen">
  <data key="d0">Unpair Device Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">interface</data>
  <data key="d2">The Unpair Device Screen prompts the user to confirm the disconnection of the CGM device from the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The Unpair Device Screen prompts the user to confirm the removal of a paired CGM device from the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="No Paired CGM Banner">
  <data key="d0">No Paired CGM Banner</data>
  <data key="d1">message</data>
  <data key="d2">The No Paired CGM Banner appears on the Home Screen when no transmitter is currently paired with the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The No Paired CGM Banner appears on the Home screen when no sensor is currently paired with the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Carb Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carb Ratio is a user-configurable and personalized setting used in insulin pump therapy to determine the amount of insulin required to cover a specific quantity of carbohydrates consumed during a meal. It is commonly defined as the number of grams of carbohydrates that are covered by one unit of insulin, and this value is essential for accurate insulin dosing in individuals managing diabetes. The setting is primarily utilized by the Bolus Wizard feature, a tool integrated into many insulin pumps that calculates the appropriate insulin bolus based on the user's carbohydrate intake and their configured Carb Ratio.

This setting is user-defined, meaning it must be individually tailored to the patient’s metabolic response and dietary patterns, and can vary throughout the day. As such, the Carb Ratio can be adjusted within 24-hour profiles to reflect changes in insulin sensitivity at different times. Accurate configuration of the Carb Ratio is critical not only for effective mealtime bolus calculations but also for the proper functioning of advanced features such as SmartGuard, which relies on precise insulin-to-carbohydrate mapping to automate insulin delivery. Overall, the Carb Ratio plays a central role in personalized diabetes management by enabling precise, data-driven insulin dosing in response to carbohydrate consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f608f07eae4ddd5409aed9d4ecef75ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Start New Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Start New Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">function</data>
  <data key="d2">Start New Sensor is a function that initiates the sensor warm-up process after the transmitter and sensor are connected.&lt;SEP&gt;Start New Sensor is a procedure initiated when a new sensor is connected, triggering a two-hour warm-up period before glucose readings are received.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Warm Up Message">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Warm Up Message</data>
  <data key="d1">message</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sensor Warm Up Message displays the remaining time before the sensor becomes fully operational, typically lasting two hours.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sensor Warm Up Message appears on the Home screen during the two-hour warm-up period after sensor insertion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reconnect Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Reconnect Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">function</data>
  <data key="d2">Reconnect Sensor is a function used to reestablish communication between the transmitter and an already-inserted sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Reconnect Sensor is a procedure used when a previously used sensor is reconnected, allowing the pump to resume monitoring without recalibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Connected Message">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Connected Message</data>
  <data key="d1">message</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sensor Connected Message appears when the transmitter is successfully reconnected to an inserted sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Connected Message confirms successful connection between the sensor and pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EA Note">
  <data key="d0">EA Note</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">EA Note refers to explanatory annotations in the text that provide additional instructions or references for settings and procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;EA Note provides additional instructions or clarifications within the user guide, such as timing expectations for system messages.&lt;SEP&gt;EA Note provides supplementary instructions and warnings related to bolus delivery features, such as stopping delivery or configuration requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;EA Note refers to explanatory annotations provided in the text to clarify conditions or behaviors related to bolus features and settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Basal Setting">
  <data key="d0">Max Basal Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Max basal setting is a configurable limit on the maximum amount of basal insulin per hour that can be programmed in Manual mode, with a factory default of 2.00 U/hr.&lt;SEP&gt;The Max basal setting limits insulin delivery in Manual mode; it is not used in SmartGuard mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Max Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Max bolus is a safety setting that limits the maximum bolus insulin dose the pump can deliver.&lt;SEP&gt;Max Bolus is a configurable limit on the maximum amount of bolus insulin that can be delivered, accessible through the Delivery Settings menu on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;A user-programmable setting that limits the maximum amount of insulin that can be delivered in a single bolus in Manual mode, ranging from 0 to 25 units.&lt;SEP&gt;The maximum bolus amount that can be programmed by the user in one dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adding An Additional Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Adding An Additional Basal Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Adding an additional basal pattern is a procedure that allows users to configure more than one basal pattern, with instructions referenced on page 250 of the manual.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Snooze">
  <data key="d0">High Snooze</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Snooze sets the duration (in 5-minute increments) before a high glucose alert is repeated if the condition persists.&lt;SEP&gt;High Snooze is a configurable alert setting that allows users to set a snooze duration in 5-minute increments from 5 minutes to 3 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;High snooze is a feature that temporarily silences high glucose alerts for a defined period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low SG Settings">
  <data key="d0">Low SG Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low SG settings allow users to define time-segmented glucose thresholds for alerts and insulin suspension based on sensor glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG settings are used to configure alerts or suspend insulin delivery when sensor glucose (SG) approaches or reaches a preset low limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG settings define the lower threshold for glucose levels in CGM, with configurable snooze and alert functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG Settings are user-defined thresholds for low sensor glucose values that trigger alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Easy Bolus Feature">
  <data key="d0">Easy Bolus Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The easy bolus feature allows users to quickly administer a bolus dose of insulin without navigating through multiple menus.&lt;SEP&gt;The Easy Bolus feature allows users to deliver a normal bolus using only the A button when the pump is in Sleep mode, with a configurable step size between 0.1 and 2.0 units of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Easy Bolus Feature is a simplified method for delivering bolus insulin without navigating through multiple menus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preset Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Preset Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Preset bolus is a feature that allows users to set up and manage predefined bolus deliveries for convenience.&lt;SEP&gt;Preset bolus allows users to define standard bolus amounts for quick selection during meals or corrections.&lt;SEP&gt;Preset bolus is a bolus type available in Manual mode that allows preconfigured insulin delivery settings.&lt;SEP&gt;A predefined bolus setting available only in Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;The Preset Bolus feature allows frequently used bolus amounts to be configured in advance, with named presets for meals or other circumstances and numbered presets from Bolus 1 to Bolus 4.&lt;SEP&gt;A Preset Bolus is a predefined insulin dose that can be delivered using specific settings and types such as Normal, Square Wave, or Dual Wave.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature to set up and save a bolus for specific meals or snacks that are frequently consumed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A Button">
  <data key="d0">A Button</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The A button is a physical control on the insulin pump used to operate the Easy Bolus feature by pressing or holding it to set and deliver bolus amounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Step Size">
  <data key="d0">Step Size</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Step Size refers to the increment of insulin (from 0.1 to 2.0 units) added with each press of the A button during Easy Bolus setup.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Bolus Amount">
  <data key="d0">Max Bolus Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Max Bolus Amount is the upper limit for bolus delivery, which constrains the Step Size setting and limits the total bolus that can be delivered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus delivery refers to the administration of a rapid dose of insulin, either manually or automatically via the SmartGuard feature, based on carbohydrate intake and glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus delivery is the administration of a measured dose of insulin to manage blood glucose levels, particularly around meals or to correct high glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Delivery is the process of administering an insulin bolus through the pump, initiated by selecting Deliver Bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus delivery refers to the administration of a measured dose of insulin, with various types and settings available for customization based on user needs and conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Delivery is the process of administering a measured dose of insulin through the pump, either immediately or over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus delivery refers to the administration of a precise amount of insulin, which can be interrupted by alarms or system errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warning">
  <data key="d0">Warning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Warning alerts users to potential safety hazards that may result in serious injury or death if not avoided, including unsafe use of device features or lack of training.&lt;SEP&gt;Warning refers to critical safety instructions that must be followed to prevent accidental insulin infusion and hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A warning indicates a risk of over-delivery of insulin if users rely solely on beeps or vibrations during Easy Bolus, emphasizing the need to verify delivery on the pump screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200c1e93d7f4cbc3027cec4d0898dc00</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tone">
  <data key="d0">Tone</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Tone refers to the generation of an alert tone, an Easy bolus step tone, and an alarm tone during the self test to confirm audio functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Tone refers to the audible signal emitted by the pump each time the A button is pressed during Easy Bolus setup to help count steps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707359</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vibration">
  <data key="d0">Vibration</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Vibration refers to the generation of two vibration tones during the self test to verify the pump's alert mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Vibration is a tactile feedback from the pump that occurs with each A button press during Easy Bolus, used to assist in counting steps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707359</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus 1">
  <data key="d0">Bolus 1</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus 1 is one of four numbered preset bolus options that can be configured for specific insulin delivery needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus 1 is one of the numbered preset bolus options available for configuration and delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707359</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus 4">
  <data key="d0">Bolus 4</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus 4 is one of four numbered preset bolus options available for custom bolus configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus 4 is one of the numbered preset bolus options available for configuration and delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707359</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stopping a Square Wave or Dual Wave Bolus Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Stopping a Square Wave or Dual Wave Bolus Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stopping a Square Wave or Dual Wave Bolus Delivery is a procedure described on page 276 for halting an ongoing extended bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707359</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CareLink Connect App">
  <data key="d0">CareLink Connect App</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The CareLink Connect app allows users to share device data from the MiniMed 780G system.&lt;SEP&gt;The CareLink Connect app (MMT-6111 for Android or MMT-6112 for iOS) is an optional app for care partners to view patient therapy data and receive selected alerts, but does not replace the primary display device for therapy decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The CareLink Connect App allows care partners to view data shared from a connected MiniMed Mobile App and requires a compatible mobile device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707360</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trend Arrow">
  <data key="d0">Trend Arrow</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Trend arrows show the direction and rate of change of the most recent glucose readings, indicating whether glucose levels are rising or falling.&lt;SEP&gt;Trend arrows indicate the rate of change in sensor glucose levels, showing whether glucose is rising or falling at specific rates over the last 20 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Insulin Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Basal Insulin Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal insulin delivery refers to the continuous, low-dose insulin delivery programmed in the pump to manage glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal insulin delivery refers to the continuous infusion of insulin to manage blood glucose levels, which can be suspended or resumed using the insulin pump system.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal insulin delivery is the continuous, low-dose insulin infusion that can be resumed after a pump update by user confirmation.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal insulin delivery is the continuous, background infusion of insulin that can be suspended and resumed based on low glucose events or user input.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal insulin delivery is the continuous, background infusion of insulin that can be suspended or manually resumed during low glucose events.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal insulin delivery is the continuous administration of insulin by the pump, which can be temporarily adjusted using preset temp basal rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delivery Settings">
  <data key="d0">Delivery Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Delivery Settings refer to a configuration menu within the insulin pump system that enables users to customize various parameters governing insulin delivery. This menu serves as a central interface for adjusting both basic and advanced insulin delivery features, ensuring personalized management of diabetes treatment. Users can configure core delivery parameters such as basal rates, bolus increments, insulin sensitivity factors, and Active Insulin Time, all of which directly influence how insulin is administered throughout the day.

Within the Delivery Settings menu, users have access to specific features like the Bolus Wizard, which calculates appropriate insulin doses based on current glucose levels, carbohydrate intake, and other factors. The menu also allows for the setup of preset boluses and temporary basal rates, offering flexibility in responding to changing physiological needs. Additionally, Delivery Settings include options to enable or disable advanced bolus delivery modes such as Square Wave and Dual Wave boluses, which distribute insulin over an extended period to better match delayed glucose absorption, particularly after meals.

The configuration of Delivery Settings is closely linked to safety and performance parameters, including Max Basal and Max Bolus limits, which help prevent accidental over-delivery of insulin. These settings also integrate with SmartGuard technology in certain pump systems, allowing automated insulin delivery adjustments based on real-time glucose data. Overall, Delivery Settings play a critical role in tailoring insulin therapy to individual needs, balancing efficacy, safety, and user control within the insulin pump interface.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654d7a203c4eab9f3a89f577edc2a5ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b0e9023a7c03c6a284d69e0930b8a9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Insulin Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Insulin Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus insulin delivery is the manual or calculated dose of insulin delivered to address meals or high glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus insulin delivery refers to the administration of a rapid dose of insulin to manage blood glucose spikes, typically around meals or to correct high blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Wizard Feature">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Wizard Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus Wizard feature in Manual mode calculates insulin bolus based on glucose levels, carbs, and insulin settings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Wizard feature is a function in the insulin pump that calculates insulin dosage based on carb intake, blood glucose levels, and insulin sensitivity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Wizard feature is a tool that calculates insulin bolus doses based on current blood glucose, insulin sensitivity, and target levels.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Wizard feature is a tool in the insulin pump that calculates insulin dosage based on current glucose levels and active insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Wizard feature calculates insulin dosage based on carb intake and blood glucose levels, and can deliver a Square Wave bolus if conditions are met.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;In Manual mode, a feature that uses individual Bolus Wizard settings to calculate an estimated bolus amount based on the BG value and the entered carbs; settings include carb ratio, insulin sensitivity factor, BG target range, and active insulin time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f608f07eae4ddd5409aed9d4ecef75ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654d7a203c4eab9f3a89f577edc2a5ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temp Basal Rates">
  <data key="d0">Temp Basal Rates</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Temp basal rates allow temporary adjustments to the basal insulin delivery rate for specific periods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Software Update">
  <data key="d0">Software Update</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Software update refers to the process of downloading and installing new firmware on the MiniMed 780G pump via the MiniMed Mobile app.&lt;SEP&gt;A software update refers to the process of upgrading the pump's firmware, which triggers a 5-hour update period for SmartGuard active insulin information.&lt;SEP&gt;Software update refers to the process of upgrading the pump's firmware, referenced on page 147.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend Before Low Event">
  <data key="d0">Suspend Before Low Event</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend Before Low event is a safety feature that pauses insulin delivery when glucose levels are predicted to drop too low.&lt;SEP&gt;A Suspend before low event occurs when insulin delivery is suspended due to predicted low sensor glucose levels, preventing hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend On Low Event">
  <data key="d0">Suspend On Low Event</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend On Low event occurs when insulin delivery is automatically stopped due to low glucose levels detected by the CGM.&lt;SEP&gt;A Suspend on low event occurs when sensor glucose readings reach or fall below the low limit, triggering suspension of insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sound &amp; Vibration Screen">
  <data key="d0">Sound &amp; Vibration Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sound &amp; Vibration Screen allows users to configure alert settings for audio and vibration feedback.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sound &amp; Vibration screen allows users to adjust volume, sound, and vibration for alerts on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Sound &amp; Vibration Screen is a settings menu for configuring audible and tactile alerts on the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin guidelines specify that only rapid-acting U-100 insulin should be used with the MiniMed 780G system.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin guidelines are recommendations for safe and effective use of insulin with the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Precautions">
  <data key="d0">Security Precautions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security precautions are measures to protect the integrity and safe operation of the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electrostatic Discharge">
  <data key="d0">Electrostatic Discharge</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Electrostatic discharge refers to the sudden flow of electricity between objects, which can interfere with electronic medical devices.&lt;SEP&gt;High levels of electrostatic discharge can reset the pump software and trigger an error alarm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Waterproof Capabilities">
  <data key="d0">Waterproof Capabilities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Waterproof capabilities describe the resistance of the MiniMed 780G system components to water damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Care Products">
  <data key="d0">Skin Care Products</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin care products are topical agents that may interact with infusion sites and affect skin integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Certain skin care products like lotions, sunscreen, and insect repellents can damage the plastic casing of the insulin pump if not cleaned promptly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reporting Serious Incidents">
  <data key="d0">Reporting Serious Incidents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reporting serious incidents involves documenting and notifying authorities of adverse events related to the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Glucose Reading">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Glucose Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor glucose (SG) readings are real-time glucose measurements collected by a continuous glucose monitor and displayed on the device.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor glucose reading is a measurement of glucose levels obtained via a continuous glucose monitor, which can be inaccurately elevated by acetaminophen or paracetamol.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor glucose reading is the real-time glucose value obtained from the CGM sensor and displayed on the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb Entry">
  <data key="d0">Carb Entry</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carb entry refers to the input of carbohydrate intake used by the SmartGuard system to calculate insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Carb Entry is the input of carbohydrate intake data, used for insulin dosing calculations and displayed on the sensor graph.&lt;SEP&gt;A carb entry is a user input indicating carbohydrate intake, used to calculate mealtime insulin boluses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Change Event">
  <data key="d0">Time Change Event</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A time change event is recorded when the device clock is adjusted and is displayed as a white clock symbol on the graph.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Desired Range">
  <data key="d0">Desired Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Desired range is the target glucose range, such as 70–180 mg/dL, used by the SmartGuard system to guide insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Desired Range is the target glucose range represented as a green band on the sensor graph, indicating optimal glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;The desired range is the target glucose level range that the SmartGuard system aims to maintain for optimal glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temp Basal Rate">
  <data key="d0">Temp Basal Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Temp Basal Rate is the adjustable insulin delivery rate set temporarily, which can be defined as a percentage of the current basal pattern or as a specific unit per hour value.&lt;SEP&gt;Temp basal rate is a temporary adjustment to the basal insulin delivery that must be stopped before SmartGuard can be activated.&lt;SEP&gt;A temporary basal rate that can be set to deliver insulin at a modified rate for a specified duration, either as a percentage or absolute value.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature that temporarily increases or decreases the current basal rate for a specified duration.&lt;SEP&gt;Temp Basal Rate is a temporary adjustment to the basal insulin delivery rate, used for short-term needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Temp Basal Rate is a temporary adjustment to the insulin pump’s basal rate for a specified duration, used to manage varying insulin needs.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Percentage">
  <data key="d0">Percentage</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Percentage in the context of temp basal refers to setting the temporary basal rate as a percentage of the programmed basal rate, ranging from 0% to 200%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fixed Rate">
  <data key="d0">Fixed Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Fixed Rate is a temp basal rate type that delivers a specific amount of insulin per hour, independent of the programmed basal pattern, limited by the Max basal rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Wizard Screen">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Wizard Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus Wizard Screen is an interface on the insulin pump used to calculate and deliver bolus insulin doses, where blood glucose readings can also be entered in Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Wizard Screen displays current blood glucose readings and allows users to calculate and deliver bolus doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Message">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Message</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An emergency message appears on the pump if insulin delivery is suspended and the low glucose alert is not cleared within a specified time.&lt;SEP&gt;An emergency message is displayed on the pump if a Suspend on low alarm is not cleared within two hours, signaling resumption of insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Two-Hour Suspend Time">
  <data key="d0">Two-Hour Suspend Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The two-hour suspend time is the maximum duration for which insulin delivery can be suspended before it automatically resumes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thirty-Minute Unavailability">
  <data key="d0">Thirty-Minute Unavailability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The thirty-minute unavailability is a period during which the Suspend before low or Suspend on low feature remains disabled after basal insulin delivery resumes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Four-Hour Unavailability">
  <data key="d0">Four-Hour Unavailability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The four-hour unavailability is a period during which the Suspend before low or Suspend on low feature remains disabled after basal insulin delivery resumes if the alert was not cleared.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77d9c07e6a38b29ecca31e8c42df37e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707367</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Meter Reading">
  <data key="d0">BG Meter Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">BG meter reading refers to the blood glucose measurement entered manually into the system to calibrate the sensor and support SmartGuard functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;A BG meter reading is a blood glucose measurement required to clear certain alerts and resume or continue use of the SmartGuard feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707367</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Checklist">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Checklist</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The SmartGuard Checklist is a screen that displays requirements needed to activate or continue using the SmartGuard feature, showing status indicators like wait or question icons.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard checklist is a system verification process that ensures all prerequisites are met before activating the SmartGuard feature.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard Checklist is a set of required steps or conditions that must be met to resume or maintain the SmartGuard feature, including sensor status, BG entry, and system settings.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard Checklist is a procedural guide users can review after exiting the SmartGuard feature to ensure proper system use.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard Checklist is a pre-activation verification list for the SmartGuard system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delivery Suspension">
  <data key="d0">Delivery Suspension</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Delivery suspension refers to the temporary halt of insulin delivery, which prevents the use of the SmartGuard feature until resolved.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lost Sensor Signal">
  <data key="d0">Lost Sensor Signal</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Lost sensor signal is an alert triggered when the insulin pump fails to communicate with the sensor for 30 minutes, requiring user intervention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pairing">
  <data key="d0">Pairing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pairing is the process of connecting the insulin pump with a CGM device or mobile device, which requires a secure environment to prevent unintended connections.&lt;SEP&gt;Pairing is the process of connecting a transmitter, sensor, or mobile device to the pump to enable communication.&lt;SEP&gt;Pairing is the process of establishing a wireless connection between the insulin pump and the CGM device to enable data transmission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="24-Hour Period">
  <data key="d0">24-Hour Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A 24-hour period is the full cycle over which insulin pump settings such as basal rates are programmed to vary.&lt;SEP&gt;A 24-hour period is a time setting used for configuring insulin delivery parameters such as sensitivity and blood glucose targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f608f07eae4ddd5409aed9d4ecef75ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Settings">
  <data key="d0">Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Settings refer to the configuration options available for customizing insulin pump functions over a 24-hour period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
