<node id="Rewinding">
  <data key="d0">Rewinding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rewinding is a process during startup where the piston returns to its start position in the reservoir compartment, indicated by a message on the screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Rewinding is a procedure performed on the pump to prepare it for a new reservoir, preventing accidental insulin infusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Rewinding is a procedure performed on the insulin pump to reset the plunger or reservoir mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc61f77b003d0086bd985ddb94fc2a98</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707375</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rewind Required Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Rewind Required Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rewind Required Alarm is an alert prompting the user to perform a rewinding operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707375</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rise Limit">
  <data key="d0">Rise Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Rise Limit defines the rate at which glucose must rise (from 1.0 to 5.0 mg/dL per minute) to trigger a Rise Alert, with options matching trend arrows or custom rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise Limit defines the rate at which sensor glucose must rise (e.g., 1, 2, or 3 mg/dL per minute) to trigger a Rise Alert, with options for custom values.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise Limit is a configurable threshold for glucose level increases that triggers alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707375</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Safety Alert">
  <data key="d0">Safety Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Safety Alert is a warning message that appears when there is uncertainty or incorrect data regarding the blood glucose reading used to calibrate the sensor, requiring user confirmation.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety Alert is a critical warning designed to prevent harm by notifying the user of dangerous conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety Alert is a critical notification related to device or therapy safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
