  <data key="d5">1778707387</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Suspend Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A feature that stops all insulin delivery until manually resumed, ensuring safety during low glucose events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707387</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TDD">
  <data key="d0">TDD</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The acronym for total daily dose, representing the cumulative amount of insulin delivered in a 24-hour period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707387</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confirm Code Screen">
  <data key="d0">Confirm Code Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Confirm Code Screen is a user interface screen that appears during the pairing process to verify a code match between the pump and the inserter label.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inserter">
  <data key="d0">Inserter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Inserter is a device used to place the sensor under the skin and contains a label with a pairing code.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inserter Label">
  <data key="d0">Inserter Label</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Inserter Label is located on the top of the inserter and displays a code used for pairing verification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired Devices Screen">
  <data key="d0">Paired Devices Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Paired Devices Screen displays connected devices and allows users to manage device pairing on the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The Paired Devices Screen displays devices currently connected to the pump and allows users to manage pairings.&lt;SEP&gt;Paired Devices Screen is a user interface menu that displays currently connected devices such as sensors and transmitters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
