</node>
<node id="Code">
  <data key="d0">Code</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Code is a numeric value (e.g., 348376) used to verify the correct pairing between the pump and the inserter or sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cancel Option">
  <data key="d0">Cancel Option</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cancel Option allows the user to abort the pairing process if the displayed code does not match the inserter label.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707389</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confirm Option">
  <data key="d0">Confirm Option</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Confirm Option finalizes the code verification step during the pairing process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707389</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unpair Option">
  <data key="d0">Unpair Option</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Unpair Option removes the current CGM device pairing from the pump, allowing a new sensor to be paired.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707389</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pair New Device Option">
  <data key="d0">Pair New Device Option</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pair New Device Option initiates the process of connecting a new transmitter or sensor to the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707389</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wireless Connection">
  <data key="d0">Wireless Connection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Wireless Connection enables communication between the pump and the CGM device during pairing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Wireless Connection enables communication between the pump and the transmitter for glucose data transmission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707389</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Security Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security Procedure involves code verification and time-limited pairing to ensure secure and accurate device pairing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707389</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Two-Hour Warm Up Period">
  <data key="d0">Two-Hour Warm Up Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Two-Hour Warm Up Period is the time required for the sensor to stabilize and begin sending glucose readings after insertion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Five-Minute Delay">
  <data key="d0">Five-Minute Delay</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Five-Minute Delay refers to the potential waiting time before the sensor warm-up message appears on the Home screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Twenty-Minute Pairing Window">
  <data key="d0">Twenty-Minute Pairing Window</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Twenty-Minute Pairing Window is the time limit within which the sensor must be paired with the pump after removing the inserter cap.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Unpairing">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Unpairing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic Unpairing occurs when pairing a new sensor causes the previously paired sensor to be disconnected from the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="iCGM 25">
  <data key="d0">iCGM 25</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">iCGM 25 is a system related to integrated continuous glucose monitoring and insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Flow Blocked Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Flow Blocked Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Insulin Flow Blocked alarm indicates that the pump has detected a blockage in basal or bolus insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Flow Blocked Alarm is a system alert indicating a blockage in insulin delivery, referenced on pages 307 and 308.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin flow blocked alarm indicates an obstruction in insulin delivery, requiring user intervention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Battery Pump Alert">
  <data key="d0">Low Battery Pump Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Low Battery Pump Alert is a notification that signals when batteries need immediate replacement to prevent interruption of insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The Low Battery Pump alert indicates that the pump battery is running low and needs replacement.&lt;SEP&gt;Low Battery Pump Alert is a notification indicating insufficient power in the insulin pump, referenced on page 309.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Basal Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Max Basal Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Max Basal Alarm is a system notification indicating a maximum basal insulin delivery limit has been reached, referenced on page 305.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Bolus Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Max Bolus Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Max Bolus Alarm is a warning triggered when the maximum bolus insulin dose limit is reached, referenced on page 305.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Device Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Medical Device Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical Device Alarm is activated when the pump suspends due to low sensor glucose and lack of user response within 10 minutes, requiring emergency assistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical Device Alarm is a general alert category for critical system issues in the insulin pump, referenced on page 324.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Restarted Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Pump Restarted Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Restarted Alarm indicates the insulin pump has rebooted, referenced on page 313.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Basal Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal delivery is the continuous, automatic infusion of insulin by the pump to maintain glucose levels between meals and overnight, adjusted based on sensor glucose values and user needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal delivery refers to the continuous, background infusion of insulin, with features like resuming and preset temp basal rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resume Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Resume Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resume Bolus is a function that allows the user to continue an interrupted bolus delivery after resolving the cause of interruption.&lt;SEP&gt;Resume Bolus is a function that allows the continuation of an interrupted bolus insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Basal Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal Patterns are customizable insulin delivery schedules that define varying basal rates throughout the day.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal Patterns are customizable schedules for basal insulin delivery, allowing different rates at different times of day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preset Temp Basal Rate">
  <data key="d0">Preset Temp Basal Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A preset temp basal rate is a configurable insulin delivery setting for temporary situations, defined by percentage or rate and duration, with up to eight available presets.&lt;SEP&gt;A predefined temporary basal rate setting that can be selected for use, subject to system limits such as maximum basal rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Preset Temp Basal Rate is a preconfigured temporary basal rate that can be activated quickly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outside Typical Range Alert">
  <data key="d0">Outside Typical Range Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Outside Typical Range Alert warns that a Max Basal setting of 6.00 U/hr may allow up to 144 U/day, which could be unsafe, advising consultation with a healthcare professional.&lt;SEP&gt;Outside Typical Range Alert is a notification indicating that glucose levels are outside the user-defined target range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Error Detected Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Power Error Detected Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Power Error Detected Alarm is a critical alert indicating a malfunction in the pump's power system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manage Settings">
  <data key="d0">Manage Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Manage Settings is a screen that provides options to save, restore, clear all settings, or clear active insulin settings on the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Manage Settings is a menu option allowing users to adjust various device configurations including clearing active insulin and viewing settings history.&lt;SEP&gt;Manage Settings is a menu function that allows users to configure various pump parameters and preferences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low SG Below XX mg/dL Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Low SG Below XX mg/dL Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Low SG Below XX mg/dL Alarm is a configurable alert triggered when sensor glucose drops below a specific user-defined threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CareLink Uploader Not Found Message">
  <data key="d0">CareLink Uploader Not Found Message</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">CareLink Uploader Not Found Message is a system notification indicating the CareLink device is not detected for data upload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservoir &amp; Set Screen">
  <data key="d0">Reservoir &amp; Set Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Reservoir &amp; Set Screen is a pump interface menu for monitoring insulin reservoir levels and infusion set status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Settings Screen">
  <data key="d0">Settings Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Settings Screen is a user interface menu for accessing and modifying pump configuration options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707394</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="History &amp; Graph Screen">
  <data key="d0">History &amp; Graph Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">History &amp; Graph Screen is a pump interface that displays past glucose readings, insulin delivery, and trends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707394</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Screen">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose Screen is a display on the pump for viewing current and historical blood glucose values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707394</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resume Basal Feature">
  <data key="d0">Resume Basal Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The resume basal feature restarts programmed basal insulin delivery after a suspension, without restarting any bolus deliveries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707395</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delivery Suspended Banner">
  <data key="d0">Delivery Suspended Banner</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The delivery suspended banner is a visual indicator on the insulin pump's home screen showing that insulin delivery has been paused.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707395</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Patterns Screen">
  <data key="d0">Basal Patterns Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The basal patterns screen displays a list of configured basal patterns and their 24-hour insulin totals, indicating the active pattern with a check mark.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707395</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Format Screen">
  <data key="d0">Format Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Format screen is an interface screen that appears during the setup process, prompting the user to select a time format.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Format">
  <data key="d0">Time Format</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time Format is a setting that allows the user to choose between different time display options, such as 24 Hour format.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="24 Hour">
  <data key="d0">24 Hour</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">24 Hour is a time format option available for selection on the Format screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enter Time Screen">
  <data key="d0">Enter Time Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enter Time screen appears after selecting the time format and allows the user to input the current time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enter Date Screen">
  <data key="d0">Enter Date Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enter Date screen appears after entering the time and prompts the user to input the current date.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707398</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Time">
  <data key="d0">Current Time</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Current Time is a displayed item on the Home screen that shows the present time, which must be set during the startup process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707398</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time In Range Screen">
  <data key="d0">Time In Range Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Time In Range Screen displays glucose level trends over time and is accessible from the Home screen when the Sensor feature is enabled.&lt;SEP&gt;The Time in Range screen displays the percentage of time glucose levels are between 70 mg/dL and 180 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707398</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Reset To Zero">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Reset To Zero</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Insulin Reset To Zero is an alarm event that triggers the display of a status icon until the specified time, indicating insulin activity has ended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707398</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Connection">
  <data key="d0">Connection</data>
  <data key="d1">status</data>
  <data key="d2">Connection is a status icon indicating the communication state between the pump and the sensor, showing whether it is active or disrupted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707399</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservoir Compartment">
  <data key="d0">Reservoir Compartment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reservoir Compartment is a part of the pump where the piston and insulin reservoir are located, and to which the piston returns during the rewinding process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707399</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Value">
  <data key="d0">BG Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">BG value refers to the blood glucose reading measured by a blood glucose meter, used as a reference for treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;BG value refers to blood glucose level, which is monitored and used in insulin management features like SmartGuard and Bolus Wizard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707399</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Meter">
  <data key="d0">BG Meter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A BG meter is a device used to measure blood glucose levels, and its readings must be manually entered into the MiniMed 780G insulin pump when requested.&lt;SEP&gt;A BG meter is a medical device used to measure blood glucose levels through a fingerstick test, required for confirming SG readings in certain situations.&lt;SEP&gt;A device that measures glucose levels in the blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707399</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid-Acting U-100 Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Rapid-Acting U-100 Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid-acting U-100 insulin is a type of insulin formulation prescribed for use with insulin pumps to manage blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid-acting U-100 insulin is a type of insulin approved for use with the MiniMed 780G system, including specific brands like Admelog, Humalog, and NovoLog.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid-acting U-100 insulin is a type of insulin used with the MiniMed 780G pump for glucose management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707400</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Tones">
  <data key="d0">Pump Tones</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump tones are audible signals emitted by the MiniMed 780G system to indicate alerts, alarms, or menu navigation cues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707400</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vibrations">
  <data key="d0">Vibrations</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Vibrations are tactile alerts produced by the insulin pump to notify the user of system events or alarms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707400</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile Communication Devices">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Communication Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Mobile communication devices such as cell phones may interfere with the MiniMed 780G system if not paired, due to radio frequency emissions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707400</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPS Navigation Systems">
  <data key="d0">GPS Navigation Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GPS navigation systems are electronic devices that may emit radio frequencies capable of interfering with the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-Theft Systems">
  <data key="d0">Anti-Theft Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti-theft systems are security devices that may emit electromagnetic signals interfering with the insulin pump’s operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RF Emitters">
  <data key="d0">RF Emitters</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">RF emitters are electronic devices with radio frequency transmitters that may interfere with the MiniMed 780G system if within close proximity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bluetooth is a wireless communication technology used in the Guardian 4 transmitter to relay sensor glucose data to the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wireless Networks">
  <data key="d0">Wireless Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Wireless networks such as Wi-Fi may emit radio frequencies that interfere with communication between the sensor and the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cordless Phones">
  <data key="d0">Cordless Phones</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cordless phones are communication devices that may emit radio frequencies capable of disrupting the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Walkie-Talkies">
  <data key="d0">Walkie-Talkies</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Walkie-talkies are two-way radios that may emit strong radio frequencies, potentially interfering with the insulin pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="First 12 Hours">
  <data key="d0">First 12 Hours</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The first 12 hours refers to the initial period of sensor use during which sensor performance may be unstable and requires special precautions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Personal Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Personal Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Personal Reminder is a user-defined alert that can be set for various purposes, with up to five allowed, and occurs daily at a specified time unless edited or deleted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Meter Reading Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Meter Reading Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific reminder type related to checking blood glucose levels, integrated into the alert system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Bg Check Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Bg Check Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus BG Check Reminder notifies the user to check blood glucose after a bolus delivery, with a configurable timer between 30 minutes and 5 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reminders">
  <data key="d0">Reminders</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Reminders is a sub-menu within Alert Settings that organizes different types of user alerts, including personal and system-specific reminders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edit">
  <data key="d0">Edit</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Edit is a function that allows users to modify the time or other details of an existing reminder.&lt;SEP&gt;Edit is a function that allows modification of a preset bolus value, type, duration, or other parameters if permitted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rename">
  <data key="d0">Rename</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rename is a function that allows users to change the name of an existing Personal Reminder by selecting from a list of available names.&lt;SEP&gt;Rename is a function that allows assigning a new name to a preset bolus from a list of available names.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delete">
  <data key="d0">Delete</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Delete is a function that removes an existing reminder entry from the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Delete is a function that removes a preset bolus configuration from the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Turn On">
  <data key="d0">Turn On</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Turn On is an action that activates a reminder, such as the Bolus BG Check or Missed Meal Bolus Reminder.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Turn Off">
  <data key="d0">Turn Off</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Turn Off is an action that deactivates a reminder without deleting its configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Timer">
  <data key="d0">Timer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Timer is a feature used in the Bolus BG Check Reminder to count down from the time a bolus was started, set between 30 minutes and 5 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="20 Mg/Dl Above Low Limit">
  <data key="d0">20 Mg/Dl Above Low Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This threshold indicates that sensor glucose must be at least 20 mg/dL above the low limit to resume insulin delivery after a suspension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="40 Mg/Dl Above Low Limit">
  <data key="d0">40 Mg/Dl Above Low Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This threshold indicates that sensor glucose must be predicted to rise more than 40 mg/dL above the low limit within 30 minutes to resume insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30 Minutes">
  <data key="d0">30 Minutes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A time interval used as a prediction window and minimum suspension duration for insulin delivery during low glucose events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Two Hours">
  <data key="d0">Two Hours</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The maximum duration for which insulin delivery can be suspended during a Suspend before low or Suspend on low event.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manually Resuming Basal Insulin Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Manually Resuming Basal Insulin Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Manually resuming basal insulin delivery is a user-initiated action to restart insulin infusion during or after a Suspend before low or Suspend on low event.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Limits">
  <data key="d0">Alert Limits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The settings that determine when low and high SG alerts are triggered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Awake Mode">
  <data key="d0">Awake Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A state in which the pump screen is on; the Home screen appears unless another screen is being used.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Check For Sensor">
  <data key="d0">BG Check For Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The pump uses a supplied blood glucose (BG) meter reading to check sensor performance, including predicting how closely the sensor glucose will match blood glucose values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Targets">
  <data key="d0">BG Targets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The high and low BG readings used for BG correction when using the Bolus Wizard feature in Manual mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibrate">
  <data key="d0">Calibrate</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The process of using a blood glucose (BG) meter reading to help the sensor glucose (SG) readings more closely match the glucose measured in the blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM)">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A monitoring tool that uses a glucose sensor placed below the skin to continuously measure the amount of glucose in the interstitial fluid.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed Mio 30 Infusion Set">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed Mio 30 Infusion Set</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed Mio 30 infusion set, identified by model numbers MMT-876A, MMT-884A, and MMT-886A, is a medical device used to deliver insulin from the pump to the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed Mio 30 infusion set is a compatible infusion set with MMT numbers MMT-905A and MMT-906A.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed Mio Advance Infusion Set">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed Mio Advance Infusion Set</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed Mio Advance infusion set, identified by model numbers MMT-905A and MMT-906A, is a medical device used to deliver insulin from the pump to the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed Mio Advance infusion set is a compatible infusion set with MMT numbers MMT-213A, MMT-242A, MMT-243A, and MMT-244A.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707407</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extended Infusion Set">
  <data key="d0">Extended Infusion Set</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Extended infusion set, identified by model numbers MMT-213A, MMT-242A, MMT-243A, and MMT-244A, is available in various pack sizes with suffixes such as A, AH, AJ, AG, and AK, and is compatible with the MiniMed 780G insulin pump system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Extended infusion set is a specific type of infusion set requiring the Extended reservoir MMT-342 for use with the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707407</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Other Infusion Sets">
  <data key="d0">Other Infusion Sets</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Other infusion sets ending with the suffix "AT" indicate different pack sizes and are compatible with the MiniMed 780G insulin pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707407</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="App Manager Device">
  <data key="d0">App Manager Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The App Manager is a compatible mobile device provided by Medtronic with the MiniMed Mobile app pre-installed, used to manage system functions such as starting the Instinct sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3323a205200ffe0b547b90ddb5919e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707407</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
