  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus 2">
  <data key="d0">Bolus 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus 2 is one of the numbered preset bolus options available for configuration and delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus 3">
  <data key="d0">Bolus 3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus 3 is one of the numbered preset bolus options available for configuration and delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preset Bolus Setup">
  <data key="d0">Preset Bolus Setup</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Preset Bolus Setup is a configuration process that enables users to define and save bolus amounts and types for future use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Type">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Type</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Type refers to the classification of a bolus as Normal, Square Wave, or Dual Wave, determining how the insulin is delivered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Amount">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Amount is the quantity of insulin specified in a preset bolus, set during configuration and displayed before delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Now % Amount">
  <data key="d0">Now % Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Now % Amount is the percentage of the total bolus delivered immediately in a Dual Wave bolus, with the remainder delivered as a square wave.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Square Amount">
  <data key="d0">Square Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Square Amount is the portion of a Dual Wave bolus delivered over time, automatically adjusted when the Now % amount is changed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Options">
  <data key="d0">Options</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Options is a menu that allows users to edit, rename, or delete an existing preset bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stopping A Bolus Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Stopping A Bolus Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stopping a bolus delivery refers to the process of halting an ongoing Square Wave or Dual Wave bolus, excluding basal insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Entry">
  <data key="d0">BG Entry</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">BG Entry refers to the manual input of blood glucose readings into the system, which may trigger calibration alerts or reminders.&lt;SEP&gt;BG Entry refers to the manual input of a blood glucose value into the pump, which is required under certain conditions to resume or continue the SmartGuard feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Min Delivery Alert">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Min Delivery Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The SmartGuard Min Delivery Alert appears when the feature has reached its time limit for minimum insulin delivery, prompting the user to enter a BG value.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Max Delivery Alert">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Max Delivery Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The SmartGuard Max Delivery Alert appears when the pump has been delivering basal insulin at its maximum limit for 7 hours, requiring the user to check the SmartGuard Checklist and enter a BG.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Act. Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Act. Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Act. Insulin refers to the active insulin currently in the body, displayed on the pump screen as part of the SmartGuard feature's real-time monitoring and delivery calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exit in X:XX hr">
  <data key="d0">Exit in X:XX hr</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Exit in X:XX hr is a message displayed on the Home screen indicating the time remaining before the pump exits the SmartGuard feature and enters Manual mode if no action is taken.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="48-Hour Warm-Up">
  <data key="d0">48-Hour Warm-Up</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The 48-hour warm-up is a required initialization period for a new sensor, which must be completed within four hours of the last SG reading to remain in the SmartGuard feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="5-Hour Warm-Up Period">
  <data key="d0">5-Hour Warm-Up Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The 5-hour warm-up period is a system state during which the SmartGuard feature cannot restart, ensuring sensor stabilization before resuming automated insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="No Calibration Occurred Alert">
  <data key="d0">No Calibration Occurred Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">No Calibration Occurred Alert indicates the sensor failed to receive calibration blood glucose readings from the pump, requiring user action to resume readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pair New Sensor Alert">
  <data key="d0">Pair New Sensor Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Pair New Sensor Alert notifies the user that only one sensor can be paired at a time and prompts confirmation to unpair the current sensor and pair a new one.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Possible Signaling Interference Alert">
  <data key="d0">Possible Signaling Interference Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Possible Signaling Interference Alert indicates communication disruption between the pump and CGM device due to nearby electronic devices, suggesting relocation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-561977d7e1e0a53f148e049c126c1970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Bolus Setting">
  <data key="d0">Max Bolus Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Max bolus setting limits the maximum amount of insulin that can be delivered in a single bolus for safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Buttons">
  <data key="d0">Pump Buttons</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump buttons are components of the insulin pump that may become stuck or unresponsive during pressure changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Pump buttons are physical controls on the insulin pump used to navigate menus and operate features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph">
  <data key="d0">Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Graph displays historical trends of insulin delivery, glucose levels, and time in range on the pump interface.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired Sensors">
  <data key="d0">Paired Sensors</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Paired sensors refer to the list of glucose sensors that are currently connected and communicating with the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fill Cannula Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Fill Cannula Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Fill Cannula alarm alerts the user when the cannula filling process has been active for 15 minutes and requires a response.&lt;SEP&gt;Fill cannula alarm prompts the user to complete the cannula filling process during infusion set setup.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consider Sensor Change Alert">
  <data key="d0">Consider Sensor Change Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Consider sensor change alert suggests upcoming sensor replacement based on performance or age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Pump Error Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Critical Pump Error Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical pump error alarm indicates a severe malfunction requiring immediate attention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Limit Message">
  <data key="d0">Device Limit Message</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Device limit message appears when a system parameter, such as delivery or bolus, reaches its programmed maximum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device No Longer Compatible Alert">
  <data key="d0">Device No Longer Compatible Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Device no longer compatible alert warns that a connected device is no longer supported by the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fill Tubing">
  <data key="d0">Fill Tubing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fill tubing is a procedure performed during pump setup to ensure insulin flows properly through the tubing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Status">
  <data key="d0">Status</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Status refers to the current operational state of the pump, displayed through icons and alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antiseptic">
  <data key="d0">Antiseptic</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">An antiseptic is a substance used to clean the insertion site as directed by a healthcare professional.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Set Insertion Site">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Set Insertion Site</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion set insertion site is the specific body location where the infusion set is inserted and must be rotated to avoid overuse.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Set Occlusion">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Set Occlusion</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion set occlusion is a blockage in the infusion set that can occur if the set is used beyond its recommended duration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Site Infection">
  <data key="d0">Site Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Site infection is a potential complication from prolonged use of the same infusion set insertion site without rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fill Cannula Action">
  <data key="d0">Fill Cannula Action</data>
  <data key="d1">procedure</data>
  <data key="d2">The Fill Cannula action is a step in the insulin pump setup process that fills the cannula with insulin after insertion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservoir Only Change">
  <data key="d0">Reservoir Only Change</data>
  <data key="d1">procedure</data>
  <data key="d2">A reservoir only change is a maintenance procedure where the reservoir is replaced without changing the infusion set, and does not require filling the cannula.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fill Cannula Screen">
  <data key="d0">Fill Cannula Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">interface</data>
  <data key="d2">The Fill Cannula screen is a display on the insulin pump that guides the user through filling the cannula and suspends insulin delivery during the process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Delivery Suspension">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Delivery Suspension</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin delivery suspension occurs when the pump is on the Fill Cannula screen, and prolonged suspension may lead to hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Introducer Needle">
  <data key="d0">Introducer Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">The introducer needle is a component used to insert the infusion set into the body and is removed after placement, after which the cannula must be filled with insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fill Amount">
  <data key="d0">Fill Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The fill amount is the quantity of insulin required to fill the cannula, which depends on the infusion set type and must be verified or adjusted before filling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Delivery History Screen">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Delivery History Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Insulin Delivery History Screen displays the delivered amount of insulin after a procedure is closed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservoir &amp; Set Option">
  <data key="d0">Reservoir &amp; Set Option</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reservoir &amp; Set Option is a pump function used to set up both the reservoir and infusion set together.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New Reservoir Only Option">
  <data key="d0">New Reservoir Only Option</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The New Reservoir Only Option allows users to replace the reservoir without changing the infusion set when the insulin runs out.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New Set Only Option">
  <data key="d0">New Set Only Option</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The New Set Only Option enables replacement of the infusion set alone when only the set needs to be changed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Rewind">
  <data key="d0">Pump Rewind</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Rewind is a procedure that returns the piston to its starting position to allow insertion of a new reservoir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time And Date Setting">
  <data key="d0">Time And Date Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Time And Date Setting on the pump must be correct before using insulin with the pump for accurate operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clearing The Active Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Clearing The Active Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Clearing The Active Insulin is a procedure required before first use of the pump to ensure accurate insulin delivery and prevent injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Washing Hands">
  <data key="d0">Washing Hands</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Washing Hands with soap and water is a preparatory step before handling the pump or changing the reservoir and infusion set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Removing The Infusion Set">
  <data key="d0">Removing The Infusion Set</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Removing The Infusion Set involves loosening the adhesive and pulling the set away from the body, followed by selecting Next on the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM Settings">
  <data key="d0">CGM Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM settings refer to the configurable parameters of a continuous glucose monitoring system, including alert thresholds and calibration options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Before High">
  <data key="d0">Time Before High</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Time Before High determines how many minutes in advance (5 to 30) the Alert Before High is triggered before the high limit may be reached.&lt;SEP&gt;Time Before High is a configurable setting that determines how many minutes in advance (5 to 30) an alert is issued before reaching the high glucose threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-63f9bd562c68fc510780d6f6629360a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Basal Limit">
  <data key="d0">Max Basal Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The upper threshold for basal insulin delivery; if a preset temp basal rate exceeds this, it becomes unavailable for selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temp Basal Banner">
  <data key="d0">Temp Basal Banner</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A visual indicator that appears on the Home screen during the delivery of a temporary basal rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scheduled Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Scheduled Basal Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The default insulin delivery pattern that resumes after a temporary basal rate is canceled.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Pattern Setup">
  <data key="d0">Basal Pattern Setup</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A procedure used to configure, add, edit, copy, or delete basal insulin delivery patterns on the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Workday">
  <data key="d0">Workday</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Workday is a named basal insulin delivery pattern that can be set up and selected on the insulin pump for use on regular workdays.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Day Off">
  <data key="d0">Day Off</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Day Off is a named basal insulin delivery pattern that can be configured for use on non-working days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sick Day">
  <data key="d0">Sick Day</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sick Day is a basal insulin delivery pattern designed for use during illness, allowing for adjusted insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal">
  <data key="d0">Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal refers to the continuous delivery of insulin to maintain blood glucose levels, which can be suspended or resumed based on system alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resumed">
  <data key="d0">Resumed</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Resumed indicates the restart of basal insulin delivery after a suspension, typically following a low glucose event.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibration Not Accepted">
  <data key="d0">Calibration Not Accepted</data>
  <data key="d1">alert</data>
  <data key="d2">Calibration Not Accepted is an alert indicating the system failed to use a blood glucose reading to calibrate the sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Calibration Not Accepted occurs when the glucose sensor calibration data is invalid or rejected by the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Simplera Sync Guardian 4">
  <data key="d0">Simplera Sync Guardian 4</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Simplera Sync Guardian 4 is a CGM device used for continuous glucose monitoring and integration with the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Check Sensor Insertion">
  <data key="d0">Check Sensor Insertion</data>
  <data key="d1">alert</data>
  <data key="d2">Check Sensor Insertion is a message indicating the sensor may not be fully inserted, affecting calibration and signal detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Change Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">alert</data>
  <data key="d2">Change Sensor is an alert instructing the user to replace the current sensor due to calibration failure or malfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Change Sensor is a prompt indicating that the current glucose sensor should be replaced.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wash Hands">
  <data key="d0">Wash Hands</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Washing hands thoroughly is a recommended step before testing blood glucose to ensure accurate readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum 2 Hour Suspend">
  <data key="d0">Maximum 2 Hour Suspend</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maximum 2 Hour Suspend is a safety limit where insulin delivery resumes automatically after two hours of suspension due to low glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Values">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Values</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus values are the numerical insulin dosage amounts entered into the pump for delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Power">
  <data key="d0">Battery Power</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery power refers to the energy source of the pump, which when exhausted, can halt insulin delivery procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fill Cannula Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Fill Cannula Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Fill Cannula procedure is a process to prepare the infusion system for insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Criticalpump">
  <data key="d0">Criticalpump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Criticalpump is an insulin delivery device that generates error messages when it cannot deliver insulin properly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delivery Limit">
  <data key="d0">Delivery Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Delivery limit refers to the maximum allowable insulin dosage settings, including basal and bolus, that can trigger an alarm if exceeded.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Factory Default Values">
  <data key="d0">Factory Default Values</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Factory default values are the original settings to which the pump reverts after encountering an unrecoverable error.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Error Code">
  <data key="d0">Error Code</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">An error code is a diagnostic identifier displayed on the pump during a malfunction, used for technical support reference.&lt;SEP&gt;An error code is a diagnostic identifier displayed during alarms, used to troubleshoot issues and shared with technical support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian Transmitter">
  <data key="d0">Guardian Transmitter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guardian Transmitter is a device that sends glucose data from the CGM to the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delivery Stopped">
  <data key="d0">Delivery Stopped</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Delivery Stopped is an alarm condition indicating that insulin delivery has been halted due to an error or system limitation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="History Screens">
  <data key="d0">History Screens</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The History screens display personal therapy data from the MiniMed 780G insulin pump, including insulin delivery and glucose values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707424</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph Screens">
  <data key="d0">Graph Screens</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Graph screens provide visual representations of sensor glucose trends and therapy data in the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707424</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="History &amp; Graph Menu">
  <data key="d0">History &amp; Graph Menu</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The History &amp; Graph menu provides access to information about insulin delivery, blood glucose readings, sensor glucose values, paired CGM devices, and alarms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707424</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="History Summary Screen">
  <data key="d0">History Summary Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The History Summary screen shows past insulin deliveries, sensor glucose readings, and blood glucose meter readings for a selected time period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707424</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Meter Readings">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Meter Readings</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose meter readings are manual glucose measurements entered into the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired CGM Devices">
  <data key="d0">Paired CGM Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Paired CGM devices are continuous glucose monitors connected to the MiniMed 780G insulin pump to provide real-time glucose data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Management Mode">
  <data key="d0">Low Management Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Management Mode is a setting in the MiniMed 780G system designed to reduce insulin delivery during low glucose events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time In SmartGuard">
  <data key="d0">Time In SmartGuard</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Time in SmartGuard indicates the number of hours and percentage of time the user was in the SmartGuard automated insulin delivery mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time In Target Range">
  <data key="d0">Time In Target Range</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Time in Target Range represents the number of hours and percentage of time glucose levels were between 70 mg/dL and 180 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Delivery Overview">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Delivery Overview</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Insulin Delivery Overview provides a summary of total daily insulin dose, basal and bolus insulin amounts, and carbohydrate intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Daily Dose">
  <data key="d0">Total Daily Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The total daily dose is the cumulative amount of insulin delivered in a 24-hour period, tracked by the SmartGuard feature and cleared under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Total Daily Dose is the total amount of insulin delivered in a day, including both basal and bolus doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Carbs">
  <data key="d0">Total Carbs</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Total Carbs is the daily amount of carbohydrates consumed, recorded in grams in the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Carb Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carb Bolus refers to insulin doses delivered using the Bolus Wizard for meals, with or without glucose correction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Correction Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Correction Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Correction Bolus refers to insulin doses delivered using the Bolus Wizard solely for correcting high glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Average BG">
  <data key="d0">Average BG</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Average BG is the mean of all manually entered blood glucose meter readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Standard Deviation">
  <data key="d0">BG Standard Deviation</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">BG Std. Dev. measures the variability of blood glucose meter readings over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low BG">
  <data key="d0">Low BG</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Low BG is the lowest recorded blood glucose meter reading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High BG">
  <data key="d0">High BG</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">High BG is the highest recorded blood glucose meter reading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="History Menu">
  <data key="d0">History Menu</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The History menu is a submenu accessible from the History &amp; Graph menu, allowing users to select specific history views like Summary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual/Square Wave Feature">
  <data key="d0">Dual/Square Wave Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Dual/Square Wave feature must be enabled in delivery settings to allow the use of Dual Wave or Square Wave boluses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Count">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Count</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate Count is the amount of carbs in a meal, entered during a food bolus calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbohydrate count of a meal is used by the Bolus Wizard to calculate the appropriate insulin dosage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Now Percentage">
  <data key="d0">Now Percentage</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Now Percentage is the portion of a Dual Wave bolus delivered immediately, adjustable by the user in the bolus setup.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Square Percentage">
  <data key="d0">Square Percentage</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Square Percentage is the portion of a Dual Wave bolus delivered gradually over a set duration, automatically adjusted when Now Percentage is changed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Delivery History">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Delivery History</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Delivery History is a record of past insulin delivery events, including bolus amounts delivered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adjustment refers to the process of modifying the calculated bolus amount before delivery in the Bolus Wizard screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Bolus Feature">
  <data key="d0">Manual Bolus Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Manual Bolus Feature allows users to deliver a bolus without using the Bolus Wizard, by directly setting the bolus amount.&lt;SEP&gt;The Manual bolus feature allows users to manually set and deliver insulin doses, including Square Wave boluses when the feature is enabled.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654d7a203c4eab9f3a89f577edc2a5ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Reading">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose reading is a direct measurement of glucose levels using a blood glucose meter, considered more accurate than sensor readings when acetaminophen or paracetamol is present.&lt;SEP&gt;The blood glucose (BG) reading is a value entered by the user to calibrate the sensor and ensure accurate glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Over-Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Over-Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Over-Delivery refers to the administration of excessive insulin, often caused by falsely high sensor glucose readings from interfering medications.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin over-delivery occurs when excessive insulin is administered, potentially leading to hypoglycemia, especially when sensor readings are falsely elevated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temporary Target">
  <data key="d0">Temporary Target</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A temporary target is a user-programmed glucose target used in the SmartGuard feature for up to eight hours after taking acetaminophen or paracetamol to improve dosing accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Healthcare Provider">
  <data key="d0">Healthcare Provider</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A healthcare provider is a professional who offers medical guidance, including recommendations on insulin pump use and treatment duration.&lt;SEP&gt;A healthcare provider is a medical professional who can advise on safe usage of the SmartGuard feature, including timing after manual insulin injections and duration of temporary targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Display">
  <data key="d0">Display</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The display is a component of the pump that turns on for up to 45 seconds during the self test to confirm functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;The display is part of the pump interface that times out after 15 seconds to conserve battery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Save Settings">
  <data key="d0">Save Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Save Settings allows users to store current pump settings for potential restoration at a later time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707430</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clear All Settings">
  <data key="d0">Clear All Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Clear All Settings erases current pump settings and returns them to factory defaults, requiring reconfiguration through the Startup Wizard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707430</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Target">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Target</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard target is a user-defined glucose level (e.g., 100 mg/dL or 110 mg/dL) that the SmartGuard system aims to maintain by adjusting insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard Target refers to the glucose level setting (100 mg/dL, 110 mg/dL, or 120 mg/dL) used by the system to optimize time in range, with 100 mg/dL as the default.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard target is a user-selected blood glucose level (100, 110, or 120 mg/dL) that the system aims to maintain using automated insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Range">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Range refers to the target interval of 70 mg/dL to 180 mg/dL within which the SmartGuard system aims to keep glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Feature">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus Feature is used to manually deliver insulin doses for meals, required even when the SmartGuard feature is active.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Measurement">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Measurement</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Measurement refers to the continuous glucose (SG) readings collected by the sensor, essential for the SmartGuard system to calculate insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb Information">
  <data key="d0">Carb Information</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carb Information is the input data used by the system to calculate meal boluses, necessary for accurate insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm-Up Period">
  <data key="d0">Warm-Up Period</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Warm-Up Period is a 48-hour initialization phase required before activating the SmartGuard feature, starting at midnight after insulin delivery begins.&lt;SEP&gt;The warm-up period is a required waiting time-48 hours after initial setup or pump reset, or 5 hours after shorter interruptions-before the SmartGuard feature can activate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predictive Low Glucose Technology">
  <data key="d0">Predictive Low Glucose Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Predictive Low Glucose technology is used by the MiniMed 780G insulin pump in Manual mode when SmartGuard is not active to anticipate and prevent low glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Predictive Low Glucose technology is a system function that forecasts low glucose events and adjusts insulin delivery accordingly.&lt;SEP&gt;Predictive Low Glucose technology predicts when glucose levels will fall below a threshold and triggers insulin suspension to prevent hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Predictive Low Glucose technology automatically suspends insulin delivery when sensor glucose levels fall below or are predicted to fall below predefined thresholds, used with compatible iCGMs, CGMs, and ACE pumps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200c1e93d7f4cbc3027cec4d0898dc00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One-Press Serter">
  <data key="d0">One-Press Serter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The One-Press Serter is a device used to insert the infusion set for the MiniMed insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="780G System">
  <data key="d0">780G System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The 780G system is an integrated diabetes management system comprising the MiniMed 780G insulin pump and compatible sensors, utilizing SmartGuard and Predictive Low Glucose technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Device Connectivity">
  <data key="d0">Smart Device Connectivity</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Smart device connectivity enables the MiniMed 780G insulin pump to wirelessly communicate with compatible smart devices for software updates and data display.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d5f110b7de186509276c52b62487bf1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump System">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed 780G insulin pump system is a medical device designed with security features to deliver insulin therapy and protect data integrity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Reset">
  <data key="d0">Pump Reset</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A pump reset refers to the restarting of the pump's software, which may occur due to an error and results in a temporary unavailability of the SmartGuard feature.&lt;SEP&gt;A pump reset caused by electrostatic discharge requires confirmation of correct settings and may disable SmartGuard for 5 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Solutions">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Solutions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin solutions are sensitive to temperature, freezing near 32 °F (0 °C) and degrading above 98.6 °F (37 °C), requiring careful environmental management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Encryption is a security method used by the insulin pump system to protect data transmitted between the pump and paired devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cryptographic Message Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Cryptographic Message Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cryptographic message authentication checks ensure the integrity and authenticity of data exchanged within the insulin pump system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Third-Party Devices">
  <data key="d0">Third-Party Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Third-party devices not authorized by Medtronic must not be connected to the insulin pump to maintain system security and functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unauthorized Software">
  <data key="d0">Unauthorized Software</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Software not authorized by Medtronic must not be used to control the insulin pump system to prevent security breaches or malfunctions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Notifications">
  <data key="d0">Pump Notifications</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump notifications, alarms, and alerts inform the user of system status and may indicate unauthorized connection attempts or interference.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cyber Security Practices">
  <data key="d0">Cyber Security Practices</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Good cyber security practices, such as using anti-virus software and keeping systems updated, are recommended to protect the insulin pump ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unpairing">
  <data key="d0">Unpairing</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Unpairing is the process of removing a sensor or transmitter from the pump’s paired devices, used to correct unintended pairings or reset connections.&lt;SEP&gt;Unpairing is the process of removing a transmitter or device from the pump’s memory to allow re-pairing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bg">
  <data key="d0">Bg</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">BG refers to blood glucose meter readings, including total count, average, standard deviation, lowest, and highest values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sg">
  <data key="d0">Sg</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SG refers to sensor glucose readings, including average and standard deviation, used for reviewing glucose history.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Suspended By">
  <data key="d0">Time Suspended By</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Time Suspended By refers to the average daily duration of insulin suspension caused by Suspend Before Low or Suspend On Low events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sg Review Screen">
  <data key="d0">Sg Review Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The SG Review Screen shows a graph of sensor glucose history based on user-defined high and low limits, which do not affect alert settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Active">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Active</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Active indicates the activation of the SmartGuard feature on the insulin pump for automated insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Exit">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Exit</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Exit indicates the deactivation or exit from the SmartGuard mode on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard exit occurs when the system stops using SmartGuard mode due to sensor deactivation, prolonged insulin delivery based on history, or uncleared suspend events.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard Exit indicates that the SmartGuard automated insulin delivery mode has been deactivated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Message">
  <data key="d0">Message</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A message is a notification from the pump indicating its status or requiring a user decision, displayed with a blue or yellow icon and accompanied by sound or vibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audio Notification">
  <data key="d0">Audio Notification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Audio notifications are tones emitted by the pump in response to messages, depending on the user's sound and vibration settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One-Pulse-Only Vibration">
  <data key="d0">One-Pulse-Only Vibration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A one-pulse-only vibration is a type of tactile feedback used by the pump to notify the user of a message.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Activity">
  <data key="d0">High Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Activity is a named preset temp basal rate option for use during periods of intense physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Moderate Activity">
  <data key="d0">Moderate Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Moderate Activity is a named preset temp basal rate option for use during periods of moderate physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Activity">
  <data key="d0">Low Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Activity is a named preset temp basal rate option for use during periods of minimal physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sick">
  <data key="d0">Sick</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sick is a named preset temp basal rate option intended for use when the user is ill.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temp 1 Through Temp 4">
  <data key="d0">Temp 1 Through Temp 4</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temp 1 through Temp 4 are additional preset temp basal rate options available for custom use in various circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preset Temp Setup">
  <data key="d0">Preset Temp Setup</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preset Temp Setup is a screen within the pump that allows users to add, edit, rename, or delete preset temp basal rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atemp Target">
  <data key="d0">Atemp Target</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Atemp target refers to a temporary setting used in insulin pump programming, typically for up to eight hours or as recommended by a healthcare provider.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Values">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Values</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose values are measurements obtained from a blood sample used for calculating insulin bolus doses and system calibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Glucose Readings">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Glucose Readings</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor glucose readings are real-time glucose measurements from a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) device, not to be used for bolus calculations when acetaminophen is present.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device">
  <data key="d0">Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The device refers to the medical equipment, including the insulin pump and CGM, used for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Choking Hazard">
  <data key="d0">Choking Hazard</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The product poses a choking hazard for young children due to small parts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User's Manual">
  <data key="d0">User's Manual</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The User's Manual is a document that contains updated safety warnings and operational instructions for the meter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fingertip">
  <data key="d0">Fingertip</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The fingertip is the recommended site for blood sampling when entering blood glucose values into the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Sample">
  <data key="d0">Blood Sample</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood samples from the fingertip are used for BG meter readings; palm samples are not recommended due to lack of study with the SmartGuard feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Palm">
  <data key="d0">Palm</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The palm is not an approved site for blood glucose sampling as it has not been studied for use with the SmartGuard feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magnetic Fields">
  <data key="d0">Magnetic Fields</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnetic fields from devices like MRI or diathermy equipment can interfere with the pump and CGM, potentially causing malfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MRI Equipment">
  <data key="d0">MRI Equipment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MRI equipment generates strong magnetic fields that can damage the pump or CGM device, requiring their removal before use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strong Magnetic Field">
  <data key="d0">Strong Magnetic Field</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exposure to a strong magnetic field can cause the pump or CGM to malfunction, leading to serious injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magnet">
  <data key="d0">Magnet</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnets, including those in pump cases with magnetic clasps, can interfere with the pump's motor and cause malfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Motor">
  <data key="d0">Motor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The motor inside the pump regulates insulin delivery; damage from magnets can lead to device malfunction and serious injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="X-Ray Scanning Machine">
  <data key="d0">X-Ray Scanning Machine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">X-ray scanning machines can damage pump components, potentially causing insulin over-delivery and hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707444</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Full-Body Scanner">
  <data key="d0">Full-Body Scanner</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Full-body scanners require the removal of all system components; users should request alternative screening methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707444</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alternative Screening Method">
  <data key="d0">Alternative Screening Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An alternative screening method should be requested to avoid removing the pump and CGM device during security checks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707444</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airport Security Systems">
  <data key="d0">Airport Security Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">system</data>
  <data key="d2">Airport security systems include x-ray and full-body scanners that may damage the pump or CGM if not properly managed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707444</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airplane">
  <data key="d0">Airplane</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The pump can be used on an airplane, but precautions listed on the Medical Emergency Card must be followed to avoid injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="General Precautions">
  <data key="d0">General Precautions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">General precautions include monitoring for infusion set leaks, insulin degradation, and skin reactions related to pump use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Skin Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin reactions such as redness, swelling, or rash may occur where the pump contacts the skin and should be monitored.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Wound">
  <data key="d0">Skin Wound</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The pump should not come into contact with skin wounds as its materials are only evaluated for use with intact skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Drop">
  <data key="d0">Pump Drop</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Dropping the pump may damage its components or compromise waterproofing, requiring glucose monitoring for four hours afterward.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Waterproof Capability">
  <data key="d0">Waterproof Capability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The pump is waterproof up to 8 feet for 30 minutes when undamaged and properly assembled.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outer Casing">
  <data key="d0">Outer Casing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The outer casing of the pump may lose waterproof properties if cracked due to impact or damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Damage">
  <data key="d0">Water Damage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">If water enters the pump, it may malfunction; users should check blood glucose and seek technical support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Date And Time Settings">
  <data key="d0">Date And Time Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">After a pump reset, users must confirm the correct date and time settings are restored.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Alarms">
  <data key="d0">Pump Alarms</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump alarms, alerts, and messages provide information on system status and malfunctions; detailed in page 301 of the manual.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cgm Device">
  <data key="d0">Cgm Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The CGM device is a medical device used for continuous glucose monitoring and is involved in various alerts and messages related to sensor pairing, calibration, and safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Expired">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Expired</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sensor Expired alert indicates that the sensor has reached the end of its useful life and must be replaced.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Expired indicates that the glucose sensor has surpassed its usable lifespan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System Component">
  <data key="d0">System Component</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">System component refers to any part of the MiniMed 780G system, including the pump, CGM devices, reservoirs, infusion sets, and software.&lt;SEP&gt;System component refers to parts of the CGM system, including the device and sensor, detailed in the user manual on page 129.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Connected">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Connected</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Connected is a message indicating that the transmitter has detected a sensor connection, prompting the user to either start a new sensor or reconnect an existing one.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Sensor Soon">
  <data key="d0">Change Sensor Soon</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Change Sensor Soon is an alert reminding the user that the sensor life is ending soon and a replacement should be prepared.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Error">
  <data key="d0">Pump Error</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Error is an alarm condition that occurs after power loss, requiring the user to restart the pump to resume operation.&lt;SEP&gt;A Pump Error alarm indicates a malfunction in the insulin pump requiring user intervention to restart.&lt;SEP&gt;Pump Error is a general alert indicating a malfunction in the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Loss">
  <data key="d0">Power Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Power loss is an event that causes a complete pump reset, requiring a 5-hour update period before SmartGuard active insulin data is valid again.&lt;SEP&gt;The Power Loss alarm appears when the AA battery was removed for more than 10 minutes or power was interrupted, requiring time and date re-entry.&lt;SEP&gt;Power Loss indicates that the device has lost power, possibly due to battery failure or disconnection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Cleared">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Cleared</data>
  <data key="d1">alert</data>
  <data key="d2">The Active Insulin Cleared alert indicates that any previously tracked active insulin has been reset to zero, requiring manual confirmation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time &amp; Date Screen">
  <data key="d0">Time &amp; Date Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">interface</data>
  <data key="d2">The Time &amp; Date screen allows the user to re-enter current time and date after a power loss event.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64e8ebad9c2de6a1aeba1645920f2e35</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High &amp; Low Alerts">
  <data key="d0">High &amp; Low Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">High &amp; Low Alerts include alerts for high and low glucose levels, such as alert on high, alert before high, alert on low, alert before low, suspend before low, and resume basal alert.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibration Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Calibration Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Calibration Alerts are notifications related to entering BG readings for calibrating the CGM device, included under All Sensor Alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Alerts Only">
  <data key="d0">High Alerts Only</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">High Alerts Only is an alert silencing option that allows users to silence only high glucose-related alerts while keeping low glucose alerts active.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2cc4a95eb5f47fc9afc3b30fb1364490</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Alert">
  <data key="d0">High Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Alert is a notification system that triggers when the glucose level reaches or exceeds a user-defined high limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Custom Rate">
  <data key="d0">Custom Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Custom Rate allows users to manually enter a specific glucose rise threshold for the Rise Alert, beyond the predefined arrow-based rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Setup Screen">
  <data key="d0">High Setup Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The High Setup Screen is an interface where users configure high glucose alert settings, including time segments and associated limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Snooze Screen">
  <data key="d0">Snooze Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Snooze Screen is an interface that allows users to set the duration before a high or low glucose alert repeats.&lt;SEP&gt;The Snooze Screen is a menu within the insulin pump system where users can configure the Low Snooze duration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Snooze High &amp; Low">
  <data key="d0">Snooze High &amp; Low</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Snooze High &amp; Low is a menu option where users can configure the High Snooze and Low Snooze durations for repeated alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG Reading">
  <data key="d0">SG Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SG reading refers to a specific measurement of sensor glucose at a given time, which may appear on the sensor graph or be used in trend analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High SG Limit">
  <data key="d0">High SG Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High SG limit is a user-defined threshold on the sensor graph indicating the upper boundary of the desired glucose range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low SG Limit">
  <data key="d0">Low SG Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low SG limit is a user-defined threshold on the sensor graph indicating the lower boundary of the desired glucose range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="3-Hour Graph">
  <data key="d0">3-Hour Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The 3-hour graph is a time-specific view of sensor glucose readings displayed on the sensor graph for detailed trend analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="6-Hour Graph">
  <data key="d0">6-Hour Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The 6-hour graph is a time-specific view of sensor glucose readings that can be navigated from the 3-hour graph for broader trend analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="12-Hour Graph">
  <data key="d0">12-Hour Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The 12-hour graph is a time-specific view of sensor glucose readings accessible via navigation on the sensor graph.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="24-Hour Graph">
  <data key="d0">24-Hour Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The 24-hour graph is a full-day view of sensor glucose readings available for trend evaluation on the sensor graph.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Alert">
  <data key="d0">Low Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Alert is a feature that notifies the user when sensor glucose (SG) values reach or fall below a preset low limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Snooze">
  <data key="d0">Low Snooze</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Snooze sets a time interval after which a low glucose alert will repeat if the condition persists.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alarms">
  <data key="d0">Alarms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alarms are critical notifications that require immediate attention, such as insulin flow blockage or low glucose levels, indicated by red icons and repeated audio signals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Messages">
  <data key="d0">Messages</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Messages are informational texts displayed on the pump screen as part of the notification system, providing instructions or status updates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Notification Icon">
  <data key="d0">Notification Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The notification icon is a visual indicator on the pump interface that displays pending notifications, with a white flap indicating multiple messages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Siren">
  <data key="d0">Pump Siren</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The pump siren is an emergency audio alarm that activates during critical errors, escalating in intensity if the condition is not resolved within 10 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Pump Error">
  <data key="d0">Critical Pump Error</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A critical pump error is a severe malfunction that stops insulin delivery, triggering a warning screen and activating the pump siren.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical Pump Error is a severe malfunction alert indicating a significant issue with the insulin pump operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Flow Blocked">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Flow Blocked</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin flow blocked is an alarm condition indicating a physical obstruction in insulin delivery, requiring immediate inspection of the reservoir and infusion set.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Flow Blocked indicates a physical obstruction preventing insulin from being delivered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Glucose Level">
  <data key="d0">Low Glucose Level</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A low glucose level is a condition that triggers an alarm, indicating the need for immediate corrective action to prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Battery">
  <data key="d0">Low Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Low battery is an alert condition indicating that the pump's power is running low and requires battery replacement soon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sound Settings">
  <data key="d0">Sound Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sound settings control the audio feedback of the pump, including alarm tones and alert beeps, based on user configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vibration Settings">
  <data key="d0">Vibration Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vibration settings determine whether the pump provides haptic feedback during alarms or alerts, configurable by the user.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Notification Screen">
  <data key="d0">Notification Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The notification screen displays active alarms, alerts, and messages, requiring user interaction to clear or address them.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Silence Icon">
  <data key="d0">Alert Silence Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">indicator</data>
  <data key="d2">The alert silence icon appears on the Home screen to indicate when sensor alerts have been silenced.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silencing Sensor Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Silencing Sensor Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">procedure</data>
  <data key="d2">Silencing sensor alerts is a temporary action that stops alert notifications, detailed on page 176.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707452</data>
