<node id="Low Battery Transmitter">
  <data key="d0">Low Battery Transmitter</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Battery Transmitter indicates that the glucose sensor transmitter has low battery power.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Basal Error">
  <data key="d0">Max Basal Error</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Max Basal Error is an alert indicating that the programmed basal insulin rate exceeds the maximum allowed limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="No Calibration Occurred">
  <data key="d0">No Calibration Occurred</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">No Calibration Occurred indicates that the glucose sensor failed to calibrate within the expected timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outside Typical Range">
  <data key="d0">Outside Typical Range</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Outside Typical Range is a notification that sensor readings are outside the normal operational range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pair New Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Pair New Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Pair New Sensor is a prompt to initiate the pairing process between the pump and a new glucose sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Possible Signal Interference">
  <data key="d0">Possible Signal Interference</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Possible Signal Interference indicates that wireless communication between devices may be disrupted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservoir Estimate">
  <data key="d0">Reservoir Estimate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Reservoir Estimate is the system's calculated amount of insulin remaining in the reservoir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Failed To Pair With Pump">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Failed To Pair With Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Failed To Pair With Pump indicates a failure in establishing a wireless connection between the sensor and the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Started">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Started</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Started indicates that the SmartGuard automated insulin delivery mode has been activated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Will Exit Soon">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Will Exit Soon</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Will Exit Soon is a warning that the SmartGuard mode will deactivate shortly, requiring user action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transmitter Battery Depleted">
  <data key="d0">Transmitter Battery Depleted</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Transmitter Battery Depleted indicates that the glucose sensor transmitter has completely lost power.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Updated Low SG Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Updated Low SG Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Updated Low SG Alarm reflects a modified threshold or behavior for low glucose alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Updated Low SG Alarm is a revised version of the low glucose alert within the SmartGuard system, improving sensitivity and response.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Yellow Icon">
  <data key="d0">Yellow Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Yellow Icon is a visual indicator displayed on the device screen to signal warnings or non-critical alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Silence In SmartGuard Feature">
  <data key="d0">Alert Silence In SmartGuard Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert Silence In SmartGuard Feature allows temporary muting of alerts while the SmartGuard mode is active.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alternate Controller Enabled">
  <data key="d0">Alternate Controller Enabled</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Alternate Controller Enabled indicates that a secondary device or method is being used to control the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose (BG)">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose (BG)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose (BG) refers to the measured concentration of glucose in the blood, used for insulin dosing decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Screen">
  <data key="d0">Basal Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal Screen is a device interface that displays current basal insulin delivery settings and history.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Radio Frequency Interference">
  <data key="d0">Radio Frequency Interference</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Radio frequency interference refers to disruptions in device communication caused by external RF-emitting devices, potentially affecting the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cellular Phones">
  <data key="d0">Cellular Phones</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cellular phones are devices that emit radio frequencies and may interfere with the MiniMed 780G system if not paired with it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wireless Technology">
  <data key="d0">Wireless Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Wireless technology includes devices such as cordless phones, walkie-talkies, and wireless networks that emit RF signals and may disrupt communication between the sensor and insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electric Can Openers">
  <data key="d0">Electric Can Openers</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Electric can openers are household appliances that emit electromagnetic fields and may affect the operation of the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microwaves">
  <data key="d0">Microwaves</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microwaves are kitchen appliances that emit electromagnetic radiation and may contribute to electromagnetic interference with the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Induction Ovens">
  <data key="d0">Induction Ovens</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Induction ovens are cooking devices that generate electromagnetic fields and may interfere with the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin To Carb Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Insulin To Carb Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin to carb ratio is a pump setting that determines insulin dosage based on carbohydrate intake and must be set before using Suspend features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alc">
  <data key="d0">Alc</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Alc refers to glycated hemoglobin, a measure of long-term blood glucose control, which may decrease rapidly during the beginning of insulin pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemic Event">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemic Event</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A hypoglycemic event is a condition of abnormally low blood glucose levels that may result from insulin over-delivery or unrecognized pump alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperglycemic Event">
  <data key="d0">Hyperglycemic Event</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A hyperglycemic event is a condition of abnormally high blood glucose levels that may occur due to under-delivery of insulin or interruption in pump function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM Device Alarms, Alerts, and Messages">
  <data key="d0">CGM Device Alarms, Alerts, and Messages</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">These are alerts from compatible CGM devices that notify users of glucose trends, system issues, or calibration needs.&lt;SEP&gt;CGM Device Alarms, Alerts, and Messages is a section in the user guide that provides information on troubleshooting alerts such as failed sensor pairing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Feature Alerts and Messages">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Feature Alerts and Messages</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">These are system-generated messages related to the operation and status of the SmartGuard technology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CareLink Software Alerts and Messages">
  <data key="d0">CareLink Software Alerts and Messages</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">CareLink software provides alerts and messages related to data management and system performance for the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consumables">
  <data key="d0">Consumables</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consumables include MiniMed or Medtronic reservoirs and infusion sets specifically designed for use with the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Verifying System Performance">
  <data key="d0">Verifying System Performance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Verifying system performance involves using blood glucose meter readings to confirm the accuracy of the CGM system, especially when using the Instinct sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Index">
  <data key="d0">Index</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The index is a reference tool at the end of the user guide for locating specific topics and information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Specifications">
  <data key="d0">Technical Specifications</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Technical specifications include detailed performance and operational data for the MiniMed 780G system, available in the Technical Guide.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Performance Data">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Performance Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical performance data provides evidence of the MiniMed 780G system's effectiveness and safety in real-world use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed 780G System Technical Guide">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed 780G System Technical Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed 780G System Technical Guide contains detailed technical specifications and clinical performance data for the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb895500e1ede1e328c1d3f50e5e9b36</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb Count">
  <data key="d0">Carb Count</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carb count is the amount of carbohydrates in a meal, entered by the user to help calculate insulin dosage for a bolus.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-654d7a203c4eab9f3a89f577edc2a5ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EMC">
  <data key="d0">EMC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The acronym for electromagnetic compatibility, referring to the ability of electronic devices to function without interference.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ESD">
  <data key="d0">ESD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The acronym for electrostatic discharge, a sudden flow of electricity between two charged objects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPS">
  <data key="d0">GPS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The acronym for global positioning system, a satellite-based navigation system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Stacking">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Stacking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Occurs when a bolus is delivered while active insulin from a previous bolus is still lowering glucose levels, potentially leading to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IV">
  <data key="d0">IV</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The acronym for intravenous, referring to administration of substances directly into a vein.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lock">
  <data key="d0">Lock</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A feature that prevents accidental button presses on the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NiMH">
  <data key="d0">NiMH</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The acronym for nickel-metal hydride, a type of rechargeable battery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Save Mode">
  <data key="d0">Power Save Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A state in which the insulin pump is fully functional, but the screen goes dark to save power.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Alert Settings">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Alert Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor alert settings define the high and low thresholds for glucose levels, used in Manual mode and with the SmartGuard feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clear Active Insulin Feature">
  <data key="d0">Clear Active Insulin Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Clear Active Insulin feature is used to reset the active insulin and total daily dose tracked by the SmartGuard feature, particularly after practice use or incorrect insulin programming.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rony">
  <data key="d0">Rony</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Rony is a person mentioned in the document, possibly an author, contributor, or contact associated with the device or documentation.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Software">
  <data key="d0">Pump Software</data>
  <data key="d1">software</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Software refers to the embedded software system running on the insulin pump, responsible for managing insulin delivery, alarms, and user interface functions.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Very High Basal Setting Alert">
  <data key="d0">Very High Basal Setting Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Very High Basal Setting Alert is a warning issued when an unusually high basal insulin rate is programmed, indicating potential risk.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm Up Not Started Alert">
  <data key="d0">Warm Up Not Started Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Warm Up Not Started Alert notifies the user that the sensor has not begun its warm-up phase after activation.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Delivery Information">
  <data key="d0">Basal Delivery Information</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal Delivery Information includes details about the ongoing and scheduled basal insulin rates delivered by the pump.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Settings History">
  <data key="d0">Pump Settings History</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Settings History is a log of past configurations and adjustments made to the insulin pump settings.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System Performance">
  <data key="d0">System Performance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">System Performance refers to the operational efficiency and accuracy of the insulin pump and its integrated components.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System Security">
  <data key="d0">System Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">System Security encompasses the protective measures in place to prevent unauthorized access or tampering with the insulin pump system.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tubing Filling">
  <data key="d0">Tubing Filling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Tubing Filling is the process of priming the insulin delivery tubing to ensure proper flow from the reservoir to the infusion site.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
