  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Compatibility">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Compatibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor compatibility refers to the requirement that sensors and pumps must be matched according to specifications to ensure proper system function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System User Guide">
  <data key="d0">System User Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The System User Guide provides instructions for use, safety information, and precautions for the MiniMed 780G system.&lt;SEP&gt;The System User Guide provides detailed instructions on sensor compatibility, pump operation, and troubleshooting procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Care">
  <data key="d0">Pump Care</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Care refers to the procedures for cleaning, storing, and maintaining the MiniMed 780G insulin pump to ensure proper function and longevity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cleaning Supplies">
  <data key="d0">Cleaning Supplies</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cleaning Supplies include soft cloths, mild detergent, clean water, 70% alcohol, cotton swabs, and cotton balls used for cleaning the MiniMed 780G insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Compartment Housing">
  <data key="d0">Battery Compartment Housing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Battery Compartment Housing is a part of the MiniMed 780G insulin pump that must be kept dry and cleaned of battery residue to prevent malfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33e0b546270469b67078fda39a4e47d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atmospheric Pressure Changes">
  <data key="d0">Atmospheric Pressure Changes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Atmospheric pressure changes can temporarily affect the functionality of the pump buttons, such as during airplane travel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airplane Travel">
  <data key="d0">Airplane Travel</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Airplane travel is an example of a situation involving atmospheric pressure changes that may cause pump button malfunctions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alkaline Battery">
  <data key="d0">Alkaline Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Alkaline batteries are a type of AA battery that can be used to power the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NiMH Battery">
  <data key="d0">NiMH Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NiMH batteries are rechargeable batteries that can be used in the pump if fully charged.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Factory Settings">
  <data key="d0">Factory Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Factory settings are the default configurations to which the pump may reset after certain errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Saved Pump Settings">
  <data key="d0">Saved Pump Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Saved pump settings are personalized configurations that can be restored after a reset.</data>
