  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A third-party reservoir refers to a non-Medtronic manufactured reservoir that is not guaranteed to work safely with the MiniMed pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Third-Party Infusion Set">
  <data key="d0">Third-Party Infusion Set</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A third-party infusion set is an infusion set not manufactured or distributed by Medtronic Diabetes, whose use with the pump is not supported or guaranteed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prescribing Information">
  <data key="d0">Prescribing Information</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Prescribing information is documentation for insulin products that includes compatibility details and safety instructions, referenced in section 2.2 for alternative insulins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unpair Device">
  <data key="d0">Unpair Device</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Unpair Device is a function that removes the current CGM device connection from the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Simplera Sync Sensor User Guide">
  <data key="d0">Simplera Sync Sensor User Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Simplera Sync Sensor User Guide provides instructions for inserting and removing the Simplera Sync sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Failed To Pair With Pump Alert">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Failed To Pair With Pump Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sensor Failed To Pair With Pump Alert is a system notification that appears when pairing between the sensor and pump fails.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM Device Alarms, Alerts, And Messages">
  <data key="d0">CGM Device Alarms, Alerts, And Messages</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM Device Alarms, Alerts, And Messages is a section in the documentation that provides information on handling device notifications, referenced on page 316.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="App Manager">
  <data key="d0">App Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The App Manager is a tool with the MiniMed Mobile app pre-installed and can be used to start the Instinct sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Instinct Product Insert">
  <data key="d0">Instinct Product Insert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Instinct Product Insert is a document provided with the Instinct sensor that contains instructions for applying the sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-888320702c9e96ce857f425bcf24f293</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Battery Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The battery alarm appears when the pump’s battery is removed or depleted, requiring a new AA battery to resume operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Life Icon">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Life Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sensor Life Icon displays the remaining operational days of the sensor and changes appearance based on status, such as turning red or showing a question mark.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Status Icon">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Status Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sensor Status Icon indicates whether the sensor is warming up, monitoring glucose, requesting a BG check, or is unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temporary Network Connection Icon">
  <data key="d0">Temporary Network Connection Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Temporary Network Connection Icon shows when the pump is connected to a remote upload device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sound And Vibration Screen">
  <data key="d0">Sound And Vibration Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sound And Vibration Screen is used to configure notification settings and temporarily silence sensor alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Check">
  <data key="d0">BG Check</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A BG Check is a blood glucose measurement requested by the system when sensor data is insufficient or requires validation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minimum Delivery Rate">
  <data key="d0">Minimum Delivery Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The minimum delivery rate is a threshold in the SmartGuard system; if delivery is below this rate for three to six hours, an alert is triggered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Delivery Limit">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Delivery Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The maximum delivery limit is a time-based threshold in the SmartGuard system that triggers an alert when reached, requiring user intervention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Suspension">
  <data key="d0">Pump Suspension</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump suspension refers to the state when insulin delivery is paused, which may trigger alerts even if no delivery is occurring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Mode With CGM">
  <data key="d0">Manual Mode With CGM</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064</data>
  <data key="d2">In Manual mode with CGM, the Suspend Before Low feature predicts low glucose and suspends insulin delivery accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707495</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="All">
  <data key="d0">All</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6</data>
  <data key="d2">The "Suspend Before Low" alert stops insulin delivery when glucose levels are approaching the low limit, prompting the user to check blood glucose and take appropriate action.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG Readings">
  <data key="d0">SG Readings</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d2">The Graph Screen displays information about SG readings and their trends over time.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Entries">
  <data key="d0">BG Entries</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d2">The Graph Screen shows BG entries made by the user alongside sensor glucose data.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Correction Bolus Deliveries">
  <data key="d0">Auto Correction Bolus Deliveries</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d2">The Graph Screen displays auto correction bolus deliveries as part of therapy tracking.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707566</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Entries">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Entries</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d2">The Graph Screen includes bolus entries made by the user for mealtime or correction doses.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Interface">
  <data key="d0">User Interface</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d2">Language setting determines the language used in the pump's user interface for better usability.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707646</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Removing Instinct">
  <data key="d0">Removing Instinct</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d2">Removing Instinct refers to the process of taking out the Instinct Sensor for replacement or troubleshooting.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707801</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Expired Alert">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Expired Alert</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sensor Expired Alert indicates the sensor has reached the end of its usable life.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778707824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Units">
  <data key="d0">Units</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d2">The Units setting allows users to specify the insulin level threshold (between 5 and 50 units) at which the Low Reservoir Reminder is triggered.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708027</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend On Low Feature">
  <data key="d0">Suspend On Low Feature</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d2">The Suspend on low feature should not be used without prior consultation and training from a healthcare professional.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708032</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delayed Food Digestion">
  <data key="d0">Delayed Food Digestion</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450</data>
  <data key="d2">A Square Wave bolus is used when food digestion is delayed due to conditions like gastroparesis or high-fat meals.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708120</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elevated Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Elevated Blood Glucose</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d89ab5e0b88b0b0ff15b22db8ae4450</data>
  <data key="d2">A Dual Wave bolus can be used when a meal bolus is combined with a correction bolus to address elevated blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708120</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Activation">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Activation</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c79aff2bfb4c32e8089ffd4b1e5eb5dd</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed Mobile App is used to start a sensor that requires mobile device activation.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Irritation">
  <data key="d0">Skin Irritation</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin irritation, redness, bruising, and pain are potential side effects associated with infusion set use.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708272</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Pump Settings">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pump Settings</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d2">The Suspend Before Low feature should not be used unless insulin pump settings such as basal rates are established.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meals">
  <data key="d0">Meals</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d2">Preset bolus allows users to save insulin doses for meals or snacks that are frequently consumed.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708344</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Interference">
  <data key="d0">Device Interference</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d2">If there is concern about unauthorized connection or interference with the device, 24-Hour Technical Support must be contacted immediately.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708503</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Body">
  <data key="d0">Body</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d2">Connecting an insulin-filled infusion set to the body during training is warned against to avoid accidental insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708511</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Components">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Components</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d2">24-Hour Technical Support provides information on the proper disposal of sensor components.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778708520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FreeStyle LibreLink">
  <data key="d0">FreeStyle LibreLink</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FreeStyle LibreLink is a smartphone application that enables scanning and reading of glucose sensor data from a mobile device and allows data sharing with other individuals or healthcare professionals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-636a6ab7d0bef06e011ae7bf2140d2e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
