  <data key="d0">FreeStyle Libre 2</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FreeStyle Libre 2 is an upcoming glucose monitoring device in Brazil that will support customizable alarms for hypoglycemia and hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-636a6ab7d0bef06e011ae7bf2140d2e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eversense XLR">
  <data key="d0">Eversense XLR</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Eversense XLR is an extended-use version of the Eversense implantable glucose sensor, designed to function for up to 180 days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-636a6ab7d0bef06e011ae7bf2140d2e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Senseonics">
  <data key="d0">Senseonics</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Senseonics is a company based in Maryland that developed the Eversense implantable glucose monitoring system.&lt;SEP&gt;Senseonics is a company that develops and manufactures the Eversense continuous glucose monitoring system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-636a6ab7d0bef06e011ae7bf2140d2e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Upper Arm">
  <data key="d0">Upper Arm</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The upper arm is the anatomical site where the Eversense sensor is implanted subcutaneously by a qualified professional.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-636a6ab7d0bef06e011ae7bf2140d2e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smartphone App">
  <data key="d0">Smartphone App</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The smartphone app is part of the Eversense system, used to receive glucose data, provide customizable alerts for high and low glucose levels, and enable remote monitoring through vibration alerts from the transmitter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-636a6ab7d0bef06e011ae7bf2140d2e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemia Risk">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycemia risk refers to the danger of low blood sugar, which has been observed to decrease with the use of the insulin infusion system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microdoses">
  <data key="d0">Microdoses</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Microdoses are small, continuous basal insulin doses delivered throughout the day via the infusion pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conventional Insulin Infusion Pump">
  <data key="d0">Conventional Insulin Infusion Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The conventional insulin infusion pump is a mechanical device with electronic controls, approximately the size of a pager and weighing 80 to 100 grams, worn externally and used for continuous insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Catheter">
  <data key="d0">Catheter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The catheter is a component of the insulin infusion pump system that delivers insulin from the reservoir into the subcutaneous tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="External Wear">
  <data key="d0">External Wear</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">External wear refers to the way the insulin pump is carried outside the body, attached to the waist or under clothing using cases, clips, or supports.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Real-Time Continuous Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Real-Time Continuous Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Real-time continuous glucose monitoring (rt-CGM) is an advanced form of glucose tracking that provides patients with immediate access to glucose levels, trends, and directional arrows indicating changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time continuous glucose monitoring is a method that provides constant glucose readings and trend data, transmitted wirelessly every 5 minutes to a display device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Oxidase">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Oxidase</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose oxidase is an enzyme used in glucose sensors that catalyzes the conversion of glucose into electrical signals for measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose Oxidase is an enzyme used in biosensor strips that reacts with glucose to produce an electrochemical signal proportional to glucose concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose oxidase is an enzyme used in electrochemical sensors for continuous glucose monitoring, catalyzing the oxidation of glucose to produce an electrical signal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Family">
  <data key="d0">Family</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Family refers to the patient's relatives who may assist in diabetes management and monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3aeabf750656ceb7619502d5fd50ebe6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian Real-Time">
  <data key="d0">Guardian Real-Time</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guardian Real-Time is a continuous glucose monitoring device developed by Medtronic that displays real-time glucose values and trend arrows on a monitor every 5 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minilink">
  <data key="d0">Minilink</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Minilink is a transmitter used in conjunction with the Guardian Real-Time system to send interstitial glucose data to the monitor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Food And Drug Administration">
  <data key="d0">Food And Drug Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is the U.S. regulatory agency that approved the Dexcom G6 system in 2018.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FreeStyle Libre Flash Glucose Monitoring System">
  <data key="d0">FreeStyle Libre Flash Glucose Monitoring System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The FreeStyle Libre Flash Glucose Monitoring System is an intermittently scanned continuous glucose monitoring device that uses a sensor applied to the upper arm and a reader to scan glucose levels and trends without requiring calibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709309</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitor">
  <data key="d0">Monitor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A monitor is a display device used in glucose monitoring systems to show real-time or scanned glucose values, trend arrows, and glucose graphs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709309</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interstitial Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Interstitial Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Interstitial glucose is the glucose measured in the fluid between cells, used by continuous glucose monitoring systems as a proxy for blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Interstitial Glucose is the glucose level in interstitial fluid, measured continuously by the Sistema De Monitorizacao Continua De Glicose.&lt;SEP&gt;Interstitial glucose refers to glucose levels measured in the fluid between cells, used as a proxy for blood glucose in continuous monitoring systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7d99aa72407a6721b69e4da3cbbcba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capillary Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Capillary glucose refers to blood glucose levels measured through fingerstick tests, traditionally used for calibration but not required in some modern systems like Dexcom G6 and FreeStyle Libre.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intermittently Viewed Continuous Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Intermittently Viewed Continuous Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermittently viewed continuous glucose monitoring, such as the FreeStyle Libre system, requires the user to scan the sensor with a reader to obtain glucose data and trends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709311</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patient Adherence">
  <data key="d0">Patient Adherence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Patient adherence refers to the extent to which patients consistently use prescribed medical devices or follow treatment plans, such as wearing glucose sensors regularly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian Real-Time System">
  <data key="d0">Guardian Real-Time System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guardian Real-Time System is a continuous glucose monitoring system developed by Medtronic, consisting of a sensor, Minilink transmitter, and monitor for real-time glucose tracking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dexcom G6 System">
  <data key="d0">Dexcom G6 System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Dexcom G6 System is a real-time continuous glucose monitoring system that transmits glucose data every 5 minutes to a receiver or smartphone without requiring capillary glucose calibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FreeStyle Libre System">
  <data key="d0">FreeStyle Libre System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The FreeStyle Libre System is a flash glucose monitoring system that uses a sensor applied to the back of the arm and a reader to scan glucose levels and trends every 14 days without calibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amgc">
  <data key="d0">Amgc</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Amgc is a method used for monitoring capillary glucose levels, allowing patients to assess glycemic control and adjust insulin doses in real time or retrospectively during medical consultations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7d99aa72407a6721b69e4da3cbbcba7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sistema De Monitorizacao Continua De Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Sistema De Monitorizacao Continua De Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sistema De Monitorizacao Continua De Glicose is a minimally invasive method that continuously tracks interstitial glucose levels, providing direction and magnitude of glucose changes and predicting imminent glycemic excursions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7d99aa72407a6721b69e4da3cbbcba7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Subcutaneo">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Subcutaneo</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Subcutaneo is a component of continuous glucose monitoring systems that measures interstitial glucose levels beneath the skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7d99aa72407a6721b69e4da3cbbcba7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smcg">
  <data key="d0">Smcg</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Smcg refers to the continuous glucose monitoring system that tracks interstitial glucose levels, providing real-time data on glucose trends and predicting imminent hypoglycemic or hyperglycemic events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7d99aa72407a6721b69e4da3cbbcba7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbAIc">
  <data key="d0">HbAIc</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">HbAIc is a blood test that measures average blood glucose levels over time and is used to assess glycemic control and its documented relationship with micro and macrovascular complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Real-Time SMCG">
  <data key="d0">Real-Time SMCG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Real-Time SMCG (tR-SMCG) is a type of continuous glucose monitoring that displays real-time interstitial glucose readings to the patient on a receiver or insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrospective SMCG">
  <data key="d0">Retrospective SMCG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Retrospective SMCG (retro-SMCG) is a type of continuous glucose monitoring that records glucose data for later analysis by healthcare professionals to adjust treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electrochemical Sensors">
  <data key="d0">Electrochemical Sensors</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Electrochemical sensors are used in SMCG devices to measure glucose levels by detecting electrical signals produced during glucose oxidation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Factory-Calibrated SMCG">
  <data key="d0">Factory-Calibrated SMCG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Factory-Calibrated SMCG (SFMG) refers to systems like FreeStyle Libre that do not require user calibration because they are calibrated during manufacturing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Monitoring Devices">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Monitoring Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose monitoring devices are instruments used to measure blood glucose levels, including modern glucose monitors based on earlier models like Dextrostix.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose monitoring devices are medical tools that measure interstitial glucose levels and include both real-time and retrospective systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nighttime Period">
  <data key="d0">Nighttime Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The nighttime period is a time of day poorly monitored by home glucose testing but effectively captured by SMCG for detecting unknown glycemic fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postprandial Period">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The postprandial period refers to the time after meals, during which glycemic fluctuations are often missed by conventional monitoring but detectable via SMCG.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Regimen">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Regimen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The insulin regimen is a treatment plan involving insulin dosing, which can be adjusted based on retrospective SMCG data to improve diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SFMG">
  <data key="d0">SFMG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SFMG refers to factory-calibrated continuous glucose monitoring systems, such as FreeStyle Libre, that do not require user calibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AMGD">
  <data key="d0">AMGD</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">AMGD stands for home blood glucose self-monitoring, a conventional method of glucose testing that has limitations in monitoring nighttime and postprandial periods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ea1c">
  <data key="d0">Ea1c</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ea1c is an estimated Hba1c value derived from continuous glucose monitoring data, representing average glucose levels but not always aligning with laboratory-measured Hba1c.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biosensor Strip">
  <data key="d0">Biosensor Strip</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Biosensor Strip is a disposable component used in glucose meters, containing enzymes like glucose dehydrogenase or glucose oxidase to detect glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Dehydrogenase">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Dehydrogenase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Dehydrogenase is an enzyme used in biosensor strips for glucose detection, enabling the electrochemical measurement of blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wang Et Al. Study">
  <data key="d0">Wang Et Al. Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Wang et al. study is an intervention study showing that very low Hba1c is not linked to reduced cardiovascular events and may indicate frailty or increased mortality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="J-Shaped Mortality Curve">
  <data key="d0">J-Shaped Mortality Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The J-Shaped Mortality Curve describes the relationship between Hba1c and all-cause mortality, with increased risk at levels below 6% and above 8%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Community">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Community</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Diabetes Community is a collective of professionals and researchers who proposed the Glucose Management Indicator to improve glycemic assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 2">
  <data key="d0">Figure 2</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 2 illustrates two cases of different glycemic variability patterns over 15 days with the same Hba1c level, highlighting limitations of Hba1c as a sole metric.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Islets of Langerhans">
  <data key="d0">Islets of Langerhans</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Islets of Langerhans are pancreatic cell clusters responsible for producing insulin and other hormones involved in glucose metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Macrovascular Diseases">
  <data key="d0">Macrovascular Diseases</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Macrovascular diseases are complications of diabetes affecting large blood vessels, such as coronary artery disease, stroke, and peripheral vascular disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microvascular Diseases">
  <data key="d0">Microvascular Diseases</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microvascular diseases are diabetes-related complications affecting small blood vessels, including retinopathy, nephropathy, and neuropathy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advanced Glycation End Products">
  <data key="d0">Advanced Glycation End Products</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Advanced Glycation End Products are compounds formed during hyperglycemia that bind to RAGE receptors, contributing to oxidative stress and inflammation in target organs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAGE Receptors">
  <data key="d0">RAGE Receptors</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">RAGE receptors are cell surface receptors that bind advanced glycation end products, triggering intracellular oxidative stress and pro-inflammatory gene activation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxidative Stress">
  <data key="d0">Oxidative Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxidative stress is a condition of cellular imbalance between free radicals and antioxidants, implicated in diabetic organ damage through epigenetic modulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Epigenetic Modulation">
  <data key="d0">Epigenetic Modulation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Epigenetic modulation refers to changes in gene expression without altering DNA sequence, activated by oxidative stress in diabetes, leading to pro-inflammatory states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptive Immunity">
  <data key="d0">Adaptive Immunity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adaptive immunity is a component of the immune system affected by metabolic changes in diabetes, contributing to chronic inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Coefficient of Variation">
  <data key="d0">Coefficient of Variation</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Coefficient of variation is a statistical marker of glycemic variability, calculated as the ratio of standard deviation to mean glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Deviation">
  <data key="d0">Standard Deviation</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard deviation is a measure of glucose variability, indicating how much glucose values deviate from the mean.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frederick Banting">
  <data key="d0">Frederick Banting</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Frederick Banting was a physician who demonstrated the survival of a diabetic dog by injecting it with canine pancreatic extract, a key step in insulin discovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="James Collip">
  <data key="d0">James Collip</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">James Collip was a scientist who purified insulin for human use, contributing to its clinical application.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Benedict's Test">
  <data key="d0">Benedict's Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Benedict's test is a chemical method used to detect reducing sugars, including glucose, in urine.&lt;SEP&gt;Benedict's Test is a historical method for detecting glycosuria by mixing urine with Benedict's solution and observing color changes after boiling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinitest">
  <data key="d0">Clinitest</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinitest is a test for glycosuria that uses reagents added to Benedict's test for detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Clinitest is a tablet-based test developed to improve glycosuria detection by enhancing the reagents used in Benedict's Test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gelatest">
  <data key="d0">Gelatest</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Gelatest is a test for glycosuria that uses reagents added to Benedict's test for detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Gelatest is a method for glycosuria assessment that added reagents to improve the sensitivity of Benedict's Test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinistix">
  <data key="d0">Clinistix</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinistix is a reagent strip test developed for evaluating glycosuria.&lt;SEP&gt;Clinistix is a reagent strip test for glycosuria, allowing easier and faster detection compared to liquid-based methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combur-Test">
  <data key="d0">Combur-Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Combur-Test is a reagent strip test used for evaluating glycosuria.&lt;SEP&gt;Combur-Test is a reagent strip method for evaluating glycosuria, providing a more convenient alternative to earlier laboratory techniques.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dextrostix">
  <data key="d0">Dextrostix</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dextrostix is the first capillary blood glucose test launched in 1964, based on an oxidase/peroxidase reaction on a semipermeable membrane.&lt;SEP&gt;Dextrostix was the first capillary blood glucose test, introduced in 1964, enabling direct measurement of blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SMGG">
  <data key="d0">SMGG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SMGG appears to be a typographical error referring to SMCG, the Continuous Glucose Monitoring System, used for assessing glycemic outcomes in diabetes treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Haemo-Glukotest">
  <data key="d0">Haemo-Glukotest</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Haemo-Glukotest is an advancement of the Dextrostix test and can still be used today for blood glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T1D Exchange">
  <data key="d0">T1D Exchange</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">T1D Exchange is a research initiative that analyzed U.S. databases and found that only a minority of individuals with type 1 diabetes meet ADA HbA1c targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AACE">
  <data key="d0">AACE</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists (AACE) recognizes point-of-care HbA1c testing in its clinical guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point of Care Testing">
  <data key="d0">Point of Care Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Point of Care (POC) testing allows HbA1c measurement using a small blood drop at the site of care without requiring patient fasting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GlucoTrack">
  <data key="d0">GlucoTrack</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GlucoTrack is a non-invasive glucose sensor that uses electromagnetic technology and heat capacity to estimate blood glucose via a portable device on the earlobe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GlucoWatch G2 Biographer">
  <data key="d0">GlucoWatch G2 Biographer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GlucoWatch G2 Biographer is a non-invasive glucose monitoring device that uses reverse iontophoresis to measure glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pendra">
  <data key="d0">Pendra</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pendra is a non-invasive glucose monitoring device that uses impedance spectroscopy to estimate blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flash Glucose Monitoring System">
  <data key="d0">Flash Glucose Monitoring System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Flash Glucose Monitoring System (SFMG) measures glucose levels in interstitial fluid and provides an alternative method for assessing glucose patterns in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Monitoring of Capillary Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Self-Monitoring of Capillary Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Self-monitoring of capillary glucose (AMGC) is a method used by patients to check their blood glucose levels using capillary blood samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Invasive Glucose Sensors">
  <data key="d0">Non-Invasive Glucose Sensors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-invasive glucose sensors are devices that measure blood glucose without requiring capillary or interstitial blood samples, using technologies such as light, electromagnetic signals, or heat capacity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reagent Strip Testing">
  <data key="d0">Reagent Strip Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Reagent strip testing is a method for evaluating glycosuria using strips such as Clinistix and Combur-Test that change color in the presence of glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semipermeable Membrane">
  <data key="d0">Semipermeable Membrane</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A semipermeable membrane in devices like Dextrostix blocks red blood cells while allowing glucose to pass through for measurement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxidase/Peroxidase Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Oxidase/Peroxidase Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The oxidase/peroxidase reaction is a chemical process used in glucose testing devices like Dextrostix to produce a color change proportional to glucose concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Light-Based Digital Pulp Sensors">
  <data key="d0">Light-Based Digital Pulp Sensors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Light-based digital pulp sensors are non-invasive glucose monitoring devices that use optical technology on fingertips, similar to pulse oximetry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electromagnetic Technology">
  <data key="d0">Electromagnetic Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Electromagnetic technology is used in non-invasive glucose sensors like GlucoTrack to estimate blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709742</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heat Capacity">
  <data key="d0">Heat Capacity</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Heat capacity is a physical property used in non-invasive glucose monitoring to estimate blood glucose via thermal response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709742</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose-Sensing Contact Lenses">
  <data key="d0">Glucose-Sensing Contact Lenses</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose-sensing contact lenses are experimental non-invasive sensors that measure glucose levels in tears, functioning like smart contact lenses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709742</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breath Sensors">
  <data key="d0">Breath Sensors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Breath sensors are non-invasive devices that detect glucose levels through analysis of exhaled breath components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709742</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nanoparticle Tattoo Sensors">
  <data key="d0">Nanoparticle Tattoo Sensors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Nanoparticle tattoo sensors are experimental non-invasive glucose monitors implanted under the skin using tattoo-like technology to detect glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93fcb9633783dfd958b918dec57d02c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709742</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycosuria">
  <data key="d0">Glycosuria</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d2">Benedict's Test was used to detect glycosuria by observing color changes in a heated urine-reagent mixture.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778709756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Care Provider">
  <data key="d0">Health Care Provider</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Health Care Provider is a medical professional who can assess and adjust treatment plans for individuals with diabetes or hypoglycemia unawareness.&lt;SEP&gt;A health care provider is responsible for adjusting blood glucose targets and treatment plans to manage hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Targets">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Targets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose targets are personalized levels that guide diabetes management to prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Treatment Plan">
  <data key="d0">Treatment Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A treatment plan is a structured approach to managing diabetes, which may be adjusted to prevent low blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemic Unawareness">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemic Unawareness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycemic unawareness is a condition where a person does not sense symptoms of low blood glucose and may require intervention to restore symptom awareness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early Warning Symptoms">
  <data key="d0">Early Warning Symptoms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Early warning symptoms are bodily signals indicating low blood glucose levels, which can be regained after avoiding lows for several weeks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A1C Level">
  <data key="d0">A1C Level</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A1C level is a measure of average blood glucose over time, which may temporarily rise when regaining hypoglycemia symptom awareness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Care Team">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Care Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The diabetes care team is a group of health professionals who help manage diabetes and develop plans to address hypoglycemic unawareness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Low Blood Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low blood glucose is a medical condition characterized by insufficient glucose levels in the blood, often associated with diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Low Blood Glucose is a condition where blood sugar levels fall below normal, typically below 70 mg/dL, triggering various physiological responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Low blood glucose occurs when glucose levels drop below 70 mg/dL and requires immediate treatment with carbohydrates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Gel Tube">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Gel Tube</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A glucose gel tube is a portable source of approximately 15 grams of carbohydrates in gel form, used for treating hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Juice">
  <data key="d0">Juice</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Juice is a fast-acting carbohydrate source, with 1/2 cup (4 ounces) providing about 15 grams of carbs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regular Soda">
  <data key="d0">Regular Soda</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Regular soda (not diet) is a source of fast-acting carbohydrates, with 1/2 cup providing about 15 grams of carbs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sugar">
  <data key="d0">Sugar</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Sugar is a fast-acting carbohydrate, with 1 tablespoon used to treat low blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Corn Syrup">
  <data key="d0">Corn Syrup</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Corn syrup is a fast-acting carbohydrate, with 1 tablespoon used to treat low blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Honey">
  <data key="d0">Honey</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Honey is a fast-acting carbohydrate suitable for children over one year old, with 1 tablespoon used to treat low blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hard Candies">
  <data key="d0">Hard Candies</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Hard candies are a source of fast-acting carbohydrates, with quantity adjusted to provide 15 grams of carbs based on nutrition labels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jellybeans">
  <data key="d0">Jellybeans</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Jellybeans are a source of fast-acting carbohydrates, with quantity adjusted to provide 15 grams of carbs based on nutrition labels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Protein And Carbohydrate Snack">
  <data key="d0">Protein And Carbohydrate Snack</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A protein and carbohydrate snack, such as cheese crackers, helps stabilize blood glucose after treating a low.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Glucose Monitor">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Glucose Monitor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Continuous Glucose Monitor (CGM) is a device that tracks glucose levels in real time and can alert users when levels are low or falling rapidly.&lt;SEP&gt;A continuous glucose monitor (CGM) is a device that tracks blood glucose levels in real time and shows trends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fiber">
  <data key="d0">Fiber</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fiber is a nutrient that slows the absorption of carbohydrates, affecting how quickly blood glucose rises.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Protein">
  <data key="d0">Protein</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Protein is a nutrient that, when combined with carbohydrates, helps maintain stable blood glucose levels after treating a low.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chocolate">
  <data key="d0">Chocolate</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Chocolate is not ideal for treating low blood glucose due to its fat content slowing glucose absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peanut Butter">
  <data key="d0">Peanut Butter</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Peanut butter is not ideal for treating low blood glucose due to its fat and protein content slowing glucose absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shelf Stable Snacks">
  <data key="d0">Shelf Stable Snacks</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Shelf stable snacks are non-perishable foods containing fast-acting carbohydrates, recommended for carrying to treat unexpected lows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Young Children">
  <data key="d0">Young Children</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Young children may require less than 15 grams of carbohydrates to treat low blood glucose, depending on individual needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infants">
  <data key="d0">Infants</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Infants may require about 8 grams of carbohydrates to treat low blood glucose, as determined by their diabetes care team.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small Children">
  <data key="d0">Small Children</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Small children may require about 10 grams of carbohydrates to treat low blood glucose, based on individualized plans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Symptoms And Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Symptoms And Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Symptoms and treatment refer to the observable signs of hypoglycemia and the methods used to manage and correct low blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Causes And Prevention">
  <data key="d0">Causes And Prevention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Causes and prevention encompass the factors leading to hypoglycemia and the strategies used to avoid its occurrence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crystal Drive">
  <data key="d0">Crystal Drive</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystal Drive is the street address where the American Diabetes Association is located in Arlington, Virginia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arlington">
  <data key="d0">Arlington</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Arlington is a city in Virginia where the headquarters of the American Diabetes Association is situated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Merrifield">
  <data key="d0">Merrifield</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Merrifield is a location in Virginia used as a mailing address for donations to the American Diabetes Association.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Center For Information">
  <data key="d0">Center For Information</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Center for Information is a service provided by the American Diabetes Association offering support via phone, email, and chat during business hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2451 Crystal Drive">
  <data key="d0">2451 Crystal Drive</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">2451 Crystal Drive is the full street address of the American Diabetes Association's office in Arlington, VA, serving as its primary physical location.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="P.O. Box 7023">
  <data key="d0">P.O. Box 7023</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">P.O. Box 7023 is the mailing address in Merrifield, VA, designated for receiving donations by the American Diabetes Association.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
