  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1-800-DIABETES">
  <data key="d0">1-800-DIABETES</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">1-800-DIABETES is the toll-free phone number provided by the American Diabetes Association for public support and information services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710331</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monday To Friday">
  <data key="d0">Monday To Friday</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Monday to Friday refers to the operating days of the Center for Information, when support services are available from 9:00 AM to 5:30 PM ET.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710331</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="9:00 AM-5:30 PM ET">
  <data key="d0">9:00 AM-5:30 PM ET</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">9:00 AM-5:30 PM ET is the time window during which the Center for Information offers live support via call, email, or chat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2823ad09fe972962f06cf3c6e063f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710331</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Epinephrine">
  <data key="d0">Epinephrine</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Epinephrine, also known as adrenaline, is a "fight-or-flight" hormone released during hypoglycemia that causes symptoms such as sweating, fast heartbeat, and anxiety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710331</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemia Unawareness">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia Unawareness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycemia Unawareness is a condition where individuals do not experience typical symptoms of low blood glucose, increasing the risk of severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Symptoms Of Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Symptoms Of Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Symptoms Of Hypoglycemia include feeling shaky, nervous, sweating, irritability, confusion, fast heartbeat, lightheadedness, hunger, nausea, pallor, sleepiness, weakness, blurred vision, tingling in lips or tongue, headaches, coordination problems, nightmares, and in severe cases, seizures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Related Content">
  <data key="d0">Related Content</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d4d239ddcb372531967a654526e4970</data>
  <data key="d2">The American Diabetes Association provides related content on hypoglycemia and diabetes management through its website.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710346</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Friends, Families, Or Roommates">
  <data key="d0">Friends, Families, Or Roommates</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d2">Friends, families, or roommates should be informed of an individual's hypoglycemia signs so they can assist during a severe hypoglycemia incident.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778710357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Hipoglicemia">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Incorrect insulin administration, such as injection into muscle, can cause hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia occurs when the dose of insulina is too high relative to the body's needs, leading to low blood sugar levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can occur when there is an excess of insulin relative to the body's glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can occur as a result of insulin therapy, especially if doses are not properly balanced with food intake or activity.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,blood sugar regulation,dosage imbalance,medical risk,medication effect,metabolic regulation,treatment dependency</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699633</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Hipoglicemia</data>
  <data key="d16">Insulina</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Agulha">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The needle is used to inject insulin into the subcutaneous tissue at the recommended angle.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery mechanism, injection process</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695768</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Agulha</data>
  <data key="d16">Insulina</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Caneta De Insulina">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A caneta de insulina é usada para administrar insulina de forma precisa e prática.&lt;SEP&gt;A caneta de insulina é usada para aplicar o medicamento, especialmente após aberto o frasco.</data>
  <data key="d10">aplicação,drug administration,medication delivery,uso diário</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696091</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Armazenamento de Insulina">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A insulina deve ser armazenada corretamente, fechada na geladeira entre 2 °C e 8 °C e, após aberta, em local fresco por até 30 dias.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin should be stored separately from heparin and vaccines to avoid mix-ups and maintain efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d10">armazenamento,conservação,contamination risk,storage safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696022</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Aplicação de Insulina">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A insulina é aplicada por meio de dispositivos como seringas, seguindo um passo a passo para garantir segurança e eficácia.</data>
  <data key="d10">administração,uso</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694557</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Insulin Storage Guidelines">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must be stored according to specific guidelines, including refrigeration between 2 °C and 8 °C when unopened and room temperature storage for up to 30 days after opening.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin must be stored according to specific temperature guidelines to maintain its efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d10">storage conditions,storage requirements,temperature control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695764</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Insulin Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The dose of insulin may change over time and requires regular medical review to ensure proper management of blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage change,medical supervision</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694560</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Bomba De Insulina">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A bomba de insulina é um método de administração de insulina usado no controle rigoroso do diabetes, especialmente em pacientes com diabetes tipo 1.&lt;SEP&gt;La bomba de insulina administra insulina al cuerpo de forma continua y programada.&lt;SEP&gt;La bomba de insulina administra insulina de accion rapida al cuerpo de forma continua.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery method,diabetes management,drug delivery,hormone administration,medical device function</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17d4cfa9183f9c1eb5a0c2212479127a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703081</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Paciente">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The patient records insulin doses to help healthcare providers adjust treatment based on glucose trends.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage tracking,treatment adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2dff1c37dd504c2e0f6d3e3541019e15</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694974</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Geladeira">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulinas não abertas devem ser armazenadas na geladeira para manter sua eficácia.&lt;SEP&gt;A insulina deve ser armazenada na geladeira em temperatura entre 2 °C e 8 °C para manter sua eficácia.</data>
  <data key="d10">armazenamento,conservação,temperatura controlada</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696089</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Bolsa Térmica">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A bolsa térmica é usada para transportar insulina com temperatura controlada.&lt;SEP&gt;A bolsa térmica é utilizada para transportar insulina mantendo a temperatura adequada, especialmente em viagens.</data>
  <data key="d10">conservação,manutenção térmica,transporte</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
