</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Seringa de Insulina">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin is drawn into and administered using an insulin syringe, requiring precise preparation to avoid air bubbles.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,dosage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695757</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Álcool 70%">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Alcohol 70% is used to disinfect the rubber stopper of the insulin vial and the injection site before insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d10">preparation,sterilization</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695758</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Algodão">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Cotton is used with alcohol to clean the injection site and vial stopper prior to insulin use.</data>
  <data key="d10">application tool,disinfection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695758</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Parede Abdominal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The abdominal wall is a recommended location for subcutaneous insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,injection site</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695760</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Coxas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The thighs are a recommended location for subcutaneous insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,injection site</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695760</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Nádegas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The buttocks are a recommended location for subcutaneous insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,injection site</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695761</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Braços">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The arms are a recommended location for subcutaneous insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,injection site</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695762</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Lipohipertrofia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Repeated insulin injections in the same area without rotation can lead to lipohipertrophy, which impairs insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication,improper use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695762</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Insulin Preparation Procedure">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must be properly prepared using a defined procedure before administration.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose preparation,medical protocol</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695764</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Insulin Administration Protocol">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin administration follows a standardized protocol to ensure safe and effective delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical practice,injection method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695765</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Hiperglicemia">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper insulin use helps prevent hyperglycemia by regulating blood sugar levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperglycemia occurs when there is insufficient insulin to regulate blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood sugar regulation,medical effect,medication deficiency</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699688</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Prega Subcutânea">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The subcutaneous skin fold technique is used to ensure correct insulin delivery into fatty tissue.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration method,proper technique</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695767</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Insulina Glargina">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin glargine must not be mixed with any other insulin in the same syringe.</data>
  <data key="d10">compatibility restriction,medication safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695769</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Insulina Detemir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin detemir cannot be mixed with other insulins in the same syringe.</data>
  <data key="d10">compatibility restriction,medication safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695769</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Transporte Da Insulina">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must be transported in hand luggage using thermal bags and protected from direct sunlight and freezing.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin must be transported in hand luggage using thermal bags with gel packs, avoiding direct sunlight and freezing temperatures to maintain efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d10">storage condition,storage requirement,temperature control,temperature sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695770</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Atividade Física">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Physical activity increases insulin absorption, raising the risk of hypoglycemia if injected into active muscles.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical activity accelerates insulin absorption, which can increase the risk of hypoglycemia if injection sites are not carefully chosen.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption rate,medical risk,physiological interaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695771</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Manual Prático Preparo E Aplicação De Insulina Sem Mistério">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The manual provides practical instructions on preparing and administering insulin safely.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration guidance,educational resource</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695771</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Diretrizes Da Sociedade Brasileira De Diabetes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The guidelines include recommendations on insulin use, mixing, and administration techniques.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical recommendation,treatment protocol</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695772</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Frasco Lacrado">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A insulina fechada deve permanecer em seu frasco lacrado até o uso, seguindo as recomendações de armazenamento.</data>
  <data key="d10">armazenamento inicial,embalagem</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696090</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Isopor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O isopor pode ser usado para transportar insulina, mas deve-se evitar contato direto com gelo para não danificar o produto.</data>
  <data key="d10">isolamento térmico,transporte</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696093</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Gelox">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O gelox é usado em bolsas térmicas para manter a temperatura durante o transporte da insulina sem congelá-la.</data>
  <data key="d10">refrigeração,transporte seguro</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696094</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Fabricante">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O fabricante fornece instruções sobre o armazenamento, transporte e validade da insulina.</data>
  <data key="d10">orientação,recomendação técnica</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696095</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Insulin Appearance">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Before using insulin, its appearance must be observed; if it is cloudy (when it should not be), has particles, or has changed color, it should not be used.</data>
  <data key="d10">quality check,safety verification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696096</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Application Site">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin should be warmed to room temperature for 15 to 30 minutes before application to avoid pain or irritation at the injection site.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection,temperature effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696096</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Levemir® FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir® FlexPen® is a device used to administer insulina in precise doses ranging from 1 to 60 units.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration method,drug delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698330</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Lipodistrofia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lipodistrofia can occur at the site of insulina administration and may delay the local absorption of the hormone.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption delay,injection site reaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698331</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Amiloidose Cutânea">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Amiloidose cutânea may develop at the insulina injection site and impair the absorption of the hormone.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption impairment,injection site reaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698333</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Novolin® R FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R FlexPen® is a device designed to deliver precise doses of insulin, with incorrect use potentially leading to improper blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage administration,drug delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b93b5769e8df2e4aa6c2c1dc9e65fd85</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699031</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Gravidez">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin requirements typically decrease in the first trimester and increase in the second and third trimesters of pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,physiological change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699633</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Amamentação">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Breastfeeding diabetic patients may need insulin dose or dietary adjustments under medical guidance.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,medical supervision</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699634</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Tiazolidinediona">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Using thiazolidinediones with insulin increases the risk of edema and heart failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Using tiazolidinediona with insulin increases the risk of edema and heart failure, particularly in patients with pre-existing heart conditions.</data>
  <data key="d10">cardiovascular risk,combination therapy,drug combination,side effect risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699635</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Pacientes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients with diabetes require insulin therapy, and their dosage may need adjustment based on diet, activity, or illness.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,treatment regimen</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699689</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Doença Renal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Kidney disease can alter insulin metabolism, requiring changes in insulin dosage.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage requirement,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699690</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Doença Hepática">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Liver disease affects glucose regulation and can influence the body's insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage requirement,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699692</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Glândulas Suprarrenais">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Adrenal gland disorders can significantly change the body's insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d10">hormonal influence,metabolic regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699695</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Hipófise">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pituitary gland disorders can affect insulin needs due to hormonal imbalances.</data>
  <data key="d10">hormonal influence,metabolic regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699696</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Tireoide">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Thyroid disorders can alter metabolism and thus influence insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d10">hormonal influence,metabolic regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699696</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Músculo">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A insulina promove o transporte intracelular de glicose e aminoácidos no músculo, estimulando o anabolismo e inibindo o catabolismo proteico.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose uptake,metabolic regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699722</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Cérebro">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O cérebro não depende da insulina para o transporte de glicose, diferentemente de outros tecidos.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic independence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699725</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Fígado">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">No fígado, a insulina promove a captação de glicose, seu armazenamento como glicogênio e a conversão do excesso em gordura, além de inibir a gliconeogênese.</data>
  <data key="d10">glycogen storage,lipogenesis</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699726</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Glicose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A insulina estimula o transporte intracelular de glicose em tecidos como músculo e fígado, regulando os níveis glicêmicos.</data>
  <data key="d10">cellular uptake,metabolic regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699726</data>
