  <data key="d13">1778703189</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="GS">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulina is administered to lower and regulate GS levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose control,hormone regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191c82775d35bbc705205ed493c43c7d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778701034</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Alarma">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Alarma indicates that insulina is not being delivered properly and requires immediate correction.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery failure,treatment interruption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191c82775d35bbc705205ed493c43c7d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778701038</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Glucosa">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">La insulina regula los niveles de glucosa en sangre para mantener el equilibrio metabólico.&lt;SEP&gt;La insulina reduce los niveles de glucosa en sangre al facilitar su traslado al interior de las células.</data>
  <data key="d10">biochemical balance,metabolic regulation,reduction,regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dfd7b4fa0ccd15d540a9299e77dbf1dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702643</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Higado">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">La insulina indica al hígado que almacene la glucosa adicional disponible en la sangre.</data>
  <data key="d10">signaling,storage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dfd7b4fa0ccd15d540a9299e77dbf1dd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702645</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Pancreas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">El páncreas produce insulina en respuesta a niveles altos de glucosa en sangre.</data>
  <data key="d10">hormone production,regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dfd7b4fa0ccd15d540a9299e77dbf1dd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702647</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Liquido Intersticial">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">La insulina facilita el paso de glucosa desde el líquido intersticial al interior de las células.</data>
  <data key="d10">diffusion,transport</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dfd7b4fa0ccd15d540a9299e77dbf1dd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702648</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Hiperglucemia">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">La hiperglucemia ocurre cuando no hay suficiente insulina disponible para cubrir la cantidad de glucosa en el organismo.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina is used to treat hiperglucemia through correction boluses.</data>
  <data key="d10">insuficiencia hormonal,regulación glucémica,therapy effect,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702804</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Bombas De Insulina">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Las bombas de insulina administran insulina de forma continua y controlada como parte del tratamiento para la diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d10">administración continua,infusión</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-369c90dae1a79813d89bb9a0b31ebfe9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702807</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Insulina Desnaturalizada">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">La insulina puede desnaturalizarse y volverse ineficaz si se expone a temperaturas altas o a luz solar directa.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina can become desnaturalizada if exposed to high temperatures or direct sunlight.</data>
  <data key="d10">degradation,drug degradation,medication efficacy,temperature sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ed992bd0ad5b80f31b2135789dcaa1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702911</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Calculo De Bolus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">El cálculo de bolus determina la cantidad de insulina necesaria para cubrir alimentos o corregir glucosa alta.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose calculation,insulin dosing</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703083</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Cálculo De Los Bolus De Comidas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">El cálculo de los bolus de comidas determina la cantidad de insulina necesaria para cubrir los carbohidratos consumidos.</data>
  <data key="d10">carbohydrate coverage,mealtime dosing</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703085</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Cálculo De Los Bolus De Corrección">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">El cálculo de los bolus de corrección permite administrar insulina adicional para normalizar niveles altos de glucosa.</data>
  <data key="d10">correction dosing,glucose regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d0fdf7fe6f512616144e110952e56f02</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703088</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Equipo De Infusión">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equipo de infusión delivers insulina from the pump to the patient’s body.</data>
  <data key="d10">infusion process,medication delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703188</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Hipoglucemia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Excessive insulina administration can lead to hipoglucemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">therapy side effect,treatment risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703190</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Caducidad De La Insulina">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Caducidad de la insulina refers to the expiration date after which insulina should not be used.</data>
  <data key="d10">expiration,medication safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-01ce95c3ebe034549347b078008daa3c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703192</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Cetoacidosis Diabetica">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">La falta de insulina provoca la aparicion de cetoacidosis diabetica.</data>
  <data key="d10">causal relationship,metabolic regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-17d4cfa9183f9c1eb5a0c2212479127a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703196</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina" target="Indice Basal Temporal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The indice basal temporal function adjusts the rate of insulin delivery for a temporary period.</data>
  <data key="d10">basal rate adjustment,insulin delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e15921d1b7d6415709a3d0c795cefc3c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704454</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Lipoatrophy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lipoatrophy occurs at insulin injection sites and involves progressive loss of subcutaneous fat, forming visible skin depressions.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication, tissue change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696031</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Insulin Injection</data>
  <data key="d16">Lipoatrophy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Needle Length">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Shorter needles (4–6 mm) are recommended for insulin injection to reduce the risk of intramuscular delivery, especially in adults and children with lower BMI.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection safety, equipment selection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695239</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Insulin Injection</data>
  <data key="d16">Needle Length</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Clothing">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin should never be injected through clothing, as it obstructs skin inspection and proper administration technique.</data>
  <data key="d10">contraindication,injection barrier</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694471</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Injection Sites">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must be injected in safe areas free from bones, joints, and major vessels, such as the abdomen, thighs, arms, and buttocks.</data>
  <data key="d10">safety,site selection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694483</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Skin Condition">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The skin must be clean, dry, and healthy before insulin injection to prevent complications.</data>
  <data key="d10">hygiene,injection safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694484</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Alcohol Cleaning">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Alcohol cleaning is recommended in public settings before insulin injection but not always necessary at home.</data>
  <data key="d10">hygiene protocol,setting-based practice</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694484</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Needle Reuse">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Reusing insulin needles is prohibited due to increased risk of infection and lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d10">contraindication,infection risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694486</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Needle Disposal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Used insulin needles must be disposed of in a rigid sharps container to prevent injury and contamination.</data>
  <data key="d10">safety protocol,waste management</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694487</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Needle Bending">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Bending the needle during use can impair insulin delivery and cause pain, so care must be taken during handling.</data>
  <data key="d10">pain prevention,risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694488</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Injection Technique">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper injection technique, including needle attachment, dose setting, and angle, ensures safe and effective insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">effectiveness,procedure adherence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694492</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin should not be injected into areas with lipodystrophy to prevent impaired absorption and further tissue damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Repeated insulin injections in the same location increase the risk of lipodystrophy, which can be prevented by rotating injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication,prevention,risk factor,site avoidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699622</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Inflammation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin should not be administered into inflamed skin to avoid worsening the condition and increasing infection risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">infection risk,site avoidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694494</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Swelling">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin injection should be avoided in swollen areas to ensure proper delivery and prevent complications.</data>
  <data key="d10">safety,site avoidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694495</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Injection Site Rotation">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper injection site rotation is essential during insulin injection to prevent skin lesions and ensure consistent insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Rotating injection sites is a recommended technique to prevent complications such as lipodystrophy and localized cutaneous amyloidosis during insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">best practice,complication prevention,prevention,site management</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699626</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Subcutaneous Fat">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must be injected into the subcutaneous fat layer to ensure proper delivery and avoid intramuscular administration.</data>
  <data key="d10">anatomical site,delivery target</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694552</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Needle Angle">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The correct needle angle, based on length and patient age, ensures insulin is delivered into the subcutaneous fat and not the muscle.&lt;SEP&gt;The correct needle angle during insulin injection ensures the insulin reaches the subcutaneous fat and not the muscle, depending on needle length and patient age.&lt;SEP&gt;The needle angle is adjusted during insulin injection based on needle length and patient characteristics to avoid intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection accuracy,injection technique,safety,safety measure,tissue targeting</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696012</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Insulin Pen">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An insulin pen is used for insulin injection, requiring a 10-second hold after administration to ensure full dose delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin pen is a device used for insulin administration, requiring the user to keep the button pressed during needle withdrawal to prevent insulin or blood reflux.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration method,device use,drug delivery,medical device</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695247</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Insulin Syringe">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An insulin syringe is used to administer insulin, involving steps like air injection, bubble removal, and proper disposal.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration method,injection procedure</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694554</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Pregnant Women">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pregnant women should consult their doctor to adjust insulin injection sites and techniques, especially avoiding the abdomen in late pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical guidance,special consideration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694555</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Alcohol 70%">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Alcohol 70% is used to clean the injection site before insulin injection to reduce the risk of infection.</data>
  <data key="d10">infection prevention,site preparation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694555</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Subcutaneous Tissue">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin is injected into the subcutaneous tissue to ensure proper absorption and avoid rapid entry into the bloodstream.&lt;SEP&gt;Healthy subcutaneous tissue is required for insulin injection, and injections should be avoided in areas with lipodystrophy until tissue recovers.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin injections must be administered into healthy subcutaneous tissue to ensure proper absorption and avoid complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is injected into the subcutaneous tissue to ensure proper absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,administration site,delivery target,drug delivery,injection site,tissue health</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696009</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Subcutaneous Fold">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The subcutaneous fold technique is used during insulin injection to ensure the needle reaches subcutaneous fat and not muscle, particularly with longer needles or in thinner patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,tissue access</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695240</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Injection Site">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Changing injection sites requires careful monitoring due to possible glycemic variation, necessitating intensified blood glucose checks and medical prescription review.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin injections are administered at specific body sites such as the abdomen, arms, or legs, which should be rotated to maintain tissue health.&lt;SEP&gt;The injection site, such as the abdomen, must be carefully assessed, especially in pregnant women, to ensure safe and effective insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration location,glycemic control,regional variation,site rotation,site selection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696016</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Brazilian Diabetes Society">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Brazilian Diabetes Society provides evidence-based recommendations on insulin injection techniques, including needle length and injection site management.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical guidelines,medical recommendations</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695242</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Syringe">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A syringe is used to administer insulin into the subcutaneous tissue, requiring proper technique to ensure complete dose delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug delivery,medical device</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695242</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Insulin Leakage">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Keeping the needle in the skin for several seconds after insulin injection helps prevent insulin leakage.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,medication retention</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695440</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="45° Angle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A 45° angle is recommended for insulin injection in pregnant individuals to ensure the needle reaches the subcutaneous tissue.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696009</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Skin Preparation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper skin preparation, including use of 70% alcohol and complete drying, is necessary before insulin injection in institutional settings.</data>
  <data key="d10">hygiene,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696010</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Subcutaneous Pinch">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The subcutaneous pinch is used during insulin injection to prevent intramuscular delivery and reduce patient discomfort.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,safety measure</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696012</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Insulin Reflux">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin reflux can occur if the needle is removed too soon; maintaining needle dwell time helps prevent this issue.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication,prevention</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696014</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="HbA1c Levels">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper insulin injection techniques, including subcutaneous pinch use, are associated with reduced HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical outcome,treatment efficacy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696015</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="5 Mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The 5 mm needle is appropriate for all individuals and typically does not require a skin fold, inserted at a 90-degree angle.</data>
  <data key="d10">recommended equipment,technique</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696025</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="4 Mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The 4 mm needle is recommended for all individuals for subcutaneous insulin injection and is considered safe and well-tolerated.</data>
  <data key="d10">recommended equipment,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696026</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Table 2">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Table 2 outlines evidence-based recommendations for safe and effective insulin injection techniques based on needle length and patient factors.</data>
  <data key="d10">best practices,clinical guidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696027</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Lipohypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lipohypertrophy develops at sites of repeated insulin injections due to frequent use of the same areas.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication,injection site effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696029</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Skin Pinch">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Maintaining the skin pinch throughout the insulin injection ensures accurate delivery into the subcutaneous tissue.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection accuracy,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696030</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Blood Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">When switching from lipohypertrophic to healthy tissue, insulin doses may need reduction, and blood glucose monitoring should be intensified to guide medical decisions.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical monitoring,dose adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696032</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Localized Cutaneous Amyloidosis">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Repeated insulin injections in the same area can lead to localized cutaneous amyloidosis, which can be avoided by proper site rotation.</data>
  <data key="d10">prevention,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699622</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="Syringes And Needles">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Syringes and needles are required for insulin injection and must be compatible with subcutaneous delivery and not shared between individuals.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration tool,medical equipment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699626</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection" target="HUMULIN R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">HUMULIN R is administered via insulin injection using subcutaneous, intramuscular, or intravenous routes.</data>
  <data key="d10">medication administration,route of delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699627</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="American Diabetes Association" target="Diabetes Care">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The American Diabetes Association publishes the journal Diabetes Care, which features clinical guidelines and research.&lt;SEP&gt;The American Diabetes Association publishes its Standards of Medical Care in Diabetes in the journal Diabetes Care.</data>
  <data key="d10">publication outlet, academic dissemination, publication, academic dissemination</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a8af713fd3913ed050d96cdd321bca3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eab57247c382bad8d5f1e5eb84a62e24</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703061</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">American Diabetes Association</data>
  <data key="d16">Diabetes Care</data>
</edge>
<edge source="American Diabetes Association" target="Injection Site Rotation">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The American Diabetes Association recommends rotating injection sites within a body area for one week before switching regions.&lt;SEP&gt;The American Diabetes Association recommends structured injection site rotation within one body area for a week before switching to another area.&lt;SEP&gt;The American Diabetes Association recommends rotating injection sites weekly, using all quadrants in one area before switching to another.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical guidelines,guideline,health recommendation,health recommendations,medical guideline,recommendation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
