  <data key="d16">Needle</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin Administration">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An Insulin Pen is a practical device used for administering insulin injections.</data>
  <data key="d10">convenience,delivery method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694480</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin Storage">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin pens should not be stored in the refrigerator as cold temperatures can damage the mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Reusable insulin pens should not be refrigerated to prevent damage to their internal mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Reusable insulin pens should not be refrigerated to avoid damaging the internal mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d10">device care,device handling,device preservation,refrigeration avoidance,storage guideline,temperature sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695449</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Needle Reuse">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Needles for insulin pens should not be reused more than three times to prevent pain, infection, and blocked delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">device safety,usage guideline</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694556</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin pens are devices used for convenient and accurate insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The insulin pen is used to deliver a precise dose of insulin during injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pens provide a modern, user-friendly method for insulin administration, especially with pre-measured doses.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,convenience,delivery device,drug delivery,medication administration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695431</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="NPH Insulin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">NPH insulin must be gently rolled before use in an insulin pen to ensure proper consistency.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,mixing required</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694980</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Regular Insulin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Regular insulin, being clear, does not require mixing before use in an insulin pen.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,no mixing</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694981</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Chatbot">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The chatbot interprets "my pen jammed" as a technical problem with the insulin pen and responds accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d10">device troubleshooting,technical issue recognition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1be43b1b23852278983f60d0f150b0f9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694987</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin Stability">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The stability of insulin in pens was unaffected by temperatures up to 37°C and cyclic temperature changes during use.</data>
  <data key="d10">device integrity,thermal resistance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695213</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin Injection Technique">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin pens are preferred for precise dosing, especially in children and patients requiring low insulin doses.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery method,dosing precision</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695233</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Needle Tip">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Priming the insulin pen until a drop appears at the needle tip confirms unobstructed flow and absence of air.</data>
  <data key="d10">device function,flow verification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695235</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Air Bubble">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Priming the insulin pen removes air bubbles to ensure the full registered dose is delivered during injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">device preparation,dosing accuracy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695236</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="HbA1c">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin pen use is associated with better mean changes in HbA1c levels compared to syringe use.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical outcome,glycemic control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695242</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients using insulin pens experience lower rates of hypoglycemia compared to those using syringes.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical benefit,risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695243</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Treatment Adherence">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Meta-analyses show improved adherence and persistence with insulin pens compared to vial and syringe methods.</data>
  <data key="d10">patient compliance,persistence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695245</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Patient Preference">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Studies indicate a trend favoring insulin pens over syringes in terms of patient preference, though some assessment tools were not validated.</data>
  <data key="d10">device satisfaction,usability</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695246</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Quality of Life">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin pen use showed improvements in certain SF-36 subscales, indicating positive effects on quality of life.</data>
  <data key="d10">health outcome,well-being</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695246</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin pens are primarily evaluated in adult patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus for glycemic control and safety.</data>
  <data key="d10">device use,treatment indication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695248</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Syringe">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An insulin pen requires a 10-second needle hold after injection, compared to 5 seconds for a syringe, to ensure full insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Compared to syringes, insulin pens offer greater convenience, portability, and access to shorter, high-flow needles.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration device,comparison,injection duration,practicality</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696026</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Botão Da Caneta">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The botão da caneta is part of the insulin pen that enhances ease and comfort during insulin application.</data>
  <data key="d10">device component,user interface</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695456</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin Cartridge">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The insulin cartridge is inserted into the insulin pen for administration of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">device component,medical use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695529</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin Nph">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin NPH must be placed in a clearly labeled insulin pen to prevent mix-up with other insulins like Insulin Regular.</data>
  <data key="d10">identification,medication assignment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695530</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin Regular">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin Regular is prescribed alongside Insulin NPH and requires its own dedicated insulin pen.</data>
  <data key="d10">identification,medication assignment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695531</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Storage Of In Use Pen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An insulin pen in use must be kept at room temperature, not exceeding 30°C, and should not be refrigerated.</data>
  <data key="d10">device preservation,temperature control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695531</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Three Year Validity">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The insulin pen is valid for three years from first use, after which it must be replaced.</data>
  <data key="d10">device lifespan,replacement cycle</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695536</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Municipal Health Secretariat">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Municipal Health Secretariat provides replacement insulin pens after the three-year period or in case of damage.</data>
  <data key="d10">device replacement,public health service</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695537</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Person With Diabetes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A person with diabetes is the user of the insulin pen and must follow proper usage, storage, and disposal procedures.</data>
  <data key="d10">device user,medical responsibility</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695538</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Needle Dwell Time">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">With an insulin pen, the injection button must be held for at least 10 seconds after delivery to prevent insulin or blood reflux into the cartridge.</data>
  <data key="d10">device operation,injection completion</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696015</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="High-Flow Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin pens are compatible with high-flow needles, which enhance insulin delivery by reducing injection force and time.</data>
  <data key="d10">device compatibility,improved injection experience</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696024</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="4 Mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The 4 mm needle is considered the best option for use with insulin pens due to its safety, tolerability, and effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d10">device compatibility,optimal choice</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696025</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Sistema Único De Saúde">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">In 2019, the Sistema Único de Saúde began dispensing disposable insulin pens, improving access to modern insulin delivery methods in Brazil.</data>
  <data key="d10">healthcare provision,treatment access</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7cb18b1ccdbe7c3a6bbce149470c1ca1</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696027</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="4 mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The 4 mm needle is the shortest available for insulin pens, designed for safe and less painful subcutaneous injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">device compatibility,short length</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696034</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin Dosing">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin pens allow precise dosing, including half-unit increments, and are suitable for both even and odd doses.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose precision,half-unit increments</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696035</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Subcutaneous Injection">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The insulin pen should only be activated after needle insertion into the skin to prevent insulin loss and underdosing.</data>
  <data key="d10">device usage,injection technique</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696038</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Manufacturer Guidelines">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Manufacturers do not recommend storing reusable insulin pens in the refrigerator due to potential internal damage.</data>
  <data key="d10">device care,usage instruction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696039</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin Flow Test">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The insulin flow test is performed on the insulin pen to confirm that insulin is flowing properly before injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">device verification,priming</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696042</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pen" target="Insulin Injection Procedure">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The insulin pen is an alternative device used in the insulin injection procedure for easier and more controlled delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration method,medical device</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696043</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Lipo-Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Rotating injection sites helps prevent the development of lipo-hypertrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Proper injection site rotation helps prevent lipo-hypertrophy, which can impair insulin absorption and glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d10">prevention strategy, risk reduction, complication prevention, skin health</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695438</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Injection Site Rotation</data>
  <data key="d16">Lipo-Hypertrophy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Healthcare Professional">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Healthcare professionals assess and adjust the injection site rotation plan during each consultation to ensure proper adherence and effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;The healthcare professional assesses the rotation scheme at every consultation and adjusts it according to patient needs and therapy progression.</data>
  <data key="d10">evaluation, guidance, evaluation, adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696010</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Healthcare Professional</data>
  <data key="d16">Injection Site Rotation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Regular rotation of injection sites helps prevent lipodystrophy associated with repeated insulin injections.&lt;SEP&gt;Patients are advised to rotate injection sites to reduce the risk of developing lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Rotating injection sites is recommended to prevent lipodystrophy in patients using insulin regularly.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication prevention,prevention,prevention strategy,risk reduction,skin health,tissue health</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699238</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Injection Site Rotation</data>
  <data key="d16">Lipodystrophy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Lipohypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Rotating insulin injection sites helps prevent lipohypertrophy caused by repeated injections in the same location.&lt;SEP&gt;Proper and consistent rotation of injection sites helps prevent the occurrence of lipohypertrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Lack of proper injection site rotation increases the risk of lipohypertrophy, which can impair insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Practicing injection site rotation helps prevent lipohypertrophy and ensures consistent insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication prevention,consistent absorption,prevention,risk factor,risk reduction,tissue health</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696011</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Abdomen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The abdomen is a recommended site for insulin injection and should be divided into quadrants for organized rotation.</data>
  <data key="d10">site selection,systematic change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694463</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Arm">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The arm can be used as an insulin injection site, particularly in the morning, as part of a rotation plan.</data>
  <data key="d10">daily routine,site selection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694464</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Glycemic Control">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper injection site rotation supports stable insulin absorption and effective glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Effective injection site rotation supports stable glycemic control by promoting reliable insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Proper injection site rotation supports stable glycemic control by ensuring consistent insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption stability,diabetes management,stability,treatment consistency,treatment outcome,treatment stability</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696012</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Leg">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The leg can be used as an insulin injection site, particularly in the evening, as part of a rotation plan.</data>
  <data key="d10">daily routine,site selection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694466</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Lipo-hypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper injection site rotation helps prevent lipo-hypertrophy by distributing insulin injections across different body areas.</data>
  <data key="d10">best practice,prevention</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694521</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Skin Lesion">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Rotating injection sites helps prevent skin lesions caused by repeated insulin injections in the same location.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication prevention,skin health</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694551</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Insulin Absorption">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Regular rotation of injection sites improves insulin absorption by maintaining healthy subcutaneous tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Rotating injection sites ensures consistent insulin absorption by allowing tissue recovery and preventing tissue damage.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption consistency,absorption efficiency,metabolic regulation,treatment efficacy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695439</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Diabetes Control">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper injection site rotation supports better diabetes control by maintaining consistent insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">disease management,treatment effectiveness</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694557</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Glycemic Variability">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Rotating injection sites is recommended to reduce glycemic variability caused by inconsistent insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption stability,treatment optimization</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695236</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Insulin Application Technique">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Rotating injection sites is recommended to prevent lipodystrophy and ensure consistent insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption consistency,tissue health</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695623</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Insulin Application">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Injection site rotation is a critical component of safe and effective insulin application, preventing lipohypertrophy and glycemic instability.</data>
  <data key="d10">best practice,complication prevention</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696009</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Cutaneous Amyloidosis">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Rotating injection sites helps prevent cutaneous amyloidosis, which can lead to delayed insulin absorption and poor glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption impact,prevention</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698153</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A sudden change in injection site from an affected to an unaffected area may cause hypoglycemia, requiring blood glucose monitoring and possible dose adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose monitoring,sudden change risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698154</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Injection Site Reactions">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Continuous rotation of injection sites within an area reduces the risk of developing injection site reactions.</data>
  <data key="d10">preventive measure,risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698155</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site Rotation" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Rotating injection sites helps prevent lipodystrophy and cutaneous amyloidosis during long-term use of Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration practice,complication prevention</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699133</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Lipo-Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lipo-hypertrophy causes irregular insulin absorption, reducing the effectiveness of insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption irregularity, treatment efficacy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694535</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Insulin Absorption</data>
  <data key="d16">Lipo-Hypertrophy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Physical Activity">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Factors such as physical activity and daily routines influence the speed and consistency of insulin absorption at injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical activity and its timing influence the rate of insulin absorption and must be considered in injection planning.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption modulation,absorption rate,physiological factor,physiological influence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695237</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Insulin Storage">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Storage temperature affects insulin absorption, with refrigerated insulin showing faster and higher peak plasma levels than room temperature insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption rate,pharmacokinetics</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695248</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">In patients with type 1 diabetes, refrigerated insulin showed faster absorption and earlier glucose infusion peaks compared to room temperature insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic response,pharmacokinetic study</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695249</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Abdomen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin is absorbed fastest in the abdomen, making it the preferred injection site.</data>
  <data key="d10">faster absorption,preferred site</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695994</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Arms">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin absorption in the arms is slightly slower than in the abdomen.</data>
  <data key="d10">moderate absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695994</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Thighs">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin absorption in the thighs is slower and can be accelerated by physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d10">exercise effect,slower absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695995</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Buttocks">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin absorption in the buttocks is the slowest among recommended injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d10">slowest absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695996</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Lipohypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lipohypertrophy at injection sites causes irregular insulin absorption and contributes to unstable glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin injected into areas with lipohypertrophy is absorbed unpredictably, leading to glycemic variability, hyperglycemia, and unexplained hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption variability,irregular absorption,metabolic impact,poor control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695997</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Physical Exercise">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Physical exercise increases insulin absorption and raises the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">hypoglycemia risk,increased absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695997</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="High Ambient Temperature">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">High ambient temperature increases insulin absorption rate, potentially causing hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">accelerated absorption,hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695998</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Fever">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Fever enhances insulin absorption due to increased circulation and metabolic activity.</data>
  <data key="d10">increased absorption,metabolic effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695999</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Hot Bath">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Taking a hot bath after insulin injection can accelerate absorption and increase hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">faster absorption,risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696000</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Hot Compress">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Applying a hot compress to an injection site speeds up insulin absorption and may lead to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">danger,enhanced absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696001</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Massage">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Massaging the injection site increases insulin absorption and should be avoided, especially in children.</data>
  <data key="d10">accelerated absorption,contraindication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696002</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Insulin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin absorption speed varies by injection site and is influenced by physiological and environmental factors.</data>
  <data key="d10">pharmacokinetics,site variation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696003</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Cold Compress">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Using a cold compress slows insulin absorption and may result in hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">hyperglycemia risk,reduced absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696003</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Cold Bath">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A cold bath reduces insulin absorption due to vasoconstriction, increasing hyperglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">decreased absorption,vasoconstriction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696004</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Dehydration">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Dehydration decreases insulin absorption and can contribute to hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic imbalance,slowed absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696005</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Human Insulin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Human insulin absorption varies by injection site, with the fastest rate in the abdomen.</data>
  <data key="d10">site-dependent variation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696006</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Human Insulin Analog">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Human insulin analogs are absorbed at similar rates across all recommended injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d10">consistent absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696006</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lipodystrophy at injection sites can delay or alter the absorption of insulin, affecting blood sugar control.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipodystrophy at injection sites may lead to delayed insulin absorption and worsened glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption impairment,pharmacokinetic effect,tissue condition,treatment efficacy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699011</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Cutaneous Amyloidosis">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Cutaneous amyloidosis at injection sites may impair local insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Cutaneous amyloidosis can impair insulin absorption and contribute to poor glucose regulation.</data>
  <data key="d10">local metabolism,metabolic impact,pharmacokinetic effect,tissue pathology</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699012</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Skin Rotation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Continuous rotation of injection sites supports more predictable insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">pharmacokinetics,treatment consistency</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699144</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Absorption" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Injection of Novolin® R into areas with lipodystrophy or amyloidosis may result in delayed insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">delayed absorption,pharmacokinetic effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699235</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Syringe">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The insulin syringe is used to draw insulin from the insulin vial after injecting air to equalize pressure.</data>
  <data key="d10">medication preparation, dose extraction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694555</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Insulin Syringe</data>
  <data key="d16">Insulin Vial</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin is stored in a vial when unopened and must be checked for physical changes before use.</data>
  <data key="d10">medication container,storage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694535</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Syringe">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The syringe is used to draw insulin from the vial for subcutaneous injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Vials such as those containing Novolin® R must be used with syringes calibrated in insulin units.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage accuracy,drug extraction,injection preparation,usage requirement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699071</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Alcohol 70%">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Alcohol 70% is used to disinfect the rubber stopper of the insulin vial before needle insertion.&lt;SEP&gt;The rubber stopper of the insulin vial should be cleaned with alcohol 70% before use to prevent contamination.</data>
  <data key="d10">aseptic technique,disinfection,preparation step,sterilization</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695435</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Air Injection">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Air is injected into the insulin vial to balance pressure and allow smooth insulin withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose accuracy,pressure equalization</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695221</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Suspension">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin suspension is stored in an insulin vial and must be gently mixed by rolling the vial between hands to ensure uniformity.</data>
  <data key="d10">containment,preparation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695447</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Application">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The insulin vial should be rolled gently, not shaken, to avoid bubbles that could interfere with accurate insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d10">bubble prevention,dosing accuracy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695448</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Application Technique">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The insulin vial must be cleaned with 70% alcohol before aspirating the dose.</data>
  <data key="d10">disinfection,preparation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695676</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Storage">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An opened insulin vial must be stored in a plastic container in the refrigerator and used within 30 to 45 days.</data>
  <data key="d10">shelf life,storage conditions</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695677</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Vial Shelf Life">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An opened insulin vial must be discarded after 30 to 45 days, depending on type and storage conditions.</data>
  <data key="d10">product expiration,usage limit</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695681</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Air Bubbles">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Air bubbles can form in an insulin vial during preparation, and if not removed, can lead to inaccurate dosing when drawing insulin into a syringe.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection safety,preparation risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696041</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Dose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin is drawn from the vial into a syringe to prepare the prescribed dose for subcutaneous injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,dose preparation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696042</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Refrigerator">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin vials, especially unopened ones, must be stored in a refrigerator between 2°C and 8°C to preserve efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d10">storage container,temperature control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696371</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Homogenization">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The insulin vial is the container in which homogenization of suspension-type insulin must be performed before drawing the dose.</data>
  <data key="d10">mixing container,preparation step</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696374</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Medical Team">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Medical Team provides the insulin vial needed to fill the reservoir if the user does not have one.</data>
  <data key="d10">supply provision,support</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703171</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Syringes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Used syringes must be placed in a sharps container to prevent injury and disease transmission.</data>
  <data key="d10">injury prevention,safe disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694495</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Needles">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Used needles must be disposed of in a sharps container to ensure safety.</data>
  <data key="d10">contamination control,safe disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694495</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Lancets">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lancets must be discarded in a sharps container to avoid accidental pricks.</data>
  <data key="d10">injury prevention,safe disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694496</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Insulin Pens">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Disposable insulin pens must be disposed of in a sharps container after use.</data>
  <data key="d10">safe disposal,waste management</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694497</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Insulin Pump Materials">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Materials from insulin pumps must be discarded in a sharps container due to contamination risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical waste,safe disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694498</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Sharps Waste">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sharps waste must be stored in a dedicated sharps container to ensure safe handling.</data>
  <data key="d10">safety,waste containment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694504</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Basic Health Unit">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Full sharps containers should be taken to a Basic Health Unit for safe disposal.</data>
  <data key="d10">public health service,waste disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694505</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Pharmacy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sharps containers can be purchased at pharmacies.</data>
  <data key="d10">acquisition,purchase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694505</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Surgical Supply Store">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Surgical supply stores sell sharps containers for safe medical waste disposal.</data>
  <data key="d10">acquisition,purchase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694507</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Softener Bottle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A rigid softener bottle with a wide mouth can be used as a substitute for a sharps container.</data>
  <data key="d10">alternative container,household reuse</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694511</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Plastic Bag">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A sealed sharps container should be placed in a plastic bag before transport.</data>
  <data key="d10">containment,transport safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694512</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Resistant Transport Bag">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A resistant transport bag is used to carry a full sharps container to a disposal site.</data>
  <data key="d10">durability,transport safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694517</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Children">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sharps containers must be kept out of reach of children to prevent injury.</data>
  <data key="d10">access prevention,safety hazard</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694518</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Pets">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sharps containers must be stored away from pets to avoid accidental injury.</data>
  <data key="d10">access prevention,safety hazard</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694518</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Collection Points">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sharps containers containing used needles and expired medications must be taken to collection points at pharmacies, clinics, or hospitals for proper disposal.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical safety,waste disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698302</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Levemir® FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Used needles from Levemir® FlexPen® must be disposed of in sharps containers to prevent injury and contamination.</data>
  <data key="d10">disposal safety,needle disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698306</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Collection Point">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sharps containers containing used syringes must be taken to designated collection points at pharmacies or health facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Sharps Containers containing used syringes should be taken to a Collection Point such as a pharmacy or hospital for proper disposal.</data>
  <data key="d10">hazardous materials,public health,waste disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699066</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Syringe">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Used syringes must be placed in sharps containers made of puncture-resistant materials to prevent injury.</data>
  <data key="d10">safety,waste disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699113</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Lipo-Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Areas with lipo-hypertrophy are less sensitive to pain, increasing the risk of needle reuse without awareness.</data>
  <data key="d10">behavioral risk, pain insensitivity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694542</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Lipo-Hypertrophy</data>
  <data key="d16">Needle Reuse</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Lipohypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Reusing needles increases the risk of lipohypertrophy, which can impair insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle reuse is a contributing factor to the development of lipohypertrophy at insulin injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Reusing needles, especially more than five times, is significantly associated with the development of lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication,correlation,risk factor,skin complication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696028</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Lipo-hypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Reusing needles more than five times increases the likelihood of developing lipo-hypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694522</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="4 mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Providing sufficient 4 mm needles reduced needle reuse and improved injection practices among diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection safety,supply adequacy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695213</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Reusing insulin needles increases the risk of lipodystrophy, especially when needles are used more than five times.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695247</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Used Needle Disposal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Used needles must be disposed of in a proper container and should not be reused more than three times to prevent complications.</data>
  <data key="d10">infection prevention,safety practice</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695436</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Insulin Application">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Needles should not be reused to prevent pain, infection, and inaccurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d10">risk avoidance,safety practice</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695453</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Insulin Administration">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Reusing insulin needles is an unsafe practice that increases the risk of complications and should be avoided.</data>
  <data key="d10">risk factor,safety violation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695991</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Insulin Pen Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Reusing insulin pen needles increases the risk of infection, pain, and needle damage, and is not recommended for safe insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d10">device safety,infection risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696036</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hemoglobina Glicada" target="Glicemia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hemoglobina Glicada reflects average blood glucose levels over time and is used to assess long-term glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood sugar control,diabetes monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694569</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hemoglobina Glicada" target="Novolin® R FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The effectiveness of Novolin® R FlexPen® in controlling blood glucose is evaluated using HbA1c levels in clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical outcome,efficacy measurement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-581b6c5da621e9091266d2b0e1919308</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699204</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Variabilidade Glicêmica" target="Glicemia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Variabilidade Glicêmica indicates how much blood glucose levels rise and fall during the day, with ideal variation below 36%.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose stability, fluctuation measurement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694570</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Glicemia</data>
  <data key="d16">Variabilidade Glicêmica</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Hipoglicemia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hipoglicemia is defined as blood glucose below 70 mg/dL and requires prompt treatment to prevent complications.</data>
  <data key="d10">low blood sugar, medical emergency</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694571</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Glicemia</data>
  <data key="d16">Hipoglicemia</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Horário Da Medição">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O horário da medição é registrado junto com o valor da glicemia para análise temporal do controle glicêmico.</data>
  <data key="d10">data logging,temporal tracking</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694544</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Refeição">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A medição da glicemia é anotada como antes ou depois da refeição para avaliar o impacto alimentar nos níveis de açúcar.</data>
  <data key="d10">contextual analysis,metabolic response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694545</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Sintomas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A presença de sintomas é registrada junto com a glicemia para ajudar no diagnóstico e ajuste terapêutico.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical correlation,symptom monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694546</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Tempo no Alvo">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Tempo no Alvo measures the percentage of time blood glucose remains between 70–180 mg/dL, a key target in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose range,treatment goal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694572</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Diabetes Tipo 1">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O controle da glicemia é essencial em pessoas com diabetes tipo 1, especialmente em situações de risco como infecções ou falhas na bomba de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d10">disease monitoring,metabolic control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694588</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Diabetes Gestacional">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O controle da glicemia é necessário em mulheres com diabetes gestacional para proteger a saúde da mãe e do bebê.</data>
  <data key="d10">disease monitoring,maternal health</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694589</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Glicemia Capilar">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A glicemia capilar é uma forma de medir os níveis de açúcar no sangue com uso de glicosímetro.</data>
  <data key="d10">medição,monitoramento</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694988</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Paciente">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The patient is instructed to treat low blood sugar promptly with fast-acting carbohydrates like juice or sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;The patient developed hypoglycemia as a result of insulin administration errors.&lt;SEP&gt;The patient experienced hypoglycemia due to administering an incorrect insulin dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Patients must learn to recognize their personal symptoms of hypoglycemia to take timely corrective actions.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,clinical outcome,emergency action,health risk,symptom response,symptomptom recognition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2dff1c37dd504c2e0f6d3e3541019e15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699632</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Hipoglicemia</data>
  <data key="d16">Paciente</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Atividade Física">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Exercising after insulin injection in active body parts like legs can lead to hypoglycemia due to faster absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">physiological effect, health risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695771</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Atividade Física</data>
  <data key="d16">Hipoglicemia</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Seringa com Agulha Removível">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O uso de seringa com agulha removível pode aumentar o risco de hipoglicemia devido à aplicação no músculo.</data>
  <data key="d10">complicações,risco</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694559</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Hipoglicemia Grave">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hipoglicemia Grave is a more severe form of hypoglycemia, occurring when glucose falls below 54 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d10">critical threshold,severity classification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694570</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Carboidrato de Ação Rápida">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Carboidrato de Ação Rápida is used to quickly raise blood glucose during hypoglycemic episodes.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose elevation,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694572</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Idosos Frágeis">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">For idosos frágeis, the focus is on avoiding hypoglycemia and ensuring comfort rather than strict glucose targets.</data>
  <data key="d10">individualized care,safety focus</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694573</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Sensor De Glicose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O uso de sensor de glicose está associado a uma redução na frequência de episódios de hipoglicemia durante a gravidez.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose monitoring,risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694591</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Levemir">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir affects blood glucose levels and may cause hipoglicemia, which can impair concentration and reaction time.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia é a reação adversa mais frequente associada ao uso de Levemir, ocorrendo quando a dose é desproporcional à necessidade do paciente.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,dose dependency,hypoglycemic effect,symptom awareness</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698218</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Mulheres Grávidas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pregnant women using insulin are at risk of hipoglicemia, which may impair their ability to drive or operate machinery, especially if warning signs are reduced.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">risk during pregnancy,symptom recognition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698220</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Direção de Veículos">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hipoglicemia can impair concentration and reaction time, posing a danger when driving or operating machinery, requiring patients to take preventive measures.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">cognitive impairment,driving risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698220</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="MedDRA">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">MedDRA provides the framework for categorizing hypoglycemia and other adverse reactions based on clinical data.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse event coding,classification system</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698318</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Glucagon">
  <data key="d8">5.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucagon is used to treat severe hipoglicemia, especially when the patient becomes unconscious, by raising blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon is administered to treat severe hypoglycemia when the patient is unconscious.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon is used to treat severe hypoglycemia in patients who have lost consciousness and cannot consume sugar orally.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon is used to treat severe hypoglycemia when patients are unable to consume sugar orally.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon administered intramuscularly or subcutaneously is used to treat severe hypoglycemia, including coma, seizures, or neurological damage.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood sugar regulation,emergency response,emergency treatment,hormonal intervention,hormone therapy,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d717433722cc9ac8e746440493df9010</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699634</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Glicose">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glicose is administered orally for mild hipoglicemia or intravenously for severe cases to restore normal blood sugar levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose is used to treat hypoglycemia, either orally for mild cases or intravenously for severe cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose is administered orally for mild hypoglycemia or intravenously for severe cases to rapidly increase blood sugar levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose is used orally for mild hypoglycemia and intravenously for severe cases unresponsive to glucagon.</data>
  <data key="d10">emergency response,medical intervention,metabolic correction,symptom management,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6ca90008a805c9c66eac7ba65db90fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699103</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Insulina Humana">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hipoglicemia is the most frequently reported adverse reaction associated with insulina humana, occurring when the dose exceeds the patient's insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The use of human insulin can lead to hypoglycemia, a common adverse effect caused by excessive insulin activity.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,blood glucose regulation,dosage risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699706</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Superdose De Insulina">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An insulin overdose can lead to progressively severe hypoglycemia, potentially resulting in unconsciousness or seizures.&lt;SEP&gt;A superdose of insulin can lead to hypoglycemia, which may progress through stages from mild to severe if not promptly treated.</data>
  <data key="d10">causal relationship,dosage error,medication error</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1954b944b779698ff7d67b256199d202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699104</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Insulinas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O uso de insulinas pode causar hipoglicemia, afetando a capacidade de concentração e reação do paciente.</data>
  <data key="d10">efeito terapêutico,risco clínico</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699106</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Capacidade De Dirigir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A hipoglicemia pode prejudicar a habilidade do paciente de dirigir ou operar máquinas.</data>
  <data key="d10">desempenho cognitivo,segurança</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699108</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Betabloqueadores">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Betabloqueadores podem mascarar os sintomas da hipoglicemia, dificultando seu reconhecimento.</data>
  <data key="d10">mascaramento de sintomas,risco clínico</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-54b65b433ba47e8bbf2d607b89776246</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699108</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Insulin Therapy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hipoglicemia is the most frequently reported adverse reaction caused by excessive insulin dosage relative to patient needs.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,metabolic imbalance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699221</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Superdose">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Superdose of insulin can lead to escalating hypoglycemia, requiring immediate treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Superdose of HUMULIN R leads to hypoglycemia, accompanied by symptoms like apathy, confusion, palpitations, sweating, vomiting, and headache.</data>
  <data key="d10">cause and effect,dose excess,progressive effect,symptom manifestation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d717433722cc9ac8e746440493df9010</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699681</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Distúrbios Do Metabolismo E Nutrição">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hipoglicemia is a common metabolic disturbance and the most frequent adverse reaction in insulin therapy, categorized under distúrbios do metabolismo e nutrição.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic disorder,treatment complication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1229dbbfb74d991d522a8d53f9383cdc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699226</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Novolin R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The use of Novolin R can lead to hypoglycemia, especially if the insulin dose exceeds the patient's requirements.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,medication risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8646d585dd04c9e67fc11499ede9ae10</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699227</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Humulin R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hipoglicemia is the most frequent adverse effect associated with Humulin R and other insulin treatments.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,treatment risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699629</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Glicose Intravenosa">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Intravenous glucose is administered in medical settings for unconscious patients or those unable to take sugar orally during severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">emergency care,medical treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699635</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Balas/Drops Açucarados">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sugary candies or drops are used to treat mild to moderate hypoglycemia by quickly raising blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">rapid treatment,symptom relief</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699636</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Tabletes De Glicose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucose tablets are a recommended fast-acting sugar source for managing mild to moderate hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">rapid treatment,symptom relief</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-19de4016c46aba524b40e489fd60f018</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699637</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Álcool">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O consumo de álcool pode causar hipoglicemia em pacientes que utilizam insulina.</data>
  <data key="d10">efeito adverso,indução</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699662</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="HUMULIN R">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A hipoglicemia em pacientes usando HUMULIN R pode prejudicar a concentração e reação, especialmente ao dirigir ou operar máquinas.&lt;SEP&gt;O HUMULIN R é contraindicado durante episódios de hipoglicemia devido ao risco de agravamento da condição.&lt;SEP&gt;Excess HUMULIN R relative to food intake or energy expenditure can cause hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,efeito adverso,medication risk,overdose risk,risco durante atividades</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6398afdc8e1faa94220df6d070a1ade7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d717433722cc9ac8e746440493df9010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699663</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Glicose Oral">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Mild episodes of hypoglycemia can be treated with oral glucose.</data>
  <data key="d10">mild episode management,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d717433722cc9ac8e746440493df9010</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699682</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Glicose Concentrada">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Severe hypoglycemic episodes are treated with concentrated glucose administered intravenously.</data>
  <data key="d10">intravenous therapy,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d717433722cc9ac8e746440493df9010</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699685</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Sistema VigiMed">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Adverse events such as hypoglycemia should be reported through Sistema VigiMed.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse event reporting,monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d717433722cc9ac8e746440493df9010</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699686</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Hipoglicemiantes Orais">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Oral hypoglycemic agents can enhance the blood sugar-lowering effect of insulin, increasing hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood sugar lowering,drug interaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699691</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Salicilatos">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Salicylates can potentiate insulin's effect, leading to increased risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood sugar lowering,drug interaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699692</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Sulfas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sulfas can interact with insulin and increase the likelihood of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood sugar lowering,drug interaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699693</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Antidepressivos">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Some antidepressants can lower blood glucose and contribute to hypoglycemia when used with insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood sugar lowering,drug interaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699695</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Bebidas Alcoólicas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Excessive alcohol consumption increases the risk of hypoglycemia, especially in insulin-treated patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">lifestyle factor,risk enhancement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699698</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Beta-Bloqueadores">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Beta-blockers can mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia, making it harder for patients to recognize low blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical awareness,symptom masking</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-619da52df301ce6db70795213fac37be</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699701</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Interações Medicamentosas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Concomitant use of drugs like oral hypoglycemics, salicylates, sulfas, and some antidepressants can increase the risk of hypoglycemia when using insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,enhanced effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699708</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Glândulas Suprarrenais">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Dysfunction of the adrenal glands can alter insulin requirements and increase susceptibility to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">hormonal regulation,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699709</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Hipófise">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pituitary disorders can affect hormonal balance and influence insulin sensitivity and glucose metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d10">endocrine regulation,insulin sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699710</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Tireoide">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Thyroid dysfunction affects basal metabolic rate, thereby influencing insulin needs and hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin demand,metabolic rate</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699711</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Doença Renal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Progressive kidney disease impairs insulin clearance, necessitating dose adjustments to prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,insulin clearance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699711</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Doença Hepática">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Liver disease compromises glycogen storage and glucose homeostasis, increasing the risk of hypoglycemia during insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose storage,metabolic instability</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b24ac2a9beff09325af7272be567cf82</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699712</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Sintomas De Alerta De Hipoglicemia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Some patients report less pronounced or different early warning symptoms of hypoglycemia after switching from animal insulin to human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">symptom perception,therapeutic transition</data>
