<edge source="Insulin" target="Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lipodystrophy is caused by repeated insulin injections in the same area, leading to skin tissue changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Repeated insulin injections in the same area without rotation can lead to lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin injection into sites affected by lipodystrophy may result in delayed absorption and poor glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipodystrophy is an uncommon adverse reaction caused by repeated insulin injections in the same area, leading to fat tissue alterations.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection site reaction, absorption impairment, tissue change, injection site effect, risk, injection practice, medical complication, injection-related</data>
