<edge source="Insulin" target="Pancreas">
  <data key="d8">6.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pancreas produces insulin naturally in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is produced by the pancreas as part of its endocrine function.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas produces insulin in response to blood glucose levels, releasing basal and bolus amounts as needed.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas naturally produces insulin, which the body uses to regulate glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pancreas naturally produces Insulin to regulate blood glucose levels in non-diabetic individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas produces insulin to regulate blood glucose levels by promoting glucose uptake into cells and storage in the liver.</data>
  <data key="d10">hormone production, physiological function, hormone production, glucose regulation, biological production, hormone origin, hormone production, physiological regulation, hormone production, endocrine function, hormone production, regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a</data>
