<edge source="Insulin" target="Diabetic Ketoacidosis">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin therapy prevents diabetic ketoacidosis, a life-threatening condition in type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insufficient insulin leads to high glucose levels and the production of ketone bodies, causing diabetic ketoacidosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Lack of sufficient insulin can lead to diabetic ketoacidosis, characterized by high glucose and ketone levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic ketoacidosis occurs when low insulin levels cause the body to use fat for energy, producing ketones.</data>
  <data key="d10">cause, prevention, prevention, complication, causal factor, disease mechanism, metabolic imbalance, disease mechanism</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23235296c6ccfffc5ec397dd6b0dc7b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdccbdc819ab6cd813190d6db8dc9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708343</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Diabetic Ketoacidosis</data>
  <data key="d16">Insulin</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Injection Site Reactions">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">As with all insulin therapies, injection site reactions such as pain, redness, and itching may occur.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection site reactions such as pain, redness, and swelling are common but generally temporary during insulin therapy.</data>
