  <data key="d13">1778695428</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Removable-Needle Syringe">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Removable-needle syringes are not recommended for insulin due to dead space, dosing inaccuracies, and risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">incompatibility,usage risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695430</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Disposable Insulin Pen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Disposable insulin pens come pre-filled with insulin and are discarded after the insulin is used.</data>
  <data key="d10">pre-filled delivery,single use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695431</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Brazil">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">In Brazil, U100 insulin is the most commonly used type, influencing syringe selection and dosing practices.</data>
  <data key="d10">concentration standard,regional usage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695432</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Intramuscular Injection">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">In emergency situations, insulin may be administered intramuscularly, leading to very fast absorption and risk of severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">emergency use,rapid absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695434</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Intravenous Injection">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">In hospital settings, insulin can be given intravenously for immediate blood sugar control under medical supervision.</data>
  <data key="d10">emergency treatment,immediate effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695436</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Intradermal Injection">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">If insulin is injected intradermally into the superficial skin layer, it acts more slowly and may not function properly.</data>
  <data key="d10">delayed action,reduced efficacy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695436</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Subcutaneous Skin Fold">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The subcutaneous skin fold technique is used to ensure insulin is injected into the fat layer and not into muscle, reducing the risk of incorrect delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration technique,proper delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695438</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Glycemic Control">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper insulin administration is essential for maintaining effective glycemic control and managing diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Proper insulin use and site rotation are essential for maintaining effective glycemic control in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic regulation,treatment goal,treatment outcome</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699014</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Cold Compress">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Using a cold compress after insulin injection can slow insulin action and raise blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption delay,blood sugar increase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695447</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Cold Bath">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Taking a cold bath after insulin injection may delay insulin absorption and lead to increased blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption delay,blood sugar increase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695448</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Dehydration">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Dehydration can slow insulin action and result in higher blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption delay,blood sugar increase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695448</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin Transport">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">When transporting insulin, it should be kept in carry-on luggage and protected from direct ice contact to prevent damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin must be transported under appropriate conditions to maintain its stability and efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d10">handling,safe handling,temperature control,temperature protection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696009</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Subcutaneous Tissue">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must be injected into the subcutaneous tissue to ensure proper absorption and avoid complications like hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration route,therapeutic delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695457</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Prega Subcutânea">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Performing a prega subcutânea ensures insulin is delivered correctly into subcutaneous fat and not into muscle.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration method,safety practice</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695458</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Diabetes Mellitus Type 1">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin is a critical treatment for individuals with diabetes mellitus type 1, who cannot produce insulin naturally.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical necessity,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695989</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Leonard Thompson">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Leonard Thompson was the first person to receive insulin therapy in 1922, marking a major milestone in diabetes treatment.</data>
  <data key="d10">first use,medical breakthrough</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695989</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Institute for Safe Medication Practices">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Institute for Safe Medication Practices classifies insulin as a high-alert medication due to the potential for serious harm from usage errors.</data>
  <data key="d10">medication safety,risk classification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695991</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Subcutaneous Route">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The subcutaneous route is the standard method for insulin administration, allowing gradual and predictable absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption,administration method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695993</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Intramuscular Route">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The intramuscular route may be used in emergencies but causes faster insulin absorption, increasing hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">accelerated absorption,emergency use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695994</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Intravenous Route">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The intravenous route is used in ICU settings under monitoring for immediate insulin action.</data>
  <data key="d10">immediate effect,intensive care</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695995</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Intradermal Route">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Intradermal insulin injection leads to slower absorption and potential dose loss, increasing hyperglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">delayed absorption,incorrect administration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695998</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin Expiration">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The date of first use must be recorded to monitor insulin expiration and ensure safe use.&lt;SEP&gt;The expiration of insulin after opening is typically 4 to 8 weeks, requiring users to record the start date of use for safety.</data>
  <data key="d10">shelf life,tracking,usage tracking</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696368</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin Appearance">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin appearance should be inspected before use to detect any signs of degradation.</data>
  <data key="d10">quality check,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696004</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Safe Insulin Practices">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Safe insulin practices encompass a range of procedures to prevent errors in preparation, storage, and administration.</data>
  <data key="d10">error prevention,protocol adherence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696005</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin Labeling">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper labeling of insulin helps distinguish it from other injectables like heparin and vaccines, reducing error risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">differentiation,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696006</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Visual Alerts">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Visual alerts are used to highlight insulin and prevent accidental misuse in clinical settings.</data>
  <data key="d10">awareness,error reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696007</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Patient Education">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper patient education ensures correct understanding and application of insulin use, reducing the risk of errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Patients and caregivers must be educated on proper insulin use, including avoiding massage after injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">caregiver instruction,safety,treatment adherence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696007</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Team Training">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Ongoing team training helps reduce insulin errors caused by inexperience or distraction.</data>
  <data key="d10">professional development,safety culture</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696008</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Blood Reflux">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Keeping the needle in place after injection prevents blood reflux into the insulin refill or reservoir.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication prevention,injection safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696017</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Subcutaneous Injection">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must be administered via subcutaneous injection, not orally, to ensure proper therapeutic effect.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration method,correct usage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696036</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Latin American Network for Safe Medication Use">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Latin American Network for Safe Medication Use identifies insulin as a high-risk medication frequently involved in clinical errors.</data>
  <data key="d10">error prevention,high-risk medication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696037</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Double-Check Procedure">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The double-check procedure in nursing helps ensure accurate insulin preparation and administration, reducing the risk of errors.</data>
  <data key="d10">error reduction,safety protocol</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696038</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Refrigeration">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must be stored under refrigeration between 2 and 8°C to maintain its stability and therapeutic action.</data>
  <data key="d10">stability,storage condition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696040</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Injection Site Pain">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Injecting cold insulin directly from the refrigerator can cause pain and irritation at the injection site.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration effect,patient comfort</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696043</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin NPH">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin NPH is a specific formulation of insulin used for intermediate-acting blood glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d10">pharmaceutical type,substance classification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696044</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Regular Insulin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Regular insulin is a short-acting form of insulin used to manage postprandial blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">pharmaceutical type,substance classification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696045</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin Packaging">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin should remain in its original packaging during storage to protect it from light and physical damage.</data>
  <data key="d10">light and temperature shielding,protection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696370</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Metal Or Plastic Container With Lid">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin stored in a refrigerator should be placed in a metal or plastic container with a lid to protect it from temperature fluctuations and light.</data>
  <data key="d10">environmental shielding,storage protection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696371</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Clinical Practice">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">In clinical practice, insulin is administered using appropriate syringes and techniques tailored to patient needs.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical application,treatment protocol</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696375</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Thiazolidinediones">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Using insulin with thiazolidinediones may increase the risk of congestive heart failure.&lt;SEP&gt;When thiazolidinediones are combined with insulin, patients should be monitored for signs of heart failure, weight gain, and edema.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones are used in combination with insulin, requiring careful monitoring for cardiac symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones may alter insulin requirements and must be monitored when used in combination with insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical monitoring,combination therapy,dosage adjustment,drug interaction,heart risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699160</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin requirements typically decrease in the first trimester of pregnancy and increase in the second and third trimesters, necessitating dose adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dose adjustments are needed during pregnancy, lactation, or when interacting medications are used.</data>
  <data key="d10">physiological change,physiological changes,treatment modification,treatment optimization</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699238</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Lactation">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin therapy during lactation is possible but requires medical evaluation for safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Women who are breastfeeding may require adjustments in insulin dosage.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin use during lactation is safe and does not harm the infant, though dosage adjustments may be necessary.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,dose adjustment,maternal care,safety,treatment compatibility,treatment consideration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699161</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Levemir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir is a type of insulin used for glycemic control in patients with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d10">medication type,therapeutic use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698161</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d8">5.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Inadequate insulin dosage or discontinuation can lead to hyperglycemia and potentially diabetic ketoacidosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Uncontrolled hyperglycemia during pregnancy increases the risk of fetal malformations, necessitating tight insulin management.&lt;SEP&gt;Poorly controlled diabetes with hyperglycemia during pregnancy increases the risk of fetal malformations and intrauterine death.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperglycemia occurs when lack of insulin leads to excessive blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Too little insulin delivery may cause hyperglycemia, a condition of elevated blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">deficiency consequence,dosage effect,glycemic control,medical risk,metabolic control,metabolic imbalance,pregnancy risk,regulation failure,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708093</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin Injection Site Reactions">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin injections may cause local reactions at the injection site, including pain and inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration issue,adverse effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698164</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Cutaneous Amyloidosis">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Cutaneous amyloidosis at insulin injection sites can result in delayed insulin absorption and poor glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Cutaneous amyloidosis is a rare condition reported during post-marketing use of insulin, with unknown frequency, linked to repeated injections.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin injection into areas with cutaneous amyloidosis can lead to impaired absorption and reduced glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption delay,absorption impairment,injection site reaction,rare skin disorder,risk,unknown frequency</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699014</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Pregnancy">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin use should continue during pregnancy with medical guidance to ensure maternal and fetal safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is safe to use during pregnancy as it does not cross the placenta, with insulin needs typically decreasing in the first trimester and increasing in the second and third.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage dynamics,medical consultation,treatment continuation,treatment safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699161</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Time Zone Change">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Traveling across time zones requires patients to adjust insulin administration schedules and coordinate with meal times under medical guidance.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosing adjustment,travel planning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698170</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Infections">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Concurrent infections increase the patient's insulin needs due to elevated metabolic demands.</data>
  <data key="d10">increased requirement,metabolic stress</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698171</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Fever">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Fever increases insulin requirements in diabetic patients, necessitating dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage change,illness impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698172</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Renal Disease">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients with kidney disease may require changes in insulin dosage due to altered clearance and metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698173</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Hepatic Disease">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Liver disease can affect insulin breakdown and action, requiring dose modifications.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698173</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Adrenal Gland Disorders">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Disorders of the adrenal glands can alter insulin sensitivity and necessitate insulin dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage change,hormonal interaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698174</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Pituitary Disorders">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pituitary disorders may disrupt hormonal balance, affecting insulin needs in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage requirement,hormonal regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698175</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Thyroid Disorders">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Thyroid disorders can change insulin sensitivity and metabolic rate, requiring insulin dosage changes.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,metabolic influence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698176</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Glucose Metabolism">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin plays a central role in regulating glucose metabolism in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin plays a central role in glucose metabolism, which can be altered by various medications that either increase or decrease insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,metabolic control,metabolic regulation,physiological regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699163</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Drug Interactions">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Various medications can either increase or decrease insulin requirements through metabolic interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Various drugs can either increase or decrease insulin requirements, necessitating dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,dosage modification,pharmacological effect,pharmacological interaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699239</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Octreotide">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Octreotide can either increase or decrease insulin requirements depending on individual patient response.&lt;SEP&gt;Octreotide can either reduce or increase insulin requirements depending on its net effect on insulin secretion and glucose metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Octreotide can either reduce or increase the insulin requirements of a patient.</data>
  <data key="d10">bidirectional effect,dosage influence,dosage modulation,drug interaction,metabolic effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699026</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Lanreotide">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lanreotide can either increase or decrease insulin requirements depending on individual patient response.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanreotide may either decrease or increase insulin needs based on individual metabolic responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanreotide can either reduce or increase the insulin requirements of a patient.</data>
  <data key="d10">bidirectional effect,dosage influence,dosage modulation,drug interaction,metabolic effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699027</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Alcohol">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Alcohol can either enhance or reduce the hypoglycemic effect of insulin, requiring caution in use.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol can either enhance or diminish the hypoglycemic effect of insulin, leading to unpredictable blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,hypoglycemia risk,pharmacological interaction,variable glycemic effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699028</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Breastfeeding">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Women who are breastfeeding may require adjustments in insulin dosage due to metabolic demands of lactation.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,physiological change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698266</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Levemir® FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Levemir® FlexPen® is used to deliver precise doses of insulin to regulate blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,drug delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5d212ccdded1e4ccf51af243a8d38b4c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698386</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Blood Sugar Level">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin administration via Levemir® FlexPen® helps regulate blood sugar level to prevent hyperglycemia or hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic effect,physiological regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5d212ccdded1e4ccf51af243a8d38b4c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
