  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Pharmacokinetics">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pharmacokinetics of insulin encompasses its absorption, distribution, metabolism, and elimination in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The pharmacokinetics of insulin are influenced by patient-specific factors such as injection site, insulin type, and subcutaneous fat thickness.</data>
  <data key="d10">body dynamics,drug behavior,drug processing,metabolic process</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699009</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Medication Interactions">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Various medications can either increase or decrease insulin requirements, necessitating careful monitoring and dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage modification,pharmacological effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699015</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitors">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Monoamine oxidase inhibitors can reduce the patient's insulin requirements by affecting glucose metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699016</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Beta-Blockers">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Beta-blockers can mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia and delay recovery, increasing the risk associated with insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,symptom masking</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699017</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="ACE Inhibitors">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">ACE inhibitors can reduce insulin needs in diabetic patients by influencing glucose metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699017</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Salicylates">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Salicylates may decrease insulin requirements due to their effects on glucose regulation.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699018</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Anabolic Steroids">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Anabolic steroids can reduce the need for insulin in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699019</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Sulfonamides">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sulfonamides may lower insulin requirements by enhancing insulin sensitivity or secretion.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699020</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Oral Contraceptives">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Oral contraceptives can increase insulin needs due to their impact on insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement increase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699020</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Thiazides">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Thiazide diuretics may increase insulin requirements by impairing glucose tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement increase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699021</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Glucocorticoids">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucocorticoids can increase insulin needs by promoting hyperglycemia through gluconeogenesis and insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement increase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699022</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Thyroid Hormones">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Thyroid hormones increase metabolic rate and glucose turnover, potentially increasing insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement increase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699023</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Sympathomimetics">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sympathomimetics stimulate glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis, leading to higher insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement increase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699024</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Growth Hormone">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Growth hormone induces insulin resistance, thereby increasing the patient's insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement increase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699025</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Danazol">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Danazol may increase insulin needs by inducing insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,insulin requirement increase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699025</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Novolin® R FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R FlexPen® delivers insulin as its active therapeutic component for diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R FlexPen® contains rapid-acting insulin used for blood glucose control in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Novolin® R FlexPen® is designed to deliver precise amounts of insulin to manage blood sugar levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R FlexPen® is used to administer insulin, specifically Novolin® R (human insulin 100 UI/mL).</data>
  <data key="d10">active ingredient,drug delivery,medical treatment,medication composition,medication formulation,therapeutic agent</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc3409d91fe33592f741a0002d70749c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ae5fe50adf25db0be3b8cdde6282e9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699030</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Travel">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Travel across time zones may require changes in insulin timing and dosing, necessitating prior medical advice.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosing adjustment,medical consultation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699031</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin Antibodies">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Circulating insulin antibodies can bind to insulin, affecting its pharmacokinetics and distribution.</data>
  <data key="d10">binding interaction,immune response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699032</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R is a formulation of insulin used for glycemic control in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R is a fast-acting insulin used in diabetes management, often combined with long-acting insulins.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R is a formulation of insulin used for managing blood glucose levels in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R contains human insulin as its active substance, formulated at 100 UI/mL.</data>
  <data key="d10">active ingredient,drug classification,medication composition,pharmaceutical composition,therapeutic use,treatment method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699120</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Saccharomyces Cerevisiae">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Human insulin in Novolin® R is produced using recombinant DNA technology in the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae.</data>
  <data key="d10">biotechnology,recombinant production</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699148</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Plasma">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin in the bloodstream has a terminal half-life of only a few minutes, indicating rapid elimination from plasma.</data>
  <data key="d10">elimination kinetics,short half-life</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699171</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Novolin® R Penfill">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R Penfill is a formulation of fast-acting insulin used to manage blood glucose levels in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">medication type,therapeutic agent</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699172</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Endogenous Insulin Production">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Residual endogenous insulin production reduces the amount of exogenous insulin needed.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage reduction,physiological factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699183</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin Syringes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must be used with insulin syringes that have a corresponding unit scale for accurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage accuracy,drug administration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699212</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Thiols">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Products containing thiols can degrade insulin and should not be mixed with insulin solutions.</data>
  <data key="d10">chemical incompatibility,drug degradation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699213</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Sulfides">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Products containing sulfides may cause degradation of insulin and are incompatible with insulin solutions.</data>
  <data key="d10">chemical incompatibility,drug degradation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699214</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Frozen Insulin Preparations">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin preparations that have been frozen must not be used as freezing can compromise their safety and effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d10">efficacy loss,storage safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699215</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Clear And Colorless Insulin Solution">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin solutions must appear clear and colorless to be considered safe for use; cloudiness or discoloration indicates potential degradation.</data>
  <data key="d10">quality check,safe use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699215</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Refractive Abnormalities">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Refractive abnormalities may occur at the start of insulin treatment due to rapid changes in blood glucose and are typically temporary.</data>
  <data key="d10">neurological side effect,transient condition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699216</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Edema">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Edema is an uncommon adverse reaction during insulin therapy, often occurring at treatment initiation.</data>
  <data key="d10">fluid retention,uncommon side effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699217</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Acute Painful Neuropathy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Acute painful neuropathy can occur with rapid improvement in glycemic control during insulin therapy and is usually reversible.</data>
  <data key="d10">neurological complication,reversibility</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699219</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Diabetic Retinopathy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Intensified insulin therapy may temporarily worsen diabetic retinopathy, though long-term glycemic control reduces progression risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">eye complication,temporary worsening</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699219</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Urticaria">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Urticaria is an uncommon adverse reaction associated with insulin use, appearing as hives at injection sites or systemically.</data>
  <data key="d10">skin reaction,uncommon effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699220</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Skin Rash">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Skin rash is an uncommon adverse event linked to insulin therapy, classified under skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders.</data>
  <data key="d10">dermatological side effect,uncommon occurrence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699221</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Anaphylactic Reactions">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Anaphylactic reactions are very rare but serious adverse effects that can occur during insulin treatment.</data>
  <data key="d10">rare occurrence,severe allergy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699222</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Metabolic And Nutritional Disorders">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin therapy is associated with metabolic and nutritional disorders, with hypoglycemia being the most common adverse effect.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse reaction classification,metabolic disturbance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699223</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Nervous System Disorders">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin treatment can lead to nervous system disorders such as acute painful neuropathy and peripheral neuropathy.</data>
  <data key="d10">classification,neurological side effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699224</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Vision Disorders">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin use is linked to vision disorders including refractive abnormalities and temporary worsening of diabetic retinopathy.</data>
  <data key="d10">classification,ocular complication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699225</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Skin And Subcutaneous Tissue Disorders">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin therapy may cause skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders such as urticaria, rash, and lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d10">classification,dermatological reaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbd230d2ccb1901e088f3bb5714424fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699226</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="General Disorders And Administration Site Conditions">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin treatment is associated with general disorders and administration site conditions like edema and injection site reactions.</data>
  <data key="d10">local effect,systemic reaction</data>
