<edge source="Sensor" target="Transmitter">
  <data key="d8">7.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The transmitter sends glucose data from the sensor to the pump and its battery status is monitored in the pump interface.&lt;SEP&gt;The transmitter sends glucose data from the sensor to the pump or display device.&lt;SEP&gt;The Transmitter connects to the Sensor to collect and relay glucose readings to the Pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The sensor connects physically to the transmitter, which then sends data wirelessly to the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The sensor must be securely connected to the transmitter for proper signal transmission to the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The transmitter must be properly connected to the sensor to transmit glucose readings to the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The sensor sends glucose data to the transmitter, which relays it to the pump; a secure connection is required.</data>
  <data key="d10">battery monitoring,connectivity,data relay,data transmission,device pairing,monitoring,physical connection,secure connection,signal transmission</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707512</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The sensor provides continuous glucose data to the insulin pump, which is used for system operation and status display.&lt;SEP&gt;Communication between the insulin pump and sensor can be disrupted by radio frequency interference from external devices.&lt;SEP&gt;The sensor integrated with the insulin pump system measures glucose levels and requires calibration using blood glucose meter readings.&lt;SEP&gt;The glucose sensor wirelessly sends collected sensor glucose data to the insulin pump or compatible mobile device.</data>
  <data key="d10">RF interference,calibration,data integration,data transmission,glucose monitoring,wireless communication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707762</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="CGM Device">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The sensor is a core component of the CGM device, responsible for detecting glucose levels in interstitial fluid.</data>
  <data key="d10">component integration,glucose monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707513</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="MiniMed Mobile App">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The MiniMed Mobile App allows users to restart or initiate a new sensor when alerts occur.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed Mobile App is used to assist in starting a new sensor with the CGM system.</data>
  <data key="d10">device control,restart function,sensor management,setup support</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
