  <data key="d13">1778707513</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="Sensor Failed To Start Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Sensor Failed To Start Alert occurs when the sensor cannot detect interstitial fluid to begin the warm-up phase.</data>
  <data key="d10">activation failure,warm-up process</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707517</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="Pump">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump connects to a sensor for glucose monitoring, and loss of signal triggers an alert.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump loses connection with the sensor, triggering the lost sensor signal alert after 30 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump detects whether a sensor is new or previously used and prompts the user to start or reconnect accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d10">communication failure,connection,detection,monitoring,pairing,signal connection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707646</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="Change Sensor Alert">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The change sensor alert appears when the sensor is not functioning or improperly connected, requiring user action to replace it.&lt;SEP&gt;A Change Sensor Alert appears when the sensor cannot be safely used, requiring the user to discard and replace it.</data>
  <data key="d10">device failure,failure response,replacement,replacement prompt</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707649</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="Glucose Reading">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The sensor generates glucose readings every 5 minutes as part of the CGM process.</data>
  <data key="d10">data generation,real-time monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707689</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="SmartGuard">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">SmartGuard relies on continuous glucose data from the sensor to function; if the sensor is not ready or paired, SmartGuard cannot activate.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard feature depends on the sensor for glucose readings, and turning off the sensor causes the system to exit SmartGuard mode.</data>
  <data key="d10">data input,deactivation trigger,system dependency</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ecb2783153f277b98dbb01bd056cf9a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707773</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="Lost Sensor Signal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The lost sensor signal alert indicates the pump cannot detect the sensor after 30 minutes, requiring user action.</data>
