<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Intramuscular Injection">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Intramuscular injection of insulin increases the risk of hypoglycemia due to faster absorption into the bloodstream.&lt;SEP&gt;Intramuscular injection of long-acting insulin can lead to rapid absorption and increase the risk of severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,medical risk,rapid absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695240</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Low blood glucose levels indicate hypoglycemia, detectable through regular glucometer use.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia occurs when blood glucose falls below 70 mg/dL, posing health risks especially in insulin-treated patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">abnormal level,health risk,low glucose,risk condition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694525</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Lipo-Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Irregular insulin absorption due to lipo-hypertrophy can lead to episodes of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,blood sugar fluctuation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694538</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Chatbot">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The chatbot interprets expressions like "I'm shaking" as signs of hypoglycemia and provides a supportive and accurate response.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical response,symptom recognition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1be43b1b23852278983f60d0f150b0f9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694985</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Meta-Analysis">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Meta-analyses showed lower incidence of hypoglycemia in patients using insulin pens versus syringes.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse event,treatment safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695247</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Massage">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Massaging the injection site can lead to hypoglycemia by accelerating insulin absorption into the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d10">physiological effect,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695437</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Application">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Improper insulin application before physical activity, such as injecting into the leg before walking, can lead to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood sugar drop,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696419</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Physical Activity">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia may occur during physical activity if insulin is absorbed too quickly from active injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical activity often causes hypoglycemia due to increased glucose utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia may occur after physical activity due to the body's process of muscle glycogen replenishment.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,delayed effect,energy expenditure,glycogen replenishment,insulin sensitivity,prevention</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63b580c3efbe7e9a671badd7807ad11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de222ffe4b47c380bbe3bc69fd7c2632</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702825</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Levemir">
  <data key="d8">7.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Incorrect dosing of Levemir can lead to hypoglycemia, especially if meals are skipped or physical activity increases.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia is a potential adverse effect of Levemir therapy, particularly during transitions or combination treatments, requiring preventive dose adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;In clinical trials, the rate of mild hypoglycemia was similar with Levemir plus liraglutide compared to placebo, with no severe episodes reported.&lt;SEP&gt;Excessive Levemir dosing relative to need can cause hypoglycemia, particularly if meals are missed or physical activity is increased.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Improper use of Levemir can lead to hypoglycemia, which impairs cognitive and motor functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia is the most frequently reported adverse reaction associated with Levemir, occurring when insulin dosage exceeds the patient's needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia is the most commonly reported adverse reaction during Levemir therapy, occurring in an estimated 12% of treated patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,adverse event,adverse reaction,dose dependency,drug effect,metabolic impact,risk,risk factor,risk mitigation,safety profile,side effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698157</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Diabetes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia is a common risk in diabetes management due to insulin or medication use.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood glucose fluctuation,treatment risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698164</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Injection Site Reactions">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sudden changes in insulin injection sites from affected to unaffected areas may trigger hypoglycemia, requiring glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d10">monitoring,treatment adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698167</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Beta-Blockers">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Beta-blockers can mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia, increasing the risk of undetected low blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta-blockers can mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia and delay the body's recovery from low blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical risk,delayed recovery,symptom masking</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699183</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Glycose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glycose is administered orally for mild hypoglycemia or intravenously for severe cases unresponsive to glucagon.</data>
  <data key="d10">emergency response,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698268</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Levemir®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Intravenous administration of Levemir® may cause severe hypoglycemia, and it has a lower risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia compared to insulin NPH.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,safety profile</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698304</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Dose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia may occur when insulin dose exceeds patient requirements, with warning symptoms varying based on treatment intensity and diabetes duration.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose sensitivity,symptom variation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699011</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Driving">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia can impair concentration and reaction time, making driving hazardous for diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can impair concentration and reaction time, posing risks for driving and operating machinery.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can impair a patient's ability to concentrate and react, making driving hazardous, especially in those with reduced warning signs.</data>
  <data key="d10">cognitive impairment,impairment,safety concern,safety risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699014</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Novolin® R FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Excessive insulin dose from Novolin® R FlexPen® relative to patient needs can cause hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia is the most common adverse reaction associated with treatment using Novolin® R FlexPen®.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta-blockers may mask hypoglycemia symptoms, and insulin in Novolin® R FlexPen® can cause hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,clinical risk,dosing risk,side effect,symptom masking</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699028</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Therapy Intensification">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Intensified insulin therapy may alter or reduce hypoglycemia warning symptoms, requiring patient education.&lt;SEP&gt;Intensification of insulin therapy, while improving glycemic control, increases the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood glucose control,patient monitoring,symptom change,treatment risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699729</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Missed Meal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A missed meal can lead to hypoglycemia in patients on insulin therapy due to unbalanced insulin levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic imbalance,trigger</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699029</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Unplanned Physical Exertion">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Unplanned physical exertion increases insulin sensitivity and glucose uptake, potentially causing hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose utilization,trigger</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699030</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Novolin® R Penfill">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia is the most common adverse reaction associated with Novolin® R treatment.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,common reaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ff021af578e58080f6a865c5f105e6d3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699094</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">5.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R can cause hypoglycemia, especially if injection sites are changed suddenly from affected to unaffected areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia is the most common adverse reaction, occurring when Novolin® R dose exceeds the patient's insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Excessive dosing of Novolin® R relative to patient needs, missed meals, or unplanned physical activity can lead to hypoglycemia, a potentially dangerous condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Excessive insulin dose relative to patient needs with Novolin® R can cause hypoglycemia, especially if meals are missed or physical activity is increased.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia is the most frequently reported adverse reaction associated with Novolin® R therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,adverse reaction,dosage sensitivity,dose imbalance,risk factor,side effect,treatment risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699145</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Severe Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Mild hypoglycemia can progress to severe hypoglycemia if untreated, leading to unconsciousness or seizures.&lt;SEP&gt;Untreated hypoglycemia can progress to severe hypoglycemia, which may result in unconsciousness, seizures, or death.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical emergency,progression,severity,symptom progression</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699732</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Sweating">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sweating, particularly cold sweat, is a common early symptom of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical manifestation,symptom</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699147</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Palpitations">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Palpitations are a typical symptom of hypoglycemia, caused by the body's stress response.</data>
  <data key="d10">physiological response,symptom</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699147</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Nausea">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Nausea is a gastrointestinal symptom that may occur during hypoglycemic episodes.</data>
  <data key="d10">gastrointestinal effect,symptom</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699148</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Headache">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Headache is a neurological symptom frequently associated with low blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">neurological effect,symptom</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699149</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Blurred Vision">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Blurred vision is a sensory symptom of hypoglycemia, affecting visual acuity.</data>
  <data key="d10">sensory disturbance,symptom</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699150</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Fatigue">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Fatigue is a common physical symptom of hypoglycemia, reflecting low energy availability.</data>
  <data key="d10">physical manifestation,symptom</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699151</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Anxiety">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Anxiety and nervousness are psychological symptoms of hypoglycemia, often accompanied by tremors.</data>
  <data key="d10">psychological response,symptom</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699151</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Confusion">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Confusion and difficulty concentrating are cognitive symptoms of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">cognitive impairment,symptom</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4db353458c93e1b1abc9f696ebf195a9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699153</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Medication Interactions">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Beta-blockers and alcohol can interact with insulin, potentially masking hypoglycemia symptoms or intensifying its effects.</data>
  <data key="d10">risk amplification,symptom masking</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699161</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Alcohol">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Alcohol can either intensify or reduce the hypoglycemic effect of insulin, altering blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,effect modulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699179</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Beta Blockers">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Non-selective beta blockers can mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia and delay recovery, increasing danger.</data>
  <data key="d10">delayed recovery,symptom masking</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699238</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sudden switch to an unaffected injection site after repeated use of lipodystrophic areas may result in hypoglycemia due to altered insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin absorption,treatment complication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699622</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="HUMULIN R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Overdose or improper use of HUMULIN R can cause hypoglycemia, a potentially serious adverse effect of insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,overdose risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699628</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Humulin R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Humulin R use can lead to hypoglycemia, which may impair cognitive and motor functions, posing risks during driving or machine operation.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699636</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Injection Technique">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A sudden switch to an unaffected injection site after using affected areas may lead to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">site rotation,treatment adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e023d3ebcda62fd027</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699675</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Overdose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin overdose can cause hypoglycemia accompanied by symptoms such as confusion, sweating, palpitations, and headache.</data>
  <data key="d10">cause and effect,overdose consequence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e023d3ebcda62fd027</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699677</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Concentrated Glucose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Concentrated glucose administered intravenously is used to treat severe hypoglycemia, especially when neurological impairment occurs.</data>
  <data key="d10">emergency care,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e023d3ebcda62fd027</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699681</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Therapy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia may occur when there is an excess of insulin relative to food intake or energy expenditure during insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage imbalance,treatment risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e023d3ebcda62fd027</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699684</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Human Insulin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An excess of human insulin relative to food intake or energy expenditure can lead to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">cause and effect,dosage imbalance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f8938c7b2cdfb8e023d3ebcda62fd027</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699686</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Hypoglycemia Symptoms">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The symptoms of hypoglycemia, such as sweating, dizziness, and tremor, are clinical manifestations of low blood glucose caused by insulin use.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse reaction,clinical manifestation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-49e5674b4a4db2a056560132addcc354</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699733</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A malfunctioning insulin pump may deliver too much insulin, resulting in hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;The insulin pump helps manage hypoglycemia through monitoring and alerts, and users are advised to contact healthcare professionals in severe cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Malfunction of the insulin pump, such as from radiation exposure, can lead to excessive insulin infusion and cause hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">alarm response,condition management,device malfunction,health complication,health risk,insulin overdose</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40aae9750bff384ac9028ae500bc1fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f5ebaa0341f051ad33cfb9895a3851</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704330</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Glucose Tablets">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucose tablets are used to treat low blood glucose levels during travel.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose tablets are used as a fast-acting treatment to manage hypoglycemic episodes.</data>
  <data key="d10">emergency response,treatment,treatment method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f9bc8ba4b622225a9f3f1bb8a9d4fb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703071</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="MiniMed 770G">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Incorrect use of the MiniMed 770G may lead to excessive insulin delivery and cause hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">improper use,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9ca77ae5b015fee5d1a21879c1a2b444</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778701053</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Autoapagado">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Autoapagado is designed to protect users who may not respond appropriately to hypoglycemia episodes.</data>
  <data key="d10">response failure,risk mitigation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4dc17381a558f271a9da13b99091c2ac</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778701056</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Meal Composition">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Meals high in fat and protein delay glucose absorption, which is relevant to hypoglycemia management.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose response,nutrient digestion</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702765</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Glucose Trend Chart">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The glucose trend chart helps identify patterns leading to hypoglycemia, such as post-exercise drops.</data>
  <data key="d10">pattern recognition,risk identification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702775</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Muscle Glycogen Replenishment">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Muscle glycogen replenishment after physical activity can cause delayed hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">delayed effect,post-activity risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702782</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Alcohol Intake">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Alcohol intake may contribute to hypoglycemia if not considered in insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic impact,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3bf188253bd9d2142b4fcf627eacc2b8</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702783</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Pump Therapy">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin pump therapy helps reduce the frequency and severity of hypoglycemic episodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pump therapy improves glucose control and reduces the frequency and severity of hypoglycemia episodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia is a potential complication of insulin pump therapy due to miscalculated insulin dosing or mismatched basal rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia is a risk in insulin pump therapy that can be managed using trend data and therapy adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication,glucose control,risk factor,risk management,risk reduction,therapy complication,therapy outcome,treatment effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-46727635453cfb706e038b6920cb2d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6367cc87b3326e358622e179b72cbfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702817</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Capillary Blood Glucose Test">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Capillary Blood Glucose Test is used to confirm low glucose values and guide treatment decisions for hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">diagnosis confirmation,therapy basis</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702854</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Carbohydrate Intake">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Carbohydrate Intake is used to treat hypoglycemia by raising blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose correction,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702861</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="SmartGuard™">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">SmartGuard™ helps protect against hypoglycemia by predicting low glucose events and automatically suspending insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard™ helps prevent hypoglycemia by automatically interrupting insulin delivery when glucose levels approach a low threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard™ is designed to prevent hypoglycemia by predicting low glucose events and adjusting insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard™ predicts approaching hypoglycemia and automatically suspends insulin delivery to prevent it.</data>
  <data key="d10">automated insulin control,insulin suspension,prediction,prevention,prevention mechanism,risk mitigation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03aab2b6261ddc73d474d0c866e7b37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702866</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Root Cause Analysis">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Root cause analysis is used to determine the underlying reasons for episodes of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">diagnosis,event investigation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-632920359f020e0873ff5b7621b1a7a3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702892</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Glucose Levels">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Frequent low glucose levels may indicate hypoglycemia, requiring intervention during insulin pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">health risk,low glucose</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-44b69a8e50a0a4230b6963fe643d8cd0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702922</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Basal Insulin Rate">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An inappropriately high basal insulin rate can cause hypoglycemia by delivering more insulin than the body needs.&lt;SEP&gt;An incorrectly set basal insulin rate that is too high can lead to hypoglycemia in individuals using insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;An incorrect or too high basal insulin rate can lead to hypoglycemia, especially during fasting or activity.</data>
  <data key="d10">cause,glycemic control,insulin adjustment,insulin management,insulin overdose,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703101</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Capillary Glucose Test">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A capillary glucose test is required to confirm a low sensor glucose value or low alert before initiating treatment for hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">diagnostic confirmation,therapy decision</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703103</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Exercise">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Exercising without adjusting the basal insulin rate can increase the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose lowering,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703106</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Alcoholic Beverages">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Consuming alcoholic beverages without carbohydrate-containing food can lead to hypoglycemia, especially during or after insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">delayed hypoglycemia,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703107</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Medical Team">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The medical team provides personalized recommendations on managing hypoglycemia and adjusting insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical guidance,treatment planning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703108</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Glucose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia is defined by abnormally low levels of glucose in the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d10">deficiency condition,metabolic imbalance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a3000f8880af4ef448483b353db654f9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia and Hyperglycemia represent opposite extremes of glucose imbalance that are both monitored in diabetes care.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical concern,glucose imbalance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703138</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="AUC &lt;70 mg/dL">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">AUC &lt;70 mg/dL measures the duration and severity of Hypoglycemia episodes.</data>
  <data key="d10">severity measurement,time in range</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703138</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Frequent glucose monitoring helps detect and prevent episodes of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">prevention,risk detection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703162</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Standard Bolus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A standard bolus may act too quickly for high-fat, high-protein meals, leading to early hypoglycemia followed by rising glucose.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin action,mismatch risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703174</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="MiniMed™ 640G System">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The MiniMed™ 640G System provides alerts for low glucose levels to help prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert system,prevention</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8f2cf8a591a83e4436ab6a76c2d30e2d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703208</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Rapid-Absorption Carbohydrates">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Rapid-absorption carbohydrates are used to treat hypoglycemia by quickly raising blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">symptom reversal,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-abe87298f323437aa2ceaea23d392930</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703218</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Infusion">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Incorrect insulin infusion due to wrong Bolus Wizard settings may result in hypoglycemia from excessive insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage error,treatment outcome</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc77598dbeb5980c719d1d54a6c3ab77</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704331</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Glucose Level">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A glucose level below 50 mg/dL defines hypoglycemia, requiring immediate treatment with carbohydrates.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical condition,threshold trigger</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704373</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Carbohydrates">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Carbohydrates are used to treat hypoglycemia by raising blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">symptom relief,treatment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704374</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Practice Basal Rate">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Using practice basal rates for actual therapy could lead to incorrect insulin dosing and result in hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">health risk,incorrect usage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704432</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Bolus Wizard">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Using Bolus Wizard too soon after a manual injection may result in excessive insulin administration, increasing the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">overdose risk,safety warning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704448</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="SmartGuard Feature">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature is designed to help prevent hypoglycemia by adjusting insulin delivery based on sensor glucose values.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard feature predicts the risk of hypoglycemia and adjusts the bolus downward to prevent it.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">automated response,prevention,risk mitigation,risk prediction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707535</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Infusion Set">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Leaving the infusion set connected to the body during rewinding may cause accidental insulin infusion, leading to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Failure to disconnect the infusion set during reservoir replacement may cause accidental insulin infusion, leading to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">health risk,medical consequence,risk factor,safety warning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc61f77b003d0086bd985ddb94fc2a98</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707547</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="MiniMed Mobile App">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Relying solely on the MiniMed Mobile App for alerts may result in missed notifications, increasing the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert failure,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707558</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Low SG Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Low SG alert is intended to detect potential hypoglycemia, but may not always reflect true BG levels at thresholds below 60 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical risk,symptom correlation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707997</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="BG Meter">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A BG meter reading is required to confirm suspected hypoglycemia before treatment.</data>
  <data key="d10">diagnosis confirmation,symptom verification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708003</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Over-Delivery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Excessive insulin delivery due to inaccurate sensor readings increases the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,medical risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708150</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Pump">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pump malfunction due to magnetic fields or radiation can lead to insulin over-delivery and severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">health risk,insulin over-delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708201</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Stacking">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin stacking can lead to hypoglycemia due to overlapping effects of multiple boluses.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin accumulation,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708347</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Hydroxyurea">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hydroxyurea can lead to hypoglycemia by causing over-delivery of insulin due to falsely high sensor glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,insulin error</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708402</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Trend Arrows">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Trend arrows indicate the direction and speed of glucose change, helping users predict and prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical alert,risk prediction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709328</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Retrospective SMCG">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Retrospective SMCG helps identify unknown hypoglycemic episodes and reduces their incidence in type 1 and type 2 diabetes patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">pattern detection,risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-dae76a096a2e7c5125f3d505a209605a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709747</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Hba1c">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Targeting low Hba1c levels increases the risk of hypoglycemia, which is a major clinical concern in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical risk,treatment trade-off</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709748</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Low Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia and Low Blood Glucose refer to the same medical condition characterized by abnormally low blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical condition,synonym</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778710353</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Epinephrine">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The release of epinephrine during hypoglycemia causes symptoms such as sweating, fast heartbeat, and anxiety.</data>
  <data key="d10">physiological response,symptom cause</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778710354</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Glucose Meter">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A glucose meter is used to confirm low blood glucose levels when symptoms of hypoglycemia are present.</data>
  <data key="d10">diagnosis method,monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778710354</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Continuous Glucose Monitor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A Continuous Glucose Monitor helps detect and alert individuals to low or falling glucose levels, especially useful for those with hypoglycemia unawareness.</data>
  <data key="d10">diagnosis method,real-time monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778710355</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Hypoglycemia Unawareness">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia Unawareness increases the risk of severe hypoglycemia because individuals do not recognize early warning symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical complication,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778710356</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Symptoms Of Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia presents with a range of symptoms such as shakiness, sweating, confusion, and fast heartbeat, which vary between individuals.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical presentation,symptom manifestation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-99d00bf995ac4c109277e3272b1236de</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778710357</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Asymptomatic Hypoglycemia" target="CGM">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">CGM is especially beneficial for individuals with asymptomatic hypoglycemia by detecting drops in glucose before symptoms occur.</data>
  <data key="d10">early detection,symptom monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694580</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Insulin Administration">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An Insulin Pump delivers insulin continuously and is beneficial for precise dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery method, continuous infusion</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694481</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Insulin Administration</data>
  <data key="d16">Insulin Pump</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="CGM">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Some CGM systems are used in conjunction with insulin pumps like Medtronic MiniMed for integrated diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;The insulin pump relies on CGM data to make informed insulin delivery decisions.&gt;</data>
