<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d8">8.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation between Basal Pattern and Insulin Pump describes a critical functional integration in diabetes management technology. The Basal Pattern, which represents a user-defined schedule of insulin delivery rates, is programmed into the Insulin Pump to regulate the continuous infusion of insulin throughout the day and night. This programming enables the pump to deliver precise amounts of insulin at specified intervals, aligning with the individual’s fluctuating metabolic needs.

The Insulin Pump serves as the operational platform for storing, managing, and executing one or more Basal Patterns. It allows users to configure multiple distinct patterns to accommodate varying daily routines, such as workdays, weekends, or periods of physical activity. These patterns are designed to maintain optimal glucose control by adjusting basal insulin delivery rates in response to physiological demands.

By executing the programmed Basal Pattern, the Insulin Pump ensures a steady, background supply of insulin, mimicking the natural secretion of insulin by a healthy pancreas. This capability is essential for effective long-term glycemic management in individuals with insulin-dependent diabetes. The flexibility to store and switch between multiple Basal Patterns enhances the personalization and responsiveness of insulin therapy, making the integration between Basal Pattern and Insulin Pump a cornerstone of modern insulin delivery systems.</data>
  <data key="d10">device programming,insulin delivery,management,programmable setting,programming,scheduling,therapy management</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cae8b84f90a8e9c929a19f036d8f1e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d15ff52c19d3f9036826d6260fd4dc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b299154da4c58d8322b7ac4e3af2f5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7220b25a27de0c76dc2804cda82d46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ad4286657624fbe3f4e7b422fa4717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7534f3bc09ac6e2eece38e12eb89cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f608f07eae4ddd5409aed9d4ecef75ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7</data>
