<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Bolus Wizard">
  <data key="d8">8.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Bolus Wizard is a built-in feature of the insulin pump designed to assist users in calculating and delivering accurate insulin bolus doses. Integrated directly into the insulin pump, this function streamlines the process of determining appropriate insulin amounts by analyzing user-provided data such as carbohydrate intake and current blood glucose levels. It leverages additional physiological parameters, including active insulin on board, to refine its dosage recommendations and prevent insulin stacking, thereby enhancing safety and precision in diabetes management.

The Bolus Wizard is configured and activated within the insulin pump, functioning as an essential tool for individuals who rely on insulin therapy. By automating complex insulin calculations, it reduces the potential for human error and supports more consistent glycemic control. Multiple descriptions emphasize its role as a core, built-in component of the insulin pump, underscoring its consistent integration across various references. Overall, the Bolus Wizard serves as a critical decision-support feature that enhances the usability and therapeutic effectiveness of insulin pump technology.</data>
  <data key="d10">device function,device functionality,device integration,dose calculation,feature integration,function activation,insulin delivery,insulin dosing,insulin management,therapy support,user assistance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-560db599319a34f19671d0bafeda5775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc17381a558f271a9da13b99091c2ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1250027f75a49e3288b12fc80a630d33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b299154da4c58d8322b7ac4e3af2f5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85d195e1f8c488146a71cdd978e8c82</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707600</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Reservoir">
  <data key="d8">8.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation between Insulin Pump and Reservoir describes a functional and structural integration essential to insulin delivery systems used in diabetes management. The reservoir is a key component of the insulin pump, serving as the storage unit for insulin that is delivered to the user. It is specifically designed to fit into the reservoir compartment of the insulin pump, where it is securely inserted to enable continuous or programmed insulin administration. This integration allows the insulin pump to access the stored insulin and deliver it through connected tubing or integrated mechanisms, depending on the pump design.

The reservoir not only holds the insulin supply but also supports monitoring features within the insulin pump system. The pump is capable of tracking the amount of insulin remaining, either by estimating the volume or by tracking the number of units dispensed. This functionality enables users and healthcare providers to monitor insulin levels and anticipate when a reservoir refill or replacement is necessary, contributing to safe and effective diabetes management. Multiple descriptions confirm that the reservoir is an integral part of the insulin pump system, emphasizing its role in both storage and delivery.

Overall, the reservoir functions as a critical subsystem within the insulin pump, ensuring a reliable supply of insulin is available for automated delivery. Its design facilitates seamless insertion and compatibility with the pump’s internal mechanisms, while also enabling real-time tracking of insulin volume. All provided descriptions consistently highlight the reservoir’s role in storing insulin and its physical and operational integration with the insulin pump, with no conflicting accounts or ambiguities present.</data>
  <data key="d10">component,component integration,device integration,drug storage,fluid delivery,fluid storage,insulin storage,level monitoring,volume monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-682b7d7aa57e01aca00a1d4393db7bd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779002dab61d888870696234d1dbdf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e93fcffd71ed0c035f0b03374608e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8e0765ea263fbb6747a09d204c99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76c99cd46001ae6a2373d3413db020f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707922</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
