<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Home Screen">
  <data key="d8">6.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The home screen is the primary interface of the insulin pump, serving as the starting point for device navigation and function access.|&lt;SEP&gt;The Home Screen of the Insulin Pump displays active statuses like "Basal Temporal" and provides access to main control options.&lt;SEP&gt;The home screen serves as the primary navigation point for accessing functions on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The Home Screen of the insulin pump serves as the central access point for key functions such as resuming basal delivery, setting temp basal rates, and entering blood glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Home Screen is part of the insulin pump interface, displaying active alerts such as "Suspended before low" and the Alert Silence icon.&lt;SEP&gt;The Home Screen displays key status indicators, including KJ when active insulin is reset.</data>
