<edge source="Children" target="4 Mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Children should use a 4 mm needle for insulin injection to match their thin skin and prevent intramuscular delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical recommendation,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694481</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Subcutaneous Prega">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Children up to 6 years old must use subcutaneous prega during insulin injection to ensure proper needle depth.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694482</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Needle Angle">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Children must use a 45° needle angle for needles 6 mm or longer to ensure safe and effective insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Children should receive insulin at a 45° angle when using needles 6 mm or longer to prevent intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">age-specific protocol,injection safety,patient-specific technique,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696014</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="4 mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The 4 mm needle is recommended for all children, especially those aged ≤6 years, to minimize intramuscular injection risk.&lt;SEP&gt;A 4 mm needle is recommended for children aged 6 years and younger to ensure subcutaneous delivery and avoid intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">device recommendation,injection safety,pediatric use,safe injection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696033</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Skin Fold Technique">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">For children aged ≤6 years, a skin fold should be used during injection with a 4 mm needle to ensure proper subcutaneous administration.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,subcutaneous delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695241</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Intramuscular Injection">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Children aged 2 to 6 years have a 20.2% rate of intramuscular injection when using a 4 mm needle without a skin fold, with higher rates for longer needles.</data>
  <data key="d10">age factor,injection risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695247</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Subcutaneous Pinch">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Children must use a subcutaneous pinch during insulin injection regardless of needle length due to limited subcutaneous tissue.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection safety,patient requirement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696012</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Insulin Dosing">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Children require small and odd-numbered insulin doses, necessitating precise measurement tools.</data>
  <data key="d10">pediatric care,precise dosing</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696028</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Lo Presti et al. Study">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Lo Presti et al. study found that children and adolescents have thin skin layers, supporting the use of 4–6 mm needles for safe insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">needle length recommendation,research finding</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696034</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Skin Pinch">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">For children aged 6 years and younger, a skin pinch is recommended when using a 4 mm needle to ensure subcutaneous delivery and prevent intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection safety,pediatric care</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696035</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Levemir">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A clinical study involving children above 2 years was extended for 12 months to assess long-term antibody formation during Levemir therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir's pharmacokinetics have been studied in children aged 1–17 years, showing no significant differences compared to adults.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">age group,long-term treatment,patient population,pediatric use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698230</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R must be kept out of reach of children to prevent accidental administration.&lt;SEP&gt;The pharmacokinetic profile of Novolin® R has been studied in children aged 6–12, with limited data suggesting possible differences in Cmax requiring individual dose adjustment.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R must be stored out of reach of Children to prevent accidental use or ingestion.</data>
  <data key="d10">access restriction,accessibility,dosage titration,pharmacokinetic study,safety precaution</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699077</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Novolin® R Penfill®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R Penfill® must be stored out of reach of children to prevent accidental use or ingestion.</data>
  <data key="d10">access restriction,safety precaution</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699178</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="Choking Hazard">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Children are at risk of choking on small parts of the product, posing a safety hazard.</data>
  <data key="d10">product danger,safety risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708191</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Diabetes Type 1" target="Insulin Therapy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin Therapy is a required treatment for individuals with Diabetes Type 1.</data>
