<edge source="Insulin NPH" target="Regular Insulin">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin NPH was mixed with regular insulin, and the storage temperature of the mixture did not affect its pharmacokinetic or pharmacodynamic properties.&lt;SEP&gt;When mixing insulin NPH and regular insulin, the regular insulin must be drawn first to prevent contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin NPH and regular insulin are mixed in the same syringe to achieve a combined therapeutic effect.</data>
  <data key="d10">combination therapy,dosing,insulin combination,mixing order,pharmacokinetics</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696042</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin NPH" target="Homogenization">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin NPH must be homogenized with 20 gentle movements to suspend insulin crystals and ensure consistent concentration.</data>
  <data key="d10">preparation method,suspension mixing</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695234</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin NPH" target="Subcutaneous Injection">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin NPH is administered via subcutaneous injection, where proper resuspension affects its pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic profile.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration route,delivery method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695237</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin NPH" target="Levemir">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A clinical study compared Levemir and insulin NPH in pregnant women with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir was compared to insulin NPH in a randomized controlled trial for managing type 1 diabetes during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;A randomized clinical trial compared Levemir and insulin NPH in pregnant women, showing similar efficacy and overall safety for both mother and fetus.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir is associated with a lower risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia compared to insulin NPH, allowing for more intensive dose titration.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical comparison,comparative efficacy,efficacy,hypoglycemia risk,study,treatment efficacy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698150</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin NPH" target="Insulin Aspart">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin NPH was used alongside insulin aspart as the prandial insulin in the control group of the study.</data>
  <data key="d10">basal-bolus regimen,combination therapy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698213</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin NPH" target="Fasting Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Mean fasting blood glucose was higher in the insulin NPH group than in the Levemir group at weeks 24 and 36 of gestation.</data>
  <data key="d10">glycemic control,treatment comparison</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698214</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin NPH" target="Insulin Detemir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin detemir shows lower variability, more predictable metabolic effect, and reduced risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia compared to insulin NPH.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical performance,comparative efficacy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-975d0ad130a42cf2fe8a0f91e4da2b29</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698252</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin NPH" target="Levemir®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir® has a lower risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia and is not associated with weight gain compared to insulin NPH.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical advantage,therapeutic comparison</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698300</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glycemic Variability" target="Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glycemic variability quantifies how much blood glucose levels rise and fall during the day, with lower variability being preferable.</data>
