<edge source="Subcutaneous Tissue" target="Subcutaneous Fold">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The subcutaneous fold is created by lifting the skin to elevate the subcutaneous tissue, facilitating correct needle placement for insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;The subcutaneous fold is created to facilitate proper needle insertion into the subcutaneous tissue.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,manual technique,needle insertion,tissue manipulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696043</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Tissue" target="Prega Subcutânea">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The prega subcutânea lifts the subcutaneous tissue to prevent intramuscular insulin injection and reduce risks.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,tissue elevation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695458</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Tissue" target="Uterine Expansion">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Uterine expansion during pregnancy causes thinning of subcutaneous tissue, necessitating adjustments in insulin injection technique.</data>
  <data key="d10">physiological change,tissue thinning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696011</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Tissue" target="Injection Site">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The injection site refers to the area of subcutaneous tissue where insulin is delivered.</data>
  <data key="d10">anatomical location,injection target</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696044</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Tissue" target="Insulin Action">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin is delivered into subcutaneous tissue, where it must travel to blood vessels, causing a delay in insulin action.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption delay,delivery site</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703175</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Tissue" target="Insulin Infusion Pump">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The insulin infusion pump administers insulin into the subcutaneous tissue via a catheter.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug administration,infusion site</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cbbd13d3e688c25e68d838e8069fec5c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709318</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="4 mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A 4 mm needle is recommended for both adults and children and is typically used without a skin fold.</data>
  <data key="d10">patient use,size recommendation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695231</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="5 mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A 5 mm needle is suitable for adults and children and is used without a skin fold, except in children under 6 years.</data>
  <data key="d10">patient use,size recommendation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695232</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Insulin Injection Technique">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The choice of needle length in insulin injection technique depends on patient age, BMI, and subcutaneous tissue availability.</data>
  <data key="d10">equipment selection,patient factors</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695232</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="6 mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A 6 mm needle requires a skin fold and is inserted at 90° in adults and 45° in children and adolescents to prevent intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection method,size recommendation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695233</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="8 mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An 8 mm needle requires a skin fold and is inserted at 90° in adults and 45° in children and adolescents, with a 45° angle advised for adults with low subcutaneous tissue.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection method,size recommendation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695234</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Skin And Subcutaneous Adipose Layer Thickness">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Skin and subcutaneous adipose layer thickness informs recommendations for appropriate needle length in insulin injections.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection safety,medical measurement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8fc83e266bdeb54c4139a50adf2b793a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695237</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Intramuscular Injection">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Using needles that are too long (≥8 mm) increases the risk of intramuscular injection, especially when inserted perpendicularly in individuals with low BMI.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection accuracy,risk prevention</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695239</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Skin Thickness">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Skin thickness varies by age and body region, and this data helps determine the appropriate needle length for safe subcutaneous insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">individualized treatment,medical guidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695240</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Needle Angle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Needle length determines the appropriate needle insertion angle, with shorter needles (4–5 mm) requiring 90° and longer needles requiring 45° in certain cases.</data>
  <data key="d10">procedural adjustment,technical parameter</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696013</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Fixed-Needle Syringe">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Fixed-needle syringes come with needle lengths of 6, 8, or 12.7 mm, with 6 mm being the preferred option.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection device feature,patient safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696374</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Insulin Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Frequent blood glucose monitoring enables patients and caregivers to adjust insulin doses in collaboration with the healthcare team.</data>
  <data key="d10">treatment personalization, clinical decision-making</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696146</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Blood Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d16">Insulin Dose Adjustment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Self-Care Education">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients are educated on performing daily blood glucose monitoring to manage their condition effectively.</data>
  <data key="d10">data collection,self-management</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696145</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Blood glucose monitoring is necessary during Novolin® R infusion to prevent hypoglycemia and adjust therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Monitoring blood glucose is recommended to optimize therapy with Novolin® R and prevent complications.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,glycemic control,treatment monitoring,treatment safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2339435aa42eeb6f0cb8bffbf4d5184</data>
