<edge source="Lipo-Hypertrophy" target="Skin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lipo-hypertrophy manifests as hardened areas or nodules on the skin, detectable through visual inspection and palpation.</data>
  <data key="d10">detection method,physical manifestation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694543</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Diabetes Type 2" target="Lipo-hypertrophy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lipo-hypertrophy affects between 28% and 64% of individuals with Diabetes Type 2.</data>
  <data key="d10">prevalence,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694516</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Diabetes Type 2" target="Adults with Type 1 or Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Adults with Type 2 Diabetes are included in the broader group of adults managed for diabetes with standard glycemic targets.</data>
  <data key="d10">adult management,disease classification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694599</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Diabetes Type 2" target="Healthcare Professional">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Healthcare professionals should avoid framing insulin use as a punishment and instead teach that it is a natural part of managing Diabetes Type 2.</data>
  <data key="d10">stigma prevention,treatment education</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695456</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Diabetes Type 2" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients with diabetes type 2 may start with lower doses of Novolin® R, such as 0.3 to 0.6 UI/kg/day.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage,therapeutic indication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699122</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina Regular" target="Insulina NPH">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Ao misturar insulina NPH e insulina regular, a insulina regular deve ser aspirada primeiro.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin NPH and regular can be mixed in the same syringe, with regular insulin drawn first.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration sequence,combinação,insulin mixing,sequência de uso</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
