  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Bolus Wizard">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Blood glucose values are input into the Bolus Wizard to calculate the appropriate insulin bolus dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose levels, such as 103 mg/dL, are input into the Bolus Wizard to calculate appropriate insulin doses.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Wizard uses current blood glucose levels to determine if a corrective insulin dose is needed.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Wizard uses blood glucose readings to calculate a correction bolus as part of the insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">correction calculation,correction factor,dosage determination,glucose monitoring,input data,input parameter</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-69f89cc6358f0fe2b490d63a60ae0581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b8d4c3fde5ebf7bc3593f47b765f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0deeba398b22b91d8da1b31653eede4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca312edfca5f05d148819c17f1d55943</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708141</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Carbohydrates">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Carbohydrates directly influence blood glucose levels, determining the required bolus insulin dose.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic impact,nutrient effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702765</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Meal Composition">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The composition of a meal, including fat, protein, and carbohydrates, influences the rate of glucose absorption and blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">digestion rate,nutrient impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-835d0624a6c9c20cffbc5a61e5f42de0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702770</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Sensor Glucose">
  <data key="d8">5.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Blood glucose and sensor glucose values may differ slightly, but both are used to monitor glucose trends, with sensor glucose derived from CGM.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor glucose and blood glucose are related but differ due to the physiological delay between blood and interstitial fluid glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Glucose lags behind Blood Glucose during rapid glucose changes, though they should be close during stable periods.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose and Sensor Glucose readings are related but not identical, with blood glucose used to calibrate the sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose readings are more accurate than sensor glucose values and should be used to verify SG when symptoms do not match.</data>
  <data key="d10">accuracy comparison,calibration,comparison,correlation,data correlation,measurement comparison,measurement discrepancy,physiological delay,time lag,verification method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b0f14c91b2fb52c8fcc6d43aa4f53f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03aab2b6261ddc73d474d0c866e7b37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86d3bb81c7595510175054c288b122fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d8c5703a9383d7fd4b6f1d14f5d5424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708240</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Glucose Sensor Value">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucose Sensor Value (SG) generally aligns with Blood Glucose (GS) during stable periods but may differ during rapid glucose changes due to sensor lag.</data>
  <data key="d10">measurement accuracy,physiological lag</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703180</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="SmartGuard Feature">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature requires manual entry of blood glucose readings after operating at maximum delivery rate for 7 hours to continue automated function.</data>
  <data key="d10">system calibration,user input</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707485</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Correction Bolus">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A correction bolus must be based on blood glucose meter readings after taking acetaminophen or paracetamol to prevent insulin errors.&lt;SEP&gt;A correction bolus is calculated based on blood glucose readings to bring levels into the target range.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">dosing accuracy,glucose correction,insulin calculation,insulin dosing</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707534</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Alert Settings">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Alert Settings use Blood Glucose levels to trigger high or low glucose alerts.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert triggering,threshold monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-583197b9760861a9bb1ee261914759fc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707551</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="CGM Device">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Blood glucose readings are used to verify the accuracy of sensor glucose data from the CGM device.&lt;SEP&gt;The CGM device is used to continuously monitor blood glucose levels over time.</data>
  <data key="d10">continuous monitoring,data comparison,health tracking,system verification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851fca8611c248b7f7b991f6dd4abbe2</data>
