</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="High Glucose Alert Reminder">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">If the High Glucose Alert Reminder is set too frequently, alerts may occur before corrective insulin has time to act during Hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert frequency,therapy feedback</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cf172904e354a6f4cca233304bf69b51</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702958</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Bolus Insulin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Bolus insulin is used to correct high blood glucose levels in cases of hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">correction therapy,glucose reduction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-20fd2bf061c46e98e4d7791fe6728699</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702966</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Insulin Infusion Set">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Problems with the insulin infusion set or site can lead to unexplained hyperglycemia and must be checked regularly.&lt;SEP&gt;A displaced or kinked insulin infusion set may cause unexplained hyperglycemia that does not respond to corrective boluses.</data>
  <data key="d10">cause analysis,device malfunction,equipment failure,infusion issues</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704377</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Basal Insulin Rate">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An incorrect or too low basal insulin rate can contribute to high glucose levels and ascending trends.</data>
  <data key="d10">glycemic control,insulin adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-75fbd29c63ccce2c6bea49f0301c1cf5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703098</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="AUC &gt;180 mg/dL">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">AUC &gt;180 mg/dL quantifies the extent and duration of Hyperglycemia events.</data>
  <data key="d10">severity measurement,time in range</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b392b58ab9f757711d038354d82e450e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703138</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Regular glucose checks help identify and prevent hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">prevention,risk detection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6e6b312daef8e67f312c6c144bbaa835</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703163</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Correction Bolus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A correction bolus is administered in response to hyperglycemia to lower elevated blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical indication,treatment response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-425759c12d133ef4832928e8f5d50896</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703173</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Glucose Absorption">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Delayed glucose absorption from high-fat, high-protein meals can lead to late hyperglycemia if insulin action does not match.</data>
  <data key="d10">delayed rise,timing mismatch</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4082de8021392199c251dff122fdc80b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703176</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Insulin Infusion">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Incorrect insulin infusion due to wrong Bolus Wizard settings may result in hyperglycemia from insufficient insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage error,treatment outcome</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc77598dbeb5980c719d1d54a6c3ab77</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704330</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Glucose Level">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A glucose level above 250 mg/dL indicates hyperglycemia, prompting ketone testing and corrective actions.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical condition,threshold trigger</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704374</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Ketone Testing">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Ketone testing is required when hyperglycemia is detected to assess the risk of diabetic ketoacidosis.</data>
  <data key="d10">diagnostic procedure,risk assessment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704375</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Insulin Reservoir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A weak insulin vial or contaminated reservoir may contribute to persistent high glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">cause analysis,equipment failure</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e910e1b2954d8b793bb4671174d8d92f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704378</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Practice Basal Rate">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Using practice basal rates for actual therapy could lead to insufficient insulin and result in hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">health risk,incorrect usage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f0f0c4f9a47c13cec124412ac6628a9b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704433</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Reservoir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Removing the reservoir while the infusion set is connected may result in incorrect insulin delivery, potentially causing hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical consequence,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707545</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="MiniMed Mobile App">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Relying solely on the MiniMed Mobile App for alerts may result in missed notifications, increasing the risk of hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert failure,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9b3a357a9c2bacf7aeb20d6f0357d7dc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707560</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Suspend All Delivery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Prolonged use of suspend all delivery without resuming basal insulin can lead to hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">health risk,therapy interruption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-03dcbf2b62aed8ffb26882713c89f9f7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707974</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="BG Meter">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A BG meter reading is required to confirm suspected hyperglycemia before treatment.</data>
  <data key="d10">diagnosis confirmation,symptom verification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708005</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Low Reservoir Reminder">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Low Reservoir Reminder helps prevent hyperglycemia by alerting users to refill insulin before under-delivery occurs.</data>
  <data key="d10">health safety,risk mitigation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708026</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Tubing Connector">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">If insulin or liquid contaminates the tubing connector, it may block vents and lead to incorrect insulin delivery, potentially causing hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">contamination risk,delivery failure</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc61f77b003d0086bd985ddb94fc2a98</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="SmartGuard Feature">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">If sensor glucose readings are much lower than actual blood glucose, the SmartGuard feature may deliver insufficient insulin, increasing the risk of hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage inaccuracy,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708153</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Pump">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">If the pump fails to deliver insulin due to leaks or errors, hyperglycemia may occur.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery failure,health risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708203</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Trend Arrows">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Trend arrows help users anticipate hyperglycemia by showing upward glucose trends.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical alert,risk prediction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bdbc37da05a342443ccfd48642dd1c3b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709329</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Transport" target="Thermal Packaging">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">When transporting insulin using thermal packaging or Styrofoam, precautions must be taken to prevent direct contact with ice to avoid freezing.</data>
  <data key="d10">temperature control,travel safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696040</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Transport" target="Hand Luggage">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must always be transported in hand luggage during travel to ensure proper temperature control and prevent loss.&lt;SEP&gt;During travel, insulin must always be carried in hand luggage to avoid exposure to extreme temperatures in cargo holds.</data>
  <data key="d10">safety,temperature stability,travel requirement,travel safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696370</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Transport" target="Thermal Insulated Container">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">When using a thermal container for transport, precautions must be taken to prevent insulin from contacting ice directly.</data>
  <data key="d10">safe transit,temperature protection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696368</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Transport" target="Hand Baggage">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin must be carried in hand baggage to avoid exposure to extreme temperatures and sunlight.</data>
  <data key="d10">safe handling,temperature control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696418</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Transport" target="Sealed Insulin Vials">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sealed insulin vials must be kept between 2 to 8°C during transport to maintain efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d10">storage conditions,temperature sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696419</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lancet" target="Finger Prick">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The lancet is used to perform a finger prick to obtain a blood sample for testing.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood collection,skin puncture</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694522</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lancet" target="Lancet Device">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The lancet is inserted into a lancet device that controls the depth and reduces pain during pricking.</data>
  <data key="d10">pain reduction,tool integration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694523</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Sensor" target="Finger Prick">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucose sensors offer a modern alternative to frequent finger pricks for people with needle fear or fatigue.</data>
  <data key="d10">alternative method,pain avoidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694527</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Sensor" target="Flash Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Flash Glucose Sensor is a type of glucose sensor that requires a reader to be scanned over it to access glucose data.</data>
  <data key="d10">data retrieval,scanning method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694577</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Sensor" target="CGM">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The CGM system relies on the glucose sensor to measure glucose levels in the interstitial fluid.</data>
  <data key="d10">data collection,technology component</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694579</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Sensor" target="Time in Range">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucose sensors enable the calculation of Time in Range by continuously tracking glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">continuous monitoring,data collection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694595</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Sensor" target="MRI">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The glucose sensor must not be exposed to MRI equipment as strong magnetic fields can cause malfunction and potential health risks.</data>
  <data key="d10">device safety,magnetic interference</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a1faf2db5ce0667a0d479a8832c2bc8d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778700997</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Sensor" target="Trend Arrows">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Glucose Sensor generates Trend Arrows to show the direction and speed of glucose level changes.&lt;SEP&gt;The glucose sensor provides data used to generate trend arrows that show the direction and speed of glucose changes.</data>
  <data key="d10">data display,glucose trend,predictive data,trend monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702790</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Sensor" target="Alerta En Limite Alto">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Alerta En Limite Alto is activated when the glucose sensor reading reaches the high glucose threshold.</data>
  <data key="d10">monitoring,trigger condition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702796</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Sensor" target="Red Symbol">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Glucose Sensor triggers the display of the Red Symbol when sensor glucose levels are below the low limit.</data>
  <data key="d10">low glucose detection,status indication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702854</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Sensor" target="Yellow Symbol">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Glucose Sensor triggers the Yellow Symbol when sensor glucose levels are above the low limit.</data>
  <data key="d10">recovery state,status indication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-96459b8c713f4d5788b5ab4023a5d992</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702857</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Sensor" target="SmartGuard™">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Glucose Sensor provides real-time glucose data that SmartGuard™ uses to make suspension and resumption decisions.</data>
  <data key="d10">data input,monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8595240fe716dd024092310ce068d824</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
