<edge source="Pancreas" target="Insulina Basal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pancreas produces small amounts of basal insulin continuously throughout the day and night.</data>
  <data key="d10">continuous secretion,hormone production</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6900fc7e5ef921c29efe412333f2e7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702928</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pancreas" target="Insulina En Bolus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pancreas produces larger amounts of bolus insulin in response to increased blood glucose after eating.</data>
  <data key="d10">hormone production,response to glucose</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6900fc7e5ef921c29efe412333f2e7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702934</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pancreas" target="Liver">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pancreas communicates with the liver via insulin and glucagon to regulate glucose storage and release.</data>
  <data key="d10">endocrine signaling,metabolic control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703202</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pancreas" target="Insulin Basal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pancreas secretes insulin basal continuously to maintain stable glucose levels between meals and during sleep.</data>
  <data key="d10">continuous secretion,metabolic stability</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703205</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pancreas" target="Insulin In Bolus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pancreas increases insulin in bolus production after eating to manage the rise in blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d10">postprandial regulation,stimulated secretion</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703208</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Bloodstream">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucose enters the bloodstream from the digestive tract and is transported throughout the body.</data>
  <data key="d10">circulation,transport</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702659</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Liver">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Excess glucose is stored in the liver and released when the body needs additional energy.&lt;SEP&gt;The liver stores excess glucose after meals and releases it into the bloodstream when glucose levels drop.</data>
  <data key="d10">energy reserve,energy storage,metabolic regulation,storage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c98e899214ad3a2eb3b7863c5d5bf</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702660</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Carbohydrates">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucose is primarily obtained through the digestion of carbohydrates in food.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic conversion,nutrient source</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702678</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Fat">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">When glucose intake exceeds immediate needs and liver storage capacity, the excess is converted into fat.</data>
  <data key="d10">energy storage,metabolic excess</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702679</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Digestive Tract">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucose is derived from carbohydrates in food as they are metabolized and absorbed through the digestive tract.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic processing,nutrient absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4cd2f791e7cc88d9bd36c809feb7b626</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702681</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Rapid Glucose Increase">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A rapid glucose increase refers to a sudden elevation in blood glucose levels, which can occur despite stable glucose management.</data>
  <data key="d10">blood glucose fluctuation,metabolic change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703102</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="High Insulin Level">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A high insulin level causes excessive movement of glucose from the bloodstream into cells, resulting in low blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose reduction,metabolic effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703106</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Interstitial Fluid Glucose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Interstitial fluid glucose levels are used by continuous glucose monitors as a proxy to estimate blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">measurement proxy,physiological correlation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-daa5dc0d158b3af5c0f7883f98cce6d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703108</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Human Body">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucose serves as the primary energy source for the Human Body, fueling vital organs and functions.</data>
  <data key="d10">energy source,metabolic function</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703168</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Brain">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Brain relies on a constant supply of Glucose to maintain thinking and regulatory functions.</data>
  <data key="d10">cognitive function,energy supply</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703170</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Heart">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Heart uses Glucose as an energy source to maintain continuous beating.</data>
  <data key="d10">energy supply,organ function</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703171</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Lungs">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Lungs require Glucose to support the energy demands of breathing.</data>
  <data key="d10">energy supply,respiration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7fbdbcaae1740f3543ed8a673ff203b0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703172</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose" target="Glucagon">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Glucagon triggers the liver to release stored glucose into the bloodstream to prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose release,metabolic regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b139e060742a21ffc13eee0fdbf0be4a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703201</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dysglycemia" target="Inflammation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Dysglycemia causes internal inflammation, contributing to long-term tissue damage.</data>
  <data key="d10">biological impact, systemic effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694540</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Dysglycemia</data>
  <data key="d16">Inflammation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dysglycemia" target="Vascular Damage">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Fluctuating blood glucose levels in dysglycemia damage blood vessels.</data>
  <data key="d10">biological impact, systemic effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694541</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Dysglycemia</data>
  <data key="d16">Vascular Damage</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dysglycemia" target="Metabolic Memory">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Dysglycemia contributes to metabolic memory, where the body retains the negative effects of past glucose imbalances.</data>
  <data key="d10">long-term consequence, physiological imprint</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694541</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">Dysglycemia</data>
  <data key="d16">Metabolic Memory</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dysglycemia" target="Macrovascular Diseases">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Dysglycemia contributes to the development of macrovascular diseases in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication,disease progression</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709753</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dysglycemia" target="Microvascular Diseases">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Dysglycemia leads to microvascular diseases such as retinopathy, nephropathy, and neuropathy.</data>
  <data key="d10">complication,disease progression</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709754</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Metabolic Memory" target="Oxidative Stress">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Metabolic memory is linked to oxidative stress, which persists even after glycemic control is achieved, contributing to organ damage.</data>
  <data key="d10">cellular damage,pathophysiological mechanism</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3a1c7be3f5278cc80c8bc958c35be31c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709753</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fasting Blood Glucose" target="Levemir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Levemir group had significantly lower mean fasting blood glucose levels compared to the insulin NPH group during pregnancy.</data>
