<edge source="Thiazolidinediones" target="Congestive Heart Failure">
  <data key="d8">6.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Thiazolidinediones can cause or worsen congestive heart failure, particularly when combined with insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Cases of congestive heart failure have been reported when thiazolidinediones are used with insulin, especially in patients with risk factors.&lt;SEP&gt;The combination of thiazolidinediones and insulin has been associated with an increased risk of congestive heart failure.&lt;SEP&gt;The combination of thiazolidinediones and insulin, including Novolin® R, has been linked to cases of congestive heart failure, particularly in predisposed patients.&lt;SEP&gt;The combination of thiazolidinediones and insulin has been linked to cases of congestive heart failure, particularly in at-risk patients.&lt;SEP&gt;The combination of thiazolidinediones and insulin has been associated with cases of congestive heart failure, particularly in at-risk patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,cardiovascular effect,combination therapy,drug combination risk,drug interaction,drug risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a6c42a674563e36382f398efac64a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ee5ffd422bf5c38703d11eefbcff6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001d95b4722fb6304af5e929d80557ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc71d03de36b3a734f3f7eff9922da5d</data>
