<edge source="Hipoglicemia Noturna" target="Levemir">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir is associated with a lower incidence of nocturnal hypoglycemia compared to NPH insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir is associated with a significantly lower risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia compared to NPH insulin, particularly in type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir is associated with a lower rate of nocturnal hypoglycemia compared to NPH insulin, as shown in studies NN304-1689 and NN304-1379.</data>
  <data key="d10">hypoglycemia risk,risk reduction,safety,safety advantage,safety profile</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
