<edge source="Insulin Sensitivity Factor" target="Bolus Wizard">
  <data key="d8">8.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Bolus Wizard utilizes the Insulin Sensitivity Factor as a critical parameter to calculate correction doses of insulin for elevated glucose levels. This feature relies on the Insulin Sensitivity Factor to determine how much insulin is needed to bring high blood glucose back into the target range. Specifically, the Insulin Sensitivity Factor quantifies the expected drop in blood glucose per unit of insulin, enabling the Bolus Wizard to compute precise correction boluses.

Multiple descriptions confirm that the Insulin Sensitivity Factor is a required input for the Bolus Wizard to function effectively in dose calculation. Without this value properly set, the system cannot accurately determine the necessary insulin dosage to correct hyperglycemia. As a key component in the algorithm, the Insulin Sensitivity Factor directly influences the amount of insulin recommended for correction, ensuring personalized and data-driven insulin delivery.

Across all provided descriptions, there is consistent agreement on the role of the Insulin Sensitivity Factor within the Bolus Wizard system: it enables the calculation of insulin correction doses based on current blood glucose levels. No conflicting entities or contradictory uses are present in the input, and all sources uniformly describe the same functional relationship. Therefore, the Bolus Wizard’s use of the Insulin Sensitivity Factor is consistently portrayed as essential for managing high blood glucose through automated insulin dosing recommendations.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration dependency,correction,correction calculation,correction dose,dosage calculation,dosage parameter,dose calculation,glucose adjustment,glucose correction,glucose lowering effect,glucose response,insulin calculation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe3d4956e4290b26b4d22092a403c4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b0e9023a7c03c6a284d69e0930b8a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b840edccb54a2c256450df95d80f4f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707639</data>
