  <data key="d9">Smcg provides dynamic glucose data that complements the static long-term measure of glycemic control given by Hba1c, enabling a more comprehensive assessment of diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d10">complementary assessment,glycemic evaluation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a7d99aa72407a6721b69e4da3cbbcba7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709746</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hba1c" target="Red Blood Cell Turnover">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Conditions affecting red blood cell turnover, such as anemias and hemoglobinopathies, can distort Hba1c readings.</data>
  <data key="d10">accuracy influence,biological interference</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709749</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hba1c" target="Chronic Kidney Disease">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Chronic Kidney Disease affects red blood cell lifespan and leads to inaccurate Hba1c results.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical limitation,measurement distortion</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709750</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hba1c" target="Ea1c">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Ea1c and Hba1c often do not align in many individuals with diabetes, leading to confusion in clinical interpretation.</data>
  <data key="d10">data discrepancy,metric comparison</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709751</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hba1c" target="J-Shaped Mortality Curve">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The J-Shaped Mortality Curve shows increased all-cause mortality at Hba1c levels below 6% and above 8%, indicating risks of both low and high glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical outcome,risk association</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709752</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hba1c" target="Wang Et Al. Study">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Wang et al. study demonstrated that very low Hba1c is not associated with reduced cardiovascular events and may increase mortality risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical evidence,health outcome</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709753</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hba1c" target="Glycated Hemoglobin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hba1c is a form of Glycated Hemoglobin used as a clinical indicator of average blood glucose levels over time.</data>
  <data key="d10">biological basis,clinical measurement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9af645f149415b242f6b7443aeb536d9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778709753</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
