<edge source="Hypoglycemia Management" target="MiniMed™ 640G">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia Management is the first step in using the MiniMed™ 640G system, focusing on avoiding glucose levels below 70 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose stability,therapy initiation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703186</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia Management" target="SAP">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hypoglycemia Management is the first structured step in the SAP therapy process, focusing on preventing low glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose control,therapy step</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4704ed3f5177349243c84d500af612b3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778703188</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Illness" target="Insulin Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">During illness, especially with nausea and vomiting, a patient's insulin needs may change, requiring dose adjustments and a pre-established management plan.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage change,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699625</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fever" target="Ketones">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The presence of fever in a diabetic individual may increase ketone production and is a recommended condition for ketone testing.</data>
  <data key="d10">infection response,metabolic stress</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694595</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Abdominal Pain" target="Ketones">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Abdominal pain is a symptom associated with elevated ketone levels and should prompt ketone testing in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical symptom,metabolic complication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694596</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Refil" target="Caneta Recarregável">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O refil é usado na caneta recarregável e deve ser do mesmo fabricante para garantir aplicação correta da dose.&lt;SEP&gt;The reusable insulin pen requires 3 mL insulin cartridges (refills) that must be replaced when empty.</data>
  <data key="d10">cartridge compatibility,compatibility,dosage accuracy,refillable system</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695441</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Refil" target="Humulin R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Humulin R is contained in a 3 mL refil specifically designed for insulin pens.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug containment,product design</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699627</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Refil" target="Caneta Aplicadora">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The refil must be used with a compatible reusable Lilly insulin pen for proper administration.</data>
  <data key="d10">device compatibility,drug delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699628</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Refil" target="Lilly">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lilly designs and tests the refil for use with their reusable insulin pens.</data>
  <data key="d10">manufacturer,product design</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699629</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Heat" target="Insulin Absorption Rate">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Exposure to heat from baths, fever, or compresses accelerates insulin absorption and can cause low blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat from fever, hot baths, or warm compresses increases insulin absorption speed and the risk of low blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d10">accelerated absorption,faster absorption,hypoglycemia risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695437</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Heat" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R must be protected from excessive heat to prevent degradation.</data>
  <data key="d10">stability,storage restriction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699111</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Cartridge" target="Storage Of Insulin Cartridges">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Unused insulin cartridges must be stored between 2 and 8°C and never frozen.</data>
  <data key="d10">refrigeration requirement,usage phase</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695530</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Exercise" target="Insulin Absorption Rate">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Physical activity increases insulin absorption and raises the risk of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise increases insulin absorption rate, raising the risk of hypoglycemia if insulin dosage is not adjusted.</data>
  <data key="d10">accelerated absorption,hypoglycemia risk,increased absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695436</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Exercise" target="Insulin Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Exercise can reduce insulin requirements and accelerate insulin action, particularly if involving the injection site, necessitating dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage change,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699627</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Exercise" target="High Glucose Trend">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Exercise during a high glucose trend must be approached cautiously, especially if ketones are present.</data>
  <data key="d10">activity consideration,therapy guidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cfc5f5eb70e79d2ce44b3ba795b76b3e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778702796</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Dose Adjustment" target="Multidisciplinary Team">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The multidisciplinary team supports patients and families in making regular insulin dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d10">collaborative care,medical supervision</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696144</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Dose Adjustment" target="Levemir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients switching to Levemir from another insulin may require dose adjustments, which can occur at the first dose or over weeks to months.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage change,treatment transition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698148</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Dose Adjustment" target="Travel">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients traveling across time zones of more than two hours must adjust their insulin dosage to maintain metabolic stability.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage change,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2df8f5e1333eed2f8c4d2dca734d5e21</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699628</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Skin Fold">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Creating a skin fold helps ensure insulin is delivered into the subcutaneous fat layer and not into muscle.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,proper delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695436</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Levemir">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir is administered subcutaneously, which influences its absorption and pharmacokinetic profile.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir must be administered via subcutaneous injection in areas such as the abdomen, thigh, or arm.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration route,drug delivery,therapeutic use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698228</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Levemir® FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir® FlexPen® is administered via subcutaneous injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration route,delivery method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-975d0ad130a42cf2fe8a0f91e4da2b29</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698252</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Cutaneous Amyloidosis">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Rotating injection sites helps prevent cutaneous amyloidosis, a potential complication of repeated insulin injections.</data>
  <data key="d10">risk mitigation,site rotation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698302</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Levemir®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir® must be administered via subcutaneous injection and should not be given intravenously or intramuscularly.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration route,injection method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1724d2e466fc891cc272dc5ef36ed31a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698303</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Novolin® R FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R FlexPen® is designed for subcutaneous administration of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration route,drug delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699024</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R is administered via subcutaneous injection, with peak plasma concentration achieved within 1.5 to 2.5 hours post-administration.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption,drug delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699211</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Pharmacokinetics">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The terminal half-life of insulin after subcutaneous administration is determined by absorption from the tissue, not by plasma elimination, lasting approximately 2 to 5 hours.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption rate,terminal half-life</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699212</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Lipodistrofia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Repeated subcutaneous insulin injections in the same location can lead to lipodistrofia.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,injection risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699628</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Humulin R">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Humulin R is primarily administered via subcutaneous injection in various body regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Humulin R is administered subcutaneously in the upper arms, thighs, buttocks, or abdomen, with site rotation recommended.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration route,injection method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e097e2326548df575159ee000923b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699628</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Administration" target="Lipoatrofia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Repeated subcutaneous insulin injections can lead to lipoatrofia, a form of lipodystrophy involving skin depression.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,tissue change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae828242172f4312fe9a98e8d49f3311</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699629</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Intravenous Administration" target="Levemir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Intravenous administration of Levemir is contraindicated as it may lead to severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">contraindication,safety risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698259</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Intravenous Administration" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R can be given intravenously by healthcare professionals using specific infusion solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R can be administered intravenously, but only under the supervision of a Healthcare Professional.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration route,medical supervision,medical use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2d59277cc4b25262a26a88992bfb526f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1d7f92cdb7923807a9067d937837a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699065</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Intravenous Administration" target="Novolin® R Penfill">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R Penfill can be administered intravenously, but only by healthcare professionals in medical settings.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical use,professional administration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699174</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Intravenous Administration" target="Novolin® R FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R FlexPen® can be administered intravenously by healthcare professionals using specific infusion systems and concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R FlexPen® can be administered intravenously under medical supervision.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration route,clinical use,medical use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ea9fa1ee045093083e543d672f1309db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699185</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Refeição" target="Paciente">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The patient administered insulin lispro too early before breakfast, leading to severe hypoglycemia due to mismatched timing.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical risk,timing mismatch</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696022</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina Glargina" target="Insulina Detemir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulina detemir provides glycemic control comparable to insulina glargina but with less weight gain.</data>
  <data key="d10">comparative efficacy,glycemic control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698242</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina Glargina" target="Levemir®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir® and insulin glargine are both long-acting insulin analogs, with differences in their variability and duration of action.</data>
  <data key="d10">comparative pharmacokinetics,therapeutic alternatives</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cba8a91b916675f6f4ef560f6976957e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698368</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pregnant Women" target="Subcutaneous Fold">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pregnant women are advised to use the subcutaneous fold technique for insulin injection to ensure safety.</data>
  <data key="d10">recommended practice,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694469</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pregnant Women" target="Abdomen">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pregnant women can inject insulin in the abdomen during the first two trimesters but should avoid it in the third trimester.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnant women should consult a doctor before injecting insulin in the abdomen and should avoid it in the third trimester.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection restriction,medical consultation,site safety,trimester-based guidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695435</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pregnant Women" target="4 Mm Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pregnant women are advised to use a 4 mm needle to ensure safe insulin delivery during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical recommendation,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778694483</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pregnant Women" target="Subcutaneous Prega">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pregnant women should use subcutaneous prega during insulin injection to prevent intramuscular delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
