</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Congenital Malformations">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The frequency of congenital malformations was 5% in the Levemir group and 7% in the insulin NPH group, with severe cases at 4% and 2%, respectively.&lt;SEP&gt;In a clinical study, the incidence of congenital malformations was 5% in the Levemir group, with 4% classified as severe.</data>
  <data key="d10">birth defect,birth defect risk,developmental risk,fetal safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698151</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Pre-Eclampsia">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The incidence of pre-eclampsia was higher in the Levemir group (10.5%) than in the insulin NPH group (7.0%).&lt;SEP&gt;In a clinical trial, the incidence of pre-eclampsia was 10.5% in the Levemir group compared to 7.0% in the insulin NPH group.</data>
  <data key="d10">incidence rate,maternal complication,pregnancy complication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698152</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Lactation">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The use of Levemir during lactation requires medical advice due to limited safety data.&lt;SEP&gt;It is unknown whether insulin detemir is excreted in human breast milk, but no metabolic effects are expected in nursing infants due to gastrointestinal breakdown.</data>
  <data key="d10">breastfeeding,caution,excretion uncertainty,medical guidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698152</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Medication Error Prevention">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients must check the label before injecting to avoid accidental substitution between Levemir and other insulins.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug mix-up,label verification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-da213aa66bddbd8e1bd2aba01ceb9f2d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698153</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Insulin Injection Site Reactions">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Use of Levemir may cause injection site reactions such as redness, itching, and swelling.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse effect,local reaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698156</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Cutaneous Amyloidosis">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Repeated insulin injections with Levemir in the same area may lead to cutaneous amyloidosis and delayed insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Repeated insulin injections with Levemir may cause cutaneous amyloidosis at injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Cutaneous amyloidosis is a rare or unknown adverse reaction associated with Levemir that may develop at the injection site.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption impact,adverse effect,rare adverse effect,rare complication,risk,tissue disorder</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698159</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Congestive Heart Failure">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The combination of Levemir and thiazolidinediones may lead to congestive heart failure, especially in at-risk patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse outcome,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698160</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="FlexPen">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">FlexPen is a device used for the subcutaneous administration of Levemir insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir is administered using the FlexPen, a pre-filled insulin injection device.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir is administered using the FlexPen, a pre-filled pen device designed for accurate and convenient insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,administration method,delivery method,device use,drug delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698162</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Medical Supervision">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Changing from another insulin to Levemir requires strict medical supervision due to potential dosage changes.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,treatment change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-00bac63e27caeb094fe802c0bfe00a44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698163</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Antidiabetics">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir can be used in combination with oral antidiabetics, with potential need for dose adjustments of concomitant medications.</data>
  <data key="d10">combination therapy,drug interaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698173</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="GLP-1 Receptor Agonist">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir can be combined with GLP-1 receptor agonists, but dose reduction of Levemir by 20% is recommended to minimize hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir can be used with GLP-1 receptor agonists, but its dose should be reduced by 20% to minimize hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d10">combination therapy,dose adjustment,hypoglycemia risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd292edf157383567920d27a920c13f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698173</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Basal-Bolus Insulin Regimen">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir is used as part of a basal-bolus insulin regimen, administered once or twice daily depending on patient needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir is used as the basal component in a basal-bolus insulin regimen, administered once or twice daily to maintain stable background insulin levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin regimen,therapeutic use,treatment integration,treatment protocol</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698174</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Renal Dysfunction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients with renal dysfunction require individualized Levemir dosing and enhanced glucose monitoring due to altered insulin clearance.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose adjustment,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698178</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Hepatic Dysfunction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients with hepatic dysfunction require personalized Levemir dosing and close monitoring due to impaired glucose regulation.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose adjustment,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698178</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Diet Change">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Changes in diet can impact glycemic control, requiring individualized adjustments in Levemir dosage.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose adjustment,glycemic influence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698180</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Concomitant Illness">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Concomitant illnesses can alter insulin requirements, warranting Levemir dose adjustments and close monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose adjustment,metabolic disruption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fcc0edfe7c2736912a3aa78c50f72b99</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698181</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Congenital Malformation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir was not associated with an excess risk of congenital malformations compared to other basal insulins in pregnant diabetic women.</data>
  <data key="d10">birth defect risk,safety monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698189</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Neonatal Death">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Neonatal death was one of the adverse outcomes assessed in the pregnancy safety study of Levemir.</data>
  <data key="d10">infant mortality,safety evaluation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698191</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Pre-eclampsia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">No significant difference was observed in the incidence of pre-eclampsia between Levemir and other basal insulins during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d10">pregnancy complication,risk assessment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698192</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Fetal Macrosomia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The risk of fetal macrosomia was evaluated in diabetic pregnancies and showed no significant difference with Levemir versus other basal insulins.</data>
  <data key="d10">fetal growth,metabolic impact</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698193</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Large For Gestational Age">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The rate of large for gestational age infants was assessed and found to be similar between Levemir and other basal insulin treatments.</data>
  <data key="d10">fetal size,growth monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698194</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Preterm Birth">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Preterm birth rates were monitored and showed no significant difference in women using Levemir compared to other basal insulins.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery outcome,gestational duration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698195</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Diabetes In Offspring">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The development of diabetes in offspring was monitored up to one year of age, with no significant difference observed between treatment groups.</data>
  <data key="d10">disease risk,long-term child health</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698196</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Levemir Penfill">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir is administered using the Levemir Penfill, a pre-filled pen device designed for insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir Penfill is a cartridge version of Levemir designed for use with specific injection devices.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration method,delivery system,drug delivery,product format</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9266b0855586c9a971861beb4d3289fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698196</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Albumin Binding">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The prolonged action of Levemir is mediated by the binding of its fatty acid side chain to albumin in the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d10">mechanism of action,prolonged effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698202</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Auto-Association">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Auto-association of Levemir molecules at the injection site contributes to delayed absorption and sustained insulin release.</data>
  <data key="d10">delayed absorption,mechanism of action</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698203</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Time-Action Profile">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir exhibits a more reproducible and less variable time-action profile compared to NPH insulin and insulin glargine.</data>
  <data key="d10">pharmacodynamic characteristic,reproducibility</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698204</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Intra-Patient Variability">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir shows lower intra-patient variability in glucose-lowering effect compared to NPH insulin in long-term clinical trials.</data>
  <data key="d10">consistency,pharmacokinetic advantage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698204</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Figure 1">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Figure 1 displays the activity profile of Levemir in patients with type 1 diabetes, illustrating its duration and consistency of action.</data>
  <data key="d10">activity profile,data visualization</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-590fb2f5c50ef31a5fd415bb01def92d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698207</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Hypoglycemia Episodes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">There was no statistically significant difference in the rate of hypoglycemia episodes between Levemir and insulin NPH during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse event,safety profile</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698208</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Adverse Maternal Events">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Levemir group had a numerically higher frequency of serious adverse maternal events (40%) compared to the insulin NPH group (31%).</data>
  <data key="d10">maternal safety,treatment risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698209</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Adverse Fetal Events">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Adverse fetal events were slightly more frequent in the Levemir group (24%) than in the insulin NPH group (20%).</data>
  <data key="d10">fetal safety,neonatal outcome</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698210</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Live Birth">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The rate of live births was 83% in the Levemir group compared to 89% in the insulin NPH group.</data>
  <data key="d10">neonatal survival,pregnancy outcome</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698210</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Cord Blood">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir was detected in cord blood in approximately 25% of newborns, indicating placental transfer during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug transfer,placental passage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e7e33f93b79c1061267614c8283508c6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698211</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Insulina Detemir">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir contains insulina detemir as its active pharmaceutical ingredient.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir contains insulina detemir as its active pharmaceutical ingredient.</data>
  <data key="d10">active ingredient,pharmaceutical composition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698214</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Mulheres Grávidas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir can be used during pregnancy if clinically necessary, with post-marketing data showing no fetal or neonatal toxicity.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical safety,pregnancy use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698215</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Insulina NPH">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir shows comparable glycemic control to NPH insulin but with a lower risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia and less weight gain.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir was compared to NPH insulin in a randomized controlled trial and showed non-inferiority in glycemic control as measured by HbA1c.&lt;SEP&gt;A randomized clinical trial compared Levemir and insulina NPH in pregnant women, showing similar efficacy and overall safety for both treatments.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir was compared to Insulina NPH in multiple studies, showing non-inferior glycemic control with better outcomes in hypoglycemia and weight gain.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical comparison,clinical trial,comparative efficacy,efficacy,insulin therapy,safety profile,therapeutic equivalence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698215</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Malformações Congênitas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">In clinical studies, 5% of infants in the Levemir group had congenital malformations, with 4% classified as severe.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">birth defect monitoring,congenital anomaly risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698216</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Controle da Glicose Sanguínea">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir is used to help control blood glucose levels in diabetic patients, especially during pregnancy.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">diabetes management,glucose regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698219</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Levemir FlexPen">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir is administered using the Levemir FlexPen, a pre-filled injection pen.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir FlexPen is the delivery device used for administering Levemir insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration device,drug delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698220</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Armazenamento do Medicamento">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir must be stored refrigerated before opening and can be kept at room temperature for up to 42 days after first use.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">shelf life,storage conditions</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698221</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Interações Medicamentosas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir's effectiveness and required dosage can be influenced by other medications that affect glucose metabolism.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,metabolic effect</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698221</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Doping">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir may cause a positive doping test, indicating its potential to affect athletic performance.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir may cause a positive result in doping tests, affecting athletes.</data>
  <data key="d10">anti-doping regulation,performance effect,regulatory risk,sports prohibition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc07da1fd30cc15e0022830f701a9c38</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698222</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Lactação">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">It is unknown whether insulin detemir from Levemir is excreted in human breast milk, but no metabolic effects are expected in nursing infants due to gastrointestinal breakdown of the peptide.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">breastfeeding,excretion uncertainty,metabolic inactivity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698223</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Direção de Veículos">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients using Levemir may experience hypoglycemia, which can impair their ability to concentrate and react, posing risks when driving vehicles.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">cognitive impairment,driving risk,hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698224</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Operação de Máquinas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The use of Levemir may lead to hypoglycemia, which can impair reaction and focus, making the operation of machinery potentially dangerous without proper precautions.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">hypoglycemia risk,machinery operation,safety precaution</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cc624fe52553cbd90a82f4181c5c0be7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698225</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Pharmacokinetic Properties">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pharmacokinetic properties describe how Levemir is absorbed, distributed, metabolized, and eliminated in the body.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical profile,drug behavior</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698225</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Serum Concentration">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir achieves peak serum concentration between 6 and 8 hours after administration, with steady-state levels reached after 2–3 doses.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">concentration kinetics,drug exposure</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698227</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Half-Life">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The half-life of Levemir ranges from 5 to 7 hours, depending on the administered dose, and is determined by subcutaneous absorption rate.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">duration of action,elimination rate</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698227</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Steady State">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Steady-state concentrations of Levemir are achieved after 2–3 twice-daily doses.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">dosing regimen,equilibrium</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a4232687a569d10d6942d933172488f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698229</data>
