  <data key="d13">1778698242</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Controle Glicêmico">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir provides glycemic control comparable to NPH insulin, as measured by HbA1c levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir demonstrated similar HbA1c trends but significantly lower fasting glucose levels compared to NPH insulin during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir provides glycemic control comparable to NPH and glargine insulins as measured by HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">HbA1c,fasting glucose,glycemic management,glycemic regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698243</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Ganho de Peso">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir is associated with less weight gain compared to NPH and glargine insulins in long-term treatment.</data>
  <data key="d10">side effect,weight management</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698245</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Anticorpos">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Antibody development has been observed with Levemir use, but it does not appear to affect glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d10">immune response,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698247</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Estudo NN304-1689">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The NN304-1689 study provided data on the efficacy and safety of Levemir in pediatric patients with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Estudo NN304-1689 provides clinical data on the efficacy and safety of Levemir in pediatric and adolescent patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Estudo NN304-1689 provided data on HbA1c, hypoglycemia, and weight change for Levemir versus NPH insulin in 347 patients.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical evidence,clinical trial,data source,efficacy data,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698247</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Estudo NN304-1379">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The NN304-1379 study evaluated Levemir versus NPH insulin in children and adolescents, showing reduced nocturnal hypoglycemia and weight gain.&lt;SEP&gt;Estudo NN304-1379 contributes to the long-term safety and efficacy profile of Levemir in young patients with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Estudo NN304-1379 evaluated Levemir over 24 months, including antibody formation and metabolic outcomes in comparison to NPH insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical evidence,clinical trial,long-term evaluation,safety,safety data</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698248</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Estudo NN1250-3561">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The NN1250-3561 study contributed to the evaluation of Levemir’s safety and efficacy in young patients with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Estudo NN1250-3561 evaluates the use of Levemir in children with type 1 diabetes, supporting its safety and efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical evidence,pediatric use</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698249</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Carpule de Levemir Penfill">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The carpule of Levemir Penfill contains 3 mL of Levemir solution, equivalent to 300 units of insulin detemir.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage form,packaging</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d80de93eae49980367cf11700b83b1ee</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698250</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Cloreto de Sódio">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Cloreto de sódio is an ingredient in Levemir used to maintain isotonicity.</data>
  <data key="d10">excipient,formulation component</data>
