</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="MedDRA">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Adverse reactions associated with Levemir are classified according to the MedDRA organ system classification in post-marketing data.</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse event classification,regulatory reporting</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ef496454c12f85ff1f62de19e8a22be4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698272</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The dose of Levemir must be individually adjusted based on self-monitored plasma glucose levels, physical activity, dietary changes, or concomitant illness.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage modification,individualized therapy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698303</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Plasma Glucose Self-Monitoring">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Plasma glucose self-monitoring is essential for guiding Levemir dose adjustments and detecting episodes of hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose tracking,treatment monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698304</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Injection Site Reaction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Injection site reactions such as pain, redness, urticaria, inflammation, bruising, edema, and pruritus are more frequently observed with Levemir than with human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">local adverse effect,skin response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698305</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Allergic Reaction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Uncommon allergic reactions, including urticaria, erythema, and skin rashes, have been reported in patients using Levemir.</data>
  <data key="d10">hypersensitivity,immune response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698306</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Anaphylactic Reaction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Anaphylactic reactions to Levemir are very rare but represent a serious systemic allergic response requiring emergency treatment.</data>
  <data key="d10">life-threatening reaction,severe hypersensitivity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698307</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Refractive Disorder">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Refractive disorders may occur at the initiation of Levemir treatment due to fluid shifts in the lens and are typically temporary.</data>
  <data key="d10">transient effect,vision change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698308</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Patients With Renal Dysfunction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients with renal dysfunction have reduced insulin clearance, increasing hypoglycemia risk and necessitating careful Levemir dose adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic adjustment,renal impairment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698310</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Patients With Hepatic Dysfunction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients with hepatic dysfunction have impaired glucose regulation, increasing hypoglycemia risk and requiring individualized Levemir dosing and close monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d10">liver impairment,metabolic adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698311</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Concomitant Medications">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The use of concomitant antidiabetic medications may require dose or timing adjustments when initiating or transitioning to Levemir therapy.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug interaction,therapy adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5a07d2f5e930a504dfb7c969e65903a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698311</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Reações No Local Da Injeção">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Reações no local da injeção, como dor, edema e prurido, são mais comuns com Levemir do que com insulina humana.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection site effect,local reaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698314</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Neuropatia Dolorosa">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Melhora rápida do controle glicêmico com Levemir pode estar associada à ocorrência de neuropatia dolorosa aguda, geralmente reversível.</data>
  <data key="d10">glycemic control,neurological complication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698315</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Lipodistrofia">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lipodistrofia é uma reação adversa incomum observada com o uso contínuo de Levemir nos locais de injeção.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection site effect,tissue alteration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698317</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Amiloidose Cutânea">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Amiloidose cutânea é uma reação adversa de frequência desconhecida associada ao uso repetido de Levemir em locais de injeção.</data>
  <data key="d10">rare complication,skin disorder</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698318</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Reações Alérgicas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Reações alérgicas, incluindo urticária e erupções cutâneas, são incomuns com Levemir em regime basal-bolus, mas mais comuns quando combinado com antidiabéticos.</data>
  <data key="d10">hypersensitivity,immune response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698319</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Reações Anafiláticas">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Reações anafiláticas são muito raras, mas potencialmente fatais, podendo ocorrer com o uso de Levemir.</data>
  <data key="d10">life-threatening reaction,severe allergy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698321</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Monitoramento Da Glicose Sanguínea">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Recomenda-se monitoramento rigoroso da glicose sanguínea durante a transição para Levemir e nas primeiras semanas de tratamento.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose regulation,treatment safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698323</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Antidiabéticos Orais">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O tratamento concomitante com antidiabéticos orais e Levemir pode requerer ajuste na dose ou no horário de administração.</data>
  <data key="d10">combination therapy,dose adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61071ebd09f043bc8e0041fda9bdf64a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698325</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Malformação Congênita Grave">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The frequency of severe congenital malformations was similar between Levemir (4%) and NPH insulin (2%) groups.</data>
  <data key="d10">congenital anomaly,safety outcome</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698327</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Malformação Congênita Leve">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The frequency of mild congenital malformations was 5% in the Levemir group and 7% in the NPH insulin group.</data>
  <data key="d10">minor congenital defect,outcome comparison</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698328</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Eventos Adversos Sérios Durante A Gravidez">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Numerically higher rates of serious adverse events were observed in both mothers (40% vs 31%) and babies (24% vs 20%) in the Levemir group compared to NPH insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">maternal and fetal safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698329</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Sangue Do Cordão-Umbilical">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir was detected in umbilical cord blood in approximately 25% of newborns at levels above 25 pmol/L, indicating placental transfer.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug transfer,fetal exposure</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698329</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Nascimento De Crianças">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The rate of live births was 83% (50 out of 60) in the Levemir group compared to 89% (55 out of 62) in the NPH insulin group.</data>
  <data key="d10">live birth rate,pregnancy outcome</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698332</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Estudo Clínico Controlado Randomizado">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A randomized controlled trial evaluated Levemir in 152 pregnant women with type 1 diabetes as part of a basal-bolus regimen.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical trial,treatment evaluation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698334</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Insulin Asparte">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir was used in combination with insulin asparte as part of a basal-bolus insulin regimen in pregnant women with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d10">basal-bolus regimen,combination therapy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ced7d025f7f3232d1a0e28251b0fb63a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698337</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Anticorpos Contra Insulina">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The development of antibodies against insulin was observed with Levemir use, but these did not negatively affect glycemic control or insulin dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;The use of Levemir led to the development of anti-insulin antibodies, which increased initially and then declined, without negatively affecting glycemic control or insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d10">immune response,long-term safety,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698383</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Liraglutida">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir combined with liraglutida and metformina leads to improved HbA1c levels in type 2 diabetes patients not controlled on oral agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Adding Levemir to liraglutida and metformina in patients not reaching glycemic targets resulted in improved HbA1c reduction from 7.6% to 7.1% over 52 weeks.</data>
  <data key="d10">combination therapy,glycemic control,treatment intensification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698383</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Tabela 29">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Tabela 29 illustrates that adding Levemir to liraglutida sustains the weight benefit in patients with type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d10">data presentation,weight benefit</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a24500f5f12a941115e4e44763af8133</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698386</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Ganho De Peso">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Levemir is associated with less weight gain than NPH insulin, with statistically significant differences in weight and BMI changes observed in clinical trials.</data>
  <data key="d10">metabolic impact,weight change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698406</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Estudo Combinado Liraglutida+Metformina E Levemir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The randomized study showed that adding Levemir to liraglutida and metformina significantly reduced HbA1c and maintained weight benefits without severe hypoglycemic episodes.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical evidence,trial outcome</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698407</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Hyperglycemic Episodes With Ketosis">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The rate of hyperglycemic episodes with ketosis was significantly higher with Levemir (1.09 episodes per patient-year) compared to insulin degludeca (0.68 episodes per patient-year).</data>
  <data key="d10">adverse event,safety comparison</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698410</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Adolescent Patients">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Efficacy and safety data for Levemir in adolescent patients with type 2 diabetes were extrapolated from studies in type 1 diabetes and adult type 2 diabetes populations.</data>
  <data key="d10">extrapolated data,treatment indication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-302e8ebf2cacce3164fd241fd39db173</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698413</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Tresiba" target="Ultra-Slow Insulin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Tresiba is a brand of ultra-slow-acting insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">brand,medication type</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
