  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Technical Note 84/2021">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Technical Note 84/2021 specifies the monthly distribution of needles based on insulin type used by the patient.</data>
  <data key="d10">distribution policy,healthcare guidelines</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695531</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Insulin Application Technique">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A needle must be attached to the insulin pen for each injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,equipment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695614</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Syringe">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The needle is attached to the syringe for insulin injection and comes in various lengths.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection,medical device assembly</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695678</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Injection Angle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Needles of 4mm and 5mm are injected at 90 degrees, while 6mm needles are injected at 90 degrees in adults and 45 degrees in children.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,patient safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695681</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Levemir® FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The needle is attached to the Levemir® FlexPen® for subcutaneous insulin delivery and must be removed after each use to prevent leakage and contamination.</data>
  <data key="d10">attachment,injection method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5561a191d3b525d406e49933648e27bf</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698353</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Novolin® R Penfill">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Needles are used to inject Novolin® R Penfill and must be discarded in puncture-resistant containers after use.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration tool,disposal requirement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699178</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Recyclable Waste">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Needles are not recyclable and must not be disposed of in regular or recyclable waste due to safety risks.</data>
  <data key="d10">disposal method,waste classification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699179</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Puncture-Resistant Container">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Used needles must be discarded in puncture-resistant containers to prevent accidental needlesticks and contamination.</data>
  <data key="d10">injury prevention,safe disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-98a0b8b861ae9af417a572907fe16408</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699181</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Novolin® R FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Novolin® R FlexPen® is used with disposable needles up to 8 mm in length, which must remain under the skin for at least 6 seconds.&lt;SEP&gt;The needle is attached to the Novolin® R FlexPen® to enable subcutaneous insulin injection and must be replaced if defective.&lt;SEP&gt;The Novolin® R FlexPen® is used with a disposable needle for insulin injection, which must not be shared.</data>
  <data key="d10">compatibility,device attachment,device component,injection mechanism,insulin administration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fc3409d91fe33592f741a0002d70749c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ae5fe50adf25db0be3b8cdde6282e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e44a4ca961f1a97305607fa263ed91</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699189</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Insulin Flow">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A drop of insulin must appear at the needle tip to confirm proper insulin flow before injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">flow verification,injection readiness</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fc3409d91fe33592f741a0002d70749c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699190</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle" target="Cross-Infection">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sharing needles with others can lead to cross-infection, posing serious health risks.</data>
  <data key="d10">health risk,safety warning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-27ae5fe50adf25db0be3b8cdde6282e9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699231</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Air Bubble" target="Levemir® FlexPen®">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Air bubbles in the carpule of the Levemir® FlexPen® must be removed before injection to ensure proper insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection safety,priming</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5d212ccdded1e4ccf51af243a8d38b4c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778698401</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Mixing" target="Fixed-Needle Syringe">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Fixed-needle syringes are the only type suitable for mixing two types of insulin in the same syringe, requiring proper training.&lt;SEP&gt;Only fixed-needle syringes should be used for mixing two types of insulin to ensure accuracy and prevent contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;A fixed-needle syringe is recommended when mixing two types of insulin to maintain sterility and accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d10">accurate dosing,clinical practice,combination therapy,contamination prevention,preparation method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696021</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Mixing" target="Vacuum Formation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Vacuum in a vial can cause unintended transfer of one insulin type into another vial during mixing.</data>
  <data key="d10">contamination risk,procedural error</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696020</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Caneta" target="Agulha">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Needles are attached to insulin pens for subcutaneous insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d10">device attachment, injection tool</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b</data>
