<edge source="Biphasic Insulin" target="Homogenization">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Biphasic insulin requires homogenization using gentle rolling to achieve uniform insulin distribution before injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">preparation method,suspension mixing</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695235</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Homogenization" target="Rolling Motion">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The rolling motion between palms or in a pendulum is the recommended physical method to homogenize insulin suspensions.</data>
  <data key="d10">mixing technique,physical method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695236</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Homogenization" target="Pharmacokinetics">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Proper homogenization of insulin NPH ensures predictable pharmacokinetics and reduces intra-individual variability.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption consistency,treatment efficacy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695237</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Homogenization" target="Pharmacodynamics">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Inadequate homogenization leads to unpredictable pharmacodynamic effects, including variable glucose-lowering responses.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical response,treatment efficacy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695237</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pharmacokinetics" target="Absorption">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Absorption affects insulin’s pharmacokinetic profile, with peak plasma levels reached 1.5–2.5 hours post-injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Absorption is a key phase of insulin pharmacokinetics, with peak plasma levels reached 1.5 to 2.5 hours after injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug uptake,plasma concentration,subcutaneous delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699010</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pharmacokinetics" target="Distribution">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin distribution is characterized by minimal plasma protein binding except for circulating insulin antibodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Distribution in pharmacokinetics shows insulin has low plasma protein binding except with circulating insulin antibodies.</data>
  <data key="d10">antibody interaction,circulation,protein binding</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699011</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pharmacokinetics" target="Metabolism">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin is metabolized by specific enzymes, resulting in inactive metabolites after hydrolysis at proposed cleavage sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolism is part of insulin pharmacokinetics involving degradation by specific enzymes into inactive metabolites.</data>
  <data key="d10">enzyme degradation,metabolic breakdown,molecular cleavage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699012</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pharmacokinetics" target="Elimination">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The terminal half-life of insulin is governed by absorption rate from subcutaneous tissue, not by direct elimination from blood.&lt;SEP&gt;Elimination of insulin is reflected in a terminal half-life of 2–5 hours, determined by subcutaneous absorption rate.</data>
  <data key="d10">absorption dependency,clearance,half-life,half-life determination</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-df59f6460ce09b02f1576e31831b6eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849980827afbc1e3097aed3d19640efe</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699012</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pharmacokinetics" target="Novolin® R">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pharmacokinetics of Novolin® R are influenced by intra- and inter-individual factors such as dose, administration site, and subcutaneous fat thickness, leading to variable absorption and half-life.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug behavior,variability</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-43208e8857e43453277beecb7a6c55d5</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778699210</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Storage Temperature Of Insulin" target="In-Use Insulin Pens">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The storage temperature of insulin affects the stability and performance of in-use insulin pens, influencing treatment outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d10">drug stability,environmental factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8fc83e266bdeb54c4139a50adf2b793a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695238</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gibney Ma" target="Skin And Subcutaneous Adipose Layer Thickness In Adults With Diabetes At Sites Used For Insulin Injections">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Gibney Ma led a study on adipose layer thickness to inform insulin needle length recommendations.</data>
  <data key="d10">anatomical research,authorship</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f7da978df74ee7f686dcc3c260d75577</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696271</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lo Presti D" target="Skin And Subcutaneous Thickness At Injecting Sites In Children With Diabetes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lo Presti D conducted ultrasound studies on injection sites in children to improve injection safety.</data>
  <data key="d10">authorship,pediatric research</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f7da978df74ee7f686dcc3c260d75577</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696271</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Skin Thickness" target="Insulin Pen Needle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The choice of insulin pen needle length should be based on patient skin thickness to ensure subcutaneous delivery and avoid intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection safety,needle length selection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696035</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fixed-Needle Syringe" target="Dead Space">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Fixed-needle syringes have less dead space than removable-needle syringes, reducing the risk of dosing errors.</data>
  <data key="d10">device design,error prevention</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695244</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fixed-Needle Syringe" target="Removable-Needle Syringe">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Removable-needle syringes are discouraged in favor of fixed-needle syringes due to higher dead space and lower dose accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d10">device comparison,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695245</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fixed-Needle Syringe" target="Insulin Combination">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A fixed-needle syringe is required for accurately mixing two types of insulin in the same syringe.</data>
  <data key="d10">accurate mixing,device requirement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696017</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fixed-Needle Syringe" target="Residual Space">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Fixed-needle syringes do not have residual space, which reduces medication waste and improves dose precision.</data>
  <data key="d10">device design,dosing accuracy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696375</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Removable-Needle Syringe" target="Dead Space">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The removable-needle syringe has a large dead space that can retain up to 10 units of insulin, leading to product waste and dosing inaccuracies.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosing error,insulin waste</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696031</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Room Temperature Insulin" target="Plasma Insulin Peak">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Room temperature insulin leads to a delayed and lower peak in plasma insulin levels compared to refrigerated insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">delayed peak,slower absorption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695249</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Multicenter Study" target="Spain">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The multicenter study on insulin injection practices and lipodystrophy was conducted in Spain across primary and specialized healthcare centers.</data>
  <data key="d10">research setting,study location</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695249</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Spain" target="Customer Service Center">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Customer Service Center provides support for Accu-Chek Solo users in Spain via a toll-free number and website.</data>
  <data key="d10">customer support,service availability</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ed5fdff66ffcd1f4d4e10a8825e7905c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/IFU Accu-Chek Guide Solo Diabetes Manager.PDF</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704671</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Hands">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Washing hands with soap and water is the first step in the insulin application technique.</data>
  <data key="d10">hygiene,preparation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695612</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Lente Insulin">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lente insulin requires 20 gentle movements of the pen before use to ensure proper mixing.</data>
  <data key="d10">medication handling,preparation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695614</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Injection Angle">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The needle must be inserted at either a 45 or 90-degree angle depending on needle length and patient age.&lt;SEP&gt;The needle should be inserted at a 45 or 90-degree angle depending on needle length and patient age.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,device use,injection technique,technique</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695680</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Needle Disposal Container">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Used needles and lancets must be discarded in a rigid container such as a fabric softener or disinfectant bottle.</data>
  <data key="d10">safety,waste management</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695621</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Health Unit">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The used needle disposal container must be delivered to the nearest health unit for proper handling.</data>
  <data key="d10">safety protocol,waste disposal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695621</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Service of Endocrinology and Diabetes - SED">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Service of Endocrinology and Diabetes - SED is responsible for the insulin use guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d10">guideline development,medical oversight</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695622</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Nurses and Nursing Residents in Diabetes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Nurses and nursing residents in diabetes at the Endocrinology Clinic developed the insulin use guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d10">guideline authorship,healthcare practice</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695623</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Hands Washing">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hands must be washed with soap and water before beginning the insulin application process.</data>
  <data key="d10">hygiene,preparation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695675</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Insulin Dose Aspiration">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The correct insulin dose must be aspirated into the syringe following proper mixing and sequence rules.</data>
  <data key="d10">administration,dosing accuracy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695678</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Air Bubble Removal">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Air bubbles must be removed from the syringe before injection to ensure accurate insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosing accuracy,safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695679</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Injection Site Prega">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A skin fold (prega) must be formed at the injection site to facilitate proper subcutaneous needle insertion.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection technique,subcutaneous delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695680</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Diabetes Nurses and Nursing Residents">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">These healthcare professionals from SED developed the insulin administration guidelines for patient use.</data>
  <data key="d10">guideline development,patient education</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695682</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Application Technique" target="Self-Care Education">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Patients are taught the insulin application technique as part of self-care education, with periodic evaluation of their performance.</data>
  <data key="d10">clinical assessment,skill training</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696144</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Skin Fold" target="Adolescents And Adults With Low Body Fat">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Adolescents and adults with low body fat are advised to use the subcutaneous skin fold technique to avoid intramuscular insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">injection safety,tissue protection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695439</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dupla Checagem" target="Práticas Seguras para Preparo e Aplicação de Insulina">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Double-checking is a key component of safe insulin practices to prevent high-risk medication errors.</data>
  <data key="d10">error prevention,safety protocol</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778696020</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Canetas Reutilizáveis De Insulina" target="SUS">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O SUS fornece gratuitamente as canetas reutilizáveis de insulina para pessoas com diabetes como parte do tratamento.</data>
  <data key="d10">healthcare access,provision</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695527</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Canetas Reutilizáveis De Insulina" target="Tubete De Insulina">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">As canetas reutilizáveis de insulina são projetadas para uso com tubetes de insulina de 3 mL, que são substituídos ao final do conteúdo.</data>
  <data key="d10">compatibility,device usage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695528</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Canetas Reutilizáveis De Insulina" target="Pessoa Com Diabetes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A pessoa com diabetes utiliza a caneta reutilizável de insulina para melhorar o engajamento e a aderência ao tratamento.</data>
  <data key="d10">patient use,treatment adherence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695529</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Canetas Reutilizáveis De Insulina" target="Período De Utilização">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A caneta reutilizável pode ser usada por até 3 anos, sendo substituível apenas em caso de quebra ou perda com justificativa.</data>
  <data key="d10">device lifespan,replacement policy</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695530</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Canetas Reutilizáveis De Insulina" target="Diabetes.org.br">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Diabetes.org.br fornece orientações sobre o uso correto e seguro das canetas reutilizáveis de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d10">health guidance,information source</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695531</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Canetas Reutilizáveis De Insulina" target="Agulha Descartável">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A agulha descartável é acoplada à caneta reutilizável para permitir a aplicação da insulina, mas não deve ser guardada acoplada após o uso.</data>
  <data key="d10">device assembly,injection mechanism</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778695532</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SUS" target="Agulha Descartável">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">O SUS fornece agulhas descartáveis compatíveis com as canetas reutilizáveis, que devem ser usadas uma única vez.</data>
  <data key="d10">medical equipment,provision</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
