<edge source="Reservoir" target="Pump">
  <data key="d8">11.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation between the pump and the reservoir is central to the operation of insulin delivery systems, particularly in devices such as the MiniMed MMT-332A. The pump is designed to contain, manage, and interface with a disposable reservoir that stores insulin for controlled delivery into the patient’s body. This reservoir is a critical component of the pump system, inserted into a dedicated reservoir compartment within the pump, where it is secured by turning it clockwise to lock it in place. Proper insertion and secure locking are essential to ensure reliable insulin delivery and to prevent leaks or disconnections.

The reservoir serves as the insulin storage unit, holding the medication before it is delivered through an infusion set connected to the patient. Specific reservoir types are required depending on the infusion set used, ensuring compatibility and effective function within the pump system. The pump displays the reservoir's capacity on its screen, allowing users to monitor insulin levels and anticipate when replacement is needed. Once the reservoir is empty, it must be replaced to maintain continuous insulin therapy.

To ensure safety during reservoir replacement, the pump must first be rewound, a step that prevents accidental insulin infusion during the insertion process. Secure connections between the reservoir and the pump are vital to maintain the integrity of insulin delivery and avoid malfunctions. Overall, the reservoir functions as a replaceable, integral part of the pump system, designed for precise, safe, and efficient insulin management.</data>
  <data key="d10">component integration,connection,consumable use,delivery component,device connection,device insertion,device integration,fluid delivery,inspection,insulin delivery,insulin storage,internal component,mechanical locking,preparation step</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc61f77b003d0086bd985ddb94fc2a98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707506</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
