  <data key="d9">The reservoir is a part of the MiniMed 780G system that stores insulin for subcutaneous delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery component,insulin storage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-faf5718341c7a791a86f965a94ffbdbc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708474</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Reservoir" target="Insulin Flow Blocked Alarm">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An empty reservoir can trigger the Insulin Flow Blocked alarm due to lack of insulin for delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">alarm cause,empty reservoir detection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708526</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Reservoir" target="Status Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Status Screen shows detailed information about the insulin remaining in the Reservoir beyond what the icon indicates.</data>
  <data key="d10">detailed monitoring,status display</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708529</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Piston" target="Mini-Computer">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The mini-computer controls the piston to administer insulin in very small, precise doses.|</data>
  <data key="d10">device control,precision dosing</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-682b7d7aa57e01aca00a1d4393db7bd9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778700991</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Piston" target="Pump">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The piston inside the pump pushes on the reservoir to move insulin into the tubing.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin delivery,mechanism</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707562</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Piston" target="Rewinding">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">During the rewinding process, the piston returns to its start position in the reservoir compartment, which may take several seconds.</data>
  <data key="d10">initialization,mechanical reset</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707989</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Piston" target="MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Piston is part of the MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump that engages the reservoir to push insulin through the tubing.</data>
  <data key="d10">device mechanism,mechanical operation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708099</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Piston" target="Pump Rewind">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pump Rewind returns the Piston to its starting position to prepare for a new reservoir insertion.</data>
  <data key="d10">mechanical reset,preparation step</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708100</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Battery" target="Battery Compartment Cap">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The battery compartment cap secures the AA battery inside the insulin pump.|</data>
  <data key="d10">component enclosure,device safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-682b7d7aa57e01aca00a1d4393db7bd9</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778700991</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Battery" target="Pump">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump is powered by a battery that displays a red bar when low and a fully black icon with red outline when immediate replacement is required.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump requires a battery to operate and deliver insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump relies on the battery for power, and low battery triggers alerts and can stop insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump relies on the battery for power, and battery status is monitored through various alarms and indicators.</data>
  <data key="d10">device operation,low power indication,operation,power dependency,power source,power supply</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c9e2bc905a98db798f2f20c77f1f950e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707564</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Battery" target="AA Lithium Battery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An AA lithium battery is recommended for optimal pump performance.</data>
  <data key="d10">battery type,compatibility</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707566</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Battery" target="AA Alkaline Battery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An AA alkaline battery is compatible with the pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">battery type,compatibility</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707568</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Battery" target="AA NiMH Battery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">An AA NiMH rechargeable battery is acceptable for use in the pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">battery type,rechargeable</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707570</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Battery" target="Carbon Zinc Battery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Carbon zinc batteries are not compatible with the pump and can cause inaccurate battery readings.</data>
  <data key="d10">incompatibility,risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707572</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Battery" target="Insert Battery Alarm">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Removing the battery triggers the Insert Battery alarm, which must be cleared with a new battery within 10 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d10">alarm trigger,power management</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707574</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Battery" target="Power Loss Alarm">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Extended power loss due to battery removal can trigger a Power loss alarm requiring time and date re-entry.</data>
  <data key="d10">alarm trigger,system reset</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707575</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Battery" target="Status Icons">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Battery status icon visually represents the charge level of the pump battery, changing color and fill as it depletes.</data>
  <data key="d10">power status,visual indicator</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
