</edge>
<edge source="Home Screen" target="Stop Bolus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Stop Bolus function is accessed from the Home screen to halt an ongoing bolus delivery.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">bolus interruption,user interface</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707536</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Home Screen" target="Pump">
  <data key="d8">8.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Home Screen serves as the primary user interface of the pump, offering centralized access to key functions and real-time system status information. It is designed to support user operations in Manual mode, enabling interaction with core features such as initiating self-tests, managing settings, and monitoring insulin delivery. Upon first use, inserting a battery triggers the appearance of the Home Screen, which then resumes basal insulin delivery, indicating its critical role in both startup and ongoing operation.

The Home Screen displays a range of system messages and alerts essential for device management and user awareness. These include notifications such as "Sensor warm up," confirmation of successful device pairing, and various operational alerts. Some alerts are only visible after returning to the Home Screen, underscoring its function as the central hub for critical updates. By consolidating status information and interactive controls, the Home Screen ensures users can efficiently monitor and operate the pump, making it integral to the overall functionality and safety of the device.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert visibility,feature access,interface control,interface display,navigation,operation resumption,status display,status update,system status,user interface,user navigation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707577</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Home Screen" target="Active Insulin Reset To Zero Alarm">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After the Active Insulin Reset To Zero Alarm, KJ appears on the Home Screen until the specified time.</data>
  <data key="d10">alarm display,status indicator</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fcdcd9414b427304808016daa676e270</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707621</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Home Screen" target="Display Options">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Display Options control how information is presented on the Home Screen.</data>
  <data key="d10">interface customization,user experience</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707644</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Home Screen" target="Pair New Device">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The user accesses the Pair New Device function from the Home Screen to begin pairing a CGM device.</data>
  <data key="d10">function initiation,navigation</data>
