</edge>
<edge source="Transmitter" target="Pump">
  <data key="d8">7.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The transmitter pairs with the pump, and a steady green LED indicates successful pairing; continued blinking may indicate incorrect pairing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Transmitter pairs with the Pump to enable data transmission and activate the Sensor Feature.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump must be paired with the transmitter to enable wireless communication with the sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump attempts to locate the transmitter signal, and if unsuccessful, triggers the possible signal interference or check connection alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump fails to detect the transmitter and cannot receive sensor glucose signals if the connection is insecure or disrupted.&lt;SEP&gt;The transmitter sends sensor data to the pump, and failure to detect it triggers the Check Connection Alert.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump pairs with the transmitter to receive glucose data from the sensor.</data>
  <data key="d10">LED indicator,communication,connection check,connectivity,data communication,data relay,data transmission,device pairing,pairing,signal detection,signal transmission</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4df342459d4afd90a81b1a3f13d859</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707527</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
