</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard" target="Suspend On Low">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">SmartGuard activates Suspend On Low when sensor glucose drops below a defined level.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend On Low operates within the SmartGuard feature to halt insulin delivery when sensor glucose reaches or falls below the set limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend On Low is an automatic action by SmartGuard to stop insulin delivery when glucose levels are too low.</data>
  <data key="d10">automated response,hypoglycemia prevention,safety feature,safety mechanism,threshold-based action,threshold-based suspension</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60422265d298e0482f6b78dc36f2a16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
