</edge>
<edge source="Manual Mode" target="MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The MiniMed 780G insulin pump operates in Manual mode, which requires user input for meal and correction boluses.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed 780G insulin pump restricts certain bolus types to Manual mode.</data>
  <data key="d10">bolus availability,operating mode,operational mode,user control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707499</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Manual Mode" target="SmartGuard Mode">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">SmartGuard mode is an advanced operating mode that users transition to after initial use in Manual mode, as directed by a healthcare provider.</data>
  <data key="d10">operating mode comparison,transition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9cb557f99f1234ecc2b21be31e823064</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707501</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Manual Mode" target="SmartGuard Feature">
  <data key="d8">6.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature is not active when the pump is in Manual mode, and users must rely on BG meter readings for treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard feature is inactive in Manual mode, where SG values should not be used.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard feature must be active for sensor glucose values to be used in bolus calculations; in Manual mode, they should not be used for treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The basal rate for Manual mode must be set before the SmartGuard feature can be activated, indicating a dependency between the two modes.&lt;SEP&gt;When conditions prevent the SmartGuard feature from continuing, the pump transitions to Manual Mode, delivering insulin at a fixed basal rate for up to 4 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard feature can exit and transition into Manual Mode when sensor glucose is unavailable or when an unsafe basal pattern is detected.</data>
  <data key="d10">feature control,feature deactivation,mode transition,operational dependency,operational state,system state change,system transition,treatment decision</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb234cb663874d4e5a473c7f3e19383b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707578</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Manual Mode" target="Max Basal Setting">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Max basal setting applies only to Manual mode and does not affect SmartGuard's automated delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The Max basal setting applies only in Manual mode to limit insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery limit,mode-specific configuration,operational constraint,user control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707662</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Manual Mode" target="Pump">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Manual mode allows the user to control insulin delivery without automated SmartGuard adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d10">operational setting,user control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707717</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Manual Mode" target="Bolus Wizard Feature">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Bolus Wizard feature is only available when the insulin pump is in Manual Mode.</data>
  <data key="d10">feature availability,operational dependency</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707794</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Manual Mode" target="MiniMed 780G System">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">In Manual mode, the MiniMed 780G system does not perform automated insulin dosing, and SG readings should not be used for treatment decisions.</data>
  <data key="d10">operational state,treatment limitation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
