<edge source="Pump" target="User">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The user operates the pump to initiate connection, confirm serial number matching, and enable pairing features.</data>
  <data key="d10">device interaction,setup process</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6b0e66412b5262a7c0a32588b9f6335a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704283</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Menu Button">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The menu button on the pump is pressed to access the main menu from the home screen.</data>
  <data key="d10">system navigation,user input</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704364</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Status Screens">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump displays status screens that provide detailed information about insulin, battery, and system functions.</data>
  <data key="d10">device monitoring,information display</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0aabf7352e5784edc898ebb03d127f44</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704365</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Configuration Assistant">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump powers on and starts the Configuration Assistant to guide the user through initial settings.</data>
  <data key="d10">device setup,initialization</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704415</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Start Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After configuration, the user arrives at the Start Screen, which serves as the main interface of the pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">main display,user interface</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704422</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Pump Housing">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump's internal components must be aligned horizontally with the pump housing as per the setup instructions.</data>
  <data key="d10">component alignment,device structure</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-08ad1da3ea94a4990f8ed72edc46798f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778704425</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="AA Battery">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump relies on an AA battery for operation and may require a new battery if power is low.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump requires an AA battery to operate and will shut down if a new battery is not inserted after removal.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump operates on an AA battery, which when low, triggers a low battery alert and requires replacement.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump operates on the AA battery when the internal power source fails to charge.</data>
  <data key="d10">battery replacement,dependency,energy depletion,operational dependency,power requirement,power source,power supply</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-636516fe857b1b2139aff0d472d8f1ec</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707484</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Power Error Alarm">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Power Error Alarm is triggered when the pump's internal power source cannot charge, prompting the user to record settings and contact support.</data>
  <data key="d10">alarm trigger,system response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707485</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Power Loss Alarm">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Power Loss Alarm activates when the AA battery is removed for over 10 minutes, requiring the user to reset time and date.</data>
  <data key="d10">alarm trigger,system reset</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707486</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Pump Error Alarm">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Pump Error Alarm indicates a critical malfunction that stops delivery and requires the pump to be restarted.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pump Error Alarm signals a general operational failure requiring user attention.</data>
  <data key="d10">device malfunction,malfunction detection,restart requirement,system integrity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707486</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="User Guide">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The User Guide provides detailed instructions for resolving various pump alarms and errors.&lt;SEP&gt;The User Guide is referenced for instructions on resolving alarms and restarting the pump after an error.&lt;SEP&gt;The User Guide provides detailed instructions for using the pump, resolving alarms, and setting up components.</data>
  <data key="d10">instruction reference,instructional resource,operational guidance,troubleshooting</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707488</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="24 Hour Technical Support">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Users are instructed to contact 24 Hour Technical Support if pump alarms occur frequently or cannot be resolved.</data>
  <data key="d10">error reporting,technical assistance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707490</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Alarm History">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Alarm History stores error codes that can be retrieved to assist technical support in diagnosing recurring issues.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump stores alarm records in the Alarm History for user review and troubleshooting.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump maintains an alarm history to log and display past alerts and warnings.</data>
  <data key="d10">diagnostic reference,error logging,error tracking,event logging,system logging</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707491</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Time And Date Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After a power loss, the user must enter the current time and date on the Time And Date Screen to restart the pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">system reset,user input</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707493</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Restore Settings">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Restore Settings function allows users to reload previously saved configurations after a pump error or restart.</data>
  <data key="d10">error recovery,settings recovery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-941b9969735807fbf7d05695bb5723ee</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707494</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Tubing">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The tubing is part of the infusion set and must be inspected for damage.&lt;SEP&gt;The tubing connects to the reservoir and pump to deliver insulin, and must not be crimped or bent.</data>
  <data key="d10">component,fluid pathway,inspection,system integrity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707506</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Low Battery Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump displays a low battery alert when battery life is 10 hours or fewer, prompting replacement.</data>
  <data key="d10">power management,status warning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707511</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Loading Incomplete Alarm">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The loading incomplete alarm occurs if @&amp; is pressed during reservoir loading, requiring restart of the procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;The Loading Incomplete Alarm indicates that the insulin reservoir was not filled completely.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery readiness,procedure interruption,reservoir filling,user action</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707513</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Manage Settings Error">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The manage settings error stops delivery and clears backup settings, though current settings remain active.</data>
  <data key="d10">settings loss,system error</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707518</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Max Fill Reached Alarm">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The max fill reached alarm triggers when insulin used to fill tubing exceeds expected units, prompting user to check for drops.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump triggers a max fill reached alarm when the reservoir or system reaches its maximum fill capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Max Fill Reached Alarm notifies the user that the insulin reservoir is full.</data>
  <data key="d10">air detection,capacity limit,fill limit exceeded,filling limit,reservoir capacity,system feedback</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707523</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="No Reservoir Detected Alarm">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The no reservoir detected alarm indicates the reservoir is missing or not properly locked, requiring reinsertion.</data>
  <data key="d10">installation verification,system check</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707524</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Power Error Detected">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The power error detected alarm indicates the pump’s internal power source cannot charge, requiring settings to be recorded via CareLink or manually.&lt;SEP&gt;Power Error Detected indicates a problem with the pump's power system or battery connection.</data>
  <data key="d10">data backup,electrical fault,internal failure,system integrity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b7b25811fc82ec9cac7c1bcd18dac0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707525</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Menu Screen">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Menu Screen allows users to navigate pump settings and features.&lt;SEP&gt;The Menu Screen is part of the pump's interface, allowing access to various system features and settings.&lt;SEP&gt;The user navigates to the menu screen on the pump to select functions such as starting a new reservoir setup.</data>
  <data key="d10">navigation,system navigation,system operation,user interface</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd001e1c01f7ba101b7beb19f131c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707542</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Checkmark">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The checkmark appears on the pump screen to indicate that a step, such as loading, has been completed.</data>
  <data key="d10">process confirmation,status indication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-edefb6aab17535eddb38eddb8b8fc7df</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707543</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Battery Cap">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The battery cap secures the battery in the pump and must be properly tightened.&lt;SEP&gt;The battery cap must be removed and replaced to check or replace the AA battery in the pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">access,battery security,component,device integrity</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707566</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Startup Wizard">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Startup Wizard appears the first time a battery is inserted to guide initial pump setup.&lt;SEP&gt;The Startup Wizard is used to re-enter personalized pump settings after a reset.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump uses the startup wizard during initial setup to guide users through configuration of basic settings.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration,initial setup,setup</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7908c9940fceb874990f2aa93b53b668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707568</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Stuck Button Alarm">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump detects a prolonged button press and triggers the Stuck Button Alarm, requiring the user to select OK to clear it.&lt;SEP&gt;The Stuck Button Alarm is triggered when a button on the pump is pressed continuously.</data>
  <data key="d10">device alarm,hardware fault,user interaction,user interface</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707580</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Very High Basal Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump issues a Very High Basal Alert when the active basal rate exceeds typical insulin needs, advising consultation with a healthcare professional.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin dosage,safety warning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707584</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Manual Mode Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump monitors the Manual Mode Basal Pattern and generates alerts if the pattern delivers excessive insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert trigger,insulin delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707586</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Insulin Delivery Suspended">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump suspends insulin delivery in response to a low glucose event detected by the CGM Device.</data>
  <data key="d10">alarm condition,safety response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707588</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Basal Delivery Resumed">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump resumes basal insulin delivery after a suspension event, indicated by the Basal Delivery Resumed message.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal Delivery Resumed indicates that the pump has restarted basal insulin delivery after a pause.</data>
  <data key="d10">continuous delivery,delivery resumption,post-suspension,resumption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707591</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="24-Hour Technical Support">
  <data key="d8">6.0</data>
  <data key="d9">If the pump is exposed to magnetic fields or damaged, users should contact 24-Hour Technical Support.&lt;SEP&gt;If the pump fails the self test or displays an error, users are instructed to contact 24-Hour Technical Support.&lt;SEP&gt;If pump issues persist after troubleshooting, users should contact 24-Hour Technical Support.&lt;SEP&gt;Users are directed to contact 24-Hour Technical Support if pump-sensor communication issues persist after troubleshooting.&lt;SEP&gt;24-Hour Technical Support assists users with resolving technical issues related to the pump and CGM system.&lt;SEP&gt;Users are advised to contact 24-Hour Technical Support if they cannot resolve persistent pump alarms.</data>
  <data key="d10">error resolution,issue resolution,malfunction reporting,support,technical assistance,troubleshooting</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-337edc64848e071f93a58a45c1196f2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb8f4a2fd599a5ec7cbad8c356a6ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b570c57fffa2f2a8caae92eb75f2bfd</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707598</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Lost Sensor Signal Alert">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Lost Sensor Signal Alert appears after 30 minutes without a sensor signal and prompts troubleshooting.&lt;SEP&gt;The lost sensor signal alert appears on the pump screen, prompting the user to follow troubleshooting steps.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sensor Signal Alert is triggered when the pump loses communication with the glucose sensor.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert display,connectivity,data loss,notification,troubleshooting trigger</data>
