  <data key="d9">Users access Device Settings from the Home Screen to manage pump functions including self test and settings management.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration access,user interface</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6cf249079ffd8aa0f06700895b8b7e9f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708153</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Alert">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump generates alerts that beep every 5 or 15 minutes and may escalate to a loud emergency siren after 10 minutes until resolved.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump issues alerts to inform the user of non-critical conditions like low battery or empty reservoir.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert management,notification system,status notification,user warning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708186</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Message">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump displays messages with blue or yellow icons and emits tones or vibrations to inform the user of status or required decisions.</data>
  <data key="d10">notification system,user interaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708187</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Audio Notification">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump emits tones as part of its audio notification system for messages, depending on user settings.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert signaling,auditory feedback</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708187</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="One-Pulse-Only Vibration">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump uses a one-pulse-only vibration to notify the user of a message, based on sound and vibration settings.</data>
  <data key="d10">notification,tactile feedback</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708188</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Magnetic Fields">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Strong magnetic fields can cause the pump to malfunction, leading to serious injury.</data>
  <data key="d10">device interference,malfunction risk</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708193</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="MRI Equipment">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump must be removed before MRI use as magnetic fields can damage it and cause malfunction.</data>
  <data key="d10">device damage,hazard exposure</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708196</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="CGM Device">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Both the pump and CGM device must be removed before exposure to magnetic fields or radiation.&lt;SEP&gt;The pump communicates with the CGM Device via a wireless connection after successful pairing.</data>
  <data key="d10">device communication,joint removal,pairing requirement,system integration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708199</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Strong Magnetic Field">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Exposure to a strong magnetic field can cause the pump to malfunction, leading to hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">health risk,malfunction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708200</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Magnet">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Magnets can interfere with the pump's motor, causing damage and serious injury.</data>
  <data key="d10">device malfunction,motor interference</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708204</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Motor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The motor inside the pump regulates insulin delivery; damage can cause malfunction.</data>
  <data key="d10">component function,insulin regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708205</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="X-Ray Scanning Machine">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">X-ray scanning machines can damage the pump, leading to insulin over-delivery and hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin over-delivery,radiation damage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708207</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Full-Body Scanner">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">All system components must be removed before full-body scanner screening; alternative methods are available.</data>
  <data key="d10">device removal,security screening</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708208</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Alternative Screening Method">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Users can request an alternative screening method to avoid removing the pump during security checks.</data>
  <data key="d10">device safety,security accommodation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708214</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Waterproof Capability">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump is waterproof up to 8 feet for 30 minutes when undamaged and properly assembled.</data>
  <data key="d10">depth and duration,water resistance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708216</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Water Damage">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">If water enters the pump, it may malfunction; users should check BG and contact technical support.</data>
  <data key="d10">malfunction risk,technical support</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708219</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Sensor Warm Up">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump displays the "Sensor warm up XX min" message during the Sensor Warm Up phase before receiving SG readings.&lt;SEP&gt;After starting a new sensor, the pump initiates a two-hour warm-up period before receiving glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d10">initialization,initialization process,system status,time-based process</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708219</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Start New Sensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump prompts the user to select Start New Sensor when a new sensor is detected, initiating the warm-up and activation process.</data>
  <data key="d10">device initialization,setup process</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708220</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Reconnect Sensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump allows the user to select Reconnect Sensor when a previously used sensor is reconnected, resuming monitoring without starting a new session.</data>
  <data key="d10">connection recovery,device resumption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708221</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Alerts">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump issues alerts for non-critical conditions like low battery, prompting user action.</data>
  <data key="d10">status monitoring,user notification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708260</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Notification Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The notification screen is part of the pump's interface where all active notifications are displayed and managed.</data>
  <data key="d10">display interface,message presentation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708263</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Alarms">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump generates alarms to signal critical conditions such as blocked insulin flow or low glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">error signaling,safety mechanism</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-54631c5494eb3fe006ea9eb279a14651</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708264</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Insulin Flow Blocked">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump generates an Insulin Flow Blocked alert when there is a physical obstruction preventing insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery interruption,device malfunction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708280</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Critical Pump Error">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Critical Pump Error is a severe alert indicating a major malfunction within the pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">emergency alert,system failure</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708281</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Pump Error">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pump Error is a general alert indicating a problem with the pump's operation.</data>
  <data key="d10">device issue,operational disruption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708282</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Pump Restarted">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pump Restarted indicates the pump has rebooted after a shutdown or error condition.</data>
  <data key="d10">reboot,system recovery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708283</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Low Reservoir">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Low Reservoir is an alert from the pump indicating that the insulin supply is running low.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin level,supply warning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708284</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="No Reservoir Detected">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">No Reservoir Detected is an alert indicating the pump cannot sense the presence of an insulin reservoir.</data>
  <data key="d10">hardware detection,setup issue</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708286</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Max Fill Reached">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Max Fill Reached indicates the pump's reservoir has reached its maximum fill capacity.</data>
  <data key="d10">capacity limit,reservoir full</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708287</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Delivery Limit Exceeded">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Delivery Limit Exceeded occurs when the pump's programmed insulin delivery exceeds the allowed maximum.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage restriction,safety limit</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708288</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Bolus Stopped">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Bolus Stopped is an alert indicating that a bolus insulin dose was interrupted during delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose delivery,interruption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708289</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Bolus Not Delivered">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Bolus Not Delivered indicates that a requested bolus dose was not administered by the pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage error,failed administration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708290</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Power Loss">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Power Loss indicates the pump has lost electrical power, potentially leading to operational stoppage.</data>
  <data key="d10">energy failure,system shutdown</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708291</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Battery Failed">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Battery Failed is a critical alert indicating the pump's battery is no longer functional.</data>
  <data key="d10">battery failure,device shutdown</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708293</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Battery Not Compatible">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Battery Not Compatible indicates the installed battery does not meet the pump's specifications.</data>
  <data key="d10">hardware incompatibility,installation error</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708294</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Replace Battery Now">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Replace Battery Now is a critical alert requiring immediate battery replacement for continued pump operation.</data>
  <data key="d10">power replacement,urgent maintenance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708296</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Low Battery Pump">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Low Battery Pump indicates the pump's battery is low and nearing depletion.</data>
  <data key="d10">battery warning,power level</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708297</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Stuck Button">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The pump detects a stuck button condition when a button is pressed for more than three minutes, triggering an alarm.&lt;SEP&gt;Stuck Button is an alert indicating a physical button on the pump is not functioning correctly.</data>
  <data key="d10">hardware defect,input detection,system fault,user interface</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c3f268f97351e2e386387fc46cbd05a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708298</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Rewind Required">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Rewind Required indicates the pump needs to rewind the reservoir, typically before refilling.</data>
  <data key="d10">maintenance,reservoir reset</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708299</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump" target="Fill Cannula">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Fill Cannula is a prompt to fill the cannula with insulin during initial setup or after replacement.</data>
  <data key="d10">priming,setup</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
