<edge source="Low SG Alarm" target="SmartGuard Feature">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature updates the low SG alarm threshold to a lower limit (e.g., 55 mg/dL) when a new sensor type is paired.</data>
  <data key="d10">alarm configuration,threshold adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707479</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Low SG Alarm" target="Low SG Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Low SG Alarm and Low SG Alert represent different levels of notification for low sensor glucose, with the alarm indicating a more critical threshold.</data>
  <data key="d10">severity level,threshold differentiation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707484</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Low SG Alarm" target="iCGM 25">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Low SG Alarm is generated by the iCGM 25 system when sensor glucose levels fall below a set threshold.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose monitoring,hypoglycemia alert</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707928</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Suspend on Low" target="SmartGuard Feature">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Suspend on Low feature is not available when the SmartGuard feature is active, limiting automatic suspension during low glucose events.</data>
  <data key="d10">feature incompatibility,system limitation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707478</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Warm Up" target="CGM Device">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The warm-up process must begin after pairing a new sensor; failure to detect interstitial fluid triggers an alert to check or replace the sensor.</data>
  <data key="d10">initialization,sensor activation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707479</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="CGM Device">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The CGM device uses the Instinct sensor to obtain glucose readings and generate alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Instinct is a specific model of CGM device that supports glucose monitoring and integration with insulin pump systems.</data>
  <data key="d10">data source,device model,product type,sensor integration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707482</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="Failed BG Check Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Instinct device displays the Failed BG Check Alert when blood glucose meter readings cannot be used to verify system performance.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert display,system feedback</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707519</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="Enter BG Now Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Instinct device shows the Enter BG Now Alert to prompt the user to enter a blood glucose value for sensor calibration.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert display,calibration prompt</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707520</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="Change Sensor Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Instinct device generates the Change Sensor Alert when a sensor change is required due to failed checks or persistent issues.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert display,system maintenance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707521</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="Sensor Glucose Not Available Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Instinct device displays the Sensor Glucose Not Available Alert when glucose readings are temporarily inaccessible.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert display,data interruption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707522</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="High SG Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Instinct device triggers the High SG Alert to notify the user of abnormally high sensor glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert display,medical notification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8394829309b48ea8c957132c29c4ea39</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707524</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="Sensor Too Hot">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Instinct system triggers the "Sensor Too Hot" alert when the device exceeds safe operating temperatures, advising the user to move it to a cooler environment.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">operational safety,temperature alert</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707532</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="Sensor Too Cold">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Instinct system triggers the "Sensor Too Cold" alert when the device falls below minimum operating temperatures, advising the user to move it to a warmer environment.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">operational safety,temperature alert</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-fb01d55e6a22a76ca93e60f11c9b4cf6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707533</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="Starting Instinct">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Starting Instinct is the process of activating the Instinct sensor for glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d10">device activation,sensor setup</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707888</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="Removing Instinct">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Removing Instinct refers to the physical removal of the Instinct sensor, often for replacement or troubleshooting.</data>
  <data key="d10">device removal,maintenance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707892</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Instinct" target="Unpairing Instinct">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Unpairing Instinct severs the wireless connection between the Instinct sensor and the pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">device management,wireless disconnection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f2667d6936a8a9a26e886ba90b060796</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707893</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Low SG Alert" target="MiniMed 780G">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Low SG Alert on the MiniMed 780G system includes a warning that users should not rely solely on sensor glucose readings and must confirm with a blood glucose meter.</data>
  <data key="d10">device warning,user guidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4dae9b37ffd9805fb682b2152950552</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707540</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Low SG Alert" target="MiniMed 780G System">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The MiniMed 780G system includes a Low SG alert to warn users of impending or current low glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert system,safety mechanism</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1a9dd84e2a3b75afe80757b7b6e602a6</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707995</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Enter BG Now">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature generates the Enter BG Now alert after operating at maximum insulin delivery for 7 hours, requiring user input to continue automated function.</data>
  <data key="d10">system requirement,user action</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-92b103916c0aae66fd1ad9496d81e3dc</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707486</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Pump Software Update">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After a pump software update, the SmartGuard feature requires a 5-hour warm-up period before it becomes active.</data>
  <data key="d10">dependency,feature activation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e26750d1b6c495640b752a31b9f0e262</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707524</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Adjustment Bolus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature calculates and adjusts the bolus dose based on glucose trends and carb intake.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d10">bolus calculation,dose adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707534</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Temp Target">
  <data key="d8">6.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A temp target is set during SmartGuard operation when acetaminophen or paracetamol is taken.&lt;SEP&gt;When acetaminophen or paracetamol is taken, a temp target should be programmed in the SmartGuard Feature for up to eight hours.&lt;SEP&gt;When a Temp Target is set, the SmartGuard feature suspends auto correction boluses to accommodate conditions like exercise.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard feature uses temp targets to temporarily adjust insulin delivery based on user-defined glucose goals.&lt;SEP&gt;The temp target influences the SmartGuard feature's calculations by changing the glucose target to 150 mg/dL.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The Temp Target is a user-defined glucose goal that temporarily modifies the SmartGuard feature's behavior for a specified duration.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose goal setting,goal setting,insulin adjustment,medication adjustment,mode override,safety protocol,system adjustment,target setting,temporary adjustment,temporary setting,therapy adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9cb3ef3e959b16d99ac4debc0210965b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bcf8f1ff0075b1e2f1edaa4bc946a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a59cce7c2f6a229062408b8278675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5904918561a819f1c95321943d91162</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707538</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
