  <data key="d13">1778708039</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Auto Correction">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature triggers Auto Correction to deliver automatic boluses when glucose levels deviate from the target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Correction must be turned on within the SmartGuard settings to enable automatic delivery of correction boluses.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard feature automatically delivers insulin corrections based on sensor glucose trends.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto correction only occurs when using the SmartGuard feature.</data>
  <data key="d10">automated adjustment,automated bolus,automated response,correction mechanism,feature activation,feature dependency,glucose regulation,insulin regulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708040</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="BG Entry">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A BG entry is required to resume the SmartGuard feature after an exit or when certain alerts such as SmartGuard Min Delivery, Max Delivery, or Enter BG Now are triggered.</data>
  <data key="d10">resumption requirement,user action</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708063</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="SmartGuard Checklist">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard Checklist screen shows the conditions that must be met to activate or remain in the SmartGuard feature.&lt;SEP&gt;The SmartGuard Checklist outlines the conditions and required steps that must be met to resume or maintain the SmartGuard feature after an interruption.</data>
  <data key="d10">activation monitoring,condition verification,operational guidance,requirement tracking</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708065</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Block Mode">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature remains active in Block Mode, allowing Auto Basal delivery and Auto correction boluses even when the pump is locked.</data>
  <data key="d10">access control,feature compatibility</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708066</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Alert Silence Feature">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Alert Silence Feature can suppress certain sensor alerts while the SmartGuard feature is active, improving usability without disabling core functionality.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert management,user experience</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708067</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="48-Hour Warm-Up">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature requires the 48-hour warm-up to be complete before it can resume operation with a new sensor.</data>
  <data key="d10">sensor initialization,system requirement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708070</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="5-Hour Warm-Up Period">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature cannot restart if it is within a 5-hour warm-up period, preventing premature reactivation.</data>
  <data key="d10">operational delay,system restriction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-53048131930fe8817679e51d5bec009b</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708071</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Very High Basal Alert">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Very High Basal Alert is activated when the SmartGuard feature detects an unsafe basal insulin delivery pattern.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert trigger,safety mechanism</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7d37ccd138ed8a095eb197006a33b8a7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708073</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="History Summary Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The History Summary screen includes data on insulin delivered via the SmartGuard feature.</data>
  <data key="d10">automated delivery,glucose control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708131</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="SmartGuard Bolus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard bolus feature allows for bolus insulin delivery within the automated SmartGuard mode.</data>
  <data key="d10">automated bolus,insulin delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708133</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Blood Glucose Reading">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">When acetaminophen or paracetamol is present, blood glucose readings should be used instead of sensor readings with the SmartGuard feature for accurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d10">accuracy,alternative input</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708150</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Temporary Target">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">A temporary target must be programmed in the SmartGuard feature after taking acetaminophen or paracetamol to ensure safer insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage adjustment,safety protocol</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708151</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="SmartGuard Target">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard Target setting (100, 110, or 120 mg/dL) is used by the SmartGuard feature to determine the ideal glucose level for insulin adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;The user selects a SmartGuard target glucose level that the system attempts to maintain through automated insulin adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose management,glucose optimization,target setting</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708157</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Glucose Range">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The primary objective of the SmartGuard feature is to maximize the time that glucose levels remain within the 70–180 mg/dL range.</data>
  <data key="d10">glycemic control,treatment goal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708158</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Bolus Feature">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Bolus Feature must be used alongside the SmartGuard feature to deliver insulin for meals, as automated meal boluses are not provided.</data>
  <data key="d10">manual intervention,meal insulin</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708160</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Sensor Measurement">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature relies on accurate sensor glucose measurements to calculate and deliver appropriate insulin doses.</data>
  <data key="d10">data dependency,real-time monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708161</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Carb Information">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Carb information is required by the SmartGuard feature to determine the correct bolus amount for meals.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin dosing,meal calculation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708162</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Warm-Up Period">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature requires a 48-hour warm-up period before activation, during which the system processes data without sensor input.&lt;SEP&gt;A warm-up period of 48 hours or 5 hours is required before the SmartGuard feature can activate after a pump reset or prolonged shutdown.</data>
  <data key="d10">activation requirement,system initialization,system readiness</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-550045a3f1fc05491e77159dba8b4fd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708163</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Pump Reset">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After a pump reset, the SmartGuard feature is unavailable for 5 hours to allow for active insulin update and system stabilization.&lt;SEP&gt;After a pump reset, the SmartGuard feature may be unavailable for 5 hours to update active insulin.</data>
  <data key="d10">active insulin update,feature unavailability,system recovery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708170</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Palm">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The palm has not been studied for use with the SmartGuard feature, so its performance is unknown.</data>
  <data key="d10">unapproved use,unknown performance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708193</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Blood Sample">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Blood glucose values from fingertip samples are used for SmartGuard calibration; palm samples are not studied.</data>
  <data key="d10">performance verification,system calibration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a4f0986d34b7b73e98fe14c73abfb6f3</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708194</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature is a core function of the MiniMed 780G insulin pump that calculates basal insulin and correction boluses based on sensor readings.&lt;SEP&gt;The MiniMed 780G insulin pump integrates the SmartGuard feature for adaptive insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">automated delivery,feature activation,glucose monitoring,insulin calculation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf9d231ade525ec71253e4464a9682e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708268</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Auto Suspend">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Auto Suspend feature continues to function even when the SmartGuard feature is active, ensuring safety.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery suspension,safety integration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708270</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Carb Ratio">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The carb ratio must be set before the SmartGuard feature can be activated or used effectively.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration requirement,system setup</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708356</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="BG Reading">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Entering a current BG reading is necessary for the SmartGuard feature to begin or continue functioning.</data>
  <data key="d10">input requirement,system operation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8556667d5fd37aa22e0f1652c667c62c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708362</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Feature" target="Total Daily Dose">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard feature tracks the total daily dose of insulin, which must be cleared under certain conditions to ensure accurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d10">data tracking,dosage monitoring</data>
