  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Suspend Before Low" target="Low SG Settings">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Suspend Before Low feature is part of the Low SG Settings and suspends insulin delivery when glucose is predicted to drop near the low limit.</data>
  <data key="d10">feature dependency,insulin control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707668</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Suspend Before Low" target="Suspend On Low">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Suspend Before Low and Suspend On Low are related features of the MiniMed 780G system designed to prevent hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend Before Low and Suspend On Low cannot be active at the same time due to system design limitations.</data>
  <data key="d10">mutual exclusion,pump feature,safety setting,system constraint</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ab4ddf6540d88f22cdfe4b96db42b88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
