  <data key="d9">Both the Daily History and Alarm History screens provide retrospective views of pump activity and alerts.</data>
  <data key="d10">event logging,system review</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707638</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Daily History Screen" target="Bolus Delivery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Daily History Screen records bolus delivery data, allowing users to check the actual amount delivered versus the intended bolus.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery tracking,dose comparison</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707760</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Daily History Screen" target="Insulin Delivery History Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Insulin Delivery History Screen and Daily History Screen are linked interfaces for viewing insulin delivery data.</data>
  <data key="d10">data access,information navigation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-30fd82ff17ab8577d82477ed97f94075</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708103</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Daily History Screen" target="Insulin Delivery History">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Daily History Screen provides access to insulin delivery history, including bolus delivery details.</data>
  <data key="d10">data display,historical access</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-73d350656ba1a2a747792507170f7346</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708146</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Daily History Screen" target="Bg">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">BG data such as meter readings are recorded and can be reviewed through actions logged on the Daily History Screen.</data>
  <data key="d10">data display,glucose monitoring</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708180</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Daily History Screen" target="SmartGuard Active">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard Active event is recorded on the Daily History Screen when the feature is activated.</data>
  <data key="d10">event logging,system status</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708182</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Daily History Screen" target="SmartGuard Exit">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SmartGuard Exit event is logged on the Daily History Screen when the feature is deactivated.</data>
  <data key="d10">event logging,system status</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ea171e9afedb933e838f1349ebb0fe50</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708183</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Missed Meal Bolus Reminder" target="Reminder">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The missed meal bolus reminder is a specific type of reminder to prompt insulin delivery at meal times.</data>
  <data key="d10">bolus management,notification type</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e90de561bcfc1f3544a690722c75e6f2</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708343</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Low Reservoir Reminder" target="Units">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Units setting allows users to specify the insulin level threshold (between 5 and 50 units) at which the Low Reservoir Reminder is triggered.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration,threshold setting</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-95d8f5f8ae713f2ed252ad1087051b50</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708029</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Block Mode" target="Insulin Flow Blocked Alarm">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin flow blocked alarm triggers block mode to stop delivery when an obstruction is detected.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery interruption,error response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e2ad78a5db5d547aed7e2552fb1ec900</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708076</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Language" target="User Interface">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Language setting determines the language used in the pump's user interface for better usability.</data>
  <data key="d10">accessibility,system settings</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707647</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Language" target="Manage Settings">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Language setting is modified through the Manage Settings menu to change the pump's display language.</data>
  <data key="d10">display setting,user interface</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-39a29f6130bd8284c7277df75ae0e90d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708270</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Temp Basal Rates" target="Additional Basal Patterns">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Preset Temp Basal Rates and Additional Basal Patterns are features that allow flexible basal insulin programming.</data>
  <data key="d10">basal customization,insulin scheduling</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1ef4fd0fa0c26a81460d7687cc37cf95</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707642</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="BG Target" target="Bolus Wizard Feature">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Bolus Wizard feature uses the BG Target to determine how much insulin is needed to correct blood glucose to the desired range.</data>
  <data key="d10">dose calculation,glucose correction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707788</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Calibration Not Accepted Alert" target="SG Graph">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SG graph displays the "Sensor signal not found - See User Guide" alert, which is associated with calibration failure when the sensor signal is lost.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert display,error indication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-03820ea21d982bc029e8a55fe1be600a</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707653</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Suspend By Sensor Icon" target="Suspend On Low Event">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The suspend by sensor icon flashes during a Suspend on low event and shows a red X when the feature is unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d10">feature availability,status indication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708034</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Suspend By Sensor Icon" target="Suspend Before Low Event">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The suspend by sensor icon flashes during a Suspend before low event and shows a red X when the feature is unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d10">feature availability,status indication</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708036</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Searching Screen" target="Select Device Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After the Searching Screen completes, the system transitions to the Select Device Screen with available CGM devices.</data>
  <data key="d10">device discovery,transition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707657</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Searching Screen" target="EA Note">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">EA Note indicates that the search process for device pairing can take up to 20 seconds.</data>
  <data key="d10">system behavior,timing information</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707661</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Serial Number" target="Paired Devices Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The serial number is used on the Paired Devices Screen to select the correct CGM device for pairing or unpairing.</data>
  <data key="d10">device matching,identification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707921</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Unpair" target="Unpair Device Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Selecting Unpair brings up the Unpair Device Screen to confirm the removal of the CGM device from the Pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">confirmation process,disconnection</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707659</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="No Paired CGM Banner" target="Unpair Device">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After unpairing, the No Paired CGM Banner appears on the pump's Home screen to indicate no active sensor connection.</data>
  <data key="d10">system status,visual feedback</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6f114a018f4d8b34373a039564245abf</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708515</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Carb Ratio" target="Bolus Wizard Feature">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Bolus Wizard uses the carb ratio setting to determine insulin dosage based on carbohydrate intake.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Wizard feature uses carb ratio to calculate the estimated bolus amount.</data>
  <data key="d10">dietary input,dose calculation,insulin calculation,insulin planning</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f608f07eae4ddd5409aed9d4ecef75ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8080e2e312ed6994d0dc059a4aeca5f7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707903</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Start New Sensor" target="Sensor Warm Up Message">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Selecting Start New Sensor triggers the display of the Sensor Warm Up Message on the Pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">function trigger,system response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707659</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor Warm Up Message" target="Reconnect Sensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Selecting Reconnect Sensor causes the Sensor Warm Up Message to appear, restarting the two-hour warm-up period.</data>
  <data key="d10">initialization,reconnection process</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707661</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor Warm Up Message" target="EA Note">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">EA Note specifies that it may take up to five minutes for the Sensor Warm Up Message to appear after initiating the sensor.</data>
  <data key="d10">initialization,timing information</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-d1dfc786d81b6125f9012b67e900b5c4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707665</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="EA Note" target="Stopping a Square Wave or Dual Wave Bolus Delivery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The EA Note directs users to page 276 for details on how to stop an ongoing Square Wave or Dual Wave bolus delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">procedural guidance,reference</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707687</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="EA Note" target="Settings">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">EA Note directs users to the Settings section for instructions on configuring parameters over a 24-hour period.</data>
  <data key="d10">instruction reference,user guidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707797</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="EA Note" target="Preset Bolus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">EA Note states that existing Preset Bolus settings remain available even if the Dual Wave or Square Wave bolus features are turned off.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration rule,feature dependency</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708062</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="EA Note" target="Options">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">EA Note indicates that a preset bolus cannot be edited, renamed, or deleted during its delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">editing constraint,usage restriction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708064</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Max Bolus" target="Delivery Settings">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Max bolus is a delivery setting that restricts the maximum bolus insulin dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Max Bolus is configured within the Delivery Settings menu under the Max Basal/Bolus option on the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d10">bolus control,insulin limit,safety limit,setting configuration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-559587c4971d344102a5ceb58d84260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b678b0be6db859b75d0af252e808c1</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707669</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="High Snooze" target="Snooze Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">High Snooze is configured through the Snooze Screen to control how often a high glucose alert repeats.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert repetition,feature configuration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708234</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="High Snooze" target="Snooze High &amp; Low">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">High Snooze is accessed and configured through the Snooze High &amp; Low menu option.</data>
  <data key="d10">feature access,setting configuration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708236</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Easy Bolus Feature" target="A Button">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The A button is used to activate and control the Easy Bolus feature by pressing it to increment the bolus amount.</data>
  <data key="d10">control mechanism,user interaction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707677</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Easy Bolus Feature" target="Step Size">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Step Size determines the insulin increment per button press when using the Easy Bolus feature and is configurable between 0.1 and 2.0 units.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration,dosage control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707682</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Bolus" target="Bolus 1">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Bolus 1 is one of the four numbered preset bolus options that can be customized for recurring insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus 1 is a specific instance of a Preset Bolus that can be configured and delivered.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration,named bolus,preset configuration,preset instance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707682</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Bolus" target="Bolus 4">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Bolus 4 is one of the four numbered preset bolus options available for user-defined insulin delivery scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus 4 is a specific instance of a Preset Bolus that can be configured and delivered.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration,named bolus,preset configuration,preset instance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-04894d0f5474b256de7a1a0bab9d3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707684</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Bolus" target="Bolus 2">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Bolus 2 is a specific instance of a Preset Bolus that can be configured and delivered.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration,preset instance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-242a9653f8dc2ed51da6a6ddd865d93f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708054</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Bolus" target="Bolus 3">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Bolus 3 is a specific instance of a Preset Bolus that can be configured and delivered.</data>
