  <data key="d13">1778708031</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Suspend On Low Event" target="40 Mg/Dl Above Low Limit">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin delivery resumes after a Suspend on low event only if sensor glucose is predicted to be more than 40 mg/dL above the low limit within 30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d10">predictive resumption,recovery expectation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708032</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Suspend On Low Event" target="30 Minutes">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Insulin delivery remains suspended for a minimum of 30 minutes during a Suspend on low event.</data>
  <data key="d10">minimum suspension,time duration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708036</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Suspend On Low Event" target="Emergency Message">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">If the Suspend on low alarm is not cleared within two hours, the pump displays an emergency message upon resuming insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">alarm escalation,system response</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708037</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Suspend On Low Event" target="Manually Resuming Basal Insulin Delivery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Basal insulin delivery can be manually resumed at any time during a Suspend on low event.</data>
  <data key="d10">manual override,user control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2ef0e6e09cd17187cd967e6d49a3e718</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708040</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Skin Care Products" target="MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump System">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Skin care products such as lotions and insect repellents can damage the plastic casing of the insulin pump if not wiped off promptly.</data>
  <data key="d10">contamination risk,material damage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708171</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor Glucose Reading" target="Insulin Over-Delivery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Falsely elevated sensor glucose readings can lead to incorrect calculation of insulin doses, resulting in over-delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">dosage error,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a99dc37db5c39ba2f813bb638414b56f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708149</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Temp Basal Rate" target="Percentage">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Temp Basal Rate can be set using a Percentage of the current basal pattern, allowing flexible insulin delivery between 0% and 200%.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin adjustment,rate calculation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707752</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Temp Basal Rate" target="Fixed Rate">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Temp Basal Rate can also be set as a Fixed Rate in units per hour, constrained by the Max Basal Rate.</data>
  <data key="d10">insulin delivery,rate specification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-ac744442f0181da5c75ae32e2e6036cf</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707753</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Temp Basal Rate" target="Preset Temp Basal Rate">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Preset temp basal rates are predefined versions of temp basal rates that can be selected for temporary insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d10">preset configuration,temporary delivery</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708108</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Temp Basal Rate" target="Scheduled Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After a temp basal rate is canceled, the system resumes the scheduled basal pattern.</data>
  <data key="d10">cancellation,delivery resumption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708110</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SmartGuard Checklist" target="SmartGuard Exit">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After a SmartGuard exit, the user is prompted to review the SmartGuard Checklist for proper system re-engagement.</data>
  <data key="d10">procedural review,user guidance</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c4edd508820d00eb32799ddeb35366f2</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708532</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pairing" target="MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump System">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Pairing the pump with a CGM or mobile device is a critical security-sensitive process that must be done in a private environment.</data>
  <data key="d10">device connection,security window</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4a597a39961d2cb246ad385f39cfb886</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708184</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="24-Hour Period" target="Settings">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Settings covering a 24-hour period allow users to configure multiple insulin sensitivity and BG target ranges throughout the day.</data>
  <data key="d10">parameter adjustment,time-based configuration</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707794</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Settings" target="Ed Note">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Ed Note refers users to the Settings covering a 24-hour period for guidance on setting up multiple sensitivity factors or blood glucose target ranges.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration setup,instruction reference</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707799</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensitivity 2/4 Screen" target="Edit Sensitivity 2/4 Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After viewing the Sensitivity 2/4 Screen, the user proceeds to the Edit Sensitivity 2/4 Screen to input values.</data>
  <data key="d10">navigation,setup progression</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707792</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="BG Target 3/4 Screen" target="Edit BG Target 3/4 Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">After viewing the BG Target 3/4 Screen, the user proceeds to the Edit BG Target 3/4 Screen to enter target ranges.</data>
  <data key="d10">navigation,setup progression</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-02b21bc8135e144a626f42f84747459d</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707794</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ed Note" target="Save Function">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Ed Note warns that if the Save function is not selected, changes to the pump settings will not be retained.</data>
  <data key="d10">data loss prevention,user instruction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f608f07eae4ddd5409aed9d4ecef75ad</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707905</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Rewinding" target="Reservoir Compartment">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The rewinding process involves the piston returning to its start position within the reservoir compartment.</data>
  <data key="d10">component location,system initialization</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8a6d7d1adf71e2872a4ddf28d3170247</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707990</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Safety Alert" target="Cgm Device">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The CGM device displays a Safety Alert if the blood glucose reading used for calibration may be incorrect or uncertain.</data>
  <data key="d10">data validation,user confirmation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e33e0df4fbd9e2d7b9a22d11de9476c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708220</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor Alerts" target="Silencing Sensor Alerts">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sensor alerts can be temporarily silenced, as described in the Silencing sensor alerts section on page 176.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert management,temporary action</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-555df1669205bcfa737c81d6936e696e</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708266</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor Alerts" target="Sound And Vibration Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Sound And Vibration Screen allows users to configure and temporarily silence sensor alerts.</data>
  <data key="d10">alert management,notification control</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-52b837d1e7373efe5b2f10e88f8f3ae4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708531</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="High SG Settings" target="High Setup Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The High Setup Screen is used to review and modify High SG Settings, including time segments and alert options.</data>
  <data key="d10">interface navigation,setting adjustment</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-04fa4143c79ef368662ed10679dc02f0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708237</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SG Review" target="History Screens">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SG Review screen is part of the History screens and displays sensor glucose values when the Sensor feature is enabled.</data>
  <data key="d10">glucose monitoring,sensor data</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-8fa0f39c0795829009a6299c85cd603c</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Save Function" target="CAUTION">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The CAUTION alert emphasizes that failing to press Save after entering settings will result in the loss of those settings, even if the screen goes dark.</data>
  <data key="d10">risk warning,system behavior</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f608f07eae4ddd5409aed9d4ecef75ad</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707907</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Confirm Code Screen" target="Cancel Option">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Cancel Option on the Confirm Code Screen allows the user to exit the pairing process if the code is incorrect.</data>
  <data key="d10">process termination,user action</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707922</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Confirm Code Screen" target="Confirm Option">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Confirm Option on the Confirm Code Screen finalizes the code verification and continues the pairing process.</data>
  <data key="d10">process continuation,user action</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707925</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Paired Devices Screen" target="Unpair Option">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Unpair Option is selected from the Paired Devices Screen to initiate the removal of a paired CGM device.</data>
  <data key="d10">device removal,user action</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707923</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Paired Devices Screen" target="Pair New Device Option">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Pair New Device Option is accessed from the Paired Devices Screen to start pairing a new transmitter or sensor.</data>
  <data key="d10">pairing initiation,user action</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707925</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Code" target="Security Procedure">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The code is used as part of a security procedure to authenticate the correct sensor and prevent incorrect pairing.</data>
  <data key="d10">authentication,verification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c5646d299deb5989a133b3e471666262</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707920</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Low Battery Pump Alert" target="Hyperglycemic Event">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Failure to replace batteries after a Low Battery Pump Alert may stop insulin delivery, potentially leading to a hyperglycemic event.</data>
  <data key="d10">device failure,treatment interruption</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c35705afcd32698e0eb1756f2c3484a4</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708325</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Max Basal Alarm" target="Basal Delivery">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Max Basal Alarm activates when the maximum allowable basal insulin rate is reached.</data>
  <data key="d10">delivery limit,system safety</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3e357d257472a32b4391dbea0465b3b0</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778707928</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Basal Patterns" target="Basal Screen">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Basal Patterns are configured and viewed on the Basal Screen of the device.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration,display</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-3f39c0ebbd9b32994a3bb5daf68794d7</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708308</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Temp Basal Rate" target="Max Basal Limit">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">If a preset temp basal rate exceeds the max basal limit, it is grayed out and cannot be selected.</data>
  <data key="d10">rate restriction,system constraint</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-bc1664dd2b2f62661bb5b9e88843be38</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708109</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Temp Basal Rate" target="High Activity">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">High Activity is one of the predefined names for a preset temp basal rate used during intense physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d10">activity-based adjustment,preset naming</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708187</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Temp Basal Rate" target="Moderate Activity">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Moderate Activity is a named preset temp basal rate option for periods of moderate physical exertion.</data>
  <data key="d10">activity-based adjustment,preset naming</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708188</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Temp Basal Rate" target="Low Activity">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Low Activity is a named preset temp basal rate option for use during minimal physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d10">activity-based adjustment,preset naming</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708189</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Temp Basal Rate" target="Sick">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sick is a named preset temp basal rate option intended for use when the user is unwell.</data>
  <data key="d10">health condition adjustment,preset naming</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708190</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Temp Basal Rate" target="Temp 1 Through Temp 4">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Temp 1 through Temp 4 are additional preset temp basal rate slots available for other custom situations.</data>
  <data key="d10">customization,flexible usage</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708191</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Preset Temp Basal Rate" target="Preset Temp Setup">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Preset Temp Setup screen allows users to add, edit, rename, or delete preset temp basal rates.</data>
  <data key="d10">configuration,editing functionality</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d804deb6af40863e070e5662228587f</data>
  <data key="d12">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1778708193</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Manage Settings" target="Save Settings">
